w Chandigarh (Mullanpur)',28,507,'140901','1','<p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 0);\">Concise Statement of Facts</span></p><ul><li>The respondent launched a residential group housing project known as Omaxe Greens situated at Ambala Chandigarh Road, Village Jharmari, Tehsil Derabassi, District Patiala (Punjab) in the year 2006. The project comprises of 9 multi storey towers, with common areas for parkas, internal roads, utilities, covered car parking, shopping complex and club facilities and areas earmarked for EWS etc.&nbsp;</li><li>The project was commenced in May 2006 and the respondent has already taken partial completion from competent authority for 5 towers. The total area of the complex is 15.884 acres comprising of residential 4.679 acres, commerical 0.540 acres, community centre 0.371 acres, green 3.472 acres, STP 0.167 acres, Water Works 0.066 acres, Roads and Open spaces 6.588 acres.&nbsp;</li><li>The development works in balance 4 towers i.e. GT 4,6,8,9 is in progress and expected to be completed by January 2019 and this phase of the project comprising of 250 apartments is registered with the Authority. The project is registered with the authority based upon revised layout plan dated 25.03.2014 indicating the areas for parks 1-8 and 1,b,c,d as 3.472 acres and roads and open spaces as 6.588 acres, commercial complex is allocated areas of 0.371 acres.</li><li>The committed facilities include the dedicated car parking, 100% power back up, 4 elevators in every tower, state of the art shopping complex, 24 hours water supply, universal club facilities. The allottees have been charges for Open Parking @ 60,000/- and Covered Parking @Rs. 1,00,000/-, Club membership @ Rs. 25,000/- and Power back up @60,000/- which is mentioned in the agreements to sell.&nbsp;</li><li><span style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 0);\">Grounds for complaint</span></li><li>Covered Parking is available approximately 70% of the total allocated and open parking space is short by half of what is charged and balance open parking is being provided through encroachment of green areas and internal roads.&nbsp;</li><li>The committed facilities of power back up, 4 elevators in every tower, shopping complex and 24 hours water supply and universal club facilities are not being provided. The Omaxe management ensured completion of the gaps in these facilities within 3 to 6 months way back in June 2015 as per MOM dated 19.06.2015. These issues are still pending.</li><li>The club facility is now being advertised for another RERA registered project of the respondent which is a separate residential complex. Club is being connected by making a special gate into the existing complex.</li><li>The respondent has been offering fit out possessions to the allottees with the objective of avoiding penalties for delay in offering possession and also maintenance services have been charged from the allottees from the date of fit out possessions.&nbsp;</li><li>As per clause G of the draft agreement for sale, Punjab RERA Rules, 2017, the residential unit is defined as apartment, garage/covered parking and proportionate share of the the common areas. As per this definition, the residential unit would be treated as complete/ready for possession when all the components of the residential units as above are fully developed.&nbsp;</li><li>The part of the ongoing project comprising of towers GT4, 6, 8,9 is registered with the authority. The respondent has not submitted status of development works of common areas/amenities along with the application for registration with a mala fide intention as it has already violated the specifications of revised layout plan dated 25.03.2014 attracting the provisions of Section 4 of the Act.</li><li>The respondent has also violated the provisions of Section 14 by not adhering to the sanctioned layout plans and Section 17 by offering fit out possessions without having completion/occupancy certificate for the project/units.</li></ul>','<p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 0);\">In view of the above</span>, it is humbly prayed that the Authority may consider and direct the respondent <a href=\"to:-\">to:-</a></p><ul><li>Submit the status of development works/amenities of the residential complex as per the revised layout plans dated 25.03.2014 to the Authority.</li><li>To complete the development works/amenities of the residential complex as per revised layout plan/committed amenities/facilities in the agreement for sale and marketing brochure.</li><li>To acquire additional piece of land in the adjoining area and provide adequate covered/open parking as charged in the agreement for sale.</li><li>Not offering fit out possessions without having completion/occupancy certificate from the competent authority for the residential complex/residential unit respectively.</li><li>To submit undertaking that the common areas would be handed over to the Association of Allottees upon obtaining completion certificate for the registered phase of the project.</li></ul><p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 0);\">In <a href=\"addition:-\">addition:-</a></span></p><ul><li>it is further prayed that the authority may declare the fit out possession without having completion/occupancy certificate invalid to enable the allottees to claim interest and compensation for the delayed period on case to case basis.</li><li>Impose strictest penalty on the respondent for violating the provisions of Section 4 read with Section 60, Section 14, 17 read with Section 61 of the Act.</li></ul><p><br></p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p><br></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',1,1,0,0,'harvindersinghomaxe','2018-08-14 21:15:48.000','harvindersinghomaxe','2018-08-14 21:15:48.000'),(72,1023,'1023',1040,'a147b67e-0e01-42fd-9e99-390d21e31f08','FormTypeM',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Mehak Aggarwal','mehakmukul@gmail.com',9878189241,0,443790646394,'H 