ject and in\r\npursuance of the said booking, he was allotted flat no. D-703 on 7</span><sup style=\"font-family: &quot;Century Gothic&quot;, sans-serif;\">th</sup><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Century Gothic&quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 14pt;\">\r\nFloor in Tower-D vide allotment letter dated 16.04.2013.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Century Gothic&quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 14pt;\">That a buyer’s agreement was signed between the\r\ncomplainant no. 1 and the respondent on 16.02.2013.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Century Gothic&quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 14pt;\">The respondent was thereafter offered possession\r\nof the said apartment on 14.08.2015 and the possession of the said apartment\r\nwas taken over by the respondent on 26.08.2015.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Century Gothic&quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Further it is pertinent to mention here that in\r\nthe possession handing over letter, the respondent had undertaken to pay the\r\nmaintenance charges after taking over possession of the said apartment and had\r\nalso undertaken to enter into a maintenance agreement. The respondent had\r\nthereafter, entered into a maintenance agreement dated 26.08.2015 with the\r\ncomplainant no. 2.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Century Gothic&quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 14pt;\">That the respondent despite been in possession\r\nof the said apartment, has not been paying the maintenance charges fixed as per\r\nthe maintenance agreement and is enjoying all the services free of cost. It is\r\nfurther pertinent to mention here that a number of public notices has been got\r\nattached in the society whereby the respondent was called upon various times\r\nfor payment of the maintenance charges but no heed was paid to the said notices\r\nby the respondent.&nbsp;</span><br></p>','<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nmso-text-indent-alt:-9.0pt;line-height:200%;ms