p><br></p><p>4. That the Amount with interest @18% rounded to Rs 16 lakh plus Rs 2lakh as harrassement and mentally torture Charges is equal to Rs 18 lakh.</p><p><br></p><p>5. Please help me in refunding my this Amount ov Rs 18 lakh from them.</p><p><br></p><p>I shall be thankful to you.</p><p><br></p><p>Hardeep Singh</p>',4750000.00,1319360.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>I want to explain that;</p><p><br></p><p>1.In view of my above explaination the Promoter totally failed in providing Service to Customers and also unable to refund the amount after the notice of 15days which very well falls under National Consumer Act 1986.</p><p><br></p><p>2.And also they have given advertisements for promotion of the project before 1 year without RERA Approval. Which very well falls under PB RERA Act 2016.</p><p><br></p><p>3. That they have been harrassed me very much by giving false statements and also tortured me mentally by saying that you can do anything and God will teach me lesson. I dont know what I have done wrong by paying them Rs 1319360. And I got problem of high BP and hypertension due to their mentally torture to me. I am now taking medicines due to them. So kindly fine them Rs 200000 for &nbsp;harrassement and mentally torture to me.</p><p><br></p><p>4. That the Amount with interest @18% rounded to Rs 16 lakh plus Rs 2lakh as harrassement and mentally torture Charges is equal to Rs 18 lakh.</p><p><br></p><p>5. Please help me in refunding my this Amount ov Rs 18 lakh from them.</p><p><br></p><p>I shall be thankful to you.</p><p><br></p><p>Hardeep Singh</p>','1','','2017-07-03 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','124 and 158','','',1,0,0,0,'HSToor','2018-09-22 18:58:18.000','HSToor','2018-09-22 18:58:18.000'),(150,1065,'1065',1120,'84277fb5-7a10-4661-b624-f0f8791464ea','FormTypeM',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Naresh Kumar Saini & Nidhi Saini','jagan2702@gmail.com',9463990426,0,0,'H. No.115-A','Jarnail Enclave, Phase-I, Zirakpur',28,527,'140603','1','H. No.115-A','Jarnail Enclave, Phase-I, Zirakpur',28,527,'140603','JAGAN NATH BHANDARI','advbhandarichd@gmail.com',9855677966,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PC0022','Maya Garden Nagnesia','Barnala Builder through Director','info@mayagardenmagnesia.com',0,0,'Barnala Builders Through Director, SCO No. 1& 2 Maya Garden City, Mangla Road, Zirakpur, ','District-Mohali',28,527,'140603','1','Barnala Builders Through Director, SCO No. 1& 2 Maya Garden City, Mangla Road, Zirakpur, ','District-Mohali',28,527,'140603','1','<p>1. That the applicants have booked three units (in partnership of specific % percentage) in Magnesia i.e. Two Fine Dining (FD-03 and FD-12 A) and one Food court (FC-08) in October 2016 under 12 % assured scheme with other partners who are made Performa respondents. The transaction took place in presence of Mr. Deepak Jindal, Director Maya Garden Magnesia and other employees i.e. Mr Kataria (Business head), Mr. Raman and Mr. Shine and Channel Partner Sh. Anil. Kindly see the share of different partners in the said project in tabular form below:\r\n</p><p>UNIT 	Naresh	Nidhi	Sheela	Rakesh	Puneet	Om Parkash\r\n</p><p>FC-8	50%					50%\r\n</p><p>FD 3 	50%		35%		15%	\r\n</p><p>FD 12 A		35%	35%	20%	10%	\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>Kindly see the MOU’s / Agreement for the same appended as Annexure A-1, Annexure A-2 &amp; Annexure A-3. \r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>2. That the respondent no. 1, Maya Garden Magnesia committed of coming up with Cineplex on 5th Floor and Entertainment zone on 4th Floor respectively. Only then the applicants made the investment in said project. \r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>3. That the respondent no.1 assured launching of project during Navratras, as the approvals were under process and first installment was to be made after start of construction in January 2017.\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>4. That in good faith and in view of past projects of Respondent no. 1, M/s Barnala Builders, applicants paid 30 % payment through cheques of each fine dining and food court unit along with other Performa respondents. Kindly see the payment record in tabular form as Annexure A- 4.\r\n</p><p>5. That later on, approvals of project got delayed by respondent no. 1 and same were taken in August/September 2017 and later on construction work started at the site. Then again applicant paid 30% payment for Food Court FC-8 to the respondent no.1. As per agreement, the second installment was due in March 2018 i.e. 6th month after starting of construction. \r\n</p><p><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Note: Remaining detailed facts are mentioned in Annexure attached as Complaint in PDF form.</span></p>','<p>In view of the facts mentioned in paragraph 4 above, the applicant prays for the following:- \r\n</p><p>I.	Since applicant and Performa respondents have reached an arrangement that food court FC-08 for which 60% payment has already been made (combined of Performa respondents), therefore 40 % payment be adjusted from the cost of both Fine Dining units (FD 3 &amp; 12 A) for which total Rs 52 Lacs approx. has been paid by Performa respondents so far and on their advise both Fine dining are therefore surrendered because of mis-commitment, non-fulfillment and false advertising by the respondents regarding Cineplex and Entertainment Zone. The respondent be penalized u/s 60 for non-conforming the provisions of Sec 4 of the RERA Act. Kindly see the payment record as Annexure 4. \r\n</p><p>II. That after settlement the amount in FC-08 price, remaining amount be refunded to applicants and Performa respondents with 12% interest as per Memorandum of Understanding (MOU) duly signed (Annexure A-1, A-2, A-3). The applicants on their discretion be allowed to invest in other units of same projects of respondent no. 1 at their own sweet will.\r\n</p><p>III. The respondent no. 1 may further be penalized for introducing material changes in violation of Sec 14 of the Act detrimental to the interest of applicants. Since a drastic change is made in layout of project from what was shown to applicants while booking &amp; taking first installment and what presently layout which is total changed then earlier as shown. Kindly Refer Annexure A-5 &amp; A-6.\r\n</p><p><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Note: Remaining reliefs&nbsp;are mentioned in Annexure attached as Complaint in PDF form.</span><br></p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\nline-height:200%;tab-stops:18.0pt\"><b><span style=\"font-size: 13pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif;\">Interim order, if prayed for: </span></b><span style=\"font-size: 13pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif;\">That\r\nthe respondent no. 1 be directed not to initiate any action, impose penalty or\r\npenal interest or any other monetary/physical harm or to units during the\r\npendency of this application. The status quo as on date for <b>FC-08</b> be kindly maintained in the\r\ninterest of justice. Further, respondent no. 1 be restrained from selling the\r\nunits in question (FC-8, FD-3, &amp; FD-12 A) to anyone till the pendency of\r\nthe dispute nor create any 3<sup>rd</sup> party interest in the favour of\r\nanyone. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\nline-height:200%;tab-stops:18.0pt\"><span style=\"font-size: 6pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif;\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'jagan2702','2018-09-24 12:47:04.000','jagan2702','2018-09-24 12:47:04.000'),(151,1065,'1065',1120,'84277fb5-7a10-4661-b624-f0f8791464ea','FormTypeM',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Naresh Kumar Saini & Nidhi Saini','jagan2702@gmail.com',9463990426,0,0,'H. No.115-A','Jarnail Enclave, Phase-I, Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','1','H. No.115-A','Jarnail Enclave, Phase-I, Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','JAGAN NATH BHANDARI','advbhandarichd@gmail.com',9855677966,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PC0022','Maya Garden Nagnesia','Barnala Builder through Director','info@mayagardenmagnesia.com',0,0,'Barnala Builders Through Director, SCO No. 1& 2 Maya Garden City, Mangla Road, Zirakpur, ','District-Mohali',28,527,'140603','1','Barnala Builders Through Director, SCO No. 1& 2 Maya Garden City, Mangla Road, Zirakpur, ','District-Mohali',28,527,'140603','1','<p>1. That the applicants have booked three units (in partnership of specific % percentage) in Magnesia i.e. Two Fine Dining (FD-03 and FD-12 A) and one Food court (FC-08) in October 2016 under 12 % assured scheme with other partners who are made Performa respondents. The transaction took place in presence of Mr. Deepak Jindal, Director Maya Garden Magnesia and other employees i.e. Mr Kataria (Business head), Mr. Raman and Mr. Shine and Channel Partner Sh. Anil. Kindly see the share of different partners in the said project in tabular form below:\r\n</p><p>UNIT 	Naresh	Nidhi	Sheela	Rakesh	Puneet	Om Parkash\r\n</p><p>FC-8	50%					50%\r\n</p><p>FD 3 	50%		35%		15%	\r\n</p><p>FD 12 A		35%	35%	20%	10%	\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>Kindly see the MOU’s / Agreement for the same appended as Annexure A-1, Annexure A-2 &amp; Annexure A-3. \r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>2. That the respondent no. 1, Maya Garden Magnesia committed of coming up with Cineplex on 5th Floor and Entertainment zone on 4th Floor respectively. Only then the applicants made the investment in said project. \r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>3. That the respondent no.1 assured launching of project during Navratras, as the approvals were under process and first installment was to be made after start of construction in January 2017.\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>4. That in good faith and in view of past projects of Respondent no. 1, M/s Barnala Builders, applicants paid 30 % payment through cheques of each fine dining and food court unit along with other Performa respondents. Kindly see the payment record in tabular form as Annexure A- 4.\r\n</p><p>5. That later on, approvals of project got delayed by respondent no. 1 and same were taken in August/September 2017 and later on construction work started at the site. Then again applicant paid 30% payment for Food Court FC-8 to the respondent no.1. As per agreement, the second installment was due in March 2018 i.e. 6th month after starting of construction. \r\n</p><p><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Note: Remaining detailed facts are mentioned in Annexure attached as Complaint in PDF form.</span></p>','<p>In view of the facts mentioned in paragraph 4 above, the applicant prays for the following:- \r\n</p><p>I.	Since applicant and Performa respondents have reached an arrangement that food court FC-08 for which 60% payment has already been made (combined of Performa respondents), therefore 40 % payment be adjusted from the cost of both Fine Dining units (FD 3 &amp; 12 A) for which total Rs 52 Lacs approx. has been paid by Performa respondents so far and on their advise both Fine dining are therefore surrendered because of mis-commitment, non-fulfillment and false advertising by the respondents regarding Cineplex and Entertainment Zone. The respondent be penalized u/s 60 for non-conforming the provisions of Sec 4 of the RERA Act. Kindly see the payment record as Annexure 4. \r\n</p><p>II. That after settlement the amount in FC-08 price, remaining amount be refunded to applicants and Performa respondents with 12% interest as per Memorandum of Understanding (MOU) duly signed (Annexure A-1, A-2, A-3). The applicants on their discretion be allowed to invest in other units of same projects of respondent no. 1 at their own sweet will.\r\n</p><p>III. The respondent no. 1 may further be penalized for introducing material changes in violation of Sec 14 of the Act detrimental to the interest of applicants. Since a drastic change is made in layout of project from what was shown to applicants while booking &amp; taking first installment and what presently layout which is total changed then earlier as shown. Kindly Refer Annexure A-5 &amp; A-6.\r\n</p><p><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Note: Remaining reliefs&nbsp;are mentioned in Annexure attached as Complaint in PDF form.</span><br></p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\nline-height:200%;tab-stops:18.0pt\"><b><span style=\"font-size: 13pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif;\">Interim order, if prayed for: </span></b><span style=\"font-size: 13pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif;\">That\r\nthe respondent no. 1 be directed not to initiate any action, impose penalty or\r\npenal interest or any other monetary/physical harm or to units during the\r\npendency of this application. The status quo as on date for <b>FC-08</b> be kindly maintained in the\r\ninterest of justice. Further, respondent no. 1 be restrained from selling the\r\nunits in question (FC-8, FD-3, &amp; FD-12 A) to anyone till the pendency of\r\nthe dispute nor create any 3<sup>rd</sup> party interest in the favour of\r\nanyone. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\nline-height:200%;tab-stops:18.0pt\"><span style=\"font-size: 6pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif;\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',1,0,0,0,'jagan2702','2018-09-24 12:58:30.000','jagan2702','2018-09-24 12:58:30.000'),(152,1066,'1066',1124,'087e73d4-6bec-4c26-b1cb-b87f1596c5c3','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Nitin  Prashar','prashar1515@gmail.com',9417408002,0,0,'Flat no. 704, Green valley towers ','oppschool, old ambala kalka highway, Zirakpur',28,507,'160104','1','Flat no. 704, Green valley towers ','oppschool, old ambala kalka highway, Zirakpur',28,507,'160104','Ashwani kumar Prashar','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PC0022','Maya garden Magnesia ','Deepak Jindal','sanjeev_ch32@yahoo.co.in',0,0,'Chandigarh-Ambala highway, opp. Mc-Donalds, zirakpur','',28,507,'140603','1','Chandigarh-Ambala highway, opp. Mc-Donalds, zirakpur','',28,507,'140603','1','<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"margin-left:54.0pt;mso-add-space:\r\nauto;text-align:justify;text-indent:-18.0pt;line-height:150%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\">a.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">No\r\nreceipt was issued &nbsp;to me for payment\r\nmade to builder/agent and no copy of any agreement was provided to me of the booked\r\ncommercial unit (virtual space) on 09/01/2018 by paying Rs. One lakh and first\r\ninstalment of Rs. 5,62,434 only totalling Rs. 6,62,434 only, but the builder\r\nand the broker are reluctant to get agreement executed on RERA prescribed\r\nproforma&nbsp; and denied to get it\r\nregistered. Now stopped paying monthly interest. Both builder and the two\r\nagents’ indifferent attitude has lead me to believe that I have been cheated by\r\nthem.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-left:54.0pt;mso-add-space:\r\nauto;text-align:justify;text-indent:-18.0pt;line-height:150%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\">b.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">The\r\nbuilder even after receiving about 25% of the total payment that is rupees\r\n6,62,434/- rupees (six lakh sixty two thousand four hundred and thirty four\r\nonly), did not keep his words to get the sale agreement on annexure ‘A’\r\n(proforma prescribed by Punjab RERA) exempted and registered denying me the\r\ncomplete information of the project. In view of reluctance on the part of\r\nbuilder to comply with rules and regulations has lead to erosion of credibility\r\nof the builder in view of cheating with me. I have been requesting the builder\r\nand the real estate agents since 01/05/2018&nbsp;\r\nto repay my whole amount which they have not done so far. You are\r\nrequested to direct the builder and the real estate agent to refund my money in\r\nfull along with interest upto date.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-left:54.0pt;mso-add-space:\r\nauto;text-align:justify;text-indent:-18.0pt;line-height:150%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\">c.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">The\r\nbuilder and the real estate agents are reluctant to issue proper receipt/invoice\r\nin token of having received token money and instalment from the undersigned\r\nhence have cheated me, an innocent young man.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"margin-left:54.0pt;mso-add-space:auto;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-indent:-18.0pt;line-height:150%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\">d.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">The\r\nreluctant and whimsical attitude of the builder along with unfair dealings have\r\nlead me to undue mental stress and humiliation.&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"margin-left:54.0pt;mso-add-space:auto;\r\ntext-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\">a.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">The\r\nbuilder be directed to refund my money i.e. Rs. 6,62,434.00, which he has taken\r\nfrom me by unfair means and further he be directed to pay me the interest\r\nthereon as agreed immediately.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n<span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:Calibri;mso-fareast-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-ansi-language:\r\nEN-IN;mso-fareast-language:EN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; b. The builder and\r\nagents be directed to compensate me for the harassment, mental torture and&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;business loss due to their false promises.</span><br></p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:Calibri;\r\nmso-fareast-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN;mso-fareast-language:\r\nEN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\">Payment of the principal amount and interest theron\r\n&nbsp;as agreed agreed i.e. 1% per month.</span><br></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',1,0,0,0,'Nitin15','2018-09-25 14:20:40.000','Nitin15','2018-09-25 14:20:40.000'),(153,1067,'1067',1115,'0c0ffa23-22c5-436e-a595-1aab1e70ec7b','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Vikas  Bhatia','bhatiavikas2009@gmail.com',7087404458,0,0,'1044 a 41 b','',6,128,'160041','1','1044 a 41 b','',6,128,'160041','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0038','GILLCO VALLEY','GILLCO DEVELOPERS AND BUILDERS PRIVATE LIMITED','info@gillcogroup.com',0,0,'GILLCO VALLEY CHANDIGARH KHARAR HIGHWAY  NH21','',28,507,'140301','1','GILLCO VALLEY CHANDIGARH KHARAR HIGHWAY  NH21','',28,507,'140301','1','<p>1. That  in January 2014, the complainant had booked a unit no. 1429 , First Floor, In Gillco Budget Homes, Gillco Valley, Chandigarh-Kharar Highway, NH-21, Kharar, Greater Mohali, for a total sale consideration of Rs. 2740000/-.</p><p>2. That the complainant had made a payment of Rs. 403500/- at the time of booking and Buyers Agreement was executed on 17.1.2014 and allotment letter was also provided to the complainant on 17.1.2014.</p><p>3. That&nbsp; the complainant availed home loan facility from HDFC Bank and made further payments of Rs. 14 Lacs to the respondent through Bank loan, on couple of occasions i.e. on 21.3.2014 –Rs. 1100000/- and 12.2.2015-Rs. 300000/-</p><p>4. That as per terms and conditions of the Buyers Agreement, the possession of the unit was to be delivered by the respondent within 12 months from the date of execution of the Buyers Agreement i.e. the possession was to be delivered on or before 17.1.2015.</p><p>5. That there being defect in title and also due to non-compliance of several laws and in absence of requisite approvals including Occupation Certificate etc., the respondent has not been able to deliver the possession of the said unit to the complainant till date i.e. even expiry of 4 years from the date of booking despite receiving Rs. 1803500/- from the complainant. Even the financial institutions have refused to release the funds/further loan amounts to respondent in absence of requisite approvals.</p><p>6. That the complainant has been visiting the office of the respondent but of no avail.</p><p>7. That the respondent has not discharged the obligations cast upon it in the terms and conditions of the Buyers Agreement and is in total breach and violation of the provisions of Punjab RERA Rules and is also guilty of cheating the allottees.</p><p>8. That due to malafide intents of the respondent, the complainant has been forced to make payment of rent to landowners as well as Pre-EMIs to the Bank.</p><p>9. That the complainant has suffered huge financial losses, mental trauma and</p>','<p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<style type=\"text/css\">\r\np.p1 {margin: 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 36.0px; text-align: justify; text-indent: -36.0px; font: 14.3px Times; -webkit-text-stroke: #000000}\r\nspan.s1 {font-kerning: none}\r\n</style>\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\">The complainant requests that the amounts worth Rs. 1803500/- paid by the complainant to the respondent towards &nbsp;the said unit be refunded alongwith interest as prescribed under law from the date of respective payment and penalty be imposed upon the respondent for the violation of the provisions of applicable statutes and rules.</span></p>',2740000.00,1803500.00,'2015-01-17 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>NIL</p>','1','','2014-01-17 00:00:00','2014-01-17 00:00:00','1429 FIRST FLOOR GILLCO BUDGET HOMES GILLCO VALLEY','','',1,0,0,0,'bhatiavikas2009@gmail.com','2018-09-26 08:00:29.000','bhatiavikas2009@gmail.com','2018-09-26 08:00:29.000'),(154,1068,'1068',1124,'087e73d4-6bec-4c26-b1cb-b87f1596c5c3','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Nitin  Prashar','prashar1515@gmail.com',9417408002,0,0,'Flat no. 704, Green valley towers ','oppschool, old ambala kalka highway, Zirakpur',28,507,'160104','1','Flat no. 704, Green valley towers ','oppschool, old ambala kalka highway, Zirakpur',28,507,'160104','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PC0022','Maya Garden Magnesia','Barnala builders','sanjeev_ch32@yahoo.co.in',0,0,'maya garden magnesia','opp. mc-donalds, chandigarh ambala highway, zirakpur',28,507,'140603','1','maya garden magnesia','opp. mc-donalds, chandigarh ambala highway, zirakpur',28,507,'140603','1','<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"margin-left:54.0pt;mso-add-space:\r\nauto;text-align:justify;text-indent:-18.0pt;line-height:150%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\">a.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">No\r\nreceipt was issued &nbsp;to me for payment\