 applicant kept on\r\napproaching the respondents for the possession and other amenities thereafter,\r\nbut nothing was informed to them. The most important clause as per the\r\nallotment letter is clause no. 6 i.e. possession and ownership as per&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif; font-size: 13pt; line-height: 200%; text-indent: -0.5in;\">Annexure A1. The\r\nclause of possession and ownership very clearly stated that possession will be\r\ngiven within 90% days from the date of issuance of allotment letter. The abovenoted\r\nclause proved to be fatal as per the agreement with the parties.</span><span style=\"font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif; font-size: 13pt; line-height: 200%; text-indent: -0.5in;\">&nbsp; </span><span style=\"font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif; font-size: 13pt; line-height: 200%; text-indent: -0.5in;\">No possession has been handed over up till now but the parties are still being charged interest and penal interest. There is no denial to the fact in\r\nthe present case that the amount of 25% was duly paid and the amount was duly\r\ncredited with the respondent.</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-justify:\r\ninter-ideograph;text-indent:-.5in;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size:\r\n13.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:11.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-justify:\r\ninter-ideograph;text-indent:-.5in;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size:\r\n13.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:11.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p>good</p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>okk</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'akhilesh','2018-10-04 15:48:50.000','akhilesh','2018-10-04 15:48:50.000'),(183,1077,'1077',1126,'c5d5539f-f896-4a4a-9808-f6498fce3578','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-10-05 12:09:37.000','narender sharma','narendersharmachd45@gmail.com',9056296154,0,0,'h.no 1632','vill. burail',6,128,'160047','1','h.no 1632','vill. burail',6,128,'160047','','',0,0,'Agent','PBRERA-SAS79-PRO329_','dara garden ','dara buildtech and developers limited','daraestates@hotmail.com',8302000555,0,'sco 3 & 4 khuni majra','kharar landran road ',28,507,'140301','1','sco 3 & 4 khuni majra','kharar landran road ',28,507,'140301','1','<p>plot is actually associated with dara kingdom project under dara garden</p><p>i have paid a part of booking amount of rs 11000 vide receipt no.0631 dated 14/01/2018 for 1 bhk top floor</p><p>i have also paid remaining 12.5% of booking amount of rs.59000 was paid on 04/03/2018</p><p>it was mutually agreed that a bank loan of rs 500000 will be started to pay the balance amount in june 2018for which company started paper work but no response received till august&nbsp;</p><p>then i contacted the company and company said it is not so easy to get a flat at this rate rather it would take 2 or 3 years</p><p>then i requested the company to return my money for which they decline my request and offer my another flat of rs 12 lack to which am not able to buy.</p><p>moreover they also offer me to deposit&nbsp; your money in for 5 years and we would give you money back at 12% interest rate&nbsp;</p><p>another day i visited their now they said we will not refund your money you will not do anything if you want to go to higher authority you can but result would be the same we know all authority persons you will not get your money back even through hook or cook.</p>','<p>i want full compensation with interest of my deposited amount&nbsp; of rs 70000 or i want possession at the decided rate of 5 lac at the time of booking&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>',570000.00,70000.00,'2019-02-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>i want full compensation with interest of my deposited amount&nbsp; of rs 70000 or i want possession at the decided rate of 5 lac at the time of booking&nbsp;&nbsp;<br></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',1,1,0,0,'NARENDER.1981','2018-10-05 12:09:34.000','NARENDER.1981','2018-10-05 12:09:34.000'),(184,1076,'1076',1120,'84277fb5-7a10-4661-b624-f0f8791464ea','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-10-06 20:10:11.000','Naresh Kumar Saini & Nidhi Saini','jagan2702@gmail.com',9463990426,0,0,'R/o #115 A, Jarnail Enclave Phase- 1, ','Zirakpur, ',28,507,'140603','1','R/o #115 A, Jarnail Enclave Phase- 1, ','Zirakpur, ',28,507,'140603','Jagan Nath Bhandari','advbhandarichd@gmail.com',9855677966,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PC0022','Maya Garden Magnesia','Barnala Builders through its Director and others','info@mayagardenmagnesia.com',0,0,' SCO 1 & 2, Maya Garden City, Opposite McDonalds , NH 22, Chd-Ambala Highway.','Nangla Road, Zirakpur, ',28,507,'140603','1',' SCO 1 & 2, Maya Garden City, Opposite McDonalds , NH 22, Chd-Ambala Highway.','Nangla Road, Zirakpur, ',28,507,'140603','1','<p style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0cm;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif;\">﻿</span><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">1. That the applicants have booked three units (in partnership of\r\nspecific % percentage) in Magnesia i.e. Two Fine Dining (FD-03 and FD-12 A) and\r\none Food court (FC-08) in October 2016 under 12 % assured scheme with other\r\npartners who are made Performa respondents. Kindly see the share of different\r\npartners in the said project in tabular form below:</span><u1:p></u1:p><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin: 0cm 0cm 7.5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">UNIT</span><u1:p></u1:p><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin: 0cm 0cm 7.5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">FC-8 50%&nbsp; Naresh 50% Om Parkash</span><u1:p></u1:p><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin: 0cm 0cm 7.5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">FD 3 50%&nbsp; Naresh 35% Sheela 15%\r\nPuneet</span><u1:p></u1:p><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin: 0cm 0cm 7.5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">FD 12 A 35% Nidhi 35% Sheela 20%\r\nRakesh 10% Puneet</span><u1:p></u1:p><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin: 0cm 0cm 7.5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">MOU/Agreements are Annexure A-1,\r\nAnnexure A-2 &amp; Annexure A-3.</span><u1:p></u1:p><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin: 0cm 0cm 7.5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">2. That the\r\nrespondent no. 1, Maya Garden Magnesia committed of coming up with Cineplex on\r\n5th Floor and Entertainment zone on 4th Floor respectively. Only then the\r\napplicants made the investment in said project. Kindly see the payment record\r\nin tabular form as Annexure A- 4.</span><u1:p></u1:p><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin: 0cm 0cm 7.5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">3. That the\r\napplicants approached Respondent no. 1 to do ‘Agreement to Sell” but surprisingly\r\nthe project layout plan was changed and more units were added to make extra\r\nprofit at the cost of applicants. Neither Cineplex nor Entertainment zone came\r\nin approved layout plan that was shown to applicants at the time of booking.\r\nThe layout plan which was shown at the time of booking is Annexure A-5 and new\r\nlayout plan is Annexure A-6.</span><u1:p></u1:p><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin: 0cm 0cm 7.5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">4. That later\r\ndespite applicants’ request for ‘Agreement to Sell’, respondent no. 1 started\r\ndemanding future payments of said project and even stopped assured return from\r\nNovember 2017 rather giving an option of compensation or adjustment due to\r\nchange in layout plans.</span><u1:p></u1:p><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin: 0cm 0cm 7.5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">5. That even\r\nafter dual standards of respondent no. 1 and false promises made by them at the\r\ntime of initial payment, applicants, instead of filing complaint in RERA and to\r\nmaintain cordial relations, have amongst themselves with all other Performa\r\nrespondents decided to surrender both the fine dining’s units (FD-03 &amp; 12\r\nA) and to retain the food court unit (FC-8) for....</span><u1:p></u1:p><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0cm;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"margin: 0cm 0cm 7.5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">Character\r\nlimit exceeded so Kindly see Attachment attach as \"Detailed Complaint\".</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p>In view of the facts mentioned in paragraph 4 above, the applicant prays for the following:- \r\n</p><p>I.	Since applicant and Performa respondents have reached an arrangement that food court FC-08 for which 60% payment has already been made (combined of Performa respondents), therefore 40 % payment be adjusted from the cost of both Fine Dining units (FD 3 &amp; 12 A) for which total Rs 52 Lacs approx. has been paid by Performa respondents so far and on their advise both Fine dining are therefore surrendered because of mis-commitment, non-fulfillment and false advertising by the respondents regarding Cineplex and Entertainment Zone. The respondent be penalized u/s 60 for non-conforming the provisions of Sec 4 of the RERA Act. Kindly see the payment record as Annexure 4. \r\n</p><p>II. That after settlement the amount in FC-08 price, remaining amount be refunded to applicants and Performa respondents with 12% interest as per Memorandum of Understanding (MOU) duly signed (Annexure A-1, A-2, A-3). The applicants on their discretion be allowed to invest in other units of same projects of respondent no. 1 at their own sweet will.\r\n</p><p>III. The respondent no. 1 may further be penalized for introducing material changes in violation of Sec 14 of the Act detrimental to the interest of applicants. Since a drastic change is made in layout of project from what was shown to applicants while booking &amp; taking first installment and what presently layout which is total changed then earlier as shown. Kindly Refer Annexure A-5 &amp; A-6.\r\n</p><p>IV. That the respondent no. 1 sold the said units on account of Cineplex and Entertainment Zone. Since both the things don’t exist at present moment, the arrangement between the applicants and Performa respondents be kindly effected as per surrender applications (Annexure A-7, A-8) and remaining amount be duly returned with interest as per calculation..</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"font-family: roboto, serif; font-size: 24px;\">Character limit exceeded so Kindly see Attachment attach as \"Detailed Complaint\".</span><br></p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\nline-height:200%;tab-stops:18.0pt\"><span style=\"font-size: 13pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif;\">That the respondent\r\nno. 1 be directed not to initiate any action, impose penalty or penal interest\r\nor any other monetary/physical harm or to units during the pendency of this\r\napplication. The status quo as on date for <b>FC-08</b>\r\nbe kindly maintained in the interest of justice. Further, respondent no. 1 be\r\nrestrained from selling the units in question (FC-8, FD-3, &amp; FD-12 A) to\r\nanyone till the pendency of the dispute nor create any 3<sup>rd</sup> party\r\ninterest in the favour of anyone.&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','\r\nProperty no. FC-08,  Property no. FD- 12 A and Property no. FD- 03 in Maya Garden Magnesia ','','',1,1,0,0,'jagan2702','2018-10-06 20:10:05.000','jagan2702','2018-10-06 20:10:05.000'),(185,1084,'1084',1144,'ad7cbb11-1936-49ae-9d5f-0132c98b241c','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Munish dhir','Munish.dhir@gmail.com',1234567891,0,0,'aaaaaa','',15,42,'147001','1','aaaaaa','',15,42,'147001','munish','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-JAL30-PM0001','ffff','test','munish.dhir@gmail.com',0,0,'fff','',18,30,'123001','1','fff','',18,30,'123001','1','<p>dd</p>','<p>dddd</p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>fffffffffff</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',1,0,0,0,'MunishC1','2018-10-07 18:02:21.000','MunishC1','2018-10-07 18:02:21.000'),(186,1085,'1085',1135,'7ce4ff29-c893-46aa-aac9-b9c5d5926814','FormTypeM',1,1,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Gurmukh singh ','akhilesh@vyaslawassociates.com',8427828900,0,0,'Nikki Mandi, Patti, ','',28,574,'143001','1','Nikki Mandi, Patti, ','',28,574,'143001','akhilesh vyas','akhilesh@vyaslawassociates.com',9855004557,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-ASR02-PR0169','Guru Ram Dass Urban Estate','Punjab Urban Planning Development Authority','ca@puda.gov.in',0,0,'PUDA Bhawan','green avenue',28,39,'143001','1','PUDA Bhawan','green avenue',28,39,'143001','1','<p>That the complainant was allotted residential plot by respondent bearing plot No. 482 measuring 500 Sq. yards at Guru Ram Dass Urban Estate Airport Road, Amritsar. The total price of the plot is Rs. 945000/- @ 18000/- per square yard.&nbsp;<span style=\"font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif; font-size: 13pt; line-height: 115%;\">&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif; font-size: 13pt; line-height: 115%;\">As per the payment schedule given in the\r\nallotment letter 25% of the allotment amount was to be paid initially and rest\r\nof the payment was to be paid after the possession. The brochure of the scheme\r\nclearly reflects that possession will be handed over on 25% payment as per the allotment letter. It\r\nadmitted by the respondent that payment of Rs. 23,62,500/- was made by the complainant and it has already been adjusted towards initial 25% of the sale\r\nprice of residential plot as mentioned in clause No. 3.1. For the balance\r\npayment of 75% the schedule as follows was settled between the parties. The complainant has paid full sale consideration amount.&nbsp;</span><font face=\"Bookman Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 17px; line-height: 19px;\">After payment of 25% of total payment first installment was due on 27.10.2017. As per Para 6(i) under the Possession and Ownership Heading of allotment letter possession was be to handed over within 90 days of issuance of allotment letter. So time limit for possession date is 22.1.2017. &nbsp;There was no scene of handing over the possession as no development work was even initiated, applicant made a request through application (diary no 4869 dated 6.917) to waive off interest. But this letter elicited no response from respondent. To be on safer side of law applicant paid first installment (Principal and interest both) and then made the full payment.</span></font></p><p><font face=\"Bookman Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 17px; line-height: 19px;\"><br></span></font></p>','<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"margin-left:.75in;mso-add-space:auto;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;text-indent:-.5in;line-height:\r\n200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\r\nmso-bidi-font-size:11.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;\">i)<span style=\"font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:\r\n11.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">That as the\r\ndepartment has not adhered to their discipline of delivering the actual\r\npossession of the property as per the contract, therefore, the applicant shall\r\nnot be liable to pay any interest and penal interest. Respondent has charged interest\r\nto the tune of Rs 943705/- which is against the natural justice.&nbsp; Applicant should be refunded back interest\r\nwhich has been charged by the respondent. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-left:.75in;mso-add-space:\r\nauto;text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:11.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;\">ii)<span style=\"font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</span></span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:\r\n11.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">Interest on\r\namount which has been paid by applicant should be paid to applicant because of\r\ndelayed payment as per section 18 of The Punjab Real Estate (Regulation and\r\nDevelopment) Act 2016.&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-left:.75in;mso-add-space:\r\nauto;text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span style=\"text-indent: -0.5in; font-size: 12pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif;\">iii)<span style=\"font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><span style=\"text-indent: -0.5in; font-size: 12pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif;\">That the\r\napplicant is liable to be sufficient compensation as per the statue as they\r\nhave been denied their physical possession up till now without any explanatory\r\nreason by the department as per section 14 and 18 of Punjab Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) act 2016. They have not been handed over the\r\npossession of their allotted plots rather the applicant has made the payment as\r\nper the schedule to the respondent department. Uptill now there is no development on the site as well. &nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-left:.75in;mso-add-space:\r\nauto;text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:11.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;\">iv)<span style=\"font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:\r\n11.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">That as stated\r\nabove that the entire payment with regard to the plot allotted has already been\r\npaid still due to the change of plot from one location to another done by the\r\nrespondent themselves, they are demanding of Rs.4,50,000/- and charges ahead.\r\nThe respondent shall be restrained from claiming any such additional amount from\r\nthe applicant as&nbsp; it is never part of the\r\ncontract and any change done whatsoever is unilaterally done by the respondent\r\ndepartment itself.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"margin-left:.75in;mso-add-space:auto;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;text-indent:-.5in;line-height:\r\n200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\r\nmso-bidi-font-size:11.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;\">v)<span style=\"font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:\r\n11.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">That the\r\napplicant is also entitled for restoration of the original plot if so settled\r\nbetween the parties as this change has been done by respondent themselves and\r\nagainst the provisions of Punjab Real Estate ( Regulation &amp; Development)\r\nAct 2016.<o:p></o:p></span></p>',9450000.00,9450000.00,'2017-01-22 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>&nbsp;<span style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -0.5in; font-size: 12pt; line-height: 32px; font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif;\">i)<span style=\"font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span><span style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -0.5in; font-size: 12pt; line-height: 32px; font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif;\">That as the department has not adhered to their discipline of delivering the actual possession of the property as per the contract, therefore, the applicant shall not be liable to pay any interest and penal interest. Respondent has charged interest to the tune of Rs 943705/- which is against the natural justice.&nbsp;&nbsp;Applicant should be refunded back interest which has been charged by the respondent.</span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-left: 0.75in; text-align: justify; text-indent: -0.5in; line-height: 28px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 32px; font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif;\">ii)<span style=\"font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</span></span><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 32px; font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif;\">Interest on amount which has been paid by applicant should be paid to applicant because of delayed payment as per section 18 of The Punjab Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Act 2016.&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-left: 0.75in; text-align: justify; text-indent: -0.5in; line-height: 28px;\"><span style=\"text-indent: -0.5in; font-size: 12pt; line-height: 32px; font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif;\">iii)<span style=\"font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span><span style=\"text-indent: -0.5in; font-size: 12pt; line-height: 32px; font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif;\">That the applicant is liable to be sufficient compensation as per the statue as they have been denied their physical possession up till now without any explanatory reason by the department as per section 14 and 18 of Punjab Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) act 2016. They have not been handed over the possession of their allotted plots rather the applicant has made the payment as per the schedule to the respondent department. Uptill now there is no development on the site as well. &nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-left: 0.75in; text-align: justify; text-indent: -0.5in; line-height: 28px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 32px; font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif;\">iv)<span style=\"font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 32px; font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif;\">That as stated above that the entire payment with regard to the plot allotted has already been paid still due to the change of plot from one location to another done by the respondent themselves, they are demanding of Rs.4,50,000/- and charges ahead. The respondent shall be restrained from claiming any such additional amount from the applicant as&nbsp;&nbsp;it is never part of the contract and any change done whatsoever is unilaterally done by the respondent department itself.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"margin-left: 0.75in; text-align: justify; text-indent: -0.5in; line-height: 28px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 32px; font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif;\">v)<span style=\"font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 32px; font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif;\">That the applicant is also entitled for restoration of the original plot if so settled between the parties as this change has been done by respondent themselves and against the provisions of Punjab Real Estate ( Regulation &amp; Development) Act 2016.</span></p>','1','','2016-10-22 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','482','','',2,0,0,0,'akhilesh','2018-10-09 16:04:08.000','akhilesh','2018-10-09 16:04:08.000'),(187,1086,'1086',1135,'7ce4ff29-c893-46aa-aac9-b9c5d5926814','FormTypeM',1,1,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Rita Kaundal','akhilesh@vyaslawassociates.com',9950693693,0,0,'House No. 89-C, Gali No. 9 Guru amardass Avenue, Ajnala Road, amritsar','',28,39,'143001','1','House No. 89-C, Gali No. 9 Guru amardass Avenue, Ajnala Road, amritsar','',28,39,'143001','akhilesh vyas','akhilesh@vyaslawassociates.com',9855004557,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-ASR02-PR0169','Guru Ram Dass Urban Estate','Punjab Urban Planning Development Authority','ca@puda.gov.in',0,0,'PUDA Bhawan','green avenue',28,39,'143001','1','PUDA Bhawan','green avenue',28,39,'143001','1','<p><span style=\"font-size:13.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:11.0pt;\r\nline-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-theme-font:minor-fareast;mso-bidi-font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;mso-ansi-language:EN-US;\r\nmso-fareast-language:EN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\">That the complainant was\r\nallotted residential plot by Punjab Urban Planning and Development Authority\r\n(hereinafter called as “PUDA”) bearing residential plot No. 152 measuring 200\r\nSq. Yards at Guru Ram Dass Urban Estate Airport Road, Amritsar. The total price\r\nof the residential plot of Rs. 36.00 lacs only @ Rs. 18000/- per Sq. Yard. As\r\nper the payment schedule given in the allotment letter 25% of the allotment\r\namount was to be paid initially and rest of the payment was to be paid after\r\nthe possession. The brochure of the scheme clearly reflects that possession on\r\n25% payment as per the allotment letter it admitted by the respondent that\r\npayment of Rs. 9.00 lacs was made by the complainant and it has already been\r\nadjusted towards initial 25% of the sale price of residential plot as mentioned\r\nin clause No. 3.1.&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size:13.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:11.0pt;\r\nline-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-theme-font:minor-fareast;mso-bidi-font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;mso-ansi-language:EN-US;\r\nmso-fareast-language:EN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\">That no possession has been handed over up till now. there is no development at the site at all. Various letters has been forwarded to the Estate Officer PUDA Amritsar and RTI applications have been filed to their officers but nothing has resulted fruitful. The possession was scheduled to be given within 90 days after making payment of 25% but nothing has been done in this regard. The complainant has approached earlier Hon\'ble Punjab and Haryana High court vide which their representation was decided and she withdrew the earlier petition for seeking relief under this act.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size:13.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:11.0pt;\r\nline-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-theme-font:minor-fareast;mso-bidi-font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;mso-ansi-language:EN-US;\r\nmso-fareast-language:EN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\"><br></span><br></p>','<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"margin-left:.75in;mso-add-space:auto;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;text-indent:-.5in;line-height:\r\n200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size:13.0pt;\r\nmso-bidi-font-size:11.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;\">i)<span style=\"font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size:13.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:\r\n11.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">That as the\r\ndepartment has not adhered to their discipline of delivering the actual\r\npossession of the property as per the contract, therefore, the applicant shall\r\nnot be liable to pay any interest and penal interest on the future payments to\r\nbe made to the respondents and further payment of Principal amount shall be\r\ndeferred till the respondents hands over the actual physical possession. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-left:.75in;mso-add-space:\r\nauto;text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size:13.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:11.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;\">ii)<span style=\"font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size:13.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:\r\n11.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">That the\r\napplicant is not liable to pay any amount by way of penal interest if any\r\ncharged by the respondent department. They are liable to get the refund of any\r\npenal interest charged up till now as the delay any occurred is because of the\r\nconduct and acts of the respondent department. &nbsp;The interest already paid shall be\r\nrefunded&nbsp; or interest amount which is\r\nalready&nbsp; been charged by the respondents\r\nshall stands adjusted in the future payments as the delay has occurred due to\r\nlapse on the part of the respondents. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"margin-left:.75in;mso-add-space:auto;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;text-indent:-.5in;line-height:\r\n200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size:13.0pt;\r\nmso-bidi-font-size:11.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;\">iii)<span style=\"font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size:13.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:\r\n11.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">That the\r\napplicant is liable to be sufficient compensation as per the statue as they\r\nhave been denied their physical possession up till now without any explanatory\r\nreason by the department. They have not been handed over the possession of\r\ntheir allotted plots rather the applicant has made the payment as per the\r\nschedule to the respondent department.&nbsp; &nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"margin-left: 0.75in; text-align: justify; text-indent: -0.5in;\"><span style=\"text-indent: -0.5in; font-size: 13pt; line-height: 34px;\"><font face=\"Bookman Old Style, serif\">iv) &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></span><span style=\"line-height: 115%; text-indent: -0.5in; font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif; font-size: 13pt;\">That as stated above the extension was sought by\r\nthe</span><span style=\"line-height: 115%; text-indent: -0.5in; font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif; font-size: 13pt;\">&nbsp; </span><span style=\"line-height: 115%; text-indent: -0.5in; font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif; font-size: 13pt;\">complainant for 180 days and during\r\nthat period interest was charged by the respondents. The respondents shall be\r\ndirected to refund that interest amount or adjust that amount in the principal\r\namount in future payments</span></p>',3600000.00,900000.00,'2017-03-13 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"margin-left: 0.75in; text-align: justify; text-indent: -0.5in; line-height: 28px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13pt; line-height: 34px; font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif;\">i)<span style=\"font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span><span style=\"font-size: 13pt; line-height: 34px; font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif;\">That as the department has not adhered to their discipline of delivering the actual possession of the property as per the contract, therefore, the applicant shall not be liable to pay any interest and penal interest on the future payments to be made to the respondents and further payment of Principal amount shall be deferred till the respondents hands over the actual physical possession.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-left: 0.75in; text-align: justify; text-indent: -0.5in; line-height: 28px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13pt; line-height: 34px; font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif;\">ii)<span style=\"font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span><span style=\"font-size: 13pt; line-height: 34px; font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif;\">That the applicant is not liable to pay any amount by way of penal interest if any charged 