 permissions when the plot was sold to complainants. A list of dates of approvals (C6) and some important approval as (C7 &amp; C8)</span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:\r\njustify;line-height:200%;mso-layout-grid-align:none;text-autospace:none\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>','<span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Directing the respondent to refund the principle amount i.e.Rs. 1387500 along with interest as contemplated under rule 16 of The Punjab RERA Rules, 2017,as the complainants have lost faith in the respondent due to misrepresentation by it about the approvals &amp; stages of development during all these years ,did not issue any allotment letter &amp; execute the agreement till date, failed to develop the project &amp; thus the complainants wish to withdraw from the project.Also the respondent has committed violation of various provisions of PAPRA &amp; conditions of various approvals granted to it,as it could not collect any amount till the exemption is received under Section 44 of PAPRA which was granted on 25.1.17.The respondent collected the money from the complainants in 2011.The approvals were granted to the respondent on the ground that it will not sell any plot &amp; collect money from the general public till exemption under Section 44 of PAPRA is received.Also, inspite of receiving 30% of sale consideration the respondent did not execute any&nbsp; agreement &amp; issue a plot number till date &amp; asking the complainants to pay more money for getting the allotment letter &amp; execution of agreement in violation of Section 13 of RERA (ii)Directing the respondent to pay the compensation of Rs.10 lacs for deficiency in services, unfair trade practices &amp; harassment caused to the complainants &amp; for using their hard earned money for such a long period.(iii)Directing the respondent to pay litigation expenses to the tune of Rs.50000(iv)To take action against respondent under Section 61 of RERA for constant violation of provision of Section 13 of RERA as the respondent failed to issue any allotment letter &amp; execute the buyer’s agreement till date, inspite of receiving 30% of sale consideration (v) For cancelling the extension granted to the respondent for constantly violating&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 14px; text-align: justify;\">various\r\nprovisions of RERA and for indulging into unfair trade practices.</span><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>',4625000.00,1387500.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>A. The respondent be directed to provide the list of allottees to whom it has allotted/sold the 862 residential plots as per the layout plan approved by GMADA on 6.10.2015 and for which it is registered under RERA</p><p>B. The respondent be directed to provide the list of hypothecated plots which are hypothecated to GMADA, out of the approved 862 residential plots and 73 commercial plots.</p><p>C. The respondent be directed to provide the list of hypothected plots sold to general public.</p><p>d. The respondent be directed to provide the details of funds collected from the general public since 2010 in lieu of 862 residential plots which are part of approved layout and registered under Section 3 of RERA and also, the detail where such amount has been utilized by the respondent.</p><p>E. The respondent be directed to provide all the bank details where such amount has been deposited&nbsp; along with the statement of accounts since the year 2010.</p><p>F. The respondent be directed to provide the details of number of booking done by it since the year 2010 for the said 862 residential plots</p><p><br></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','NO ALLOTMENT AND AGREEMENT YET','','',2,0,0,0,'rerafilingformn','2018-10-26 22:03:21.000','rerafilingformn','2018-10-26 22:03:21.000'),(219,1095,'1095',1172,'fe8a123a-24f0-4e44-a8e1-3e154d6acf61','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Bhupinder Dogra','adv.ashish1087@gmail.com',9418066670,0,0,'village Dasoli','Tehsil Chopal',14,533,'171211','1','House No.253','Sector 4, Mansa Devi Complex',13,15,'134114','Sanjeev Gupta','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0093','PALM GARDEN','M/s Manohar Infrastructure & Constructions Pvt Ltd','nbs@manoharrealty.com',1725033524,0,'SCO- 139 -141, ','Sector-17C',6,128,'160017','1','SCO- 139 -141, ','Sector-17C',6,128,'160017','1','<p><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Complainants,on 18.10.2011 booked a(C1)250 sq yards plot @RS. 18500 per sq yd from the respondent in Palm Garden.Before booking of said plot,the respondent had assured the complainants that the development would be started very soon and possession will be delivered in 2 years.Complainant paid Rs. 1387500 i.e. 30% of sale consideration vide cheque(C2)dated 18.10.11.Insipte of repeated requests, respondent did not issue any allotment letter and execute the agreement. Respondent had even concealed that it was not having CLU.Infact the respondent had not even applied the necessary permissions when the plot was sold.The respondent vide its letter(C3),which was received by the complainants in Sept,2014,had assured to allot the plot by Dec,2014 but it failed to do so.After that the complainants,many times requested the respondent to issue the allotment letter and execute the agreement,but the respondent did not pay any heed to their request.Instead it started demanding more money for issuing allotment letter &amp; executing the agreement.The complainants visited the office of respondent many times during the year 2015, 2016, 2017 &amp; 2018 for redressal of their grievances but to no avail.A letter dated 3.7.17(C4)was also received by the complainants vide which the respondent invited the complainants to visit the project site.Accordingly the complainants visited the project site in Oct,2017 but the respondent started demanding more money for issuing the plot number and executing the agreement.The complainants again visited the office of respondent in Dec,2017 and Mar,2018 for getting the allotment letter and agreement but to no avail.The respondent always kept the complainants in dark about the approvals and development.It has failed to develop the project.It had not even applied the necessary permissions when the plot was sold to complainants.A list of dates of approvals (C5) and some important approval as (C6&amp;C7).Complaint for registration of FIR to vigilance 1.10.18 as C8</span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:\r\njustify;line-height:200%;mso-layout-grid-align:none;text-autospace:none\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Directing the respondent to refund the principle amount i.e.Rs. 1387500 along with interest as contemplated under rule 16 of The Punjab RERA Rules, 2017,as the complainants have lost faith in the respondent due to misrepresentation by it about the approvals &amp; stages of development during all these years ,did not issue any allotment letter &amp; execute the agreement till date, failed to develop the project &amp; thus the complainants wish to withdraw from the project.Also the respondent has committed violation of various provisions of PAPRA &amp; conditions of various approvals granted to it,as it could not collect any amount till the exemption is received under Section 44 of PAPRA which was granted on 25.1.17.The respondent collected the money from the complainants in 2011.The approvals were granted to the respondent on the ground that it will not sell any plot &amp; collect money from the general public till exemption under Section 44 of PAPRA is received.Also, inspite of receiving 30% of sale consideration the respondent did not execute any&nbsp; agreement &amp; issue a plot number till date &amp; asking the complainants to pay more money for getting the allotment letter &amp; execution of agreement in violation of Section 13 of RERA </span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">(ii)Directing the respondent to pay the compensation of Rs.10 lacs for deficiency in services, unfair trade practices &amp; harassment caused to the complainants &amp; for using their hard earned money for such a long period.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">(iii)Directing the respondent to pay litigation expenses to the tune of Rs.50000</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">(iv)To take action against respondent under Section 61 of RERA for constant violation of provision of Section 13 of RERA as the respondent failed to issue any allotment letter &amp; execute the buyer’s agreement till date, inspite of receiving 30% of sale consideration</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"> (v) For cancelling the extension granted to the respondent for constantly violating&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 14px; text-align: justify;\">various\r\nprovisions of RERA and for indulging into unfair trade practices.</span><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p></p>',4625000.00,1387500.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>A. The respondent be directed to provide the list of allottees to whom it has allotted/sold the 862 residential plots as per the layout plan approved by GMADA on 6.10.2015 and for which it is registered under RERA</p><p>B. The respondent be directed to provide the list of hypothecated plots which are hypothecated to GMADA, out of the approved 862 residential plots and 73 commercial plots.</p><p>C. The respondent be directed to provide the list of hypothected plots sold to general public.</p><p>d. The respondent be directed to provide the details of funds collected from the general public since 2010 in lieu of 862 residential plots which are part of approved layout and registered under Section 3 of RERA and also, the detail where such amount has been utilized by the respondent.</p><p>E. The respondent be directed to provide all the bank details where such amount has been deposited&nbsp; along with the statement of accounts since the year 2010.</p><p>F. The respondent be directed to provide the details of number of booking done by it since the year 2010 for the said 862 residential plots</p><p><br></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','NO ALLOTMENT AND AGREEMENT YET','','',2,0,0,0,'rerafilingformn','2018-10-26 22:45:50.000','rerafilingformn','2018-10-26 22:45:50.000'),(220,1095,'1095',1172,'fe8a123a-24f0-4e44-a8e1-3e154d6acf61','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Bhupinder Dogra','adv.ashish1087@gmail.com',9418066670,0,0,'village Dasoli','Tehsil Chopal',14,533,'171211','1','House No.253','Sector 4, Mansa Devi Complex',13,15,'134114','Sanjeev Gupta','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0093','PALM GARDEN','M/s Manohar Infrastructure & Constructions Pvt Ltd','nbs@manoharrealty.com',1725033524,0,'SCO- 139 -141, ','Sector-17C',6,128,'160017','1','SCO- 139 -141, ','Sector-17C',6,128,'160017','1','<p><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Complainants,on 18.10.2011 booked a(C1)250 sq yards plot @RS. 18500 per sq yd from the respondent in Palm Garden.Before booking of said plot,the respondent had assured the complainants that the development would be started very soon and possession will be delivered in 2 ye