ited the project site in Oct,2017 but the respondent started demanding more money for issuing the plot number and executing the agreement.The complainants again visited the office of respondent in Dec,2017 and Mar,2018 for getting the allotment letter and agreement but to no avail.The respondent always kept the complainants in dark about the approvals and development.It has failed to develop the project.It had not even applied the necessary permissions when the plot was sold to complainants.A list of dates of approvals (C5) and some important approval as (C6&amp;C7).Complaint for registration of FIR to vigilance 1.10.18 as C8</span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:\r\njustify;line-height:200%;mso-layout-grid-align:none;text-autospace:none\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Directing the respondent to refund the principle amount i.e.Rs. 1387500 along with interest as contemplated under rule 16 of The Punjab RERA Rules, 2017,as the complainants have lost faith in the respondent due to misrepresentation by it about the approvals &amp; stages of development during all these years ,did not issue any allotment letter &amp; execute the agreement till date, failed to develop the project &amp; thus the complainants wish to withdraw from the project.Also the respondent has committed violation of various provisions of PAPRA &amp; conditions of various approvals granted to it,as it could not collect any amount till the exemption is received under Section 44 of PAPRA which was granted on 25.1.17.The respondent collected the money from the complainants in 2011.The approvals were granted to the respondent on the ground that it will not sell any plot &amp; collect money from the general public till exemption under Section 44 of PAPRA is received.Also, inspite of receiving 30% of sale consideration the respondent did not execute any&nbsp; agreement &amp; issue a plot number till date &amp; asking the complainants to pay more money for getting the allotment letter &amp; execution of agreement in violation of Section 13 of RERA </span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">(ii)Directing the respondent to pay the compensation of Rs.10 lacs for deficiency in services, unfair trade practices &amp; harassment caused to the complainants &amp; for using their hard earned money for such a long period.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">(iii)Directing the respondent to pay litigation expenses to the tune of Rs.50000</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">(iv)To take action against respondent under Section 61 of RERA for constant violation of provision of Section 13 of RERA as the respondent failed to issue any allotment letter &amp; execute the buyer’s agreement till date, inspite of receiving 30% of sale consideration</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"> (v) For cancelling the extension granted to the respondent for constantly violating&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 14px; text-align: justify;\">various\r\nprovisions of RERA and for indulging into unfair trade practices.</span><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p></p>',4625000.00,1387500.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>A. The respondent be directed to provide the list of allottees to whom it has allotted/sold the 862 residential plots as per the layout plan approved by GMADA on 6.10.2015 and for which it is registered under RERA</p><p>B. The respondent be directed to provide the list of hypothecated plots which are hypothecated to GMADA, out of the approved 862 residential plots and 73 commercial plots.</p><p>C. The respondent be directed to provide the list of hypothected plots sold to general public.</p><p>d. The respondent be directed to provide the details of funds collected from the general public since 2010 in lieu of 862 residential plots which are part of approved layout and registered under Section 3 of RERA and also, the detail where such amount has been utilized by the respondent.</p><p>E. The respondent be directed to provide all the bank details where such amount has been deposited&nbsp; along with the statement of accounts since the year 2010.</p><p>F. The respondent be directed to provide the details of number of booking done by it since the year 2010 for the said 862 residential plots</p><p><br></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','NO ALLOTMENT AND AGREEMENT YET','','',1,1,0,0,'rerafilingformn','2018-10-26 23:02:47.000','rerafilingformn','2018-10-26 23:02:47.000'),(222,1096,'1096',1112,'29af80b1-85ed-4b88-8344-b429d2f24eca','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-10-27 23:26:00.000','Amandeep Sharma','savindersinghgill@gmail.com',9988861126,0,0,'2753, Sector-15, Near Jain Mandir','Kharar',28,507,'140301','1','2753, Sector-15, Near Jain Mandir','Kharar',28,507,'140301','Savinder Singh Gill','savindersinghgill@gmail.com',9988861126,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0093','PALM GARDEN','Manohar Infrastructure and Constructions Private Limited','nbs@manoharrealty.com',0,1725033524,'SCO 139-141','Sector- 17 C',6,128,'160017','1','SCO 139-141','Sector- 17 C',6,128,'160017','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:\r\njustify;line-height:normal;mso-layout-grid-align:none;text-autospace:none\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">The complainant on 29.10.2011 booked\r\n(C-1) a 250 sq yards plot @ RS.18000/- per sq yd (excluding EDC &amp; PLC) from\r\nthe respondent in the project Palm Garden, Mullanpur, Mohali. It was assured by\r\nthe respondent that it has received all the approvals except one or two which\r\nwill be obtained within 2-3 months and the possession of the plot will be\r\ndelivered in 2 years. The applicant paid Rs. 1350000 i.e. 30% of total sale\r\nconsideration along with the application. The present complaint is being filed\r\nthrough general power of attorney holder of the complainant, i.e. Sh. Shyam Lal\r\nSharma (C-2). The respondent issued an acknowledgement(C-3) for the 250 sq\r\nyards plot wherein it arbitrarily incorporated the condition of paying the IDC\r\nwhich was never agreed between the parties. The complainant made another\r\npayment of 900000 on 04.06.2014 (C-4). When resisted by the applicant, the\r\nrespondent threatened the applicant that his money will be forfeited if IDC\r\ncharges are not paid. Inspite of number of visits, repeated requests and\r\nassurances, the respondent execute the buyer’s agreement till date and were\r\nasking for more money in order to execute the same (C-5). A legal notice(C-6)\r\nwas also sent to it but to no avail. The respondent has misrepresented the\r\napplicant since beginning and never informed him about the true picture of the\r\napprovals and the development. It had not even applied the permissions when the\r\nplot was sold to the applicant. A list of approvals and main agreement are\r\nattached as C-7 and C-8.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;\r\nmargin-bottom:0in;margin-left:.75in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;mso-add-space:auto;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;line-height:normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;\r\nmso-layout-grid-align:none;text-autospace:none\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:Arial\">(i)<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Directing\r\nthe respondent to refund the principle amount i.e. Rs. 22,50,000/- as per\r\nSection 18 of RERA along with interest to be calculated at the rate as\r\ncontemplated under rule 16 of The Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation and\r\nDevelopment) Rules, 2017, as the applicant has lost faith in the respondent due\r\nto misrepresentation by it about the approvals and stages of development during\r\nall these years, did not issue any allotment letter and execute the buyer\'s\r\nagreement till date and thus the applicant wish to withdraw from the project.\r\nAlso the respondent has committed violation of various provisions of PAPRA and\r\nconditions of various approvals granted to it, as it could not collect any\r\namount till the exemption is received under Section 44 of PAPRA which was\r\nreceived on 25.01.2017. The respondent collected the money from the applicant\r\nin 2011. The approvals were granted to the respondent on the ground that it\r\nwill not sell any land/plot/space and collect money from the general public\r\ntill exemption under Section 44 of PAPRA is received. Also, inspite of\r\nreceiving 30% of sale consideration the respondent did not execute any sale\r\nagreement and pressurizing the applicant to pay more money or getting the\r\nallotment letter and execution of buyer\'s agreement.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;\r\nmargin-bottom:0in;margin-left:.75in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;mso-add-space:auto;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;line-height:normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;\r\nmso-layout-grid-align:none;text-autospace:none\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:Arial\">(ii)<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Directing\r\nthe respondent to pay the compensation of Rs. 10 lacs for deficiency in\r\nservices, unfair trade practices and harassment caused to the applicant and for\r\nusing the hard earned money of the applicant for such a long period. Inspite of\r\nrepeated requests visits by the applicant the respondent did not execute the buyer\'s\r\nagreement till date. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;\r\nmargin-bottom:0in;margin-left:.75in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;mso-add-space:auto;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;line-height:normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;\r\nmso-layout-grid-align:none;text-autospace:none\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:Arial\">(iii)<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Directing\r\nthe respondent to pay litigation expenses to the tune of Rs. 50000/-.<o:p></o:p></span></p>',4500000.00,2250000.00,'2013-10-29 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.75in; text-align: justify; text-indent: -0.5in; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Directing the respondent to refund the principle amount i.e. Rs. 22,50,000/- as per Section 18 of RERA along with interest to be calculated at the rate as contemplated under rule 16 of The Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Rules, 2017, as the applicant has lost faith in the respondent due to misrepresentation by it about the approvals and stages of development during all these years, did not issue any allotment letter and execute the buyer\'s agreement till date and thus the applicant wish to withdraw from the project. Also the respondent has committed violation of various provisions of PAPRA and conditions of various approvals granted to it, as it could not collect any amount till the exemption is received under Section 44 of PAPRA which was received on 25.01.2017. The respondent collected the money from the applicant in 2011. The approvals were granted to the respondent on the ground that it will not sell any land/plot/space and collect money from the general public till exemption under Section 44 of PAPRA is received. Also, inspite of receiving 30% of sale consideration the respondent did not execute any sale agreement and pressurizing the applicant to pay more money or getting the allotment letter and execution of buyer\'s agreement.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.75in; text-align: justify; text-indent: -0.5in; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">(ii)<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Directing the respondent to pay the compensation of Rs. 10 lacs for deficiency in services, unfair trade practices and harassment caused to the applicant and for using the hard earned money of the applicant for such a long period. Inspite of repeated requests visits by the applicant the respondent did not execute the buyer\'s agreement till date.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.75in; text-align: justify; text-indent: -0.5in; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">(iii)<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Directing the respondent to pay litigation expenses to the tune of Rs. 50000/-.</span></p>','1','','2011-10-29 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','1146','','',1,1,0,0,'BeeG','2018-10-27 22:45:00.000','BeeG','2018-10-27 22:45:00.000'),(223,1097,'1097',1178,'02e82b67-7f34-47ae-80b9-cc89681213d6','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Kanavdeep Singh','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9896165550,0,0,'H NO 1497 Sector 9 ','',13,10,'132001','1','H NO 1497 Sector 9 ','',13,10,'132001','Kamal Dahiya','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9729902009,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0085','Sushma Chandigarh Grande\r\n','Sushma Buildtech Ltd','customercare@sushmabuildtech.com',9872889933,0,'Unit No B 107 - Business Complex - Elante Mall, 1st Floor ','Industrial Area, Phase I',6,128,'160002','1','Unit No B 107 - Business Complex - Elante Mall, 1st Floor ','Industrial Area, Phase I',6,128,'160002','1','<p>as per attached</p>','<p>as per attached<br></p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>as per attached<br></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'JurisAxisRera','2018-10-28 15:21:42.000','JurisAxisRera','2018-10-28 15:21:42.000'),(224,1097,'1097',1178,'02e82b67-7f34-47ae-80b9-cc89681213d6','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Kanavdeep Singh','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9896165550,0,0,'H NO 1497 Sector 9 ','',13,10,'132001','1','H NO 1497 Sector 9 ','',13,10,'132001','Kamal Dahiya','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9729902009,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0085','Sushma Chandigarh Grande\r\n','Sushma Buildtech Ltd','customercare@sushmabuildtech.com',9872889933,0,'Unit No B 107 - Business Complex - Elante Mall, 1st Floor ','Industrial Area, Phase I',6,128,'160002','1','Unit No B 107 - Business Complex - Elante Mall, 1st Floor ','Industrial Area, Phase I',6,128,'160002','1','<div>SUSHMA CHANDIGARH GRANDE is a Residential Group Housing Project - the Project - being developed by the Respondent, situated in the revenue estate of Village Bishangarh and Bishanpura, MC Zirakpur, Distt SAS Nagar - Mohali, hereinafter referred to as the Land, wherein the complainant had booked a flat in Tower No ie H002, Ground Floor, herein after referred as Flat in the said project.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>Initially the flat was booked by the complainant and an amount of&nbsp; Rs 12,39,038 was paid by the complainant as a booking amount.</div><div><br></div><div>The respondent had allotted a Flat bearing no H002 on Ground floor&nbsp; in Tower No having an area of 2085 sq ft vide allotment letter dated 4th September 2012 to the complainant.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>Buyers Agreement was executed between the parties on dated 04-09-2012 for the said flat. As per ABA, the respondent was supposed to deliver the possession of the apartment within 50 months from the date of allotment of the apartment. So the stipulated period of 50 months ends on December 2016.</div><div><br></div><div>The possession of the said apartment was committed in the month of December 2016 but the respondent did not give any possession to the complainant and the agent of respondent namely Anuj asked the complainant to replace his flat ie H002 Ground Floor to 702, Tower-H as it would be delivered in April 2017 and the flat on ground floor will take much more time.</div><div><br></div><div>The complainant was allotted with Flat No 702 Tower-H and the new ABA was executed between the respondent and the complainant for the said flat. It was executed on 21st February 2017 and as per the terms of the agreement the possession is to be delivered in April 2017.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>Thus, the respondent has delayed the possession of Apartment deliberately or for reasons known best to them.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>The complainant has paid Rs 81,37,349 ie nearly 100 percent of&nbsp; payment out of total consideration, but the respondents failed to deliver the possession of the flat till date.</div>','<p>as per attached<br></p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>as per attached<br></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'JurisAxisRera','2018-10-28 15:25:34.000','JurisAxisRera','2018-10-28 15:25:34.000'),(225,1097,'1097',1178,'02e82b67-7f34-47ae-80b9-cc89681213d6','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Kanavdeep Singh','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9896165550,0,0,'H NO 1497 Sector 9 ','',13,10,'132001','1','H NO 1497 Sector 9 ','',13,10,'132001','Kamal Dahiya','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9729902009,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0085','Sushma Chandigarh Grande\r\n','Sushma Buildtech Ltd','customercare@sushmabuildtech.com',9872889933,0,'Unit No B 107 - Business Complex - Elante Mall, 1st Floor ','Industrial Area, Phase I',6,128,'160002','1','Unit No B 107 - Business Complex - Elante Mall, 1st Floor ','Industrial Area, Phase I',6,128,'160002','1','<div>SUSHMA CHANDIGARH GRANDE is a Residential Group Housing Project - the Project - being developed by the Respondent, situated in the revenue estate of Village Bishangarh and Bishanpura, MC Zirakpur, Distt SAS Nagar - Mohali, hereinafter referred to as the Land, wherein the complainant had booked a flat in Tower No ie H002, Ground Floor, herein after referred as Flat in the said project.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>Initially the flat was booked by the complainant and an amount of&nbsp; Rs 12,39,038 was paid by the complainant as a booking amount.</div><div><br></div><div>The respondent had allotted a Flat bearing no H002 on Ground floor&nbsp; in Tower No having an area of 2085 sq ft vide allotment letter dated 4th September 2012 to the complainant.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>Buyers Agreement was executed between the parties on dated 04-09-2012 for the said flat. As per ABA, the respondent was supposed to deliver the possession of the apartment within 50 months from the date of allotment of the apartment. So the stipulated period of 50 months ends on December 2016.</div><div><br></div><div>The possession of the said apartment was committed in the month of December 2016 but the respondent did not give any possession to the complainant and the agent of respondent namely Anuj asked the complainant to replace his flat ie H002 Ground Floor to 702, Tower-H as it would be delivered in April 2017 and the flat on ground floor will take much more time.</div><div><br></div><div>The complainant was allotted with Flat No 702 Tower-H and the new ABA was executed between the respondent and the complainant for the said flat. It was executed on 21st February 2017 and as per the terms of the agreement the possession is to be delivered in April 2017.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>Thus, the respondent has delayed the possession of Apartment deliberately or for reasons known best to them.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>The complainant has paid Rs 81,37,349 ie nearly 100 percent of&nbsp; payment out of total consideration, but the respondents failed to deliver the possession of the flat till date.</div>','<div>i To give necessary directions to the respondents for return of the payment made in lieu of unit-apartment till date along with the prescribed rate of interest from the date of execution of&nbsp; Allotment Letter till realization as per the provisions of Section 18 and 19-4 of the RERA Act.</div><div><br></div><div>ii To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 60 of RERA Act for willful default committed by them.</div><div><br></div><div>iii To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 61 of RERA Act for contravention of Sec.12, Sec.14, Sec. 15 and Sec. 16 of RERA Act.</div><div><br></div><div>iv To direct the respondents to pay penalty upto 10 percent of project cost to the complainant under Sec. 59 of RERA, Act, 2016.</div><div><br></div><div>v To direct the respondents to refund the amount collected from the complainant in lieu of interest, penalty for delayed payments under Rule 23-3-c of Punjab RERA Rules,2017.</div><div><br></div><div>vi To issue directions to make liable every officer concerned i.e. Director, Manager, Secretary, or any other officer of the respondent company at whose instance, connivance, acquiescence, neglect any of the offences has been committed as mentioned in Sec.69 of RERA Act,2016 to be read with Punjab RERA Rules,2017.</div><div><br></div><div>vii To direct respondent to deliver the flat to the complainant without charging the additional charges for the increased area of the flat.</div><div><br></div><div>viii To recommend criminal action against the respondents for the criminal offence of cheating, fraud and criminal breach of trust under section 420,406 and 409 of the Indian Penal Code.</div><div><br></div><div>ix To issue direction to pay the cost of litigation.</div><div><br></div><div>x Any other relief which this Hon-ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances of this complaint.</div>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>NA<br></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'JurisAxisRera','2018-10-28 15:30:24.000','JurisAxisRera','2018-10-28 15:30:24.000'),(226,1097,'1097',1178,'02e82b67-7f34-47ae-80b9-cc89681213d6','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Kanavdeep Singh','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9896165550,0,0,'H NO 1497 Sector 9 ','',13,10,'132001','1','H NO 1497 Sector 9 ','',13,10,'132001','Kamal Dahiya','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',97