flat. It was executed on 21st February 2017 and as per the terms of the agreement the possession is to be delivered in April 2017.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>Thus, the respondent has delayed the possession of Apartment deliberately or for reasons known best to them.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>The complainant has paid Rs 81,37,349 ie nearly 100 percent of&nbsp; payment out of total consideration, but the respondents failed to deliver the possession of the flat till date.</div>','<div>i To give necessary directions to the respondents for return of the payment made in lieu of unit-apartment till date along with the prescribed rate of interest from the date of execution of&nbsp; Allotment Letter till realization as per the provisions of Section 18 and 19-4 of the RERA Act.</div><div><br></div><div>ii To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 60 of RERA Act for willful default committed by them.</div><div><br></div><div>iii To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 61 of RERA Act for contravention of Sec.12, Sec.14, Sec. 15 and Sec. 16 of RERA Act.</div><div><br></div><div>iv To direct the respondents to pay penalty upto 10 percent of project cost to the complainant under Sec. 59 of RERA, Act, 2016.</div><div><br></div><div>v To direct the respondents to refund the amount collected from the complainant in lieu of interest, penalty for delayed payments under Rule 23-3-c of Punjab RERA Rules,2017.</div><div><br></div><div>vi To issue directions to make liable every officer concerned i.e. Director, Manager, Secretary, or any other officer of the respondent company at whose instance, connivance, acquiescence, neglect any of the offences has been committed as mentioned in Sec.69 of RERA Act,2016 to be read with Punjab RERA Rules,2017.</div><div><br></div><div>vii To direct respondent to deliver the flat to the complainant without charging the additional charges for the increased area of the flat.</div><div><br></div><div>viii To recommend criminal action against the respondents for the criminal offence of cheating, fraud and criminal breach of trust under section 420,406 and 409 of the Indian Penal Code.</div><div><br></div><div>ix To issue direction to pay the cost of litigation.</div><div><br></div><div>x Any other relief which this Hon-ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances of this complaint.</div>',8260250.00,8137349.00,'2018-10-21 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>NA<br></p>','1','','2012-09-04 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Flat No 702 Tower H','','',2,0,0,0,'JurisAxisRera','2018-10-28 15:38:45.000','JurisAxisRera','2018-10-28 15:38:45.000');
INSERT INTO `verified_table_tbl_rera_complaint_formm_details` VALUES (227,1097,'1097',1178,'02e82b67-7f34-47ae-80b9-cc89681213d6','FormTypeM',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Kanavdeep Singh','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9896165550,0,0,'H NO 1497 Sector 9 ','',13,10,'132001','1','H NO 1497 Sector 9 ','',13,10,'132001','Kamal Dahiya','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9729902009,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0085','Sushma Chandigarh Grande\r\n','Sushma Buildtech Ltd','customercare@sushmabuildtech.com',9872889933,0,'Unit No B 107 - Business Complex - Elante Mall, 1st Floor ','Industrial Area, Phase I',6,128,'160009','1','Unit No B 107 - Business Complex - Elante Mall, 1st Floor ','Industrial Area, Phase I',6,128,'160009','1','<div>SUSHMA CHANDIGARH GRANDE is a Residential Group Housing Project - the Project - being developed by the Respondent, situated in the revenue estate of Village Bishangarh and Bishanpura, MC Zirakpur, Distt SAS Nagar - Mohali, hereinafter referred to as the Land, wherein the complainant had booked a flat in Tower No ie H002, Ground Floor, herein after referred as Flat in the said project.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>Initially the flat was booked by the complainant and an amount of&nbsp; Rs 12,39,038 was paid by the complainant as a booking amount.</div><div><br></div><div>The respondent had allotted a Flat bearing no H002 on Ground floor&nbsp; in Tower No having an area of 2085 sq ft vide allotment letter dated 4th September 2012 to the complainant.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>Buyers Agreement was executed between the parties on dated 04-09-2012 for the said flat. As per ABA, the respondent was supposed to deliver the possession of the apartment within 50 months from the date of allotment of the apartment. So the stipulated period of 50 months ends on December 2016.</div><div><br></div><div>The possession of the said apartment was committed in the month of December 2016 but the respondent did not give any possession to the complainant and the agent of respondent namely Anuj asked the complainant to replace his flat ie H002 Ground Floor to 702, Tower-H as it would be delivered in April 2017 and the flat on ground floor will take much more time.</div><div><br></div><div>The complainant was allotted with Flat No 702 Tower-H and the new ABA was executed between the respondent and the complainant for the said flat. It was executed on 21st February 2017 and as per the terms of the agreement the possession is to be delivered in April 2017.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>Thus, the respondent has delayed the possession of Apartment deliberately or for reasons known best to them.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>The complainant has paid Rs 81,37,349 ie nearly 100 percent of&nbsp; payment out of total consideration, but the respondents failed to deliver the possession of the flat till date.</div>','<div>i To give necessary directions to the respondents for return of the payment made in lieu of unit-apartment till date along with the prescribed rate of interest from the date of execution of&nbsp; Allotment Letter till realization as per the provisions of Section 18 and 19-4 of the RERA Act.</div><div><br></div><div>ii To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 60 of RERA Act for willful default committed by them.</div><div><br></div><div>iii To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 61 of RERA Act for contravention of Sec.12, Sec.14, Sec. 15 and Sec. 16 of RERA Act.</div><div><br></div><div>iv To direct the respondents to pay penalty upto 10 percent of project cost to the complainant under Sec. 59 of RERA, Act, 2016.</div><div><br></div><div>v To direct the respondents to refund the amount collected from the complainant in lieu of interest, penalty for delayed payments under Rule 23-3-c of Punjab RERA Rules,2017.</div><div><br></div><div>vi To issue directions to make liable every officer concerned i.e. Director, Manager, Secretary, or any other officer of the respondent company at whose instance, connivance, acquiescence, neglect any of the offences has been committed as mentioned in Sec.69 of RERA Act,2016 to be read with Punjab RERA Rules,2017.</div><div><br></div><div>vii To direct respondent to deliver the flat to the complainant without charging the additional charges for the increased area of the flat.</div><div><br></div><div>viii To recommend criminal action against the respondents for the criminal offence of cheating, fraud and criminal breach of trust under section 420,406 and 409 of the Indian Penal Code.</div><div><br></div><div>ix To issue direction to pay the cost of litigation.</div><div><br></div><div>x Any other relief which this Hon-ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances of this complaint.</div>',8260250.00,8137349.00,'2018-10-21 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>NA<br></p>','1','','2012-09-04 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Flat No 702 Tower H','','',2,0,0,0,'JurisAxisRera','2018-10-28 15:59:25.000','JurisAxisRera','2018-10-28 15:59:25.000'),(228,1097,'1097',1178,'02e82b67-7f34-47ae-80b9-cc89681213d6','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-10-29 12:56:00.000','Kanavdeep Singh','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9896165550,0,0,'H NO 1497 Sector 9 ','',13,10,'132001','1','H NO 1497 Sector 9 ','',13,10,'132001','Kamal Dahiya','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9729902009,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0085','Sushma Chandigarh Grande\r\n','Sushma Buildtech Ltd','customercare@sushmabuildtech.com',9872889933,0,'Unit No B 107 - Business Complex - Elante Mall, 1st Floor ','Industrial Area, Phase I',6,128,'160009','1','Unit No B 107 - Business Complex - Elante Mall, 1st Floor ','Industrial Area, Phase I',6,128,'160009','1','<div>SUSHMA CHANDIGARH GRANDE is a Residential Group Housing Project - the Project - being developed by the Respondent, situated in the revenue estate of Village Bishangarh and Bishanpura, MC Zirakpur, Distt SAS Nagar - Mohali, hereinafter referred to as the Land, wherein the complainant had booked a flat in Tower No ie H002, Ground Floor, herein after referred as Flat in the said project.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>Initially the flat was booked by the complainant and an amount of&nbsp; Rs 12,39,038 was paid by the complainant as a booking amount.</div><div><br></div><div>The respondent had allotted a Flat bearing no H002 on Ground floor&nbsp; in Tower No having an area of 2085 sq ft vide allotment letter dated 4th September 2012 to the complainant.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>Buyers Agreement was executed between the parties on dated 04-09-2012 for the said flat. As per ABA, the respondent was supposed to deliver the possession of the apartment within 50 months from the date of allotment of the apartment. So the stipulated period of 50 months ends on December 2016.</div><div><br></div><div>The possession of the said apartment was committed in the month of December 2016 but the respondent did not give any possession to the complainant and the agent of respondent namely Anuj asked the complainant to replace his flat ie H002 Ground Floor to 702, Tower-H as it would be delivered in April 2017 and the flat on ground floor will take much more time.</div><div><br></div><div>The complainant was allotted with Flat No 702 Tower-H and the new ABA was executed between the respondent and the complainant for the said flat. It was executed on 21st February 2017 and as per the terms of the agreement the possession is to be delivered in April 2017.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>Thus, the respondent has delayed the possession of Apartment deliberately or for reasons known best to them.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>The complainant has paid Rs 81,37,349 ie nearly 100 percent of&nbsp; payment out of total consideration, but the respondents failed to deliver the possession of the flat till date.</div>','<div>i To give necessary directions to the respondents for return of the payment made in lieu of unit-apartment till date along with the prescribed rate of interest from the date of execution of&nbsp; Allotment Letter till realization as per the provisions of Section 18 and 19-4 of the RERA Act.</div><div><br></div><div>ii To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 60 of RERA Act for willful default committed by them.</div><div><br></div><div>iii To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 61 of RERA Act for contravention of Sec.12, Sec.14, Sec. 15 and Sec. 16 of RERA Act.</div><div><br></div><div>iv To direct the respondents to pay penalty upto 10 percent of project cost to the complainant under Sec. 59 of RERA, Act, 2016.</div><div><br></div><div>v To direct the respondents to refund the amount collected from the complainant in lieu of interest, penalty for delayed payments under Rule 23-3-c of Punjab RERA Rules,2017.</div><div><br></div><div>vi To issue directions to make liable every officer concerned i.e. Director, Manager, Secretary, or any other officer of the respondent company at whose instance, connivance, acquiescence, neglect any of the offences has been committed as mentioned in Sec.69 of RERA Act,2016 to be read with Punjab RERA Rules,2017.</div><div><br></div><div>vii To direct respondent to deliver the flat to the complainant without charging the additional charges for the increased area of the flat.</div><div><br></div><div>viii To recommend criminal action against the respondents for the criminal offence of cheating, fraud and criminal breach of trust under section 420,406 and 409 of the Indian Penal Code.</div><div><br></div><div>ix To issue direction to pay the cost of litigation.</div><div><br></div><div>x Any other relief which this Hon-ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances of this complaint.</div>',8260250.00,8137349.00,'2018-10-21 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>As per attached complaint</p>','1','','2012-09-04 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Flat No 702 Tower H','','',2,0,0,0,'JurisAxisRera','2018-10-28 16:34:35.000','JurisAxisRera','2018-10-28 16:34:35.000'),(229,1083,'1083',1135,'7ce4ff29-c893-46aa-aac9-b9c5d5926814','FormTypeM',1,1,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','naresh  kumar','akhilesh@vyaslawassociates.com',7087973992,0,0,'29-C, Kashmir avenue, Amritsar','',28,39,'143001','1','29-C, Kashmir avenue, Amritsar','',28,39,'143001','akhilesh vyas','akhilesh@vyaslawassociates.com',9855004557,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-ASR02-PR0169','Sh. Guru Ram \r\nDass, Urban \r\nEstate','Punjab Urban Planning Development Authority','ca@puda.gov.in',0,0,'PUDA Bhawan','green avenue',28,39,'143001','1','PUDA Bhawan','green avenue',28,39,'143001','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-justify:\r\ninter-ideograph;text-indent:-.5in;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size:13.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:11.0pt;\r\nline-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-theme-font:minor-fareast;mso-bidi-font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;mso-ansi-language:EN-US;\r\nmso-fareast-language:EN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\">That the applicant was\r\nallotted residential plot by Punjab Urban Planning and Development Authority\r\n(hereinafter called as “PUDA”) bearing residential plot No. 344 measuring 300\r\nSq. Yards at Guru Ram Dass Urban Estate Airport Road, Amritsar. The total price\r\nof the residential plot of Rs. 54.00 lacs only @ Rs. 18000/- per Sq. Yard. As\r\nper the payment schedule given in the allotment letter 25% of the allotment\r\namount was to be paid initially and rest of the payment was to be paid after\r\nthe possession. The brochure of the scheme clearly reflects that possession on\r\n25% payment as per the allotment letter it admitted by the respondent that\r\npayment of Rs. 13,50,000/- lacs was made by the applicant and it has already\r\nbeen adjusted towards initial 25% of the sale price of residential plot as\r\nmentioned in clause No. 3.1.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif; font-size: 13pt; line-height: 16.75pt;\">For the balance payment of 75%, the complainant is always ready\r\nand willing to pay the amount as per schedule.&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-justify:\r\ninter-ideograph;text-indent:-.5in;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif; font-size: 13pt; line-height: 16.75pt;\"><br></span><span style=\"font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif; font-size: 13pt; line-height: 16.75pt;\">That no possession has been handed over up till now. there is no\r\ndevelopment at the site at all. Various letters has been forwarded to the\r\nEstate Officer PUDA Amritsar and RTI applications have been filed to their\r\nofficers but nothing has resulted fruitful. The possession was scheduled to be\r\ngiven within 90 days after making payment of 25% but nothing has been done in\r\nthis regard. The complainant has approached earlier Hon\'ble Punjab and Haryana\r\nHigh court vide which their representation was decided and she withdrew the\r\nearlier petition for seeking relief under this act.</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-justify:\r\ninter-ideograph;text-indent:-.5in;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size:\r\n13.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:11.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-justify:\r\ninter-ideograph;text-indent:-.5in;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size:\r\n13.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:11.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p>i) &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; That as the department has not adhered to their discipline of delivering the actual possession of the property as per the contract, therefore, the applicant shall not be liable to pay any interest and penal interest on the future payments to be made to the respondents and further payment of Principal amount shall be deferred till the respondents hands over the actual physical possession.</p><p>ii) &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; That the applicant is not liable to pay any amount by way of penal interest if any charged by the respondent department. They are liable to get the refund of any penal interest charged up till now as the delay any occurred is because of the conduct and acts of the respondent department. &nbsp;The interest already paid shall be refunded &nbsp;or interest amount which is already &nbsp;been charged by the respondents shall stands adjusted in the future payments as the delay has occurred due to lapse on the part of the respondents.</p><p>iii) &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;That the applicant is liable to be sufficient compensation as per the statue as they have been denied their physical possession up till now without any explanatory reason by the department. They have not been handed over the possession of their allotted plots rather the applicant has made the payment as per the schedule to the respondent department. &nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>iv) &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;That as stated above the extension was sought by the &nbsp;complainant for 180 days and during that period interest was charged by the respondents. The respondents shall be directed to refund that interest amount or adjust that amount in the principal amount in future payments. &nbsp;</p><p><br></p>',5400000.00,1350000.00,'2017-03-02 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>i) &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; That as the department has not adhered to their discipline of delivering the actual possession of the property as per the contract, therefore, the applicant shall not be liable to pay any interest and penal interest on the future payments to be made to the respondents and further payment of Principal amount shall be deferred till the respondents hands over the actual physical possession.</p><p>ii) &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; That the applicant is not liable to pay any amount by way of penal interest if any charged by the respondent department. They are liable to get the refund of any penal interest charged up till now as the delay any occurred is because of the conduct and acts of the respondent department. &nbsp;The interest already paid shall be refunded &nbsp;or interest amount which is already &nbsp;been charged by the respondents shall stands adjusted in the future payments as the delay has occurred due to lapse on the part of the respondents.</p><p>iii) &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;That the applicant is liable to be sufficient compensation as per the statue as they have been denied their physical possession up till now without any explanatory reason by the department. They have not been handed over the possession of their allotted plots rather the applicant has made the payment as per the schedule to the respondent department. &nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>iv) &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;That as stated above the extension was sought by the &nbsp;complainant for 180 days and during that period interest was charged by the respondents. The respondents shall be directed to refund that interest amount or adjust that amount in the principal amount in future payments. &nbsp;</p><div><br></div>','1','','2016-12-02 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','344, Guru Ram Dass Urban Estate, Airport Road, Amritsar    ','','',2,0,0,0,'akhilesh','2018-10-28 16:58:53.000','akhilesh','2018-10-28 16:58:53.000'),(230,1098,'1098',1141,'971b1ae7-f8bc-4323-80a7-088b81f8b7db','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Neetu Sharma','kapilsharma145@yahoo.com',9501142800,0,0,'House No. 694','Sector-69',28,507,'160069','1','Sector 4, Mansa Devi Complex','Sector 4, Mansa Devi Complex',13,15,'134114','Sanjeev Gupta','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0093','PALM SPRINGS','M/s Manohar Infrastructure & Constructions Pvt Ltd','nbs@manoharrealty.com',0,1725033524,'SCO 139-142','Sector-17C',6,128,'160017','1','SCO 139-142','Sector-17C',6,128,'160017','1','<p>abc</p>','<p>abc</p>',4500000.00,1350000.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>abc</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','No allotment and Agreement Yet','','',1,0,0,0,'rerafilingformm','2018-10-28 18:13:36.000','rerafilingformm','2018-10-28 18:13:36.000'),(231,1082,'1082',1132,'1cc1b298-c384-4c23-8f77-3e560c57343c','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-10-29 12:15:15.000','Col Shiv Kumar Anand','sk.anand1581@gmail.com',9815001098,0,0,'1581, Sector 34-D','',6,128,'160022','1','1581, Sector 34-D','',6,128,'160022','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PM0089','Aeropolis City\r\n(formerly known as Yellowstone\r\nLandmark Infocity)','Aeropolis Infrastructure Pvt. Ltd.','tejindersbhatia@gmail.com',9592969696,0,'Aeropolis Infrastructure Pvt. Ltd.','Aeropolis City, Sector 66-A',28,507,'160062','1','Aeropolis Infrastructure Pvt. Ltd.','Aeropolis City, Sector 66-A',28,507,'160062','1','<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0.0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 150%; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%\">Applied for an IT plot of 400 sq yds in 2011. The same have not been handed over, till date\r\n&amp; there is no development of the area. The company has changed its name,\r\nkept its customers ignorant. This could only be found out on visit to your\r\noffice. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0.0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 150%; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%\">Since last eight years payments have\r\nbeen made, as per the development plan, as indicated by Yellowstone. Actually,\r\non the ground there is zero development. The Yellowstone has been cheating the\r\ncustomers &amp; utilizing the funds in other projects. Since the company had\r\nlaid down the conditions for timely payments, imposing interest of 18% for late\r\npayments, had no choice. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0.0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 150%; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%\">I am 75 year old &amp; have requested\r\nthe company many a times, but to no avail. In case of the plot, I have paid Rs 22.94 lakhs, over the period.&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0.0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 150%; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%\">It is eight years since, started\r\npaying for the plot. Considering the normal time of three years of completion\r\nof the project, the company has already taken five years over &amp; above the\r\nbasic necessary period.&nbsp;&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0.0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 150%; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%\">RERA is requested, to order the\r\ncompany to hand over the plot at the earliest. RERA is further requested to\r\norder the AEROPOLIS to pay interest @18% pa for retaining the money for so\r\nlong. In case they can’t hand over the plots, then they should hand your 400 sq\r\nyds of free hold land in Sector 66-A, SAS Nagar and pay interest at 18% from\r\n2011 to the date of settlement. In case the company is handing over the plots, then\r\nin that case they should give 18% rate of interest for the period over &amp;\r\nabove the basic period of 3 years required for the completion of the project,\r\nfor keeping the money for so long.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0.0001pt; line-height: 150%; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><span style=\"font-size:\r\n14.0pt;line-height:150%\">In case the company is not able to hand over the\r\nplot, then it should give, 400 sq yds of land with free title in Sector 66A,\r\nSAS Nagar, along with interest of 18% from Aug 2011 to date, for keeping the\r\nmoney, for the period from the date of allotment to the date of settlement\r\n.<o:p></o:p></span></p>',2960000.00,2294000.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0.0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 150%; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%\">Before completion of your order &amp;\r\nhanding over plot, you are requested to order the company to hand over the\r\ninterest at 18% pa, the rate the company was charging from its customers, for\r\nthe period that they have retained the money &amp; used it for other purposes\r\nfor their benefit.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0.0001pt; line-height: 150%; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><span style=\"font-size:\r\n14.0pt;line-height:150%\">Company should also be penalized for cheating &amp;\r\nharassing their customers &amp; retaining &amp; using the money for other\r\nprojects.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','1','','2011-06-07 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Plot number not given as yet','','',1,1,0,0,'sk.anand1581@gmail.com','2018-10-29 12:07:22.000','sk.anand1581@gmail.com','2018-10-29 12:07:22.000'),(232,1092,'1092',1156,'fe9d0b35-d692-47a7-ad8a-e66a989164d1','FormTypeM',1,1,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Jai Bhushan Chandan','jb.chandan@yahoo.com',8360074813,0,703317526144,'23-B','Moti nagar',28,366,'141010','1','23-B','Moti nagar',28,366,'141010','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0086','Casa Espana','ATS Infrabuild Pvt. Ltd','email@atsgreens.com',0,0,' ATS Infrabuild Pvt. Ltd.',' 711/92, Deepali, Nehru Place',10,429,'110019','1',' ATS Infrabuild Pvt. Ltd.',' 711/92, Deepali, Nehru Place',10,429,'110019','1','<p>1) Agreement dated 04.01.18 provided for possession&nbsp; by 31.03.18 but till date possession not handed over.</p><p>2) All the payments ( Rs. 92.40 Lacs) except the amount payable on possession&nbsp;timely made &amp; acknowledged.&nbsp;</p><p>3) Project registered at Mohali under RERA vide No. PBRERA-SAS80-PR0086. </p><p>4) Clause 9.2 (ii) of the Agreement&nbsp; provides that \".... he (Allottee) shall be paid, by the promoter, interest at the rate specified in the rules, for every month of delay till the 