 ensures to hand over possession of&nbsp; the apartment by 31.03.18&nbsp; ( page 10)</p><p>6) Clause 9.2 (ii) of the Agreement&nbsp; provides that \".... he (Allottee) shall be paid, by the promoter, interest at the rate specified in the rules, for every month of delay till the offer of possession of the Apartment.&nbsp;</p><p>7) Interest payable specified in the rules learned SBI MCLR + 2 %&nbsp;</p><p><br></p>','<p>&nbsp;1) Clause 9.2 (ii) of the Agreement&nbsp; provides that \".... he (Allottee) shall be paid, by the promoter, interest at the rate specified in the rules, for every month of delay till the offer of possession of the Apartment.&nbsp;</p><p>2) Interest&nbsp; at the rate specified in the rules, for every month of delay till the offer of possession of the Apartment.<br></p><p>3) Interest payable specified in the rules learned SBI MCLR + 2 %&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><div><p><br></p></div>',9697570.00,9249570.00,'2018-03-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>&nbsp;1) Clause 9.2 (ii) of the Agreement&nbsp; provides that \".... he (Allottee) shall be paid, by the promoter, interest at the rate specified in the rules, for every month of delay till the offer of possession of the Apartment.&nbsp;</p><p>2) Interest&nbsp; at the rate specified in the rules, for every month of delay till the offer of possession of the Apartment.<br></p><p>3) Interest payable specified in the rules learned SBI MCLR + 2 %&nbsp;</p><p><br></p>','1','','2018-01-04 00:00:00','2018-01-04 00:00:00','Flat No. 10171, Tower 10','','',1,1,0,0,'JBchandan','2018-10-29 14:23:34.000','JBchandan','2018-10-29 14:23:34.000'),(235,1099,'1099',1174,'1fd7a7f3-6621-4fc2-bf77-23a5487e5d18','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Rahul Khandelwal','rahul.khandelwal@jujuscafes.com',9988999852,0,0,'House No 250, FF, Sector 15A','',6,128,'160015','1','House No 250, FF, Sector 15A','',6,128,'160015','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0007','ATS Golf Meadows Lifestyle\r\nCompany - ATS Estates Pvt Ltd','Site Manager, ATS Golf Meadows Lifestyle','lifestylesales@atsgreens.com',8288033311,0,'ATS Golf Meadows Lifestyle, Village Madhopur, Tehsil Derabassi','',28,507,'140507','1','ATS Golf Meadows Lifestyle, Village Madhopur, Tehsil Derabassi','',28,507,'140507','1','<p>abc&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>','<p>abc</p>',9777388.00,8466852.00,'2016-09-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>abc</p>','1','','2013-02-16 00:00:00','2013-03-11 00:00:00','Flat No 05104, 10th Floor, Tower 5','','',2,0,0,0,'Rahul28','2018-10-30 10:25:15.000','Rahul28','2018-10-30 10:25:15.000'),(236,1099,'1099',1174,'1fd7a7f3-6621-4fc2-bf77-23a5487e5d18','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Rahul Khandelwal','rahul.khandelwal@jujuscafes.com',9988999852,0,0,'House No 250, FF, Sector 15A','',6,128,'160015','1','House No 250, FF, Sector 15A','',6,128,'160015','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0007','ATS Golf Meadows Lifestyle\r\nCompany - ATS Estates Pvt Ltd','Site Manager, ATS Golf Meadows Lifestyle','lifestylesales@atsgreens.com',8288033311,0,'ATS Golf Meadows Lifestyle, Village Madhopur, Tehsil Derabassi','',28,507,'140507','1','ATS Golf Meadows Lifestyle, Village Madhopur, Tehsil Derabassi','',28,507,'140507','1','<p>The complainant with an intention to have a residential flat for his own residential purpose decided to purchase a 4 BHK Flat measuring approximately 2950 square feet at a Basic Sale Price of 9271250/-. The total price of the flat including power backup charges of 1, 00,000/- and maintenance deposit of 50,000/- was 9777388/ (Inclusive of all taxes). Accordingly the complainant made a payment of Rs 8466852, out of which Rs 1513115 was paid from own funds and Rs 6953737 was paid by HDFC Bank under a subvention loan of Rs 7417000. The remaining amount of Rs 1148176 is to be paid at the time of possession.&nbsp; Details of all payments made till date with Cheque numbers and dates are provided in Annexure 1. As per clause 14 of the buyer agreement (Annexure 2), the committed date of handing over the possession was 36 months with a period of six months grace from the start of actual construction of the tower. The flat was allotted on 16/02/2013 and therefore the due date for possession after 36 month and 6 months grace period was 1st September 2016. However, over two years have passed now and the possession is not offered by the builder. I have written multiple letters to Site Manager and Director of ATS estates (Annexure 3) but there is no official reply. After pursuing the builder endlessly on email, I got a reply from ATS relationship officer on 03 July 2017, wherein the possession date was told as April 2018. Again on 16th February’2018, the possession date was confirmed as September 2018 and finally on 3rd July 2018, possession date shared is Q1’2019. All these mails exchange are shared in Annexure 4. The complainant was provided with Prospectus(Annexure 5) for the said flat indicating features, specifications, facilities, amenities and layout of 4BHK Flat. However, no update is shared on the status of these facilities inspite of multiple reminders.</p>','<ul><li>To refund the total amount paid of Rs 84,66,852/- along with interest at the rate of 12.4% per annum from the different dates of deposit of different amounts till the date of actual payment.</li><li>To reimburse the total amount of rent of the current accommodation of the complainant from 1.03.2016 till date. The complainant is forced to take up a rented accommodation due to delay in possession of the flat.</li><li>To provide a sum of Rs 5,00,000 as compensation for the harassment and mental agony suffered by the complainant.</li></ul><p>As per Real Estate(Regulation and Development) Act, 2016 clause 19(4), the complainant is entitled for refund along with prescribed interest in case of promoter not fulfilling his obligations as per the agreement.</p>',9777388.00,8466852.00,'2016-09-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>To reimburse the total amount of rent of the current accommodation of the complainant from 1.03.2016 till the continuation of the case.&nbsp;</p><p>The complainant is forced to take up a rented accommodation in Chandigarh, due to delay in possession of the flat booked in ATS. The current rent of the accommodation is Rs 38100 per month which is over and above the EMI per month for ATS Flat of Rs 59850. This is leading to double financial burden and loss to the complainant. The rent of the current accommodation is paid through neft every month and the copy of the rent agreement is attached as Annexure 6.</p>','1','','2013-02-16 00:00:00','2013-03-11 00:00:00','Flat No 05104, 10th Floor, Tower 5','','',2,0,0,0,'Rahul28','2018-10-30 10:42:00.000','Rahul28','2018-10-30 10:42:00.000'),(237,1099,'1099',1174,'1fd7a7f3-6621-4fc2-bf77-23a5487e5d18','FormTypeM',1,1,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Rahul Khandelwal','rahul.khandelwal@jujuscafes.com',9988999852,0,0,'House No 250, FF, Sector 15A','',6,128,'160015','1','House No 250, FF, Sector 15A','',6,128,'160015','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0007','ATS Golf Meadows Lifestyle\r\nCompany - ATS Estates Pvt Ltd','Site Manager, ATS Golf Meadows Lifestyle','lifestylesales@atsgreens.com',8288033311,0,'ATS Golf Meadows Lifestyle, Village Madhopur, Tehsil Derabassi','',28,507,'140507','1','ATS Golf Meadows Lifestyle, Village Madhopur, Tehsil Derabassi','',28,507,'140507','1','<p>The complainants with an intention to have a residential flat for his own residential purpose decided to purchase a 4 BHK Flat measuring approximately 2950 square feet at a Basic Sale Price of 9271250/-. The total price of the flat including power backup charges of 1, 00,000/- and maintenance deposit of 50,000/- was 9777388/ (Inclusive of all taxes). Accordingly the complainant made a payment of Rs 8466852, out of which Rs 1513115 was paid from own funds and Rs 6953737 was paid by HDFC Bank under a subvention loan of Rs 7417000. The remaining amount of Rs 1148176 is to be paid at the time of possession.&nbsp; Details of all payments made till date with Cheque numbers and dates are provided in Annexure 1. As per clause 14 of the buyer agreement (Annexure 2), the committed date of handing over the possession was 36 months with a period of six months grace from the start of actual construction of the tower. The flat was allotted on 16/02/2013 and therefore the due date for possession after 36 month and 6 months grace period was 1st September 2016. However, over two years have passed now and the possession is not offered by the builder. I have written multiple letters to Site Manager and Director of ATS estates (Annexure 3) but there is no official reply. After pursuing the builder endlessly on email, I got a reply from ATS relationship officer on 03 July 2017, wherein the possession date was told as April 2018. Again on 16th February’2018, the possession date was confirmed as September 2018 and finally on 3rd July 2018, possession date shared is Q1’2019. All these mails exchange are shared in Annexure 4. The complainants were provided with Prospectus(Annexure 5) for the said flat indicating features, specifications, facilities, amenities and layout of 4BHK Flat. However, no update is shared on the status of these facilities inspite of multiple reminders.</p>','<ul><li>To refund the total amount paid of Rs 84,66,852/- along with interest at the rate of 12.4% per annum from the different dates of deposit of different amounts till the date of actual payment.</li><li>To reimburse the total amount of rent of the current accommodation of the complainant from 1.03.2016 till date. The complainant is forced to take up a rented accommodation due to delay in possession of the flat.</li><li>To provide a sum of Rs 5,00,000 as compensation for the harassment and mental agony suffered by the complainant.</li></ul><p>As per Real Estate(Regulation and Development) Act, 2016 clause 19(4), the complainant is entitled for refund along with prescribed interest in case of promoter not fulfilling his obligations as per the agreement.</p>',9777388.00,8466852.00,'2016-09-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>To reimburse the total amount of rent of the current accommodation of the complainant from 1.03.2016 till the continuation of the case.&nbsp;</p><p>The complainant is forced to take up a rented accommodation in Chandigarh, due to delay in possession of the flat booked in ATS. The current rent of the accommodation is Rs 38100 per month which is over and above the EMI per month for ATS Flat of Rs 59850. This is leading to double financial burden and loss to the complainant. The rent of the current accommodation is paid through neft every month and the copy of the rent agreement is attached as Annexure 6.</p>','1','','2013-02-16 00:00:00','2013-03-11 00:00:00','Flat No 05104, 10th Floor, Tower 5','','',2,0,0,0,'Rahul28','2018-10-30 10:43:10.000','Rahul28','2018-10-30 10:43:10.000'),(238,1100,'1100',1176,'f299f7e2-246f-4825-9112-8a28b786bed6','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','trishla buildetc pvt ltd','mdtrishla66@gmail.com',8168460262,0,0,'h.no. 257 trishla plus homes','peer Mushalla, PO Dhakoli',28,507,'160104','1','h.no. 257 trishla plus homes','peer Mushalla, PO Dhakoli',28,507,'160104','Munish Gupta','guptalegal44@gmail.com',9814061084,0,'Allottee','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0050','trishla homes','Vimona Alamjit Kaur','cosabonar1@hotmail.com',9876080037,0,'h.no. 3065','sector 27D',6,128,'160019','1','h.no. 3065','sector 27D',6,128,'160019','1','<p>Respondents were allotted flat no. 709, 9th floor of glory tower in \'Trishla City\' developed by complainant at Derabassi, Mohali, Punjab for sale consideration of Rs. 6150000.\r\n</p><p>Respondents on different occasions deposited  Rs. 2243375 vide nine different cheques between 23.01.2012 to 03.12.2013.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>Respondents did not made timely payments from the beginning and as per para 2(c)(ii) of Buyer Agreement dt. 23.04.2012, the agreement stood terminated if the payments are not made within extended period of 90 days from the day they become due.\r\n</p><p>Various Reminder letters were sent to respondent to make the balance payments, to which respondent paid no heed and ultimately the Agreement was terminated as per para 2(c)(ii) supra and the provisional allotment in their favor cancelled. The respondents were informed about termination and cancellation vide letter dt. 7.7.2014. </p><p>On request of the Respondent, the above letter and the termination of agreement as well as cancellation of provisional allotment were withdrawn on condition that respondents have to deposit the outstanding amount within 10 days.&nbsp;</p><p>When no such amount was paid in the stipulated time, the Agreement was terminated on 27.01.2015 and the respondents were offered Rs 1288470 after making deductions as per terms given under para 2(c)(ii) supra by way of Demand Draft of the same date. The respondents never came forward to accept the said Demand Draft.\r\n</p><p>Now, after more than 3 years, Respondents have sent a legal notice dt 12.09.2017 without disclosing the above facts has leveled false allegations of fraud and cheating on the complainant. That Respondent is further alleging that the complainant has failed to hand over the possession of the flat to the Respondents  and further seeking refund of the amount deposited along with the compensation.</p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:150%\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:11.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Verdana&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">In view of the facts mentionedabove,\r\nthe complainant prays for the following relief (s) :-</span><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:150%\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:11.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Verdana&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-indent:0in;line-height:\r\n150%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\r\nmso-bidi-font-size:11.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:Verdana;mso-bidi-font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">(i)</span><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 14px; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:\r\n11.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Legal Notice dated\r\n12.09.2017 issued by the respondents seeking refund of the deposited amount be\r\ndeclared to be illegal, null and void and may kindly be set aside. </span><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;line-height:150%\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:11.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Verdana&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">(ii)</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Issuance\r\nof necessary directions to the respondents, to make payment of the outstanding\r\namount from the due date alongwith interest, although the unit of the\r\ncomplainants has been cancelled but showing its bonafide, the complainant is\r\nstill ready to handover possession of the Kohinoor Category Unit to the\r\nrespondents.</span><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" align=\"center\" style=\"text-align:center;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:11.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Verdana&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Or</span><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:.5in;\r\nline-height:150%\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:11.0pt;\r\nline-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">In the alternative,\r\ndeclare the allotment to have been cancelled on account of defaults committed\r\nby the respondents and also order that the amounts paid by the respondents\r\nstands forfeited. </span><o:p></o:p></span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">\r\n\r\n</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">\r\n\r\n</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">\r\n\r\n</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">\r\n\r\n</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">\r\n\r\n</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">\r\n\r\n</span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:11.0pt;line-height:115%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-theme-font:minor-fareast;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\r\nmso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;mso-ansi-language:EN-US;mso-fareast-language:\r\nEN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Any other relief which this Hon’ble Court may\r\ndeem fit may also be granted in favour of the complainant/applicant.</span>&nbsp;</span><br></p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-indent:.5in;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:11.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Verdana&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Pending final decision on the complaint, the\r\ncomplainant seeks issue of the following interim order: </span><o:p></o:p></span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">\r\n\r\n</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-indent:.5in;line-height:150%\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:11.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Verdana&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Operation of the legal notice dated 12.09.2017 may\r\nkindly be stayed.</span><o:p></o:p></span></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',1,0,0,0,'Nihal','2018-10-30 18:25:01.000','Nihal','2018-10-30 18:25:01.000'),(239,1099,'1099',1174,'1fd7a7f3-6621-4fc2-bf77-23a5487e5d18','FormTypeM',1,1,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Rahul Khandelwal','rahul.khandelwal@jujuscafes.com',9988999852,0,0,'House No 250, FF, Sector 15A','',6,128,'160015','1','House No 250, FF, Sector 15A','',6,128,'160015','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0007','ATS Golf Meadows Lifestyle\r\nCompany - ATS Estates Pvt Ltd','Site Manager, ATS Golf Meadows Lifestyle','lifestylesales@atsgreens.com',8288033311,0,'ATS Golf Meadows Lifestyle, Village Madhopur, Tehsil Derabassi','',28,507,'140507','1','ATS Golf Meadows Lifestyle, Village Madhopur, Tehsil Derabassi','',28,507,'140507','1','<p>The complainants with an intention to have a residential flat for his own residential purpose decided to purchase a 4 BHK Flat measuring approximately 2950 square feet at a Basic Sale Price of 9271250/-. The total price of the flat including power backup charges of 1, 00,000/- and maintenance deposit of 50,000/- was 9777388/ (Inclusive of all taxes). Accordingly the complainant made a payment of Rs 8466852, out of which Rs 1513115 was paid from own funds and Rs 6953737 was paid by HDFC Bank under a subvention loan of Rs 7417000. The remaining amount of Rs 1148176 is to be paid at the time of possession.&nbsp; Details of all payments made till date with Cheque numbers and dates are provided in Annexure 1. As per clause 14 of the buyer agreement (Annexure 2), the committed date of handing over the possession was 36 months with a period of six months grace from the start of actual construction of the tower. The flat was allotted on 16/02/2013 and therefore the due date for possession after 36 month and 6 months grace period was 1st September 2016. However, over two years have passed now and the possession is not offered by the builder. I have written multiple letters to Site Manager and Director of ATS estates (Annexure 3) but there is no official reply. After pursuing the builder endlessly on email, I got a reply from ATS relationship officer on 03 July 2017, wherein the possession date was told as April 2018. Again on 16th February’2018, the possession date was confirmed as September 2018 and finally on 3rd July 2018, possession date shared is Q1’2019. All these mails exchange are shared in Annexure 4. The complainants were provided with Prospectus(Annexure 5) for the said flat indicating features, specifications, facilities, amenities and layout of 4BHK Flat. However, no update is shared on the status of these facilities inspite of multiple reminders.</p>','<ul><li>To refund the total amount paid of Rs 84,66,852/- along with interest at the rate of 12.4% per annum from the different dates of deposit of different amounts till the date of its realization in full and final.</li><li>Provide for damages equal to the total amount of rent of the current accommodation of the complainant from 1.03.2016 till the date of final settlement of complaint. The complainant is forced to take up a rented accommodation due to delay in possession of the flat.</li><li>To penalize the promoter of a sum of Rs 10,00,000 for the harassment and mental agony suffered by the complainant.</li></ul><p>As per Real Estate(Regulation and Development) Act, 2016 clause 19(4), the complainant is entitled for refund along with prescribed interest in case of promoter not fulfilling his obligations as per the agreement.</p>',9777388.00,8466852.00,'2016-09-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>To reimburse the total amount of rent of the current accommodation of the complainant from 1.03.2016 till the continuation of the case.&nbsp;</p><p>The complainant is forced to take up a rented accommodation in Chandigarh, due to delay in possession of the flat booked in ATS. The current rent of the accommodation is Rs 38100 per month which is over and above the EMI per month for ATS Flat of Rs 59850. This is leading to double financial burden and loss to the complainant. The rent of the current accommodation is paid through neft every month and the copy of the rent agreement is attached as Annexure 6.</p>','1','','2013-02-16 00:00:00','2013-03-11 00:00:00','Flat No 05104, 10th Floor, Tower 5','','',2,0,0,0,'Rahul28','2018-10-30 19:52:16.000','Rahul28','2018-10-30 19:52:16.000'),(240,1099,'1099',1174,'1fd7a7f3-6621-4fc2-bf77-23a5487e5d18','FormTypeM',1,1,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Rahul Khandelwal','rahul.khandelwal@jujuscafes.com',9988999852,0,0,'House No 250, FF, Sector 15A','',6,128,'160015','1','House No 250, FF, Sector 15A','',6,128,'160015','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0007','ATS Golf Meadows Lifestyle\r\nCompany - ATS Estates Pvt Ltd','Site Manager, ATS Golf Meadows Lifestyle','lifestylesales@atsgreens.com',8288033311,0,'ATS Golf Meadows Lifestyle, Village Madhopur, Tehsil Derabassi','',28,507,'140507','1','ATS Golf Meadows Lifestyle, Village Madhopur, Tehsil Derabassi','',28,507,'140507','1','<p>The complainants with an intention to have a residential flat for their own residential purpose decided to purchase a 4 BHK Flat measuring approximately 2950 square feet at a Basic Sale Price of 9271250/-. The total price of the flat including power backup charges of 1, 00,000/- and maintenance deposit of 50,000/- was 9777388/ (Inclusive of all taxes). Accordingly the complainant made a payment of Rs 8466852, out of which Rs 1513115 was paid from their own funds and Rs 6953737 was paid out of a subvention loan from HDFC bank of Rs 7417000. The remaining amount of Rs 1148176 is to be paid at the time of possession.&nbsp; Details of all payments made till date with Cheque numbers and dates are provided in Annexure 1. As per clause 14 of the buyer agreement (Annexure 2), the committed date of handing over the possession was 36 months with a period of six months grace from the start of actual construction of the tower. The flat was allotted on 16/02/2013 and therefore the due date for possession after 36 month and 6 months grace period was 1st September 2016. However, over two years have passed now and the possession is not offered by the builder. The complainants have written multiple letters to Site Manager and Director of ATS estates (Annexure 3) but there is no official reply. After pursuing the builder endlessly on email,&nbsp; a reply was shared by designated ATS relationship officer on 03 July 2017, wherein the possession date was told as April 2018. Again on 16th February’2018, the possession date was confirmed on mail as September 2018. All these mails exchange are shared in Annexure 4. The complainants were provided with Prospectus(Annexure 5) for the said flat indicating features, specifications, facilities, amenities and layout of 4BHK Flat. However, no update is shared on the status of these facilities inspite of multiple reminders.</p>','<ul><li>Refund the total amount paid of Rs 84,66,852/- along with interest at the rate of 12.4% per annum from the different dates of deposit of different amounts till the date of its realization in full and final.</li><li>Provide for damages equal to the total amount of rent of the current accommodation of the complainant from 1.03.2016 till the date of final settlement of complaint. The complainant is forced to take up a rented accommodation due to delay in possession of the flat.</li><li>To penalize the promoter of a sum of Rs 10,00,000 for the harassment and mental agony suffered by the complainant.</li></ul><p>As per Real Estate(Regulation and Development) Act, 2016,</p><p>Clause 19(4) The allottee shall be entitled to claim the refund of amount paid along with interest\r\nat such rate as may be prescribed and compensation in the manner as provided under this\r\nAct, from the promoter, if the promoter fails to comply or is unable to give possession of the\r\napartment, plot or building, as the case may be, in accordance with the terms of agreement for\r\nsale or due to discontinuance of his business as a developer on account of suspension or\r\nrevocation of his registration under the provisions of this Act or the rules or regulations\r\nmade there under.</p><p>Clause 12. Where any person makes an advance or a deposit on the basis of the information\r\n contained in the notice advertisement or prospectus, or on the basis of any model apartment, as the case may be, and sustains any loss or damage by reason of any incorrect, false statement included therein, he shall be compensated by the promoter in the manner as provided under this Act. </p><p><br></p>',9777388.00,8466852.00,'2016-09-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>To provide for damages equal to the total amount of rent of the current accommodation of the complainant from 1.03.2016 till the continuation of this complaint.&nbsp;</p><p>The complainant is forced to take up a rented accommodation in Chandigarh, due to delay in possession of the flat booked in ATS. The current rent of the accommodation is Rs 38100 per month which is over and above the EMI per month for ATS Flat of Rs 59850. This is leading to double financial burden and loss to the complainant. The rent of the current accommodation is paid through neft every month and the copy of the rent agreement is attached as Annexure 6.</p>','1','','2013-02-16 00:00:00','2013-03-11 00:00:00','Flat No 05104, 10th Floor, Tower 5','','',2,0,0,0,'Rahul28','2018-10-30 20:12:11.000','Rahul28','2018-10-30 20:12:11.000'),(241,1085,'1085',1135,'7ce4ff29-c893-46aa-aac9-b9c5d5926814','FormTypeM',1,1,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Gurmukh singh ','akhilesh@vyaslawassociates.com',8427828900,0,0,'Nikki Mandi, Patti, ','',28,574,'143001','1','Nikki Mandi, Patti, ','',28,574,'143001','akhilesh vyas','akhilesh@vyaslawassociates.com',9855004557,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-ASR02-PR0169','Guru Ram Dass Urban Estate','Punjab Urban Planning Development Authority','ca@puda.gov.in',0,0,'PUDA Bhawan','green avenue',28,39,'143001','1','PUDA Bhawan','green avenue',28,39,'143001','1','<p>That the complainant was allotted residential plot by respondent bearing plot No. 482 measuring 500 Sq. yards at Guru Ram Dass Urban Estate Airport Road, Amritsar. The total price of the plot is Rs. 945000/- @ 18000/- per square yard.&nbsp;<span style=\"font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif; font-size: 13pt; line-height: 115%;\">&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif; font-size: 13pt; line-height: 115%;\">As per the payment schedule given in the\r\nallotment letter 25% of the allotment amount was to be paid initially and rest\r\nof the payment was to be paid after the possession. The brochure of the scheme\r\nclearly reflects that possession will be handed over on 25% payment as per the allotment letter. It\r\nadmitted by the respondent that payment of Rs. 23,62,500/- was made by the complainant and it has already been adjusted towards initial 25% of the sale\r\nprice of residential plot as mentioned in clause No. 3.1.The complainant has paid full sale consideration amount.&nbsp;</span><font face=\"Bookman Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 17px; line-height: 19px;\">After payment of 25% of total payment first installment was due on 27.10.2017. As per Para 6(i) under the Possession and Ownership Heading of allotment letter possession was be to handed over within 90 days of issuance of allotment letter. So time limit for possession date is 22.1.2017. &nbsp;There was no scene of handing over the possession as no development work was even initiated, applicant made a request through application (diary no 4869 dated 6.917) to waive off interest. But this letter elicited no response from respondent. To be on safer side of law applicant paid first installment (Principal and interest both) and then made the full payment.</span></font></p><p><font face=\"Bookman Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 17px; line-height: 19px;\"><br></span></font></p>','<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"margin-left:.75in;mso-add-space:auto;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;text-indent:-.5in;line-height:\r\n200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\r\nmso-bidi-font-size:11.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;\">i)<span style=\"font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:\r\n11.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">That as the\r\ndepartment has not adhered to their discipline of delivering the actual\r\npossession of the property as per the contract, therefore, the applicant shall\r\nnot be liable to pay any interest and penal interest. Respondent has charged interest\r\nto the tune of Rs 943705/- which is against the natural justice.&nbsp; Applicant should be refunded back interest\r\nwhich has been charged by the respondent. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-left:.75in;mso-add-space:\r\nauto;text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:11.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;\">ii)<span style=\"font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</span></span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:\r\n11.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">Interest on\r\namount which has been paid by applicant should be paid to applicant because of\r\ndelayed payment as per section 18 of The Punjab Real Estate (Regulation and\r\nDevelopment) Act 2016.&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-left:.75in;mso-add-space:\r\nauto;text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span style=\"text-indent: -0.5in; font-size: 12pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif;\">iii)<span style=\"font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><span style=\"text-indent: -0.5in; font-size: 12pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif;\">That the\r\napplicant is liable to be sufficient compensation as per the statue as they\r\nhave been denied their physical possession up till now without any explanatory\r\nreason by the department as per section 14 and 18 of Punjab Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) act 2016. They have not been handed over the\r\npossession of their allotted plots rather the applicant has made the payment as\r\nper the schedule to the respondent department. Uptill now there is no development on the site as well. &nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-left:.75in;mso-add-space:\r\nauto;text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:11.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;\">iv)<span style=\"font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:\r\n11.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">That as stated\r\nabove that the entire payment with regard to the plot allotted has already been\r\npaid still due to the change of plot from one location to another done by the\r\nrespondent themselves, they are demanding of Rs.4,50,000/- and charges ahead.\r\nThe respondent shall be restrained from claiming any such additional amount from\r\nthe applicant as&nbsp; it is never part of the\r\ncontract and any change done whatsoever is unilaterally done by the respondent\r\ndepartment itself.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"margin-left:.75in;mso-add-space:auto;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;text-indent:-.5in;line-height:\r\n200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\r\nmso-bidi-font-size:11.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;\">v)<span style=\"font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:\r\n11.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">That the\r\napplicant is also entitled for restoration of the original plot if so settled\r\nbetween the parties as this change has been done by respondent themselves and\r\nagainst the provisions of Punjab Real Estate ( Regulation &amp; Development)\r\nAct 2016.<o:p></o:p></span></p>',9450000.00,9450000.00,'2017-01-22 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>&nbsp;<span style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -0.5in; font-size: 12pt; line-height: 32px; font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif;\">i)<span style=\"font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span><span style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -0.5in; font-size: 12pt; line-height: 32px; font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif;\">That as the department has not adhered to their discipline of delivering the actual possession of the property as per the contract, therefore, the applicant shall not be liable to pay any interest and penal interest. Respondent has charged interest to the tune of Rs 943705/- which is against the natural justice.&nbsp;&nbsp;Applicant should be refunded back interest which has been charged by the respondent.</span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-left: 0.75in; text-align: justify; text-indent: -0.5in; line-height: 28px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 32px; font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif;\">ii)<span style=\"font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</span></span><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 32px; font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif;\">Interest on amount which has been paid by applicant should be paid to applicant because of delayed payment as per section 18 of The Punjab Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Act 2016.&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-left: 0.75in; text-align: justify; text-indent: -0.5in; line-height: 28px;\"><span style=\"text-indent: -0.5in; font-size: 12pt; line-height: 32px; font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif;\">iii)<span style=\"font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span><span style=\"text-indent: -0.5in; font-size: 12pt; line-height: 32px; font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif;\">That the applicant is liable to be sufficient compensation as per the statue as they have been denied their physical possession up till now without any explanatory reason by the department as per section 14 and 18 of Punjab Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) act 2016. They have not been handed over the possession of their allotted plots rather the applicant has made the payment as per the schedule to the respondent department. Uptill now there is no development on the site as well. &nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-left: 0.75in; text-align: justify; text-indent: -0.5in; line-height: 28px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 32px; font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif;\">iv)<span style=\"font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 32px; font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif;\">That as stated above that the entire payment with regard to the plot allotted has already been paid still due to the change of plot from one location to another done by the respondent themselves, they are demanding of Rs.4,50,000/- and charges ahead. The respondent shall be restrained from claiming any such additional amount from the applicant as&nbsp;&nbsp;it is never part of the contract and any change done whatsoever is unilaterally done by the respondent department itself.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"margin-left: 0.75in; text-align: justify; text-indent: -0.5in; line-height: 28px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 32px; font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif;\">v)<span style=\"font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 32px; font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif;\">That the applicant is also entitled for restoration of the original plot if so settled between the parties as this change has been done by respondent themselves and against the provisions of Punjab Real Estate ( Regulation &amp; Development) Act 2016.</span></p>','1','','2016-10-22 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','482','','',2,0,0,0,'akhilesh','2018-10-31 11:47:40.000','akhilesh','2018-10-31 11:47:40.000'),(242,1099,'1099',1174,'1fd7a7f3-6621-4fc2-bf77-23a5487e5d18','FormTypeM',1,1,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Rahul Khandelwal','rahul.khandelwal@jujuscafes.com',9988999852,0,0,'House No 250, FF, Sector 15A','',6,128,'160015','1','House No 250, FF, Sector 15A','',6,128,'160015','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0007','Project - ATS Golf Meadows Lifestyle1\r\nCompany - ATS Estates Pvt Ltd','Site Manager, ATS Golf Meadows Lifestyle','lifestylesales@atsgreens.com',8288033311,0,'ATS Golf Meadows Lifestyle, Village Madhopur, Tehsil Derabassi','',28,507,'140507','1','ATS Golf Meadows Lifestyle, Village Madhopur, Tehsil Derabassi','',28,507,'140507','1','<p>The complainants with an intention to have a residential flat for their own residential purpose decided to purchase a 4 BHK Flat measuring 2950 sq ft at a Basic Sale Price of 9271250/-. The total price of the flat including power backup charges of 1, 00,000/- and maintenance deposit of 50,000/- was 9777388/ (Inclusive of all taxes). Accordingly the complainant made a payment of Rs 8466852, out of which Rs 1513115 was paid from their own funds and Rs 6953737 was paid out of a subvention loan from HDFC bank of Rs 7417000. The remaining amount of Rs 1148176 is to be paid at the time of possession.&nbsp; Details of all payments made till date with Cheque numbers and dates are provided in Annexure 1. As per clause 14 of the buyer agreement (Annex 2), the committed date of handing over the possession was 36 months with a period of six months grace from the start of actual construction of the tower. The flat was allotted on 16/02/2013 and therefore the due date for possession after 36 month and 6 months grace period was 1st Sep 2016. However, over two years have passed now and the possession is not offered by the builder. The complainants have written multiple letters to Site Manager and Director of ATS estates (Annexure 3) but there is no official reply. After pursuing the builder endlessly on email,&nbsp; a reply was shared by designated ATS relationship officer on 03 July 2017, wherein the possession date was told as April 2018. Again on 16th February’2018, the possession date was confirmed on mail as Sept 2018. All these mails exchange are shared in Annexure 4. The complainants were provided with Prospectus(Annexure 5) for the said flat indicating features, specifications, facilities, amenities and layout of 4BHK Flat. However, no update is shared on the status of these facilities inspite of multiple reminders. Due to non-delivery of possession as agreed and in present set of facts and circumstances, we want to withdraw from the project seeking reliefs mentioned here under.</p>','<ul><li>Refund the total amount paid of Rs 84,66,852/- along with interest at the rate of 12.4% per annum from the different dates of deposit of different amounts till the date of its realization in full and final.</li><li>Provide for damages equal to the total amount of rent of the current accommodation of the complainant from 1.03.2016 till the date of final settlement of complaint. The complainant is forced to take up a rented accommodation due to delay in possession of the flat.</li><li>To penalize the promoter of a sum of Rs 10,00,000 for the harassment and mental agony suffered by the complainant.</li></ul><p>As per Real Estate(Regulation and Development) Act, 2016,</p><p>Clause 19(4) The allottee shall be entitled to claim the refund of amount paid along with interest\r\nat such rate as may be prescribed and compensation in the manner as provided under this\r\nAct, from the promoter, if the promoter fails to comply or is unable to give possession of the\r\napartment, plot or building, as the case may be, in accordance with the terms of agreement for\r\nsale or due to discontinuance of his business as a developer on account of suspension or\r\nrevocation of his registration under the provisions of this Act or the rules or regulations\r\nmade there under.</p><p>Clause 12. Where any person makes an advance or a deposit on the basis of the information\r\n contained in the notice advertisement or prospectus, or on the basis of any model apartment, as the case may be, and sustains any loss or damage by reason of any incorrect, false statement included therein, he shall be compensated by the promoter in the manner as provided under this Act. </p><p><br></p>',9777388.00,8466852.00,'2016-09-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>To provide for damages equal to the total amount of rent of the current accommodation of the complainant from 1.03.2016 till the continuation of this complaint.&nbsp;</p><p>The complainant is forced to take up a rented accommodation in Chandigarh, due to delay in possession of the flat booked in ATS. The current rent of the accommodation is Rs 38100 per month which is over and above the EMI per month for ATS Flat of Rs 59850. This is leading to double financial burden and loss to the complainant. The rent of the current accommodation is paid through neft every month and the copy of the rent agreement is attached as Annexure 6.</p>','1','','2013-02-16 00:00:00','2013-03-11 00:00:00','Flat No 05104, 10th Floor, Tower 5','','',2,0,0,0,'Rahul28','2018-10-31 14:18:52.000','Rahul28','2018-10-31 14:18:52.000'),(243,1099,'1099',1174,'1fd7a7f3-6621-4fc2-bf77-23a5487e5d18','FormTypeM',1,1,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Rahul Khandelwal','rahul.khandelwal@jujuscafes.com',9988999852,0,0,'House No 250, FF, Sector 15A','',6,128,'160015','1','House No 250, FF, Sector 15A','',6,128,'160015','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0007','Project - ATS Golf Meadows Lifestyle1\r\nCompany - ATS Estates Pvt Ltd','Site Manager, ATS Golf Meadows Lifestyle','lifestylesales@atsgreens.com',8288033311,0,'ATS Golf Meadows Lifestyle, Village Madhopur, Tehsil Derabassi','',28,507,'140507','1','ATS Golf Meadows Lifestyle, Village Madhopur, Tehsil Derabassi','',28,507,'140507','1','<p>The complainants with an intention to have a residential flat for their own residential purpose decided to purchase a 4 BHK Flat measuring 2950 sq ft at a Basic Sale Price of 9271250/-. The total price of the flat including power backup charges of 1, 00,000/- and maintenance deposit of 50,000/- was 9777388/ (Inclusive of all taxes). Accordingly the complainant made a payment of Rs 8466852, out of which Rs 1513115 was paid from their own funds and Rs 6953737 was paid out of a subvention loan from HDFC bank of Rs 7417000. The remaining amount of Rs 1148176 is to be paid at the time of possession.&nbsp; Details of all payments made till date with Cheque numbers and dates are provided in Annexure 1. As per clause 14 of the buyer agreement (Annex 2), the committed date of handing over the possession was 36 months with a period of six months grace from the start of actual construction of the tower i.e Feb 2013. The committed date of possession after 36 months was 1st Mar 2016 and with six month grace period it was 1st Sep 2016. However, over two years have passed now and the possession is not offered by the builder. The complainants have written multiple letters to Site Manager and Director of ATS estates (Annex 3) but there is no official reply. After pursuing the builder endlessly on email,&nbsp; a reply was shared by designated ATS relationship officer on 03 July 2017, wherein the possession date was told as April 2018. Again on 16th February’2018, the possession date was confirmed on mail as Sept 2018. All these mails exchange are shared in Annex 4. The complainants were provided with Prospectus(Annex 5) for the said flat indicating features, specifications, facilities, amenities and layout of 4BHK Flat. However, no update is shared on the status of these facilities inspite of multiple reminders. Due to non-delivery of possession as agreed and in present set of facts and circumstances, we want to withdraw from the project seeking reliefs mentioned here under.</p>','<ul><li>Refund the total amount paid of Rs 84,66,852/- along with interest at the rate of 12.4% per annum from the different dates of deposit of different amounts till the date of its realization in full and final.</li><li>Provide for damages equal to the total amount of rent of the current accommodation of the complainant from 1.03.2016 till the date of final settlement of complaint. The complainant is forced to take up a rented accommodation due to delay in possession of the flat. Current rent per month is Rs 38100. Rent agreement of the accommodation is shared in Annexure 6.</li><li>To penalize the promoter of a sum of Rs 10,00,000 for the harassment and mental agony suffered by the complainant.</li></ul><p>As per Real Estate(Regulation and Development) Act, 2016 and&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Rules, Punjab 2017 thereof.</span></p><p><br></p><p><br></p>',9777388.00,8466852.00,'2016-03-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>To provide for damages equal to the total amount of rent of the current accommodation of the complainant from 1.03.2016 till the continuation of this complaint.&nbsp;</p><p>The complainant is forced to take up a rented accommodation in Chandigarh, due to delay in possession of the flat booked in ATS. The current rent of the accommodation is Rs 38100 per month which is over and above the EMI per month for ATS Flat of Rs 59850. This is leading to double financial burden and loss to the complainant. The rent of the current accommodation is paid through neft every month and the copy of the rent agreement is attached as Annexure 6.</p>','1','','2013-02-16 00:00:00','2013-03-11 00:00:00','Flat No 05104, 10th Floor, Tower 5','','',2,0,0,0,'Rahul28','2018-10-31 14:32:49.000','Rahul28','2018-10-31 14:32:49.000'),(244,1099,'1099',1174,'1fd7a7f3-6621-4fc2-bf77-23a5487e5d18','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-10-31 14:33:55.000','Rahul Khandelwal','rahul.khandelwal@jujuscafes.com',9988999852,0,0,'House No 250, FF, Sector 15A','',6,128,'160015','1','House No 250, FF, Sector 15A','',6,128,'160015','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0007','Project - ATS Golf Meadows Lifestyle1\r\nCompany - ATS Estates Pvt Ltd','Site Manager, ATS Golf Meadows Lifestyle','lifestylesales@atsgreens.com',8288033311,0,'ATS Golf Meadows Lifestyle, Village Madhopur, Tehsil Derabassi','',28,507,'140507','1','ATS Golf Meadows Lifestyle, Village Madhopur, Tehsil Derabassi','',28,507,'140507','1','<p>The complainants with an intention to have a residential flat for their own residential purpose decided to purchase a 4 BHK Flat measuring 2950 sq ft at a Basic Sale Price of 9271250/-. The total price of the flat including power backup charges of 1, 00,000/- and maintenance deposit of 50,000/- was 9777388/ (Inclusive of all taxes). Accordingly the complainant made a payment of Rs 8466852, out of which Rs 1513115 was paid from their own funds and Rs 6953737 was paid out of a subvention loan from HDFC bank of Rs 7417000. The remaining amount of Rs 1148176 is to be paid at the time of possession.&nbsp; Details of all payments made till date with Cheque numbers and dates are provided in Annexure 1. As per clause 14 of the buyer agreement (Annex 2), the committed date of handing over the possession was 36 months with a period of six months grace from the start of actual construction of the tower i.e Feb 2013. The committed date of possession after 36 months was 1st Mar 2016 and with six month grace period it was 1st Sep 2016. However, over two years have passed now and the possession is not offered by the builder. The complainants have written multiple letters to Site Manager and Director of ATS estates (Annex 3) but there is no official reply. After pursuing the builder endlessly on email,&nbsp; a reply was shared by designated ATS relationship officer on 03 July 2017, wherein the possession date was told as April 2018. Again on 16th February’2018, the possession date was confirmed on mail as Sept 2018. All these mails exchange are shared in Annex 4. The complainants were provided with Prospectus(Annex 5) for the said flat indicating features, specifications, facilities, amenities and layout of 4BHK Flat. However, no update is shared on the status of these facilities inspite of multiple reminders. Due to non-delivery of possession as agreed and in present set of facts and circumstances, we want to withdraw from the project seeking reliefs mentioned here under.</p>','<ul><li>Refund the total amount paid of Rs 84,66,852/- along with interest at the rate of 12.4% per annum from the different dates of deposit of different amounts till the date of its realization in full and final.</li><li>Provide for damages equal to the total amount of rent of the current accommodation of the complainant from 1.03.2016 till the date of final settlement of complaint. The complainant is forced to take up a rented accommodation due to delay in possession of the flat. Current rent per month is Rs 38100. Rent agreement of the accommodation is shared in Annexure 6.</li><li>To penalize the promoter of a sum of Rs 10,00,000 for the harassment and mental agony suffered by the complainant.</li></ul><p>As per Real Estate(Regulation and Development) Act, 2016 and&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Rules, Punjab 2017 thereof.</span></p><p><br></p><p><br></p>',9777388.00,8466852.00,'2016-03-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>To provide for damages equal to the total amount of rent of the current accommodation of the complainant from 1.03.2016 till the continuation of this complaint.&nbsp;</p><p>The complainant is forced to take up a rented accommodation in Chandigarh, due to delay in possession of the flat booked in ATS. The current rent of the accommodation is Rs 38100 per month which is over and above the EMI per month for ATS Flat of Rs 59850. This is leading to double financial burden and loss to the complainant. The rent of the current accommodation is paid through neft every month and the copy of the rent agreement is attached as Annexure 6.</p>','1','','2013-02-16 00:00:00','2013-03-11 00:00:00','Flat No 05104, 10th Floor, Tower 5','','',1,1,0,0,'Rahul28','2018-10-31 14:33:39.000','Rahul28','2018-10-31 14:33:39.000'),(245,1090,'1090',1143,'750cff8c-f4c0-4b3b-853b-c94fcf3d7864','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-10-15 17:02:49.000','Sandeep Kaur','sandeepbajwa27@gmail.com',9888087374,0,0,'House No.577, First Floor','pocket-4, Omaxe, New Chandigarh, Mullanpur',28,507,'140901','0','HOUSE NO 253','Sector 4 Mansa Devi Complex',13,15,'134114','Sanjeev Gupta','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0007','ATS Golf Meadows Lifestyle 1','ATS Estates Pvt. Ltd.','pradeep.rathee@atsgreens.com',8288033311,0,'Village Madhopur','Tehsil Derabassi',28,507,'140507','0','711/92, DEEPALI','NEHRU PLACE',10,429,'110019','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-height:\r\n150%\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">That applicant along with her mother Gurdarshan kaur had purchased a 3 BHK flat bearing Registration No 355, apartment No 6032, 6th floor, Tower 1, in ATS Golf Meadows Lifestyle, in 2013(C-1). A sum of Rs. 5550000 was paid by them towards the sale consideration(C-2).\r\n</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-height:\r\n150%\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">That applicant and Gurdarshan Kaur in December, 2014 decided to have bigger accommodation and thus requested the respondent to allot them 4 BHK flat instead. Accordingly, the respondent vide allotment letter dated 28-Jan-2015 (C-3) allotted flat No 04032, 3rd floor, Tower 4, Registration No 432, measuring 2950 sq ft in ATS Gold Meadows Lifestyle for total sale consideration of Rs 6147500. The respondent assured to deliver the possession in August, 2015. All the previous payments made by the applicant and Gurdarshan Kaur amounting to Rs.5550000 were transferred to this apartment\r\n</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-height:\r\n150%\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">Buyer agreement(C-4) in respect of said apartment was executed on 28-Jan-2015 and as per clause 14, the possession of the flat was to be delivered within 36 months from the date start of construction of particular tower in which flat is allotted. The construction of Tower No 4 was started in August, 2012 as intimated by the respondent vide letter dated 18.09.2014 (C-5) which was sent to the applicant on 27.04.2018. The period of 36 months expired in August, 2015. Thus, the respondent was bound to deliver the possession by August, 2015. But till date the respondent has failed to deliver the possession.\r\n</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-height:\r\n150%\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">The applicant along with Gurdarshan Kaur is living in a rented accommodation and thus the respondent is also liable to pay the amount towards the rent paid by the applicant for staying in rented accommodation with effect from September, 2015 till the date of possession.\r\n</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-height:\r\n150%\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">That the applicant has become the absolute owner of said apartment after the transfer of share by Gurdarshan Kaur, in her favor and the respondent&nbsp; duly acknowledged the same by executing a supplementary agreement dated 4.9.2018(C-6). Statement of Account(C-7)</span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-height:\r\n150%\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\nCalibri;mso-fareast-theme-font:minor-latin\">To offer possession of apartment No\r\n04032, on 3rd Floor in Tower No 4 complete in all aspects&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 18px;\">(with all the basic\r\nfacilities made available at the site)&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 150%;\">along with interest, as contemplated\r\nunder rule 16 of The Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development)\r\nRules, 2017, on the already deposited amount i.e. </span><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 150%;\">Rs. 5550000, </span><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 150%;\">for the period of delay in possession with\r\neffect from September, 2015 till offer of the possession of the said apartment.</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-height:\r\n150%\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\nCalibri;mso-fareast-theme-font:minor-latin\">To pay Rs. 500000 as compensation\r\nfor deficiency in service, unfair trade practice and mental harassment suffered\r\nby the complainant and </span><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%\">damages\r\nfor the physical and mental torture, agony, discomfort and undue hardships\r\ncaused to the complainant. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-height:\r\n150%\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\nCalibri;mso-fareast-theme-font:minor-latin\">To pay the amount calculated at the\r\nrate Rs. 12700 per month w.e.f &nbsp;September,2015\r\nto April, 2016 towards the rent paid by the applicant along with maintenance\r\ncharges at the rate of Rs. 1500 per month for said period, and to pay amount\r\ncalculated at the rate of Rs. 13970 per month w.e.f May, 2016 to March,2017\r\ntowards the rent paid by the applicant along with maintenance charges at the\r\nrate of Rs. 2200 per month, for the period of delay in possession w.e.f.\r\nSeptember, 2015 till offer of the possession of the said apartment.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-height:\r\n150%\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\nCalibri;mso-fareast-theme-font:minor-latin\">To pay Rs. 100000 as litigation\r\nexpenses to the complainant in the interest of justice.</span><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>',6147500.00,5550000.00,'2015-08-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<div class=\"WordSection1\">\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:150%\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%\">It is further prayed that during the\r\npendency of instant application, the respondent be directed not to create any\r\nthird party rights over the said apartment and not to create any charge over\r\nit.<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:7.5pt;text-align:justify;line-height:\r\n21.0pt\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n</div><p>\r\n\r\n<span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><br clear=\"all\" style=\"page-break-before:always;mso-break-type:section-break\"></span></p>','1','','2015-01-28 00:00:00','2015-01-28 00:00:00','Flat No - 04032, 3rd Floor, Tower No. 4','','',2,0,0,0,'Sa