r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:4.7pt;margin-left:0cm;\r\ntext-align:justify\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">(ii)\r\ndirections for completion of the development works of the project and the\r\nconstruction of the independent residential floor in question without any\r\nfurther delay and also offer the possession after the grant of Occupation\r\nCertificate of the Building and the Completion Certificate of the Wave Estate\r\nProject alongwith interest and compensation prescribed under Real Estate\r\n(Regulation and Development) Act 2016 as the action of the Respondents.<o:p></o:p></span></p>',4000000.00,3600000.00,'2016-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">The\r\nrespondents be directed to complete the development works of the project and\r\nthe construction of the independent residential floor in question without any\r\nfurther delay and also offer the possession after the grant of occupation\r\ncertificate of the Building and the Completion Certificate of the Wave Estate\r\nProject.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px;\">The Promoter be also\r\ndirected to pay interim monthly interest and compensation till the completion\r\nof the project and the complex in question in the pendency of the complaint.</span><br></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','2013-09-03 00:00:00','“Independent Residential Floors” Bearing No. 28 on 2nd Floor in Sector ‘G’','','',1,1,0,0,'RajeevAnand','2018-11-09 17:09:46.000','RajeevAnand','2018-11-09 17:09:46.000'),(272,1104,'1104',1091,'e2da2916-c5af-4a15-acce-51dcf84d70a2','FormTypeM',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Prem Datt','dattprem@gmail.com',9417323627,0,0,'House No. 3175 B','Sector 24 D',6,128,'160024','1','House No. 2378, Sector 35-C,','',6,128,'160035','Rajeev Anand','anandlawoffice2378@gmail.com',9417870805,1722622364,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0153','Wave Estate Project','M/s Country Colonizers Pvt Ltd Through its MD','customercare@waveestate.in',0,0,'PO Rayon and Silk Mills','Adjoining Coca Cola Depot GT Road, Chheharta',28,39,'143105','0','M/s Country Colonizers Pvt Ltd. Wave Estate Project site office sector 85','SAS Nagar Mohali',28,507,'140308','1','<p>The Complainant booked Apartment 66 FF, Sector G, Wave Floor, Sector 99 Mohali on 21.03.2013 making initial payment (Annexure C-1). Agreement dated 19.07.2013 (Annexure C-2) was executed with Respondent for saleable area 1060sqFt @ 3773.58/sqFt. As per Clause 5.2, the Project was to be developed and the Apartment was to be handed over in 24 months and by Cl. 5.5 the delay entailed Rs. 5/sqFt/month for delay. On 20.01.2014, the Complainant was made to fill another Agreement (Annexure C-3), the Apartment was unilaterally changed by issuing a letter (Annexure C-4) with new number 42/FF, Wave Floor Sector 99, Mohali (Relocated Apartment). \r\n</p><p>The Complainant took a Loan (Annexure C-5) for the unit. The Complainant found that site plan has been changed of the Apartment by changing bathroom door opening in bedroom etc.. Having found the Project and the Apartment delayed, the Complainant gave a representation 11.01.2017 (Annexure C-6) that construction started with 2 years delay and not completed. The complainant gave another representation dated 05.08.2017 (Annexure C-7) that even after 4 1/2 years possession not offered. On 03.09.2017 (Annexure C-8) the Complainant wanted to meet the senior executive but no time was given for meeting for delivery of possession. The Complainant upon interest liability and EMI burden spent his life savings and repaid loan on 01.03.2017 (Annexure C-9).    \r\n</p><p>Now the offer of possession is made in third week of Oct 2018, but the Apartment is incomplete. The apartment was to be completed by 19.01.2016 but not done against which Complainant gave representation dated 23.09.2017 (Annexure C-10). The Respondent made a unilateral Deed of Settlement on 16.12.2017 (Annexure C-11) to give interest &amp; also give possession by March 2018 but since not honoured by Respondent, the Deed of Settlement became redundant. \r\n</p><p>Now On 14.08.2018 (Annexure C-12) a Statement of Account has been given wherein area increased and money charged without any increase in Apartment</p>','<p style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:4.7pt;margin-left:0cm;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">The Apartment was to be handed over after\r\ncompleting the Project in 24 months + 6 Months i.e. from 23.07.2013 by\r\n23.01.2016. Even the monthly compensation of Rs5/SqFt/month was to be paid from\r\nJanuary 2016 onwards till date NOT PAID.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:4.7pt;margin-left:0cm;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">The Respondent&nbsp;has taken the total\r\nsale price in advance at the time of signing of Agreement to the tune of Rs. 3\r\nLakhs (+Service Tax) on 05.02.2013 and 3 lakhs(+Service Tax)&nbsp;&nbsp;on\r\n21.03.2013+ Rs 968658 (+Service Tax) on 05.02.2015 + Rs 231342 (+ Service Tax)\r\non 31.03.2015+ 1055264/- (+ service Tax) on 16.11.2015 +Rs. 144736/- (+ service\r\nTax) on 16.11.2015+ 559382/- lakhs (+ service Tax) on 18.06.2016 + 40618 (+\r\nservice Tax) on 14.06.2016, totaling 36 Lakhs (+ service Tax) as also EMIs with\r\ninterest.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">The possession of\r\nthe Apartment was to be given to the Applicant / Allottee within 24 + 6 = 30\r\nmonths. Inspite of elapsing of over 5 years of Agreement, no development and\r\nconstruction works have been completed in the Complex and the Respondent\r\nPromoter has failed in its obligation towards the Complex and Independent\r\nResidential Floor allotted to the Applicant. The Promoter is liable to pay the\r\ninterest on the payment so received for the period of delay in offering\r\npossession after the completion of the development works of the project and the\r\ncompletion of the construction of the Independent Residential Floor. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:4.7pt;margin-left:0cm;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">In view of the above : <o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:4.7pt;margin-left:0cm;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">(i) The Applicant / Allottee is seeking\r\ncompensation as applicable in Para 5.5 of Agreement dated 19.07.2013 from\r\nJanuary 2016 onwards till date; <o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">(ii) directions for completion of the development works of the project\r\nand the construction of the independent residential floor in question without\r\nany further delay and also offer the possession after the grant of Occupation\r\nCertificate of the Building and the Completion Certificate of the Wave Estate\r\nProject alongwith interest and compensation prescribed under Real Estate\r\n(Regulation and Development) Act 2016 as the action of the Respondents.</span><br></p>',4000000.00,3600000.00,'2016-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:\r\njustify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;line-height:200%;mso-layout-grid-align:\r\nnone;text-autospace:none\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">The\r\nrespondents be directed to complete the development works of the project and\r\nthe construction of the independent residential floor in question without any\r\nfurther delay and also offer the possession after the grant of occupation\r\ncertificate of the Building and the Completion Certificate of the Wave Estate\r\nProject.&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px;\">The Promoter be also\r\ndirected to pay interim monthly interest and compensation till the completion\r\nof the project and the complex in question in the pendency of the complaint.</span></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','2013-07-23 00:00:00','Independent Residential Floor Bearing No. 43/FF in Sector 99','','',2,0,0,0,'RajeevAnand','2018-11-09 17:58:09.000','RajeevAnand','2018-11-09 17:58:09.000'),(273,1102,'1102',1141,'971b1ae7-f8bc-4323-80a7-088b81f8b7db','FormTypeM',1,1,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Vinay Vohra','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9814010363,0,0,'House No.413, Dalima Vihar','Rajpura',28,454,'140401','1','253','Sector 4, Mansa Devi Complex',13,15,'134114','Sanjeev Gupta','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0093','PALM SPRING','M/s Manohar Infrastructure & Constructions Pvt Ltd','nbs@manoharrealty.com',0,1725033524,'SCO 139-141','Sector-17C',6,128,'160017','1','SCO 139-141','Sector-17C',6,128,'160017','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">Complainant,on\r\n21.4.11 booked a(C-1)250 sq yards plot @RS.18000 per sq yd (excluding EDC &amp;\r\nPLC)from the respondent in Palm spring.Before booking of said plot,the\r\nrespondent had assured the complainant that development would be started very\r\nsoon &amp; possession will be delivered in 2 years.Complainant paid Rs. 1350000\r\ni.e Rs 850000 in cash on 18.4.2011 &amp; Rs. 500000 on 21.4.11 by cheque. An\r\nacknowledgment (C-2) was issued by respondent in which it arbitrarily\r\nincorporated the condition of paying the IDC.When complainant resisted about\r\nthe same, the respondent threatened to forfeit the money paid by complainant if\r\nsuch charges are not paid by him.Insipte of repeated requests, respondent did\r\nnot issue any allotment letter &amp; execute the agreement.Respondent assured\r\nto issue allotment letter &amp; execute agreement on further payment of Rs.9\r\nlacs i.e 20 % sale consideration.In the hope of getting the same, the\r\ncomplainant paid the said amount of Rs. 9 lacs on 19.7.13 i.e.Rs. 4 lacs in\r\ncash &amp; Rs. 5 lac by cheque(C-3).But inspite of receiving the said\r\namount,respondent did not issue any allotment letter &amp; execute the\r\nagreement. Complainant many times requested the respondent to issue the\r\nallotment letter &amp; execute the agreement, but respondent did not pay any\r\nheed to his request. Instead it started demanding more money for issuing\r\nallotment letter &amp; executing the agreement.Respondent only issued registration\r\nnumber (C-4) after receiving 50% of sale consideration.Complainant visited the\r\noffice of respondent many times during the year 2014,2015,2016, 2017 &amp; 2018 for\r\nredressal of his grievances but to no avail. Inspite of paying Rs.2250000/-\r\ni.e. 50% sale consideration, the complainant is still empty handed.Respondent\r\nalways kept the complainant in dark about the approvals &amp; development.It\r\nhas failed to develop the project.It had not even applied the necessary\r\npermissions when the plot was sold to complainant.A list of dates of approvals\r\n(C-5) and some important approval as (C-6&amp;C-7)</span><o:p></o:p></p>','<ol><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">Directing\r\nthe respondent to refund the principle amount i.e.Rs. 2250000/- along with\r\ninterest as contemplated under rule 16 of The Punjab RERA Rules, 2017,as the\r\ncomplainant does not wish to have a plot in the project being developed by the\r\nrespondent, as the complainant has lost faith in the respondent due to\r\nmisrepresentation by it about the approvals &amp; stages of development during\r\nall these years ,did not issue any allotment letter &amp; execute the agreement\r\ntill date, failed to develop the project.Also the respondent has committed\r\nviolation of various provisions of PAPRA &amp; conditions of various approvals\r\ngranted to it,as it could not collect any amount till the exemption is received\r\nunder Section 44 of PAPRA which was granted on 25.1.17.The respondent collected\r\nthe money from the complainant in 2011.The approvals were granted to the\r\nrespondent on the ground that it will not sell any plot &amp; collect money\r\nfrom the general public till exemption under Section 44 of PAPRA is\r\nreceived.Also, inspite of receiving 50% of sale consideration the respondent\r\ndid not execute any agreement &amp; issue a plot number till date &amp; asking\r\nthe complainant to pay more money for getting the allotment letter &amp;\r\nexecution of agreement in violation of Section 13 of RERA.</span></li><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Directing the respondent to pay the\r\ncompensation of Rs.10 lacs for deficiency in services, unfair trade practices\r\n&amp; harassment caused to the complainant &amp; for using their hard earned\r\nmoney for such a long period.</span></li><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Directing\r\nthe respondent to pay litigation expenses to the tune of Rs.50000.</span></li><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">To\r\ntake action against respondent under Section 61 of RERA for constant violation\r\nof provision of Section 13 of RERA as the respondent failed to issue any\r\nallotment letter &amp; execute the buyer’s agreement till date, inspite of\r\nreceiving 50% of sale consideration.</span></li><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">For cancelling the extension granted to the respondent for constantly violating\r\nvarious provisions of RERA and for indulging into unfair trade practices.</span></li></ol>',4500000.00,2250000.00,'2013-04-20 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<ol><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The respondent be directed to provide the list\r\nof allottees to whom it has allotted/sold the 862 residential plots as per the\r\nlayout plan approved by GMADA on 6.10.2015. The respondent has been duly registered under RERA for the said approved layout plan. As per the said approved layout plan, the respondent can sell 862 residential plots and 73 commercial plots/spaces.</span></li><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The respondent be directed to provide the list\r\nof hypothecated plots ,which are hypothecated to GMADA, out of the said approved 862\r\nresidential and 73 commercial plots</span></li><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The respondent be directed to provide the list\r\nof hypothected plots already </span><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">allotted</span><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">/sold to general public.</span></span></li><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The respondent be directed to provide the\r\ndetails of funds collected from the general public since 2010 in lieu of the said approved 862\r\nresidential plots which are part of approved layout plan and for which the respondent is duly registered under\r\nSection 3 of RERA and also, the detail where such amount has been utilized by\r\nthe respondent</span></li><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The respondent be directed to provide all the\r\nbank details where such amount has been deposited along with the statement of\r\naccounts since the year 2010</span></li><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The\r\nrespondent be directed to provide the details in respect of number of bookings made by the respondent since the year 2010 for the said 862 residential plots</span><o:p></o:p></span></p></li></ol>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','NO ALLOTMENT & AGREEMENT YET','','',2,0,0,0,'rerafilingformm','2018-11-09 18:37:05.000','rerafilingformm','2018-11-09 18:37:05.000'),(274,1102,'1102',1141,'971b1ae7-f8bc-4323-80a7-088b81f8b7db','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-11-09 18:37:31.000','Vinay Vohra','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9814010363,0,0,'House No.413, Dalima Vihar','Rajpura',28,454,'140401','1','253','Sector 4, Mansa Devi Complex',13,15,'134114','Sanjeev Gupta','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0093','PALM SPRING','M/s Manohar Infrastructure & Constructions Pvt Ltd','nbs@manoharrealty.com',0,1725033524,'SCO 139-141','Sector-17C',6,128,'160017','1','SCO 139-141','Sector-17C',6,128,'160017','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">Complainant,on\r\n21.4.11 booked a(C-1)250 sq yards plot @RS.18000 per sq yd (excluding EDC &amp;\r\nPLC)from the respondent in Palm spring.Before booking of said plot,the\r\nrespondent had assured the complainant that development would be started very\r\nsoon &amp; possession will be delivered in 2 years.Complainant paid Rs. 1350000\r\ni.e Rs 850000 in cash on 18.4.2011 &amp; Rs. 500000 on 21.4.11 by cheque. An\r\nacknowledgment (C-2) was issued by respondent in which it arbitrarily\r\nincorporated the condition of paying the IDC.When complainant resisted about\r\nthe same, the respondent threatened to forfeit the money paid by complainant if\r\nsuch charges are not paid by him.Insipte of repeated requests, respondent did\r\nnot issue any allotment letter &amp; execute the agreement.Respondent assured\r\nto issue allotment letter &amp; execute agreement on further payment of Rs.9\r\nlacs i.e 20 % sale consideration.In the hope of getting the same, the\r\ncomplainant paid the said amount of Rs. 9 lacs on 19.7.13 i.e.Rs. 4 lacs in\r\ncash &amp; Rs. 5 lac by cheque(C-3).But inspite of receiving the said\r\namount,respondent did not issue any allotment letter &amp; execute the\r\nagreement. Complainant many times requested the respondent to issue the\r\nallotment letter &amp; execute the agreement, but respondent did not pay any\r\nheed to his request. Instead it started demanding more money for issuing\r\nallotment letter &amp; executing the agreement.Respondent only issued registration\r\nnumber (C-4) after receiving 50% of sale consideration.Complainant visited the\r\noffice of respondent many times during the year 2014,2015,2016, 2017 &amp; 2018 for\r\nredressal of his grievances but to no avail. Inspite of paying Rs.2250000/-\r\ni.e. 50% sale consideration, the complainant is still empty handed.Respondent\r\nalways kept the complainant in dark about the approvals &amp; development.It\r\nhas failed to develop the project.It had not even applied the necessary\r\npermissions when the plot was sold to complainant.A list of dates of approvals\r\n(C-5) and some important approval as (C-6&amp;C-7)</span><o:p></o:p></p>','<ol><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">Directing\r\nthe respondent to refund the principle amount i.e.Rs. 2250000/- along with\r\ninterest as contemplated under rule 16 of The Punjab RERA Rules, 2017,as the\r\ncomplainant does not wish to have a plot in the project being developed by the\r\nrespondent, as the complainant has lost faith in the respondent due to\r\nmisrepresentation by it about the approvals &amp; stages of development during\r\nall these years ,did not issue any allotment letter &amp; execute the agreement\r\ntill date, failed to develop the project.Also the respondent has committed\r\nviolation of various provisions of PAPRA &amp; conditions of various approvals\r\ngranted to it,as it could not collect any amount till the exemption is received\r\nunder Section 44 of PAPRA which was granted on 25.1.17.The respondent collected\r\nthe money from the complainant in 2011.The approvals were granted to the\r\nrespondent on the ground that it will not sell any plot &amp; collect money\r\nfrom the general public till exemption under Section 44 of PAPRA is\r\nreceived.Also, inspite of receiving 50% of sale consideration the respondent\r\ndid not execute any agreement &amp; issue a plot number till date &amp; asking\r\nthe complainant to pay more money for getting the allotment letter &amp;\r\nexecution of agreement in violation of Section 13 of RERA.</span></li><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Directing the respondent to pay the\r\ncompensation of Rs.10 lacs for deficiency in services, unfair trade practices\r\n&amp; harassment caused to the complainant &amp; for using their hard earned\r\nmoney for such a long period.</span></li><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Directing\r\nthe respondent to pay litigation expenses to the tune of Rs.50000.</span></li><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">To\r\ntake action against respondent under Section 61 of RERA for constant violation\r\nof provision of Section 13 of RERA as the respondent failed to issue any\r\nallotment letter &amp; execute the buyer’s agreement till date, inspite of\r\nreceiving 50% of sale consideration.</span></li><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">For cancelling the extension granted to the respondent for constantly violating\r\nvarious provisions of RERA and for indulging into unfair trade practices.</span></li></ol>',4500000.00,2250000.00,'2013-04-20 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<ol><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The respondent be directed to provide the list\r\nof allottees to whom it has allotted/sold the 862 residential plots as per the\r\nlayout plan approved by GMADA on 6.10.2015. The respondent has been duly registered under RERA for the said approved layout plan. As per the said approved layout plan, the respondent can sell 862 residential plots and 73 commercial plots/spaces.</span></li><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The respondent be directed to provide the list\r\nof hypothecated plots ,which are hypothecated to GMADA, out of the said approved 862\r\nresidential and 73 commercial plots</span></li><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The respondent be directed to provide the list\r\nof hypothected plots already </span><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">allotted</span><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">/sold to general public.</span></span></li><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The respondent be directed to provide the\r\ndetails of funds collected from the general public since 2010 in lieu of the said approved 862\r\nresidential plots which are part of approved layout plan and for which the respondent is duly registered under\r\nSection 3 of RERA and also, the detail where such amount has been utilized by\r\nthe respondent</span></li><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The respondent be directed to provide all the\r\nbank details where such amount has been deposited along with the statement of\r\naccounts since the year 2010</span></li><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The\r\nrespondent be directed to provide the details in respect of number of bookings made by the respondent since the year 2010 for the said 862 residential plots</span><o:p></o:p></span></p></li></ol>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','NO ALLOTMENT & AGREEMENT YET','','',1,1,0,0,'rerafilingformm','2018-11-09 18:37:28.000','rerafilingformm','2018-11-09 18:37:28.000'),(275,1104,'1104',1091,'e2da2916-c5af-4a15-acce-51dcf84d70a2','FormTypeM',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Prem Datt','dattprem@gmail.com',9417323627,0,0,'House No. 3175 B','Sector 24 D',6,128,'160024','1','House No. 2378,','Sector 35-C',6,128,'160035','Rajeev Anand','anandlawoffice2378@gmail.com',9417870805,1722622364,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0153','Wave Estate Project','M/s Country Colonizers Pvt Ltd Through its MD','customercare@waveestate.in',0,0,'PO Rayon and Silk Mills','Adjoining Coca Cola Depot GT Road, Chheharta',28,39,'143105','0','M/s Country Colonizers Pvt Ltd. Wave Estate Project site office sector 85','SAS Nagar Mohali',28,507,'140308','1','<p>The Complainant booked Apartment 66 FF, Sector G, Wave Floor, Sector 99 Mohali on 21.03.2013 making initial payment (Annexure C-1). Agreement dated 19.07.2013 (Annexure C-2) was executed with Respondent for saleable area 1060sqFt @ 3773.58/sqFt. As per Clause 5.2, the Project was to be developed and the Apartment was to be handed over in 24 months and by Cl. 5.5 the delay entailed Rs. 5/sqFt/month for delay. On 20.01.2014, the Complainant was made to fill another Agreement (Annexure C-3), the Apartment was unilaterally changed by issuing a letter (Annexure C-4) with new number 42/FF, Wave Floor Sector 99, Mohali (Relocated Apartment). \r\n</p><p>The Complainant took a Loan (Annexure C-5) for the unit. The Complainant found that site plan has been changed of the Apartment by changing bathroom door opening in bedroom etc.. Having found the Project and the Apartment delayed, the Complainant gave a representation 11.01.2017 (Annexure C-6) that construction started with 2 years delay and not completed. The complainant gave another representation dated 05.08.2017 (Annexure C-7) that even after 4 1/2 years possession not offered. On 03.09.2017 (Annexure C-8) the Complainant wanted to meet the senior executive but no time was given for meeting for delivery of possession. The Complainant upon interest liability and EMI burden spent his life savings and repaid loan on 01.03.2017 (Annexure C-9).    \r\n</p><p>Now the offer of possession is made in third week of Oct 2018, but the Apartment is incomplete. The apartment was to be completed by 19.01.2016 but not done against which Complainant gave representation dated 23.09.2017 (Annexure C-10). The Respondent made a unilateral Deed of Settlement on 16.12.2017 (Annexure C-11) to give interest &amp; also give possession by March 2018 but since not honoured by Respondent, the Deed of Settlement became redundant. \r\n</p><p>Now On 14.08.2018 (Annexure C-12) a Statement of Account has been given wherein area increased and money charged without any increase in Apartment</p>','<p style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:4.7pt;margin-left:0cm;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">The Apartment was to be handed over after\r\ncompleting the Project in 24 months + 6 Months i.e. from 23.07.2013 by\r\n23.01.2016. Even the monthly compensation of Rs5/SqFt/month was to be paid from\r\nJanuary 2016 onwards till date NOT PAID.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:4.7pt;margin-left:0cm;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">The Respondent&nbsp;has taken the total\r\nsale price in advance at the time of signing of Agreement to the tune of Rs. 3\r\nLakhs (+Service Tax) on 05.02.2013 and 3 lakhs(+Service Tax)&nbsp;&nbsp;on\r\n21.03.2013+ Rs 968658 (+Service Tax) on 05.02.2015 + Rs 231342 (+ Service Tax)\r\non 31.03.2015+ 1055264/- (+ service Tax) on 16.11.2015 +Rs. 144736/- (+ service\r\nTax) on 16.11.2015+ 559382/- lakhs (+ service Tax) on 18.06.2016 + 40618 (+\r\nservice Tax) on 14.06.2016, totaling 36 Lakhs (+ service Tax) as also EMIs with\r\ninterest.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">The possession of\r\nthe Apartment was to be given to the Applicant / Allottee within 24 + 6 = 30\r\nmonths. Inspite of elapsing of over 5 years of Agreement, no development and\r\nconstruction works have been completed in the Complex and the Respondent\r\nPromoter has failed in its obligation towards the Complex and Independent\r\nResidential Floor allotted to the Applicant. The Promoter is liable to pay the\r\ninterest on the payment so received for the period of delay in offering\r\npossession after the completion of the development works of the project and the\r\ncompletion of the construction of the Independent Residential Floor. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:4.7pt;margin-left:0cm;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">In view of the above : <o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:4.7pt;margin-left:0cm;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">(i) The Applicant / Allottee is seeking\r\ncompensation as applicable in Para 5.5 of Agreement dated 19.07.2013 from\r\nJanuary 2016 onwards till date; <o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">(ii) directions for completion of the development works of the project\r\nand the construction of the independent residential floor in question without\r\nany further delay and also offer the possession after the grant of Occupation\r\nCertificate of the Building and the Completion Certificate of the Wave Estate\r\nProject alongwith interest and compensation prescribed under Real Estate\r\n(Regulation and Development) Act 2016 as the action of the Respondents.</span><br></p>',4000000.00,3600000.00,'2016-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:\r\njustify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;line-height:200%;mso-layout-grid-align:\r\nnone;text-autospace:none\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">The\r\nrespondents be directed to complete the development works of the project and\r\nthe construction of the independent residential floor in question without any\r\nfurther delay and also offer the possession after the grant of occupation\r\ncertificate of the Building and the Completion Certificate of the Wave Estate\r\nProject.&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px;\">The Promoter be also\r\ndirected to pay interim monthly interest and compensation till the completion\r\nof the project and the complex in question in the pendency of the complaint.</span></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','2013-07-23 00:00:00','Independent Residential Floor Bearing No. 43/FF in Sector 99','','',2,0,0,0,'RajeevAnand','2018-11-09 18:53:59.000','RajeevAnand','2018-11-09 18:53:59.000'),(276,1104,'1104',1091,'e2da2916-c5af-4a15-acce-51dcf84d70a2','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-11-12 09:13:55.000','Prem Datt','dattprem@gmail.com',9417323627,0,0,'House No. 3175 B','Sector 24 D',6,128,'160024','1','House No. 2378,','Sector 35-C',6,128,'160035','Rajeev Anand','anandlawoffice2378@gmail.com',9417870805,1722622364,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0153','Wave Estate Project','M/s Country Colonizers Pvt Ltd Through its MD','customercare@waveestate.in',0,0,'PO Rayon and Silk Mills','Adjoining Coca Cola Depot GT Road, Chheharta',28,39,'143105','0','M/s Country Colonizers Pvt Ltd. Wave Estate Project site office sector 85','SAS Nagar Mohali',28,507,'140308','1','<p>The Complainant booked Apartment 66 FF, Sector G, Wave Floor, Sector 99 Mohali on 21.03.2013 making initial payment (Annexure C-1). Agreement dated 19.07.2013 (Annexure C-2) was executed with Respondent for saleable area 1060sqFt @ 3773.58/sqFt. As per Clause 5.2, the Project was to be developed and the Apartment was to be handed over in 24 months and by Cl. 5.5 the delay entailed Rs. 5/sqFt/month for delay. On 20.01.2014, the Complainant was made to fill another Agreement (Annexure C-3), the Apartment was unilaterally changed by issuing a letter (Annexure C-4) with new number 42/FF, Wave Floor Sector 99, Mohali (Relocated Apartment). \r\n</p><p>The Complainant took a Loan (Annexure C-5) for the unit. The Complainant found that site plan has been changed of the Apartment by changing bathroom door opening in bedroom etc.. Having found the Project and the Apartment delayed, the Complainant gave a representation 11.01.2017 (Annexure C-6) that construction started with 2 years delay and not completed. The complainant gave another representation dated 05.08.2017 (Annexure C-7) that even after 4 1/2 years possession not offered. On 03.09.2017 (Annexure C-8) the Complainant wanted to meet the senior executive but no time was given for meeting for delivery of possession. The Complainant upon interest liability and EMI burden spent his life savings and repaid loan on 01.03.2017 (Annexure C-9).    \r\n</p><p>Now the offer of possession is made in third week of Oct 2018, but the Apartment is incomplete. The apartment was to be completed by 19.01.2016 but not done against which Complainant gave representation dated 23.09.2017 (Annexure C-10). The Respondent made a unilateral Deed of Settlement on 16.12.2017 (Annexure C-11) to give interest &amp; also give possession by March 2018 but since not honoured by Respondent, the Deed of Settlement became redundant. \r\n</p><p>Now On 14.08.2018 (Annexure C-12) a Statement of Account has been given wherein area increased and money charged without any increase in Apartment</p>','<p style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:4.7pt;margin-left:0cm;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">The Apartment was to be handed over after\r\ncompleting the Project in 24 months + 6 Months i.e. from 23.07.2013 by\r\n23.01.2016. Even the monthly compensation of Rs5/SqFt/month was to be paid from\r\nJanuary 2016 onwards till date NOT PAID.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:4.7pt;margin-left:0cm;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">The Respondent&nbsp;has taken the total\r\nsale price in advance at the time of signing of Agreement to the tune of Rs. 3\r\nLakhs (+Service Tax) on 05.02.2013 and 3 lakhs(+Service Tax)&nbsp;&nbsp;on\r\n21.03.2013+ Rs 968658 (+Service Tax) on 05.02.2015 + Rs 231342 (+ Service Tax)\r\non 31.03.2015+ 1055264/- (+ service Tax) on 16.11.2015 +Rs. 144736/- (+ service\r\nTax) on 16.11.2015+ 559382/- lakhs (+ service Tax) on 18.06.2016 + 40618 (+\r\nservice Tax) on 14.06.2016, totaling 36 Lakhs (+ service Tax) as also EMIs with\r\ninterest.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">The possession of\r\nthe Apartment was to be given to the Applicant / Allottee within 24 + 6 = 30\r\nmonths. Inspite of elapsing of over 5 years of Agreement, no development and\r\nconstruction works have been completed in the Complex and the Respondent\r\nPromoter has failed in its obligation towards the Complex and Independent\r\nResidential Floor allotted to the Applicant. The Promoter is liable to pay the\r\ninterest on the payment so received for the period of delay in offering\r\npossession after the completion of the development works of the project and the\r\ncompletion of the construction of the Independent Residential Floor. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:4.7pt;margin-left:0cm;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">In view of the above : <o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:4.7pt;margin-left:0cm;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">(i) The Applicant / Allottee is seeking\r\ncompensation as applicable in Para 5.5 of Agreement dated 19.07.2013 from\r\nJanuary 2016 onwards till date; <o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">(ii) directions for completion of the development works of the project\r\nand the construction of the independent residential floor in question without\r\nany further delay and also offer the possession after the grant of Occupation\r\nCertificate of the Building and the Completion Certificate of the Wave Estate\r\nProject alongwith interest and compensation prescribed under Real Estate\r\n(Regulation and Development) Act 2016 as the action of the Respondents.</span><br></p>',4000000.00,3600000.00,'2016-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:\r\njustify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;line-height:200%;mso-layout-grid-align:\r\nnone;text-autospace:none\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">The\r\nrespondents be directed to complete the development works of the project and\r\nthe construction of the independent residential floor in question without any\r\nfurther delay and also offer the possession after the grant of occupation\r\ncertificate of the Building and the Completion Certificate of the Wave Estate\r\nProject.&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px;\">The Promoter be also\r\ndirected to pay interim monthly interest and compensation till the completion\r\nof the project and the complex in question in the pendency of the complaint.</span></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','2013-07-23 00:00:00','Independent Residential Floor Bearing No. 43/FF in Sector 99','','',1,1,0,0,'RajeevAnand','2018-11-10 11:29:21.000','RajeevAnand','2018-11-10 11:29:21.000'),(277,1105,'1105',1180,'61e07eb0-c813-4129-a767-52572ef143fe','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-11-10 13:29:01.000','Narendra  Bahadur kharya','amitshri1983@gmail.com',9910532073,0,0,'B-501, Kartik Kunj Apartments','Plot No. D-13, Sector 44, Noida',33,216,'201303','1','B-501, Kartik Kunj Apartments','Plot No. D-13, Sector 44, Noida',33,216,'201303','Amit Kumar Srivastav and Umesh Chauhan','amitshri1983@gmail.com',9910532073,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-JAL11-PMO1111','Ludhiana City Centre','M/s Today Homes & Infrastructure Pvt. Ltd','contact@todayhomes.co.in',0,0,'Upper Ground Floor 8 to 9, Pragati Tower, Rajendra Place, New Delhi – 110008','',10,120,'110008','1','Upper Ground Floor 8 to 9, Pragati Tower, Rajendra Place, New Delhi – 110008','',10,120,'110008','1','<p>a)That the complainant is a law-abiding citizen of India and residing at the above said address and presently working in USA and residing in USA.\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>b)That the complaint is being preferred by the GPA (General Power of Attorney) Mr. Surendra Kumar Kharya who is the real brother of the complainant and the complainant executed GPA in favour of his brother Mr. Surendra Bahadur Kharya on 8.04.2011 for taking any action or filing case on his behalf in the interest of his property in all over India. Copy of GPA dated 08/04/2011 is annexed herewith as Annexure-1.\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>c)That the complainant approached to the Respondent in 2006 for booking of an office space in newly introduced project of the respondent as “Ludhiana City Centre” Situated at Plot No. 476, Citizen Road, Shaheed Bhagat Singh Nagar, Ludhiana, Punjab-141001,  and the respondent allotted  Unit no. 538, Super built area 1239.24 sq.ft in consideration the complainant paid booking amount of Rs. 4,00,000/- (Rupees Four Lakh Only) on 05.05.2006 vide cheque no.434680 to the respondent and submit booking form for the said booking. Copy of booking form and copy of cheque dated 05.05.2006 is annexed herewith as Annexure- 1. \r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>d)That the complainant further paid Rs. 53,784/- on 02.07.2006 and Rs. 5,50,000/- on 05.07.2006 vide Cheque no.353627, dated 02.07.2006 and vide cheque No. 353781 dated 05.07.2006. Copy of cheque dated 02.07.2006 and 05.07.2006 is annexed herewith as Annexure-3 (colly).\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>e)That this booking was done at the pre launch stage and the complainant advised that the unit will be allot after getting all approval and sanction plan from the concern Authority. That it was informed by the respondent that this project is a premium project and all the approvals will come soon. \r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>f)That on the good faith on the respondent and Govt. complainant kept waiting for the further update from the respondent but it was very depressing for the complainant that after making payment of a huge amount he has  not received any</p>','<p class=\"MsoBodyText\" style=\"margin-left:54.0000pt;text-indent:-36.0000pt;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; font-size: 14pt;\">I.&nbsp;</span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"mso-spacerun:\'yes\';font-family:\'Times New Roman\';line-height:200%;font-size:14.0000pt;\">direct the respondent to refund the entire paid amount to the complainant and consequently pay to the complainant an amount of Rs. 10,03,784/- (Rupees &nbsp;Ten Lakhs Three Thousand Seven Hundred Eighty Four Only) with interest @ 18% per annum calculated from the date of respective deposit till the date of actual realization;</span><span style=\"mso-spacerun:\'yes\';font-family:\'Times New Roman\';line-height:200%;font-size:14.0000pt;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoBodyText\" style=\"margin-left:54.0000pt;text-indent:-36.0000pt;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; font-size: 14pt;\">II.&nbsp;</span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"mso-spacerun:\'yes\';font-family:\'Times New Roman\';line-height:200%;font-size:14.0000pt;\">award cost of &nbsp;litigation of Rs.1 lac in favour of the complainant and against the respondent; and </span><span style=\"mso-spacerun:\'yes\';font-family:\'Times New Roman\';line-height:200%;font-size:14.0000pt;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoBodyText\" style=\"margin-left:54.0000pt;text-indent:-36.0000pt;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; font-size: 14pt;\">III.&nbsp;</span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"mso-spacerun:\'yes\';font-family:\'Times New Roman\';line-height:200%;font-size:14.0000pt;\">pass such other and further order(s) as this Hon’ble Regulatory Authority may deem fit and proper in the facts and circumstances of the present case;</span><span style=\"mso-spacerun:\'yes\';font-family:\'Times New Roman\';line-height:200%;font-size:14.0000pt;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>',0.00,0.00,'2009-11-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p class=\"MsoBodyText\" style=\"margin-left:54.0000pt;text-indent:-36.0000pt;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; font-size: 14pt;\">I.&nbsp;</span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"mso-spacerun:\'yes\';font-family:\'Times New Roman\';line-height:200%;font-size:14.0000pt;\">direct the respondent to refund the entire paid amount to the complainant and consequently pay to the complainant an amount of Rs. 10,03,784/- (Rupees &nbsp;Ten Lakhs Three Thousand Seven Hundred Eighty Four Only) with interest @ 18% per annum calculated from the date of respective deposit till the date of actual realization;</span><span style=\"mso-spacerun:\'yes\';font-family:\'Times New Roman\';line-height:200%;font-size:14.0000pt;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoBodyText\" style=\"margin-left:54.0000pt;text-indent:-36.0000pt;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; font-size: 14pt;\">II.&nbsp;</span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"mso-spacerun:\'yes\';font-family:\'Times New Roman\';line-height:200%;font-size:14.0000pt;\">award cost of &nbsp;litigation of Rs.1 lac in favour of the complainant and against the respondent; and </span><span style=\"mso-spacerun:\'yes\';font-family:\'Times New Roman\';line-height:200%;font-size:14.0000pt;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoBodyText\" style=\"margin-left:54.0000pt;text-indent:-36.0000pt;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; font-size: 14pt;\">III.&nbsp;</span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"mso-spacerun:\'yes\';font-family:\'Times New Roman\';line-height:200%;font-size:14.0000pt;\">pass such other and further order(s) as this Hon’ble Regulatory Authority may deem fit and proper in the facts and circumstances of the present case;</span><span style=\"mso-spacerun:\'yes\';font-family:\'Times New Roman\';line-height:200%;font-size:14.0000pt;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',1,1,0,0,'Umesh','2018-11-10 13:18:32.000','Umesh','2018-11-10 13:18:32.000'),(278,1106,'1106',1205,'bdf116c7-892a-4e63-949e-5384dd531181','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-11-12 10:40:13.000','DHARMINDER KUMAR','dharminder.sethi@gmail.com',9646012355,0,945054656287,'# 1535','SECTOR 18D',6,128,'160018','1','SCO 106-107','SECTOR 17C',6,128,'160017','','',0,0,'Allottee','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0067','CITY OF DREAMS/CREDO ASSETS PRIVATE LIMITED[SBP GROUP}','Mr. Sheeshpal Thakur','cod@sbpgroup.in',9216771145,0,'SCO 146-148','1ST FLOOR, SECTOR 43B',6,128,'160043','1','SCO 146-148','1ST FLOOR, SECTOR 43B',6,128,'160043','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Dear Sir</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">My name is Dharminder Kumar and I had booked a 2 BHK flat in\r\na project name City of Dreams under Credo Assets Private Limited a subsidiary of\r\nSBP Group {Singla Builders &amp; Promoters} situated at Sector 116,\r\nLandran-Kharar Road Mohali, Punjab on dated 18<sup>th</sup> May, 2018.</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">I had given an amount of Rs. 15000/- as advance amount to\r\nbook the above said flat on dated 16<sup>th</sup> May, 2018 through NEFT from\r\nmy saving bank account.</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">But later on due to some personal issues I had cancelled the\r\nflat on dated 1<sup>st</sup> July, 2018 through written communication on whats\r\napp for which I also have the proof, after my cancellation communication the\r\ncompany dealing person said that he will send the reimbursement form at my e\r\nmail but in spite three reminders he didn’t send me the reimbursement form.</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Later on when I pressurize him to share the form he sent it\r\non my email id on dated 25<sup>th</sup> October. 2018 and I fill the form, notarized\r\nit and submitted it within three days at their office.</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">But now they are refusing to payback my Rs. 15000/- as they\r\nare saying that refund is possible within 60 days as per company policy, but as\r\nper my communication I had cancelled the flat well before time and further more\r\nthey didn’t tell about any type of policy while booking the flat, moreover they\r\nAssured me that i can take my money back at any point of time if I don’t want\r\nto final it.</p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">I request the PBRERA to help me to get back my Rs. 15000/-\r\non immediately basis and also take strict legal action against Credo Assets\r\nPrivate Limited Under SBP Group.</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Sincerly</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Dharminder Kumar</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">+91-9646012355</p>','<p>I want my Rs. 15000/- back on immediate basis and i also want that PBRERA take strict legal action against the Credo Assets Private Limited of SBP Group</p>',2790000.00,15000.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Please direct credo assets private limited {SBP Group} to payback Rs. 15000/- on immediate basis.</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',1,1,0,0,'dharminder123','2018-11-10 16:14:56.000','dharminder123','2018-11-10 16:14:56.000'),(279,1107,'1107',1201,'d13879ef-66b7-4eba-aca7-a4e1732b278f','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-11-13 11:39:20.000','RAVINDER KUMAR MAHAN','dr.ravindermahan05@gmail.com',9876748037,0,588375995207,'5324 B','SECTOR 38 WEST',6,128,'160014','1','5324 B','SECTOR 38 WEST',6,128,'160014','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0255','SUNNY ENCLAVE/AMAZON CITY','MR JARNAIL SINGH BAJWA','bajwadeveloperltd@gmail.com',9814014381,0,'M/S BAJWA DEVELOPERS LTD','SUNNY BUSSINESS CENTRE,5TH FLOOR,NEW SUNNY ENCLAVE,KHARAR,SAS NAGAR,MOHALI',28,507,'140301','1','M/S BAJWA DEVELOPERS LTD','SUNNY BUSSINESS CENTRE,5TH FLOOR,NEW SUNNY ENCLAVE,KHARAR,SAS NAGAR,MOHALI',28,507,'140301','1','<p>I bought a plot No. 810 in sector 123 ,New sunny Enclave,Mohali  being developed and sold by BDL. This plot was registered in my name in Dec 2016. To buy the said plot i raised a loan of rupees.17.10 Lacs from PNB.As i am living in a rented accommodation, I bought this plot to build my own house and move and save on rent which would have been helpful to pay the EMI of the loan raised. After getting the registration done i visited the office BDL to get the physical possession of the plot. I was shocked to learn that  this particular plot was not demarcated and plot was falling in the land of some farmer. Due to this there was no road, sewerage or water connection possible in this area. I was asked by the developer to wait.  I had no option but to wait. After making several rounds of the office I decided to meet the proprietor,Mr Bajwa. I explained to him, how i was incurring financial losses and mental harassment due to their wrongdoing and fraudulent sale of plots to innocent public. Mr Bajwa told me that plot will be cleared in few weeks. I had no option but to wait..After waiting for 18months I was asked to deposit the possession fee and get the possession. In compliance with their demand I deposited the said fee and was purportedly given the possession of plot.  As I wanted to start construction I took my Contracter to the site and started digging for foundation.. During this the villagers and land owners of that area gathered at the spot and forced us to stop the construction. According to them my plot area was encroaching the revenue road leading to their fields. I had to stop the construction work.. I contacted BDL office to visit the site and give my a clear plot so that I could resume the construction.. Mr Bajwa and his staff visited the site and did some adjustments, the plot is still encroaching upon the berm.Now the situation is that I have the paper possession(from last 2 years) of plot but I cannot start the constuction .</p>','<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:\'Gurmukhi MN\';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"> I have been duped by Mr Jarnail Singh Bajwa, because although i am a registered owner of the said plot but Bajwa developers have failed to deliver me the said plot. Because i raised a loan of rupees 17.10 lacs for this plot, i am also paying interest @14500 pm from last two years. As i am living in a rented accommodation and paying a rent of rupees 20000 PM and this is also causing lot of financial burden on me. Had i been given the possession of plot in time, I would have constructed my own house and shifted in that by now. </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><font face=\"Gurmukhi MN\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px; white-space: pre-wrap;\">In addition to that i am loosing on the rent i would have earned by renting out the additional area of my house. i also spent money on planning by paying to various architects. I paid fee to GMADA to get the plan approved. i also paid advance to contractor 100000 to start the construction. I spent rupees 10000 for bhumi poojan of the said plot. </span></font></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><font face=\"Gurmukhi MN\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><br></span></font></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:\'Gurmukhi MN\';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\">It is clear from the above that Mr Jarnail singh Bajwa through his company Bajwa Developers Limited has caused me huge financial losses, and also put me through mental agony and mental harassment by duping me of my hard earned money and fraudulently selling me a plot status of which is &nbsp;still in jeopardy.</span></p><p><b style=\"font-weight:normal;\" id=\"docs-internal-guid-e744d878-7fff-a193-7758-366fa250a130\"><br></b></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:\'Gurmukhi MN\';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\">I pray to you that strict action should be taken against Mr Bajwa in order to get my PLOT along with interest and other losses refunded as soon as possible. An FIR should be &nbsp;got registered against him and his licence should be cancelled  for duping me of my hard earned money and to desist him from looting the innocent public of their hard earned money.</span></p><p></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:\'Gurmukhi MN\';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><div><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:\'Gurmukhi MN\';color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><br></span></div>',0.00,0.00,'2016-12-26 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>interim relief should be awarded according to the following details</p><p>1. loss due to payment of&nbsp; rent for last 2 years: 480000</p><p>2. loss due to payment of interest on housing loan: 35000</p><p>3. loss of income from rent i would have earned: 720000</p><p>4. loss due to expenditure on planning fee to architect etc. : 150000</p><p>5. loss due to advance payment to contractor : 100000</p><p>6. fee paid to GMADA for approval of plan: 60000</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>;-</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',1,0,0,0,'ravindermahan','2018-11-10 16:26:27.000','ravindermahan','2018-11-10 16:26:27.000'),(280,1108,'1108',1098,'81775a1c-ad46-40a6-b51a-c95cca91809d','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-11-13 10:29:38.000','Abhimanyu Singh Vinayak','abhi.vinayak@yahoo.co.in',9992015557,0,0,'44-45 SHIVAJI PARK','MODEL TOWN',13,21,'135001','1','T-1, 301, BESTECH PARK VIEW RESIDENCES','SECTOR 66',28,507,'160062','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PM0004','JLPL Falcon View Apartments, Phase-2, Tower C to H, Sector 66, Mohali - Punjab','JANTA LAND PROMOTERS PVT LTD','janta@jantahousing.com',8427100082,0,'Regd. Office and Corporate Office : SCO 39-42, Sector 82,','SAS Nagar, Mohali, Punjab',28,507,'140306','1','Regd. Office and Corporate Office : SCO 39-42, Sector 82,','SAS Nagar, Mohali, Punjab',28,507,'140306','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:18.0pt;line-height:115%\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">In compliance with the orders of the Hon’ble\r\nAdjudicating Officer, passed on 1-11-18, in my Complaint No. AdCNo10222018,\r\nwhereby my complaint seeking compensation and interest has been returned. While\r\napplying circular No. RERA/Pb/ENF/14 dated 29.10.18 to my complaint, with\r\nRetrospective effect, I have been advised to file fresh complaint in Form M, which\r\nI hereby do.</span><o:p></o:p></span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">\r\n\r\n</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:18.0pt;line-height:115%\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">In my capacity as KARTA of Abhimanyu\r\nSingh Vinayak HUF, I, purchased an apartment from M/s. Janta Land Promoters Pvt\r\nLtd. The apartment Unit No. is 101, Tower D, Falcon View, sized 3122 sq ft. The\r\ntotal cost of the property was fixed at Rs.96,17,477/- Plus taxes. I paid\r\nRs.96,43,228/- including taxes, to the company. I paid Rs.84,35,750/- vide\r\nReceipt No. 6518 dated 13/8/2016, Rs.11,12,000/- vide Receipt No. 3104 dated\r\n13/8/2016 &amp; Rs.95,478/- vide Receipt No. 6826 dated 28/9/2016.Thus I\'ve\r\npaid 96% of the Total consideration amount. The Company, vide Allotment Letter\r\ndated 13/08/2016, promised to complete construction &amp; handover the\r\napartment in 12 months. Thus the effective date of possession was\r\n13/08/2017.Unfortunately, despite having paid 96% of the total amount, the\r\ncompany has failed to deliver the possession of the flat. Thus our joint family\r\nis compelled to live separately. My parents live in Yamunanagar whereas I,\r\nalong with my wife &amp; son live in Mohali in a small accommodation. We have\r\nbeen compelled to compromise with our comfort &amp; our future plannings. I\'ve\r\nbeen running from pillar to post to get the true status of construction &amp;\r\nthe date of actual possession, but to no avail. The office bearers of the\r\ncompany refuse to entertain my requests &amp; divulge any relevant information.\r\nI\'ve sent dozens of e-mails to the company &amp; its top officials, for\r\nconfirming the date of possession &amp; for seeking compensation for inordinate\r\ndelay. I\'ve visited the company office score of times but all my pleadings fall\r\non deaf ears.&nbsp;</span><o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">That as per the allotment cum agreement, the company is charging penal interest from the buyers @10% for delay of first month, @12% for delay of second month &amp; @15% for delay thereafter. Whereas, after having paid Rs.96,43,228/- to the company, I\'ve merely received one cheque for Rs.44,413/- dated 12-2-18 from the Company/Builder, which amounts to 0.46% for years of delay.\r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Thus I seek parity &amp; equity between the interest paid by the buyer &amp; the interest paid by the builder company. The interest that the builder/company ought to pay should be at par with what they charge from the helpless buyers. Here it also worth mentioning that during this entire period of inordinate delay, there has not been any force majure or circumstances beyond the control of the developers, behind which the company might try to hide &amp; wriggle out from discharge of their lawful liability. HERE, I ALSO WISH TO BRING TO YOUR KIND NOTICE, TWO OTHER VERY IMPORTANT FACTORS, REGARDING WHICH THE CAUSE OF ACTION HAS NOT YET ARISEN, BUT IF THE COMPANY/BUILDER DELAYS FURTHER, I MAY SUFFER HUGE LOSSES IN THE FUTURE. Firstly : That I sold my industrial unit on 12 August 2016 &amp; purchased this apartment on 13 August 2016.Thus I saved Long Term Capitals Gain Tax . As per I.T. Act, if I do not get possession of new residential property in 36 months from date of sale of industrial unit, I shall have to return, entire LTCG Tax Rebate availed, with interest, which in my case may be about Rs.15 Lac Loss, for no fault of mine. Secondly : That Punjab Government has given a rebate of 3% on stamp duty for registrations till 31-3-2019. If the company delays in possession, I may suffer another loss of about Rs.3 Lac. However, I reserve my right to approach appropriate legal forums to recover these losses, if &amp; when they occur. RELIEF SOUGHT IN THE PRESENT COMPLAINT : I seek interest as per the relevant provisions of RERA, for inordinate delay in possession, after having paid 96% of the total amount i.e.Rs.96,43,228/-</span></p>',9617477.00,9643228.00,'2017-08-13 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:18.0pt;line-height:115%\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">That during the pendency of this\r\npresent complaint, if the builder secures occupation certificate and offers\r\npossession to the buyers, the builder be directed to handover the possession to\r\nme, without forcing or coercing me to withdraw the present complaint. In that\r\ncase, the builder/company may kindly be directed to deliver possession, pending\r\nfinal outcome/award.</span><o:p></o:p></span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">\r\n\r\n</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:18.0pt;line-height:115%\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">It is also prayed that since I have\r\nalready paid 96% of the total sale consideration, the builder be directed not\r\nto ask for any more amount until final order in this present complaint is\r\npassed by the Hon’ble Authority.&nbsp;</span><o:p></o:p></span></p>','1','','2016-08-13 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Flat No.101, Tower-D, Falcon View, Sector 66-A, Mohali-Punjab.','','',2,0,0,0,'rachnabhi','2018-11-12 21:16:39.000','rachnabhi','2018-11-12 21:16:39.000'),(281,1109,'1109',1211,'962b01f9-ce50-4ce8-b650-bb1037f1b9e3','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-11-13 15:31:31.000','Yuvraj Verma','vermauvraj@gmail.com',9650106013,0,0,'Flat No .112, Ground Floor, Noor Homes','Kharar Landranroad, Sector 111, Mohali',28,507,'160055','1','Flat No .112, Ground Floor, Noor Homes','Kharar Landranroad, Sector 111, Mohali',28,507,'160055','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0219','Noor Homes, Sector 115, Village Santemajra,\r\nTehsil Kharar, SAS\r\nNagar, Mohali','M/s. GGP Buildtech Private Limited','ajayguptaggp@gmail.com',9815990640,9056607575,'Mr. Ajay Gupta, # 402, Shivalik City, Sector 127','Kharar, SAS Nagar, Mohali',28,507,'160055','1','Mr. Ajay Gupta, # 402, Shivalik City, Sector 127','Kharar, SAS Nagar, Mohali',28,507,'160055','1','<ol><li><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">That the project named Noor Homes is currently being promoted/developed by GGP Buildtech Pvt Limited.&nbsp;</span></li><li>The Promoters of M/s GGP BUILDTECH PVT LTD started their business initially with a Partnership firm M/s Singla Builders &amp; Promoters in which Sh. Ajay Gupta and Sh. Amandeep Singla were partners. </li><li>That the Project Named Noor Homes is launched by GGP Buildtech Pvt Limited in February 2014. </li><li>That the Builder (GGP Buildtech Pvt Limited) had come up with advertisement/public offer to sell 1, 2, 3 BHK Apartments &amp; 3 BHK Villas to be constructed at Sector 115, Village Sante Majra, Tehsil Kharar, District Mohali with a construction target to be completed in 2017. </li><li>That the Complainants (society members) start booking flats from Builder from 2014. </li><li>That to some Complainants the flats were forcefully handed over by builder in incomplete stage. </li><li>That some Complainants were forced to pay 100% payment to Builder for incomplete flats by threatening them from goons hired by builders. </li><li>That Some Complainants were forced to execute sale deed for less price paying money in cash or for shell companies (Daya Infra) and thus frauding with GST and service tax.</li><li>That These flats are incomplete to such extent that there is no permanent water connection,internal roads, electricity, sewerage connections, Sewerage treatment plant, staircase, streetlights, fire protection system etc.</li><li>That these flats are handed over without obtaining occupancy certificate from MC kharar</li><li>That Builder was approached time to time and several MOM’s were signed but till date.</li><li>That MOM is attached as Annexure-1, where in Builder has initially agreed to complete the project by 31-March 2016.</li><li>That vide MOM dated 30-April-2017 Builder agreed to complete the project by 31-Jan-2018.\r\n</li><li>\r\nThat again MOM vide 18.09.2017 Builder agreed to complete project in next 6 months i.e Mar-2018.&nbsp;</li><li>\r\nThat status of project is same&nbsp; as mentioned in point No.9</li></ol>','<p><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-fb04cf99-7fff-ac21-7c10-02d06f896346\"></span></p><ol style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><ol style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:lower-alpha;font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial;color:#666666;background-color:#ffffff;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial;color:#666666;background-color:#ffffff;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\">Direct PSPCL for permanent electricity connections for the 65 families (Complainant).</span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:lower-alpha;font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial;color:#666666;background-color:#ffffff;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial;color:#666666;background-color:#ffffff;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\">Direct MC kharar for permanent water and sewerage connections to the society.</span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:lower-alpha;font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial;color:#666666;background-color:#ffffff;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial;color:#666666;background-color:#ffffff;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\">Direct Inquiry against involvement of Municipal Corporation with Builder in cheating the Public by allowing sale deed to be executed without issuing occupancy certificate.</span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:lower-alpha;font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial;color:#666666;background-color:#ffffff;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial;color:#666666;background-color:#ffffff;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;white-space:pre-wrap;\">Direct Inquiry against Builder regarding diversion of project funds to other shell companies.</span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:lower-alpha;font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial;color:#666666;background-color:#ffffff;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;text-align: justify;\