ular bearing no. RERA/Pb/.ENF/14 dated 29.10.2018 , relevant is item no. 7.4 i.e. Role of the Adjudicating officer in the context of complaint in form \'M\' and \'N\'.&nbsp;</p><p>5 That the complaint may be revived from the same stage where the above Complaint no. ADC/1011/2018 instituted on 31.08.2018 is returned vide order dated 02.11.2018 in the interest of justice and complainant\'s interest since no prejudice will be caused to either of the parties.</p><p>6 Any other relief temporary or be it permanent which this authority may deem fit may also be granted in the favour of complainant.&nbsp;</p>','1','','2016-08-26 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Plot no. 165/Park Facing, Sector 118-119, Gateway City, S.A.S Nagar, Mohali- 160055','','',1,1,0,0,'Satish','2018-11-15 22:57:43.000','Satish','2018-11-15 22:57:43.000'),(307,1119,'1119',1206,'2cb8b1e2-1fc2-489e-8344-754c96cec127','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','ANITA JULIET SINGH','avsinghtima@yahoo.com',9839007280,0,0,'FLAT NO 303, BLOCK A-1, NIRMAL CHHAYA TOWERS,','V.I.P. ROAD, ZIRAKPUR',28,507,'140603','1','FLAT NO 303, BLOCK A-1, NIRMAL CHHAYA TOWERS,','V.I.P. ROAD, ZIRAKPUR',28,507,'140603','mandeep singh khillan','mandeepkhillan@gmail.com',9779525511,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PC0010','chandigarh city centre','citi center developers','info@chandigarhciticenter.in',9023490234,0,'chandigarh citi center vip road Zirakpur','',28,507,'140603','1','chandigarh citi center vip road Zirakpur','',28,507,'140603','1','<p>abcc</p>','<p>acbcb</p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>adsd</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'ANITAJULIETSINGH','2018-11-16 15:41:14.000','ANITAJULIETSINGH','2018-11-16 15:41:14.000'),(308,1119,'1119',1206,'2cb8b1e2-1fc2-489e-8344-754c96cec127','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','ANITA JULIET SINGH','avsinghtima@yahoo.com',9839007280,0,0,'FLAT NO 303, BLOCK A-1, NIRMAL CHHAYA TOWERS,','V.I.P. ROAD, ZIRAKPUR',28,507,'140603','1','FLAT NO 303, BLOCK A-1, NIRMAL CHHAYA TOWERS,','V.I.P. ROAD, ZIRAKPUR',28,507,'140603','mandeep singh khillan','mandeepkhillan@gmail.com',9779525511,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PC0010','chandigarh city centre','citi center developers','info@chandigarhciticenter.in',9023490234,0,'chandigarh citi center vip road Zirakpur','',28,507,'140603','1','chandigarh citi center vip road Zirakpur','',28,507,'140603','1','<p>FACTS</p><ul><li>The Respondent No.1 is a partnership firm and Resp. No.2 and 3 are its partners who are developing commercial project Chandigarh Citi Centre at VIP Road, Zirakpur. Both the partners are in control of the Project and are managing the business of Firm&nbsp;</li><li>The Complainant was allotted SCO No.12A, LGF, Block A vide Agreement to Sell dated 09.10.2015 subject to payment of 49.00 Lakhs by the Respondent.&nbsp;</li><li>The Complainant have paid Rs. 51,55,100 to the Respondent including all amounts demanded other than basic price.&nbsp;</li><li>Possession as per agreement was to be handover on or before 8th April, 2018 complete in all respects.&nbsp;</li><li>It was agreed that Common Area Maintenance CAM shall be within 3 Rs. Per Sq.Ft. and as car parking was not allotted as such no charges were fixed or agreed for car parking.</li></ul><p>GREVIANCE</p><ul><li>The Respondent has failed to given possession as per Agreement to Sell inspite of full consideration having been paid.&nbsp;</li><li>The Respondent are demanding CAM Charges at the rate of Rs. 10 per Sq. Ft. and that too to be paid in advance for 2 years for the period 01.01.2019 to 31.12.2020 whereas the same was agreed on monthly basis and cannot be demanded otherwise.&nbsp;</li><li>The Respondent are demanding Car Parking Maintenance Charges and that too to be paid in advance for 2 years for the period 01.01.2019 to 31.12.2020 which was never agreed</li><li>The Common Area Maintenance Charges being demanded &amp; the services being proposed to be provided are not in conformity with the provisions of per section 11 4 d of RERA Act as prima facie they appear to be neither essential services nor the charges are reasonable charges.&nbsp;</li><li>The Respondents have neither explained the utility of services being offered to the Complainants for which CAM Charges are being levied neither have explained how the CAM Charges have been arrived at or how the CAM&nbsp; Charges have been allocated to the various units including unsold units with the Respondent.&nbsp;</li></ul>','<p>acbcb</p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>adsd</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'ANITAJULIETSINGH','2018-11-16 15:53:38.000','ANITAJULIETSINGH','2018-11-16 15:53:38.000'),(309,1119,'1119',1206,'2cb8b1e2-1fc2-489e-8344-754c96cec127','FormTypeM',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','ANITA JULIET SINGH','avsinghtima@yahoo.com',9839007280,0,0,'FLAT NO 303, BLOCK A-1, NIRMAL CHHAYA TOWERS,','V.I.P. ROAD, ZIRAKPUR',28,507,'140603','1','FLAT NO 303, BLOCK A-1, NIRMAL CHHAYA TOWERS,','V.I.P. ROAD, ZIRAKPUR',28,507,'140603','mandeep singh khillan','mandeepkhillan@gmail.com',9779525511,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PC0010','chandigarh city centre','citi center developers','info@chandigarhciticenter.in',9023490234,0,'chandigarh citi center vip road Zirakpur','',28,507,'140603','1','chandigarh citi center vip road Zirakpur','',28,507,'140603','1','<p>FACTS</p><ul><li>The Respondent No.1 is a partnership firm and Resp. No.2 and 3 are its partners who are developing commercial project Chandigarh Citi Centre at VIP Road, Zirakpur. Both the partners are in control of the Project and are managing the business of Firm&nbsp;</li><li>The Complainant was allotted SCO No.12A, LGF, Block A vide Agreement to Sell dated 09.10.2015 subject to payment of 49.00 Lakhs by the Respondent.&nbsp;</li><li>The Complainant have paid Rs. 51,55,100 to the Respondent including all amounts demanded other than basic price.&nbsp;</li><li>Possession as per agreement was to be handover on or before 8th April, 2018 complete in all respects.&nbsp;</li><li>It was agreed that Common Area Maintenance CAM shall be within 3 Rs. Per Sq.Ft. and as car parking was not allotted as such no charges were fixed or agreed for car parking.</li></ul><p>GREVIANCE</p><ul><li>The Respondent has failed to given possession as per Agreement to Sell inspite of full consideration having been paid.&nbsp;</li><li>The Respondent are demanding CAM Charges at the rate of Rs. 10 per Sq. Ft. and that too to be paid in advance for 2 years for the period 01.01.2019 to 31.12.2020 whereas the same was agreed on monthly basis and cannot be demanded otherwise.&nbsp;</li><li>The Respondent are demanding Car Parking Maintenance Charges and that too to be paid in advance for 2 years for the period 01.01.2019 to 31.12.2020 which was never agreed</li><li>The Common Area Maintenance Charges being demanded &amp; the services being proposed to be provided are not in conformity with the provisions of per section 11 4 d of RERA Act as prima facie they appear to be neither essential services nor the charges are reasonable charges.&nbsp;</li><li>The Respondents have neither explained the utility of services being offered to the Complainants for which CAM Charges are being levied neither have explained how the CAM Charges have been arrived at or how the CAM&nbsp; Charges have been allocated to the various units including unsold units with the Respondent.&nbsp;</li></ul>','<p>acbcb</p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>adsd</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'ANITAJULIETSINGH','2018-11-16 15:54:22.000','ANITAJULIETSINGH','2018-11-16 15:54:22.000'),(310,1120,'1120',1206,'2cb8b1e2-1fc2-489e-8344-754c96cec127','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','ANITA JULIET SINGH','avsinghtima@yahoo.com',9839007280,0,0,'FLAT NO 303, BLOCK A-1, NIRMAL CHHAYA TOWERS,','V.I.P. ROAD, ZIRAKPUR',28,507,'140603','1','VIP Road','111',28,507,'140603','Mandeep','mandeepkhillan@gmail.com',9779525511,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PC0010','Chanidgarh Citi Center','Citi Center Developers','info@chandigarhciticenter.in',9023490234,0,'CCC VIP Road Zirakpur','',28,507,'140603','1','CCC VIP Road Zirakpur','',28,507,'140603','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><b>FACTS<o:p></o:p></b></p><ul><li style=\"text-align: justify;\">The\r\nRespondent No.1 is a partnership firm and Resp. No.2 and 3 are its partners who\r\nare developing commercial project, Chandigarh Citi Centre at VIP Road,\r\nZirakpur. Both partners are in complete control of the management &amp; day to\r\nday business of Firm </li><li style=\"text-align: justify;\">The\r\nComplainant was allotted SCO No.12A, LGF, Block A vide Agreement to Sell dated\r\n09.10.2015 subject to payment of 49.00 Lakhs by the Respondent. </li><li style=\"text-align: justify;\">The\r\nComplainant have paid Rs. 51,55,100 to the Respondent including all amounts\r\ndemanded other than basic price. </li><li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Possession\r\nas per agreement was to be handover on or before 8th April, 2018 complete in\r\nall respects. </li><li style=\"text-align: justify;\">It\r\nwas agreed that Common Area Maintenance CAM shall be within 3 Rs. Per Sq.Ft.\r\nand as car parking was not allotted &amp; was in common area as such no charges\r\nwere fixed or agreed for car parking &amp; its maintenance comes under CAM.</li></ul><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><b>GREVIANCE<o:p></o:p></b></p><ul><li style=\"text-align: justify;\">The\r\nRespondent has failed to given possession as per ATS inspite of full\r\nconsideration having been paid. </li><li style=\"text-align: justify;\">The\r\nRespondent are demanding CAM Charges at the rate of Rs. 10 per Sq. Ft. and that\r\ntoo to be paid in advance for 2 years from 01.01.2019 to 31.12.2020 whereas the\r\nsame was agreed on monthly basis. </li><li style=\"text-align: justify;\">The\r\nRespondent are demanding Car Parking Maintenance Charges and that too to be\r\npaid in advance for 2 years for the period 01.01.2019 to 31.12.2020 which was\r\nnever agreed as comes under CAM</li><li style=\"text-align: justify;\">The\r\nCommon Area Maintenance Charges being demanded and the services being proposed\r\nto be provided are not in conformity with the provisions of per section 11, 4, &nbsp;d &nbsp;of\r\nRERA Act as prima facie they appear to be neither essential services nor the\r\ncharges are reasonable charges. </li><li>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</li><li style=\"text-align: justify;\">The\r\nRespondents have neither explained the utility of services being offered to the\r\nComplainants for which CAM Charges are being levied neither have explained how\r\nthe CAM Charges have been arrived at or how the CAM Charges have been allocated\r\nto the individual units.&nbsp;</li></ul>','<ul><li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Direct\r\nthe Respondent to handover the possession of the unit allotted to the\r\nComplainant at earliest complete in all respects after obtaining completion\r\ncertificate for the whole project.</li><li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Further\r\nset aside the arbitrary demands of the Respondent mentioned as under </li><li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Charging\r\nof Common Area Maintenance Charges at the rate of Rs. 10 per Sq. Ft.</li><li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Demand\r\nof 2 years advance Common Area Maintenance Charges and Car Parking Maintenance\r\nCharges from 01.01.2019 to 31.12.2020 being illegal and ultra vires of the\r\nAgreement to Sell. The identical issue has already been dealt by this Honourable Authority in the matter of Jai Gopal Mahajan Vs Barnala Builders and Property\r\nConsultants, Comp. No. 44&nbsp; 1268 of 2017 &nbsp;vide order dated 12 02 2018 wherein it was\r\nheld that the builder cannot make a coercive demand for prepayment of any\r\nfuture liability as the maintenance charges are leviable on monthly basis.</li><li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Direct\r\nthe Respondent to demarcate, define the essential services for common area;\r\nscope of essential services for common area; mechanism of budgeting and\r\nallocation of common area maintenance charges and reason ability of charges as\r\nintended by the legislature vide Section 11, 4 ,d &nbsp;of the Act and in the event they fail to do so\r\nor act arbitrary, indulgence of this Honourable&nbsp;Authority is sought for the same. </li><li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Further\r\npass necessary orders, directions directing the Respondent to pay the monthly\r\ninterest as per section 18 of the Act to the Complainant for the delayed period\r\ni.e. period post expiry of 30 months as per the agreement till the actual and\r\nphysical handing over of the possession of the allotted unit at the prescribed\r\nrates.</li><li>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</li><li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Pass\r\nany other order or direction which this Honourable Authority thinks fit and\r\nnecessary for adjudication of the present complaint in interest of justice and\r\nequity.</li></ul>',4900000.00,5155100.00,'2018-04-08 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<ul><li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Restrain\r\nthe Respondent from imposing any penalty, interest, holding charges etc. under\r\nwhatever name they may refer and intimated vide letter dated 1.11.18, 9.11.18,\r\nas the Complainant have paid the complete amount in all respects and is ready\r\nand willing to take the possession and pay the Common Area Maintenance Charges\r\nas per agreed rates as mentioned in Agreement to Sell only, to be charged only\r\nfrom the date of handing over of the actual physical possession of the unit\r\nwhich should be complete in all respects and in a totally completed project.\r\nWhereas the Respondent are not ready to give the possession until the arbitrary\r\nand illegal demands of payment of 2 years advance Common Area Maintenance\r\nCharges at the arbitrary rates of Rs. 10 per Sq.Ft. and the Car Parking\r\nMaintenance Charges are met with which are otherwise illegal and ultra vires to\r\nthe Agreement to Sell. Even otherwise the Complainants have under protest and\r\ndue to the coercion and threat of cancellation have submitted the PDC for the\r\nsame vide letter dated 12.11.18.</li><li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Restrain\r\nthe Respondents from Cancelling the allotment of the unit allotted to the\r\nComplainant as intended vide their letter dated 01.11.2018 and or further\r\nallotting the same to any third party or further creating any third party\r\nright, charge or lien over the allotted unit.</li><li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Charging\r\nany charges including Common Area Maintenance Charges under which ever head\r\ntill the actual physical possession of the allotted unit is handed over to the\r\nComplainant, complete in all respects in the completed project and even\r\nthereafter not in excess of the rate agreed, till the adjudication of the\r\npresent complainant.</li><li>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</li><li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Not\r\nto en cash the cheques issued against CAM Charges by the Complainant under\r\ncoercion and threat and under protest vide letter dated 12 11 2018 till\r\ndisposal of this complaint.</li></ul>','1','','2015-10-09 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','SCO 12A Block A LGF','','',2,0,0,0,'ANITAJULIETSINGH','2018-11-17 08:08:44.000','ANITAJULIETSINGH','2018-11-17 08:08:44.000'),(311,1119,'1119',1206,'2cb8b1e2-1fc2-489e-8344-754c96cec127','FormTypeM',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','ANITA JULIET SINGH','avsinghtima@yahoo.com',9839007280,0,0,'FLAT NO 303, BLOCK A-1, NIRMAL CHHAYA TOWERS,','V.I.P. ROAD, ZIRAKPUR',28,507,'140603','1','FLAT NO 303, BLOCK A-1, NIRMAL CHHAYA TOWERS,','V.I.P. ROAD, ZI