r Sq.Ft.\r\nand as car parking was not allotted &amp; was in common area as such no charges\r\nwere fixed or agreed for car parking &amp; its maintenance comes under CAM.</li></ul><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><b>GREVIANCE<o:p></o:p></b></p><ul><li style=\"text-align: justify;\">The\r\nRespondent has failed to given possession as per ATS inspite of full\r\nconsideration having been paid. </li><li style=\"text-align: justify;\">The\r\nRespondent are demanding CAM Charges at the rate of Rs. 10 per Sq. Ft. and that\r\ntoo to be paid in advance for 2 years from 01.01.2019 to 31.12.2020 whereas the\r\nsame was agreed on monthly basis. </li><li style=\"text-align: justify;\">The\r\nRespondent are demanding Car Parking Maintenance Charges and that too to be\r\npaid in advance for 2 years for the period 01.01.2019 to 31.12.2020 which was\r\nnever agreed as comes under CAM</li><li style=\"text-align: justify;\">The\r\nCommon Area Maintenance Charges being demanded and the services being proposed\r\nto be provided are not in conformity with the provisions of per section 11, 4, &nbsp;d &nbsp;of\r\nRERA Act as prima facie they appear to be neither essential services nor the\r\ncharges are reasonable charges. </li><li>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</li><li style=\"text-align: justify;\">The\r\nRespondents have neither explained the utility of services being offered to the\r\nComplainants for which CAM Charges are being levied neither have explained how\r\nthe CAM Charges have been arrived at or how the CAM Charges have been allocated\r\nto the individual units.&nbsp;</li></ul>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\">RELIEF\r\nSOUGHT</p><ul><li style=\"text-align: justify;\">The\r\nComplainant prays for grant of the following Relief by passing of directions,\r\norders which this Hon’ble Authority deems fit and appropriate </li><li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Direct\r\nthe Respondent to handover the possession of the unit allotted to the\r\nComplainant at earliest complete in all respects after obtaining completion\r\ncertificate for the whole project.</li><li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Further\r\nset aside the arbitrary demands of the Respondent mentioned as under </li><li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Charging\r\nof Common Area Maintenance Charges at the rate of Rs. 10 per Sq. Ft.</li><li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Demand\r\nof 2 years advance Common Area Maintenance Charges and Car Parking Maintenance\r\nCharges from 01.01.2019 to 31.12.2020 being illegal and ultra vires of the\r\nAgreement to Sell. The identical issue has already been dealt by this Hon’ble\r\nAuthority in the matter of Jai Gopal Mahajan Vs Barnala Builders and Property\r\nConsultants, Comp. No. 44 1268 of 2017 vide order dated 12.02.2018 wherein it\r\nwas held that the builder cannot make a coercive demand for prepayment of any\r\nfuture liability as the maintenance charges are leviable on monthly basis.</li><li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Direct\r\nthe Respondent to demarcate, define the essential services for common area;\r\nscope of essential services for common area; mechanism of budgeting and\r\nallocation of common area maintenance charges and reasonability of charges as\r\nintended by the legislature vide Section 11, 4 ,d &nbsp;of the Act and in the event they fail to do so\r\nor act arbitrary, indulgence of this Hon’ble Authority is sought for the same. </li><li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Further\r\npass necessary orders, directions directing the Respondent to pay the monthly\r\ninterest as per section 18 of the Act to the Complainant for the delayed period\r\ni.e. period post expiry of 30 months as per the agreement till the actual and\r\nphysical handing over of the possession of the allotted unit at the prescribed\r\nrates.</li><li>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</li><li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Pass\r\nany other order or direction which this Hon’ble Authority thinks fit and\r\nnecessary for adjudication of the present complaint in interest of justice and\r\nequity.</li></ul>',4900000.00,5155100.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<ul><li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Restrain\r\nthe Respondent from imposing any penalty, interest, holding charges etc. under\r\nwhatever name they may refer and intimated vide letter dated 1.11.18, 9.11.18,\r\nas the Complainant have paid the complete amount in all respects and is ready\r\nand willing to take the possession and pay the Common Area Maintenance Charges\r\nas per agreed rates as mentioned in Agreement to Sell only, to be charged only\r\nfrom the date of handing over of the actual physical possession of the unit\r\nwhich should be complete in all respects and in a totally completed project.\r\nWhereas the Respondent are not ready to give the possession until the arbitrary\r\nand illegal demands of payment of 2 years advance Common Area Maintenance\r\nCharges at the arbitrary rates of Rs. 10 per Sq.Ft. and the Car Parking\r\nMaintenance Charges are met with which are otherwise illegal and ultra vires to\r\nthe Agreement to Sell. Even otherwise the Complainants have under protest and\r\ndue to the coercion and threat of cancellation have submitted the PDC for the\r\nsame vide letter dated 12.11.18.</li><li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Restrain\r\nthe Respondents from Cancelling the allotment of the unit allotted to the\r\nComplainant as intended vide their letter dated 01.11.2018 and or further\r\nallotting the same to any third party or further creating any third party\r\nright, charge or lien over the allotted unit.</li><li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Charging\r\nany charges including Common Area Maintenance Charges under which ever head\r\ntill the actual physical possession of the allotted unit is handed over to the\r\nComplainant, complete in all respects in the completed project and even\r\nthereafter not in excess of the rate agreed, till the adjudication of the\r\npresent complainant.</li><li>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</li><li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Not\r\nto en cash the cheques issued against CAM Charges by the Complainant under\r\ncoercion and threat and under protest vide letter dated 12.11.2018 till\r\ndisposal of this complaint.</li></ul>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',1,0,0,0,'ANITAJULIETSINGH','2018-11-17 09:47:20.000','ANITAJULIETSINGH','2018-11-17 09:47:20.000'),(318,1121,'1121',1217,'73a53831-3543-4742-8333-59abaf5f88cd','FormTypeM',1,1,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Anil Vivan  Singh','mandeepkhillan@gmail.com',9779525511,0,0,'A1 303 Nirmal Chhaya Towers VIP Road Zirakpur','',28,507,'140603','1','A1 303 Nirmal Chhaya Towers VIP Road Zirakpur','',28,507,'140603','Mandeep Singh Khillan','mandeepkhillan@gmail.com',9779525511,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PC0010','CCC Zirakpur','Citi Center Developers','info@chandigarhciticenter.in',9023490234,0,'CCC VIP road Zirakpur','',28,507,'140603','1','CCC VIP road Zirakpur','',28,507,'140603','1','<ul type=\"disc\">FACTS</ul><ul><li><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>The Respondent No.1 is a partnership firm and\r\n     Resp. No.2 and 3 are its partners who are developing commercial project,\r\n     Chandigarh Citi Centre at VIP Road, Zirakpur. Both partners are in\r\n     complete control of the management &amp; day to day business of Firm</span></li><li><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>The Complainant was allotted SCO No.9, LGF,\r\n     Block A vide Agreement to Sell dated 10.03.2015 subject to payment of 33.50\r\n     Lakhs by the Respondent. </span></li><li><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>The Complainant have paid Rs. 35,15,542 to the\r\n     Respondent including all amounts demanded other than basic price</span><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>Possession as per agreement was to be handover\r\n     on or before 09.09.17 complete in all respects. </span></li><li><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>It was agreed that Common Area Maintenance CAM\r\n     shall be within 3 Rs. Per Sq.Ft. and as car parking was not allotted &amp;\r\n     was in common area as such no charges were fixed or agreed for car parking\r\n     &amp; its maintenance comes under CAM.</span><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'><br></span></li><li><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'><br></span></li><li><b><span style=\'margin: 0px; color: black; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>GREVIANCE</span></b><span style=\'margin: 0px; color: black; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 7pt;\'></span></li><li><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>The Respondent has failed to given possession\r\n     as per ATS inspite of full consideration having been paid. </span></li><li><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>The Respondent are demanding CAM Charges at\r\n     the rate of Rs. 10 per Sq. Ft. and that too to be paid in advance for 2\r\n     years from 01.01.2019 to 31.12.2020 whereas the same was agreed on monthly\r\n     basis. </span></li><li><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>The Respondent are demanding Car Parking\r\n     Maintenance Charges and that too to be paid in advance for 2 years for the\r\n     period 01.01.2019 to 31.12.2020 which was never agreed as comes under CAM</span></li><li><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>The Common Area Maintenance Charges being\r\n     demanded and the services being proposed to be provided are not in\r\n     conformity with the provisions of per section 11, 4, &nbsp;d &nbsp;of RERA\r\n     Act as prima facie they appear to be neither essential services nor the\r\n     charges are reasonable charges. </span></li><li><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>The Respondents have neither explained the\r\n     utility of services being offered to the Complainants for which CAM\r\n     Charges are being levied neither have explained how the CAM Charges have\r\n     been arrived at or how the CAM Charges have been allocated to the\r\n     individual units.&nbsp;</span></li>\r\n</ul><p>\r\n\r\n<b></b><i></i><u></u><sub></sub><sup></sup><strike></strike><font face=\"Times New Roman\"></font><br></p>','<p>The Complainant prays for grant of the following Relief by passing of directions, orders which this Hon’ble Authority deems fit and appropriate&nbsp; </p><ul><li>Direct the Respondent to handover the possession of the unit allotted to the Complainant at earliest complete in all respects after obtaining completion certificate for the whole project.&nbsp;</li><li>Further set aside the arbitrary demands of the Respondent mentioned as under &nbsp;</li><li>Charging of Common Area Maintenance Charges at the rate of Rs. 10 per Sq. Ft.&nbsp;</li><li>Demand of 2 years advance Common Area Maintenance Charges and Car Parking Maintenance Charges from 01.01.2019 to 31.12.2020 being illegal and ultra vires of the Agreement to Sell. The identical issue has already been dealt by this Hon’ble Authority in Jai Gopal Mahajan Vs Barnala Builders and Property Consultants, Comp. No. 44 1268 of 2017 vide order dated 12.02.2018 wherein it was held that the builder cannot make a coercive demand for prepayment of any future liability as the maintenance charges are leviable on monthly basis.&nbsp;</li><li>Direct the Respondent to demarcate, define the essential services for common area; scope of essential services for common area; mechanism of budgeting and allocation of common area maintenance charges and reasonability of charges as intended by the legislature vide Section 11, 4 ,d&nbsp; of the Act and in the event they fail to do so or act arbitrary, indulgence of this Hon’ble Authority is sought for the same. &nbsp;</li><li>Further pass necessary orders, directions directing the Respondent to pay the monthly interest as per section 18 of the Act to the Complainant for the delayed period i.e. period post expiry of 30 months as per the agreement till the actual and physical handing over of the possession of the allotted unit at the prescribed rates.&nbsp;</li><li>Award cost including litigation Cost&nbsp;</li><li>Pass any other order or direction which this Hon’ble Authority thinks fit and necessary for adjudication of the present complaint in interest of justice and equity</li></ul>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>\r\n\r\n</p><ul type=\"disc\">\r\n <li style=\'margin: 0px 0px 13.33px; text-align: justify; color: black; line-height: normal; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 7pt; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400;\'><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>Restrain the Respondent from imposing any\r\n     penalty, interest, holding charges etc. under whatever name they may refer\r\n     and intimated vide letter dated 1.11.18, 9.11.18, as the Complainant have\r\n     paid the complete amount in all respects and is ready and willing to take\r\n     the possession and pay the Common Area Maintenance Charges as per agreed\r\n     rates as mentioned in Agreement to Sell only, to be charged only from the\r\n     date of handing over of the actual physical possession of the unit which\r\n     should be complete in all respects and in a totally completed project.\r\n     Whereas the Respondent are not ready to give the possession until the\r\n     arbitrary and illegal demands of payment of 2 years advance Common Area\r\n     Maintenance Charges at the arbitrary rates of Rs. 10 per Sq.Ft. and the\r\n     Car Parking Maintenance Charges are met with which are otherwise illegal\r\n     and ultra vires to the Agreement to Sell. Even otherwise the Complainants\r\n     have under protest and due to the coercion and threat of cancellation have\r\n     submitted the PDC for the same vide letter dated 12.11.18.</span></li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">\r\n </span><li style=\'margin: 0px 0px 13.33px; text-align: justify; color: black; line-height: normal; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 7pt; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400;\'><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>Restrain the Respondents from Cancelling the\r\n     allotment of the unit allotted to the Complainant as intended vide their\r\n     letter dated 01.11.2018 and or further allotting the same to any third\r\n     party or further creating any third party right, charge or lien over the\r\n     allotted unit.</span></li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">\r\n </span><li style=\'margin: 0px 0px 13.33px; text-align: justify; color: black; line-height: normal; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 7pt; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400;\'><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>Charging any charges including Common Area\r\n     Maintenance Charges under which ever head till the actual physical\r\n     possession of the allotted unit is handed over to the Complainant,\r\n     complete in all respects in the completed project and even thereafter not\r\n     in excess of the rate agreed, till the adjudication of the present\r\n     complainant.</span></li><li style=\'margin: 0px 0px 13.33px; text-align: justify; color: black; line-height: normal; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 7pt; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400;\'><span style=\'margin: 0px; color: black; line-height: 115%; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>Not to encash the cheques issued against CAM Charges by the Complainant\r\nunder coercion and threat and under protest vide letter dated 12.11.2018 till\r\ndisposal of this complaint.</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"></span><b></b><i></i><u></u><sub></sub><sup></sup><strike></strike><br></li></ul>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'AnilVivanSingh','2018-11-17 10:24:26.000','AnilVivanSingh','2018-11-17 10:24:26.000'),(319,1122,'1122',1215,'5a742e73-25d2-42df-a9b7-b464b77d9442','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','GURDARSHAN  SAINI','sainigs62@gmail.com',9876765688,0,622031176082,'C # 18','PACL OLD COLONY',28,501,'140126','1','C # 18','PACL OLD COLONY',28,501,'140126','NA','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0271','ANSAL PROPERTIES & INFRASTRUCTURE LTD','Himanshu Pant','himanshu@ansalapi.com',9899882126,0,'SCO 183-184, FIRST FLOOR, SEC 9C , CHANDIGARH','',28,507,'160009','1','SCO 183-184, FIRST FLOOR, SEC 9C , CHANDIGARH','',28,507,'160009','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:16.0pt;line-height:115%\">I have\r\nbooked flat No B – 244 ( Ground Floor) in Golf Link -11 Victoria Floor , Sec\r\n116 , Mohali from M/S Ansal &nbsp;Properties\r\n&amp; Infrastructure Ltd&nbsp; Chandigarh on\r\n30<sup>th</sup> Dec , 2013 under Subvention Scheme, and builder is supposed to\r\nhand over flat within stipulated time of 36 months as per agreement i.e 30<sup>th</sup>\r\nDec 2016. Initial I have deposited Rs 14,03, 445/ and balance take loan from\r\nHDFC, Chandigarh Rs 35 lacs . So far builder has not given possession as the\r\nsame flat is not yet completed for possession.&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:16.0pt;line-height:115%\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; On the other hand builder\r\npromised to hand over completed flat no B – 254 (First Floor),&nbsp; but same also not given so far. My deposited\r\nwith Ansal &nbsp;&nbsp;Properties Rs 14,03,445/ is kept without any\r\ncompensation in shape of interest and my loan is still pending . Had the\r\npossession given at right time, lot of money in shape of EMI could have been\r\npaid to the lender bank.&nbsp; As no response\r\nis received from builder, thereby I have no option to file a case with RERA.\r\nNow the builder is not picking the phone and not available to resolve the\r\nissue. I have to go abroad in 2 months, so I am very much concern to take\r\npossession of flat.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><u><span style=\"font-size:16.0pt;line-height:115%\">Relief sought<o:p></o:p></span></u></b></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><b><span style=\"font-size:16.0pt;line-height:115%\">Relief Grant</span></b><span style=\"font-size:16.0pt;line-height:115%\"> :</span> <span style=\"font-size:\r\n16.0pt;line-height:115%\">Bank is pressurizing&nbsp;\r\nfor EMI , whereas&nbsp; I neither have\r\nflat nor my money which I deposited has been used so far. I have not yet\r\nreceived flat , otherwise I have returned my EMI for&nbsp; 3 years. I should get handsome compensation\r\nfor the amount which I deposited Rs 14,03,445/</span>&nbsp;&nbsp; <span style=\"font-size:16.0pt;line-height:\r\n115%\">in shape of prevailing rate of interest .</span> </p>',4850000.00,1403445.00,'2016-12-30 00:00:00.000','2017-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><b><u><span style=\"font-size:16.0pt;line-height:115%\">Interim relief<o:p></o:p></span></u></b></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:16.0pt;\r\nline-height:115%\">1.&nbsp; I should pay\r\nhandsome amount of compensation in lieu of amount deposited of Rs 14,03,445/\r\nand I have paid Rs 4 lac extra in the initial deposit than actual should have\r\nbeen deposited as per norms of agreement for purchase of flat and &nbsp;compensation on that also be given.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','1','','2013-12-30 00:00:00','2013-12-30 00:00:00','B -234 (GROUND FLOOR), GOLF LINK 11\r\n VICTORIA FLOOR, SECTOR 116, MOHALI , SAS NAGAR','','',1,0,0,0,'GURMEET','2018-11-17 10:31:33.000','GURMEET','2018-11-17 10:31:33.000'),(320,1123,'1123',1218,'fc7cffe1-0d0a-43d5-82bb-eae26e26997f','FormTypeM',1,1,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Vandna  Singh','mandeepkhillan@gmail.com',9779525511,0,0,'A1 303 VIP Road Nirmal Chhaya towers','Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','1','A1 303 VIP Road Nirmal Chhaya towers','Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','Mandeep Singh Khillan','mandeepkhillan@gmail.com',9779525511,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PC0010','Chandigarh Citi Center','Citi Centre Developers','info@chandigahciticenter.in',9023490234,0,'CCC VIP Road, Zirakpur','',28,507,'140603','1','CCC VIP Road, Zirakpur','',28,507,'140603','0','<p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 6.66px; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;\"><b><span style=\'margin: 0px; color: black; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>FACTS</span></b><span style=\'margin: 0px; color: black; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 7pt;\'></span></p><ul><li><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>The Respondent No.1 is a partnership firm and\r\n     Resp. No.2 and 3 are its partners who are developing commercial project,\r\n     Chandigarh Citi Centre at VIP Road, Zirakpur. Both partners are in\r\n     complete control of the management &amp; day to day business of Firm </span></li><li><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>The Complainant was allotted SCO No.13, LGF,\r\n     Block A vide Agreement to Sell dated 30.04.2016 subject to payment of\r\n     49.00 Lakhs by the Respondent. </span></li><li><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>The Complainant have paid Rs. 5155100 to the\r\n     Respondent including all amounts demanded other than basic price. </span></li><li><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>Possession as per agreement was to be handover\r\n     on or before 29.10.2018 complete in all respects.&nbsp;</span><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'><br></span></li><li><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>It was agreed that Common Area Maintenance CAM\r\n     shall be within 3 Rs. Per Sq.Ft. and as car parking was not allotted &amp;\r\n     was in common area as such no charges were fixed or agreed for car parking\r\n     &amp; its maintenance comes under CAM.</span></li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">\r\n</span></ul><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">\r\n\r\n</span></p><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 6.66px; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;\"><b><span style=\'margin: 0px; color: black; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>GREVIANCE</span></b><span style=\'margin: 0px; color: black; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 7pt;\'></span></p><ul><li><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>The Respondent has failed to given possession\r\n     as per ATS inspite of full consideration having been paid. </span></li><li><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>The Respondent are demanding CAM Charges at\r\n     the rate of Rs. 10 per Sq. Ft. and that too to be paid in advance for 2\r\n     years from 01.01.2019 to 31.12.2020 whereas the same was agreed on monthly\r\n     basis. </span></li><li><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>The Respondent are demanding Car Parking\r\n     Maintenance Charges and that too to be paid in advance for 2 years for the\r\n     period 01.01.2019 to 31.12.2020 which was never agreed as comes under CAM</span></li><li><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>The Common Area Maintenance Charges being\r\n     demanded and the services being proposed to be provided are not in\r\n     conformity with the provisions of per section 11, 4, &nbsp;d &nbsp;of RERA\r\n     Act as prima facie they appear to be neither essential services nor the\r\n     charges are reasonable charges. </span></li><li><span style=\'margin: 0px; color: black; line-height: 115%; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>The Respondents have neither explained the utility of services being\r\noffered to the Complainants for which CAM Charges are being levied neither have\r\nexplained how the CAM Charges have been arrived at or how the CAM Charges have\r\nbeen allocated to the individual units.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"></span><b></b><i></i><u></u><sub></sub><sup></sup><strike></strike><br></li></ul>','<ul><li><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>The Complainant prays for grant of the\r\n     following Relief by passing of directions, orders which this Hon’ble\r\n     Authority deems fit and appropriate </span></li><li><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>Direct the Respondent to handover the\r\n     possession of the unit allotted to the Complainant at earliest complete in\r\n     all respects after obtaining completion certificate for the whole project.</span></li><li><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>Further set aside the arbitrary demands of the\r\n     Respondent mentioned as under </span></li><li><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>Charging of Common Area Maintenance Charges at\r\n     the rate of Rs. 10 per Sq. Ft.</span></li><li><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>Demand of 2 years advance Common Area\r\n     Maintenance Charges and Car Parking Maintenance Charges from 01.01.2019 to\r\n     31.12.2020 being illegal and ultra vires of the Agreement to Sell. The\r\n     identical issue has already been dealt by this Hon’ble Authority in the\r\n     matter of Jai Gopal Mahajan Vs Barnala Builders and Property Consultants,\r\n     Comp. No. 44 1268 of 2017 vide order dated 12.02.2018 wherein it was held\r\n     that the builder cannot make a coercive demand for prepayment of any\r\n     future liability as the maintenance charges are leviable on monthly basis.</span></li><li><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>Direct the Respondent to demarcate, define the\r\n     essential services for common area; scope of essential services for common\r\n     area; mechanism of budgeting and allocation of common area maintenance\r\n     charges and reasonability of charges as intended by the legislature vide\r\n     Section 11, 4 ,d &nbsp;of the Act and in the event they fail to do so or\r\n     act arbitrary, indulgence of this Hon’ble Authority is sought for the\r\n     same. </span></li><li><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>Further pass necessary orders, directions\r\n     directing the Respondent to pay the monthly interest as per section 18 of\r\n     the Act to the Complainant for the delayed period i.e. period post expiry\r\n     of 30 months as per the agreement till the actual and physical handing\r\n     over of the possession of the allotted unit at the prescribed rates.</span></li><li><font face=\'\"roboto\",\"serif\"\'><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>Award cost including litigation Cost</span></font></li><li><font face=\'\"roboto\",\"serif\"\'>P<span style=\"margin: 0px; color: black; line-height: 115%; font-size: 14px;\">ass any other order or direction which this Hon’ble Authority thinks\r\nfit and necessary for adjudication of the present complaint in interest of\r\njustice and equity.</span></font><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"></span><b></b><i></i><u></u><sub></sub><sup></sup><strike></strike><br></li></ul>',4900000.00,5155100.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>\r\n\r\n<br></p><ul><li style=\"margin: 0px 0px 13.33px 24px; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\'margin: 0px; color: black; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>Restrain the Respondent from imposing any penalty,\r\ninterest, holding charges etc. under whatever name they may refer and intimated\r\nvide letter dated 1.11.18, 9.11.18, as the Complainant have paid the complete\r\namount in all respects and is ready and willing to take the possession and pay\r\nthe Common Area Maintenance Charges as per agreed rates as mentioned in\r\nAgreement to Sell only, to be charged only from the date of handing over of the\r\nactual physical possession of the unit which should be complete in all respects\r\nand in a totally completed project. Whereas the Respondent are not ready to\r\ngive the possession until the arbitrary and illegal demands of payment of 2\r\nyears advance Common Area Maintenance Charges at the arbitrary rates of Rs. 10\r\nper Sq.Ft. and the Car Parking Maintenance Charges are met with which are\r\notherwise illegal and ultra vires to the Agreement to Sell. Even otherwise the\r\nComplainants have under protest and due to the coercion and threat of\r\ncancellation have submitted the PDC for the same vide letter dated 12.11.18.</span></li><li style=\"margin: 0px 0px 13.33px 24px; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\'margin: 0px; color: black; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>Restrain the Respondents from Cancelling the\r\nallotment of the unit allotted to the Complainant as intended vide their letter\r\ndated 01.11.2018 and or further allotting the same to any third party or\r\nfurther creating any third party right, charge or lien over the allotted unit.</span></li><li style=\"margin: 0px 0px 13.33px 24px; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\'margin: 0px; color: black; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>Charging any charges including Common Area\r\nMaintenance Charges under which ever head till the actual physical possession\r\nof the allotted unit is handed over to the Complainant, complete in all\r\nrespects in the completed project and even thereafter not in excess of the rate\r\nagreed, till the adjudication of the present complainant.</span></li><li style=\"margin: 0px 0px 13.33px 24px; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\'margin: 0px; color: black; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>Not to encash the cheques issued against CAM\r\nCharges by the Complainant under coercion and threat and under protest vide\r\nletter dated 12.11.2018 till disposal of this complaint.</span></li></ul><p>\r\n\r\n<b></b><i></i><u></u><sub></sub><sup></sup><strike></strike><font face=\"Times New Roman\"></font><br></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'Vandnasingh','2018-11-17 11:13:14.000','Vandnasingh','2018-11-17 11:13:14.000'),(321,1120,'1120',1206,'2cb8b1e2-1fc2-489e-8344-754c96cec127','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-11-18 08:22:08.000','ANITA JULIET SINGH','avsinghtima@yahoo.com',9839007280,0,0,'FLAT NO 303, BLOCK A-1, NIRMAL CHHAYA TOWERS, Zirakpur','V.I.P. ROAD, ZIRAKPUR',28,507,'140603','1','FLAT NO 303, BLOCK A-1, NIRMAL CHHAYA TOWERS, Zirakpur','V.I.P. ROAD, ZIRAKPUR',28,507,'140603','Mandeep','mandeepkhillan@gmail.com',9779525511,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PC0010','Chanidgarh Citi Center','Citi Center Developers','info@chandigarhciticenter.in',9023490234,0,'Chandigarh Citi Center  VIP Road Zirakpur','',28,507,'140603','1','Chandigarh Citi Center  VIP Road Zirakpur','',28,507,'140603','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><b>FACTS<o:p></o:p></b></p><ul><li style=\"text-align: justify;\">The\r\nRespondent No.1 is a partnership firm and Resp. No.2 and 3 are its partners who\r\nare developing commercial project, Chandigarh Citi Centre at VIP Road,\r\nZirakpur. Both partners are in complete control of the management &amp; day to\r\nday business of Firm </li><li style=\"text-align: justify;\">The\r\nComplainant was allotted SCO No.12A, LGF, Block A vide Agreement to Sell dated\r\n09.10.2015 subject to payment of 49.00 Lakhs by the Respondent. </li><li style=\"text-align: justify;\">The\r\nComplainant have paid Rs. 51,55,100 to the Respondent including all amounts\r\ndemanded other than basic price. </li><li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Possession\r\nas per agreement was to be handover on or before 8th April, 2018 complete in\r\nall respects. </li><li style=\"text-align: justify;\">It\r\nwas agreed that Common Area Maintenance CAM shall be within 3 Rs. Per Sq.Ft.\r\nand as car parking was not allotted &amp; was in common area as such no charges\r\nwere fixed or agreed for car parking &amp; its maintenance comes under CAM.</li></ul><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><b>GREVIANCE<o:p></o:p></b></p><ul><li style=\"text-align: justify;\">The\r\nRespondent has failed to given possession as per ATS inspite of full\r\nconsideration having been paid. </li><li style=\"text-align: justify;\">The\r\nRespondent are demanding CAM Charges at the rate of Rs. 10 per Sq. Ft. and that\r\ntoo to be paid in advance for 2 years from 01.01.2019 to 31.12.2020 whereas the\r\nsame is illegal and was agreed on monthly basis. </li><li style=\"text-align: justify;\">The\r\nRespondent are demanding Car Parking Maintenance Charges and that too to be\r\npaid in advance for 2 years for the period 01.01.2019 to 31.12.2020 which was\r\nnever agreed as comes under CAM</li><li style=\"text-align: justify;\">The\r\nCommon Area Maintenance Charges being demanded and the services being proposed\r\nto be provided are not in conformity with the provisions of per section 11, 4, &nbsp;d &nbsp;of\r\nRERA Act as prima facie many of them are neither essential services nor the\r\ncharges are reasonable.&nbsp;</li><li style=\"text-align: justify;\">The\r\nRespondents have neither explained the utility of services being offered to the\r\nComplainants for which CAM Charges are being levied neither have explained how\r\nthe CAM Charges have been arrived at or how the CAM Charges have been allocated\r\nto the individual units.&nbsp;</li></ul>','<ul><li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Direct\r\nthe Respondent to handover the possession of the unit allotted to the\r\nComplainant at earliest complete in all respects after obtaining completion\r\ncertificate for the whole project.</li></ul><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Further\r\nset aside the arbitrary demands of the Respondent mentioned as under </p><ul><li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Charging\r\nof Common Area Maintenance Charges at the rate of Rs. 10 per Sq. Ft.</li><li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Demand\r\nof 2 years advance Common Area Maintenance Charges and Car Parking Maintenance\r\nCharges from 01.01.2019 to 31.12.2020 being illegal and ultra vires of the\r\nAgreement to Sell. The identical issue has already been dealt by this Honourable Authority in the matter of Jai Gopal Mahajan Vs Barnala Builders and Property\r\nConsultants, Comp. No. 44&nbsp; 1268 of 2017 &nbsp;vide order dated 12 02 2018 wherein it was\r\nheld that the builder cannot make a coercive demand for prepayment of any\r\nfuture liability as the maintenance charges are leviable on monthly basis.</li><li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Direct\r\nthe Respondent to demarcate, define the essential services for common area, scope of essential services for common area, mechanism of budgeting and\r\nallocation of common area maintenance charges and reasonability of charges as\r\nintended by the legislature vide Section 11, 4 ,d &nbsp;of the Act &amp; Annex A of Act and in the event they fail to do so\r\nor act arbitrary, indulgence of this Honourable&nbsp;Authority is sought for the same. </li><li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Further\r\npass necessary orders, directions directing the Respondent to pay the monthly\r\ninterest as per section 18 of the Act to the Complainant for the delayed period\r\ni.e. period post expiry of 30 months as per the agreement till the actual and\r\nphysical handing over of the possession of the allotted unit at the prescribed\r\nrates.</li><li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Pass\r\nany other order or direction which this Honourable Authority thinks fit and\r\nnecessary for adjudication of the present complaint in interest of justice and\r\nequity.</li></ul>',4900000.00,5155100.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<ul><li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Restrain\r\nthe Respondents from imposing any penalty, interest, holding charges etc. under\r\nwhatever name they may refer and intimated vide letter dated 1.11.18, 9.11.18,\r\nas the Complainant have paid the complete amount in all respects and is ready\r\nand willing to take the possession and pay the Common Area Maintenance Charges\r\nas per agreed rates as mentioned in Agreement to Sell only, to be charged only\r\nfrom the date of handing over of the actual physical possession of the unit\r\nwhich should be complete in all respects and in a totally completed project.\r\nWhereas the Respondent are not ready to give the possession until the arbitrary\r\nand illegal demands of payment of 2 years advance Common Area Maintenance\r\nCharges at the arbitrary rates of Rs. 10 per Sq.Ft. and the Car Parking\r\nMaintenance Charges are met with which are otherwise illegal and ultra vires to\r\nthe Agreement to Sell. Even otherwise the Complainants have under protest and\r\ndue to the coercion and threat of cancellation have submitted the PDC for the\r\nsame vide letter dated 12.11.18.</li><li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Restrain\r\nthe Respondents from Cancelling the allotment of the unit allotted to the\r\nComplainant as intended vide their letter dated 01.11.2018 and or further\r\nallotting the same to any third party or further creating any third party\r\nright, charge or lien over the allotted unit.</li><li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Charging\r\nany charges including Common Area Maintenance Charges under which ever head\r\ntill the actual physical possession of the allotted unit is handed over to the\r\nComplainant, complete in all respects in the completed project and even\r\nthereafter not in excess of the rate agreed, till the adjudication of the\r\npresent complainant.</li><li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Not\r\nto encash the cheques issued against CAM Charges by the Complainant under\r\ncoercion and threat and under protest vide letter dated 12 11 2018 till\r\ndisposal of this complaint.</li></ul>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','SCO 12A Block A LGF','','',1,1,0,0,'ANITAJULIETSINGH','2018-11-18 08:20:32.000','ANITAJULIETSINGH','2018-11-18 08:20:32.000'),(322,1121,'1121',1217,'73a53831-3543-4742-8333-59abaf5f88cd','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-11-18 08:44:16.000','Anil Vivan  Singh','mandeepkhillan@gmail.com',9779525511,0,0,'A1 303 Nirmal Chhaya Towers VIP Road Zirakpur','',28,507,'140603','1','A1 303 Nirmal Chhaya Towers VIP Road Zirakpur','',28,507,'140603','Mandeep Singh Khillan','mandeepkhillan@gmail.com',9779525511,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PC0010','CCC Zirakpur','Citi Center Developers','info@chandigarhciticenter.in',9023490234,0,'CCC VIP road Zirakpur','',28,507,'140603','1','CCC VIP road Zirakpur','',28,507,'140603','1','<ul><li><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>The Respondent No.1 is a partnership firm and\r\n     Resp. No.2 and 3 are its partners who are developing commercial project,\r\n     Chandigarh Citi Centre at VIP Road, Zirakpur. Both partners are in\r\n     complete control of the management &amp; day to day business of Firm</span></li><li><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>The Complainant was allotted SCO No.9, LGF,\r\n     Block A vide Agreement to Sell dated 10.03.2015 subject to payment of 33.50\r\n     Lakhs by the Respondent. </span></li><li><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>The Complainant have paid Rs. 35,15,542 to the\r\n     Respondent including all amounts demanded other than basic price </span><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>Possession as per agreement was to be handover\r\n     on or before 09.09.17 complete in all respects. </span></li><li><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>It was agreed that Common Area Maintenance CAM\r\n     shall be within 3 Rs. Per Sq.Ft. and as car parking was not allotted &amp;\r\n     was in common area as such no charges were fixed or agreed for car parking\r\n     &amp; its maintenance comes under CAM.</span><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'><br></span></li><li><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>The Respondent has failed to given possession\r\n     as per ATS inspite of full consideration having been paid.&nbsp;</span><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'><br></span></li><li><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>The Respondent are demanding CAM Charges at\r\n     the rate of Rs. 10 per Sq. Ft. and that too to be paid in advance for 2\r\n     years from 01.01.2019 to 31.12.2020 whereas the same is illegal and was agreed on monthly\r\n     basis.<font face=\"roboto\"> T</font></span><span style=\"margin: 0px; font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></li><li><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'><font face=\"roboto\"></font>The Respondent are demanding Car Parking\r\n     Maintenance Charges and that too to be paid in advance for 2 years for the\r\n     period 01.01.2019 to 31.12.2020 which was never agreed as comes under CAM</span><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'><br></span></li><li><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>The Common Area Maintenance Charges being\r\n     demanded and the services being proposed to be provided are not in\r\n     conformity with the provisions of per section 11, 4, &nbsp;d &nbsp;of RERA\r\n     Act as prima facie many of them are neither essential services nor the\r\n     charges are reasonable charges.<font face=\"roboto\"> T</font></span><span style=\"margin: 0px; font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></li><li><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'><font face=\"roboto\"></font>The Respondents have neither explained the\r\n     utility of services being offered to the Complainants for which CAM\r\n     Charges are being levied neither have explained how the CAM Charges have\r\n     been arrived at or how the CAM Charges have been allocated to the\r\n     individual units.&nbsp;</span></li></ul><ul>\r\n</ul><p>\r\n\r\n<b></b><i></i><u></u><sub></sub><sup></sup><strike></strike><font face=\"Times New Roman\"></font><br></p>','<p>The Complainant prays for grant of the following Relief by passing of directions, orders which this Hon’ble Authority deems fit and appropriate&nbsp; </p><ul><li>Direct the Respondent to handover the possession of the unit allotted to the Complainant at earliest complete in all respects after obtaining completion certificate for the whole project.&nbsp;</li><li>Further set aside the arbitrary demands of the Respondent mentioned as under &nbsp;</li><li>Charging of Common Area Maintenance Charges at the rate of Rs. 10 per Sq. Ft.&nbsp;</li><li>Demand of 2 years advance Common Area Maintenance Charges and Car Parking Maintenance Charges from 01.01.2019 to 31.12.2020 being illegal and ultra vires of the Agreement to Sell. The identical issue has already been dealt by this Hon’ble Authority in Jai Gopal Mahajan Vs Barnala Builders and Property Consultants, Comp. No. 44 1268 of 2017 vide order dated 12.02.2018 wherein it was held that the builder cannot make a coercive demand for prepayment of any future liability as the maintenance charges are leviable on monthly basis.&nbsp;</li><li>Direct the Respondent to demarcate, define the essential services for common area; scope of essential services for common area; mechanism of budgeting and allocation of common area maintenance charges and reasonability of charges as intended by the legislature vide Section 11, 4 ,d&nbsp; of the Act and in the event they fail to do so or act arbitrary, indulgence of this Hon’ble Authority is sought for the same. &nbsp;</li><li>Further pass necessary orders, directions directing the Respondent to pay the monthly interest as per section 18 of the Act to the Complainant for the delayed period i.e. period post expiry of 30 months as per the agreement till the actual and physical handing over of the possession of the allotted unit at the prescribed rates.&nbsp;</li><li>Award cost including litigation Cost&nbsp;</li><li>Pass any other order or direction which this Hon’ble Authority thinks fit and necessary for adjudication of the present complaint in interest of justice and equity</li></ul>',3350000.00,3515542.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>\r\n\r\n</p><ul type=\"disc\">\r\n <li style=\'margin: 0px 0px 13.33px; text-align: justify; color: black; line-height: normal; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 7pt; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400;\'><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>Restrain the Respondent from imposing any\r\n     penalty, interest, holding charges etc. under whatever name they may refer\r\n     and intimated vide letter dated 1.11.18, 9.11.18, as the Complainant have\r\n     paid the complete amount in all respects and is ready and willing to take\r\n     the possession and pay the Common Area Maintenance Charges as per agreed\r\n     rates as mentioned in Agreement to Sell only, to be charged only from the\r\n     date of handing over of the actual physical possession of the unit which\r\n     should be complete in all respects and in a totally completed project.\r\n     Whereas the Respondent are not ready to give the possession until the\r\n     arbitrary and illegal demands of payment of 2 years advance Common Area\r\n     Maintenance Charges at the arbitrary rates of Rs. 10 per Sq.Ft. and the\r\n     Car Parking Maintenance Charges are met with which are otherwise illegal\r\n     and ultra vires to the Agreement to Sell. Even otherwise the Complainants\r\n     have under protest and due to the coercion and threat of cancellation have\r\n     submitted the PDC for the same vide letter dated 12.11.18.</span></li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">\r\n </span><li style=\'margin: 0px 0px 13.33px; text-align: justify; color: black; line-height: normal; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 7pt; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400;\'><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>Restrain the Respondents from Cancelling the\r\n     allotment of the unit allotted to the Complainant as intended vide their\r\n     letter dated 01.11.2018 and or further allotting the same to any third\r\n     party or further creating any third party right, charge or lien over the\r\n     allotted unit.</span></li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">\r\n </span><li style=\'margin: 0px 0px 13.33px; text-align: justify; color: black; line-height: normal; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 7pt; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400;\'><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>Charging any charges including Common Area\r\n     Maintenance Charges under which ever head till the actual physical\r\n     possession of the allotted unit is handed over to the Complainant,\r\n     complete in all respects in the completed project and even thereafter not\r\n     in excess of the rate agreed, till the adjudication of the present\r\n     complainant.</span></li><li style=\'margin: 0px 0px 13.33px; text-align: justify; color: black; line-height: normal; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 7pt; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400;\'><span style=\'margin: 0px; color: black; line-height: 115%; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>Not to encash the cheques issued against CAM Charges by the Complainant\r\nunder coercion and threat and under protest vide letter dated 12.11.2018 till\r\ndisposal of this complaint.</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"></span><b></b><i></i><u></u><sub></sub><sup></sup><strike></strike><br></li></ul>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',1,1,0,0,'AnilVivanSingh','2018-11-18 08:44:05.000','AnilVivanSingh','2018-11-18 08:44:05.000'),(323,1123,'1123',1218,'fc7cffe1-0d0a-43d5-82bb-eae26e26997f','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-11-18 08:53:57.000','Vandna  Singh','mandeepkhillan@gmail.com',9779525511,0,0,'A1 303 VIP Road Nirmal Chhaya towers','Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','1','A1 303 VIP Road Nirmal Chhaya towers','Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','Mandeep Singh Khillan','mandeepkhillan@gmail.com',9779525511,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PC0010','Chandigarh Citi Center','Citi Centre Developers','info@chandigahciticenter.in',9023490234,0,'CCC VIP Road, Zirakpur','',28,507,'140603','1','CCC VIP Road, Zirakpur','',28,507,'140603','1','<p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 6.66px; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;\"><b><span style=\'margin: 0px; color: black; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>FACTS</span></b><span style=\'margin: 0px; color: black; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 7pt;\'></span></p><ul><li><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>The Respondent No.1 is a partnership firm and\r\n     Resp. No.2 and 3 are its partners who are developing commercial project,\r\n     Chandigarh Citi Centre at VIP Road, Zirakpur. Both partners are in\r\n     complete control of the management &amp; day to day business of Firm </span></li><li><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>The Complainant was allotted SCO No.13, LGF,\r\n     Block A vide Agreement to Sell dated 30.04.2016 subject to payment of\r\n     49.00 Lakhs by the Respondent. </span></li><li><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>The Complainant have paid Rs. 5155100 to the\r\n     Respondent including all amounts demanded other than basic price. </span></li><li><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>Possession as per agreement was to be handover\r\n     on or before 29.10.2018 complete in all respects.&nbsp;</span><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'><br></span></li><li><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>It was agreed that Common Area Maintenance CAM\r\n     shall be within 3 Rs. Per Sq.Ft. and as car parking was not allotted &amp;\r\n     was in common area as such no charges were fixed or agreed for car parking\r\n     &amp; its maintenance comes under CAM.</span></li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">\r\n</span></ul><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">\r\n\r\n</span></p><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 6.66px; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;\"><b><span style=\'margin: 0px; color: black; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>GREVIANCE</span></b><span style=\'margin: 0px; color: black; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 7pt;\'></span></p><ul><li><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>The Respondent has failed to given possession\r\n     as per ATS inspite of full consideration having been paid. </span></li><li><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>The Respondent are demanding CAM Charges at\r\n     the rate of Rs. 10 per Sq. Ft. and that too to be paid in advance for 2\r\n     years from 01.01.2019 to 31.12.2020 whereas the same is illegal and otherwise was agreed on monthly\r\n     basis. </span></li><li><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>The Respondent are demanding Car Parking\r\n     Maintenance Charges and that too to be paid in advance for 2 years for the\r\n     period 01.01.2019 to 31.12.2020 which was never agreed as comes under CAM</span></li><li><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>The Common Area Maintenance Charges being\r\n     demanded and the services being proposed to be provided are not in\r\n     conformity with the provisions of per section 11, 4, d &nbsp;of RERA\r\n     Act as prima facie they appear to be neither essential services nor the\r\n     charges are reasonable charges. </span></li><li><span style=\'margin: 0px; color: black; line-height: 115%; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>The Respondents have neither explained the utility of services being\r\noffered to the Complainants for which CAM Charges are being levied neither have\r\nexplained how the CAM Charges have been arrived at or how the CAM Charges have\r\nbeen allocated to the individual units.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"></span><b></b><i></i><u></u><sub></sub><sup></sup><strike></strike><br></li></ul>','<ul><li><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>The Complainant prays for grant of the\r\n     following Relief by passing of directions, orders which this Hon’ble\r\n     Authority deems fit and appropriate </span></li><li><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>Direct the Respondent to handover the\r\n     possession of the unit allotted to the Complainant at earliest complete in\r\n     all respects after obtaining completion certificate for the whole project.</span></li><li><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>Further set aside the arbitrary demands of the\r\n     Respondent mentioned as under </span></li><li><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>Charging of Common Area Maintenance Charges at\r\n     the rate of Rs. 10 per Sq. Ft.</span></li><li><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>Demand of 2 years advance Common Area\r\n     Maintenance Charges and Car Parking Maintenance Charges from 01.01.2019 to\r\n     31.12.2020 being illegal and ultra vires of the Agreement to Sell. The\r\n     identical issue has already been dealt by this Hon’ble Authority in the\r\n     matter of Jai Gopal Mahajan Vs Barnala Builders and Property Consultants,\r\n     Comp. No. 44 1268 of 2017 vide order dated 12.02.2018 wherein it was held\r\n     that the builder cannot make a coercive demand for prepayment of any\r\n     future liability as the maintenance charges are leviable on monthly basis.</span></li><li><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>Direct the Respondent to demarcate, define the\r\n     essential services for common area; scope of essential services for common\r\n     area; mechanism of budgeting and allocation of common area maintenance\r\n     charges and reasonability of charges as intended by the legislature vide\r\n     Section 11, 4 ,d &nbsp;of the Act and in the event they fail to do so or\r\n     act arbitrary, indulgence of this Hon’ble Authority is sought for the\r\n     same. </span></li><li><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>Further pass necessary orders, directions\r\n     directing the Respondent to pay the monthly interest as per section 18 of\r\n     the Act to the Complainant for the delayed period i.e. period post expiry\r\n     of 30 months as per the agreement till the actual and physical handing\r\n     over of the possession of the allotted unit at the prescribed rates.</span></li><li><font face=\'\"roboto\",\"serif\"\'><span style=\'margin: 0px; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>Award cost including litigation Cost</span></font></li><li><font face=\'\"roboto\",\"serif\"\'>P<span style=\"margin: 0px; color: black; line-height: 115%; font-size: 14px;\">ass any other order or direction which this Hon’ble Authority thinks\r\nfit and necessary for adjudication of the present complaint in interest of\r\njustice and equity.</span></font><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"></span><b></b><i></i><u></u><sub></sub><sup></sup><strike></strike><br></li></ul>',4900000.00,5155100.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>\r\n\r\n<br></p><ul><li style=\"margin: 0px 0px 13.33px 24px; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\'margin: 0px; color: black; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>Restrain the Respondent from imposing any penalty,\r\ninterest, holding charges etc. under whatever name they may refer and intimated\r\nvide letter dated 1.11.18, 9.11.18, as the Complainant have paid the complete\r\namount in all respects and is ready and willing to take the possession and pay\r\nthe Common Area Maintenance Charges as per agreed rates as mentioned in\r\nAgreement to Sell only, to be charged only from the date of handing over of the\r\nactual physical possession of the unit which should be complete in all respects\r\nand in a totally completed project. Whereas the Respondent are not ready to\r\ngive the possession until the arbitrary and illegal demands of payment of 2\r\nyears advance Common Area Maintenance Charges at the arbitrary rates of Rs. 10\r\nper Sq.Ft. and the Car Parking Maintenance Charges are met with which are\r\notherwise illegal and ultra vires to the Agreement to Sell. Even otherwise the\r\nComplainants have under protest and due to the coercion and threat of\r\ncancellation have submitted the PDC for the same vide letter dated 12.11.18.</span></li><li style=\"margin: 0px 0px 13.33px 24px; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\'margin: 0px; color: black; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>Restrain the Respondents from Cancelling the\r\nallotment of the unit allotted to the Complainant as intended vide their letter\r\ndated 01.11.2018 and or further allotting the same to any third party or\r\nfurther creating any third party right, charge or lien over the allotted unit.</span></li><li style=\"margin: 0px 0px 13.33px 24px; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\'margin: 0px; color: black; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>Charging any charges including Common Area\r\nMaintenance Charges under which ever head till the actual physical possession\r\nof the allotted unit is handed over to the Complainant, complete in all\r\nrespects in the completed project and even thereafter not in excess of the rate\r\nagreed, till the adjudication of the present complainant.</span></li><li style=\"margin: 0px 0px 13.33px 24px; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\'margin: 0px; color: black; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 14px;\'>Not to encash the cheques issued against CAM\r\nCharges by the Complainant under coercion and threat and under protest vide\r\nletter dated 12.11.2018 till disposal of this complaint.</span></li></ul><p>\r\n\r\n<b></b><i></i><u></u><sub></sub><sup></sup><strike></strike><font face=\"Times New Roman\"></font><br></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',1,1,0,0,'Vandnasingh','2018-11-18 08:51:41.000','Vandnasingh','2018-11-18 08:51:41.000'),(324,1124,'1124',1010,'a182232b-88d6-4711-8baa-f8a026fb675f','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','SUJATHA RAGHUNANDAN','lawofficeofhimanshuraj@gmail.com',9988100005,1724181010,711442413353,'#102, Sector 10 A','',6,128,'160011','1','#102, Sector 10 A','',6,128,'160011','HIMANSHU RAJ','lawofficeofhimanshuraj@gmail.com',9988200001,1724190909,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0013','ATS GOLF MEADOWS 1','ATS ESTATES PRIVATE LIMITED','pradeep.rathee@atsgreens.com',8288033311,0,'ATS TOWER, PLOT NO.16','SECTOR 35, NOIDA',33,216,'201305','1','ATS TOWER, PLOT NO.16','SECTOR 35, NOIDA',33,216,'201305','1','<p>Facts in Brief</p><p>i<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That the complainant is a citizen of India and is residing at the above mentioned address. The Aadhar card of the complainant is annexed as ANNEXURE C 1. The complainant has given her hard earned money in the OPs Project ATS GOLF MEADOWS I situated in Dera Bassi SAS Nagar Mohali Punjab for purchasing the residential plot based on assurance and promises of the OP which later on proved to be the false assurances and promises.</p><p><br></p><p>ii<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That the opposite party is a Company and has at all material points of time been and is still engaged in the commercial business of developing and selling housing projects flats plots and other construction layouts to various individuals and or others in lieu of valuable considerations for profit being their primary objective.</p><p><br></p><p>iii<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That the OP is a Builder Company and as part of their business venture decided to develop a residential space in the name of ATS GOLF MEADOWS I situated in Dera bassi SAS Nagar Punjab. The OP Builder had published various web and news advertisements as well as visual advertisements to attract the public at large to purchase residential space in the said project The OP had promised the complainant state of the art residential spaces that are affordable yet modern and well equipped residential project within a stipulated time period.</p><p><span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span></p><p><span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Rest of the facts of the case is enclosed as a complaint</p>','<p>Relief Sought</p><p><span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To direct the OP to compensate the complainant in the shape of refund of the complete amount which has been deposited against the residential property so booked by the complainant along with an Interest on the amount from the date of deposit at the rate of 20 per sent&nbsp; till the actual realization of the complete amount within 90 days according to section 18 1 Real Estate Regulation And Development Act 2016 18 2 Real Estate Regulation And Development Act 2016 Section 19 4 of The Real Estate Regulation And Development Act 2016 r w Rule 16 and Rule 17 of Punjab State Real Estate Regulation and Development Rules 2017.</p><p><span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span></p><p><span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Rest of the relief sought of the case is enclosed as a complaint</p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Not prayed</p>','1','','2009-04-25 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'lawofficeofhimanshuraj','2018-11-19 11:28:00.000','lawofficeofhimanshuraj','2018-11-19 11:28:00.000'),(325,1125,'1125',1191,'16dedd0c-2e6f-4eb1-85bb-f16106f43c42','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Nitin Jindal','nitin.email2me@gmail.com',8800669083,0,0,'D2 065 DLF NEW TOWN','Westend heights begur',17,67,'560068','1','D2 065 DLF NEW TOWN','Westend heights begur',17,67,'560068','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0084','Sushma Crescent ','Sushma Buildtech Limited','bharat@sushmabuildtech.com',0,0,'B-107, First Floor',', Business Complex at Elante Mall, Industrial Area - 1 ',6,128,'160002','1','B-107, First Floor',', Business Complex at Elante Mall, Industrial Area - 1 ',6,128,'160002','1','<p><br></p>