espondent and a compensation of Rs. 10,00,000/- for the economic and mental sufferings to the applicant.</li><li></li></ul><div><br></div>',9287213.00,0.00,'2016-01-17 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','NIL','1','','2012-12-16 00:00:00','2013-01-17 00:00:00','Unit No. 802, Tow-T1, Eight Floor, GH-10, Sector-90-91, JLPL, Mohali (Pb)','','',2,0,0,0,'kathuria.prashant','2018-11-20 14:55:21.000','kathuria.prashant','2018-11-20 14:55:21.000'),(336,1113,'1113',1213,'884b4d58-4c66-46bb-bc48-a198d34830a7','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-11-20 18:49:07.000','Prashant Kathuria','prashantkathuria@gmail.com',7009180831,0,0,'H. No. 2, Near Police Lines','Opposite DAV Public School, Amritsar',28,39,'143001','1','H. No. 2, Near Police Lines','Opposite DAV Public School, Amritsar',28,39,'143001','Ved Parkash','csvedparkash@gmail.com',7837223098,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0124','Acme Eden Court','Acme Builders Pvt. Ltd.','contact@acmebuilders.in',8592122888,0,'GH-10, Sector-90-91','JLPL, Mohali',28,507,'160022','1','GH-10, Sector-90-91','JLPL, Mohali',28,507,'160022','1','<div><div>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;CONCISE STATEMENT OF FACTS AND GROUNDS OF COMPLAINT</div><div><br></div><ul><li>That the respondent has purchased land for the purpose of developing group Housing Colony from the Master Developer (Janta Land Promoters Limited) who is the owner of land in Sector 91,SAS Nagar, District Mohali in the State of Punjab and developing township project under the name and style of “JLPL Township in Sector 90-91 in accordance with the approval granted by the Town and Country Planning Department Punjab.</li></ul><div><br></div><ul><li>That the respondent is developing Group Housing on land so purchased from the Master Developer under all approvals from the Master Developer that are under the provisions of laws of State of Punjab.</li></ul><div><br></div><ul><li>That respondent is developing Group Housing under the name and style of “Acme Eden Court” in the “JLPL Township” Sector 90-91, SAS Nagar, District Mohali. The respondent has been vested with rights to execute all agreements, issue allotments and re-allotments, collect monies, construct the areas purchased by it and market the products and act on behalf of the Master Developer for all reasons for the benefit of this agreement.</li></ul><p><br></p><p>The Other Details are continued in the Annexure to the complaint.</p></div><div><br></div>','<ul><li></li><li>That the respondent has also revised the layout plans of the residential project twice which has shattered the confidence of the applicant. The applicant wishes to withdraw from the project on account of abnormal delay in completing development works, changes in original layout plan without the consent of the applicant and other allottees.</li><li>As per clause 15 of the Builder Buyer Agreement, the possession of the allotted unit was to be offered within 36 months from the date of signing of the said agreement i.e. on 17.01.2016 which has already expired.</li><li>The provisions of RERA for ongoing projects provide equal rights to the existing allottees, who have signed contracts before the commencement of the Act. Therefore the applicant is seeking relief under the provisions of RERA.&nbsp;</li><li>In view of the points above, it is clearly established that the respondent has violated the provisions of Section 12, 14, 18 &amp; 19 of Real Estate (Development &amp; Regulations) Act, 2016.</li><li>It, is therefore, humbly prayed that the Hon’ble Authority may consider the applicant’s submissions and order the respondent to refund our total amount of Rs. 88,14,938/- along with interest as per RERA provisions from the respective dates of payments made to the respondent and a compensation of Rs. 10,00,000/- for the economic and mental sufferings to the applicant.</li><li></li></ul><div><br></div>',9287213.00,0.00,'2016-01-17 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','NA','1','','2012-12-16 00:00:00','2013-01-17 00:00:00','Unit No. 802, Tow-T1, Eight Floor, GH-10, Sector-90-91, JLPL, Mohali (Pb)','','',2,0,0,0,'kathuria.prashant','2018-11-20 16:05:47.000','kathuria.prashant','2018-11-20 16:05:47.000'),(337,1085,'1085',1135,'7ce4ff29-c893-46aa-aac9-b9c5d5926814','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-10-31 18:11:18.000','Gurmukh singh ','akhilesh@vyaslawassociates.com',8427828900,0,0,'Nikki Mandi, Patti, ','',28,574,'143001','1','Nikki Mandi, Patti, ','',28,574,'143001','akhilesh vyas','akhilesh@vyaslawassociates.com',9855004557,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-ASR02-PR0169','Guru Ram Dass Urban Estate','Punjab Urban Planning Development Authority','ca@puda.gov.in',0,0,'PUDA Bhawan','green avenue',28,39,'143001','1','PUDA Bhawan','green avenue',28,39,'143001','1','<p><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">That the complainant was allotted residential plot by respondent bearing plot No. 482 measuring 500 Sq. yards at Guru Ram Dass Urban Estate Airport Road, Amritsar. The total price of the plot is Rs. 945000/- @ 18000/- per square yard.</span>&nbsp;<span style=\"font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif; font-size: 13pt; line-height: 115%;\">&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif; font-size: 13pt; line-height: 115%;\">As per the payment schedule given in the\r\nallotment letter 25% of the allotment amount was to be paid initially and rest\r\nof the payment was to be paid after the possession. The brochure of the scheme\r\nclearly reflects that possession will be handed over on 25% payment as per the allotment letter. It\r\nis admitted by the respondent that payment of Rs. 23,62,500/- was made by the complainant and thereafter entire payment has been made by complainant as per the settle sale\r\nprice of residential plot as mentioned in clause No. 3.1.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif; font-size: 13pt; line-height: 115%;\">The complainant has paid full sale consideration amount.</span><font face=\"Bookman Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 17px; line-height: 19px;\"> As per Para 6(i) under the Possession and Ownership Heading of allotment letter possession was be to handed over within 90 days of issuance of allotment letter. So time limit for possession date is 22.1.2017. &nbsp;There is no chance of handing over the possession as no development work was even initiated, applicant made a request through application (diary no 4869 dated 6.917) to waive off interest. But this letter was never responded from respondent. To be on safer side of law applicant paid first installment (Principal and interest both) and then made the full payment. <br></span></font></p><p><font face=\"Bookman Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 17px; line-height: 19px;\">PUDA has even changed the plan of site without getting 2/3 rd of allottees and they are changing plot of applicant as well. <br></span></font></p>','<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"margin-left:.75in;mso-add-space:auto;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;text-indent:-.5in;line-height:\r\n200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:\r\n11.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">1. The complainant is entitled for possession with all the development possible as per agreed terms and conditions.</span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"margin-left:.75in;mso-add-space:auto;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;text-indent:-.5in;line-height:\r\n200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:\r\n11.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">2. That the PUDA should refund interest which has been charged by them. </span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"margin-left:.75in;mso-add-space:auto;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;text-indent:-.5in;line-height:\r\n200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:\r\n11.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">3. PUDA should pay interest on amount which has been paid to it under section 18 of RERA act,2016.</span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"margin-left:.75in;mso-add-space:auto;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;text-indent:-.5in;line-height:\r\n200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:\r\n11.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">4. The complainant is entitled for compensation of Rs. 10,00,000/- on account of mental agony and litigation charges.</span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"margin-left:.75in;mso-add-space:auto;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;text-indent:-.5in;line-height:\r\n200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:\r\n11.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">5. PUDA should not change plan of site and should restore my original plot. <br><o:p></o:p></span></p>',9450000.00,9450000.00,'2017-01-22 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:\r\n11.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">1. The complainant is entitled for possession with all the development possible as per agreed terms and conditions.</span><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"margin-left:.75in;mso-add-space:auto;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;text-indent:-.5in;line-height:\r\n200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:\r\n11.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">2. That the PUDA should refund interest which has been charged by them. </span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"margin-left:.75in;mso-add-space:auto;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;text-indent:-.5in;line-height:\r\n200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:\r\n11.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">3. PUDA should pay interest on amount which has been paid to it under section 18 of RERA act,2016.</span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"margin-left:.75in;mso-add-space:auto;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;text-indent:-.5in;line-height:\r\n200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:\r\n11.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">4. The complainant is entitled for compensation of Rs. 10,00,000/- on account of mental agony and litigation charges.</span></p><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:\r\n11.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">5. PUDA should not change plan of site and should restore my original plot.</span>','1','','2016-10-22 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','482','','',2,0,0,0,'akhilesh','2018-11-21 16:27:36.000','akhilesh','2018-11-21 16:27:36.000'),(338,1128,'1128',1225,'fafedfd6-7d94-407d-bfcd-4cea99a9625a','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','J N Singh','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9816400801,0,0,'312 2 Rani Ka Bagh ','Shimla Road, NAHAN',14,544,'173001','1','312 2, Rani Ka Bagh','Shimla Road, NAHAN',14,544,'173001','Kamal Dahiya','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9729902009,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0093','Palm Garden','Manohar Infrastructure and Constructions Private Limited','nbs@manoharrealty.com',0,1725016888,'SCO 139 141 Level 1 Sector 17C','',6,128,'160017','1','SCO 139 141 Level 1 Sector 17C','',6,128,'160017','1','<div>List of Dates and Events</div><div><br></div><div>2012<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>The PALM GARDEN is a Residential Group Housing Colony Project (the Project) being developed by Respondent on a parcel of land admeasuring 103 acres at revenue estate of Mullanpur i.e. New Chandigarh, District- Mohali, Punjab.</div><div><br></div><div>26.03.2012<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>The complainant had purchased a plot in the said project having an approximate 250 sq. yard. The complainant had made payment of Rs 13,87,500/- at the time of allotment, on which the respondent had issued a letter for expression of interest to the complainant dated 26.03.2012.</div><div><br></div><div>------------<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>The respondent had sent a letter to the complainant wherein they had assured that they would deliver the possession of the plot by year 2015.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>17.03.2014<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>The respondent had issued a letter dated 17.03.2014 wherein the respondent requested for further amount of Rs 9,25,000/- and assured that the project has reached its final stage and they would be in a position to deliver the possession of said plot within stipulated time.</div><div><br></div><div>09.01.2018<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>The complainant had paid Rs 15,00,000/- to the respondent vide cheque dated 09.01.2018.</div><div><br></div><div>02.02.2018<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>The respondent had issued a letter to the complainant dated 02.02.2018 wherein the complainant was allotted with plot no. 702 and also the respondent levied the charges of IDC, PLC, Possession charges or any arbitrary charges which were not disclosed or agreed for at the time of initial booking of the plot.</div><div><br></div><div>Jan 2018<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>The complainant has paid Rs 28,87,500/- (Twenty Eight Lakh Eighty Seven Thousand Five Hundred) i.e. 70% of the payment out of total consideration.</div><div><br></div><div>March 2015<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>The possession of the project was committed in the month of March 2015 and now in the month of November 2018 i.e. delay of 44 months from the date of the commitment, only 30% project is completed thus delaying the possession of the plot deliberately or for reasons known best to them.</div><div><br></div>','<p>--</p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>--</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'JNSingh1','2018-11-21 16:34:52.000','JNSingh1','2018-11-21 16:34:52.000'),(339,1085,'1085',1135,'7ce4ff29-c893-46aa-aac9-b9c5d5926814','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-10-31 18:11:18.000','Gurmukh singh ','akhilesh@vyaslawassociates.com',8427828900,0,0,'Nikki Mandi, Patti, ','',28,574,'143001','1','Nikki Mandi, Patti, ','',28,574,'143001','akhilesh vyas','akhilesh@vyaslawassociates.com',9855004557,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-ASR02-PR0169','Guru Ram Dass Urban Estate','Punjab Urban Planning Development Authority','ca@puda.gov.in',0,0,'PUDA Bhawan','green avenue',28,39,'143001','1','PUDA Bhawan','green avenue',28,39,'143001','1','<p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">That the complainant was allotted residential plot by respondent bearing plot No. 482 measuring 500 Sq. yards at Guru Ram Dass Urban Estate Airport Road, Amritsar. The total price of the plot is Rs. 945000/- @ 18000/- per square yard.</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif; font-size: 14px; line-height: 115%;\">&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif; font-size: 14px; line-height: 115%;\">As per the payment schedule given in the\r\nallotment letter 25% of the allotment amount was to be paid initially and rest\r\nof the payment was to be paid after the possession. The brochure of the scheme\r\nclearly reflects that possession will be handed over on 25% payment as per the allotment letter. It\r\nis admitted by the respondent that payment of Rs. 23,62,500/- was made by the complainant and thereafter entire payment has been made by complainant as per the settle sale\r\nprice of residential plot as mentioned in clause No. 3.1.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif; font-size: 14px; line-height: 115%;\">The complainant has paid full sale consideration amount.</span><font face=\"Bookman Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 17px; line-height: 19px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"> As per Para 6(i) under the Possession and Ownership Heading of allotment letter possession was be to handed over within 90 days of issuance of allotment letter. So time limit for possession date is 22.1.2017. &nbsp;There is no chance of handing over the possession as no development work was even initiated, applicant made a request through application (diary no 4869 dated 6.917) to waive off interest. But this letter was never responded from respondent. To be on safer side of law applicant paid first installment (Principal and interest both) and then made the full payment. </span><br></span></font></p><p><font face=\"Bookman Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 17px; line-height: 19px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">That earlier the complainant filed his petition before the Hon\'ble Punjab and Haryana High court where the petitioner was withdrawn for filing it before RERA, for which the relevant order is already attached. That the applicant has also sent representation to the department and the photographs of the incomplete site as attached alongwith the petition. PUDA has even changed the plan of site without getting 2/3 rd of allottees and they are changing plot of applicant as well. </span><br></span></font></p>','<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"margin-left:.75in;mso-add-space:auto;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;text-indent:-.5in;line-height:\r\n200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:\r\n11.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">1. The complainant is entitled for possession with all the development possible as per agreed terms and conditions.</span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"margin-left:.75in;mso-add-space:auto;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;text-indent:-.5in;line-height:\r\n200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:\r\n11.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">2. That the PUDA should refund interest which has been charged by them. </span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"margin-left:.75in;mso-add-space:auto;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;text-indent:-.5in;line-height:\r\n200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:\r\n11.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">3. PUDA should pay interest on amount which has been paid to it under section 18 of RERA act,2016.</span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"margin-left:.75in;mso-add-space:auto;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;text-indent:-.5in;line-height:\r\n200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:\r\n11.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">4. The complainant is entitled for compensation of Rs. 10,00,000/- on account of mental agony and litigation charges.</span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"margin-left:.75in;mso-add-space:auto;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;text-indent:-.5in;line-height:\r\n200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:\r\n11.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">5. PUDA should not change plan of site and should restore my original plot. <br><o:p></o:p></span></p>',9450000.00,9450000.00,'2017-01-22 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:\r\n11.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">1. The complainant is entitled for possession with all the development possible as per agreed terms and conditions.</span><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"margin-left:.75in;mso-add-space:auto;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;text-indent:-.5in;line-height:\r\n200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:\r\n11.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">2. That the PUDA should refund interest which has been charged by them. </span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"margin-left:.75in;mso-add-space:auto;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;text-indent:-.5in;line-height:\r\n200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:\r\n11.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">3. PUDA should pay interest on amount which has been paid to it under section 18 of RERA act,2016.</span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"margin-left:.75in;mso-add-space:auto;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;text-indent:-.5in;line-height:\r\n200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:\r\n11.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">4. The complainant is entitled for compensation of Rs. 10,00,000/- on account of mental agony and litigation charges.</span></p><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:\r\n11.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">5. PUDA should not change plan of site and should restore my original plot.</span>','1','','2016-10-22 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','482','','',2,0,0,0,'akhilesh','2018-11-21 16:48:11.000','akhilesh','2018-11-21 16:48:11.000'),(340,1085,'1085',1135,'7ce4ff29-c893-46aa-aac9-b9c5d5926814','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-11-21 16:54:21.000','Gurmukh singh ','akhilesh@vyaslawassociates.com',8427828900,0,0,'Nikki Mandi, Patti, ','',28,574,'143001','1','Nikki Mandi, Patti, ','',28,574,'143001','akhilesh vyas','akhilesh@vyaslawassociates.com',9855004557,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-ASR02-PR0169','Guru Ram Dass Urban Estate','Punjab Urban Planning Development Authority','ca@puda.gov.in',0,0,'PUDA Bhawan','green avenue',28,39,'143001','1','PUDA Bhawan','green avenue',28,39,'143001','1','<p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">That the complainant was allotted residential plot by respondent bearing plot No. 482 measuring 500 Sq. yards at Guru Ram Dass Urban Estate Airport Road, Amritsar. The total price of the plot is Rs. 945000/- @ 18000/- per square yard.</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif; font-size: 14px; line-height: 115%;\">&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif; font-size: 14px; line-height: 115%;\">As per the payment schedule given in the\r\nallotment letter 25% of the allotment amount was to be paid initially and rest\r\nof the payment was to be paid after the possession. The brochure of the scheme\r\nclearly reflects that possession will be handed over on 25% payment as per the allotment letter. It\r\nis admitted by the respondent that payment of Rs. 23,62,500/- was made by the complainant and thereafter entire payment has been made by complainant as per the settle sale\r\nprice of residential plot as mentioned in clause No. 3.1.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif; font-size: 14px; line-height: 115%;\">The complainant has pai