 style=\"font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif;\"><b style=\"\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">&nbsp;That in-spite of the receipt of substantial amount against the said apartment the respondents have failed to complete the said apartment and further failed to offer the possession of the said apartment upto 01.02.2016.&nbsp;</span></b></span></p><p><span style=\"font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif;\"><b style=\"\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">That recently the applicant have come to know that the entire project of the respondents is illegal as the respondent have started the construction of the project without obtaining clearance from the environment and forest department as required under notification dated 14.09.2006 and the State Level Environment Impact Assessment Authority (SEIAA) had already initiated action against.<br></span><br></b></span><br></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\nline-height:97%\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:97%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:Times\">In view of the facts\r\nmentioned in paragraph 4 above, the complainant prays for the following\r\nrelief(s)</span><span style=\"font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif;\">That as\r\nthe respondents have failed to comply with the terms and conditions of the\r\nallotment letter dated 02.08.2013 (Annexure C-1) and have failed to deliver the\r\npossession of the apartment/flat within the stipulated time. Therefore, the\r\napplicant as per section 18 of the RERA Act. 2016, is entitled for</span><b><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif;\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></b></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:8.0pt;\r\nmargin-left:.25in;text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;text-indent:\r\n-22.5pt;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif;\">i)<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif;\">Refund principal amount of Rs.</span><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif;\">10,580,830/- </span><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif;\">of the\r\napplicant </span><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif;\">along</span><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif;\"> with interest @ 18% P.a. from the date of actual payment till\r\nrealization. <b><o:p></o:p></b></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:8.0pt;\r\nmargin-left:.25in;text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;text-indent:\r\n-22.5pt;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif;\">ii)<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif;\">Pay compensation of Rs.5,00,000/- to the applicant for mental\r\nharassment, mental agony <b><o:p></o:p></b></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:8.0pt;\r\nmargin-left:.25in;text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;text-indent:\r\n-22.5pt;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif;\">iii)<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><font face=\"Tahoma, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Any other relief which this Hon’ble authority deems fit may also\r\nbe passed in&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">favour</span><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">&nbsp;of the applicant.</span></font><b style=\"font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\"><o:p></o:p></b></p>',10825200.00,0.00,'2016-02-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Interim Order date - 30.10.2018</p><p>The adjudicating officer now can not deal with the case of the refund and interest and for that purpose the complaint has to be filled in the Form-M before the authority . For compensation only ,the party may file complaint in form-N.Thus , in view of these circumstances, the Adjudicating officer lacks the jurisdiction to grant relief of refund or interest thereon. Therefore, in the larger interest of justice, the complaint is ordered to be returned to the complainant , who is at liberty to file a fresh complaint before the authority as per the decision of learned authority. Copy of this order&nbsp; be supplied to&nbsp; both&nbsp; the parties under rules.</p>','1','','2013-08-02 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Flat no- E401,4th floor, Wing E, \r\nPhase II, Sector 66-A mohali','','',2,0,0,0,'GVstarLLP','2018-11-22 12:10:51.000','GVstarLLP','2018-11-22 12:10:51.000'),(348,1132,'1132',1193,'109a020f-7ac8-4af7-9194-064fff6a2fe0','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-11-27 13:27:50.000','Bhupinder Singh','parveen.ch.2@gmail.com',8882950006,0,0,'Ward No. 10, Balachaur','tehsil Balachaur',28,527,'144521','1','Ward No. 10, Balachaur','tehsil Balachaur',28,527,'144521','PARVEEN CHAUDHARY','parveen.ch.2@gmail.com',8882950006,0,'Allottee','PBRERA-SAS81-PM0039','Chandigarh Overseas Pvt. Ltd','Chandigarh overseas Pvt. Ltd','jbp@j90.in',0,1149879480,'M/s. Chandigarh Overseas Pvt. Ltd., SCO 249, Sector 44-C, Chandigarh.','',6,128,'160047','1','M/s. Chandigarh Overseas Pvt. Ltd., SCO 249, Sector 44-C, Chandigarh.','',6,128,'160047','1','<p>1. That the respondent M/s Chandigarh overseas Pvt. Ltd launched a scheme called “Small Investors Scheme” vide which a share in design studio of an area measuring 100 sq feet on the 4th floors of Industrial Knowledge(Fashion Technology) Park Sector 90, SAS Nagar was offered to the Prospector Buyer(s) on the free hold basis as a co-owner of  Design Studio.\r\n</p><p>2.	That the complainant Trilok Singh submitted application No. 104045 dated 18.01.2008 for purchase of one unit i.e. measuring 100 Sq feet for total consideration of Rs. 6,50,000/- and  again he purchased six more unit @ Rs. 6,50,000/- per unit, vide another Developer Buyer Agreement dated  18.03.2018 and lease deed was executed between complainant and respondent No. 2.  As per above said agreement, complainant paid        Rs. 50,000/- to respondent No. 1 vide receipt dated 18.01.2008 and further sum of Rs. 34,56,000/- was paid to respondent vide receipt dated 18.03.2008.  Further Rs. 5,26,000/- was paid to respondent No. 1 vide receipt dated 19.03.2008.  Complainant had paid sum of                 Rs. 40,32,000/- for purchase of said seven units to respondents.\r\n</p><p>3.	That as per Developer Buyer Agreements the possession was to be delivered after 30 months from the date of allotment, but till filing of the complaint, respondent has failed to deliver physical possession of said units to complainant.&nbsp; An additional lease agreement was also made as mentioned in para 5th of the developer buyer agreement regarding rent with M/s Green Field Sites Management pvt ltd and no rent has been paid till now as mentioned in the agreement.</p>','<p><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 115%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">It is therefore submitted through this complaint\r\nthat the respondents have failed to comply with the conditions mentioned in the developer buyer agreement so the respondents may be directed to give the possession of units as per the\r\ndeveloper buyer agreements dated 31.01.2008 &amp; 18.03.2008 along with the\r\nrent or the interest as described in the agreements qua and if the respondent\r\ndo not give the possession as per the agreements qua, in that event the amount\r\nof Rs. 40,32,000/- along with the interest @ Rs. 1% per month on the principle\r\namount may be paid to the complainant.</span><br></p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;\r\nmso-add-space:auto;text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;text-indent:\r\n-18.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">1.</span><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 14px; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">That\r\nduring the pendency of the complaint the property of respondent may be attached\r\nand amount paid by the complainant to the respondent may be got returned.</span><o:p></o:p></span></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'parveenchaudhary','2018-11-22 12:22:49.000','parveenchaudhary','2018-11-22 12:22:49.000'),(349,1133,'1133',1061,'feb522a9-b591-42ad-b827-d1fac41495ae','FormTypeM',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','SUDESH KUMAR  DHAWAN','vikas3dhawan@gmail.com',9785325611,0,0,'#3B-51, JAWAHAR NAGAR','',29,213,'335001','1','#3B-51, JAWAHAR NAGAR','',29,213,'335001','BIRENDER SINGH DHILLON','CSPURIDHILLON@GMAIL.COM',9988933636,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PC0001','ROYAL BUSINESS PARK','MOTIA DEVELOPERS PRIVATE LIMITED','INFO@MOTIAGROUP.COM',8558844525,0,'Royal Citi','Chandigarh-Ambala Highway',28,507,'140603','1','Royal Citi','Chandigarh-Ambala Highway',28,507,'140603','1','<p>A</p>','<p>B</p>',4963632.00,3500000.00,'2017-11-15 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>B</p>','1','','2014-11-04 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Shop No 6, Ground Floor, Royal Business Park, Zirakpur (PB)','','',2,0,0,0,'SUDESHKUMARDHAWAN','2018-11-22 13:20:50.000','SUDESHKUMARDHAWAN','2018-11-22 13:20:50.000'),(350,1134,'1134',1203,'1cc7ee4f-bdbb-4adc-aaba-bf2382465ef3','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Ajit  Singh','ajitsinghin@rediffmail.com',9814711221,0,0,'2004, Verka Enclave','Sector 49',6,128,'160047','1','2004, Verka Enclave','Sector 49',6,128,'160047','Vipin Kumar','vipin268@gmail.com',9914099255,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0086','Casa Espana ','ATS Infrabuild Pvt. Ltd','email@atsgreens.com',0,0,'ATS Infrabuild Pvt. Ltd. ','Regd. Office - 711/92, Deepali',10,557,'110019','1','ATS Infrabuild Pvt. Ltd. ','Regd. Office - 711/92, Deepali',10,557,'110019','1','<p>abc</p>','<p>ab c</p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>qbc</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'vipinK','2018-11-22 13:25:01.000','vipinK','2018-11-22 13:25:01.000'),(351,1128,'1128',1225,'fafedfd6-7d94-407d-bfcd-4cea99a9625a','FormTypeM',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','J N Singh','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9816400801,0,0,'312 2 Rani Ka Bagh ','Shimla Road, NAHAN',14,544,'173001','1','312 2, Rani Ka Bagh','Shimla Road, NAHAN',14,544,'173001','Kamal Dahiya','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9729902009,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0093','Palm Eco City','Manohar Infrastructure and Constructions Private Limited','nbs@manoharrealty.com',0,1725016888,'SCO 139 141 Level 1 Sector 17C','',6,128,'160017','1','SCO 139 141 Level 1 Sector 17C','',6,128,'160017','1','<div><div>The complainant had purchased a plot in the said project having an approximate 250 sq. yard.</div><div>The complainant had made payment of Rs 23,12,500/- at the time of allotment, on which the respondent had issued a letter for expression of interest to the complainant dated 26.03.2012 -<b><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">Annexure C-1</span></b>&nbsp;</div><div>The respondent sent a letter and assured that they would deliver the possession of plot by year 2015 -<b><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">Annexure C-2</span></b></div><div>The respondent had issued a letter in 17.03.2014 wherein they assured that the project has reached its final stage and they would be in a position to deliver the possession of plot by 2015&nbsp;</div><div>That being influenced by the assurances and representations made by the respondent, the complainant paid Rs.10,00,000/- on the asking of the respondent vide cheque dated 09 Jan 2018 -<b><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">Annexure C-3</span></b></div><div>The respondent had allotted plot No. 1035 admeasuring 250 sq. yard area in year 2018 to the complainant.&nbsp; The respondent had issued a letter to the complainant dated 02.02.2018 wherein the respondent levied the charges of IDC, PLC, Possession charges or any arbitrary charges which were not disclosed or agreed for at the time of initial booking of the plot -&nbsp;<b><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">Annexure C-4</span></b></div><div>It is pertinent to mention here that the respondent has the intention to cheat the complainant since the beginning as it is proved by the malafide act and conduct of the respondent.</div><div>The Complainant has paid INR 33,12,500/- i.e. more than 80% of payment out of total consideration i.e. Basic Sale Price, agreed at the time of booking the plot till Jan.18 -&nbsp;<b><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">Annexure- C-5</span></b></div><div>The possession of the project was committed in the month of March 2015 and now in the month of November 2018 i.e. delay of 44 months from the date of the commitment, only 30% project is completed thus delaying the possession of the plot deliberately or for reasons known best to them.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div>','<p>In view of the facts mentioned in preceding paragraphs, the complainant prays for the following relief(s):-&nbsp;</p><p>i.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To give necessary directions to the respondents for delivery of possession of plot&nbsp; along with interest for delay in delivery of possession till realization as per the provisions of Sec. 18 and Sec.19(3)of the RERA Act read with Rule 16 of PSRE(R&amp;D)Rules,2017.</p><p>ii.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 60 of RERA Act for willful default committed by them.</p><p>iii.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 61 of RERA Act for contravention of Sec.12, Sec.14, and Sec. 16 of RERA Act.</p><p>iv.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To issue directions to make liable every officer concerned i.e. Director, Manager, Secretary, or any other officer of the respondent’s company at whose instance, connivance, acquiescence, neglect any of the offences has been committed as mentioned in Sec.69 of RERA Act,2016 to be read with Punjab RERA Rules,2017.</p><p>v.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To recommend criminal action against the respondents for the criminal offence of cheating, fraud and criminal breach of trust under section 420,406 and 409 of the Indian Penal Code.</p><p>vi.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To issue direction to pay the cost of litigation.</p><p>vii.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To issue direction to pay the compensation to complainant for compensation for his mental agony, pain and harassment.</p><p>viii.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Any other relief which this Hon’ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances of this complaint.</p><div><br></div>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>--</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'JNSingh1','2018-11-22 13:47:26.000','JNSingh1','2018-11-22 13:47:26.000'),(352,1135,'1135',1160,'09581713-6148-49dc-9291-17a00d6bad73','FormTypeM',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','krishan kumar ','adv.karanjindal@gmail.com',9041500006,0,0,'House no 125','Bank Colony Patiala',28,454,'147001','1','House no 125','Bank Colony Patiala',28,454,'147001','j.p singla','adv.karanjindal@gmail.com',9815482240,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0153','wave floors, wave estate sector-99, SAS mohali','country colonisers pvt ltd','rera@waveestate.in',7290015352,0,'country colonisers pvt ltd','sector-85 mohali',28,507,'160062','1','country colonisers pvt ltd','sector-85 mohali',28,507,'160062','1','<p><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;line-height:107%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-ascii-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\nCalibri;mso-fareast-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-hansi-theme-font:minor-latin;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;\r\nmso-ansi-language:EN-IN;mso-fareast-language:EN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">The\r\ncomplainant has booked a flat and paid Rs.618540/- ( Six Lakh Eighteen Thousand\r\nFive Hundred And forty only) through bank transfer against booking<span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"> of a flat\r\nno. WF/G/52 First Floor in project Wave Estate Sector-99, Mohali. At the time\r\nof booking the developer has assured the sanctioning of loan (subvention\r\nScheme) for the purchase of the flat from the bank. But later on bank\r\nauthorities refused him to give the sanction letter under subvention scheme\r\nbecause of the meagre pension the complainant was drawing. The complainant\r\nbrought this matter into the notice of the developer and requested the\r\nrespondent to refund his booking amount but the developer has not refunded his\r\nmoney paid to them as booking amount. The complainant is retired government\r\nem</span>ployee and is getting basic pension of Rupees 9931/- only. Moreover, the wife\r\nof the complainant is suffering from serious heart ailment and is bed ridden.\r\nThe complainant has personally requested the authorities of the respondent\r\ndeveloper so many times for the refund of his booking amount but the respondent\r\nresponded to his request. Finally, a registered legal notice was served upon\r\nthe respondent on dated 15-06-2018 through Sh. J.P Singla advocate Punjab &amp;\r\nHaryna High Court the copy of which is annexed as annexure P-1. The respondent\r\ndeveloper has neither bothered to reply the same nor the</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">&nbsp; </span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">booking amount has been refunded.</span></span><br></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\">The complainant seek the refund of his booking amount along\r\nwith interest @18% per annum for not refunding his booking amount along with\r\nRs.1 Lakh as compensation for mental harassment and Rs.55000 as legal costs\r\npaid by him to his advocate.<o:p></o:p></p>',0.00,618540.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p><br></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','WF/G/52FF PROJECT WAVE FLOOR -99 AT WAVE ESTATE','','',2,0,0,0,'adv.karanjindal','2018-11-22 14:56:45.000','adv.karanjindal','2018-11-22 14:56:45.000'),(353,1135,'1135',1160,'09581713-6148-49dc-9291-17a00d6bad73','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-11-22 15:49:45.000','krishan kumar ','adv.karanjindal@gmail.com',9041500006,0,0,'House no 125','Bank Colony Patiala',28,454,'147001','1','House no 125','Bank Colony Patiala',28,454,'147001','j.p singla','adv.karanjindal@gmail.com',9815482240,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0153','wave floors, wave estate sector-99, SAS mohali','country colonisers pvt ltd','rera@waveestate.in',7290015352,0,'country colonisers pvt ltd','sector-85 mohali',28,507,'160062','1','country colonisers pvt ltd','sector-85 mohali',28,507,'160062','1','<p><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;line-height:107%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-ascii-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\nCalibri;mso-fareast-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-hansi-theme-font:minor-latin;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;\r\nmso-ansi-language:EN-IN;mso-fareast-language:EN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">The\r\ncomplainant has booked a flat and paid Rs.618540/- ( Six Lakh Eighteen Thousand\r\nFive Hundred And forty only) through bank transfer against booking<span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"> of a flat\r\nno. WF/G/52 First Floor in project Wave Estate Sector-99, Mohali. At the time\r\nof booking the developer has assured the sanctioning of loan (subvention\r\nScheme) for the purchase of the flat from the bank. But later on bank\r\nauthorities refused him to give the sanction letter under subvention scheme\r\nbecause of the meagre pension the complainant was drawing. The complainant\r\nbrought this matter into the notice of the developer and requested the\r\nrespondent to refund his booking amount but the developer has not refunded his\r\nmoney paid to them as booking amount. The complainant is retired government\r\nem</span>ployee and is getting basic pension of Rupees 9931/- only. Moreover, the wife\r\nof the complainant is suffering from serious heart ailment and is bed ridden.\r\nThe complainant has personally requested the authorities of the respondent\r\ndeveloper so many times for the refund of his booking amount but the respondent\r\nresponded to his request. Finally, a registered legal notice was served upon\r\nthe respondent on dated 15-06-2018 through Sh. J.P Singla advocate Punjab &amp;\r\nHaryna High Court the copy of which is annexed as annexure P-1. The respondent\r\ndeveloper has neither bothered to reply the same nor the</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">&nbsp; </span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">booking amount has been refunded.</span></span><br></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\">The complainant seek the refund of his booking amount along\r\nwith interest @18% per annum for not refunding his booking amount along with\r\nRs.1 Lakh as compensation for mental harassment and Rs.55000 as legal costs\r\npaid by him to his advocate.<o:p></o:p></p>',0.00,618540.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p><br></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','WF/G/52FF PROJECT WAVE FLOOR -99 AT WAVE ESTATE','','',1,1,0,0,'adv.karanjindal','2018-11-22 15:31:35.000','adv.karanjindal','2018-11-22 15:31:35.000'),(354,1131,'1131',1225,'fafedfd6-7d94-407d-bfcd-4cea99a9625a','FormTypeM',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','J N Singh','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9816400801,0,0,'312 2, Rani Ka Bagh','Shimla Road, NAHAN',14,544,'173001','1','312 2, Rani Ka Bagh','Shimla Road, NAHAN',14,544,'173001','Kamal Dahiya','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9729902008,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0093','Palm Garden','Manohar Infrastructure and Constructions Private Limited','nbs@manoharrealty.com',0,1725016888,'SCO 139 141 Level 1 Sector 17C','',6,128,'160017','1','SCO 139 141 Level 1 Sector 17C','',6,128,'160017','1','<p>The complainant had purchased a plot in the said project having an approximate 250 sq. yard.</p><p>The complainant had made payment of Rs 13,87,500/- at the time of allotment, on which the respondent had issued a letter for expression of interest to the complainant dated 26.03.2012 -<b><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">Annexure C-1</span></b>&nbsp;</p><p>The respondent sent a letter and assured that they would deliver the possession of plot by year 2015 -<b><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">Annexure C-2</span></b></p><p>The respondent had issued a letter in 17.03.2014 wherein they requested for further sum of deposit to the tune of Rs. 9,25,000/- and assured that the project has reached its final stage and they would be in a position to deliver the possession of plot by 2015 -&nbsp;<b><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">Annexure C-3</span></b></p><p>That being influenced by the assurances and representations made by the respondent, the complainant paid Rs.15,00,000/- on the asking of the respondent vide cheque dated 09 Jan 2018 -<b><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">Annexure C-4</span></b></p><p>The respondent had allotted plot No. 702 admeasuring 250 sq. yard area in year 2018 to the complainant.&nbsp; The respondent had issued a letter to the complainant dated 02.02.2018 wherein the respondent levied the charges of IDC, PLC, Possession charges or any arbitrary charges which were not disclosed or agreed for at the time of initial booking of the plot -&nbsp;<b><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">Annexure C-5</span></b></p><p>It is pertinent to mention here that the respondent has the intention to cheat the complainant since the beginning as it is proved by the malafide act and conduct of the respondent.</p><p>The Complainant has paid INR 28,87,500/- i.e. more than 70% of payment out of total consideration i.e. Basic Sale Price, agreed at the time of booking the plot till Jan.18 -&nbsp;<b><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">Annexure- C-6</span></b></p><p>The possession of the project was committed in the month of March 2015 and now in the month of November 2018 i.e. delay of 44 months from the date of the commitment, only 30% project is completed thus delaying the possession of the plot deliberately or for reasons known best to them.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p>','<p>In view of the facts mentioned in preceding paragraphs, the complainant prays for the following relief(s):-&nbsp;</p><p>i.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To give necessary directions to the respondents for delivery of possession of plot&nbsp; along with interest for delay in delivery of possession till realization as per the provisions of Sec. 18 and Sec.19(3)of the RERA Act read with Rule 16 of PBRE(R&amp;D)Rules,2017.</p><p>ii.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 60 of RERA Act for willful default committed by them.</p><p>iii.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 61 of RERA Act for contravention of Sec.12, Sec.14, and Sec. 16 of RERA Act.</p><p>iv.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To issue directions to make liable every officer concerned i.e. Director, Manager, Secretary, or any other officer of the respondent’s company at whose instance, connivance, acquiescence, neglect any of the offences has been committed as mentioned in Sec.69 of RERA Act,2016 to be read with Punjab RERA Rules,2017.</p><p>v.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To recommend criminal action against the respondents for the criminal offence of cheating, fraud and criminal breach of trust under section 420,406 and 409 of the Indian Penal Code.</p><p>vi.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To issue direction to pay the cost of litigation.</p><p>vii.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To issue direction to pay the compensation to complainant for compensation for his mental agony, pain and harassment.<br></p><p>vii.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Any other relief which this Hon’ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances of this complaint.</p><div><br></div>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>-</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'JNSingh1','2018-11-22 16:32:31.000','JNSingh1','2018-11-22 16:32:31.000'),(355,1131,'1131',1225,'fafedfd6-7d94-407d-bfcd-4cea99a9625a','FormTypeM',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','J N Singh','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9816400801,0,0,'312 2, Rani Ka Bagh','Shimla Road, NAHAN',14,544,'173001','1','312 2, Rani Ka Bagh','Shimla Road, NAHAN',14,544,'173001','Kamal Dahiya','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9729902008,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0093','Palm Garden','Manohar Infrastructure and Constructions Private Limited','nbs@manoharrealty.com',0,1725016888,'SCO 139 141 Level 1 Sector 17C','',6,128,'160017','1','SCO 139 141 Level 1 Sector 17C','',6,128,'160017','1','<p>The complainant had purchased a plot in the said project having an approximate 250 sq. yard.</p><p>The complainant had made payment of Rs 13,87,500/- at the time of allotment, on which the respondent had issued a letter for expression of interest to the complainant dated 26.03.2012 -<b><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">Annexure C-1</span></b>&nbsp;</p><p>The respondent sent a letter and assured that they would deliver the possession of plot by year 2015 -<b><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">Annexure C-2</span></b></p><p>The respondent had issued a letter in 17.03.2014 wherein they requested for further sum of deposit to the tune of Rs. 9,25,000/- and assured that the project has reached its final stage and they would be in a position to deliver the possession of plot by 2015 -&nbsp;<b><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">Annexure C-3</span></b></p><p>That being influenced by the assurances and representations made by the respondent, the complainant paid Rs.15,00,000/- on the asking of the respondent vide cheque dated 09 Jan 2018 -<b><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">Annexure C-4</span></b></p><p>The respondent had allotted plot No. 702 admeasuring 250 sq. yard area in year 2018 to the complainant.&nbsp; The respondent had issued a letter to the complainant dated 02.02.2018 wherein the respondent levied the charges of IDC, PLC, Possession charges or any arbitrary charges which were not disclosed or agreed for at the time of initial booking of the plot -&nbsp;<b><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">Annexure C-5</span></b></p><p>It is pertinent to mention here that the respondent has the intention to cheat the complainant since the beginning as it is proved by the malafide act and conduct of the respondent.</p><p>The Complainant has paid INR 28,87,500/- i.e. more than 70% of payment out of total consideration i.e. Basic Sale Price, agreed at the time of booking the plot till Jan.18 -&nbsp;<b><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">Annexure- C-6</span></b></p><p>The possession of the project was committed in the month of March 2015 and now in the month of November 2018 i.e. delay of 44 months from the date of the commitment, only 30% project is completed thus delaying the possession of the plot deliberately or for reasons known best to them.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p>','<p>In view of the facts mentioned in preceding paragraphs, the complainant prays for the following relief(s):-&nbsp;</p><p>i.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To give necessary directions to the respondents for delivery of possession of plot&nbsp; along with interest for delay in delivery of possession till realization as per the provisions of Sec. 18 and Sec.19(3)of the RERA Act read with Rule 16 of PBRE(R&amp;D)Rules,2017.</p><p>ii.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 60 of RERA Act for willful default committed by them.</p><p>iii.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 61 of RERA Act for contravention of Sec.12, Sec.14, and Sec. 16 of RERA Act.</p><p>iv.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To issue directions to make liable every officer concerned i.e. Director, Manager, Secretary, or any other officer of the respondent’s company at whose instance, connivance, acquiescence, neglect any of the offences has been committed as mentioned in Sec.69 of RERA Act,2016 to be read with Punjab RERA Rules,2017.</p><p>v.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To recommend criminal action against the respondents for the criminal offence of cheating, fraud and criminal breach of trust under section 420,406 and 409 of the Indian Penal Code.</p><p>vi.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To issue direction to pay the cost of litigation.</p><p>vii.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To issue direction to pay the compensation to complainant for compensation for his mental agony, pain and harassment.<br></p><p>viii.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Any other relief which this Hon’ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances of this complaint.</p><div><br></div>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>-</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'JNSingh1','2018-11-22 16:35:47.000','JNSingh1','2018-11-22 16:35:47.000'),(356,1128,'1128',1225,'fafedfd6-7d94-407d-bfcd-4cea99a9625a','FormTypeM',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','J N Singh','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9816400801,0,0,'312 2 Rani Ka 