%; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">Annexure C-4</span></b></div><div>It is pertinent to mention here that the respondent has the intention to cheat the complainant since the beginning as it is proved by the malafide act and conduct of the respondent.</div><div>The Complainant has paid INR 33,12,500/- i.e. more than 80% of payment out of total consideration i.e. Basic Sale Price, agreed at the time of booking the plot till Jan.18 -&nbsp;<b><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">Annexure- C-5</span></b></div><div>The possession of the project was committed in the month of March 2015 and now in the month of November 2018 i.e. delay of 44 months from the date of the commitment, only 30% project is completed thus delaying the possession of the plot deliberately or for reasons known best to them.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div>','<p>In view of the facts mentioned in preceding paragraphs, the complainant prays for the following relief(s):-&nbsp;</p><p>i.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To give necessary directions to the respondents for delivery of possession of plot&nbsp; along with interest for delay in delivery of possession till realization as per the provisions of Sec. 18 and Sec.19(3)of the RERA Act read with Rule 16 of PSRE(R&amp;D)Rules,2017.</p><p>ii.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 60 of RERA Act for willful default committed by them.</p><p>iii.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 61 of RERA Act for contravention of Sec.12, Sec.14, and Sec. 16 of RERA Act.</p><p>iv.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To issue directions to make liable every officer concerned i.e. Director, Manager, Secretary, or any other officer of the respondent’s company at whose instance, connivance, acquiescence, neglect any of the offences has been committed as mentioned in Sec.69 of RERA Act,2016 to be read with Punjab RERA Rules,2017.</p><p>v.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To recommend criminal action against the respondents for the criminal offence of cheating, fraud and criminal breach of trust under section 420,406 and 409 of the Indian Penal Code.</p><p>vi.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To issue direction to pay the cost of litigation.</p><p>vii.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To issue direction to pay the compensation to complainant for compensation for his mental agony, pain and harassment.</p><p>viii.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Any other relief which this Hon’ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances of this complaint.</p><div><br></div>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>--</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'JNSingh1','2018-11-22 16:46:15.000','JNSingh1','2018-11-22 16:46:15.000'),(357,1087,'1087',1135,'7ce4ff29-c893-46aa-aac9-b9c5d5926814','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-11-22 17:05:34.000','Prem Nath Sharma','akhilesh@vyaslawassociates.com',9815065180,0,0,'3549, Bank Wali Gali, Vijay Nagar, Batala road, Amritsar','',28,39,'143001','1','3549, Bank Wali Gali, Vijay Nagar, Batala road, Amritsar','',28,39,'143001','akhilesh vyas','akhilesh@vyaslawassociates.com',9855004557,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-ASR02-PR0169','Guru Ram Dass Urban Estate','Punjab Urban Planning Development Authority','ca@puda.gov.in',0,0,'PUDA Bhawan','green avenue',28,39,'143001','1','PUDA Bhawan','green avenue',28,39,'143001','1','<p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:8.35pt;margin-left:\r\n0in;line-height:16.75pt\"><span style=\"font-size:13.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:11.0pt;\r\nline-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-theme-font:minor-fareast;mso-bidi-font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;mso-ansi-language:EN-US;\r\nmso-fareast-language:EN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\">That the complainant was\r\nallotted residential plot by Punjab Urban Planning and Development Authority\r\n(hereinafter called as “PUDA”) bearing residential plot No. 334 measuring 300\r\nSq. Yards at Guru Ram Dass Urban Estate Airport Road, Amritsar. The total price\r\nof the residential plot of Rs. 54.00 lacs only @ Rs. 18000/- per Sq. Yard. As\r\nper the payment schedule given in the allotment letter 25% of the allotment\r\namount was to be paid initially and rest of the payment was to be paid after\r\nthe possession. The brochure of the scheme clearly reflects that possession on\r\n25% payment as per the allotment letter it admitted by the respondent that\r\npayment of Rs. 1350000/- was made by the applicant and it has already been\r\nadjusted towards initial 25% of the sale price of residential plot as mentioned\r\nin clause No. 3.1. For the balance payment of 75%, the complainant is always ready and willing to pay the amount as per schedule.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 13pt; font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif;\"><br></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:8.35pt;margin-left:\r\n0in;line-height:16.75pt\"><span style=\"font-size: 13pt; font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif;\">That no possession has been handed over up till now and there is no\r\ndevelopment at the site at all. Various letters, representations has been forwarded to the\r\nEstate Officer PUDA Amritsar and RTI applications have been filed to their\r\nofficers but nothing has resulted fruitful. The possession was scheduled to be\r\ngiven within 90 days after making payment of 25% but nothing has been done in\r\nthis regard. The complainant has approached earlier Hon\'ble Punjab and Haryana\r\nHigh court vide which their representation was decided and she withdrew the\r\nearlier petition for seeking relief under this act.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:8.35pt;margin-left:\r\n0in;line-height:16.75pt\"><span style=\"font-size: 13pt; font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif;\">That the copy of the photographs of the site, RTI Application, letters to Estate Officers, speaking order and order of High Court are attached as annexures for the kind perusal of the court.&nbsp;</span></p>','<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"margin-left:.75in;mso-add-space:auto;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;text-indent:-.5in;line-height:\r\n200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size:13.0pt;\r\nmso-bidi-font-size:11.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;\">i)<span style=\"font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Th</span></span></span><span style=\"font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif; line-height: 17.55pt; text-indent: -0.5in; font-size: 14px;\">e respondents shall be directed to hand over the possession\r\nalongwith entire development as per agreed terms and conditions to be done by\r\nthe respondents.&nbsp;</span></p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">\r\n\r\n</span><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-left:.75in;mso-add-space:\r\nauto;text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size:13.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:11.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">ii)</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: normal; font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; </span></span><span style=\"font-size:13.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:\r\n11.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">That the respondent shall directed that applicant/ complainant is not liable to pay any amount by way of penal interest if any\r\ncharged by the respondent department. The respondent shall further be directed to refund any\r\npenal interest charged up till now as the delay any occurred is because of the\r\nconduct and acts of the respondent department. &nbsp;Further respondent shall be directed that the interest already paid shall be\r\nrefunded or interest amount which is\r\nalready&nbsp; been charged by the respondents\r\nshall stands adjusted in the future payments as the delay has occurred due to\r\nlapse on the part of the respondents.&nbsp;</span><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-left:.75in;mso-add-space:\r\nauto;text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size:13.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:11.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">iii)</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: normal; font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; </span></span><span style=\"font-size:13.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:\r\n11.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">That the respondent shall be directed to pay sufficient compensation as per the statue &nbsp;to the complainant as they\r\nhave been denied their physical possession up till now without any explanatory\r\nreason by the department. &nbsp;&nbsp;</span><o:p></o:p></span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"margin-left:.75in;mso-add-space:auto;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;text-indent:-.5in;line-height:\r\n200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size:13.0pt;\r\nmso-bidi-font-size:11.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">iv)</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: normal; font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; </span></span><span style=\"font-size:13.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:\r\n11.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">That as stated\r\nabove the extension was sought by the complainant for 180 days and during that period interest was charged by\r\nthe respondents. The respondents shall be directed to refund that interest\r\namount or adjust that amount in the principal amount in future payments.&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><o:p></o:p></span></p>',5400000.00,1350000.00,'2017-03-02 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"margin-left: 0.75in; text-align: justify; text-indent: -0.5in; line-height: 28px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13pt; line-height: 34px; font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">i) &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; That the interest and penal interest on the pending payments, if any, shall be put to moratorium during the pendency by the department till the date of handing over the final possession.&nbsp;</span></span></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"margin-left: 0.75in; text-align: justify; text-indent: -0.5in; line-height: 28px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13pt; line-height: 34px; font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">ii) &nbsp; &nbsp;Th</span></span></span><span style=\"font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif; line-height: 17.55pt; text-indent: -0.5in;\">e respondents shall be directed to hand over the possession alongwith entire development as per agreed terms and conditions to be done by the respondents.&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-left: 0.75in; text-align: justify; text-indent: -0.5in; line-height: 28px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13pt; line-height: 34px; font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">iii)</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: normal; font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span><span style=\"font-size: 13pt; line-height: 34px; font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">That the respondent shall directed that applicant/ complainant is not liable to pay any amount by way of penal interest if any charged by the respondent department. The respondent shall further be directed to refund any penal interest charged up till now as the delay any occurred is because of the conduct and acts of the respondent department. &nbsp;Further respondent shall be directed that the interest already paid shall be refunded or interest amount which is already&nbsp; been charged by the respondents shall stands adjusted in the future payments as the delay has occurred due to lapse on the part of the respondents.&nbsp;</span><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-left: 0.75in; text-align: justify; text-indent: -0.5in; line-height: 28px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13pt; line-height: 34px; font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">iv)</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: normal; font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span><span style=\"font-size: 13pt; line-height: 34px; font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">That the respondent shall be directed to pay sufficient compensation as per the statue &nbsp;to the complainant as they have been denied their physical possession up till now without any explanatory reason by the department. &nbsp;&nbsp;</span><o:p></o:p></span></p><p></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"margin-left:.75in;mso-add-space:auto;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;text-indent:-.5in;line-height:\r\n200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span style=\"line-height: 20px; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px;\"></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"margin-left: 0.75in; text-align: justify; text-indent: -0.5in; line-height: 28px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13pt; line-height: 34px; font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">v)</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: normal; font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span><span style=\"font-size: 13pt; line-height: 34px; font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">That as stated above the extension was sought by the&nbsp; complainant for 180 days and during that period interest was charged by the respondents. The respondents shall be directed to refund that interest amount or adjust that amount in the principal amount in future payments. &nbsp;</span></span></p>','1','','2016-12-02 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','334','','',1,1,0,0,'akhilesh','2018-11-22 16:58:17.000','akhilesh','2018-11-22 16:58:17.000'),(358,1093,'1093',1135,'7ce4ff29-c893-46aa-aac9-b9c5d5926814','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-11-22 17:24:25.000','Gursharan Singh','akhilesh@vyaslawassociates.com',9855004557,0,0,'house No. 4475, Ranjitpura PO Khalsa College, Amritsar ','',28,39,'143001','1','house No. 4475, Ranjitpura PO Khalsa College, Amritsar ','',28,39,'143001','akhilesh vyas','akhilesh@vyaslawassociates.com',9855004557,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-ASR02-PR0169','Guru Ram Dass Urban Estate','Punjab Urban Planning Development Authority','ca@puda.gov.in',0,0,'PUDA Bhawan','green avenue',28,39,'143001','1','PUDA Bhawan','green avenue',28,39,'143001','1','<p><span style=\"font-size:13.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:11.0pt;\r\nline-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-theme-font:minor-fareast;mso-bidi-font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;mso-ansi-language:EN-US;\r\nmso-fareast-language:EN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\">That the complainant was\r\nallotted residential plot by Punjab Urban Planning and Development Authority\r\n(hereinafter called as “PUDA”) bearing residential plot No. 345 measuring 300\r\nSq. Yards at Guru Ram Dass Urban Estate Airport Road, Amritsar. The total price\r\nof the residential plot of Rs. 54.00 lacs only @ Rs. 18000/- per Sq. Yard. As\r\nper the payment schedule given in the allotment letter 25% of the allotment\r\namount was to be paid initially and rest of the payment was to be paid after\r\nthe possession. The brochure of the scheme clearly reflects that possession on\r\n25% payment as per the allotment letter it admitted by the respondent that\r\npayment of Rs. 1350000/-was made by the complainant and it has already been\r\nadjusted towards initial 25% of the sale price of residential plot as mentioned\r\nin clause No. 3.1.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif; font-size: 13pt; line-height: 16.75pt;\">For the balance payment of 75%, the complainant is always ready\r\nand willing to pay the amount as per schedule.&nbsp;</span></p><p><font face=\"Bookman Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 17px; line-height: 22.328125px;\">That the copy of the photographs of the site, RTI Application, letters to Estate Officers and order of High Court are attached as annexures for the kind perusal of this Hon\'ble court.&nbsp;</span></font><br><span style=\"font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif; font-size: 13pt; line-height: 16.75pt;\">That no possession has been handed over up till now. there is no\r\ndevelopment at the site at all. Various letters has been forwarded to the\r\nEstate Officer PUDA Amritsar and RTI applications have been filed to their\r\nofficers but nothing has resulted fruitful. The possession was scheduled to be\r\ngiven within 90 days after making payment of 25% but nothing has been done in\r\nthis regard. The complainant has approached earlier Hon\'ble Punjab and Haryana\r\nHigh court vide which their representation was decided and she withdrew the\r\nearlier petition for seeking relief under this act.</span><br></p>','<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:\r\n6.25pt;margin-left:.75in;text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\ntext-indent:-.5in;line-height:17.55pt;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 9pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">i)</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: normal; font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Th</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px; font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif;\">e\r\nrespondents shall be directed to hand over the possession alongwith entire\r\ndevelopment as per agreed terms and conditions to be done by the respondents.</span><span style=\"font-size: 9pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:\r\n6.25pt;margin-left:.75in;text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\ntext-indent:-.5in;line-height:17.55pt\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px; font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif;\">ii)</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px; font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif;\">That the respondent shall directed\r\nthat applicant/ complainant is not liable to pay any amount by way of penal\r\ninterest if any charged by the respondent department. The respondent shall\r\nfurther be directed to refund any penal interest charged up till now as the\r\ndelay any occurred is because of the conduct and acts of the respondent\r\ndepartment. &nbsp;Further respondent shall be directed that the interest\r\nalready paid shall be refunded or interest amount which is already&nbsp; been\r\ncharged by the respondents shall stands adjusted in the future payments as the\r\ndelay has occurred due to lapse on the part of the respondents.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 9pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:\r\n6.25pt;margin-left:.75in;text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\ntext-indent:-.5in;line-height:17.55pt\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px; font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif;\">iii)</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px; font-family: \'Bookman Old Style\', serif;\">That\r\nthe respondent shall be directed to pay sufficient compensation as per the\r\nstatue &nbsp;to the complainant as they have been denied their physical\r\npossession up till now without any explanatory reason by the department.\r\n&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 9pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:\r\n6.25pt;margin-left:.75in;text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\ntext-indent:-.5in;line-height:17.55pt\"><span style=\