ment out of total consideration i.e. Basic Sale Price, agreed at the time of booking the plot till Jan.18 -&nbsp;<b><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">Annexure- C-6</span></b></p><p>The possession of the project was committed in the month of March 2015 and now in the month of November 2018 i.e. delay of 44 months from the date of the commitment, only 30% project is completed thus delaying the possession of the plot deliberately or for reasons known best to them.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p>','<p>In view of the facts mentioned in preceding paragraphs, the complainant prays for the following relief(s):-&nbsp;</p><p>i.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To give necessary directions to the respondents for delivery of possession of plot&nbsp; along with interest for delay in delivery of possession till realization as per the provisions of Sec. 18 and Sec.19(3)of the RERA Act read with Rule 16 of PBRE(R&amp;D)Rules,2017.</p><p>ii.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 60 of RERA Act for willful default committed by them.</p><p>iii.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 61 of RERA Act for contravention of Sec.12, Sec.14, and Sec. 16 of RERA Act.</p><p>iv.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To issue directions to make liable every officer concerned i.e. Director, Manager, Secretary, or any other officer of the respondent’s company at whose instance, connivance, acquiescence, neglect any of the offences has been committed as mentioned in Sec.69 of RERA Act,2016 to be read with Punjab RERA Rules,2017.</p><p>v.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To recommend criminal action against the respondents for the criminal offence of cheating, fraud and criminal breach of trust under section 420,406 and 409 of the Indian Penal Code.</p><p>vi.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To issue direction to pay the cost of litigation.</p><p>vii.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To issue direction to pay the compensation to complainant for compensation for his mental agony, pain and harassment.<br></p><p>viii.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Any other relief which this Hon’ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances of this complaint.</p><div><br></div>',4625000.00,2887500.00,'2015-12-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>i. To direct the respondent not to demand further amount from the complainant.</p><p>ii. The respondent should be restrained from harassing the complainant in any&nbsp;manner whatsoever.<br></p><p><br></p>','1','','2012-03-26 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Plot Number 702  Villages Mullanpur Dhanauran and Masatgarh LPAMullanpur\r\nSAS Nagar\r\n','','',2,0,0,0,'JNSingh1','2018-11-22 18:02:37.000','JNSingh1','2018-11-22 18:02:37.000'),(364,1128,'1128',1225,'fafedfd6-7d94-407d-bfcd-4cea99a9625a','FormTypeM',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','J N Singh','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9816400801,0,0,'312 2 Rani Ka Bagh ','Shimla Road, NAHAN',14,544,'173001','1','312 2, Rani Ka Bagh','Shimla Road, NAHAN',14,544,'173001','Kamal Dahiya','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9729902009,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0093','Palm Eco City','Manohar Infrastructure and Constructions Private Limited','nbs@manoharrealty.com',0,1725016888,'SCO 139 141 Level 1 Sector 17C','',6,128,'160017','1','SCO 139 141 Level 1 Sector 17C','',6,128,'160017','1','<div><div>The complainant had purchased a plot in the said project having an approximate 250 sq. yard.</div><div>The complainant had made payment of Rs 23,12,500/- at the time of allotment, on which the respondent had issued a letter for expression of interest to the complainant dated 26.03.2012 -<b><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">Annexure C-1</span></b>&nbsp;</div><div>The respondent sent a letter and assured that they would deliver the possession of plot by year 2015 -<b><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">Annexure C-2</span></b></div><div>The respondent had issued a letter in 17.03.2014 wherein they assured that the project has reached its final stage and they would be in a position to deliver the possession of plot by 2015&nbsp;</div><div>That being influenced by the assurances and representations made by the respondent, the complainant paid Rs.10,00,000/- on the asking of the respondent vide cheque dated 09 Jan 2018 -<b><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">Annexure C-3</span></b></div><div>The respondent had allotted plot No. 1035 admeasuring 250 sq. yard area in year 2018 to the complainant.&nbsp; The respondent had issued a letter to the complainant dated 02.02.2018 wherein the respondent levied the charges of IDC, PLC, Possession charges or any arbitrary charges which were not disclosed or agreed for at the time of initial booking of the plot -&nbsp;<b><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">Annexure C-4</span></b></div><div>It is pertinent to mention here that the respondent has the intention to cheat the complainant since the beginning as it is proved by the malafide act and conduct of the respondent.</div><div>The Complainant has paid INR 33,12,500/- i.e. more than 80% of payment out of total consideration i.e. Basic Sale Price, agreed at the time of booking the plot till Jan.18 -&nbsp;<b><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">Annexure- C-5</span></b></div><div>The possession of the project was committed in the month of March 2015 and now in the month of November 2018 i.e. delay of 44 months from the date of the commitment, only 30% project is completed thus delaying the possession of the plot deliberately or for reasons known best to them.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div>','<p>In view of the facts mentioned in preceding paragraphs, the complainant prays for the following relief(s):-&nbsp;</p><p>i.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To give necessary directions to the respondents for delivery of possession of plot&nbsp; along with interest for delay in delivery of possession till realization as per the provisions of Sec. 18 and Sec.19(3)of the RERA Act read with Rule 16 of PSRE(R&amp;D)Rules,2017.</p><p>ii.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 60 of RERA Act for willful default committed by them.</p><p>iii.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 61 of RERA Act for contravention of Sec.12, Sec.14, and Sec. 16 of RERA Act.</p><p>iv.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To issue directions to make liable every officer concerned i.e. Director, Manager, Secretary, or any other officer of the respondent’s company at whose instance, connivance, acquiescence, neglect any of the offences has been committed as mentioned in Sec.69 of RERA Act,2016 to be read with Punjab RERA Rules,2017.</p><p>v.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To recommend criminal action against the respondents for the criminal offence of cheating, fraud and criminal breach of trust under section 420,406 and 409 of the Indian Penal Code.</p><p>vi.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To issue direction to pay the cost of litigation.</p><p>vii.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To issue direction to pay the compensation to complainant for compensation for his mental agony, pain and harassment.</p><p>viii.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Any other relief which this Hon’ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances of this complaint.</p><div><br></div>',4625000.00,3312500.00,'2015-12-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>i. To direct the respondent not to demand any further amount from the Complainant.</p><p>ii. The respondent should be restrained from harassing the complainant in any manner whatsoever.</p><p></p><p>iii.<span style=\"white-space: pre;\">	</span>Any other interim relief which this Hon’ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances of this complaint.</p><div><br></div>','1','','2012-03-26 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Plot Number 1035 Villages Mullanpur Dhanauran and Masatgarh LPAMullanpur\r\nSAS Nagar','','',1,0,0,0,'JNSingh1','2018-11-22 18:12:26.000','JNSingh1','2018-11-22 18:12:26.000'),(365,1131,'1131',1225,'fafedfd6-7d94-407d-bfcd-4cea99a9625a','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-11-22 18:33:20.000','J N Singh','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9816400801,0,0,'312 2, Rani Ka Bagh','Shimla Road, NAHAN',14,544,'173001','1','312 2, Rani Ka Bagh','Shimla Road, NAHAN',14,544,'173001','Kamal Dahiya','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9729902008,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0093','Palm Garden','Manohar Infrastructure and Constructions Private Limited','nbs@manoharrealty.com',0,1725016888,'SCO 139 141 Level 1 Sector 17C','',6,128,'160017','1','SCO 139 141 Level 1 Sector 17C','',6,128,'160017','1','<p>The complainant had purchased a plot in the said project having an approximate 250 sq. yard.</p><p>The complainant had made payment of Rs 13,87,500/- at the time of allotment, on which the respondent had issued a letter for expression of interest to the complainant dated 26.03.2012 -<b><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">Annexure C-1</span></b>&nbsp;</p><p>The respondent sent a letter and assured that they would deliver the possession of plot by year 2015 -<b><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">Annexure C-2</span></b></p><p>The respondent had issued a letter in 17.03.2014 wherein they requested for further sum of deposit to the tune of Rs. 9,25,000/- and assured that the project has reached its final stage and they would be in a position to deliver the possession of plot by 2015 -&nbsp;<b><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">Annexure C-3</span></b></p><p>That being influenced by the assurances and representations made by the respondent, the complainant paid Rs.15,00,000/- on the asking of the respondent vide cheque dated 09 Jan 2018 -<b><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">Annexure C-4</span></b></p><p>The respondent had allotted plot No. 702 admeasuring 250 sq. yard area in year 2018 to the complainant.&nbsp; The respondent had issued a letter to the complainant dated 02.02.2018 wherein the respondent levied the charges of IDC, PLC, Possession charges or any arbitrary charges which were not disclosed or agreed for at the time of initial booking of the plot -&nbsp;<b><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">Annexure C-5</span></b></p><p>It is pertinent to mention here that the respondent has the intention to cheat the complainant since the beginning as it is proved by the malafide act and conduct of the respondent.</p><p>The Complainant has paid INR 28,87,500/- i.e. more than 70% of payment out of total consideration i.e. Basic Sale Price, agreed at the time of booking the plot till Jan.18 -&nbsp;<b><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">Annexure- C-6</span></b></p><p>The possession of the project was committed in the month of March 2015 and now in the month of November 2018 i.e. delay of 44 months from the date of the commitment, only 30% project is completed thus delaying the possession of the plot deliberately or for reasons known best to them.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p>','<p>In view of the facts mentioned in preceding paragraphs, the complainant prays for the following relief(s):-&nbsp;</p><p>i.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To give necessary directions to the respondents for delivery of possession of plot&nbsp; along with interest for delay in delivery of possession till realization as per the provisions of Sec. 18 and Sec.19(3)of the RERA Act read with Rule 16 of PBRE(R&amp;D)Rules,2017.</p><p>ii.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 60 of RERA Act for willful default committed by them.</p><p>iii.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 61 of RERA Act for contravention of Sec.12, Sec.14, and Sec. 16 of RERA Act.</p><p>iv.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To issue directions to make liable every officer concerned i.e. Director, Manager, Secretary, or any other officer of the respondent’s company at whose instance, connivance, acquiescence, neglect any of the offences has been committed as mentioned in Sec.69 of RERA Act,2016 to be read with Punjab RERA Rules,2017.</p><p>v.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To recommend criminal action against the respondents for the criminal offence of cheating, fraud and criminal breach of trust under section 420,406 and 409 of the Indian Penal Code.</p><p>vi.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To issue direction to pay the cost of litigation.</p><p>vii.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To issue direction to pay the compensation to complainant for compensation for his mental agony, pain and harassment.<br></p><p>viii.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Any other relief which this Hon’ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances of this complaint.</p>',4625000.00,2887500.00,'2015-12-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>i. To direct the respondent not to demand any further amount whatsoever from the complainant.</p><p>ii. The respondent should be restrained from harassing the complainant in any&nbsp;manner whatsoever.<br></p><p>iii. Any other interim relief which this Hon’ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances of this complaint.<br></p>','1','','2012-03-26 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Plot Number 702  Villages Mullanpur Dhanauran and Masatgarh LPAMullanpur\r\nSAS Nagar\r\n','','',1,1,0,0,'JNSingh1','2018-11-22 18:20:34.000','JNSingh1','2018-11-22 18:20:34.000'),(366,1136,'1136',1010,'a182232b-88d6-4711-8baa-f8a026fb675f','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-11-22 19:57:37.000','MANUJESHWAR SINGH ','lawofficeofhimanshuraj@gmail.com',9988100005,1724181010,947441237195,'#102, Sector 10 A','',6,128,'160011','1','#102, Sector 10 A','',6,128,'160011','HIMANSHU RAJ','lawofficeofhimanshuraj@gmail.com',9988200001,1724190909,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0240','MUIRWOODS','Altus Space Builders Private Limited','altusoffice@yahoo.co.in',1724003734,0,'SCO 22','1ST FLOOR, PHASE X, MOHALI',28,39,'160062','1','SCO 22','1ST FLOOR, PHASE X, MOHALI',28,39,'160062','1','<p>Facts in Brief</p><p>1.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That the complainant is a citizen of India and is residing at the above mentioned address. The Aadhar card of the complainant is annexed as ANNEXURE C 1. The complainant had applied for a plot in the OP s project by submitting the duly filled application form annexed as ANNEXURE C 2 after perusing the brochure given by the OP to the public at large as well as the complainant. Moreover The complainant had given his hard earned money in the OP s Project MUIRWOODS situated in Village Bhagat Majra Palheri Mullanpur Tehsil Kharar Distt. SAS Nagar Mohali Punjab for purchasing the residential plot based on assurance and promises of the OP which later on proved to be the false assurances and promises of the OP as well as the agents authorized representatives of the ALTUS SPACE BUILDERS PRIVATE LIMITED OP.</p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Rest of the Facts of the case is annexed as a complaint</p>','<p>Relief Sought</p><p>i<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To direct the OP to compensate the complainant in the shape of refund of the complete amount which has been deposited against the residential property so booked by the complainant along with an Interest on the amount from the date of deposit at the rate of 20 per cent&nbsp; till the actual realization of the complete amount within 90 days according to section 18 1 Real Estate Regulation And Development Act 2016 18 2 Real Estate Regulation And Development Act 2016 Section 19 4 of The Real Estate Regulation And Development Act 2016 r w Rule 16 and Rule 17 of Punjab State Real Estate Regulation and Development Rules 2017.</p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Rest of the Facts of the case is annexed as a complaint</p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Not Prayed','1','','2015-08-30 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'lawofficeofhimanshuraj','2018-11-22 18:25:00.000','lawofficeofhimanshuraj','2018-11-22 18:25:00.000'),(367,1137,'1137',1091,'e2da2916-c5af-4a15-acce-51dcf84d70a2','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Vivek Jaggi','captvivekjaggi@yahoo.com',9582854003,0,0,'House No. 192, Lane D,','Lakshapuram Ladpur, Raipur Road, Dehradun',34,162,'248008','1','House No. 2378, Sector 35-C,','',6,128,'160035','Rajeev Anand','anandlawoffice2378@gmail.com',9417870805,1722622364,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0153','Wave Estate Project','M/s Country Colonizers Pvt Ltd Through its MD','customercare@waveestate.in',0,0,'PO Rayon and Silk Mills','Adjoining Coca Cola Depot GT Road, Chheharta',28,39,'143105','0','M/s Country Colonizers Pvt Ltd. Wave Estate Project site office sector 85','SAS Nagar Mohali',28,507,'140308','1','<p style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0cm;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">The Complainant booked Apartment&nbsp;No.\r\n67 SF, 2nd Floor Sec- G, Wave Floor, Sec 99 Mohali on 05.02.2013 making initial\r\npayments <b>(Annexure C-1)﻿.</b> Agreement\r\nwas executed for area 1060sqFt @ 3773.58/sqFt.&nbsp;As per Clause 5.2, the\r\nProject was to be developed and Apartment was to be handed over in 24 months\r\n&amp; by Cl. 5.5, Rs. 5/sqFt/month was to be paid for delay but copy of\r\nAgreement though signed not given to Complainant. The Complainant was given\r\nloan in June 2013<b>.</b>&nbsp;On 27.01.2015,\r\nthe Complainant was made to fill another Agreement <b>(Annexure C-2)</b> and the Apartment of the Complainant was\r\nunilaterally changed with new No. 44/SF, Wave Floor Sec 99, Mohali.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0cm;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">The Complainant found that site plan of\r\nApartment has been changed by closing bathroom door opening in bedroom etc.\r\nHaving found the Project and the Apartment delayed, the Complainant being in\r\nArmy and handicapped in monitoring the development pace due to hard and remote\r\narea posting kept approaching the Promoter Office telephonically that\r\nconstruction started with 2 years delay &amp; not completed &amp; that even\r\nafter 4 1/2 years possession not offered. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0cm;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">The apartment was to be completed &amp;\r\nhanded over by January 2016 but not done against which Complainant visited and\r\nmet the officials of the Promoter. The Respondent made unilateral Deed of\r\nSettlement on 28.06.2018 <b>(Annexure C-3)</b>\r\nto give interest and also possession but since not honoured by Respondent, the\r\nDeed of Settlement became redundant.&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0cm;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Now on 08.10.2018 <b>(Annexure C-4)</b> a Statement of Account has been given wherein area\r\nincreased and money charged for that without any increase in Apartment area.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">The Complainant has no shelter inspite of spending huge amount &amp;\r\nleft in lurch.</span><br></p>','<p>The Apartment was to be handed over after completing the Project in 24 months +6 Months &amp; monthly compensation of Rs5/SqFt/month was to be paid from Jan 2016 onwards till date but NOT PAID.\r\n</p><p>The Respondent has taken the total sale price as Rs. 3 Lakhs on 05.02.13 and 3 lakhs on 30.03.13 + 2 Lakhs on 27.03.15 + 10 Lakhs on 31.03.2015 + 42000 on 15.11.15 + 10 Lakhs on 18.11.2015 + 6 lakhs on 26.06.17 + 26000 on 30.07.17 + 86000 on 11.01.2018 totaling 36 Lakhs (+ service Tax on each payment) as also EMIs with interest.\r\n</p><p>Inspite of elapsing of over 5 years of Agreement, no development &amp; construction works have been completed in the Complex and the Respondent Promoter has failed in its obligation towards the Complex and Independent Floor allotted to the Complainant. The Respondent Promoter is liable to pay the interest on the payment so received for the period of delay in offering possession after the completion of the development works of the project and the completion of the construction of the Independent Residential Floor. The possession is given in incomplete project. The relative of an Allottee who took possession recently suffered electrocution and was in ICU as received injuries and burns. The Apartment is not finished. The electric wires are open, potholes are not covered etc. The Promoter is just trying to meet the time limit without completion and full development.  \r\n</p><p>In view of the above : \r\n</p><p>(i) The Applicant is seeking compensation as applicable in Para 5.5 of Agreement from January 2016 onwards till date; \r\n</p><p>(ii) directions for completion of the development works of the project and the construction of the independent residential floor in question without any further delay and also offer the possession after the grant of Occupation Certificate of the Building and the Completion Certificate of the Wave Estate Project alongwith interest and compensation prescribed under Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Act 2016 as the action of the Respondent.</p>',4000000.00,3600000.00,'2016-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:\r\njustify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;line-height:150%;mso-layout-grid-align:\r\nnone;text-autospace:none\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:150%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Pending final decision on the complaint the\r\ncomplainant seeks issue of the following interim order :<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:\r\njustify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;line-height:150%;mso-layout-grid-align:\r\nnone;text-autospace:none\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:150%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">The respondents be directed to complete the\r\ndevelopment works of the project and the construction of the independent\r\nresidential floor in question without any further delay and also offer the\r\npossession after the grant of occupation certificate of the Building and the\r\nCompletion Certificate of the Wave Estate Project.&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">The Promoter be also\r\ndirected to pay interim monthly interest and compensation till the completion\r\nof the project and the complex in question in the pendency of the complaint</span>.</span></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','2015-01-27 00:00:00','Independent Residential Floor Bearing No. 67 SF, 2nd Floor Sec- G, Wave Floor, Sec 99 Mohali','','',2,0,0,0,'RajeevAnand','2018-11-23 14:59:32.000','RajeevAnand','2018-11-23 14:59:32.000'),(368,1138,'1138',1091,'e2da2916-c5af-4a15-acce-51dcf84d70a2','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Chaman Chandel','chamanchandel@gmail.com',8146000152,0,0,'House No. 146-A, ','Sector 42-A,',6,128,'160036','1','House No. 2378, ','Sector 35-C,',6,128,'160035','Rajeev Anand','anandlawoffice2378@gmail.com',9417807085,1722622364,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0153','Wave Estate Project','M/s Country Colonizers Pvt Ltd Through its MD','customercare@waveestate.in',0,0,'PO Rayon and Silk Mills','Adjoining Coca Cola Depot GT Road, Chheharta',28,39,'143105','0','M/s Country Colonizers Pvt Ltd. Wave Estate Project site office sector 85','SAS Nagar Mohali',28,507,'140308','1','<p>The Complainant booked Unit No. 61 SF, 2nd Floor Sec- G, Wave Floor, Sec 99 Mohali on 05.02.2013 making initial payments (Annexure C-1). Agreement dated 11.07.2013 (Annexure C-2) was executed for area 1060sqFt @ 3773.58/sqFt. As per Clause 5.2, the Project was to be developed and Apartment was to be handed over in 24 months &amp; by Cl. 5.5, Rs. 5/sqFt/month was to be paid for delay. The Complainant was given loan in May 2013 &amp; revalidated in November 2014 (Annexure C-3). On 20.01.2015, the Complainant was made to fill another Agreement (Annexure C-4) and the Apartment of the Complainant was unilaterally changed (Annexure C-5) with new No. 43/SF, Wave Floor Sec 99, Mohali.\r\n</p><p>The Complainant’s Loan account facility was endorsed (Annexure C-6) for the Apartment. The Complainant found that site plan of Apartment has been changed by closing bathroom door opening in bedroom etc.. Having found the Project and the Apartment delayed, Complainant gave representation 31.10.2016 (Annexure C-7) that construction started with 2 years delay &amp; not completed. The complainant gave another representation by email in May 2017 (Annexure C-8) &amp; another representation dated 01.09.2017 (Annexure C-9) that even after 4 1/2 years possession not offered. On 03.09.2017 (Annexure C-10) the Complainant wanted to meet the senior executive but no time was given for meeting for delivery of possession. \r\n</p><p>The apartment was to be completed &amp; handed over by 23.01.2016 but not done against which Complainant gave representation dated 23.09.2017 (Annexure C-11).  The Respondent made unilateral Deed of Settlement on 16.12.2017 (Annexure C-12) to give interest and also possession by March 2018 but since not honoured by Respondent, the Deed of Settlement became redundant. Now on 08.10.2018 (Annexure C-13) a Statement of Account has been given wherein area increased and money charged for that without any increase in Apartment area.\r\n</p><p>The Complainant has no shelter inspite of spending huge amount &amp; left in lurch.</p>','<p>The Apartment was to be handed over after completing the Project in 24 months + 6 Months i.e. from 11.07.13 by 11.01.16 &amp; monthly compensation of Rs5/SqFt/month was to be paid from Jan 2016 onwards till date but NOT PAID.\r\n</p><p>The Respondent has taken the total sale price as Rs. 3 Lakhs on 05.02.13 and 3 lakhs on 21.03.13+ Rs 968658 on 13.02.15 + Rs 231342 on 31.03.15+ 1057177 on 16.11.15 +Rs. 142823 on 16.11.15+ 6 lakhs on 22.04.17 totaling 36 Lakhs (+ service Tax on each payment) as also EMIs with interest.\r\n</p><p>Inspite of elapsing of over 5 years of Agreement, no development &amp; construction works have been completed in the Complex and the Promoter has failed in its obligation towards the Complex and Independent Residential Floor allotted to the Complainant. The Respondent Promoter is liable to pay the interest on the payment so received for the period of delay in offering possession after the completion of the development works of the project and the completion of the construction of the Independent Residential Floor. The possession is given in incomplete project. The relative of an Allottee who took possession recently suffered electrocution and was in ICU as received injuries and burns. The Apartment is not finished. The electric wires are open, potholes are not covered etc. The Promoter is just trying to meet the time limit without completion and full development.  \r\n</p><p>In view of the above : \r\n</p><p>(i) The Applicant is seeking compensation as applicable in Para 5.5 of Agreement dated 19.07.2013 from January 2016 onwards till date; \r\n</p><p>(ii) directions for completion of the development works of the project and the construction of the independent residential floor in question without any further delay and also offer the possession after the grant of Occupation Certificate of the Building and the Completion Certificate of the Wave Estate Project alongwith interest and compensation prescribed under Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Act 2016 as the action of the Respondent</p>',4000000.00,3600000.00,'2016-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:\r\njustify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;line-height:150%;mso-layout-grid-align:\r\nnone;text-autospace:none\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:150%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Pending final decision on the complaint the\r\ncomplainant seeks issue of the following interim order </span><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">:</span></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:\r\njustify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;line-height:150%;mso-layout-grid-align:\r\nnone;text-autospace:none\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:150%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><br></span><o:p></o:p></span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">\r\n\r\n</span><span style=\"font-size: 18px; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">The\r\nrespondents be directed to complete the development works of the project and the\r\nconstruction of the independent residential floor in question without any\r\nfurther delay and also offer the possession after the grant of occupation\r\ncertificate of the Building and the Completion Certificate of the Wave Estate\r\nProject.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 18px;\">The Promoter be also\r\ndirected to pay interim monthly interest and compensation till the completion\r\nof the project and the complex in question in the pendency of the complaint.</span><br></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','2013-07-11 00:00:00','Independent Residential Floor No. 61 SF, 2nd Floor Sec- G, Wave Floor, Sec 99 Mohali','','',2,0,0,0,'RajeevAnand','2018-11-23 15:15:47.000','RajeevAnand','2018-11-23 15:15:47.000'),(369,1139,'1139',1211,'962b01f9-ce50-4ce8-b650-bb1037f1b9e3','FormTypeM',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Sanjay Dhiman','vermauvraj@gmail.com',9569656520,0,416668848153,'Flat No .115, Ground Floor, Noor Homes','Kharar Landranroad, Sector 115, Mohali',28,507,'160055','1','Flat No .115, Ground Floor, Noor Homes','Kharar Landranroad, Sector 115, Mohali',28,507,'160055','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0219','M/S. GGP BUILDTECH PRIVATE LIMITED','Mr. Ajay Gupta','ajayguptaggp@gmail.com',9815990640,0,'402, Shivalik City, Sector 127','Kharar , SAS Nagar',28,507,'160055','1','402, Shivalik City, Sector 127','Kharar , SAS Nagar',28,507,'160055','1','<p lang=\"en-US\" class=\"western\" align=\"JUSTIFY\" style=\"margin-left: 0.12in; margin-right: 0.12in; line-height: 103%\">&nbsp;That the project named Noor Homes is currently being\r\npromoted/developed by GGP Buildtech Pvt Limited. The Promoters of M/s\r\nGGP BUILDTECH PVT LTD started their business initially with a\r\nPartnership firm M/s Singla Builders &amp; Promoters in which Sh.\r\nAjay Gupta and Sh. Amandeep Singla were partners. That the Project\r\nNamed Noor Homes is launched by GGP Buildtech Pvt Limited in February\r\n2014. That the Builder (GGP Buildtech Pvt Limited) had come up with\r\nadvertisement/public offer to sell 1, 2, 3 BHK Apartments &amp; 3 BHK\r\nVillas to be constructed at Sector 115, Village Sante Majra, Tehsil\r\nKharar, District Mohali with a construction target to be completed in\r\n2017. That the Complainants (society members) start booking flats\r\nfrom Builder from 2014. That to some Complainants the flats were\r\nforcefully handed over by builder in incomplete stage. That some\r\nComplainants were forced to pay 100% payment to Builder for\r\nincomplete flats by threatening them from goons hired by builders.\r\nThat Some Complainants were forced to execute sale deed for less\r\nprice paying money in cash or for shell companies (Daya Infra) and\r\nthus frauding with GST and service tax.That These flats are\r\nincomplete to such extent that there is no permanent water\r\nconnection,internal roads, electricity, sewerage connections,\r\nSewerage treatment plant, staircase, streetlights, fire protection\r\nsystem etc.That these flats are handed over without obtaining\r\noccupancy certificate from MC khararThat Builder was approached time\r\nto time and several MOM’s were signed but till date.That MOM is\r\nattached as Annexure-1, where in Builder has initially agreed to\r\ncomplete the project by 31-March 2016.That vide MOM dated\r\n30-April-2017 Builder agreed to complete the project by 31-Jan-2018.\r\nThat again MOM vide 18.09.2017 Builder agreed to complete project in\r\nnext 6 months i.e Mar-2018. That status of project is same as\r\nmentioned in point No.9</p>','<p lang=\"en-US\" class=\"western\" align=\"JUSTIFY\" style=\"margin-left: 0.12in; margin-right: 0.13in; line-height: 103%\">Transfer of All Unsold Properties to Society (will be incorporated within 15 days of order by RERA)</p><p lang=\"en-US\" class=\"western\" align=\"JUSTIFY\" style=\"margin-left: 0.12in; margin-right: 0.13in; line-height: 103%\">Direct PSPCL for permanent electricity connections for the 65\r\nfamilies (Complainant).</p><p lang=\"en-US\" class=\"western\" align=\"JUSTIFY\" style=\"margin-left: 0.12in; margin-right: 0.13in; line-height: 103%\">Direct MC kharar for permanent water and\r\nsewerage connections to the society.</p><p lang=\"en-US\" class=\"western\" align=\"JUSTIFY\" style=\"margin-left: 0.12in; margin-right: 0.13in; line-height: 103%\">Direct Inquiry against\r\ninvolvement of Municipal Corporation with Builder in cheating the\r\nPublic by allowing sale deed to be executed without issuing occupancy\r\ncertificate.</p><p lang=\"en-US\" class=\"western\" align=\"JUSTIFY\" style=\"margin-left: 0.12in; margin-right: 0.13in; line-height: 103%\">Direct Inquiry against Builder regarding diversion of\r\nproject funds to other shell companies.</p><p lang=\"en-US\" class=\"western\" align=\"JUSTIFY\" style=\"margin-left: 0.12in; margin-right: 0.13in; line-height: 103%\">Action against Builder for non\r\ncompletion of Project.Direct Inquiry against Builder regarding theft\r\nof GST.</p><p lang=\"en-US\" class=\"western\" align=\"JUSTIFY\" style=\"margin-left: 0.12in; margin-right: 0.13in; line-height: 103%\">Pledge/Stay on selling if the Properties of Builder,\r\nPromoters, Directors with immediate effect to avoid misuse of\r\ndiverted funds.</p><p lang=\"en-US\" class=\"western\" align=\"JUSTIFY\" style=\"margin-left: 0.12in; margin-right: 0.13in; line-height: 103%\"><br></p><p lang=\"en-US\" class=\"western\" align=\"JUSTIFY\" style=\"margin-left: 0.12in; margin-right: 0.13in; line-height: 103%\">Pass any other order/orders which PBRERA may deem fit\r\nin the facts and circumstances of the case.</p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p><span style=\"text-align: justify;\">Transfer of All Unsold Properties to Society (will be incorporated within 15 days of order by RERA)</span><br></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'uvrajverma','2018-11-23 17:47:59.000','uvrajverma','2018-11-23 17:47:59.000'),(370,1140,'1140',1216,'11d722ae-bbbb-479b-bed1-c40adf90f1de','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Jaswant  Singh','sjaswants803@gmail.com',9466694194,0,0,'85 SCC Area Nilokheri Dist karnal','',13,10,'132117','1','85 SCC Area Nilokheri Dist karnal','',13,10,'132117','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0316','Green Valley Heights  ','Harbans Lal Singla','greenvalleyheights2010@yahoo.co.in',9876718666,0,'M/s Green Valley Heights,Village Kishanpura,Behind sector 20 Panchkula','MC Zirakpur, SAS Nagar Mohali Punjab',28,507,'140603','1','M/s Green Valley Heights,Village Kishanpura,Behind sector 20 Panchkula','MC Zirakpur, SAS Nagar Mohali Punjab',28,507,'140603','1','<p>i) I booked a semi- furnished 2 BHK of 1285 sq. ft. (Annex-) for fixed price (Annex.)  as per construction linked plan(Annex-) in green valley heights for rupees 28,50,000/- on 11.7,2011 by paying Rs 285000/- ( Annex-) and subsequently on 15-10 2011 I was allotted with flat No. 512 in this project on paying of Rs 427500/- i.e. 25 % of the cost of the flat as a second installment by then total Rs. 7,12,500/-(Annex.-2A). The delivery of  flat was promised within three years (36 Months) from the date of booking/allotment/provisional allotment means by 15-10 2014 i.e.(15-10-2011 to14-10-2014) as per clause 11 of the agreement/provisional allotment and as per Para 17 of (Annex-) from this agreement 28-09-2011. Physical possession was delivered on 13-07-2018(Annex-22).Total payments made Rs. 30,46,384/-including taxes of Rs.90,134/-(Annex,-)\r\n</p><p>ii) On 8-2-2013 respondents handed over a printed Buyer’s apartment agreement (Annex-) very late after lapse of nearly 19 months from the date of booking which should have been simultaneously executed. This delay in executing the agreement was deliberate, abuse of dominance, unfair trade practice and modus operandi module in practice by the   respondents to stop delay meter not getting agreement signed within reasonable time.\r\n</p><p>iii)  A letter for offer of possession (Annex.-) dated 30-04-16 issued in haste without completion of flat as the possession was already late by about 58 months without taking completion/ occupancy certificates which is the mandatory requirements of the act (Annex.-).Thus the offer of possession was illegal before this as per the act, “No flat can be legally offered without completion and occupancy certificates. It is not legal possession but a mere paper possession.” Thus on 15-4-2017 I served legal notices to substantiate my claims but got no reply. On 09-05-17 I conceded all lustful demands of respondents and  obtained ’No dues certificate’ with the hope of getting possession and delayed interest and compen</p>','<p>(i)	The date of booking is 11-07-2011, allotment on 15-10-2011 and possession date is 13-07-2018,That the possession of the flat is late by more than 41 months from the date of allotment plus 39 months i.e. 14-01-2015 to 13-07-2018.I am eligible for delay interest Rs,11,78,239/- @ 10.65 (MCLR+2%)  interest for every month of delay as per section 18(1) means compound interest till this date in violations/contravention of section 18 of RERA along with other provisions and as per Sec.2 za (i),(ii) interest is due from the date of booking. \r\n</p><p>(ii)	 Refund of Rs. 1, 41,946/- may be granted charged illegally, unreasonable and without the proper consent of mine for 64 sq. ft.  in the name of super area enhancement &amp; second lift whereas no area has increased as it is physically verified. The super area &amp; carpet area are also not in proper ratio as required as per the rules. It may be verified again. Refund of UPVC windows Rs. 24,000/-, Gas Connection fitting Rs. 5,500/-. Interest on late payment Rs.53768/- and holding charges Rs.74, 195/-(Annex,-) is illegal before completion and possession. Interest on late payments of installment was charged @18% pa and holding charges were illegally imposed by the respondents.\r\n</p><p>(iii)	The possession of the flat should be considered from 15-10-2011 as a deemed date of allotment on payment of 25 % of the total cost as per CLP.\r\n</p><p>(iv)	The respondent’s offer of possession and possession letter were issued without completing the flat in all aspect including the facility of second lift, club house &amp; its amenities and the furnishings in the flat etc.as the project is not yet completed in all aspects as they have only partial completion certificate only. Hence interest may be paid till completion certificate is given, as the complainant suffers deficiency in proper dwelling for which he has paid.\r\n</p><p>(v)	The interest on the amount due from 14-07-2018 to till the decision of case or till all the dues paid by the respondents kindly be awarded @ 12% PA.</p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt\">The\r\nfollowing reliefs may be awarded:-<o:p></o:p></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt\">A) Layout\r\nplan along with the breakup of carpet area, built up area and super area may be\r\nprovided as the alleged enhancement of area by the respondents seems to be\r\nfraud or illegal manipulation in order to grab more money.<o:p></o:p></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt\">B) The area\r\nof the flat may be ordered to be verified and measured again as on physically\r\nmeasuring it there is no increase in the carpet and buildup area as claimed by\r\nthe respondents but instead it has decreased.<o:p></o:p></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt\">C) The\r\ndirection to complete the project in all aspect to complete the project with\r\nthe full enjoyment of the dwelling unit as it still lacks all facilities &amp;\r\namenities<b>.<o:p></o:p></b></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'jaswantsingh2','2018-11-23 20:02:21.000','jaswantsingh2','2018-11-23 20:02:21.000'),(371,1111,'1111',1119,'dae2bb68-2fa2-473d-a49d-c15de93bd3da','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','RAJEEV SALWAN','advravinder@gmail.com',9815700280,0,0,'H. NO. 1462, PHASE 3B2','SAS NAGAR MOHALI',28,507,'160059','1','D-711, Ravindra Apartments, Ravindra Enclave, Baltana','ZIrakpur',28,507,'140604','Ravinderpal Singh','advravinder@gmail.com',9815700280,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0155','GOLF LINKS - I (RESIDENTIAL)','ANSAL PROPERTIES & INFRASTRUCTURE LTD.','info@ansalapi.com',0,0,'SCO NO. 183-184, SECTOR 9-C, CHANDIGARH','',6,128,'160009','1','SCO NO. 183-184, SECTOR 9-C, CHANDIGARH','',6,128,'160009','1','<p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Respondents all</span><font face=\"Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">otted Plot no. 401 measuring 500 sq. yds Sector 114 Mohali on 14.08.2014 under LAND POOLING SCHEME concealing the discrepancies and defects. No approved plan was ever provide to complainants. Development agreement for allotment of plot was executed on 08.09.2013 under which possession was to be given in 2 years. Rs.60,00,000/- paid by 11.02.2014 plus Rs.8,79,500 as EDC and Rs.15,00,000/- as PLC. No EDC amount receipt (deposited with GMADA) was provided to complainants. PLC was illegally charged as adjoining the plot there is Ganda Nalah carrying Sewerage and Urinal Waste is flowing. Nallah also carrying long bushes, jungle and country grass all over. On another side of plot there is a jungle upto last boundry of complex. Plot is down by 2-3 feet from road and adjoining plots due to digging earth by Respondents to make the Katcha passage while constructing complex. Ganda Nallah mentioned above was previously naturally rainy storm water drain in monsoon season, but from the last 2-3 years it was converted into sewerage and urinal waste of adjoining villages and swaraj mazda factory which is in the vicinity of complex. Now this Ganda Nallah running throughout the year which is breeding ground for mosquitoes,&nbsp; insects and dangerous reptiles like snakes. Infrastructure of complex like sewerage, lighting, roads, habitable environment are incomplete. Paper possession of the plot was given on 20.07.2015 concealing the material fact as mentioned above and falsely assured that the discrepancies shall be set right. But till date nothing has been done. Plot is inhabitable. Complainants wrote regd. letters dated 10.10.2014, 08.08.2016, 14.09.2016, 23.11.2017 and 16.12.2017 for taking the action to remove discrepancies but all in vain. It is an inhabitable and unhealthy location where nobody can live-in. Respondent No.2 started demanding maintenance Charges when they are doing nothing on account of maintenance and when the plot is not habitable.&nbsp;</span></font></p>','<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"margin-left:85.05pt;mso-add-space:\r\nauto;text-align:justify;text-indent:-28.35pt;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,serif\">a).&nbsp;&nbsp; Relocation of the plot no. 401 measuring 500\r\nsq. yards be done to a suitable place, as per the choice of the complainants,\r\nat a preferable location (Corner Plot) with all amenities, facilities like\r\nroad, sewerage and water connection, metalled roads, street lights, levelling of\r\nplot at road level etc.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-left:85.05pt;mso-add-space:\r\nauto;text-align:justify;text-indent:-28.35pt;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,serif\">b)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Refund of the excess amount of\r\nRs.15,00,000/- charged from the complainants on account of PLC;<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-left:85.05pt;mso-add-space:\r\nauto;text-align:justify;text-indent:-28.35pt;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,serif\">c)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Respondents be directed to provide the proof\r\nof the EDC/ IDC deposited by the respondents with the GMADA/ any other\r\ncompetent authority out of the amount charged from the complainants.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-left:85.05pt;mso-add-space:\r\nauto;text-align:justify;text-indent:-28.35pt;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,serif\">d)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Respondents may be restrained to demand the\r\nmaintenance charges till the time relocation to a habitable plot is not done.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-left:85.05pt;mso-add-space:\r\nauto;text-align:justify;text-indent:-28.35pt;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,serif\">e).&nbsp;&nbsp; Pay interest @18% per annum from the dates of\r\nrespective payments till the date of actual realization of the amount;</span><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif; font-size: 14pt; text-indent: -28.35pt;\">&nbsp;and</span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-left:85.05pt;mso-add-space:\r\nauto;text-align:justify;text-indent:-28.35pt;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,serif\">f).&nbsp;&nbsp; Pay Rs.1,10,000/- as the litigation charges\r\nand expenses incurred by it.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-left:85.05pt;mso-add-space:\r\nauto;text-align:justify;text-indent:-28.35pt;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,serif\">g).&nbsp;&nbsp; Order any other relief that this Hon’ble\r\nCourt, SAS Nagar, Mohali, Pujab may deem fit and proper in the circumstances of\r\nthe present complaint.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-left:56.7pt;mso-add-space:\r\nauto;text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,serif\">IN\r\nCASE RESPONDENTS FAILS TO RELOCATE THE PLOT AS PRAYED ABOVE, ALTERNATIVELY &nbsp;&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></b></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-left:84.3pt;mso-add-space:\r\nauto;text-align:justify;text-indent:-27.6pt;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,serif\">i)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Refund entire deposited amount of Rs.84,05,365/-.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-left:85.05pt;mso-add-space:\r\nauto;text-align:justify;text-indent:-28.35pt;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,serif\">j).&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Pay interest @18% per annum from the dates\r\nof respective payments till the date of actual realization of the amount;<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-left:85.05pt;mso-add-space:\r\nauto;text-align:justify;text-indent:-28.35pt;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif; font-size: 14pt; text-indent: -28.35pt;\">k).&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Pay Rs.1,10,000/- as the litigation charges\r\nand expenses incurred by it.</span><br></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"margin-left:85.05pt;mso-add-space:\r\nauto;text-align