and Letters from the respondent. as per annexure V</li></ul></div>','<ul><li>As per the Clause I of Builder Buyer Agreement 30% payment was to be made by the applicant from their own sources which has already been done&nbsp; as detailed above in annexures II and V.</li><li>Balance 70% was to be paid out of Home Loan from approved bank/financial Organisation. The Company has agreed that there shall be no EMI, No interest on the disbursed loan amount till 24 months&nbsp; from the date of first disbursal of the loan amount or offer of possession whichever is earlier.</li><li>Accordingly the respondent applied for home loan from DHFL through the respondent and got the letter of offer cum acceptance for a known amount of Rs.60,00,00/-on the terms and conditions specified in the said letter of offer cum acceptance annexed at Annexure VI</li><li>Thus, the total amount of Rs.57,00,000/-was released by the bank against Sanctioned amount of Rs.60,00,000/-.Details of the Payment Conformations from DHFL are as per annexure VII.</li><li>That the residential project is still not complete. Some of the towers are in&nbsp; advanced stage and the progress of development of common areas is very low. The applicant has taken recent photographs of the project site as attached at Annexure VIII. These pics clearly indicate that the development works are still underway and the respondent may not be able to offer possession in near future after obtaining completion certificate.</li><li>As per clause 15 of the Builder Buyer Agreement, the possession of the allotted unit was to be offered within 36 months from the date of signing of the said agreement i.e. on 17.01.2016 which has already expired.</li><li>It, is therefore, humbly prayed that the Hon’ble Authority may consider the applicant’s submissions and order the respondent to refund our total amount of Rs. 88,14,938/- along with interest as per RERA provisions from the respective dates of payments made to the respondent.</li><li>Therefore the applicant is seeking relief under the provisions of RERA.<br></li></ul><div><br></div>',9287213.00,8814938.00,'2016-01-17 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','NA','1','','2012-12-16 00:00:00','2013-01-17 00:00:00','Unit No. 802, Tow-T1, Eight Floor, GH-10, Sector-90-91, JLPL, Mohali (Pb)','','',1,1,0,0,'kathuria.prashant','2018-11-28 18:44:32.000','kathuria.prashant','2018-11-28 18:44:32.000'),(421,1150,'1150',1229,'6166bf56-8baf-4aa7-a05e-6b75f196cc86','FormTypeM',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Ranveer  Sharma','advamitgoyal@hotmail.com',9527700001,0,0,'1003-B, Sterling Seaface, Annie Besant Road, ','Near Poonam Chambers, Worli',21,400,'400018','1','1003-B, Sterling Seaface, Annie Besant Road, ','Near Poonam Chambers, Worli',21,400,'400018','Amit Goyal','advamitgoyal@hotmail.com',9527700001,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0143','Parkwood Grade Tower C ','Parkwood Depelopers Pvt. Ltd.','mail@parkwoodgroup.in',0,1130324952,'M/s Parkwood Developers Pvt. Ltd. ','1001, Hemkunt Chambers, 89 Nehru Place,',10,429,'110019','1','M/s Parkwood Developers Pvt. Ltd. ','1001, Hemkunt Chambers, 89 Nehru Place,',10,429,'110019','1','\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<ol><li style=\"margin: 0cm 0cm 10pt 36pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-ansi-language:EN-US\">Respondents\r\ngave various advertisements &amp; showed a rosy picture about the project.\r\nComplainants relied heavily on these representations &amp;</span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;color:#1A1A1A\"> entered\r\ninto agreement dated 08.12.12 <b>(Annexure C-1)</b> with Respondents for total\r\nconsideration of Rs. </span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">49,97475 for </span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;color:#1A1A1A\">Flat No. C003 Tower C with\r\nSuper Built up Area 1725 sqft.</span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\"> </span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;color:#1A1A1A\">Possession was to be delivered latest by\r\n30.06.15 (clause 19 (a))</span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">.</span></li><li style=\"margin-left: 36pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;color:#1A1A1A\">Complainants\r\nmade initial payment of 300000 (para 6a of agreement). Thereafter payments were\r\nmade as per the demand notes from time to time between Dec 12 &amp; Nov 13.</span></li><li style=\"margin-left: 36pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;color:#1A1A1A\">Next demand\r\nnote was raised by respondent in Feb 16 i.e. after 26 months. Complainants\r\nqueried the Promoter on the status of the project and reminded that in their\r\nprevious site visit </span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n200%;color:#212121\">they found work running&nbsp;behind schedule &amp; therefore\r\nPromoter had no right to raise demand.</span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:\r\n14.0pt;line-height:200%;color:#1A1A1A\"> Complainants sought relevant documents\r\nconfirming progress of work. No response was received.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"margin-left: 36pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;color:#1A1A1A\">Respondent raised\r\nanother demand on 05.04.17 <b>(Annexure C2)</b>. Complainants again queried the\r\nPromoter vide email dated 10.04.17 <b>(Annexure C3)</b> on project progress</span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;color:#212121\">.&nbsp;No\r\nresponse was received. </span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;color:#1A1A1A;mso-bidi-font-style:italic\">This demand note also\r\nsummarised all payments made by Complainants.</span></li><li style=\"margin-left: 36pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;color:#1A1A1A\">Complainants\r\nvisited site in July 17 and again found no progress. Reminder sent to the\r\nPromoter on 01.08.18. Respondents assured they will inform within week but\r\ndidn’t respond despite reminders.</span></li><li style=\"margin-left: 36pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;color:#1A1A1A\">Complainants\r\nlost confidence in the Promoter and in its ability to provide flat within\r\nstipulated time. Complainants therefore sent letter dated 12.03.18 seeking\r\nrefund with interest. Reminder also sent on 12.04.18 <b>(C-4). </b>Promoter\r\ndidn’t respond.</span></li><li style=\"margin-left: 36pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\nCalibri;mso-bidi-font-family:Raavi\">Given the construction status &amp; snail’s\r\npace of work, it is impossible that </span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:\r\n14.0pt;line-height:200%\">respondents</span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:\r\n14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-fareast-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-font-family:\r\nRaavi\"> will deliver possession in near future. T</span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%\">ill date</span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-fareast-font-family:Calibri;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:Raavi\"> no substantial work has been done on site. Actual\r\nvisit will show that only structure has been built (usual practice of all\r\nbuilders). Photographs depicting work as in Nov, 18 are annexed as <b>C-</b></span><b><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%\">5</span></b><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\nCalibri;mso-bidi-font-family:Raavi\">.</span><a name=\"_GoBack\"></a><b><i><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;color:#1A1A1A\"><o:p></o:p></span></i></b></li></ol>','\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<ol><li style=\"margin-left: 18pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;color:#1A1A1A\">Refund of\r\nthe Principal amount paid to date to the Promoter ie INR 42,77,666/-.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"margin: 10pt 0cm 10pt 18pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%\">As per </span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\nCalibri\">clause 2(a) of agreement respondents are charging interest @18% p.a.\r\non account of delay in payment.</span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"> Therefore complainants be also awarded interest at the same\r\nrate-&nbsp;</span>Or- </li><li style=\"margin: 10pt 0cm 10pt 18pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\">Interest as\r\nprovided under <span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">Section 18 and 19(4) of the RERA Act r/w </span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; color: rgb(26, 26, 26);\">Rule 16 of\r\nthe Regulation and Development Rules 2017 on the above Principal amount from\r\nthe respective dates it was paid to the respondent till the date of payment ie\r\nState Bank of India’s (“SBI”) highest Marginal Cost of Lending Rate (“MCLR”)\r\nplus 2%. The current SBI MCLR is 8.50% pa so applicable interest rate for the\r\nrefund is taken as 10.50% pa..</span></li><li style=\"margin-left: 18pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;color:#1A1A1A\">Direct the\r\nrespondent to repay to the complainants the expenses directly incurred by the\r\nComplainants in filing the RERA application ie </span>Litigation\r\nexpenses– for representing the Complainants before this Ld. Authority ie INR\r\n55,000 <b style=\"color: rgb(26, 26, 26); font-size: 14pt;\">(Annexure C-6)</b></li><li style=\"margin: 0cm 0cm 10pt 18pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;color:#1A1A1A\">Compensation for Mental\r\nharassment to the tune of Rs. 1,00,000/- </span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-ansi-language:EN-US\"><o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"margin: 0cm 0cm 10pt 18pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-ansi-language:EN-US\">To impose\r\npenalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 61 of RERA Act\r\nfor contravention of Sections 11(3)(b) and 18 of the RERA Act.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"margin: 0cm 0cm 10pt 18pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-ansi-language:EN-US\">To issue\r\ndirections to make liable every officer concerned i.e. Director, Manager,\r\nSecretary, or any other officer of the respondent’s company at whose instance,\r\nconnivance, acquiescence, neglect any of the offences has been committed as\r\nmentioned in Sec. 69 of RERA Act, 2016 read with Punjab RERA Rules, 2017.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"margin: 0cm 0cm 10pt 18pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-ansi-language:EN-US\">To recommend\r\ncriminal action against the respondents for the criminal offence of cheating,\r\nfraud and criminal breach of trust under section 420, 406 and 409 of the Indian\r\nPenal Code.</span></li><li style=\"margin: 0cm 0cm 10pt 18pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-ansi-language:EN-US\">Any other\r\nrelief which this Hon’ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of the\r\nfacts and circumstances of this complaint.<o:p></o:p></span></li></ol><ol></ol>',4997475.00,4277666.00,'2015-06-30 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-height:\r\n200%\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-ansi-language:\r\nEN-US\">No interim relief is being sought. The complainants only pray that the\r\npromoters be directed to return the amount paid with interest.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','2012-12-08 00:00:00','Village Santemajra, Tehsil Kharar, District S.A.S. Nagar,  Punjab','','',2,0,0,0,'Ranveerneha','2018-11-28 18:46:46.000','Ranveerneha','2018-11-28 18:46:46.000'),(422,1150,'1150',1229,'6166bf56-8baf-4aa7-a05e-6b75f196cc86','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-11-28 20:02:18.000','Ranveer  Sharma','advamitgoyal@hotmail.com',9527700001,0,0,'1003-B, Sterling Seaface, Annie Besant Road, ','Near Poonam Chambers, Worli',21,400,'400018','1','1003-B, Sterling Seaface, Annie Besant Road, ','Near Poonam Chambers, Worli',21,400,'400018','Amit Goyal','advamitgoyal@hotmail.com',9527700001,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0143','Parkwood Grade Tower C ','Parkwood Depelopers Pvt. Ltd.','mail@parkwoodgroup.in',0,1130324952,'M/s Parkwood Developers Pvt. Ltd. ','1001, Hemkunt Chambers, 89 Nehru Place,',10,429,'110019','1','M/s Parkwood Developers Pvt. Ltd. ','1001, Hemkunt Chambers, 89 Nehru Place,',10,429,'110019','1','\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<ol><li style=\"margin: 0cm 0cm 10pt 36pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-ansi-language:EN-US\">Respondents\r\ngave various advertisements &amp; showed a rosy picture about the project.\r\nComplainants relied heavily on these representations &amp;</span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;l