133,'1133',1061,'feb522a9-b591-42ad-b827-d1fac41495ae','FormTypeM',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','SUDESH KUMAR  DHAWAN','vikas3dhawan@gmail.com',9785325611,0,0,'#3B-51, JAWAHAR NAGAR','',29,213,'335001','1','#3B-51, JAWAHAR NAGAR','',29,213,'335001','BIRENDER SINGH DHILLON','CSPURIDHILLON@GMAIL.COM',9988933636,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PC0001','ROYAL BUSINESS PARK','MOTIA DEVELOPERS PRIVATE LIMITED','INFO@MOTIAGROUP.COM',8558844525,0,'Royal Citi','Chandigarh-Ambala Highway',28,507,'140603','1','Royal Citi','Chandigarh-Ambala Highway',28,507,'140603','1','<p>On 20/10/2014 the complainant&nbsp; applied for office space in commercial project name “Royal Business Park” situated at Chandigarh- Ambala Highway, Zirakpur (PB) for unit No 6, Ground Floor&nbsp; with super area approx. 620.454 sq.ft for Total cost of Rs.49,63,632/- (Rupees Forty Nine Lakh sixty three thousand six hundred Thity Two only)&nbsp; with Booking amount of Rs 500000/- which is managed by Motia Developers Private Limited.</p><p>27/10/2014&nbsp; &nbsp;The complainant paid Rs 7,25,000.</p><p>28/10/2014&nbsp; &nbsp;The complainant paid Rs 3,46,866.</p><p>31/10/2014&nbsp; &nbsp;The complainant paid Rs 3,28,134.</p><p>02/11/2014&nbsp; &nbsp;The complainant paid Rs 3,50,000</p><p>05/11/2014&nbsp; &nbsp;The complainant paid Rs 3,50,000.</p><p>07/11/2014&nbsp; &nbsp;The complainant paid Rs 4,00,000.</p><p>11/11/2014&nbsp; &nbsp;The complainant paid Rs 5,00,000.</p><p>11/11/2014&nbsp; The Pending balance as on date Rs 13,94,418.</p><p>15/11/2017&nbsp; The possession was to delivered within 36 months of the execution of the aforesaid agreement</p><p>April 2015&nbsp; The respondent raised a demand for the&nbsp; instalment due on 02/04/2015 with balance amount mention&nbsp; of Rs 16,53,765/- still pending. It is pertinent to mention here that&nbsp; the demand was not legible as per the buyer agreement.</p><p>The complaint talk telephonically with respondent several times between April 2015 and December 2015 to get the proper detail of amount&nbsp; demand. Thereafter, the complainant denied&nbsp; to make the payment because of&nbsp; unfair demand raised and failed to explain the demand raised.</p><p>The complainant visited the respondent office to get the detail of&nbsp; illegal and illegitimate demands of the respondent with clarification. The officials of respondent explained that the amount raised was calculated on the bases of super area i.e&nbsp; 680 sqft.</p><p>The complainant has stop paying further instalment because he came to know that the demand raised was for the shop having super area 680 sq.ft but as per the signed agreement, the allotment was for the&nbsp; shop having&nbsp; super area of 620.454 sq.ft.</p>','<p>1. To direct the respondent to hand over the physical possession of the shop as per agreement&nbsp; to the complainant or to direct the respondent to refund the entire amount paid by the complainant i.e. ₹ 3500000 along with 24% interest from the date of respective payment till the actual realization of the entire amountTo direct the respondent to hand over the physical possession of the flat/apartme.&nbsp;</p><p>2. To pay complaint for the torture, sufferings, harassment and embarrassment etc caused to the complaint the reports their neglectful attitude in dealing with the complainant.&nbsp;</p><p>3. To impose penalty upon the respondent for not entering into a written&nbsp; agreement for sale and register the said agreement for sale which is required under section 13 of RERA act 2016 because the respondent accept a some more than 10% of the cost of shop.&nbsp;</p><p>4. Any other relief (s) which this Hon\'ble Authority may deem fit and proper may also be granted in favour of the complainant and against the respondent.</p>',4963632.00,3500000.00,'2017-11-15 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Not Required</p>','1','','2014-11-04 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Shop No 6, Ground Floor, Royal Business Park, Zirakpur (PB)','','',2,0,0,0,'SUDE