laint talk telephonically with respondent several times between April 2015 and December 2015 to get the proper detail of amount&nbsp; demand. Thereafter, the complainant denied&nbsp; to make the payment because of&nbsp; unfair demand raised and failed to explain the demand raised.</p><p>The complainant visited the respondent office to get the detail of&nbsp; illegal and illegitimate demands of the respondent with clarification. The officials of respondent explained that the amount raised was calculated on the bases of super area i.e&nbsp; 680 sqft.</p><p>The complainant has stop paying further instalment because he came to know that the demand raised was for the shop having super area 680 sq.ft but as per the signed agreement, the allotment was for the&nbsp; shop having&nbsp; super area of 620.454 sq.ft.</p>','<p>1. To direct the respondent to hand over the physical possession of the shop as per agreement&nbsp; to the complainant or to direct the respondent to refund the entire amount paid by the complainant i.e. ₹ 3500000 along with 24% interest from the date of respective payment till the actual realization of the entire amountTo direct the respondent to hand over the physical possession of the flat/apartme.&nbsp;</p><p>2. To pay complaint for the torture, sufferings, harassment and embarrassment etc caused to the complaint the reports their neglectful attitude in dealing with the complainant.&nbsp;</p><p>3. To impose penalty upon the respondent for not entering into a written&nbsp; agreement for sale and register the said agreement for sale which is required under section 13 of RERA act 2016 because the respondent accept a some more than 10% of the cost of shop.&nbsp;</p><p>4. Any other relief (s) which this Hon\'ble Authority may deem fit and proper may also be granted in favour of the complainant and against the respondent.</p>',4963632.00,3500000.00,'2017-11-15 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Not Required</p>','1','','2014-11-04 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Shop No 6, Ground Floor, Royal Business Park, Zirakpur (PB)','','',1,1,0,0,'SUDESHKUMARDHAWAN','2018-11-30 15:03:45.000','SUDESHKUMARDHAWAN','2018-11-30 15:03:45.000'),(438,1159,'1159',1241,'985f4264-4985-42ed-94fc-64d8a6d1a4ec','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Parshant Gajanan Pathak','advamitgoyal@hotmail.com',9527700001,0,0,'Flat no. 603, Lotus Tower, Bollywood Heights,','Near sector-20 Panchkula Peer Machalla, Dhakoli, ',28,507,'140603','1','Flat no. 603, Lotus Tower, Bollywood Heights,','Near sector-20 Panchkula Peer Machalla, Dhakoli, ',28,507,'140603','Amit Goyal','advamitgoyal@hotmail.com',9527700001,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0086','M/s ATS Infrabuild Private Limited.','M/s ATS Infrabuild Private Limited ','email@atsgreens.com',0,0,'M/s ATS Infrabuild Private Limited  Registered Office at 711/92, Deepali','Nehru Place, New Delhi',10,429,'110019','1','M/s ATS Infrabuild Private Limited  Registered Office at 711/92, Deepali','Nehru Place, New Delhi',10,429,'110019','1','<p>abc</p>','<p>abc</p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>abc</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',1,0,0,0,'Parshantshilpa','2018-11-30 19:48:09.000','Parshantshilpa','2018-11-30 19:48:09.000'),(439,1160,'1160',1221,'371492c6-7a9d-4ed1-b340-1b73bc92dac4','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-26 09:21:15.000','AMRINDER KAUR','charanjitpsegs@gmail.com',9888793050,0,0,'2321 C Block 29','Housing Board Flats Sector 63',6,128,'160062','1','House No 1577','Sector 70 Mohali',28,507,'160071','CHARANJIT SINGH','charanjitcan@gmail.com',9888793050,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0367','UNIWORLD CITY MOHALI','M/S UNITECH LIMITED ','sanctions_hry@unitechgroup.com',9821227005,1244835300,'m/s unitech limited','UNITECH HOUSE, L-BLOCK, SOUTH CITY-1',13,5,'122007','1','M/S UNITECH LIMITED','UNITECH HOUSE, L-BLOCK, SOUTH CITY-1',13,5,'122007','1','<p>A.	The complainant purchased a two bedroom flat jointly with my mother in law named Kuldeep Kaur from respondent Unitech Ltd in their project Singleton Floors, Uniworld City Mohali on 26.08.09.The name of my mother in law was deleted on 26.12.11(p11).&nbsp;<br></p><p>B.	The agreement was signed with the respondent’s Unitech Ltd. and the Alice developers private Ltd on 12.11.2009(p12-32).\r\n</p><p>C.	 The cost of the above unit was fixed Rs 2458727/-(p30).The complainant paid Rs 1978144/(p36) to respondents till October 2013 on demand. \r\n</p><p>D.	The complainant never delayed the payment or breached any condition of the agreement.\r\n</p><p>E.	 The possession of the flat was to be offered within 36 months I.e is up-to 11.11.2012 by the respondents from the date of signing the agreement i.e. 12.11.2009(p20,4a). However the respondents offered possession on 13.11.2018(p34)&nbsp; &nbsp;. \r\n</p><p>F.	There is delay of 72 months in offering the possession.\r\n</p><p>G.	The respondents issued a demand notice amounting to Rs 6, 64,288/- to the claimant along with the offer of possession without adjusting the amount of compensation as per agreement(p36). \r\n</p><p>H.	The cost of the unit was increased to the tune of Rs 93000/- on a/c of revised super area in this aforesaid demand notice(p-35). This was applicable to Unihomes Scheme not to The Singleton Scheme in the same block of units. \r\n</p><p>I.	The final demand notice include a sum of Rs 60000/- club charges whereas no such club is constructed or exists in the aforesaid project. \r\n</p><p>J.	The liability of complainant towards Service Tax/ GST increased due to non-delivery of Unit on time by the respondents(p36).  \r\n</p><p>K.	The claimant discussed the aforesaid facts   with the representative of respondents Sh. Robin Singh (Mentioned in final notice of possession for contact) who refused to adjust any compensation.\r\n</p><p>L.	The claimant is paying an instalment of Rs 4600/- P.M to HDFC on a/c of availed loan as well as family is paying house rent to the tune of   Rs 13500/- P.M.\r\n</p><p><br></p>','<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;\r\nmargin-bottom:0cm;margin-left:70.9pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;mso-add-space:auto;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-indent:-18.0pt;line-height:normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin;\r\nmso-ansi-language:EN-CA\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 14px; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">1.&nbsp;</span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-ansi-language:EN-CA\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">The claimant should be given\r\npossession immediately after payment of external electrification charges and\r\nwater and sewer connection charges.</span></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;\r\nmargin-bottom:0cm;margin-left:70.9pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;mso-add-space:auto;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-indent:-18.0pt;line-height:normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span style=\"text-indent: -18pt;\">2.</span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span style=\"text-indent: -18pt;\">The claimant is filing request\r\nfor compensation in Form N separately.</span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;\r\nmargin-bottom:0cm;margin-left:70.9pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;mso-add-space:auto;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-indent:-18.0pt;line-height:normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-ansi-language:EN-CA\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">3.</span></span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-ansi-language:EN-CA\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">The false increased cost of unit to the tune\r\nof Rs 93000/- should be reduced.</span><o:p></o:p></span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">\r\n\r\n</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">\r\n\r\n</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">\r\n\r\n</span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;\r\nmargin-bottom:0cm;margin-left:70.9pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;mso-add-space:auto;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-indent:-18.0pt;line-height:normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-ansi-language:EN-CA\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">4.</span></span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-ansi-language:EN-CA\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">The club charges to the tune\r\nof Rs. 60000/- should be deducted from the final demand as the respondents have\r\nfailed to start construction of club even after a span of 10 years. The\r\nclaimant has doubt on the integrity of the respondents.</span></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;\r\nmargin-bottom:0cm;margin-left:70.9pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;mso-add-space:auto;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-indent:-18.0pt;line-height:normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-ansi-language:EN-CA\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">5</span></span>&nbsp; &nbsp; The increased cost of GST due to delayed delivery should be paid by the respondents.</p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<span style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -24px;\">The claimant should be given possession immediately after payment of external electrification charges and water and sewer connection charges.</span>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'lovely','2018-12-03 08:01:56.000','lovely','2018-12-03 08:01:56.000'),(440,1140,'1140',1216,'11d722ae-bbbb-479b-bed1-c40adf90f1de','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Jaswant  Singh','sjaswants803@gmail.com',9466694194,0,0,'85 SCC Area Nilokheri Dist karnal','',13,10,'132117','1','85 SCC Area Nilokheri Dist karnal','',13,10,'132117','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0316','Green Valley Heights  ','Harbans Lal Singla','greenvalleyheights2010@yahoo.co.in',9876718666,0,'M/s Green Valley Heights,Village Kishanpura,Behind sector 20 Panchkula','MC Zirakpur, SAS Nagar Mohali Punjab',28,507,'140603','1','M/s Green Valley Heights,Village Kishanpura,Behind sector 20 Panchkula','MC Zirakpur, SAS Nagar Mohali Punjab',28,507,'140603','1','i) I booked a semi- furnished 2 BHK of 1285 sq. ft. for fixed price as per construction linked plan in green valley heights for Rs 2850000/- on 11.7.11 by paying Rs 285000/- and subsequently on 15-10-11. I was allotted with flat No. 512 on paying of Rs 427500/-. The delivery of  flat was promised within three years (36+ 3 months) from the date of booking/allotment/provisional allotment by 14-01- 15. Physical possession was delivered on 13-07-18.Total payments made Rs. 3046384/-including taxes Rs.90134/. On 8-2-13 respondents handed over a printed Buyer’s apartment agreement very late after lapse of nearly 19 months from the date of booking which should have been simultaneously executed. This delay in executing the agreement was deliberate, abuse of dominance, unfair trade practice by the respondents to stop delay meter not getting agreement signed within reasonable time.\r\n<div>\r\n</div><div>ii)A letter for ‘offer of possession’ dated 30-04-16 issued in haste without completion of flat as the possession was already late by about 58 months without taking completion/occupancy certificates which is the mandatory requirements of the act. Thus the offer of possession was illegal before this, “No flat can be legally offered without completion and occupancy certificates. It is not legal possession but a mere paper possession.” Legal notice was served on 15-04-17 but got no reply. On 09-05-17 I conceded all lustful demands and  obtained ’No dues certificate’ with the hope of getting possession and delayed interest and compensations but thwarted. My time and again interactions for claims were of no avail. The respondents duped me under duress to deposit all the original documents in order to issue new to adjust interest o/o this arrangement. The respondents also alleged to have enhanced the area of my flat by 64 Sq. Ft. and charged for Rs. 1, 41946/-. Arbitrarily and illegally without my consent, approvals of competent authority, failed to provide the breakup of area and details of layout plan.</div>','<p>(i)	The date of booking is 11-07-2011, allotment on 15-10-2011 and possession date is 13-07-2018,That the possession of the flat is late by more than 41 months from the date of allotment plus 39 months i.e. 14-01-2015 to 13-07-2018.I am eligible for delay interest Rs,11,78,239/- @ 10.65 (MCLR+2%)  interest for every month of delay as per section 18(1) means compound interest till this date in violations/contravention of section 18 of RERA along with other provisions and as per Sec.2 za (i),(ii) interest is due from the date of booking. \r\n</p><p>(ii)	 Refund of Rs. 1, 41,946/- may be granted charged illegally, unreasonable and without the proper consent of mine for 64 sq. ft.  in the name of super area enhancement &amp; second lift whereas no area has increased as it is physically verified. The super area &amp; carpet area are also not in proper ratio as required as per the rules. It may be verified again. Refund of UPVC windows Rs. 24,000/-, Gas Connection fitting Rs. 5,500/-. Interest on late payment Rs.53768/- and holding charges Rs.74, 195/-(Annex,-) is illegal before completion and possession. Interest on late payments of installment was charged @18% pa and holding charges were illegally imposed by the respondents.\r\n</p><p>(iii)	The possession of the flat should be considered from 15-10-2011 as a deemed date of allotment on payment of 25 % of the total cost as per CLP.\r\n</p><p>(iv)	The respondent’s offer of possession and possession letter were issued without completing the flat in all aspect including the facility of second lift, club house &amp; its amenities and the furnishings in the flat etc.as the project is not yet completed in all aspects as they have only partial completion certificate only. Hence interest may be paid till completion certificate is given, as the complainant suffers deficiency in proper dwelling for which he has paid.\r\n</p><p>(v)	The interest on the amount due from 14-07-2018 to till the decision of case or till all the dues paid by the respondents kindly be awarded @ 12% PA.</p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt\">The\r\nfollowing reliefs may be awarded:-<o:p></o:p></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt\">A) Layout\r\nplan along with the breakup of carpet area, built up area and super area may be\r\nprovided as the alleged enhancement of area by the respondents seems to be\r\nfraud or illegal manipulation in order to grab more money.<o:p></o:p></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt\">B) The area\r\nof the flat may be ordered to be verified and measured again as on physically\r\nmeasuring it there is no increase in the carpet and buildup area as claimed by\r\nthe respondents but instead it has decreased.<o:p></o:p></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt\">C) The\r\ndirection to complete the project in all aspect to complete the project with\r\nthe full enjoyment of the dwelling unit as it still lacks all facilities &amp;\r\namenities<b>.<o:p></o:p></b></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'jaswantsingh2','2018-12-03 11:46:22.000','jaswantsingh2','2018-12-03 11:46:22.000'),(441,1140,'1140',1216,'11d722ae-bbbb-479b-bed1-c40adf90f1de','FormTypeM',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Jaswant  Singh','sjaswants803@gmail.c