abuse of dominance, unfair trade practice by the respondents to stop delay meter not getting agreement signed within reasonable time.\r\n<div>\r\n</div><div>ii)A letter for ‘offer of possession’ dated 30-04-16 issued in haste without completion of flat as the possession was already late by about 58 months without taking completion/occupancy certificates which is the mandatory requirements of the act. Thus the offer of possession was illegal before this, “No flat can be legally offered without completion and occupancy certificates. It is not legal possession but a mere paper possession.” Legal notice was served on 15-04-17 but got no reply. On 09-05-17 I conceded all lustful demands and  obtained ’No dues certificate’ with the hope of getting possession and delayed interest and compensations but thwarted. My time and again interactions for claims were of no avail. The respondents duped me under duress to deposit all the original documents in order to issue new to adjust interest o/o this arrangement. The respondents also alleged to have enhanced the area of my flat by 64 Sq. Ft. and charged for Rs. 1, 41946/-. Arbitrarily and illegally without my consent, approvals of competent authority, failed to provide the breakup of area and details of layout plan.</div>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\">i)The date of booking is 11-07-2011, allotment on 15-10-2011\r\nand possession date is 13-07-2018,That the possession of the flat is late by\r\nmore than 41 months from the date of allotment plus 39 months i.e. 14-01-2015\r\nto 13-07-2018.I am eligible for delay interest Rs,11,78,239/- @ 10.65\r\n(MCLR+2%)&nbsp; interest for every month of\r\ndelay as per section 18(1) means compound interest till this date in\r\nviolations/contravention of section 18 of RERA along with other provisions and\r\nas per Sec.2 za (i),(ii) interest is due from the date of booking. <o:p></o:p></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">ii)Refund of Rs. 1, 41,946/- may be granted charged\r\nillegally, unreasonable and without the proper consent of mine for 64 sq. ft.&nbsp; in the name of super area enhancement &amp;\r\nsecond lift whereas no area has increased as it is physically verified. The\r\nsuper area &amp; carpet area are also not in proper ratio as required as per\r\nthe rules. Refund of UPVC windows Rs. 24,000/-, Gas Connection fitting Rs. 5,500/-.\r\nInterest on late payment Rs.53768/- and holding charges Rs.74, 195/-(Annex,-)\r\nis illegal before completion and possession. Interest on late payments of\r\ninstallment was charged @18% pa and holding charges were illegally imposed by\r\nthe respondents.<o:p></o:p></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">iii)The possession of the flat should be considered from\r\n15-10-2011 as a deemed date of allotment on payment of 25 % of the total cost\r\nas per CLP.<o:p></o:p></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">iv)The respondent’s offer of possession and possession\r\nletter were issued without completing the flat in all aspect including the\r\nfacility of second lift, club house &amp; its amenities and the furnishings in\r\nthe flat etc.as the project is not yet completed in all aspects as they have\r\nonly partial completion certificate only. Hence interest may be paid till\r\ncompletion certificate is given, as the complainant suffers deficiency in\r\nproper dwelling for which he has paid.<o:p></o:p></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">v)The interest on the amount due from 14-07-2018 to till the\r\ndecision of case or till all the dues paid by the respondents may be awarded @\r\n12% PA.</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><o:p></o:p></p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt\">The\r\nfollowing reliefs may be awarded:-<o:p></o:p></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt\">A) Layout\r\nplan along with the breakup of carpet area, built up area and super area may be\r\nprovided as the alleged enhancement of area by the respondents seems to be\r\nfraud or illegal manipulation in order to grab more money.</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt\">B) The area\r\nof the flat may be ordered to be verified and measured again as on physically\r\nmeasuring it there is no increase in the carpet and buildup area as claimed by\r\nthe respondents but instead it has decreased.</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><o:p></o:p></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt\">C) The\r\ndirection to complete the project in all aspect with the full enjoyment of the dwelling\r\nunit as it still lacks all facilities &amp; amenities<b>.<o:p></o:p></b></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',1,1,0,0,'jaswantsingh2','2018-12-03 12:07:38.000','jaswantsingh2','2018-12-03 12:07:38.000'),(444,1161,'1161',1178,'02e82b67-7f34-47ae-80b9-cc89681213d6','FormTypeM',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Kanavdeep Singh','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9896165550,0,0,'H NO 1497 Sector 9 ','',13,10,'132001','1','H NO 1497 Sector 9 ','',13,10,'132001','Kamal Dahiya','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9729902009,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0085','Sushma Chandigarh Grande','Sushma Buildtech Ltd','customercare@sushmabuildtech.com',9872889933,0,'Unit No B 107 Business Complex Elante Mall 1st Floor Industrial Area Phase I Chandigarh','',6,128,'160009','1','Unit No B 107 Business Complex Elante Mall 1st Floor Industrial Area Phase I Chandigarh','',6,128,'160009','1','<p>The Complainant had purchased a flat/apartment in the said Project having an approximate 2085 sq. foot. The Complainant had been allotted Flat in Tower no. H i.e H002 (Ground Floor) admeasuring 2085 sq. feet vide Allotment Letter dated 04.09.2012- Annexure C-1. An ABA was executed on 04.09.2012. It has been specifically mentioned in of ABA, that the complainant has already paid booking amount of Rs. 12,39,038. towards purchase of the said apartment which form the part of the total consideration. The basic sale price of the said apartment was Rs. 82,60,250. The Complainant had opted for construction linked plan. The Complainant has paid INR 81,37,349 i.e. nearly 100% of payment out of total consideration till date including loan from HDFC Bank i.e Rs.60,00,000-Annexure C-2. As per the ABA, the date of possession is December 2016 but respondents didn’t give any possession to complainant and the agent of respondents namely Anuj asked complainant to replace his flat i.e H002 Ground Floor to 702, Tower-H as it would be delivered in April, 2017 and flat on ground floor will take much more time. Thereafter,Tower H was allotted to complainant. New ABA was entered on 21.02.2017 and as per terms possession is to be delivered in April 2017-Annexure C-3. Now in month of December 2018 i.e. delay of 19 months from date of commitment, only 70% project is completed thus delaying the possession of Apartment deliberately or for reasons known best to them. The complainant has also sent legal notice to respondents but of no avail -Annexures C-4 &amp; C-5. That the respondent had refunded only Rs 12,00,000/- to the complainant which was earlier charged as additional area for previous allotted flat i.e. H002 Ground Floor. That the respondent had not reverted back to complainant of legal notice dated 25.05.2018. The complainant had obtained a loan of Rs 60,00,000 from the HDFC bank and has been paying Rs 47,000 per month an amount of interest to the bank.</p><div><br></div>','<p>i) To give necessary directions to the respondents for return of the payment made in lieu of unit/apartment till date along with the prescribed rate of interest from the date of execution of Allotment Letter till realization as per the provisions of Section 18 and 19(4) of the RERA Act.</p><p>ii) To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 60 of RERA Act for willful default committed by them.</p><p>iii) To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 61 of RERA Act for contravention of Sec.12, Sec.14, Sec. 15 and Sec. 16 of RERA Act.</p><p>iv) To direct the respondents to pay penalty upto 10% of project cost to the complainant under Sec. 59 of RERA, Act, 2016.</p><p>v) To direct the respondents to refund the amount collected from the complainant in lieu of interest, penalty for delayed payments under Rule 23(3)(c) of Punjab RERA Rules,2017.</p><p>vi) To issue directions to make liable every officer concerned i.e. Director, Manager, Secretary, or any other officer of the respondent’s company at whose instance, connivance, acquiescence, neglect any of the offences has been committed as mentioned in Sec.69 of RERA Act,2016 to be read with Punjab RERA Rules,2017.</p><p>vii) To direct respondent to deliver the flat to the complainant without charging the additional charges for the increased area of the flat.</p><p>viii) To recommend criminal action against the respondents for the criminal offence of cheating, fraud and criminal breach of trust under section 420,406 and 409 of the Indian Penal Code.</p><p>ix) To issue direction to pay the cost of litigation.</p><p>x) Any other relief which this Hon’ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances of this complaint.</p><p><br></p>',8260250.00,8137349.00,'2016-12-31 00:00:00.000','2017-04-30 00:00:00.000','<p>i. To direct the respondent not to demand any further amount whatsoever from the complainant.</p><p>ii. The respondent should be restrained from harassing the complainant in any manner whatsoever.</p><p>ii. Any other interim relief which this Hon\'ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances of this complaint.</p>','1','','2012-09-04 00:00:00','2017-02-21 00:00:00','Flat No 702 Tower H','','',1,0,0,0,'JurisAxisRera','2018-12-03 15:16:06.000','JurisAxisRera','2018-12-03 15:16:06.000'),(445,1097,'1097',1178,'02e82b67-7f34-47ae-80b9-cc89681213d6','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-10-29 12:56:00.000','Kanavdeep Singh','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9896165550,0,0,'H NO 1497 Sector 9 ','',13,10,'132001','1','H NO 1497 Sector 9 ','',13,10,'132001','Kamal Dahiya','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9729902009,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0085','Sushma Chandigarh Grande\r\n','Sushma Buildtech Ltd','customercare@sushmabuildtech.com',9872889933,0,'Unit No B 107 - Business Complex - Elante Mall, 1st Floor ','Industrial Area, Phase I',6,128,'160009','1','Unit No B 107 - Business Complex - Elante Mall, 1st Floor ','Industrial Area, Phase I',6,128,'160009','1','<p>The Complainant had purchased a flat/apartment in the said Project having an approximate 2085 sq. foot. The Complainant had been allotted Flat in Tower no. H i.e H002 (Ground Floor) admeasuring 2085 sq. feet vide Allotment Letter dated 04.09.2012- Annexure C-1. An ABA was executed on 04.09.2012. It has been specifically mentioned in of ABA, that the complainant has already paid booking amount of Rs. 12,39,038. towards purchase of the said apartment which form the part of the total consideration. The basic sale price of the said apartment was Rs. 82,60,250. The Complainant had opted for construction linked plan. The Complainant has paid INR 81,37,349 i.e. nearly 100% of payment out of total consideration till date including loan from HDFC Bank i.e Rs.60,00,000-Annexure C-2. As per the ABA, the date of possession is December 2016 but respondents didn’t give any possession to complainant and the agent of respondents namely Anuj asked complainant to replace his flat i.e H002 Ground Floor to 702, Tower-H as it would be delivered in April, 2017 and flat o