e respondents for return of the payment made in lieu of unit/apartment till date along with the prescribed rate of interest from the date of execution of Allotment Letter till realization as per the provisions of Section 18 and 19(4) of the RERA Act.</p><p>ii) To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 60 of RERA Act for willful default committed by them.</p><p>iii) To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 61 of RERA Act for contravention of Sec.12, Sec.14, Sec. 15 and Sec. 16 of RERA Act.</p><p>iv) To direct the respondents to pay penalty upto 10% of project cost to the complainant under Sec. 59 of RERA, Act, 2016.</p><p>v) To direct the respondents to refund the amount collected from the complainant in lieu of interest, penalty for delayed payments under Rule 23(3)(c) of Punjab RERA Rules,2017.</p><p>vi) To issue directions to make liable every officer concerned i.e. Director, Manager, Secretary, or any other officer of the respondent’s company at whose instance, connivance, acquiescence, neglect any of the offences has been committed as mentioned in Sec.69 of RERA Act,2016 to be read with Punjab RERA Rules,2017.</p><p>vii) To direct respondent to deliver the flat to the complainant without charging the additional charges for the increased area of the flat.</p><p>viii) To recommend criminal action against the respondents for the criminal offence of cheating, fraud and criminal breach of trust under section 420,406 and 409 of the Indian Penal Code.</p><p>ix) To issue direction to pay the cost of litigation.</p><p>x) Any other relief which this Hon’ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances of this complaint.</p><div><br></div>',8260250.00,8137349.00,'2016-12-31 00:00:00.000','2017-04-30 00:00:00.000','<p>i. To direct the respondent not to demand any further amount whatsoever from the complainant.</p><p>ii. The respondent should be restrained from harassing the complainant in any manner whatsoever.</p><p>ii. Any other interim relief which this Hon\'ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances of this complaint.</p>','1','','2012-09-04 00:00:00','2017-02-21 00:00:00','Flat No 702 Tower H','','',2,0,0,0,'JurisAxisRera','2018-12-03 15:42:15.000','JurisAxisRera','2018-12-03 15:42:15.000'),(447,1097,'1097',1178,'02e82b67-7f34-47ae-80b9-cc89681213d6','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-10-29 12:56:00.000','Kanavdeep Singh','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9896165550,0,0,'H NO 1497 Sector 9 ','',13,10,'132001','1','H NO 1497 Sector 9 ','',13,10,'132001','Kamal Dahiya','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9729902009,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0085','Sushma Chandigarh Grande\r\n','Sushma Buildtech Ltd','customercare@sushmabuildtech.com',9872889933,0,'Unit No B 107 - Business Complex - Elante Mall, 1st Floor ','Industrial Area, Phase I',6,128,'160009','1','Unit No B 107 - Business Complex - Elante Mall, 1st Floor ','Industrial Area, Phase I',6,128,'160009','1','<p>The Complainant had purchased a flat/apartment in the said Project having an approximate 2085 sq. foot. The Complainant had been allotted Flat in Tower no. H i.e H002 (Ground Floor) admeasuring 2085 sq. feet vide Allotment Letter dated 04.09.2012- Annexure C-1. An ABA was executed on 04.09.2012. It has been specifically mentioned in of ABA, that the complainant has already paid booking amount of Rs. 12,39,038. towards purchase of the said apartment which form the part of the total consideration. The basic sale price of the said apartment was Rs. 82,60,250. The Complainant had opted for construction linked plan. The Complainant has paid INR 81,37,349 i.e. nearly 100% of payment out of total consideration till date including loan from HDFC Bank i.e Rs.60,00,000-Annexure C-2. As per the ABA, the date of possession is December 2016 but respondents didn’t give any possession to complainant and the agent of respondents namely Anuj asked complainant to replace his flat i.e H002 Ground Floor to 702, Tower-H as it would be delivered in April, 2017 and flat on ground floor will take much more time. Thereafter,Tower H was allotted to complainant. New ABA was entered on 21.02.2017 and as per terms possession is to be delivered in April 2017-Annexure C-3. Now in month of December 2018 i.e. delay of 19 months from date of commitment, only 70% project is completed thus delaying the possession of Apartment deliberately or for reasons known best to them. The complainant has also sent legal notice to respondents but of no avail -Annexures C-4 &amp; C-5. That the respondent had refunded only Rs 12,00,000/- to the complainant which was earlier charged as additional area for previous allotted flat i.e. H002 Ground Floor. That the respondent had not reverted back to complainant of legal notice dated 25.05.2018. The complainant had obtained a loan of Rs 60,00,000 from the HDFC bank and has been paying Rs 47,000 per month an amount of interest to the bank.</p><div><br></div>','<p>i) To give necessary directions to the respondents for return of the payment made in lieu of unit/apartment till date along with the prescribed rate of interest from the date of execution of Allotment Letter till realization as per the provisions of Section 18 and 19(4) of the RERA Act.</p><p>ii) To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 60 of RERA Act for willful default committed by them.</p><p>iii) To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 61 of RERA Act for contravention of Sec.12, Sec.14, Sec. 15 and Sec. 16 of RERA Act.</p><p>iv) To direct the respondents to pay penalty upto 10% of project cost to the complainant under Sec. 59 of RERA, Act, 2016.</p><p>v) To direct the respondents to refund the amount collected from the complainant in lieu of interest, penalty for delayed payments under Rule 23(3)(c) of Punjab RERA Rules,2017.</p><p>vi) To issue directions to make liable every officer concerned i.e. Director, Manager, Secretary, or any other officer of the respondent’s company at whose instance, connivance, acquiescence, neglect any of the offences has been committed as mentioned in Sec.69 of RERA Act,2016 to be read with Punjab RERA Rules,2017.</p><p>vii) To direct respondent to deliver the flat to the complainant without charging the additional charges for the increased area of the flat.</p><p>viii) To recommend criminal action against the respondents for the criminal offence of cheating, fraud and criminal breach of trust under section 420,406 and 409 of the Indian Penal Code.</p><p>ix) To issue direction to pay the cost of litigation.</p><p>x) Any other relief which this Hon’ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances of this complaint.</p><div><br></div>',8260250.00,8137349.00,'2016-12-31 00:00:00.000','2017-04-30 00:00:00.000','<p>i. To direct the respondent not to demand any further amount whatsoever from the complainant.</p><p>ii. The respondent should be restrained from harassing the complainant in any manner whatsoever.</p><p>ii. Any other interim relief which this Hon\'ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances of this complaint.</p>','1','','2012-09-04 00:00:00','2017-02-21 00:00:00','Flat No 702 Tower H','','',2,0,0,0,'JurisAxisRera','2018-12-03 15:56:05.000','JurisAxisRera','2018-12-03 15:56:05.000'),(448,1162,'1162',1225,'fafedfd6-7d94-407d-bfcd-4cea99a9625a','FormTypeM',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','J N Singh','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9816400801,0,0,'312 2, Rani Ka Bagh','Shimla Road, NAHAN',14,544,'173001','1','312 2, Rani Ka Bagh','Shimla Road, NAHAN',14,544,'173001','KAMALJEET DAHIYA','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9729902009,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0093','PALM ECO CITY','MANOHAR INFRASTRUCTURE AND CONSTRUCTION PRIVATE LIMITED','nbs@manoharrealty.com',1725016888,1725016888,'SCO 139 141 LEVEL 1 SECTOR 17C','',6,128,'160017','1','SCO 139 141 LEVEL 1 SECTOR 17C','',6,128,'160017','1','<p>The complainant had purchased a plot in the said project having an approximate 250 sq. yard.The complainant had made payment of Rs 23,12,500/- at the time of allotment, on which the respondent had issued a letter for expression of interest to the complainant dated 26.03.2012 -Annexure C-1. The respondent sent a letter and assured that they would deliver the possession of plot by year 2015 -Annexure C-2.The respondent had issued a letter in 17.03.2014 wherein they assured that the project has reached its final stage and they would be in a position to deliver the possession of plot by 2015.That being influenced by the assurances and representations made by the respondent, the complainant paid Rs.10,00,000/- on the asking of the respondent vide cheque dated 09 Jan 2018 -Annexure C-3. The respondent had allotted plot No. 1035 admeasuring 250 sq. yard area in year 2018 to the complainant.&nbsp; The respondent had issued a letter to the complainant dated 02.02.2018 wherein the respondent levied the charges of IDC,PLC, Possession charges or any arbitrary charges which were not disclosed or agreed for at the time of initial booking of the plot - Annexure C-4. It is pertinent to mention here that the respondent has the intention to cheat the complainant since the beginning as it is proved by the malafide act and conduct of the respondent.The Complainant has paid INR 33,12,500/- i.e. more than 80% of payment out of total consideration i.e. Basic Sale Price, agreed at the time of booking the plot till Jan.18 - Annexure- C-5.The possession of the project was committed in the month of March 2015 and now in the month of November 2018 i.e. delay of 44 months from the date of the commitment, only 30% project is completed thus delaying the possession of the plot deliberately or for reasons known best to them.<br></p>','<p>In view of the facts mentioned in preceding paragraphs, the complainant prays for the following relief(s):-&nbsp;</p><p>i.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To give necessary directions to the respondents for delivery of possession of plot&nbsp; along with interest for delay in delivery of possession till realization as per the provisions of Sec. 18 and Sec.19(3)of the RERA Act read with Rule 16 of PSRE(R&amp;D)Rules,2017.</p><p>ii.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 60 of RERA Act for willful default committed by them.</p><p>iii.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 61 of RERA Act for contravention of Sec.12, Sec.14, and Sec. 16 of RERA Act.</p><p>iv.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To issue directions to make liable every officer concerned i.e. Director, Manager, Secretary, or any other officer of the respondent’s company at whose instance, connivance, acquiescence, neglect any of the offences has been committed as mentioned in Sec.69 of RERA Act,2016 to be read with Punjab RERA Rules,2017.</p><p>v.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To recommend criminal action against the respondents for the criminal offence of cheating, fraud and criminal breach of trust under section 420,406 and 409 of the Indian Penal Code.</p><p>vi.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To issue direction to pay the cost of litigation.</p><p>vii.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To issue direction to pay the compensation to complainant for compensation for his mental agony, pain and harassment.</p><p>viii.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Any other relief which this Hon’ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances of this complaint.</p><div><br></div>',4625000.00,3312500.00,'2015-12-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>i. To direct the respondent not to demand any further amount whatsoever from the complainant.</p><p>ii. The respondent should be restrained from harassing the complainant in any manner whatsoever.</p><p>iii. Any other interim relief which this Hon\'ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances of this complaint.</p>','1','','2012-03-26 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','PLOT NO 1035 VILLAGE MULLANPUR DHANAURAN AND MASATGARH LPA MULLANPUR SAS NAGAR','','',2,0,0,0,'JNSingh1','2018-12-03 16:46:30.000','JNSingh1','2018-12-03 16:46:30.000'),(449,1097,'1097',1178,'02e82b67-7f34-47ae-80b9-cc89681213d6','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-03 17:17:23.000','Kanavdeep Singh','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9896165550,0,0,'H NO 1497 Sector 9 ','',13,10,'132001','1','H NO 1497 Sector 9 ','',13,10,'132001','Kamal Dahiya','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9729902009,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0085','Sushma Chandigarh Grande\r\n','Sushma Buildtech Ltd','customercare@sushmabuildtech.com',9872889933,0,'Unit No B 107 - Business Complex - Elante Mall, 1st Floor ','Industrial Area, Phase I',6,128,'160009','1','Unit No B 107 - Business Complex - Elante Mall, 1st Floor ','Industrial Area, Phase I',6,128,'160009','1','<p>The Complainant had purchased a flat/apartment in the said Project having an approximate 2085 sq. foot. The Complainant had been allotted Flat in Tower no. H i.e H002 (Ground Floor) admeasuring 2085 sq. feet vide Allotment Letter dated 04.09.2012- Annexure C-1. An ABA was executed on 04.09.2012. It has been specifically mentioned in of ABA, that the complainant has already paid booking amount of Rs. 12,39,038. towards purchase of the said apartment which form the part of the total consideration. The basic sale price of the said apartment was Rs. 82,60,250. The Complainant had opted for construction linked plan. The Complainant has paid INR 81,37,349 i.e. nearly 100% of payment out of total consideration till date including loan from HDFC Bank i.e Rs.60,00,000-Annexure C-2. As per the ABA, the date of possession is December 2016 but respondents didn’t give any possession to complainant and the agent of respondents namely Anuj asked complainant to replace his flat i.e H002 Ground Floor to 702, Tower-H as it would be delivered in April, 2017 and flat on ground floor will take much more time. Thereafter,Tower H was allotted to complainant. New ABA was entered on 21.02.2017 and as per terms possession is to be delivered in April 2017-Annexure C-3. Now in month of December 2018 i.e. delay of 19 months from date of commitment, only 70% project is completed thus delaying the possession of Apartment deliberately or for reasons known best to them. The complainant has also sent legal notice to respondents but of no avail -Annexures C-4 &amp; C-5. That the respondent had refunded only Rs 12,00,000/- to the complainant which was earlier charged as additional area for previous allotted flat i.e. H002 Ground Floor. That the respondent had not reverted back to complainant of legal notice dated 25.05.2018. The complainant had obtained a loan of Rs 60,00,000 from the HDFC bank and has been paying Rs 47,000 per month an amount of interest to the bank.</p><div><br></div>','<p>i) To give necessary directions to the respondents for return of the payment made in lieu of unit/apartment till date along with the prescribed rate of interest from the date of execution of Allotment Letter till realization as per the provisions of Section 18 and 19(4) of the RERA Act.</p><p>ii) To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 60 of RERA Act for willful default committed by them.</p><p>iii) To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 61 of RERA Act for contravention of Sec.12, Sec.14, Sec. 15 and Sec. 16 of RERA Act.</p><p>iv) To direct the respondents to pay penalty upto 10% of project cost to the complainant under Sec. 59 of RERA, Act, 2016.</p><p>v) To direct the respondents to refund the amount collected from the complainant in lieu of interest, penalty for delayed payments under Rule 23(3)(c) of Punjab RERA Rules,2017.</p><p>vi) To issue directions to make liable every officer concerned i.e. Director, Manager, Secretary, or any other officer of the respondent’s company at whose instance, connivance, acquiescence, neglect any of the offences has been committed as mentioned in Sec.69 of RERA Act,2016 to be read with Punjab RERA Rules,2017.</p><p>vii) To direct respondent to deliver the flat to the complainant without charging the additional charges for the increased area of the flat.</p><p>viii) To recommend criminal action against the respondents for the criminal offence of cheating, fraud and criminal breach of trust under section 420,406 and 409 of the Indian Penal Code.</p><p>ix) To issue direction to pay the cost of litigation.</p><p>x) Any other relief which this Hon’ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances of this complaint.</p><div><br></div>',8260250.00,8137349.00,'2016-12-31 00:00:00.000','2017-04-30 00:00:00.000','<p>i. To direct the respondent not to demand any further amount whatsoever from the complainant.</p><p>ii. The respondent should be restrained from harassing the complainant in any manner whatsoever.</p><p>ii. Any other interim relief which this Hon\'ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances of this complaint.</p>','1','','2012-09-04 00:00:00','2017-02-21 00:00:00','Flat No 702 Tower H','','',1,1,0,0,'JurisAxisRera','2018-12-03 17:16:20.000','JurisAxisRera','2018-12-03 17:16:20.000'),(450,1162,'1162',1225,'fafedfd6-7d94-407d-bfcd-4cea99a9625a','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-04 18:32:27.000','J N Singh','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9816400801,0,0,'312 2, Rani Ka Bagh','Shimla Road, NAHAN',14,544,'173001','1','312 2, Rani Ka Bagh','Shimla Road, NAHAN',14,544,'173001','KAMALJEET DAHIYA','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9729902009,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0093','PALM ECO CITY','MANOHAR INFRASTRUCTURE AND CONSTRUCTION PRIVATE LIMITED','nbs@manoharrealty.com',1725016888,1725016888,'SCO 139 141 LEVEL 1 SECTOR 17C','',6,128,'160017','1','SCO 139 141 LEVEL 1 SECTOR 17C','',6,128,'160017','1','<p>The co