 necessary directions to the respondents for delivery of possession of plot&nbsp; along with interest for delay in delivery of possession till realization as per the provisions of Sec. 18 and Sec.19(3)of the RERA Act read with Rule 16 of PSRE(R&amp;D)Rules,2017.</p><p>ii.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 60 of RERA Act for willful default committed by them.</p><p>iii.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 61 of RERA Act for contravention of Sec.12, Sec.14, and Sec. 16 of RERA Act.</p><p>iv.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To issue directions to make liable every officer concerned i.e. Director, Manager, Secretary, or any other officer of the respondent’s company at whose instance, connivance, acquiescence, neglect any of the offences has been committed as mentioned in Sec.69 of RERA Act,2016 to be read with Punjab RERA Rules,2017.</p><p>v.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To recommend criminal action against the respondents for the criminal offence of cheating, fraud and criminal breach of trust under section 420,406 and 409 of the Indian Penal Code.</p><p>vi.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To issue direction to pay the cost of litigation.</p><p>vii.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To issue direction to pay the compensation to complainant for compensation for his mental agony, pain and harassment.</p><p>viii.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Any other relief which this Hon’ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances of this complaint.</p><div><br></div>',4625000.00,3312500.00,'2015-12-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>i. To direct the respondent not to demand any further amount whatsoever from the complainant.</p><p>ii. The respondent should be restrained from harassing the complainant in any manner whatsoever.</p><p>iii. Any other interim relief which this Hon\'ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances of this complaint.</p>','1','','2012-03-26 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','PLOT NO 1035 VILLAGE MULLANPUR DHANAURAN AND MASATGARH LPA MULLANPUR SAS NAGAR','','',1,1,0,0,'JNSingh1','2018-12-03 17:27:12.000','JNSingh1','2018-12-03 17:27:12.000'),(451,1163,'1163',1243,'6e878da0-60b6-4cac-b4e4-c86508c84474','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-05 15:55:46.000','Ambika Khullar','rkaushal009@gmail.com',9041176988,0,0,'H. No. 898, 2nd Floor, Phase VII, SAS Nagar, Mohali','',28,507,'160055','1','H. No. 898, 2nd Floor, Phase VII, SAS Nagar, Mohali','',28,507,'160055','Rachit Kaushal','rkaushal009@gmail.com',9464500306,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0084','SUSHMA CRESCENT','Sushma Buildtech Limited','bhupinder@sushmabuildtech.com',9872889933,0,'B-107, Business Complex, Elante Mall, 1st Floor, Industrial Area Phase I, Chandigarh','',6,128,'160009','1','B-107, Business Complex, Elante Mall, 1st Floor, Industrial Area Phase I, Chandigarh','',6,128,'160009','1','<p>1. Project Applied for allotment in: Sushma Crescent, Zirakpur</p><p>2. Application form: 05.11.2011</p><p>3. Unit Allotted: C-201, 2nd Floor, Tower C, Sushma Crescent, Super Area 1609 sq ft, Village Gazipur, Municipal Corporation Zirakpur, Distt SAS Nagar, Mohali, Punjab.</p><p>4. Basic Sale Price: 41,38,810/-&nbsp;</p><p>5. Payment made without respondents entering into Buyers\' Agreement - Rs. 21,61,347/- (Approx 52%)&nbsp;</p><p>6. Buyers\' Agreement Executed on 16.10.2013, i.e., after almost two years of allotment and after taking a substantial amount. (Annexure C-1)</p><p>7. Allotment Letter dated 25.10.2013 (Annexure C-2)</p><p>8. Clause 14(d) of Buyers\' Agreement mandated possession within 36 months with 6 months grace period. Even from agreement date, the possession of the unit was to be handed last by 16.04.2017.&nbsp;</p><p>9. Loan Facility availed by the Complainant and loan was sanctioned vide Sanction Letter dated 10.10.2013 (Annexure C-3) from HDFC Ltd and a loan of Rs. 22,52,000/- was sanctioned, out of which Rs. 20,64,443/- has been disbursed by the HDFC Ltd on account of the Complainants and an EMI of Rs. 19,196/- is being paid by the Complainants since 12.11.2013. Copy of Accounts Statement from HDFC (C-4).</p><p>10. Till date a total amount of Rs. 47,22,836/- has been paid by the complainants.&nbsp;</p><p>11. Letter of Offer of possession dated 20.03.2018&nbsp; (Annexure C-5) was sent by the respondents along with Possession demand Letter dated 20.03.2018 (Annexure C-6) demanding Rs. 5,65,707/-.</p><p>12. That Vide Cheque no 000173 dated 07.04.2018, Drawn on Kotak Mahindra Bank, Complainants again paid Rs. 2,82,473/- to the respondents. (Annexure C-7)</p><p>13. Complainant is constrained to live on rent awaiting the possession of their apartment. Copies of rent receipts and Rent Agreements are annexed as Annexures C-8 &amp; C-9.</p><p>Aggrieved by the illegal and baseless demand of interest in alleged delayed payment, the Complainants are moving this Hon\'ble Authority with a prayer for compensation and physical possession.</p>','<p>In view of the factual matrix as mentioned in para 4 of this complaint, the Complainants seek the kind indulgence of this Hon’ble Authority in granting the following reliefs:</p><p>1.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To hand over the actual physical possession of the unit as promised by the Respondent company with immediate effect;</p><p>2.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To direct the respondent company to waive off its demand of interest for delayed payments (C-9);</p><p>3.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To direct the respondent to pay interest to the Complainants for keeping an amount of Rs. 21,61,347/- from the date of respective deposits till date of execution of buyers\' agreement dated 16.10.2013;</p><p>4.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To direct the respondent to pay a compensation of Rs. 2 Lakh for mental agony and harassment meted out to the Complainants on account of delay in possession and illegal demands;&nbsp;</p><p>5.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To direct the respondent to pay for the rent of the Complainant No 1&nbsp; from the date the possession was to fall due had the respondents executed the buyers\' agreement in 2011 itself, when the respondent accepted the first payment from the Complainants;</p><p>6.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>The Complaint may be allowed with Costs and of Litigation&nbsp; expenses amounting to Rs. 100,000/- (Rupees One Lakh only);</p><p>7.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Any other relief that this Hon’ble Authority may deem fit and appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances of the present complaint</p><div><br></div>',4138810.00,4722836.00,'2017-04-16 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>NIL</p>','1','','2013-10-25 00:00:00','2018-12-16 00:00:00','C-201, 2nd Floor, Tower C, Sushma Crescent, Zirakpur, Distt SAS Nagar, Mohali','','',1,1,0,0,'RERACOMPLAINT@rachit','2018-12-03 17:43:12.000','RERACOMPLAINT@rachit','2018-12-03 17:43:12.000'),(452,1164,'1164',1078,'d8d4f172-3c37-4e70-b72a-876b113f98f3','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-29 12:53:00.000','Keshav Rai Dhanda ','vikramsinghchahal@gmail.com',9781750447,0,0,'H. No.B-1-1315','Opposite Old Courts, Civil Lines',28,366,'141001','1','H. No.B-1-1315','Opposite Old Courts, Civil Lines',28,366,'141001','Vikram Singh Chahal','vikramsinghchahal@gmail.com',9781750447,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-LDH45-PR0060','M/s. Ireo Waterfront Pvt. Ltd','IREO Waterfront Pvt. Ltd','iwp@ireo.in',0,0,'A-11, 1st Floor, Neeti Bagh, New Delhi South Delhi','',10,557,'110049','1','A-11, 1st Floor, Neeti Bagh, New Delhi South Delhi','',10,557,'110049','1','<p>The complainant fell fray to the tall claims made by the O.Ps. wherein they claimed for setting up a Township in Ludhiana(Punjab) in more than 500 acres of land and the complainant considering his need for owning a residential property for his self and his family members, decided to purchase one Villa on Construction Linked Plan. On 31.03.2011 complainant paid a sum of Rs.16,43,000/- towards the booking price of Villa No.C-I-167. The said Villa was to be constructed upto second floor having built up area of 4556 sq. ft. on plot measuring 374.56 sq. Yds., having basic sale price of Rs.1,59,46,000/-.  Villa Buyer’s Agreement dated 23.09.2011 was executed. As per clause No.11.3 of the said agreement the possession was to be offered on or before 22.09.2013. The complainant from time to time made the payment of the consideration money and also availed loan from Bank of India amounting to Rs.74,50,000/- and executed a Tripartite Agreement in May 2012. The complainant as such made the total payment of Rs.1,60,82,520/- . Inspite of the complainant having made the payments as above the progress of construction at the site was hopelessly slow and the development of the project was nowhere near completion. The amenities as promised in the agreement were far from being completed, as such the O.Ps. had left the project in lurch. The O.Ps. however, for all this time were just continuously demanding for more and more money. The complainant visited the site in July 2013 and was shocked to note that the project was nowhere near future inspite of the fact that the Construction Linked Plan is 75% of the money was received from the complainant&nbsp;<span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 12.5pt;\">but neither of the amenity promised in the\r\nagreement were provided/ completed.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 12.5pt;\">It may be mentioned here that the complainant\r\nall this time was making the payment by availing loan from financial\r\ninstitution and was also paying interest upon the loan so taken.</span></p>','<p><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:13.5pt;mso-bidi-font-size:\r\n11.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\nCalibri;mso-fareast-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN;mso-fareast-language:\r\nEN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\"></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:6.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:6.0pt;\r\nmargin-left:0cm;text-align:justify;line-height:150%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">That the present complaint is\r\nwithin limitation as the letter dated 12.02.2016 has till date not been\r\nresponded to by the Opposite Parties. Further the Opposite Parties have failed\r\nto obtain the Completion and Occupation Certificate and complete the\r\ndevelopment work as per the Agreement, as such the cause of action are\r\ncontinuing in nature.&nbsp;</span></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:6.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:6.0pt;\r\nmargin-left:0cm;text-align:justify;line-height:150%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; line-height: 115%;\">That this Hon’ble Court has the jurisdiction to\r\nentertain the present complaint as the project of the Opposite Parties has been\r\nregistered under the “RERA Act” vide PR0060POCKET-I and is located at Ludhiana\r\nwhich is within the jurisdiction of this Hon’ble Court.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><br></span><o:p></o:p></span></p><p><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:13.5pt;mso-bidi-font-size:\r\n11.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\nCalibri;mso-fareast-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN;mso-fareast-language:\r\nEN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; line-height: 115%;\">That earlier the complainants had filed\r\ncomplaint before this Hon’ble Court the same was dismissed in default vide\r\norder 21.03.2018 on account of noting down of wrong date. The complaint of the\r\ncomplainant was yet to be registered and no notice was sent to the O.Ps.\r\ntherefore, res-judicata is not applicable to the present case. Further the\r\nsubsequent complaint filed by the complainants was disposed off by the\r\nAdjudicating Officer vide order dated 01.11.2018 on account of the passing of\r\nthe Circular dated 29.10.2018.</span><br></span></p><p><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 18px; line-height: 115%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">RELIEF: The complainant being fed up by the acts of\r\nomission and commission on the part of the O.Ps. is left with no other option\r\nbut to file the present complaint seeking the refund of the amount of the\r\nRs.1,60,82,520/- alongwith interest @ 12% beside cost of litigation to the tune\r\nof Rs.2,00,000/- and compensation of Rs.10,00,000/-.</span><br></p>',15946000.00,16082520.00,'2013-09-29 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>NA</p>','0','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','2011-09-23 00:00:00','Villa No.C-I-167','','',2,0,0,0,'P43982017','2018-12-03 17:53:08.000','P43982017','2018-12-03 17:53:08.000'),(453,1165,'1165',1146,'7dfad30e-4afa-4859-8a26-94b85edcd0f5','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Ashish Kumar Jain','jarnailthakur@yahoo.com',9815695783,0,0,'C/o Sandeep Jain # 5368-C, Nicholson Road, Punjabi Mohalla, Ambala Cantt','Amabala Cantt',13,1,'133001','1','C/o Sandeep Jain # 5368-C, Nicholson Road, Punjabi Mohalla, Ambala Cantt','Amabala Cantt',13,1,'133001','J S Thakur','jarnailthakur@yahoo.com',9815695779,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PM0010','Fashion Technology Park, Sector 90 Mohali','Chandigarh Overseas Pvt. Ltd','sanjaychugh.biz@gmail.com',0,1725001170,'sco 196-197 Top Floor, Sector 34A Chandigarh','Chandigarh',6,128,'160022','1','sco 196-197 Top Floor, Sector 34A Chandigarh','Chandigarh',6,128,'160022','1','<p><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:115%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-ascii-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-theme-font:minor-fareast;mso-hansi-theme-font:\r\nminor-latin;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;\r\nmso-ansi-language:EN-US;mso-fareast-language:EN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\">The\r\nrespondents came up with a project in sector 90, Mohali, named as Fashion\r\nTechnology Park in the year 2006. The complainant booked 4 units of 100/125 sq.\r\nft. each. On 02.09.2006and paid Rs. 5 lac out of the total amount payable Rs.\r\n20 lac @ Rs. 5 lac per unit. Total payment made by the complainant is Rs.19\r\nlac. Construction was to commence in 2<sup>nd</sup> week of sep 2006. He was\r\nallotted 4 units of 100 sq. ft. each in Design Studio no. 6 on 5<sup>th</sup>\r\nfloor. The respondents assured of fixed returns as also of a buy back scheme\r\n@7.5 lac per unit. The construction was to be completed in 30 months from Sep\r\n2006, but the same was never done. Further the Respondents &nbsp;purported to enter into a Developer Buyer\r\nagreement and one Lease agreement, obtained the complainant’s signatures\r\nthereon, asked him to collect the said agreements duly signed and dated by the\r\nauthorised persons which was never done.&nbsp;\r\nThe Respondents sent a letter dated 22.06.2009 offering to buy back the\r\n4 units @7.5 lac per unit. The complainant accepted the offer and was\r\nacknowledged by the Respondents &nbsp;vide\r\ntheir letter dated 13.01.2010. The Respondents paid a sum of Rs. 7.5 lac for\r\nbuy back of one unit, but the balance amount of Rs. 22.50 lac for remaining\r\nthree units was never paid. The complainant was also assured of compensation\r\nfor delay@ Rs. 50 per sq. ft per month as per clause 28 of Developer Buyer\r\nagreement. Accordingly they paid a sum of Rs.48388/- vide cheque dated\r\n31.03.2010 only once and nothing thereafter. The Respondents have made the\r\ncomplainant to run from pillar to post and have caused him great harassment and\r\nmental torture.</span><br></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><i><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n115%\">The complainant</span></i><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:115%\">\r\nprays for a direction to the Respondents:<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-justify:\r\ninter-ideograph;text-indent:-.25in\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n115%\">1. To pay the balance amount of Rs.22,50,000/- with interest @18% p.a.\r\nwith effect from 02.03.2010 till actual payment.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-justify:\r\ninter-ideograph;text-indent:-.25in\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n115%\">2. To pay for delay @Rs.50/- per square foot per month w.e.f. 02.03.2010 along\r\nwith interest @18% per annum till actual payment.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-justify:\r\ninter-ideograph;text-indent:-.25in\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n115%\">3.To pay a sum of Rs.10 lacs for the mental torture, agony and harassment\r\nto the complainant and for making him run from pillar to post to avail his\r\nrights.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-justify:\r\ninter-ideograph;text-indent:-.25in\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n115%\">4. To pay litigation costs to the tune of Rs.1,10,000/- which he has so\r\nfar incurred.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-justify:\r\ninter-ideograph;text-indent:-.25in\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n115%\">5.&nbsp; To not to alienate, cancel the\r\nallotment,&nbsp; sell, transfer, mortgage,\r\netc. the allotted units in Design Studio no. 6 in the Fashion Technology Park\r\nSector 90, Mohali.<o:p></o:p></span></p>',2000000.00,1900000.00,'2010-01-02 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><i><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n115%\">The complainant</span></i><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:115%\">\r\nprays for a direction to the Respondents:<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-justify:\r\ninter-ideograph;text-indent:-.25in\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n115%\">1. To pay the balance amount of Rs.22,50,000/- with interest @18% p.a.\r\nwith effect from 02.03.2010 till actual payment.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-justify:\r\ninter-ideograph;text-indent:-.25in\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n115%\">2. To pay for delay @Rs.50/- per square foot per month w.e.f. 02.03.2010 along\r\nwith interest @18% per annum till actual payment.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-justify:\r\ninter-ideograph;text-indent:-.25in\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n115%\">3.To pay a sum of Rs.10 lacs for the mental torture, agony and harassment\r\nto the complainant and for making him run from pillar to post to avail his\r\nrights.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-justify:\r\ninter-ideograph;text-indent:-.25in\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n115%\">4. To pay litigation costs to the tune of Rs.1,10,000/- which he has so\r\nfar incurred.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-justify:\r\ninter-ideograph;text-indent:-.25in\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n115%\">5.&nbsp; To not to alienate, cancel the\r\nallotment,&nbsp; sell, transfer, mortgage,\r\netc. the allotted units in Design Studio no. 6 in the Fashion Technology Park\r\nSector 90, Mohali.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','4 Units in Design Studio No.6','','',1,0,0,0,'jarnailthakur','2018-12-03 19:30:32.000','jarnailthakur','2018-12-03 19:30:32.000'),(454,1166,'1166',1244,'04c5757f-b88d-445e-8905-46acb1e6dbed','FormTypeM',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','SUMIT  KUMAR','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9729902009,0,0,'4E/10 NORTH SRI KRISHNA PURI RAM KRISHNA PATH PATNA','',5,455,'800013','1','4E/10 NORTH SRI KRISHNA PURI RAM KRISHNA PATH PATNA','',5,455,'800013','KAMALJEET DAHIYA','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9729902009,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0093','PALM GARDEN','MANOHAR INFRASTRUCTURE AND CONSTRUCTIONS PVT. LTD.','nbs@manoharrealty.com',1725016888,1725016888,'SCO 139 141 LEVEL 1 SECTOR 17 C','',6,128,'160017','1','SCO 139 141 LEVEL 1 SECTOR 17 C','',6,128,'160017','1','<p>The complainant had purchased a plot in the said project having an approximate 250 sq. yard.The complainant had made payment of Rs 13,87,500/- at the time of allotment, on which the respondent had issued an Application Acknowledgment to the complainant dated 09.04.2012 -Annexure C-1. The respondent sent a letter and assured that they would deliver the possession of plot by year 2015 -Annexure C-2. The respondent had issued a letter in 18.03.2014 wherein they requested for further sum of deposit to the tune of Rs. 9,25,000/- and assured that the project has reached its final stage and they would be in a position to deliver the possession of plot by 2015 - Annexure C-3.The complainant had paid Rs 15,50,000/- to the respondent, for which the respondent had issued receipts to the complainant dated 29.01.2018 Annexure C-4.The respondent had allotted plot No. 1069 admeasuring 250 sq. yard area in year 2018 to the complainant.&nbsp; The respondent had issued a letter to the complainant dated 15.02.2018 wherein the respondent levied the charges of IDC,PLC, Possession charges or any arbitrary charges which were not disclosed oragreed for at the time of initial booking of the plot - Annexure C-5. It is pertinent to mention here that the respondent has the intention to cheat the complainant since the beginning as it is proved by the malafide act and conduct of the respondent. The Complainant has paid INR 21,87,500/- i.e. more than 70% of payment out of total consideration i.e. Basic Sale Price, agreed at the time of booking the plot till Jan.18 - Annexure C-6.The possession of the project was committed in the month of March 2015 and now in the month of November 2018 i.e. delay of 44 months from the date of the commitment, only 30% project is completed thus delaying the possession of the plot deliberately or for reasons known best to them.<br></p>','<p>In view of the facts mentioned in preceding paragraphs, the complainant prays for the following relief(s):-&nbsp;</p><p>i.To give necessary directions to the respondent for the compensation as the respondent has fail to give the possession as per the provisions of Sec. 18 and Sec.19(4)of the RERA Act read with Rule 16 of PBRE(R&amp;D)Rules,2017.</p><p>ii.To direct the respondent to pay the compensation under section 12 of the RERA Act, 2016.</p><p>iii.To issue directions to make liable every officer concerned i.e. Director, Manager, Secretary, or any other officer of the respondent’s company at whose instance, connivance, acquiescence, neglect any of the offences has been committed as mentioned in Sec.69 of RERA Act,2016 to be read with Punjab RERA Rules, 2017.</p><p>iv.To recommend criminal action against the respondents for the criminal offence of cheating, fraud and criminal breach of trust under section 420,406 and 409 of the Indian Penal Code.</p><p>v.To issue direction to pay the cost of litigation.</p><p>vi.To issue direction to pay the compensation to complainant for compensation for his mental agony, pain and harassment.</p><p>vii.Any other relief which this Hon’ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances of this complaint.</p>',4625000.00,2187500.00,'2015-03-30 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>i. To direct the respondent not to demand any further amount whatsoever from the complainant. ii. The Respondent should be restrained from harassing the complainant in any manner whatsoever. iii. Any other interim relief which this Hon\'ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances of this complaint.</p>','1','','2012-04-09 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','PLOT NUMBER 1069 VILLAGES MULLANPUR DHANAURAN AND MASATGARH LPA MULLANPUR SAS NAGAR','','',2,0,0,0,'sumitkumar001','2018-12-04 11:24:20.000','sumitkumar001','2018-12-04 11:24:20.000'),(455,1103,'1103',1197,'48449df7-379b-405e-98c2-f285f525d12f','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-11-09 16:48:57.000','Jasbir Singh','csvedparkash@gmail.com',9814700360,0,0,'Churchview, 1St. Peters Close','Burnham SLI 7HS, United Kingdom',28,507,'160059','1','H. NO. 360','Phase-4, SAS Nagar',28,507,'160059','Manjit Singh','',9814700360,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0119','The Views at Mohali Hills','EMAAR MGF Land Limited','enquiries@emaarmgf.com',1723314801,0,'EMAAR MGF Land Private Limited','1st Floor, SCO No. 120-122, Sector-17C, Chandigarh',6,128,'160017','1','EMAAR MGF Land Private Limited','1st Floor, SCO No. 120-122, Sector-17C, Chandigarh',6,128,'160017','1','<ul><li><li>That the Applicants are the residents of U.K. and are British subjects and desirous and looking forward to buy a residential house for themselves.&nbsp; The Applicants came across a brochure issued by the Respondent that they have been granted the approvals and exemptions to construct a Group Housing Complex and has planned for constructing the same the Colony, known as the ‘Mohali Hills’, to be constructed on the land consisting of high-end Apartments and Pent Houses, Car parking spaces, recreational facilities etc.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>That the Applicants being allured with the information about the approvals and legal rights of the Respondent, known as Company, moved an Application on 13.07.2007 for registration/ provisional allotment of a residential apartment in the Group Housing Complex and the Applicants deposited Rs.1,62,080/- for booking deposit of the area of 1,750 sq. feet under Order No. 601685 with the Customer Code No. TVM/454 and issued a provisional Allotment of Unit No./ Apartment No. L-3/1103 with total consideration of Rs.57,01,543/-.&nbsp; A copy of the letter dated 23.07.2007 is annexed herewith as ANNEXURE A-1.&nbsp;</li><li>That thereafter, the Claimant deposited a sum of Rs.5,37,920/- and Rs.3,46,208/- on 30.09.2007 and further a sum of Rs.40,49,131/- on 31.10.2007 (Total paid amount : Rs.50,95,339/-.&nbsp;</li><li>That the Claimant was allotted Unit No. L-3/1103 in Tower No. ‘L’ with a total cost of Rs.57,01,543/- in the Project known as ‘The Views’ vide letter dated 23.07.2007 and an Agreement was signed/executed on 11.02.2008 through the Authorized Signatory of the Respondent.&nbsp; The details of the Apartments have also been mentioned in para No. 1.1 of the Agreement with three Bed Rooms and three toilets and super area of 1,750 sq. feet @ Rs.2,950/- per sq. feet.&nbsp; &nbsp;A copy of the Agreement is annexed herewith as ANNEXURE A-2.</li></li></ul>','<p>In view of the facts mentioned in Paragraph 4 above, the Applicant prays for the following compensation(s):-</p><p>Refund of an amount of Rs.50,95,339/- paid by the Applicants along with interest (highest marginal cost of lending rate of the State Bank of India+2%) from the respective dates of deposit till actual realization as per Sections 18 and 19(4) of the Act read with Rule 16 of the Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017.</p><p>Payment of compensation of Rs.10.00 lacs due to the inordinate delay on the part of the Respondent in failing to handover possession of the Allotted Unit; mental agony, harassment and escalation in the prices of the Real Estate as per Sections 18 and 19(4) of the Act read with Rule 16 of the Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017.</p><p>Any other relief which the Applicants are entitled for under the Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Act, 2016 and the Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017.&nbsp;</p><div><br></div>',5701543.00,0.00,'2010-10-05 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<div><br></div><ul><li>Refund of an amount of Rs.50,95,339/- paid by the Applicants along with interest (highest marginal cost of lending rate of the State Bank of India+2%) from the respective dates of deposit till actual realization as per Sections 18 and 19(4) of the Act read with Rule 16 of the Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017.</li></ul>','1','','2007-10-05 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Unit No.TVM-L3-F11-1103 Tower No.F,The Views at Mohali Hills, Sector-105, SAS Nagar Mohali (Pb)','','',2,0,0,0,'jasbirsinghc','2018-12-04 13:45:57.000','jasbirsinghc','2018-12-04 13:45:57.000'),(456,1103,'1103',1197,'48449df7-379b-405e-98c2-f285f525d12f','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-11-09 16:48:57.000','Jasbir Singh','csvedparkash@gmail.com',9814700360,0,0,'Churchview, 1St. Peters Close','Burnham SLI 7HS, United Kingdom',28,507,'160059','1','H. NO. 360','Phase-4, SAS Nagar',28,507,'160059','Manjit Singh','',9814700360,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0119','The Views at Mohali Hills','EMAAR MGF Land Limited','enquiries@emaarmgf.com',1723314801,0,'EMAAR MGF Land Private Limited','1st Floor, SCO No. 120-122, Sector-17C, Chandigarh',6,128,'160017','1','EMAAR MGF Land Private Limited','1st Floor, SCO No. 120-122, Sector-17C, Chandigarh',6,128,'160017','1','<ul><li><li>That the Applicants are the residents of U.K. and are British subjects and desirous and looking forward to buy a residential house for themselves.&nbsp; The Applicants came across a brochure issued by the Respondent that they have been granted the approvals and exemptions to construct a Group Housing Complex and has planned for constructing the same the Colony, known as the ‘Mohali Hills’, to be constructed on the land consisting of high-end Apartments and Pent Houses, Car parking spaces, recreational facilities etc.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>That the Applicants being allured with the information about the approvals and legal rights of the Respondent, known as Company, moved an Application on 13.07.2007 for registration/ provisional allotment of a residential apartment in the Group Housing Complex and the Applicants deposited Rs.1,62,080/- for booking deposit of the area of 1,750 sq. feet under Order No. 601685 with the Customer Code No. TVM/454 and issued a provisional Allotment of Unit No./ Apartment No. L-3/1103 with total consideration of Rs.57,01,543/-.&nbsp; A copy of the letter dated 23.07.2007 is annexed herewith as ANNEXURE A-1.&nbsp;</li><li>That thereafter, the Claimant deposited a sum of Rs.5,37,920/- and Rs.3,46,208/- on 30.09.2007 and further a sum of Rs.40,49,131/- on 31.10.2007 (Total paid amount : Rs.50,95,339/-.&nbsp;</li><li>That the Claimant was allotted Unit No. L-3/1103 in Tower No. ‘L’ with a total cost of Rs.57,01,543/- in the Project known as ‘The Views’ vide letter dated 23.07.2007 and an Agreement was signed/executed on 11.02.2008 through the Authorized Signatory of the Respondent.&nbsp; The details of the Apartments have also been mentioned in para No. 1.1 of the Agreement with three Bed Rooms and three toilets and super area of 1,750 sq. feet @ Rs.2,950/- per sq. feet.&nbsp; &nbsp;A copy of the Agreement is annexed herewith as ANNEXURE A-2.</li></li></ul>','<p>In view of the facts mentioned in Paragraph 4 above, the Applicant prays for the following compensation(s):-</p><p>Refund of an amount of Rs.50,95,339/- paid by the Applicants along with interest (highest marginal cost of lending rate of the State Bank of India+2%) from the respective dates of deposit till actual realization as per Sections 18 and 19(4) of the Act read with Rule 16 of the Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017.</p><p>Payment of compensation of Rs.10.00 lacs due to the inordinate delay on the part of the Respondent in failing to handover possession of the Allotted Unit; mental agony, harassment and escalation in the prices of the Real Estate as per Sections 18 and 19(4) of the Act read with Rule 16 of the Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017.</p><p>Any other relief which the Applicants are entitled for under the Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Act, 2016 and the Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017.&nbsp;</p><div><br></div>',5701543.00,0.00,'2010-10-05 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<div><br></div><ul><li>Refund of an amount of Rs.50,95,339/- paid by the Applicants along with interest (highest marginal cost of lending rate of the State Bank of India+2%) from the respective dates of deposit till actual realization as per Sections 18 and 19(4) of the Act read with Rule 16 of the Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017.</li></ul>','1','','2007-10-05 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Unit No.TVM-L3-F11-1103 Tower No.F,The Views at Mohali Hills, Sector-105, SAS Nagar Mohali (Pb)','','',2,0,0,0,'jasbirsinghc','2018-12-04 13:46:07.000','jasbirsinghc','2018-12-04 13:46:07.000'),(457,1103,'1103',1197,'48449df7-379b-405e-98c2-f285f525d12f','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-04 13:53:49.000','Jasbir Singh','csvedparkash@gmail.com',9814700360,0,0,'Churchview, 1St. Peters Close','Burnham SLI 7HS, United Kingdom',28,507,'160059','1','H. NO. 360','Phase-4, SAS Nagar',28,507,'160059','Manjit Singh','',9814700360,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0119','The Views at Mohali Hills','EMAAR MGF Land Limited','enquiries@emaarmgf.com',1723314801,0,'EMAAR MGF Land Private Limited','1st Floor, 