ssion of plot by 2015 - Annexure C-3. The complainant had paid Rs 15,50,000/- to the respondent, for which the respondent had issued receipts to the complainant dated 29.01.2018 Annexure C-4. The respondent had allotted plot No. 1069 admeasuring 250 sq. yard area in year 2018 to the complainant.&nbsp; The respondent had issued a letter to the complainant dated 15.02.2018 wherein the respondent levied the charges of IDC,PLC, Possession charges or any arbitrary charges which were not disclosed or agreed for at the time of initial booking of the plot - Annexure C-5. It is pertinent to mention here that the respondent has the intention to cheat the complainant since the beginning as it is proved by the malafide act and conduct of the respondent. The Complainant has paid INR 21,87,500/- i.e. more than 70% of payment out of total consideration i.e. Basic Sale Price, agreed at the time of booking the plot till Jan.18 - Annexure C-6.The possession of the project was committed in the month of March 2015 and now in the month of November 2018 i.e. delay of 44 months from the date of the commitment, only 30% project is completed thus delaying the possession of the plot deliberately or for reasons known best to them.<br></p>','<p>In view of the facts mentioned in preceding paragraphs, the complainant prays for the following relief(s):-&nbsp;</p><p>i.To give necessary directions to the respondents for delivery of possession of plot along with interest for delay in delivery of possession till realization as per the provisions of Sec. 18 and Sec.19(3)of the RERA Act read with Rule 16 of PSRE(R&amp;D)Rules,2017.</p><p>ii.To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 60 of RERA Act for willful default committed by them.</p><p>iii.To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 61 of RERA Act for contravention of Sec.12, Sec.14, and Sec. 16 of RERA Act.</p><p>iv.To issue directions to make liable every officer concerned i.e. Director, Manager, Secretary, or any other officer of the respondent’s company at whose instance, connivance, acquiescence, neglect any of the offences has been committed as mentioned in Sec.69 of RERA Act,2016 to be read with Punjab RERA Rules,2017.</p><p>v.To recommend criminal action against the respondents for the criminal offence of cheating, fraud and criminal breach of trust under section 420,406 and 409 of the Indian Penal Code.</p><p>vi.To issue direction to pay the cost of litigation.</p><p>vii.To issue direction to pay the compensation to complainant for compensation for his mental agony, pain and harassment.</p><p>viii.Any other relief which this Hon’ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances of this complaint.</p>',4625000.00,2187500.00,'2015-03-30 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>i. To direct the respondent not to demand any further amount whatsoever from the complainant. </p><p>ii. The Respondent should be restrained from harassing the complainant in any manner whatsoever. </p><p>iii. Any other interim relief which this Hon\'ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances of this complaint.</p>','1','','2012-04-09 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','PLOT NUMBER 1069 VILLAGES MULLANPUR DHANAURAN AND MASATGARH LPA MULLANPUR SAS NAGAR','','',1,1,0,0,'sumitkumar001','2018-12-05 12:15:47.000','sumitkumar001','2018-12-05 12:15:47.000'),(467,1167,'1167',1234,'d78857a3-82bc-4872-8c7b-248177bcab69','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Tarun Singhal','tarunsinghal.adv@gmail.com',9988595908,0,0,'House no.80, Huda Colony, Sector 1, Shahabad Markanda.','',13,11,'136135','1','Chamber No. 126, New lawyer\'s Building, Punjab and Haryana High Court, Chandigarh','',6,128,'160001','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0039','OMAXE GREENS','OMAXE LTD.','info@omaxe.com',0,0,'M/s. Omaxe Ltd., Corporate Office :7, Local Shopping Centre, Kalkaji, New Delhi','',10,429,'110019','1','M/s. Omaxe Ltd., Corpor