an&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-language:EN-ZW\">Till the time development is done, developer may\r\nkindly be directed to pay interest @18% or as prescribed under RERA on all the expenses incurred in this\r\nregard i.e. on Rs. 22.60 Lakhs (details as above ) from the date of purchase of\r\nthe said plot i.e. 31.12.2013 as an opportunity cost of all options lost during\r\nthe period of 5 years.&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'malkit.singh@nabard.org','2018-12-06 16:36:49.000','malkit.singh@nabard.org','2018-12-06 16:36:49.000'),(482,1168,'1168',1233,'d2a1f0ed-7a16-44e8-9590-5e568e27fcb7','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-06 20:07:53.000','Malkit Singh','malkit.singh@nabard.org',6239648955,1722972303,0,'Flat no. B 303 ','NABARD Vihar',28,507,'160062','1','Flat no. B 303 ','NABARD Vihar',28,507,'160062','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0227','Sunny Enclave - Chando Gobindgarg','J S Bajwa','bajwadeveloperltd@gmail.com',9814014381,1605035000,'Bajwa Developers Ltd., Sunny Business Centre','5th Floor, New Sunny Enclave, Kharar, Mohali',28,507,'140301','1','Bajwa Developers Ltd., Sunny Business Centre','5th Floor, New Sunny Enclave, Kharar, Mohali',28,507,'140301','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span lang=\"EN-ZW\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Georgia&quot;,serif\">I ,\r\nMalkit Singh alongwith my wife Mrs . Namarta Singh had purchased a 200 sq&nbsp; yards plot number 2225 in Sector 123 Jandpur\r\n, Kharar , Distt. Mohali on 31.12.2013. <o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span lang=\"EN-ZW\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Georgia&quot;,serif\">At the\r\ntime of purchase in addition to consideration of Rs. 17.00 Lakh given for purchase,\r\nRs. 1.70 Lakh was incurred as registry charges &amp; Rs. 10000 as transfer charges,\r\nI was also made to pay Rs. 3.80 Lakhs as External Development Charges (EDC)\r\nwith a commitment to develop the roads &amp; provide other basic amenities within a year with further grace period of three months from the date of sale deed. But respondent failed to deliver possession of the plot and also develop the project with promised facilities and amenities.&nbsp; The respondent has not demarcated the plot and only certificate of possession was incorporated in the sale deed. No development work has been&nbsp; done at the spot and its also not possible to identify the said plot at the site.<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span lang=\"EN-ZW\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Georgia&quot;,serif\">Sir , a\r\nperiod of nearly 5 years have since lapsed , the said plot till date doesn’t\r\nhave access to pucca road in absence of which we are neither able to construct\r\nhouse for self-living. We\r\nhave been visiting the developer from time to time but no attention has been\r\npaid in this regard.&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><span lang=\"EN-ZW\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Georgia&quot;,serif;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-language:EN-ZW\">The developer may kindly be directed to provide all amenities &amp; facilities as promised and get the plot demarcated at the spot to be identifiable and to develop\r\nthe road immediately to enable us to construct the house.\r\nDelayed development has deprived us to construct our house. Our valuable hard earned is blocked and we are suffering losses as construction cost is increasing day by day. Apart from it, our plans to shift to the residential unit have been shattered. We are entitled to get interest as prescribed under RERA for the delayed period as no facility or amenities as promised have been provided at spot by the respondent.<o:p></o:p></span></p>',2260000.00,2260000.00,'2014-12-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><span lang=\"EN-ZW\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Georgia&quot;,serif;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-language:EN-ZW\">Till the time development is done, developer may\r\nkindly be directed to pay interest @18% or as prescribed under RERA on all the expenses incurred in this\r\nregard i.e. on Rs. 22.60 Lakhs (details as above ) from the date of purchase of\r\nthe said plot i.e. 31.12.2013 as an opportunity cost of all options lost during\r\nthe period of 5 years.&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p>','1','','2013-12-31 00:00:00','2013-12-31 00:00:00','Plot no not allotted','','',2,0,0,0,'malkit.singh@nabard.org','2018-12-06 16:38:41.000','malkit.singh@nabard.org','2018-12-06 16:38:41.000'),(483,1169,'1169',1148,'d6b33f13-0c3f-4ab1-b43d-e6d1dcd0a882','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-06 22:33:51.000','DEEPAK GARG','cadeepakgarg@gmail.com',9855519149,1724641410,0,'HOUSE NO 3003','TRIBUNE SOCIETY SECTOR 50 D',6,128,'160047','1','HOUSE NO 3003','TRIBUNE SOCIETY SECTOR 50 D',6,128,'160047','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0086','ATS INFRABUILD PRIVATE LIMITED','ATS INFRABUILD PRIVATE LIMITED','EMAIL@ATSGREENS.COM',0,0,'SITE OFFICE ATS INFRABUILD PRIVATE LIMITED, SECTOR 121','NEAR VERKA MILK PLANT, MOHALI',28,507,'160055','1','SITE OFFICE ATS INFRABUILD PRIVATE LIMITED, SECTOR 121','NEAR VERKA MILK PLANT, MOHALI',28,507,'160055','1','<p>Booking: </p><p>On 9th April, 2017, We ( Deepak Garg &amp; Shilpa Gupta) had booked a residential flat (3+1 BHK, Type B, Flat No 7032, Floor 3rd, Tower 7th) by giving an advance of Rs. 5,00,000/- (receipt no. CSAMR/03150 dt. 13th April, 2017) FOR Rs. 98,78,000/- </p><p>Execution of Agreement:</p><p>the 30 (Thirty) page apartment buyer agreement was duly executed on dated 11th May, 2017, wherein</p><p>date of Completion of Construction was described as December 2017 with a grace period of 3 Months.</p><p>(Refer para 6.2 on page 12 of said agreement). </p><p>Payments made till date: </p><p>Total amount till date was paid against Basic Cost is Rs. 85,71,866/- along with service tax of Rs. 385734/- Possession not handed over. Even after passing of Eleven (11) Months from the date of completion mentioned in agreement the completion of property is still under construction and possession letter is not offered. </p><p>GROUND OF CLAIMS: </p><p>1. Even after passing of Eleven (11) Months from the date as mentioned in agreement to sell, the promoters are failed to handover the possession. </p><p>2. We had paid Rs. 8571866 (against Unit Price) + 385734( against service tax) till date yet no possession. </p><p>3. We had taken a housing loan of Rs. 7528040/-and we are paying monthly instalment of Rs. 65000/- </p><p>4. We are still living in rental accommodation and paying an amount of Rs. 24200/-per month as rent. </p><p>5. We are facing great mental agony along with financial loss due to failure of promoters</p>','<p>COMPENSATION/ RELIEF SOUGHTS </p><p>1. LUMPSUM INTEREST U/S 18(1) FROM JANUARY 2018 TILL DECISION OF CASE: </p><p>Interest U/s 18(1) of THE REAL ESTATE (REGULATION AND DEVELOPMENT) ACT, 2016 on amount paid of Rs. 85,71,866/- at the rate specified in Clause 16 &amp; 17 of THE REAL ESTATE (REGULATION AND DEVELOPMENT) RULES. Also in reference to settled law by Hon’ble Real Estate Regularity Authority, Punjab in case of Nikhil Kawatra and Ranjani G Vs. Mr. Kulwant Singh M.D. M/s Janta Land Promoters Private Limited. </p><p>2. MONTHLY INTEREST U/S 18(1) FROM THE DATE OF DECISION OF CASE TILL POSSESSION OF FLAT </p><p>Interest U/s 18(1) of THE REAL ESTATE (REGULATION AND DEVELOPMENT) ACT, 2016 on amount paid of Rs. 85,71,866/- at the rate specified in Clause 16 &amp; 17 of THE REAL ESTATE (REGULATION AND DEVELOPMENT) RULES. also in reference to settled law by Hon’ble Real Estate Regularity Authority, Punjab in case of Nikhil Kawatra and Ranjani G Vs. Mr. Kulwant Singh M.D. M/s Janta Land Promoters Private Limited.</p><p>3. ANY OTHER RELIEF AS FEEL THINKS FIT BY HON’BLE AUTHORITY</p>',9878000.00,8571866.00,'2017-12-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>As Hon\'ble Authority Thinks Fit.</p>','1','','2017-05-11 00:00:00','2017-05-11 00:00:00','FLAT NO 7032, 3RD FLOOR, 7TH TOWER, ATS CASA ESPANA, SECTOR 121\r\nNEAR VERKA MILK PLANT, MOHALI','','',1,1,0,0,'deepsgargi','2018-12-06 22:14:25.000','deepsgargi','2018-12-06 22:14:25.000'),(484,1139,'1139',1211,'962b01f9-ce50-4ce8-b650-bb1037f1b9e3','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-07 10:43:27.000','Sanjay Dhiman','vermauvraj@gmail.com',9569656520,0,416668848153,'Flat No .115, Ground Floor, Noor Homes','Kharar Landranroad, Sector 115, Mohali',28,507,'160055','1','Flat No .115, Ground Floor, Noor Homes','Kharar Landranroad, Sector 115, Mohali',28,507,'160055','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0219','M/S. GGP BUILDTECH PRIVATE LIMITED','Mr. Ajay Gupta','ajayguptaggp@gmail.com',9815990640,0,'402, Shivalik City, Sector 127','Kharar , SAS Nagar',28,507,'160055','1','402, Shivalik City, Sector 127','Kharar , SAS Nagar',28,507,'160055','1','<p lang=\"en-US\" class=\"western\" align=\"JUSTIFY\" style=\"margin-left: 0.12in; margin-right: 0.12in; line-height: 103%\">&nbsp;That the project named Noor Homes is currently being\r\npromoted/developed by GGP Buildtech Pvt Limited. </p><p lang=\"en-US\" class=\"western\" align=\"JUSTIFY\" style=\"margin-left: 0.12in; margin-right: 0.12in; line-height: 103%\">The Promoters of M/s\r\nGGP BUILDTECH PVT LTD started their business initially with a\r\nPartnership firm M/s Singla Builders &amp; Promoters in which Sh.\r\nAjay Gupta and Sh. Amandeep Singla were partners. </p><p lang=\"en-US\" class=\"western\" align=\"JUSTIFY\" style=\"margin-left: 0.12in; margin-right: 0.12in; line-height: 103%\">That the Project\r\nNamed Noor Homes is launched by GGP Buildtech Pvt Limited in February\r\n2014. That the Builder (GGP Buildtech Pvt Limited) had come up with\r\nadvertisement/public offer to sell 1, 2, 3 BHK Apartments &amp; 3 BHK\r\nVillas to be constructed at Sector 115, Village Sante Majra, Tehsil\r\nKharar, District Mohali with a construction target to be completed in\r\n2017. </p><p lang=\"en-US\" class=\"western\" align=\"JUSTIFY\" style=\"margin-left: 0.12in; margin-right: 0.12in; line-height: 103%\">That the Complainants (society members) start booking flats\r\nfrom Builder from 2014. </p><p lang=\"en-US\" class=\"western\" align=\"JUSTIFY\" style=\"margin-left: 0.12in; margin-right: 0.12in; line-height: 103%\">That to some Complainants the flats were\r\nforcefully handed over by builder in incomplete stage. </p><p lang=\"en-US\" class=\"western\" align=\"JUSTIFY\" style=\"margin-left: 0.12in; margin-right: 0.12in; line-height: 103%\">That some\r\nComplainants were forced to pay 100% payment to Builder for\r\nincomplete flats by threatening them from goons hired by builders.</p><p lang=\"en-US\" class=\"western\" align=\"JUSTIFY\" style=\"margin-left: 0.12in; margin-right: 0.12in; line-height: 103%\">\r\nThat Some Complainants were forced to execute sale deed for less\r\nprice paying money in cash or for shell companies (Daya Infra) and\r\nthus frauding with GST and service tax.</p><p lang=\"en-US\" class=\"western\" align=\"JUSTIFY\" style=\"margin-left: 0.12in; margin-right: 0.12in; line-height: 103%\">That These flats are\r\nincomplete to such extent that there is no permanent water\r\nconnection,internal roads, electricity, sewerage connections,\r\nSewerage treatment plant, staircase, streetlights, fire protection\r\nsystem etc.</p><p lang=\"en-US\" class=\"western\" align=\"JUSTIFY\" style=\"margin-left: 0.12in; margin-right: 0.12in; line-height: 103%\">That these flats are handed over without obtaining\r\noccupancy certificate from MC kharar</p><p lang=\"en-US\" class=\"western\" align=\"JUSTIFY\" style=\"margin-left: 0.12in; margin-right: 0.12in; line-height: 103%\">That Builder was approached time\r\nto time and several MOM’s were signed but till date.That MOM is\r\nattached, where in Builder has initially agreed to\r\ncomplete the project by 31-March 2016.That vide MOM dated\r\n30-April-2017 Builder agreed to complete the project by 31-Jan-2018.\r\n</p><p lang=\"en-US\" class=\"western\" align=\"JUSTIFY\" style=\"margin-left: 0.12in; margin-right: 0.12in; line-height: 103%\">That again MOM vide 18.09.2017 Builder agreed to complete project in\r\nnext 6 months i.e Mar-2018. </p><p lang=\"en-US\" class=\"western\" align=\"JUSTIFY\" style=\"margin-left: 0.12in; margin-right: 0.12in; line-height: 103%\">That status of project is non completed till date</p>','<p lang=\"en-US\" class=\"western\" align=\"JUSTIFY\" style=\"margin-left: 0.12in; margin-right: 0.13in; line-height: 103%\">Transfer of All Unsold Properties to Society (will be incorporated within 15 days of order by RERA)</p><p lang=\"en-US\" class=\"western\" align=\"JUSTIFY\" style=\"margin-left: 0.12in; margin-right: 0.13in; line-height: 103%\">Direct PSPCL for permanent electricity connections for the 65\r\nfamilies (Complainant).</p><p lang=\"en-US\" class=\"western\" align=\"JUSTIFY\" style=\"margin-left: 0.12in; margin-right: 0.13in; line-height: 103%\">Direct MC kharar for permanent water and\r\nsewerage connections to the society.</p><p lang=\"en-US\" class=\"western\" align=\"JUSTIFY\" style=\"margin-left: 0.12in; margin-right: 0.13in; line-height: 103%\">Direct Inquiry against\r\ninvolvement of Municipal Corporation with Builder in cheating the\r\nPublic by allowing sale deed to be executed without issuing occupancy\r\ncertificate.</p><p lang=\"en-US\" class=\"western\" align=\"JUSTIFY\" style=\"margin-left: 0.12in; margin-right: 0.13in; line-height: 103%\">Direct Inquiry against Builder regarding diversion of\r\nproject funds to other shell companies.</p><p lang=\"en-US\" class=\"western\" align=\"JUSTIFY\" style=\"margin-left: 0.12in; margin-right: 0.13in; line-height: 103%\">Action against Builder for non\r\ncompletion of Project.Direct Inquiry against Builder regarding theft\r\nof GST.</p><p lang=\"en-US\" class=\"western\" align=\"JUSTIFY\" style=\"margin-left: 0.12in; margin-right: 0.13in; line-height: 103%\">Pledge/Stay on selling if the Properties of Builder,\r\nPromoters, Directors with immediate effect to avoid misuse of\r\ndiverted funds.</p><p lang=\"en-US\" class=\"western\" align=\"JUSTIFY\" style=\"margin-left: 0.12in; margin-right: 0.13in; line-height: 103%\"><br></p><p lang=\"en-US\" class=\"western\" align=\"JUSTIFY\" style=\"margin-left: 0.12in; margin-right: 0.13in; line-height: 103%\">Pass any other order/orders which PBRERA may deem fit\r\nin the facts and circumstances of the case.</p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p><span style=\"text-align: justify;\">Instruct Builder to complete the project within 3 months.</span></p><p><span style=\"text-align: justify;\">Transfer of All Unsold Properties to Society (will be incorporated within 15 days of order by RERA)</span><br></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',1,1,0,0,'uvrajverma','2018-12-07 09:54:27.000','uvrajverma','2018-12-07 09:54:27.000'),(485,1167,'1167',1234,'d78857a3-82bc-4872-8c7b-248177bcab69','FormTypeM',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','RAM KUMAR CHAUHAN','rkchau78@gmail.com',8937802109,0,968815109374,'VPO-Khudda Kalan, Distt-Ambala, Haryana','',13,1,'133104','1','Chamber No. 126, New lawyer\'s Building, Punjab and Haryana High Court, Chandigarh','',6,128,'160001','TARUN SINGHAL','tarunsinghal.adv@gmail.com',9988595908,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0039','OMAXE GREENS','OMAXE LTD.','info@omaxe.com',1141896680,1141896653,'M/s. Omaxe Ltd., Corporate Office :7, Local Shopping Centre, Kalkaji, New Delhi','',10,429,'110019','1','M/s. Omaxe Ltd., Corporate Office :7, Local Shopping Centre, Kalkaji, New Delhi','',10,429,'110019','1','<p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; font-family: Roboto;\">1). ﻿</span><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">﻿</span><span style=\"font-size: 18px; font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif;\">That\r\nthe complainant is a law abiding citizen of india and is an Ex- service man\r\npresently working with Indian Bank at Sec 21 Panchkula Branch.</span><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;2) That the Complainant approached the\r\nrespondents on 30.08.2011 to book a flat (i.e. Flat No. 105/GT/06 Vide Client\r\nID OGD/629) in Newly introduced project of the Respondents Namely “OMAXE\r\nGREENS” Situated at Ambala-Chandigarh Road, Jhamari, Tehsil Dera Bassi, Distt.\r\nPatiala(Punjab)</span><span style=\"font-size: 18px; font-family: Roboto;\">﻿&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 18px; font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif;\">3).\r\nThat the Respondent allotted Unit No. 105, First Floor, Tower GT-6, Build Area\r\n1630 SQ. FT. and for that complainant paid Rs. 1.50 lacs for confirming the\r\nbooking on 30.08.2011&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">annexed\r\nas&nbsp;</span><b><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Annexure\r\nC-1</span></b><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;and afterwards gave two cheques of Rs.\r\n5,150</span><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">00/-</span><b></b><b><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;</span></b><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">copies annexed as&nbsp;</span><b><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Annexure C-2&nbsp;</span></b><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif; font-size: 18px;\">and </span><b style=\"font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif; font-size: 10.5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">C-3.</span>&nbsp;</b><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">4).\r\nThat these cheques were never issued by the respondent and after a dalay of\r\nmore than a year when complainant came to know about this, he reissued the\r\ncheques on their request and for that respondents penalize&nbsp;the complainant&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">with&nbsp; Rs. 1,33000 and they also delayed the\r\nComplainant’s allotment agreement Which was got executed on</span><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">05.03.2013\r\nannexed as&nbsp;</span><b><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Annexure C-4</span></b><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;with</span><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">a\r\ndelay of more than one year. but no possession was given after many requests&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">5).\r\nThat&nbsp; Respondents issued a letter stating offer of fit out possession on\r\n22.06.2017</span><span style=\"font-size: 16pt; font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">copy\r\nis</span></span><span style=\"font-size: 16pt; font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">annexed</span></span><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;</span><b><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Annexure C-5</span></b><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">.\r\nand it was assured by the respondent that after the whole payment the\r\npossession will be given to him. On believing this and after suffering a lot,\r\ncomplainant agreed to their terms and cleared all the dues (approx Rs. 32 lacs)\r\ndated 29.03.2018&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">copy is\r\nannexed as&nbsp;</span><b><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Annexure C-6.</span><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;</span></b><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">6).</span><span style=\"font-size: 18px; font-family: Roboto;\">&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">that after giving all the\r\npayment possession was still not given and then on 06.09.2018&nbsp;respondents\r\nasked the complainant to sign the&nbsp;settlement agreement and having no other\r\noption complainant&nbsp;signed it in hope of getting the possession but still\r\nno possession was given . Then the&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Complainant sent the legal notice </span><b><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Annexure C-7</span></b><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;to the respondents and\r\nthen the possession was given in the end of november</span><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">.</span></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-height:\r\n150%\"><span style=\"font-size:16.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">1).\r\nDirect the respondent to pay and Compensate for all the delay, inconvenience,\r\nharassment given to the complainant by the respondent and further the amount of\r\ninterest till the physical possession &nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">given\r\nby them from the date of booking of the flat at the tune of Rs. Ten Lacs. 2). Award cost of litigation of\r\nRs. 1 lac in favor of the complainant and against the respondent. 3). Pass such\r\nother and further order(s) as this Hon’ble authority may deem fit and proper in\r\nthe facts and circumstances of the present case.</span><o:p></o:p></span></p><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">\r\n\r\n</span><p class=\"MsoNormal\"