ab)</span><span style=\"font-size: 18px; font-family: Roboto;\">﻿&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 18px; font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif;\">3).\r\nThat the Respondent allotted Unit No. 105, First Floor, Tower GT-6, Build Area\r\n1630 SQ. FT. and for that complainant paid Rs. 1.50 lacs for confirming the\r\nbooking on 30.08.2011&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">annexed\r\nas (</span><b><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Annexure\r\nC-1)</span></b><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;and afterwards gave two cheques of Rs.\r\n5,150</span><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">00/-</span><b></b><b><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;</span></b><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;(</span><b><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Annexure C-2&nbsp;</span></b><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif; font-size: 18px;\">and </span><b style=\"font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif; font-size: 10.5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">C-3).</span>&nbsp;</b><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">4).\r\nThat these cheques were never issued by the respondent and after a delay of\r\nmore than a year when complainant came to know about this, he reissued the\r\ncheques on their request and for that respondents penalize&nbsp;the complainant&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">with&nbsp; Rs. 1,33000 and they also delayed the\r\nComplainant’s allotment agreement Which was got executed on</span><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">05.03.2013 (</span><b><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Annexure C-4)</span></b><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;with</span><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">a\r\ndelay of more than one year. but no possession was given after many requests&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">5).\r\nThat&nbsp; Respondents issued a letter stating offer of fit out possession on\r\n22.06.2017<font face=\"Bookman Old Style, serif\">&nbsp;(</font></span><b><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Annexure C-5)</span></b><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">.\r\nand it was assured by the respondent that after the whole payment the\r\npossession will be given to him. On believing this and after suffering a lot,\r\ncomplainant agreed to their terms and cleared all the dues (approx Rs. 32 lacs)\r\ndated 29.03.2018</span><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;(</span><b><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Annexure C-6).</span><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;</span></b><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">6).</span><span style=\"font-size: 18px; font-family: Roboto;\">&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">that after giving all the\r\npayment possession was still not given and then on 06.09.2018&nbsp;respondents\r\nasked the complainant to sign the&nbsp;settlement agreement&nbsp;</span></span><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif; font-size: 18px; font-weight: 700;\">(</span><span style=\"font-size: 18px; font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif; font-weight: 700;\">C-8)</span><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif; font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;and having no other\r\noption complainant&nbsp;signed it, in hope of getting the possession but still\r\nno possession was given . Then the&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif; font-size: 18px;\">Complainant sent the legal notice (</span><b style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">Annexure C-9)</span></b><font face=\"Bookman Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;to the respondents and\r\nthen the possession was given in the end of November. But no interest has been paid till date.</span></font></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-height:\r\n150%\"><span style=\"font-size:16.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">1).\r\nDirect the respondent to pay and Compensate for all the delay, inconvenience,\r\nharassment given to the complainant by the respondent and further the amount of\r\ninterest till the physical possession &nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">given\r\nby them from the date of booking of the flat at the tune of Rs. Ten Lacs. 2). Award cost of litigation of\r\nRs. 1 lac in favor of the complainant and against the respondent. 3). Pass such\r\nother and further order(s) as this Hon’ble authority may deem fit and proper in\r\nthe facts and circumstances of the present case.</span><o:p></o:p></span></p><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">\r\n\r\n</span><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:12.0pt;text-align:justify;line-height:\r\n150%\"><span style=\"font-size: 18px; line-height: 150%; font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif;\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>',2927100.00,3197102.00,'2015-09-05 00:00:00.000','2018-11-23 00:00:00.000','<p>Not Applicable</p>','1','','2013-03-05 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Unit No. 105, First Floor, Tower GT-6, Build Area 1630 SQ. FT','','',1,1,0,0,'Trozan','2018-12-07 13:56:19.000','Trozan','2018-12-07 13:56:19.000'),(489,1144,'1144',1146,'7dfad30e-4afa-4859-8a26-94b85edcd0f5','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-07 15:42:32.000','Ashish Kumar Jain','jarnailthakur@yahoo.com',9815695783,0,495798240541,'c/o Sandeep Jain, 5368-C, Nicholson Road, Punjabi Mohalla, Ambala Cantt.','Ambala',13,1,'133001','1','c/o Sandeep Jain, 5368-C, Nicholson Road, Punjabi Mohalla, Ambala Cantt.','Ambala',13,1,'133001','J S Thakur','jarnailthakur@yahoo.com',9815695783,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PM0010','Fashion Technology Park\r\n(formerly registered as Jade Business Park)','Chandigarh Overseas Pvt. Ltd.','sanjaychugh.biz@gmail.com',9876499777,0,'SCO 196-197, Top Floor, Sector 34-A, Chandigarh','Chandigarh',6,128,'160022','1','SCO 196-197, Top Floor, Sector 34-A, Chandigarh','Chandigarh',6,128,'160022','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:115%\">The respondents came up with a\r\nproject in sector 90, Mohali, named as Fashion Technology Park in the year\r\n2006. The complainant booked 4 units of 100/125 sq. ft. each. On 02.09.2006and\r\npaid Rs. 5 lac out of the total amount payable Rs. 20 lac @ Rs. 5 lac per unit.\r\nTotal payment made by the complainant is Rs.19 lac. Construction was to\r\ncommence in 2<sup>nd</sup> week of sep 2006. He was allotted 4 units of 100 sq.\r\nft. each in Design Studio no. 6 on 5<sup>th</sup> floor. The respondents\r\nassured of fixed returns as also of a buy back scheme @7.5 lac per unit. The\r\nconstruction was to be completed in 30 months from Sep 2006, but the same was\r\nnever done. Further the Respondents &nbsp;purported to enter into a Developer Buyer\r\nagreement and one Lease agreement, obtained the complainant’s signatures thereon,\r\nasked him to collect the said agreements duly signed and dated by the\r\nauthorised persons which was never done.&nbsp;\r\nThe Respondents sent a letter dated 22.06.2009 offering to buy back the\r\n4 units @7.5 lac per unit. The complainant accepted the offer and was acknowledged\r\nby the Respondents &nbsp;vide their letter\r\ndated 13.01.2010. The Respondents paid a sum of Rs. 7.5 lac for buy back of one\r\nunit, but the balance amount of Rs. 22.50 lac for remaining three units was\r\nnever paid. The complainant was also assured of compensation for delay@ Rs. 50\r\nper sq. ft per month as per clause 28 of Developer Buyer agreement. Accordingly\r\nthey paid a sum of Rs.48388/- vide cheque dated 31.03.2010 only once and\r\nnothing thereafter. The Respondents have made the complainant to run from\r\npillar to post and have caused him great harassment and mental torture.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><i><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n115%\">The complainant</span></i><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:115%\">\r\nprays for a direction to the Respondents:<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-justify:\r\ninter-ideograph;text-indent:-.25in\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n115%\">1. To pay the balance amount of Rs.22,50,000/- with interest @18% p.a.\r\nwith effect from 02.03.2010 till actual payment.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-justify:\r\ninter-ideograph;text-indent:-.25in\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n115%\">2. To pay for delay @Rs.50/- per square foot per month w.e.f. 02.03.2010 along\r\nwith interest @18% per annum till actual payment.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-justify:\r\ninter-ideograph;text-indent:-.25in\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n115%\">3.To pay a sum of Rs.10 lacs for the mental torture, agony and harassment\r\nto the complainant and for making him run from pillar to post to avail his\r\nrights.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-justify:\r\ninter-ideograph;text-indent:-.25in\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n115%\">4. To pay litigation costs to the tune of Rs.1,10,000/- which he has so\r\nfar incurred.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-justify:\r\ninter-ideograph;text-indent:-.25in\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n115%\">5.&nbsp; To not to alienate, cancel the\r\nallotment,&nbsp; sell, transfer, mortgage,\r\netc. the allotted units in Design Studio no. 6 in the Fashion Technology Park\r\nSector 90, Mohali.<o:p></o:p></span></p>',2000000.00,1900000.00,'2010-03-02 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><i><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n115%\">The complainant</span></i><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:115%\">\r\nprays for a direction to the Respondents:<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-justify:\r\ninter-ideograph;text-indent:-.25in\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n115%\">1. To pay the balance amount of Rs.22,50,000/- with interest @18% p.a.\r\nwith effect from 02.03.2010 till actual payment.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-justify:\r\ninter-ideograph;text-indent:-.25in\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n115%\">2. To pay for delay @Rs.50/- per square foot per month w.e.f. 02.03.2010 along\r\nwith interest @18% per annum till actual payment.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-justify:\r\ninter-ideograph;text-indent:-.25in\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n115%\">3.To pay a sum of Rs.10 lacs for the mental torture, agony and harassment\r\nto the complainant and for making him run from pillar to post to avail his\r\nrights.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-justify:\r\ninter-ideograph;text-indent:-.25in\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n115%\">4. To pay litigation costs to the tune of Rs.1,10,000/- which he has so\r\nfar incurred.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-justify:\r\ninter-ideograph;text-indent:-.25in\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n115%\">5.&nbsp; To not to alienate, cancel the\r\nallotment,&nbsp; sell, transfer, mortgage,\r\netc. the allotted units in Design Studio no. 6 in the Fashion Technology Park\r\nSector 90, Mohali.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','1','','2006-08-12 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Design Studio No.6 \r\nFour units of 100 sq ft each','','',2,0,0,0,'jarnailthakur','2018-12-07 15:42:05.000','jarnailthakur','2018-12-07 15:42:05.000'),(490,1170,'1170',1249,'633d568c-6bc4-4a67-ac48-2650be8f8a83','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Meenu Minocha','kangan_1993@yahoo.in',9810617548,0,0,'E-3, Lajpat Nagar-III','2nd Floor, Delhi-24',10,557,'110024','1','E-3, Lajpat Nagar-III','2nd Floor, Delhi-24',10,557,'110024','Baani Chhibber','baanichbr@gmail.com',9876658773,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PM0010','Industrial Knowledge (Fashion Technology) Park, Sector 90, SAS Nagar, Mohali, Punjab','M/s Chandigarh Overseas Pvt. Ltd.','chdoverseas@rediffmail.com',0,0,'SCO 249','Sector 44-C',6,128,'160047','0','SCO 196-197, Top Floor','Sector 34-A',6,128,'160032','1','<p><br></p><p>The complainant had entered into two developer buyer agreements with the Respondent, dated 24.12.2007 for the purchase of super area measuring 125 square feet each in the design studio bearing No. 11, Floor No. 6, Block A-1 in the Industrial Knowledge (Fashion Technology) Park, Sector 90, SAS Nagar, Mohali.&nbsp;</p><p>The complainant has made a total payment of Rs. 9,50,000 till date for both the units. The Complainant was promised the delivery of possession within the period of 30 months from the date of start of construction. However, the possession of the said super area has not been delivered to the complainant so far. The construction of the project was grossly delayed and by the promised date i.e by the end of 2009 &amp; till now the construction of the said project is incomplete.&nbsp;</p><p>That under the developer buyer agreement, the complainant was entitled to receive Rs. 50 per square feet per month as delay charges if the possession was not delivered at the agreed time. The said delay charges were paid from 26.03.2010 till 02.01.2012 only amounting to Rs. 2,92,742 and thereafter no delay charges have been paid to the complainant.&nbsp;</p><p>The detailed facts of the case are enumerated in the hard copy of the complaint.</p>','<p>The complainant prays for the following reliefs:</p><p>(i) an order/direction to the respondent to deliver the possession of the units as per the Developer Buyer Agreement, along with interest @10.15 % p.a. i,e prevailing applicable State Bank of India Highest Marginal Cost of Lending Rate plus two percent from the date of payments till the date of possession of the units &amp; accept the balance payment.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>(ii) Levy a penalty of 5% of the estimated cost of the real estate project for breach of its obligation to deliver possession on time under the Act.</p><p>(iii) Pass an order/direction to the respondent to pay an amount of Rs.12,500/- (Rupees Ten Lakh Fifty Thousand only) p.m for both the units as delay charges from the period starting from 01.02.2012 till actual realization to the complainant, along with the interest @ 10.15% p.a i,e prevailing applicable State Bank of India Highest Marginal Cost of Lending Rate plus two percent.&nbsp;</p><p>(iv) If the Respondent is not able to give the possession of the units as per the agreement then in the alternative, direction to the Respondent to return the amounts paid with interest from the date of payment till the actual realization as per the RERA Rule 15 with the prevailing applicable State Bank of India Highest Marginal Cost of Lending Rate plus two percent i.e. 10.15%</p><p>(v) Pass any other order/direction in favour of the complainant &amp; against the respondent as deem fit by the authority.</p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Pending final decision on the complaint the complainant seeks issue of direction to the Respondent not to sell/transfer/allot the units to any third person.</p><div><br></div>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'BaaniChhibber','2018-12-07 17:24:59.000','BaaniChhibber','2018-12-07 17:24:59.000'),(491,1170,'1170',1249,'633d568c-6bc4-4a67-ac48-2650be8f8a83','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-11 11:34:36.000','Meenu Minocha','kangan_1993@yahoo.in',9810617548,0,0,'E-3, Lajpat Nagar-III','2nd Floor, Delhi-24',10,557,'110024','1','E-3, Lajpat Nagar-III','2nd Floor, Delhi-24',10,557,'110024','Baani Chhibber','baanichbr@gmail.com',9876658773,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PM0010','Industrial Knowledge (Fashion Technology) Park, Sector 90, SAS Nagar, Mohali, Punjab','M/s Chandigarh Overseas Pvt. Ltd.','chdoverseas@rediffmail.com',0,0,'SCO 249','Sector 44-C',6,128,'160047','0','SCO 196-197, Top Floor','Sector 34-A',6,128,'160032','1','<p><br></p><p>The complainant had entered into two developer buyer agreements with the Respondent, dated 24.12.2007 for the purchase of super area measuring 125 square feet each in the design studio bearing No. 11, Floor No. 6, Block A-1 in the Industrial Knowledge (Fashion Technology) Park, Sector 90, SAS Nagar, Mohali.&nbsp;</p><p>The complainant has made a total payment of Rs. 9,50,000 till date for both the units. The Complainant was promised the delivery of possession within the period of 30 months from the date of start of construction. However, the possession of the said super area has not been delivered to the complainant so far. The construction of the project was grossly delayed and by the promised date i.e by the end of 2009 &amp; till now the construction of the said project is incomplete.&nbsp;</p><p>That under the developer buyer agreement, the complainant was entitled to receive Rs. 50 per square feet per month as delay charges if the possession was not delivered at the agreed time. The said delay charges were paid from 26.03.2010 till 02.01.2012 only amounting to Rs. 2,92,742 and thereafter no delay charges have been paid to the complainant.&nbsp;</p><p>The detailed facts of the case are enumerated in the hard copy of the complaint.</p>','<p>The complainant prays for the following reliefs:</p><p>(i) an order/direction to the respondent to deliver the possession of the units as per the Developer Buyer Agreement, along with interest @10.15 % p.a. i,e prevailing applicable State Bank of India Highest Marginal Cost of Lending Rate plus two percent from the date of payments till the date of possession of the units &amp; accept the balance payment.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>(ii) Levy a penalty of 5% of the estimated cost of the real estate project for breach of its obligation to deliver possession on time under the Act.</p><p>(iii) Pass an order/direction to the respondent to pay an amount of Rs.12,500/- (Rupees Ten Lakh Fifty Thousand only) p.m for both the units as delay charges from the period starting from 01.02.2012 till actual realization to the complainant, along with the interest @ 10.15% p.a i,e prevailing applicable State Bank of India Highest Marginal Cost of Lending Rate plus two percent.&nbsp;</p><p>(iv) If the Respondent is not able to give the possession of the units as per the agreement then in the alternative, direction to the Respondent to return the amounts paid with interest from the date of payment till the actual realization as per the RERA Rule 15 with the prevailing applicable State Bank of India Highest Marginal Cost of Lending Rate plus two percent i.e. 10.15%</p><p>(v) Pass any other order/direction in favour of the complainant &amp; against the respondent as deem fit by the authority.</p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Pending final decision on the complaint the complainant seeks issue of direction to the Respondent not to sell/transfer/allot the units to any third person.</p><div><br></div>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'BaaniChhibber','2018-12-07 17:25:28.000','BaaniChhibber','2018-12-07 17:25:28.000'),(492,1171,'1171',1112,'29af80b1-85ed-4b88-8344-b429d2f24eca','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-08 11:45:59.000','Amarjit Kaur','savindersinghgill@gmail.com',9988861126,0,0,'House No. 2853','Old Sunny Enclave, Kharar',28,507,'140301','1','House No. 2853','Old Sunny Enclave, Kharar',28,507,'140301','Savinder Singh Gill ','savindersinghgill@gmail.com',9988861126,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0093','The Palm','Manohar Infrastructure and Constructions Private Limited','nbs@manoharrealty.com',0,0,'SCO 139-141','Sector-17 C',6,128,'160017','1','SCO 139-141','Sector-17 C',6,128,'160017','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 115%; font-family: &quot;Century Gothic&quot;, sans-serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">That the husband of the\r\napplicant initially booked four plots with the respondent having different\r\nsizes, two of them measuring 500 Square yards each @ Rs. 18,500/- in the\r\nproject “Palm Garden” and two of them measuring 250 Square Yards each @ Rs.\r\n18,000 per Sq. yard in the project “Palm Spring”, Mullanpur (New Chandigarh),\r\nnear Chandigarh being developed by the respondent.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">The booking amount against the\r\nplots was directly paid to the company by the applicant. Before purchasing\r\nthese plots, the applicant contacted the respondent who assured them that it\r\nwas having all the approvals and sanctions for the said project and possession\r\nof the plot will be delivered within 2 years.&nbsp; It was assured to the\r\napplicant that the possession of the plots will be delivered within 2 years and\r\nthe buyer’s agreement will be executed within 3-4 months.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">That thereafter the husband of\r\nthe applicant visited the project site in the month of June, 2013 and was\r\nshocked to see that only open fields were there and the respondent had not\r\nstarted any development. On the same day the applicant visited the office of\r\nrespondent who assured the applicant that development will be started soon and\r\nthe further payment would be demanded when the development work would be\r\nstarted.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: &quot;Century Gothic&quot;, sans-serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><span style=\"text-align: start; font-size: 14px;\">That thereafter the husband of the applicant died in September, 2016 and\r\nthe Plots were transferred in the name of applicant.&nbsp;</span></span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 7pt; line-height: 115%; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 14px;\">&nbsp;</span></span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 115%; font-family: &quot;Century Gothic&quot;, sans-serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">That the applicant after the death of her husband, visited\r\nthe site of the project and saw no development at the site and asked the\r\nrespondent to refund the amount but respondents showed their inability to\r\nrefund the amount and persuaded the applicant that she should get the deposited\r\namount adjusted into a single plot.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: &quot;Century Gothic&quot;, sans-serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><span style=\"text-align: start; font-size: 14px;\">That thereafter, the amount of the applicant was adjusted against the one\r\nplot and Plot no. 418 measuring 402.32 Sq. yds. (Approx.) was allotted to the\r\napplicant on 24.05.2018. That the respondent thereafter in June, 2018 offered\r\nPlot Buyer’s Agreement for execution after delay of 6 yrs</span></span><o:p></o:p></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: roboto, serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">(i) Directing the respondent to\r\nrefund the principal amount i.e. Rs. 9562500/- as per Section 18 of RERA along\r\nwith interest to be calculated at the rate as contemplated under rule 16 of The\r\nPunjab State Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Rules, 2017, as the\r\napplicants have lost faith in the respondent due to misrepresentation by it\r\nabout the approvals and stages of development during all these years and thus\r\nthe applicants wish to withdraw from the project. Also the respondent has\r\ncommitted violation of various provisions of PAPRA and conditions of various\r\napprovals granted to it, as it could not collect any amount till the exemption\r\nis received under Section 44 of PAPRA which was received on 25.01.2017. The\r\nrespondent collected the money from the applicants in 2012. The approvals were\r\ngranted to the respondent on the ground that it will not sell any\r\nland/plot/space and collect money from the general public till exemption under\r\nSection 44 of PAPRA is received. Also, inspite of receiving more than 100% of sale consideration\r\nthe respondent did not execute any sale agreement&nbsp; and the same was offered for execution after a delay of more than 6 years and after having received more\r\nthan 100% of the sale consideration. (ii) Directing the respondent to pay litigation\r\nexpenses to the tune of Rs. 50000/-. (iv) To take action against respondent\r\nunder Section 61 of RERA for constant violation of provision of Section 13 of\r\nRERA as the respondent failed to issue any allotment letter &amp; execute the\r\nbuyer’s agreement on time. For cancelling the extension granted to the respondent\r\nfor constantly violating various provisions of RERA and for indulging into\r\nunfair trade practices and further cancelling the main registration of the\r\nrespondent under RERA.</span><o:p></o:p></p>',8472457.00,9562500.00,'2014-02-05 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: roboto, serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">The\r\nrespondent be directed to provide the list of allottees to whom it has\r\nallotted/sold the 862 residential plots as per the layout plan approved by\r\nGMADA on 6.10.2015. The respondent has been duly registered under RERA for the\r\nsaid approved layout plan. As per the said approved layout plan, the respondent\r\ncan sell 862 residential plots and 73 commercial plots/spaces. The respondent\r\nbe directed to provide the list of hypothecated plots, which are hypothecated\r\nto GMADA, out of the said approved 862 residential and 73 commercial plots. The\r\nrespondent be directed to provide the list of hypothecated plots already\r\nallotted/sold to general public. The respondent be directed to provide the\r\ndetails of funds collected from the general public since 2010 in lieu of the\r\nsaid approved 862 residential plots which are part of approved layout plan and\r\nfor which the respondent is duly registered under Section 3 of RERA and also,\r\nthe detail where such amount has been utilized by the respondent. The\r\nrespondent be directed to provide all the bank details where such amount has\r\nbeen deposited along with the statement of accounts since the year 2010. The\r\nrespondent be directed to provide the details in respect of number of bookings\r\nmade by the respondent since the year 2010 for the said 862 residential plots.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 115%; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>','1','','2018-05-24 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','418','','',1,1,0,0,'BeeG','2018-12-07 18:54:19.000','BeeG','2018-12-07 18:54:19.000'),(493,1172,'1172',1078,'d8d4f172-3c37-4e70-b72a-876b113f98f3','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-12 15:08:31.000','Avneet Kaur','vikramsinghchahal@gmail.com',9781750447,0,0,'H.No.28-B, Model Town Phagwara','Punjab',28,300,'144401','1','H.No.28-B, Model Town Phagwara','Punjab',28,300,'144401','Vikram Singh Chahal','vikramsinghchahal@gmail.com',9781750447,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0231','Mohali Hills, M/s EMAAR MGF Land  Pvt. Ltd','EMAAR MGF LAND PVT LTD','feedback@emaar-india.com',0,0,'ECE House, Level-1, 28 Kasturba  Ghandhi Marg','New Delhi  ',10,429,'110001','0','28 KASTURBA GANDHI MARG','',10,429,'110001','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:36.0pt;text-align:justify;line-height:\r\n150%\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:11.0pt;line-height:150%\">Complainant\r\nopted for the purchase of independent plot developed by the respondents and\r\nentered into an agreement dated 04.07.2007 wherein the said plot No 104 measuring\r\n400sq yards in Augusta Green in Sector 109, for the total sale price of Rs.54,00,472/-\r\nand the possession of the said plot as the agreement was to be handed over to\r\nthe complainant on or before 03.07.2010. &nbsp;The complainant made the payment of Rs.53,01,648/-\r\nas per the demand raised by the respondent. The respondent had assured as per\r\nthe agreement that the possession shall be offered on or before July 2010 but\r\nafter the elapse of approximately eight years from the said cutoff date still\r\nthere are no signs of the possession being offered. The complainant has been\r\ncheated by the respondents by not delivering the possession as per the\r\nagreement and further cancelling the allotment of the said plot without\r\ninforming the complainant without any reason. The complainant is concerned\r\nabout the fate of his investment, as such the present complainant seeking the\r\nrefund of the amount deposited by the complainant along with interest and\r\ncompensation.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p><i><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:Calibri;mso-fareast-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-bidi-theme-font:\r\nminor-bidi;mso-ansi-language:EN-US;mso-fareast-language:EN-US;mso-bidi-language:\r\nAR-SA\">Refund of the total amount after deducting Rs.37,55,255/- (the amount\r\ndirectly refunded to the respondent Bank by the respondent no 1 to 3) &nbsp;from Rs 53,01,648 along with interest.&nbsp;</span></i><br></p>',5400472.00,5301648.00,'2010-07-03 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Any relief as it deems fit to the Honorable Authority in the present facts and circumstances of the case in the interest of justice and equity.&nbsp;</p>','1','','2007-07-04 00:00:00','2007-07-04 00:00:00','Plot No 104 measuring 400sq yards in Augusta Green in Sector 109, Mohali','','',2,0,0,0,'P43982017','2018-12-09 11:45:30.000','P43982017','2018-12-09 11:45:30.000'),(494,1173,'1173',1099,'457255aa-fa7f-413a-97b0-0c60c887671e','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-10 08:40:03.000','MANOJ SHARMA','sharma8686@gmail.com',9888860686,0,658383219967,'#215, First Floor, Noor Homes Society, Kharar Landran Road','Sector-115, Mohali-160055',28,507,'160055','1','#215, First Floor, Noor Homes Society, Kharar Landran Road','Sector-115, Mohali-160055',28,507,'160055','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0219','G.G.P. Buildtech Pvt. Ltd.','Ajay Gupta','ajayguptaggp@gmail.com',0,0,'Ajay Gupta S/o Late Sh. K. C. Gupta , Managing Director - G.G.P. Buildtech Pvt. Ltd., H. No. 402,','Shivalik Enclave, Sector-127 Greater Mohali, Distt. S.A.S. Nagar, Mohali, Punjab- 140301, India',28,507,'160055','1','Ajay Gupta S/o Late Sh. K. C. Gupta , Managing Director - G.G.P. Buildtech Pvt. Ltd., H. No. 402,','Shivalik Enclave, Sector-127 Greater Mohali, Distt. S.A.S. Nagar, Mohali, Punjab- 140301, India',28,507,'160055','1','<p style=\"margin-bottom: 0in\">Dear Sir/ Madam,</p><p style=\"margin-bottom: 0in\">I have purchased 2 BHK flat having Flat\r\nno. 215, First Floor in Noor Homes Society situated at Sector-115,\r\nKharar- Landran Road, Mohali -140307, Punjab through GGP Buildtech\r\nPvt. Ltd. I have bought this flat in Rs. 22 Lacs. <font size=\"4\"><u><b>Builder\r\nhas taken GST @12% i.e. an amount of Rs. 2.62 Lacs from me.</b></u></font><font size=\"4\">\r\n</font>Builder charged me maintenance charges of Rs. 15000/- from me\r\nin advance for one year. Registry of Flat done on 03-Jan-2018 and\r\nfull payment has been done to builder. As I had to shift to my flat\r\nat earliest possible, so after assurance from builder that pending\r\nworks (listed below) will be completed soon I shifted to my flat. But\r\ntill date works are still pending and builder is not replying\r\npositively. I am feeling very much harassed as I am staying in very\r\nbad conditions although I have made full payment. Kindly help me to\r\nget out of these worst conditions.</p><p style=\"margin-bottom: 0in\">Pending Works:-</p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><ol>\r\n	<li><p style=\"margin-bottom: 0in\">Plaster of outer walls. Water is\r\n	seeping inside in rains.</p>\r\n	</li><li><p style=\"margin-bottom: 0in\">Single coat of painting on walls\r\n	which has come out in most of walls. Although double coat of paint\r\n	was promised.</p>\r\n	</li><li><p style=\"margin-bottom: 0in\">Tiles are coming out and colour of\r\n	balcony tiles have faded.</p>\r\n	</li><li><p style=\"margin-bottom: 0in\">Walls have started cracking.</p>\r\n	</li><li><p style=\"margin-bottom: 0in\">The timber used for the window\r\n	architrave is of low quality. So Chokhat has come out.</p>\r\n	</li><li><p style=\"margin-bottom: 0in\">No wiring in balcony electrical\r\n	points.</p>\r\n	</li><li><p style=\"margin-bottom: 0in\">Water leakage in pipes fitted\r\n	inside walls of bathroom. So tiles were broken to rectify it.</p>\r\n	</li><li><p style=\"margin-bottom: 0in\">No permanent connection of\r\n	electrical power, power being supplied through temporary connection\r\n	that builder has taken for construction purpose.</p>\r\n	</li><li><p style=\"margin-bottom: 0in\">No Govt. water connection. Water\r\n	is supplied through bore well and the water supply is very poor.</p>\r\n	</li><li><p style=\"margin-bottom: 0in\">No Sewage Treatment Plant for\r\n	treating the sewage.</p>\r\n	</li><li><p style=\"margin-bottom: 0in\">No proper parking has been\r\n	provided.</p>\r\n	</li><li><p style=\"margin-bottom: 0in\">Lot of water accumulation outside\r\n	flat leading to mosquitoes.</p>\r\n</li></ol>','<p style=\"margin-bottom: 0in\">We want that either all of our pending\r\nworks should be completed or refund our all money. And we should be\r\nrefunded the extra amount of GST that builder has taken from us.</p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>We want that either all of our pending works should be completed or refund our all money. And we should be refunded the extra amount of GST that builder has taken from us.<br></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',1,1,0,0,'sharma8686','2018-12-09 14:55:36.000','sharma8686','2018-12-09 14:55:36.000'),(495,1174,'1174',1239,'d25b078a-2844-47e7-9d66-87c143312e53','FormTypeM',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','LEENA KUMARI','cmavishal85@gmail.com',8968318866,0,0,'Flat No .226, Ground Floor, Noor Homes','Kharar Landranroad, Sector 111, Mohali',28,507,'160055','1','Flat No .226, Ground Floor, Noor Homes','Kharar Landranroad, Sector 111, Mohali',28,507,'160055','','',0,0,'Allottee','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0219','GGP Buildtech Private Limited','M/S. GGP BUILDTECH PRIVATE LIMITED','ajayguptaggp@gmail.com',9815990640,0,'Mr. Ajay Gupta, # 402, Shivalik City, Sector 127','Kharar, SAS Nagar, Mohali',28,507,'160055','1','Mr. Ajay Gupta, # 402, Shivalik City, Sector 127','Kharar, SAS Nagar, Mohali',28,507,'160055','1','<p>That the project named Noor Homes is currently being promoted/developed by GGP Buildtech Pvt Limited. The Promoters of M/s GGP BUILDTECH PVT LTD started their business initially with a Partnership firm M/s Singla Builders &amp; Promoters in which Sh. Ajay Gupta and Sh. Amandeep Singla were partners. That the Project Named Noor Homes is launched by GGP Buildtech Pvt Limited in February 2014. That the Builder (GGP Buildtech Pvt Limited) had come up with advertisement/public offer to sell 1, 2, 3 BHK Apartments &amp; 3 BHK Villas to be constructed at Sector 115, Village Sante Majra, Tehsil Kharar, District Mohali with a construction target to be completed in 2017. That the Complainants (society members) start booking flats from Builder from 2014. That to some Complainants the flats were forcefully handed over by builder in incomplete stage. That some Complainants were forced to pay 100% payment to Builder for incomplete flats by threatening them from goons hired by builders. That Some Complainants were forced to execute sale deed for less price paying money in cash or for shell companies (Daya Infra) and thus frauding with GST and service tax.That These flats are incomplete to such extent that there is no permanent water connection,internal roads, electricity, sewerage connections, Sewerage treatment plant, staircase, streetlights, fire protection system etc.That these flats are handed over without obtaining occupancy certificate from MC khararThat Builder was approached time to time and several MOM’s were signed but till date.That MOM is attached as Annexure-1, where in Builder has initially agreed to complete the project by 31-March 2016.That vide MOM dated 30-April-2017 Builder agreed to complete the project by 31-Jan-2018. That again MOM vide 18.09.2017 Builder agreed to complete project in next 6 months i.e Mar-2018.&nbsp; That status of project is same&nbsp; as mentioned in point No.9</p><div><br></div>','<p>Direct PSPCL for permanent electricity connections for the 65 families (Complainant).Direct MC kharar for permanent water and sewerage connections to the society.Direct Inquiry against involvement of Municipal Corporation with Builder in cheating the Public by allowing sale deed to be executed without issuing occupancy certificate.Direct Inquiry against Builder regarding diversion of project funds to other shell companies.Action against Builder for non completion of Project.Direct Inquiry against Builder regarding theft of GST.Pledge/Stay on&nbsp; selling if the Properties of Builder, Promoters, Directors with immediate effect to avoid misuse of diverted funds.Pass any other order/orders which PBRERA may deem fit in the facts and circumstances of the case.</p><div><br></div>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Direct PSPCL for permanent electricity connections for the 65 families (Complainant).Direct MC kharar for permanent water and sewerage connections to the society.Direct Inquiry against involvement of Municipal Corporation with Builder in cheating the Public by allowing sale deed to be executed without issuing occupancy certificate.Direct Inquiry against Builder regarding diversion of project funds to other shell companies.Action against Builder for non completion of Project.Direct Inquiry against Builder regarding theft of GST.Pledge/Stay on&nbsp; selling if the Properties of Builder, Promoters, Directors with immediate effect to avoid misuse of diverted funds.Pass any other order/orders which PBRERA may deem fit in the facts and circumstances of the case.</p><div><br></div>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',1,0,0,0,'LeenaKumari','2018-12-10 10:14:04.000','LeenaKumari','2018-12-10 10:14:04.000'),(496,1175,'1175',1239,'d25b078a-2844-47e7-9d66-87c143312e53','FormTypeM',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','LEENA KUMARI','cmavishal85@gmail.com',8968318866,0,0,'Flat No .226, Ground Floor, Noor Homes','Kharar Landranroad, Sector 111, Mohali',28,507,'160055','1','Flat No .226, Ground Floor, Noor Homes','Kharar Landranroad, Sector 111, Mohali',28,507,'160055','','',0,0,'Allottee','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0219','M/S. GGP BUILDTECH PRIVATE LIMITED','M/S. GGP BUILDTECH PRIVATE LIMITED','ajayguptaggp@gmail.com',9815990640,0,'Mr. Ajay Gupta, # 402, Shivalik City, Sector 127','Kharar, SAS Nagar, Mohali',28,507,'160055','1','Mr. Ajay Gupta, # 402, Shivalik City, Sector 127','Kharar, SAS Nagar, Mohali',28,507,'160055','1','<p>That the project named Noor Homes is currently being promoted/developed by GGP Buildtech Pvt Limited. The Promoters of M/s GGP BUILDTECH PVT LTD started their business initially with a Partnership firm M/s Singla Builders &amp; Promoters in which Sh. Ajay Gupta and Sh. Amandeep Singla were partners. That the Project Named Noor Homes is launched by GGP Buildtech Pvt Limited in February 2014. That the Builder (GGP Buildtech Pvt Limited) had come up with advertisement/public offer to sell 1, 2, 3 BHK Apartments &amp; 3 BHK Villas to be constructed at Sector 115, Village Sante Majra, Tehsil Kharar, District Mohali with a construction target to be completed in 2017. That the Complainants (society members) start booking flats from Builder from 2014. That to some Complainants the flats were forcefully han