ithin 24 months along with an extended grace period of 6 months.<o:p></o:p></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">Accordingly, I arranged for accommodation on\r\nrent in Apr’2017 and have been paying both rent and EMIs as the subvention\r\nperiod had lapsed. Due to inordinate delay I lost faith in the project and requested\r\nthe developers through e-mails to refund my deposits. However there was no\r\nresponse from their end as they continued to defer possession and progress on\r\nsite was very slow. They agreed to settle only pre-EMI interest from Aug’17 (24+6\r\nmonths from date of agreement) onwards and offered to deliver possession in Mar’18.\r\nDeveloper even failed to meet that deadline and possession has not been offered\r\ntill date.</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\">Now when I informed the builder that I have filed complaint in RERA on 15.11.2018 they have sent possession letter on 29.11.2018 which is dated 08.10.2018 just to get away with the complaint as it is not possible that they can keep the letter with themselves for over 50 days.</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">After so much of agony, I do not want to remain\r\nassociated with the developer and request for return of all deposits (including\r\nEMIs) with interest.&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">In\r\nlight of the case facts brought out hereinabove, association with the project has not only been loss of time,\r\nmoney and effort but has caused a lot of mental harassment. It is therefore requested to refund entire\r\ndeposits including EMIs paid to bank with interest.&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p>',4000000.00,3000000.00,'2017-08-07 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','It is prayed to stop the EMIs till final decision as I am not able to pay both rent and EMI.&nbsp;','1','','2015-02-07 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','40, First Floor, Sector-99, Mohali','','',2,0,0,0,'mukesh013128','2018-12-10 16:31:54.000','mukesh013128','2018-12-10 16:31:54.000'),(501,1115,'1115',1214,'236d33c7-52c2-47c2-9d91-8289ee07ebac','FormTypeM',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Mukesh Gupta','mukeshgupta.31@gmail.com',9417217902,0,0,'B-3, 302, Nirmal Chayya Towers','VIP road, Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','1','B-3, 302, Nirmal Chayya Towers','VIP road, Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PC0019','M/s Country Colonisers Pvt. Ltd. ','M/s Country Colonisers Pvt. Ltd. ','rera@waveestate.in',0,0,' M/s Country Colonisers Pvt. Ltd. ','Sector-85, SAS Nagar (Mohali)',28,507,'140308','1',' M/s Country Colonisers Pvt. Ltd. ','Sector-85, SAS Nagar (Mohali)',28,507,'140308','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">I had booked independent first floor in Wave\r\nEstate, Sector-99 under subvention scheme by initial payment of Rs.\r\n3,00,000/- vide cheque no. 60113 dated 08.02.2013. Next payment was made vide\r\ncheque no. 60117 dated 19.04.2013 amounting Rs. 3,18,540/-. It was committed to\r\nmake delivery within 2 years.&nbsp;</span>However, M/s Country Colonisers Pvt.\r\nLtd. executed the agreement on 07.02.2015 as per which possession was to be\r\noffered within 24 months along with an extended grace period of 6 months.<o:p></o:p></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">Accordingly, I arranged for accommodation on\r\nrent in Apr’2017 and have been paying both rent and EMIs as the subvention\r\nperiod had lapsed. Due to inordinate delay I lost faith in the project and requested\r\nthe developers through e-mails to refund my deposits. However there was no\r\nresponse from their end as they continued to defer possession and progress on\r\nsite was very slow. They agreed to settle only pre-EMI interest from Aug’17 (24+6\r\nmonths from date of agreement) onwards and offered to deliver possession in Mar’18.\r\nDeveloper even failed to meet that deadline and possession has not been offered\r\ntill date.</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\">Now when I informed the builder that I have filed complaint in RERA on 15.11.2018 they have sent possession letter on 29.11.2018 which is dated 08.10.2018 just to get away with the complaint as it is not possible that they can keep the letter with themselves for over 50 days.</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">After so much of agony, I do not want to remain\r\nassociated with the developer and request for return of all deposits (including\r\nEMIs) with interest.&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">In\r\nlight of the case facts brought out hereinabove, association with the project has not only been loss of time,\r\nmoney and effort but has caused a lot of mental harassment. It is therefore requested to refund entire\r\ndeposits including EMIs paid to bank with interest.&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p>',4000000.00,3000000.00,'2017-08-07 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','It is prayed to stop the EMIs till final decision as I am not able to pay both rent and EMI.&nbsp;','1','','2015-02-07 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','40, First Floor, Sector-99, Mohali','','',2,0,0,0,'mukesh013128','2018-12-10 16:32:43.000','mukesh013128','2018-12-10 16:32:43.000'),(502,1176,'1176',1257,'c1104234-21e5-41f4-9b9d-64c03c6afb7d','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Harjot Kaur  Khera','jagdeepkhera@gmail.com',9417000453,0,0,'21 D (White Gate) ','Sarabha Nagar',28,366,'141001','1','21 D (White Gate) ','Sarabha Nagar',28,366,'141001','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0154','M/S Country Colonisers Pvt Ltd\r\nWave Estate, Sector 85 \r\nSAS Nagar, Mohali 140308','CEO','rera@waveestate.in',0,0,'Country Colonisers Pvt Ltd','Wave Estate, Sector 85',28,507,'140308','1','Country Colonisers Pvt Ltd','Wave Estate, Sector 85',28,507,'140308','1','<p>1. Initial application for allotment made on 16-10-2006 along with payment of Rs 396000</p><p>2. No work done on ground till 2014. Meanwhile changes of plans, change of project name, change of master plans done.&nbsp;</p><p>3. Fresh agreement done on 30-01-14 along with allotment of unit number K 401 in Kannedia Tower of group housing scheme.&nbsp;</p><p>4. Promoter has been unable to deliver the mentioned unit number K 401 till date, even after demanding and accepting payments on construction linked plan.&nbsp;</p><p>5. Promoter has arbitrarily and forcibly shifted allocation of unit from K tower to F tower on 28-07-17</p><p>6. Complainants have made application to builder for cancellation of allotment along with refund of payments made on 23-10-17 but no reply or refund received from builder.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p>','<p>Refund of payments done along with applicable interest&nbsp;</p><p>1. 396000 since 16-10-2006</p><p>2. 209685 since 14-03-2014</p><p>3. 411946 since 25-06-2014</p><p>4. 426321 since 28-03-2016</p><p><br></p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p><br></p>','0','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'jskhera','2018-12-10 21:48:22.000','jskhera','2018-12-10 21:48:22.000'),(503,1176,'1176',1257,'c1104234-21e5-41f4-9b9d-64c03c6afb7d','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-25 12:40:05.000','Harjot Kaur  Khera','jagdeepkhera@gmail.com',9417000453,0,0,'21 D (White Gate) ','Sarabha Nagar',28,366,'141001','1','21 D (White Gate) ','Sarabha Nagar',28,366,'141001','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0154','M/S Country Colonisers Pvt Ltd\r\nWave Estate, Sector 85 \r\nSAS Nagar, Mohali 140308','CEO','rera@waveestate.in',0,0,'Country Colonisers Pvt Ltd','Wave Estate, Sector 85',28,507,'140308','1','Country Colonisers Pvt Ltd','Wave Estate, Sector 85',28,507,'140308','1','<p>1. Initial application for allotment made on 16-10-2006 along with payment of Rs 396000</p><p>2. No work done on ground till 2014. Meanwhile changes of plans, change of project name, change of master plans done.&nbsp;</p><p>3. Fresh agreement done on 30-01-14 along with allotment of unit number K 401 in Kannedia Tower of group housing scheme.&nbsp;</p><p>4. Promoter has been unable to deliver the mentioned unit number K 401 till date, even after demanding and accepting payments on construction linked plan.&nbsp;</p><p>5. Promoter has arbitrarily and forcibly shifted allocation of unit from K tower to F tower on 28-07-17</p><p>6. Complainants have made application to builder for cancellation of allotment along with refund of payments made on 23-10-17 but no reply or refund received from builder.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p>','<p>Refund of payments done along with applicable interest&nbsp;</p><p>1. 396000 since 16-10-2006</p><p>2. 209685 since 14-03-2014</p><p>3. 411946 since 25-06-2014</p><p>4. 426321 since 28-03-2016</p><p><br></p>',0.00,1443952.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p><br></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'jskhera','2018-12-10 21:52:49.000','jskhera','2018-12-10 21:52:49.000'),(504,1177,'1177',1152,'b523945f-6c84-4b60-989c-1c236269509d','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Raveena  Riar','raveena7riar@yahoo.com',8054055302,0,0,'ATS Golfmeadows Prelude, Apartment number 1412, Tower 14','Derabassi',28,507,'140507','1','ATS Golfmeadows Prelude, Apartment number 1412, Tower 14','Derabassi',28,507,'140507','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0086','CASA ESPANA','Getamber Anand','getamber@atsgreens.com',8288033311,0,'ATS Infrabuild Pvt. Ltd.','C-226 , Sector 44, Noida',33,216,'201301','1','ATS Infrabuild Pvt. Ltd.','C-226 , Sector 44, Noida',33,216,'201301','1','<p>abc</p>','<p>abc</p>',9125000.00,5526546.00,'2017-12-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>abc</p>','1','','2015-01-21 00:00:00','2015-10-17 00:00:00','Apartment No. 05082, 8th Floor, Tower No. 5, ATS Casa Espana','','',2,0,0,0,'RaveenaRiar','2018-12-11 12:00:21.000','RaveenaRiar','2018-12-11 12:00:21.000'),(505,1177,'1177',1152,'b523945f-6c84-4b60-989c-1c236269509d','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Raveena  Riar','raveena7riar@yahoo.com',8054055302,0,0,'ATS Golfmeadows Prelude, Apartment number 1412, Tower 14','Derabassi',28,507,'140507','1','ATS Golfmeadows Prelude, Apartment number 1412, Tower 14','Derabassi',28,507,'140507','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0086','CASA ESPANA','Getamber Anand','getamber@atsgreens.com',8288033311,0,'ATS Infrabuild Pvt. Ltd.','C-226 , Sector 44, Noida',33,216,'201301','1','ATS Infrabuild Pvt. Ltd.','C-226 , Sector 44, Noida',33,216,'201301','1','<p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<style type=\"text/css\">\r\nli.li1 {margin: 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px \'Helvetica Neue\'}\r\nol.ol1 {list-style-type: decimal}\r\n</style>\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><ol class=\"ol1\">\r\n<li class=\"li1\">We have booked a 3+1 BHK Residential Apartment No. 05082, 8<sup>th</sup>&nbsp;Floor, Tower No. 5 having Super-built up Area of 2400 sq. ft., Built-up Area of 2087 sq. ft. in the project, Type-B with car-parking space in the project known as&nbsp;<b><i>‘ATS Casa Espana’&nbsp;</i></b>for the basic sale price of Rs. 91,25,000 (Rs. ninty one&nbsp; Lac twenty-Five Thousand Only)<b>&nbsp;</b>developed by the respondents/ developer vide application dated 07.05.2014, situated in village Budmajra, Sector 121 Mohali-160055, SAS Nagar, Punjab.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">We paid an amount of&nbsp;<b>Rs.31,17,513/-</b>&nbsp;(Rupees Thirty One Lac Seventeen Thousands Five Hundred and Thirteen Only) towards part-payment of the total amount on 17.10.2015 before signing an Agreement to Sell (Apartment Buyer Agreement) was duly entered into between the parties and thereafter Allotment letter was issued by the respondents.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">That as per the agreement dated 17.10.2015, the completion of the construction of the apartment has to be completed by December 2017 and the possession of the said apartment was to be delivered to us thereafter i.e. in December 2017 but till date, we have not been offered the possession.&nbsp;</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">That after the execution of the agreement, we have been duly depositing the demanded installments of the amount with the respondents to the tune of Rs. 55,26,546 out of the total BSP of Rs. 91,25,000. But still, till date the possession of the aforesaid apartment has not been given to us as per the terms of agreement sell dated 17/10/2015.&nbsp;</li>\r\n</ol>','<p>abc</p>',9125000.00,5526546.00,'2017-12-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>abc</p>','1','','2015-01-21 00:00:00','2015-10-17 00:00:00','Apartment No. 05082, 8th Floor, Tower No. 5, ATS Casa Espana','','',2,0,0,0,'RaveenaRiar','2018-12-11 12:01:55.000','RaveenaRiar','2018-12-11 12:01:55.000'),(506,1177,'1177',1152,'b523945f-6c84-4b60-989c-1c236269509d','FormTypeM',1,1,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Raveena  Riar','raveena7riar@yahoo.com',8054055302,0,0,'ATS Golfmeadows Prelude, Apartment number 1412, Tower 14','Derabassi',28,507,'140507','1','ATS Golfmeadows Prelude, Apartment number 1412, Tower 14','Derabassi',28,507,'140507','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0086','CASA ESPANA','Getamber Anand','getamber@atsgreens.com',8288033311,0,'ATS Infrabuild Pvt. Ltd.','C-226 , Sector 44, Noida',33,216,'201301','1','ATS Infrabuild Pvt. Ltd.','C-226 , Sector 44, Noida',33,216,'201301','1','<p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<style type=\"text/css\">\r\nli.li1 {margin: 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px \'Helvetica Neue\'}\r\nol.ol1 {list-style-type: decimal}\r\n</style>\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><ol class=\"ol1\">\r\n<li class=\"li1\">We have booked a 3+1 BHK Residential Apartment No. 05082, 8<sup>th</sup>&nbsp;Floor, Tower No. 5 having Super-built up Area of 2400 sq. ft., Built-up Area of 2087 sq. ft. in the project, Type-B with car-parking space in the project known as&nbsp;<b><i>‘ATS Casa Espana’&nbsp;</i></b>for the basic sale price of Rs. 91,25,000 (Rs. ninty one&nbsp; Lac twenty-Five Thousand Only)<b>&nbsp;</b>developed by the respondents/ developer vide application dated 07.05.2014, situated in village Budmajra, Sector 121 Mohali-160055, SAS Nagar, Punjab.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">We paid an amount of&nbsp;<b>Rs.31,17,513/-</b>&nbsp;(Rupees Thirty One Lac Seventeen Thousands Five Hundred and Thirteen Only) towards part-payment of the total amount on 17.10.2015 before signing an Agreement to Sell (Apartment Buyer Agreement) was duly entered into between the parties and thereafter Allotment letter was issued by the respondents.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">That as per the agreement dated 17.10.2015, the completion of the construction of the apartment has to be completed by December 2017 and the possession of the said apartment was to be delivered to us thereafter i.e. in December 2017 but till date, we have not been offered the possession.&nbsp;</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">That after the execution of the agreement, we have been duly depositing the demanded installments of the amount with the respondents to the tune of Rs. 55,26,546 out of the total BSP of Rs. 91,25,000. But still, till date the possession of the aforesaid apartment has not been given to us as per the terms of agreement sell dated 17/10/2015.&nbsp;</li>\r\n</ol>','<span style=\"color: rgb(38, 40, 42); font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14.4444px;\">That as per the provision of the aforesaid Act and rules made thereunder, we are entitled&nbsp;to&nbsp;interest on the amount i.e Rs. 55,26,546, which we have paid to the respondents till date as the respondents have been utilizing the amount and the project has been delayed beyond the contractually agreed period as per the terms of agreement sell dated 17/10/2015. As per the agreement the respondent was required to hand over the possession of the said apartment till December 31st, 2017 which he has failed to do so. Though as per the clause 6.3 of the said agreement the respondent was required to pay Rs 5 per month/per square feet of the Super Built-up Area 2400sqft has not paid us even a single penny. In this account now</span><span class=\"yiv6797582936ydp921cad73Apple-converted-space\" style=\"color: rgb(38, 40, 42); font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14.4444px;\"></span><span style=\"color: rgb(38, 40, 42); font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14.4444px;\">&nbsp;we are entitled to rate of interest on the deposited amount as prescribed in the act for the period of delay in handing over the possession from the date of respective deposits of the amount till the realization of the said apartment in physical possession.</span><span class=\"yiv6797582936ydp921cad73Apple-converted-space\" style=\"color: rgb(38, 40, 42); font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14.4444px;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span style=\"color: rgb(38, 40, 42); font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14.4444px;\">We are forced to indulge in an unwanted litigation as such also incurred the litigation expenses to the tune of Rs. 50,000.</span><span class=\"yiv6797582936ydp921cad73Apple-converted-space\" style=\"color: rgb(38, 40, 42); font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14.4444px;\">&nbsp;</span>',9125000.00,5526546.00,'2017-12-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Not required</p>','1','','2015-01-21 00:00:00','2015-10-17 00:00:00','Apartment No. 05082, 8th Floor, Tower No. 5, ATS Casa Espana','','',2,0,0,0,'RaveenaRiar','2018-12-11 12:03:36.000','RaveenaRiar','2018-12-11 12:03:36.000'),(507,1178,'1178',1249,'633d568c-6bc4-4a67-ac48-2650be8f8a83','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-11 15:55:27.000','Harish Minocha ','kangan_1993@yahoo.in',9810617548,0,0,'E-3, Lajpat Nagar-III','2nd Floor, Delhi-24',10,557,'110024','1','E-3, Lajpat Nagar-III','2nd Floor, Delhi-24',10,557,'110024','Baani Chhibber','baanichbr@gmail.com',9876658773,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PM0010','Industrial Knowledge (Fashion Technology) Park, Sector 90, SAS Nagar, Mohali','M/s Chandigarh Overseas Project Ltd.','chdoverseas@rediffmail.com',0,0,'SCO 249','Sector 44-C',6,128,'160047','0','SCO 196-197, Top Floor','Sector 34-A',6,128,'160047','1','<p>The complainant had entered into two developer buyer agreements with the Respondent, dated 24.12.2007 for the purchase of super area measuring 125 square feet each in the design studio bearing No. 11, Floor No. 6, Block A-1 in the Industrial Knowledge (Fashion Technology) Park, Sector 90, SAS Nagar, Mohali.&nbsp;</p><p>The complainant has made a total payment of Rs. 9,50,000 till date for both the units. The Complainant was promised the delivery of possession within the period of 30 months from the date of start of construction. However, the possession of the said super area has not been delivered to the complainant so far. The construction of the project was grossly delayed and by the promised date i.e by the end of 2009 &amp; till now the construction of the said project is incomplete.&nbsp;</p><p>That under the developer buyer agreement, the complainant was entitled to receive Rs. 50 per square feet per month as delay charges if the possession was not delivered at the agreed time. The said delay charges were paid from 26.03.2010 till 02.01.2012 only amounting to Rs. 3,30,242 and thereafter no delay charges have been paid to the complainant.&nbsp;</p><p>The detailed facts of the case are enumerated in the hard copy of the complaint.</p>','<p>The Complainant prays for the following reliefs</p><p>(i) Pass an order/direction to the respondent to deliver the possession of the units as per the Developer Buyer Agreement, along with interest @10.15 % p.a. i,e prevailing applicable State Bank of India Highest Marginal Cost of Lending Rate plus two percent from the date of payments till the date of possession of the units &amp; accept the balance payment.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>(ii)Levy a penalty of 5% of the estimated cost of the real estate project for breach of its obligation to deliver possession on time under the Act.</p><p>(iii) Pass an order/direction to the respondent to pay an amount of Rs.12,500/- (Rupees Ten Lakh Fifty Thousand only) p.m for both the units as delay charges from the period starting from 01.02.2012 till actual realization to the complainant, along with the interest @ 10.15% p.a i,e prevailing applicable State Bank of India Highest Marginal Cost of Lending Rate plus two percent.&nbsp;</p><p>(iv) If the Respondent is not able to give the possession of the units as per the agreement then in the alternative, direction to the Respondent to return the amounts paid with interest from the date of payment till the actual realization as per the RERA Rule 15 with the prevailing applicable State Bank of India Highest Marginal Cost of Lending Rate plus two percent i.e. 10.15%</p><p>(v) Pass any other order/direction in favour of the complainant &amp; against the respondent as deem fit by the authority.</p><div><br></div>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Pending final decision on the complaint the complainant seeks issue of a direction to the Respondent not to sell/transfer/allot the units to any third person.</p><div><br></div>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'BaaniChhibber','2018-12-11 12:22:54.000','BaaniChhibber','2018-12-11 12:22:54.000'),(508,1115,'1115',1214,'236d33c7-52c2-47c2-9d91-8289ee07ebac','FormTypeM',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Mukesh Gupta','mukeshgupta.31@gmail.com',9417217902,0,0,'B-3, 302, Nirmal Chayya Towers','VIP road, Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','1','B-3, 302, Nirmal Chayya Towers','VIP road, Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PC0019','M/s Country Colonisers Pvt. Ltd. ','M/s Country Colonisers Pvt. Ltd. ','rera@waveestate.in',0,0,' M/s Country Colonisers Pvt. Ltd. ','Sector-85, SAS Nagar (Mohali)',28,507,'140308','1',' M/s Country Colonisers Pvt. Ltd. ','Sector-85, SAS Nagar (Mohali)',28,507,'140308','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">I had booked independent first floor in Wave\r\nEstate, Sector-99 under subvention scheme by initial payment of Rs.\r\n3,00,000/- vide cheque no. 60113 dated 08.02.2013. Next payment was made vide\r\ncheque no. 60117 dated 19.04.2013 amounting Rs. 3,18,540/-. It was committed to\r\nmake delivery within 2 years.&nbsp;</span>However, M/s Country Colonisers Pvt.\r\nLtd. executed the agreement on 07.02.2015 as per which possession was to be\r\noffered within 24 months along with an extended grace period of 6 months.<o:p></o:p></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">Accordingly, I arranged for accommodation on\r\nrent in Apr’2017 and have been paying both rent and EMIs as the subvention\r\nperiod had lapsed. Due to inordinate delay I lost faith in the project and requested\r\nthe developers through e-mails to refund my deposits. However there was no\r\nresponse from their end as they continued to defer possession and progress on\r\nsite was very slow. They agreed to settle only pre-EMI interest from Aug’17 (24+6\r\nmonths from date of agreement) onwards and offered to deliver possession in Mar’18.\r\nDeveloper even failed to meet that deadline and n</span>ow when I informed the builder that I have filed complaint in RERA on 15.11.2018 they have sent possession letter on 29.11.2018 which is dated 08.10.2018 just to get away with the complaint as it is not possible that they can keep the letter with themselves for over 50 days.</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">After so much of agony, I do not want to remain\r\nassociated with the developer and request for return of all deposits (including\r\nEMIs) with interest.&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">In\r\nlight of the case facts brought out hereinabove, association with the project has not only been loss of time,\r\nmoney and effort but has caused a lot of mental harassment. It is therefore requested to refund entire\r\ndeposits including EMIs paid to bank with interest.&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p>',4000000.00,3000000.00,'2017-08-07 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','It is prayed to stop the EMIs till final decision as I am not able to pay both rent and EMI.&nbsp;','1','','2015-02-07 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','40, First Floor, Sector-99, Mohali','','',2,0,0,0,'mukesh013128','2018-12-11 14:36:33.000','mukesh013128','2018-12-11 14:36:33.000'),(509,1115,'1115',1214,'236d33c7-52c2-47c2-9d91-8289ee07ebac','FormTypeM',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Mukesh Gupta','mukeshgupta.31@gmail.com',9417217902,0,0,'B-3, 302, Nirmal Chayya Towers','VIP road, Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','1','B-3, 302, Nirmal Chayya Towers','VIP road, Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PC0019','M/s Country Colonisers Pvt. Ltd. ','M/s Country Colonisers Pvt. Ltd. ','rera@waveestate.in',0,0,' M/s Country Colonisers Pvt. Ltd. ','Sector-85, SAS Nagar (Mohali)',28,507,'140308','1',' M/s Country Colonisers Pvt. Ltd. ','Sector-85, SAS Nagar (Mohali)',28,507,'140308','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">I had booked independent first floor in Wave\r\nEstate, Sector-99 under subvention scheme by initial payment of Rs.\r\n3,00,000/- vide cheque no. 60113 dated 08.02.2013. Next payment was made vide\r\ncheque no. 60117 dated 19.04.2013 amounting Rs. 3,18,540/-. It was committed to\r\nmake delivery within 2 years.&nbsp;</span>However, M/s Country Colonisers Pvt.\r\nLtd. executed the agreement on 07.02.2015 as per which possession was to be\r\noffered within 24 months along with an extended grace period of 6 months.<o:p></o:p></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">Accordingly, I arranged for accommodation on\r\nrent in Apr’2017 and have been paying both rent and EMIs as the subvention\r\nperiod had lapsed. Due to inordinate delay I lost faith in the project and requested\r\nthe developers through e-mails to refund my deposits. However there was no\r\nresponse from their end as they continued to defer possession and progress on\r\nsite was very slow. They agreed to settle only pre-EMI interest from Aug’17 (24+6\r\nmonths from date of agreement) onwards and offered to deliver possession in Mar’18.\r\nDeveloper even failed to meet that deadline and n</span>ow when I informed the builder that I have filed complaint in RERA on 15.11.2018 they have sent possession letter on 29.11.2018 which is dated 08.10.2018 just to get away with the complaint as it is not possible that they can keep the letter with themselves for over 50 days.</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">After so much of agony, I do not want to remain\r\nassociated with the developer and request for return of all deposits (including\r\nEMIs) with interest.&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">In\r\nlight of the case facts brought out hereinabove, association with the project has not only been loss of time,\r\nmoney and effort but has caused a lot of mental harassment. It is therefore requested to refund entire\r\ndeposits including EMIs paid to bank with interest.&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p>',4000000.00,3000000.00,'2017-08-07 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','It is prayed to stop the EMIs till final decision as I am not able to pay both rent and EMI.&nbsp;','1','','2015-02-07 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','40, First Floor, Sector-99, Mohali','','',2,0,0,0,'mukesh013128','2018-12-11 14:45:09.000','mukesh013128','2018-12-11 14:45:09.000'),(510,1177,'1177',1152,'b523945f-6c84-4b60-989c-1c236269509d','FormTypeM',1,1,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Raveena  Riar','raveena7riar@yahoo.com',8054055302,0,0,'ATS Golfmeadows Prelude, Apartment number 1412, Tower 14','Derabassi',28,507,'140507','1','ATS Golfmeadows Prelude, Apartment number 1412, Tower 14','Derabassi',28,507,'140507','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0086','CASA ESPANA','Getamber Anand','getamber@atsgreens.com',8288033311,0,'ATS Infrabuild Pvt. Ltd.','C-226 , Sector 44, Noida',33,216,'201301','1','ATS Infrabuild Pvt. Ltd.','C-226 , Sector 44, Noida',33,216,'201301','1','<p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<style type=\"text/css\">\r\nli.li1 {margin: 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px \'Helvetica Neue\'}\r\nol.ol1 {list-style-type: decimal}\r\n</style>\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><ol class=\"ol1\">\r\n<li class=\"li1\">We have booked a 3+1 BHK Residential Apartment No. 05082, 8<sup>th</sup>&nbsp;Floor, Tower No. 5 having Super-built up Area of 2400 sq. ft., Built-up Area of 2087 sq. ft. in the project, Type-B with car-parking space in the project known as&nbsp;<b><i>‘ATS Casa Espana’&nbsp;</i></b>for the basic sale price of Rs. 91,25,000 (Rs. ninty one&nbsp; Lac twenty-Five Thousand Only)<b>&nbsp;</b>developed by the respondents/ developer vide application dated 07.05.2014, situated in village Budmajra, Sector 121 Mohali-160055, SAS Nagar, Punjab.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">We paid an amount of&nbsp;<b>Rs.31,17,513/-</b>&nbsp;(Rupees Thirty One Lac Seventeen Thousands Five Hundred and Thirteen Only) towards part-payment of the total amount on 17.10.2015 before signing an Agreement to Sell (Apartment Buyer Agreement) was duly entered into between the parties and thereafter Allotment letter was issued by the respondents.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">That as per the agreement dated 17.10.2015, the completion of the construction of the apartment has to be completed by December 2017 and the possession of the said apartment was to be delivered to us thereafter i.e. in December 2017 but till date, we have not been offered the possession.&nbsp;</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">That after the execution of the agreement, we have been duly depositing the demanded installments of the amount with the respondents to the tune of Rs. 55,26,546 out of the total BSP of Rs. 91,25,000. But still, till date the possession of the aforesaid apartment has not been given to us as per the terms of agreement sell dated 17/10/2015.&nbsp;</li>\r\n</ol>','<span style=\"color: rgb(38, 40, 42); font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14.4444px;\">That as per the provision of the aforesaid Act and rules made thereunder, we are entitled&nbsp;to&nbsp;interest on the amount i.e Rs. 55,26,546, which we have paid to the respondents till date as the respondents have been utilizing the amount and the project has been delayed beyond the contractually agreed period as per the terms of agreement sell dated 17/10/2015. As per the agreement the respondent was required to hand over the possession of the said apartment till December 31st, 2017 which he has failed to do so. Though as per the clause 6.3 of the said agreement the respondent was required to pay Rs 5 per month/per square feet of the Super Built-up Area 2400sqft has not paid us even a single penny. In this account now</span><span class=\"yiv6797582936ydp921cad73Apple-converted-space\" style=\"color: rgb(38, 40, 42); font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14.4444px;\"></span><span style=\"color: rgb(38, 40, 42); font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14.4444px;\">&nbsp;we are entitled to rate of interest on the deposited amount as prescribed in the act for the period of delay in handing over the possession from the date of respective deposits of the amount till the realization of the said apartment in physical possession.</span><span class=\"yiv6797582936ydp921cad73Apple-converted-space\" style=\"color: rgb(38, 40, 42); font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14.4444px;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span style=\"color: rgb(38, 40, 42); font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14.4444px;\">We are forced to indulge in an unwanted litigation as such also incurred the litigation expenses to the tune of Rs. 50,000.</span><span class=\"yiv6797582936ydp921cad73Apple-converted-space\" style=\"color: rgb(38, 40, 42); font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14.4444px;\">&nbsp;</span>',9125000.00,5526546.00,'2017-12-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Not required</p>','1','','2015-01-21 00:00:00','2015-10-17 00:00:00','Apartment No. 05082, 8th Floor, Tower No. 5, ATS Casa Espana','','',2,0,0,0,'RaveenaRiar','2018-12-11 15:38:44.000','RaveenaRiar','2018-12-11 15:38:44.000'),(511,1177,'1177',1152,'b523945f-6c84-4b60-989c-1c236269509d','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-11 15:39:31.000','Raveena  Riar','raveena7riar@yahoo.com',8054055302,0,0,'ATS Golfmeadows Prelude, Apartment number 1412, Tower 14','Derabassi',28,507,'140507','1','ATS Golfmeadows Prelude, Apartment number 1412, Tower 14','Derabassi',28,507,'140507','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0086','CASA ESPANA','Getamber Anand','getamber@atsgreens.com',8288033311,0,'ATS Infrabuild Pvt. Ltd.','C-226 , Sector 44, Noida',33,216,'201301','1','ATS Infrabuild Pvt. Ltd.','C-226 , Sector 44, Noida',33,216,'201301','1','<p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<style type=\"text/css\">\r\nli.li1 {margin: 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px \'Helvetica Neue\'}\r\nol.ol1 {list-style-type: decimal}\r\n</style>\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><ol class=\"ol1\">\r\n<li class=\"li1\">We have booked a 3+1 BHK Residential Apartment No. 05082, 8<sup>th</sup>&nbsp;Floor, Tower No. 5 having Super-built up Area of 2400 sq. ft., Built-up Area of 2087 sq. ft. in the project, Type-B with car-parking space in the project known as&nbsp;<b><i>‘ATS Casa Espana’&nbsp;</i></b>for the basic sale price of Rs. 91,25,000 (Rs. ninty one&nbsp; Lac twenty-Five Thousand Only)<b>&nbsp;</b>developed by the respondents/ developer vide application dated 07.05.2014, situated in village Budmajra, Sector 121 Mohali-160055, SAS Nagar, Punjab.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">We paid an amount of&nbsp;<b>Rs.31,17,513/-</b>&nbsp;(Rupees Thirty One Lac Seventeen Thousands Five Hundred and Thirteen Only) towards part-payment of the total amount on 17.10.2015 before signing an Agreement to Sell (Apartment Buyer Agreement) was duly entered into between the parties and thereafter Allotment letter was issued by the respondents.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">That as per the agreement dated 17.10.2015, the completion of the construction of the apartment has to be completed by December 2017 and the possession of the said apartment was to be delivered to us thereafter i.e. in December 2017 but till date, we have not been offered the possession.&nbsp;</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">That after the execution of the agreement, we have been duly depositing the demanded installments of the amount with the respondents to the tune of Rs. 55,26,546 out of the total BSP of Rs. 91,25,000. But still, till date the possession of the aforesaid apartment has not been given to us as per the terms of agreement sell dated 17/10/2015.&nbsp;</li>\r\n</ol>','<span style=\"color: rgb(38, 40, 42); font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14.4444px;\">That as per the provision of the aforesaid Act and rules made thereunder, we are entitled&nbsp;to&nbsp;interest on the amount i.e Rs. 55,26,546, which we have paid to the respondents till date as the respondents have been utilizing the amount and the project has been delayed beyond the contractually agreed period as per the terms of agreement sell dated 17/10/2015. As per the agreement the respondent was required to hand over the possession of the said apartment till December 31st, 2017 which he has failed to do so. Though as per the clause 6.3 of the said agreement the respondent was required to pay Rs 5 per month/per square feet of the Super Built-up Area 2400sqft has not paid us even a single penny. In this account now</span><span class=\"yiv6797582936ydp921cad73Apple-converted-space\" style=\"color: rgb(38, 40, 42); font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14.4444px;\"></span><span style=\"color: rgb(38, 40, 42); font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14.4444px;\">&nbsp;we are entitled to rate of interest on the deposited amount as prescribed in the act for the period of delay in handing over the possession from the date of respective deposits of the amount till the realization of the said apartment in physical possession.</span><span class=\"yiv6797582936ydp921cad73Apple-converted-space\" style=\"color: rgb(38, 40, 42); font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14.4444px;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span style=\"color: rgb(38, 40, 42); font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14.4444px;\">We are forced to indulge in an unwanted litigation as such also incurred the litigation expenses to the tune of Rs. 50,000.</span><span class=\"yiv6797582936ydp921cad73Apple-converted-space\" style=\"color: rgb(38, 40, 42); font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14.4444px;\">&nbsp;</span>',9125000.00,5526546.00,'2017-12-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Not required</p>','1','','2015-01-21 00:00:00','2015-10-17 00:00:00','Apartment No. 05082, 8th Floor, Tower No. 5, ATS Casa Espana','','',1,1,0,0,'RaveenaRiar','2018-12-11 15:39:22.000','RaveenaRiar','2018-12-11 15:39:22.000'),(512,1179,'1179',1098,'81775a1c-ad46-40a6-b51a-c95cca91809d','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-11 21:40:19.000','RACHNA VINAYAK','abhi.vinayak@yahoo.co.in',9992015557,0,691285130931,'44-45 SHIVAJI PARK','MODEL TOWN',13,21,'135001','1','T-1, 301, BESTECH PARK VIEW RESIDENCES','SECTOR 66',28,507,'160062','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0086','ATS CASA ESPANA \r\nVillage Budmajra, Kharar, Sector 121, S.A.S. Nagar, Mohali','M/s. ATS Infrabuild Pvt. Ltd.,','email@atsgreens.com',8288099915,0,'M/s. ATS Infrabuild Pvt. Ltd., Regd. Office: 711/92,','Deepali, Nehru Place, New Delhi-110019.',10,557,'110019','1','M/s. ATS Infrabuild Pvt. Ltd., Regd. Office: 711/92,','Deepali, Nehru Place, New Delhi-110019.',10,557,'110019','1','<p>I booked an apartment from M/s. ATS Infrabuild Pvt. Ltd. The apartment Unit No. is 4022, Tower 4,\r\nSecond Floor, ATS Casa Espana, sized 2400 sq ft. The total cost of the property was fixed at\r\nRs.9158000/- Plus taxes. I’ve already paid a total amount of Rs.88,30,492/- to the company. I paid\r\nRs.50,000/- on dated 31/1/2017, Rs.49,50,000/- on dated 31/1/2017, Rs.33,39,101/- on dated 31/3/2017,\r\nRs.83,391/- on dated 31/3/2017 &amp; Rs.4,08,000/- on dated 4/4/2017. The Company, executed Apartment\r\nBuyer Agreement and issued Provisional Allotment of the flat in question, on 9th February, 2017. The\r\nbuilder/company promised to complete construction &amp; handover the apartment by December 2017. Unfortunately, despite having paid more than 95% of the total amount,\r\nthe company has failed to deliver the possession of the flat. Here it is also pertinent to mention that I\r\nhave taken a HOME LOAN from HDFC Ltd and I’m paying huge amount of interest, every month. Here it\r\nis also relevant to mention that since I have taken home loan from HDFC, all the documents like allotment\r\nletter, apartment buyer agreement, payment receipts pertaining to the flat unit in question were handed\r\nover by the builder company directly to the bank/financier. The builder company only handed over Copy of\r\nApartment Buyer Agreement to me and no other document whatsoever. I\'ve been visiting the builder /\r\ncompany office and contacting the officials of the company/builder regularly, seeking compensation and to\r\nknow the actual date of possession, to no avail though.&nbsp; I\'ve&nbsp; filed a complaint No. : AdCNo10422018, under FORM \"N\" before Ld. Adjudicating Officer of Punjab Rera, seeking Compensation, which is yet to come up for hearing.<br></p>','<p>That as per the allotment letter cum agreement, the company is charging penal interest from the buyers\r\n@12% to 18% per annum, for delay in making payment, as and when demanded by the\r\nbuilder/company. I’ve paid more than 95% of the total sale consideration amount, i.e. Rs. 88,30,492/- to\r\nthe company since last almost 2 years. However, the builder/company has delayed the possession of the apartment, for no rhyme\r\nor reason. The builder has not offered possession yet. Here it also worth mentioning that during this entire period of inordinate\r\ndelay, there has not been any force majure or circumstances beyond the control of the developers, behind\r\nwhich the company might try to hide &amp; wriggle out from discharge of their lawful liability. </p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;<span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14pt; text-align: justify;\">Thus I seek parity &amp; equity between the\r\ninterest paid by the buyer to the builder &amp; the interest payable by the builder/company to the buyer. The\r\ninterest that the builder/company ought to pay as compensation, should be equal and at\r\npar with what they charge from the helpless buyers. </span><b style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14pt; text-align: justify;\"><u>RELIEF SOUGHT\r\nIN THE PRESENT COMPLAINT :</u></b><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14pt; text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;SINCE I AM PAYING HUGE AMOUNT OF BANK INTEREST TO HDFC LTD. FOR MY HOME LOAN, I SEEK COMPENSATION IN FORM OF INTEREST, AS PER THE RELEVANT PROVISIONS OF RERA, for inordinate delay in possession.</span></p>',9158000.00,8830492.00,'2018-03-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>That during the pendency of this present complaint, if the builder secures occupation certificate and offers\r\npossession to the buyers, the builder be directed to handover the possession to me, without forcing or\r\ncoercing me to withdraw the present complaint. In such case, the builder/company may kindly be directed\r\nto deliver possession, pending final outcome/award. It is also prayed that since I have already paid more than 95%\r\nof the total sale consideration, the builder be directed not to ask for any more amount until final order in\r\nthis present complaint is passed by the Hon’ble Authority.&nbsp;<br></p>','1','','2017-02-09 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Flat No.4022, Tower-4, Second Floor, ATS Casa Espana, Sector 121, Mohali - Punjab.','','',1,1,0,0,'rachnabhi','2018-12-11 17:10:15.000','rachnabhi','2018-12-11 17:10:15.000'),(513,1115,'1115',1214,'236d33c7-52c2-47c2-9d91-8289ee07ebac','FormTypeM',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Mukesh Gupta','mukeshgupta.31@gmail.com',9417217902,0,0,'B-3, 302, Nirmal Chayya Towers','VIP road, Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','1','B-3, 302, Nirmal Chayya Towers','VIP road, Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PC0019','M/s Country Colonisers Pvt. Ltd. ','M/s Country Colonisers Pvt. Ltd. ','rera@waveestate.in',0,0,' M/s Country Colonisers Pvt. Ltd. ','Sector-85, SAS Nagar (Mohali)',28,507,'140308','1',' M/s Country Colonisers Pvt. Ltd. ','Sector-85, SAS Nagar (Mohali)',28,507,'140308','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">I had booked independent first floor in Wave\r\nEstate, Sector-99 under subvention scheme by initial payment of Rs.\r\n3,00,000/- vide cheque no. 60113 dated 08.02.2013. Next payment was made vide\r\ncheque no. 60117 dated 19.04.2013 amounting Rs. 3,18,540/-. It was committed to\r\nmake delivery within 2 years.&nbsp;</span>However, M/s Country Colonisers Pvt.\r\nLtd. executed the agreement on 07.02.2015 as per which possession was to be\r\noffered within 24 months along with an extended grace period of 6 months.<o:p></o:p></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">Accordingly, I arranged for accommodation on\r\nrent in Apr’2017 and have been paying both rent and EMIs as the subvention\r\nperiod had lapsed. Due to inordinate delay I lost faith in the project and requested\r\nthe developers through e-mails to refund my deposits. However there was no\r\nresponse from their end as they continued to defer possession and progress on\r\nsite was very slow. They agreed to settle only pre-EMI interest from Aug’17 (24+6\r\nmonths from date of agreement) onwards and offered to deliver possession in Mar’18.\r\nDeveloper even failed to meet that deadline and n</span>ow when I informed the builder that I have filed complaint in RERA on 15.11.2018 they have sent possession letter on 29.11.2018 which is dated 08.10.2018 just to get away with the complaint as it is not possible that they can keep the letter with themselves for over 50 days.</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">After so much of agony, I do not want to remain\r\nassociated with the developer and request for return of all deposits (including\r\nEMIs) with interest.&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">In\r\nlight of the case facts brought out hereinabove, association with the project has not only been loss of time,\r\nmoney and effort but has caused a lot of mental harassment. It is therefore requested to refund entire\r\ndeposits including EMIs paid to bank with interest.&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p>',4000000.00,3000000.00,'2017-08-07 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','It is prayed to stop the EMIs till final decision as I am not able to pay both rent and EMI.&nbsp;','1','','2015-02-07 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','40, First Floor, Sector-99, Mohali','','',2,0,0,0,'mukesh013128','2018-12-12 10:06:38.000','mukesh013128','2018-12-12 10:06:38.000'),(514,1180,'1180',1172,'fe8a123a-24f0-4e44-a8e1-3e154d6acf61','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Ramesh Mittal','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9934787251,0,0,'Mittal House, Main Road','Near Pankaj Cinema, Raxaul',5,188,'845305','1','253','Sector 4, Mansa Devi Complex',13,15,'134114','Sanjeev Gupta','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0093','PALM SPRING','M/s Manohar Infrastructure & Constructions Pvt Ltd','nbs@manoharrealty.com',0,1725033524,'SCO 139-142','Sector-17C',6,128,'160017','1','SCO 139-142','Sector-17C',6,128,'160017','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:\r\njustify;line-height:150%;mso-layout-grid-align:none;text-autospace:none\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">Applicant,\r\non 21.10.2013 booked a (C1) 250 sq yards plot @RS. 20000 per sq yd from the\r\nrespondent in Palm Spring.Respondent assured that it has all approvals except\r\nlayout which will be obtained within 2-3 months &amp; possession will be\r\ndelivered in 2 years.A broacher (C2) was also provided to applicant before\r\nbooking. Applicant paid Rs. 1500000 i.e 30% of sale consideration vide two\r\ncheques (C3) dated 21.10.13 &amp; 19.12.13. Insipte of repeated\r\nrequests,respondent did not issue any allotment letter &amp; execute the\r\nagreement.Respondent had even concealed that it was not having CLU &amp; it was\r\nin September,2014(C4)it informed the applicant that it has received the CLU now\r\n&amp; allotment shall be made in Dec,2014.The applicant was shocked after\r\nknowing that, as he was under impression that respondent was having all the\r\napprovals. Since the respondent assured to make allotment in Dec, 2014 the\r\napplicant chose to have the plot since substantial amount was already paid by\r\nhim.But the respondent did not issue any allotment letter even by the said\r\ndate.The respondent even failed to start any development.Inspite of number of\r\nvisits,repeated requests and assurances, the respondent did not issue any\r\nallotment letter &amp; execute the agreement during year 2014 to 2018.Email was\r\nalso sent to respondent on 17.08.18 (C5)requesting the respondent to refund the\r\namount since the respondent failed to issue any allotment letter &amp; execute\r\nagreement.Then the respondent telephonically informed the applicant that it\r\nwill sell the plot at premium of Rs. 2000 per sq yd and refund the amount to\r\nhim, And for that purpose also asked the bank detail,which was duly sent by the\r\napplicant vide email dated 21.08.18(C6).The respondent has misrepresented the\r\napplicant since beginning and never informed him about the true picture of the approvals\r\nand development.It had not even applied the necessary permissions when the plot\r\nwas sold to applicant.A list of dates of approvals C7 and some important\r\napprovals as C8 &amp; C9<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<ol><li><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:\r\njustify;line-height:150%;mso-layout-grid-align:none;text-autospace:none\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">Directing\r\nthe respondent to refund the principle amount i.e. Rs. 1500000 along with\r\ninterest as contemplated under rule 16 of The Punjab RERA Rules, 2017, as the\r\ncomplainants have lost faith in the respondent due to misrepresentation by it\r\nabout the approvals &amp; stages of development during all these years ,did not\r\nissue any allotment letter &amp; execute the agreement till date, failed to\r\ndevelop the project &amp; thus the complainants wish to withdraw from the\r\nproject. Also the respondent has committed violation of various provisions of\r\nPAPRA &amp; conditions of various approvals granted to it, as it could not\r\ncollect any amount till the exemption is received under Section 44 of PAPRA\r\nwhich was granted on 25.1.17.The respondent collected the money from the\r\ncomplainant in 2013.The approvals were granted to the respondent on the ground\r\nthat it will not sell any plot &amp; collect money from the general public till\r\nexemption under Section 44 of PAPRA is received.Also, inspite of receiving 30%\r\nof sale consideration the respondent did not execute any agreement &amp; issue\r\na plot number till date &amp; asking the complainant to pay more money for\r\ngetting the allotment letter &amp; execution of agreement in violation of\r\nSection 13 of RERA.</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:\r\njustify;line-height:150%;mso-layout-grid-align:none;text-autospace:none\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;line-height:\r\nnormal;mso-layout-grid-align:none;text-autospace:none\"><span style=\"font-family:\r\n&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">To take action against respondent under Section 61 of\r\nRERA for constant violation of provision of Section 13 of RERA as the\r\nrespondent failed to issue any allotment letter &amp; execute the buyer’s\r\nagreement till date, inspite of receiving 30% of sale consideration&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:\r\njustify;line-height:150%;mso-layout-grid-align:none;text-autospace:none\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><o:p><br></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:\r\njustify;line-height:150%;mso-layout-grid-align:none;text-autospace:none\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><o:p><br></o:p></span></p></li></ol>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>abc</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'rerafilingformn','2018-12-12 12:40:22.000','rerafilingformn','2018-12-12 12:40:22.000'),(515,1181,'1181',1261,'87a17578-cb7d-4b63-b1e8-f97fd8b674d5','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Ravikant Sawhney','gaurav.chopra@hotmail.com',9815400414,0,0,'B-XXX-891','near Mothu Ram Pump, sherpur, Sherpur',28,366,'142036','1','B-XXX-891','near Mothu Ram Pump, sherpur, Sherpur',28,366,'142036','Gaurav Chopra','gaurav.chopra@hotmail.com',9814013127,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0119','Mohali Hills (Group Housing)','Emaar MGF Land Ltd','sorabh.kakar@emaarmgf.com',0,0,'40, Ground Floor','Central Plaza, sector 105',28,507,'140306','1','40, Ground Floor','Central Plaza, sector 105',28,507,'140306','1','<p><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">•	Applicant: M/s APS International Pvt Ltd \r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">•	Allotment letter : 15.1.2008\r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">•	Allotted Unit: Apartment No. K3-FPH-PH-01 in “The Views” at Mohali Hills in Sector-105, SAS Nagar, District Mohali</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">• Buyer\'s Agreement :29.2.2008\r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">•	Total sale consideration of Rs. 1,10,52,008/- at the rate of Rs. 2950/- per sq. foot of super area of 3250 sq. ft.   \r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">•	Construction Linked Instalment Plan amount paid till date: Rs. 1,01,71,173/- was paid by the Applicant to the Respondent upto 28.10.2014. \r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">•	As per Clause 21.1 of the Buyer’s Agreement, the Respondent was under a contractual obligation to handover possession of the Allotted Unit within a period of 36 months from the date of allotment with a further relaxation of 90 days over and above the stipulated time period for the purpose of applying for and obtaining an Occupation Certificate in respect of the Group Housing Complex.  \r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">•	That Clause 21.1 of the Agreement read with Clause 23.1 made it abundantly clear that time was the essence of the contract and hence, possession of the Allotted Unit was required to be handed over to the Applicant by the Respondent positively on or before 15.4.2011.  Till date, however, despite a lapse of more than 6 years, possession of the Allotted Unit has not been offered or handed over to the Applicant and this willful omission and lapse on the part of the Respondent constitutes a willful and material breach of the Agreement dated 29.2.2008 executed between the parties.  \r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">•	Aggrieved by the aforesaid omission and lapse of the Respondent, the Applicant had written a letter/e-mail dated 29.9.2017 to the Respondent for rescinding the contract and for seeking refund of the principal amount paid by the Applicant in respect of the Allotted Unit alongwith interest.  Till date, however, the aforesaid demand raised by the Applicant has not been acceded to by the Respondent and thus, vide the instant complaint, the Applicant seek refund of the monies paid by it to the Respondent alongwith interest</span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:1.0in;text-align:justify;text-indent:\r\n-.5in;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n200%;font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">i)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Refund of an amount of Rs. 1,01,71,173/-\r\npaid by the Applicant alongwith interest (highest marginal cost of lending rate\r\nof the State Bank of India + 2%) from the respective dates of deposit till\r\nactual realization as per Sections 18 and 19(4) of the Act read with Rule 16 of\r\nthe Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:1.0in;text-align:justify;text-indent:\r\n-.5in;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n200%;font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">ii)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Any other relief which the Applicant is\r\nentitled for under the Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Act, 2016 and\r\nthe Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017.&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p>',11052008.00,10171173.00,'2011-04-15 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>N.A.</p>','1','','2008-01-15 00:00:00','2008-02-29 00:00:00','K3-FPH-PH-01 “The Views” at Mohali Hills in Sector-105, SAS Nagar, District Mohali','','',2,0,0,0,'APSInternational','2018-12-12 12:42:28.000','APSInternational','2018-12-12 12:42:28.000'),(516,1115,'1115',1214,'236d33c7-52c2-47c2-9d91-8289ee07ebac','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-12 16:38:20.000','Mukesh Gupta','mukeshgupta.31@gmail.com',9417217902,0,0,'B-3, 302, Nirmal Chayya Towers','VIP road, Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','1','B-3, 302, Nirmal Chayya Towers','VIP road, Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PC0019','M/s Country Colonisers Pvt. Ltd. ','M/s Country Colonisers Pvt. Ltd. ','rera@waveestate.in',0,0,' M/s Country Colonisers Pvt. Ltd. ','Sector-85, SAS Nagar (Mohali)',28,507,'140308','1',' M/s Country Colonisers Pvt. Ltd. ','Sector-85, SAS Nagar (Mohali)',28,507,'140308','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">I had booked independent first floor in Wave\r\nEstate, Sector-99 under subvention scheme by initial payment of Rs.\r\n3,00,000/- vide cheque no. 60113 dated 08.02.2013. Next payment was made vide\r\ncheque no. 60117 dated 19.04.2013 amounting Rs. 3,18,540/-. It was committed to\r\nmake delivery within 2 years.&nbsp;</span>However, M/s Country Colonisers Pvt.\r\nLtd. executed the agreement on 07.02.2015 as per which possession was to be\r\noffered within 24 months along with an extended grace period of 6 months.<o:p></o:p></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">Accordingly, I arranged for accommodation on\r\nrent in Apr’2017 and have been paying both rent and EMIs as the subvention\r\nperiod had lapsed. Due to inordinate delay I lost faith in the project and requested\r\nthe developers through e-mails to refund my deposits. However there was no\r\nresponse from their end as they continued to defer possession and progress on\r\nsite was very slow. They agreed to settle only pre-EMI interest from Aug’17 (24+6\r\nmonths from date of agreement) onwards and offered to deliver possession in Mar’18.\r\nDeveloper even failed to meet that deadline and n</span>ow when I informed the builder that I have filed complaint in RERA on 15.11.2018 they have sent possession letter on 29.11.2018 which is dated 08.10.2018 just to get away with the complaint as it is not possible that they can keep the letter with themselves for over 50 days.</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">After so much of agony, I do not want to remain\r\nassociated with the developer and request for return of all deposits (including\r\nEMIs) with interest.&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">In\r\nlight of the case facts brought out hereinabove, association with the project has not only been loss of time,\r\nmoney and effort but has caused a lot of mental harassment. It is therefore requested to refund entire\r\ndeposits including EMIs paid to bank with interest.&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p>',4000000.00,3000000.00,'2017-08-07 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','It is prayed to stop the EMIs till final decision as I am not able to pay both rent and EMI.&nbsp;','1','','2015-02-07 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','40, First Floor, Sector-99, Mohali','','',2,0,0,0,'mukesh013128','2018-12-12 14:35:14.000','mukesh013128','2018-12-12 14:35:14.000'),(517,1182,'1182',1010,'a182232b-88d6-4711-8baa-f8a026fb675f','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-13 16:57:03.000','VIKAS MIGLANI and ROHIT MIGLANI ','lawofficeofhimanshuraj@gmail.com',9988100005,1724181010,478144878549,'#102, Sector 10 A','',6,128,'160011','1','#102, Sector 10 A','',6,128,'160011','HIMANSHU RAJ','lawofficeofhimanshuraj@gmail.com',9988200001,1724190909,'Promoter','PBRERA-LDH45-PR0060','IREO WATERFRONT','IREO WATERFRONT PRIVATE LIMITED','iwpl@ireo.in',1613040290,0,'SCO 16-17, BASEMENT, FORTUNE CHAMBERS','OPP. LUDHIANA STOCK EXCHANE, FEROZE GANDHI MARKET, LUDHIANA',28,366,'141001','1','SCO 16-17, BASEMENT, FORTUNE CHAMBERS','OPP. LUDHIANA STOCK EXCHANE, FEROZE GANDHI MARKET, LUDHIANA',28,366,'141001','0','<p>Facts in brief\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>1.	That the complainants are the citizens of India and are residing at the address Flat No. 1401, Tower no.4 A, Suncity Parikrama, Sector 20, Panchkula, Haryana. The Aadhar cards of the complainants are annexed as ANNEXURE C  1 COLLY. The complainants are aggrieved persons who have given their hard earned money to IREO WATERFRONT situated at Sidhwan Canal Road, Off Ferozepur Road, Ludhiana, PUNJAB. They have booked a residential property having specification of villa type L bearing the no.567 at IREO WATERFRONT based on assurance and promises, which later on proved to be the false assurances and promises by the agents of the IREO Waterfront Pvt. Ltd. The definition of aggrieved person is, a person who is distressed or troubled. And in this case the complainants fall under the definition of the same primarily due to the false assurance and promises made by the OP, which will be elaborated in the following paragraphs.\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>2.	That the opposite party is a Company and has, at all material points of time, been and is still engaged in the commercial business of developing and selling commercial and housing projects flats and other construction layouts to various individuals and or others in lieu of valuable considerations for profit being their primary objective. \r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>3.	That the opposite Party is private limited company, incorporated under the Companies Act, 1956, having its office at addresses mentioned above, engaged in the business of developing and promoting constructed and under constructed residential areas.  That the OP Builder Company as part of their business venture decided to develop a Residential property IREO WATERFRONT in Sidhawan Canal Road, Off Ferozepur Road, Ludhiana, PUNJAB. The OP had published various web and news advertisements as well as visual advertisements to attract the public at large to purchase Residential property in the said project.</p>','<p class=\"normal\" style=\"line-height:200%\"><b><u><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Thorndale&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:Tahoma;mso-bidi-font-family:Tahoma;color:windowtext\">Relief\r\nSought<o:p></o:p></span></u></b></p><p class=\"normalCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:\r\n0cm;margin-left:36.0pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;mso-add-space:auto;text-align:\r\njustify;text-indent:-18.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Thorndale&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:Thorndale;mso-bidi-font-family:Thorndale;color:windowtext\">1.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Thorndale&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:Tahoma;\r\ncolor:windowtext\">To direct the OP to compensate the complainant in the shape\r\nof refund of the complete amount which has been deposited against the\r\nresidential property so booked by the complainant along with an Interest on the\r\namount from the date of deposit at the rate of 20 per cent till the actual\r\nrealization of the complete amount within 90 days according to section 18 1\r\nReal Estate Regulation And Development Act, 2016, 18 2 Real Estate Regulation\r\nAnd Development Act, 2016, Section 19 4 of The Real Estate Regulation And\r\nDevelopment Act, 2016, r w Rule 16 and Rule 17 of Punjab State Real Estate Regulation\r\nand Development Rules, 2017.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"normalCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:\r\n0cm;margin-left:36.0pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;mso-add-space:auto;text-align:\r\njustify;text-indent:-18.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Thorndale&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:Thorndale;mso-bidi-font-family:Thorndale;color:windowtext\">2.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Thorndale&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:Tahoma;\r\ncolor:windowtext\">To direct the Opposite party to reimburse litigation cost of\r\nRs Rs. 2,00,000 two lakhs to the complainants as they were constrained to file\r\nthe same because of the callous and indifferent attitude of the Opposite Party\r\nand the same has been handed over to the lawyer. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"normalCxSpLast\" style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:\r\n0cm;margin-left:36.0pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;mso-add-space:auto;text-align:\r\njustify;text-indent:-18.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Thorndale&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:Thorndale;mso-bidi-font-family:Thorndale;color:windowtext\">3.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Thorndale&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:Tahoma;\r\ncolor:windowtext\">Any other relief or claim which the Hon ble Authority deems\r\nappropriate.<o:p></o:p></span></p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Not Prayed</p>','1','','2014-12-17 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'lawofficeofhimanshuraj','2018-12-12 19:33:23.000','lawofficeofhimanshuraj','2018-12-12 19:33:23.000'),(518,1149,'1149',1066,'3568b05d-bd51-44d0-b387-09a3505b7441','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-13 13:42:05.000','GVStar Estates LLP LLP','ramsingh.dil@gmail.com',8699904514,0,0,'House no 726, Sector 2 Panchkula','',13,15,'134102','1','House no 2322 sector 66 mohali','',28,507,'160062','Neeraj Sobti','Advocatesobti@yahoo.co.in',9872279500,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PM0004','Falcon View , Phase-2 sector-66A, mohali','JANTA LAND PROMOTERS LTD','janta@jantahousing.com',8284045724,0,'SCO 39-42, sector 82','industrial area , mohali',28,507,'160062','1','SCO 39-42, sector 82','industrial area , mohali',28,507,'160062','1','<p>That applicant vide their application dated 02.04.2013 applied for an apartment and accordingly 4 BHK Apartment i.e. No. E-401, 4th Floor, wing E, Facing Green, Falcon View, Phase-II, (wrongly mentioned as Phase-I, the total sale consideration amount was fixed as Rs.1,08,25,200/-. Copy of allotment letter is Annexure C-1.\r\n</p><p>That as per the demands ,applicant paid the following amount to the respondents copies of all the receipts are Annexure C-2 to C-11\r\n</p><p>That as per Clause no.2.24 of the allotment letter dated 02.08.2013 (annexure C-1) the possession of the said apartment complete in all respects shall be delivered to the applicant by 01.02.2016, i.e. 30 months from the date of allotment letter i.e. 02.08.2013.\r\n</p><p>Reminder and postal receipts are Annexure C-12 to C-17. The applicant on 01.07.2018 took some photographs in his mobile showing the present incomplete status of the tower in which the flat of the applicant exist. Copies of the photographs are Annexure C-18 Colly.\r\n</p><p>The entire project of the respondents is illegal as the project without obtaining clearance from the environment and forest department as required under notification dated 14.09.2006 and the State Level Environment Impact Assessment Authority (SEIAA) had already initiated action against the respondent.\r\n</p><p>That earlier the complainant has filed a complaint before this Hon’ble court i.e. Complaint No. ADC/1007/2018, which was returned vide order dated 30.10.2018, with liberty to file fresh complaint on Form – M, copy of order is Annexure C-19. However during complaint the respondents have issued reply dated 24.08.2018, to the reminder notice of the complainant Annexure C-15, whereby the respondents have admitted the contents of notice and agreed to refund Rs.88,52,809/- to the complainant out of the total principal amount received. Copy of reply is Annexure C-20, The respondents are not legally entitled to deduct any amount. REF.- in CWP. No.13152 of 2014,&nbsp; the Hon’ble Punjab &amp; Haryan C-21.</p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\nline-height:97%\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:97%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:Times\">In view of the facts\r\nmentioned in paragraph 4 above, the complainant prays for the following\r\nrelief(s) <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif;\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif;\">That as\r\nthe respondents have failed to comply with the terms and conditions of the\r\nallotment letter dated 02.08.2013 (Annexure C-1) and have failed to deliver the\r\npossession of the apartment/flat within the stipulated time. Therefore, the\r\napplicant as per section 18 of the RERA Act. 2016, is entitled for<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.25in;text-align:justify;text-justify:\r\ninter-ideograph\"><b><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif;\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></b></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:8.0pt;\r\nmargin-left:.25in;text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;text-indent:\r\n-22.5pt;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif;\">i)<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif;\">Refund principal amount of Rs.</span><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif;\">10,580,830/- </span><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif;\">of the\r\napplicant </span><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif;\">along</span><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif;\"> with interest @ 18% P.a. from the date of actual payment till\r\nrealization. <b><o:p></o:p></b></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:8.0pt;\r\nmargin-left:.25in;text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;text-indent:\r\n-22.5pt;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif;\">ii)<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif;\">Pay compensation of Rs.5,00,000/- to the applicant for mental\r\nharassment, mental agony <b><o:p></o:p></b></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:8.0pt;\r\nmargin-left:.25in;text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;text-indent:\r\n-22.5pt;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif;\">iii)<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif;\