21','NH 21',28,507,'160055','1','<p>1.That the Respondents in the first instance, had launched a Group Housing Project in Mohali, Sector 121, Punjab, under the name and style of “ATS Casa Espana”.&nbsp; The complainant booked an apartment on 28.02.2014.&nbsp; In the interregnum, the Respondents had issued an Allotment Letter dated 20-06-2014 confirming the allotment of a Residential apartment No. 09062, on 6th floor of tower no.9 having super built up area of 222.97 sq.mtr equivalent to 2400 sq.feet, at sector 121 Mohali, Punjab(hereinafter referred to as the “Allotted Unit”).&nbsp; As per the recitals of the aforesaid agreement, the total sale consideration of the Allotted Unit was fixed at Rs. 99,50,000/- which is as per ‘schedule III’ of allotment letter. A statement showing the account status of the respondents reflecting the amount of plot is annexed as Annexure C/1 and Allotment Letter dated 20-06-2014 issued by the Respondents as ANNEXURE C/2.</p><p>2.That to the surprise of the complainant, the respondents had issued a demand letter demanding EDC charges dated 07.08.2018 to the tune of 487476/- and now more than 5 lakhs vide subsequent demand letters with interest. It is pertinent to mention here that the EDC charges were promised to be paid by the respondents including change in EDC charges (if any) as already included in the total sale consideration i.e 99,50,000/- and hence, they were specifically deleted from the SCHEDULE III of the Allotment Letter Dated 20.06.2014, so that there is no confusion afterwards. Schedule III is appended with the allotment letter annexed as ANNEXURE C/2 and demand letters are annexed as ANNEXURE C/3.&nbsp;</p><p>3. That even as per the trecitals of the allotment letter Annexure C/2, clause 4.1 \"The entire consideration payable by the buyer, towards the absolute purchase of the apartment along with exclusive right to use and occupy the car park space in terms of this agreement, shall be the \'Total Amount Payable\' as mentioned in Schedule III thereto.\" Hence demands for EDC again is unlawful.</p><p><br></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\">﻿﻿<span style=\"font-family:&quot;roboto&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">That in view of the\r\nfacts and circumstances of the case detailed hereinabove, the Respondent on account\r\nof &nbsp;being deficient in rendering services\r\nto the Complainant and by virtue of having adopting unfair trade practices and\r\nas such, this Hon’ble Authority may be pleased to allow the above mentioned\r\ncomplaint as under:- <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;roboto&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">1.To restrain the\r\nRespondent from demanding the EDC Charges which has already been paid by the\r\nComplainant.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;roboto&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">2.To order the\r\nRespondent from raising any other arbitrary demands and charges which the\r\nComplainant has already paid.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;roboto&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">It is, therefore,\r\nrespectfully prayed that in the light of the facts and circumstances detailed\r\nhereinabove, the instant complaint may kindly be allowed and the relief, as\r\nprayed for in the forgoing paragraph of the instant complaint, may kindly be\r\nawarded in favor of the Complainant and against the Respondent in the interests\r\nof justice, equity and good conscience.</span></p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Notice of motion be issued to the Respondents and stay in favour of the Complainant against the respondent for EDC charges Demands because an interest on the EDC charges are being added in the demand of EDC charges.<br></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'amit.heman@gmail.com','2018-12-16 20:05:59.000','amit.heman@gmail.com','2018-12-16 20:05:59.000'),(534,1189,'1189',1247,'79ebe