nfusion afterwards. Schedule III is appended with the allotment letter annexed as ANNEXURE C/1 and demand letters are annexed as ANNEXURE C/3.&nbsp;</p><p>3. That even as per the recitals of the allotment letter Annexure C/1, clause 4.1 \"The entire consideration payable by the buyer, towards the absolute purchase of the apartment along with exclusive right to use and occupy the car park space in terms of this agreement, shall be the \'Total Amount Payable\' as mentioned in Schedule III thereto.\" Hence demands for EDC again is unlawful.</p><p><br></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\">﻿﻿<span style=\"font-family:&quot;roboto&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">That in view of the\r\nfacts and circumstances of the case detailed hereinabove, the Respondent on account\r\nof &nbsp;being deficient in rendering services\r\nto the Complainant and by virtue of having adopting unfair trade practices and\r\nas such, this Hon’ble Authority may be pleased to allow the above mentioned\r\ncomplaint as under:- <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;roboto&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">1.To restrain the\r\nRespondent from demanding the EDC Charges which has already been paid by the\r\nComplainant.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;roboto&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">2.To order the\r\nRespondent from raising any other arbitrary demands and charges which the\r\nComplainant has already paid.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;roboto&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">It is, therefore,\r\nrespectfully prayed that in the light of the facts and circumstances detailed\r\nhereinabove, the instant complaint may kindly be allowed and the relief, as\r\nprayed for in the forgoing paragraph of the instant complaint, may kindly be\r\nawarded in favor of the Complainant and against the Respondent in the interests\r\nof justice, equity and good conscience.</span></p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Notice of motion be issued to the Respondents and stay in favour of the Complainant against the respondent for EDC charges Demands because an interest on the EDC charges are being added in the demand of EDC charges.<br></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'amit.heman@gmail.com','2018-12-16 20:11:35.000','amit.heman@gmail.com','2018-12-16 20:11:35.000'),(535,1190,'1190',1256,'d72e4c4b-b5ec-4480-ad45-a996edad35da','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-18 08:37:30.000','SANJAY NEGI','sanket.dhall@gmail.com',9888159159,0,0,'HOUSE NO 630,PANCHKULA HEIGHTS','PEER MUCHALLA ROAD DHAKAULI ZIRAKPUR',28,507,'140603','1','163 SUNNY ENCLAVE ','ZIRAKPUR',28,507,'160055','SANKET DHALL','sanketdhall@gmail.com',9888159159,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0242','CASA HOMES BY FUTURE CITY DEVELOPERS PVT LTD','BHOLA RAM GOYAL','casahomes2016@gmail.com',8128881288,0,'FUTURE CITY DEVELOPERS PVT LTD,AMARI HEIGHTS','SECTOR-115 KHARAR LANDRAN ROAD MOHALI',28,507,'160055','1','FUTURE CITY DEVELOPERS PVT LTD,AMARI HEIGHTS','SECTOR-115 KHARAR LANDRAN ROAD MOHALI',28,507,'160055','1','<p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">THAT THE COMPLAINANT BOOKED AN APARTMENT AT CASA HOMES A&nbsp; PROJECT WITH FUTURE CITY DEVELOPERS AT SECTOR 115 KHARAR LANDRAN ROAD MOHALI, VIDE AGREEMENT TO SELL DATED 23-12-2017 AND ALLOTMENT LETTER DATED 5-4-2018 IN WHICH THE RESPONDENT HAS PROMISED THE COMPLAINANT THAT HE WILL DELIVER THE POSSESSION OF THE FLAT IN JUNE 2018 AND IF NOT POSSIBLE IN JUNE DUE TO NATURAL CALAMINITY THEN THE POSSESSION WILL BE GIVEN ON OCTOBER 2018,BUT TILL DATE RESPONDENT HAS NOT HANDED OVER THE POSSESSION TO THE COMPLAINANT BECAUSE THE WORK IN THE CASA HOMES PROJECT HAS&nbsp; NOT BEEN COMPLETED AS YET,THEREFORE THE SAID POSSESSION HAS NOT BEEN HANDED OVER AS YET,TO SEE THE DEVELOPMENT WORK AT THE SITE, PHOTOGRAPHS OF THE PROJECT AND MY APARTMENT HAS BEEN ANNEXED WITH THE COMPLAINT.THE TOTAL COST OF THE APARTMENT IS 31,80,800/- AND THE COMPLAINANT HAS PAID RUPEES 190,8480/- LAKH TILL DATE TO THE RESPONDENT VIDE RECEIPT NOS 232 AND 257 DATED 21-4-18 AND 14-5-18.THAT THE COMPLAINANT IS READY TO PAY THE PENDING AMOUNT ALSO BUT THE PROJECT IS NOT READY AND THE MONEY THE COMPLAINANT HAS ALREADY PAID TO THE RESPONDENT IS ALL WASTED BECAUSE THE SAID PROJECT IS NOT READY AND RTESPONDENT IS MAKING FOOL OF THE RESPONDENT A DAY AND THE OTHER. AS IT IS THE HARD EARNED MONEY OF THE COMPLAINANT BECAUSE HE IS DOING A PRIVATE JOB AND HAS TAKEN LOAN FROM THE FINANCE COMPANY AMOUNTING TO RS 31,00,000/-,AND PAYING MONTHLY INSTALLEMENTS TO THE LOAN AGENCY FROM HIS HARD EARNED MONEY BUT THE RESPONDENT IS PLAYING WITH THE HARD EARNED MONEY OF THE COMPLAINANT AND DID NOT DELIVER THE POSSESSION&nbsp; TO THE COMPLAINANT TILL DATE. IT IS THEREFORE PRAYED TAHT KINDLY LOOK INTO THE MATTER IN THE INTEREST OF JUSTICE.</span><br></p>','<p>TO REFUND THE AMOUNT OF RS 1908480/-ALONG WITH INTEREST @24% P.A FROM THE DATE OF BOOKING OF THE SAID FLAT.</p>',3180800.00,1908480.00,'2018-06-30 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>N/A</p>','1','','2018-04-05 00:00:00','2018-12-23 00:00:00','CASA HOMES  F-4,TOWER-F4 ,SECTOR-115,KHARAR LANDRAN ROAD MOHALI','','',2,0,0,0,'sanket.dhall','2018-12-17 13:42:59.000','sanket.dhall','2018-12-17 13:42:59.000'),(536,1145,'1145',1112,'29af80b1-85ed-4b88-8344-b429d2f24eca','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-17 17:43:47.000','Pebam Sudesh','savindersinghgill@gmail.com',9988861126,0,0,'H.No. 206 C, New Type-5','PGI Flats, Sector 24-A',6,128,'160023','1','H.No. 206 C, New Type-5','PGI Flats, Sector 24-A',6,128,'160023','Savinder Singh Gill','savindersinghgill@gmail.com',9988861126,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0093','THE PALM','MANOHAR INFRASTRUCTURE AND CONSTRUCTIONS PRIVATE LIMITED','nbs@manoharrealty.com',0,0,'SCO 139-141','SECTOR 17-C',6,128,'160017','1','SCO 139-141','SECTOR 17-C',6,128,'160017','1','<p><span style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 115%; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">The\r\napplicants on 29.02.2012 booked (C-1) a 250 sq yards plot @ RS.17500/- per sq\r\nyd (excluding EDC &amp; PLC) from the respondent in the project Palm Garden,\r\nMullanpur, Mohali. It was assured by the respondent that it has received all\r\nthe approvals except one or two which will be obtained within 2-3 months and\r\nthe possession of the plot will be delivered in 2 years. The applicant paid Rs.\r\n1312500 i.e. 30% of total sale consideration along with the application. The applicants\r\nvisited the office of the respondent and asked for allotment letter and buyer’s\r\nagreement, but the respondent insisted on more payment. It was only after a lot\r\nof persuasion that on confirmation of allotment letter (C-3) of plot no. 1370\r\nwas issued. Plot Buyer’s Agreement (C-4) executed between the applicants and\r\nrespondent on 28.04.2017, whereby even the area and the price was increased and\r\nthe applicants were not left with an option to protest as the respondent\r\nthreatened them about forfeiture of their money. The applicants have availed\r\nloan of Rs. 3062500 from HDFC Ltd. (C-5). The applicants have made a payment of Rs. 4677500 to the respondent (C-2 (colly.). The respondent\r\nhas misrepresented the applicants since beginning and never informed them about the true picture of the\r\napprovals and the development. It had not even applied the permissions when the plot was sold to the\r\napplicants. A list of approvals and main agreement are attached as C-6 and C-7. The agreement executed by the respondent is also not as per the RERA Act. The applicants had earlier filed consumer complaint no. 270 of 2018 and the same was withdrawn with liberty to avail any other remedy available as per law (C-8).</span><br></p>','<p>(i) Directing the respondent to refund the principal amount i.e. Rs. 4677500/- as per Section 18\r\nof RERA along with interest to be calculated at the rate as contemplated under rule 16 of The Punjab\r\nState Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Rules, 2017, as the applicants have lost faith in the\r\nrespondent due to misrepresentation by it about the approvals and stages of development during all these\r\nyears and thus the applicants wish to withdraw from the project. Also the respondent has committed violation of various provisions of\r\nPAPRA and conditions of various approvals granted to it, as it could not collect any amount till the\r\nexemption is received under Section 44 of PAPRA which was received on 25.01.2017. The respondent\r\ncollected the money from the applicants in 2012. The approvals were granted to the respondent on the\r\nground that it will not sell any land/plot/space and collect money from the general public till exemption\r\nunder Section 44 of PAPRA is received. Also, inspite of receiving 50% of sale consideration the\r\nrespondent did not execute any sale agreement&nbsp; and the same was executed afeter a delay of more than 5 years and after having received more than 65% of the sale consideration. (ii) Directing the respondent to pay the compensation of Rs.10 lacs for deficiency in services, unfair trade practices &amp; harassment caused to the complainant &amp; for using their hard earned money for such a long period. (iii) Directing the respondent to pay litigation expenses to the tune of Rs. 50000/-. (iv) To take action against respondent under Section 61 of RERA for constant violation of provision of Section 13 of RERA as the respondent failed to issue any allotment letter &amp; execute the buyer’s agreement on time. For cancelling the extension granted to the respondent for constantly violating various provisions of RERA and for indulging into unfair trade practices and further cancelling the main registration of the respondent under RERA.</p>',5948405.00,4677500.00,'2019-09-06 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>The respondent be directed to provide the list of allottees to whom it has allotted/sold the 862 residential plots as per the layout plan approved by GMADA on 6.10.2015. The respondent has been duly registered under RERA for the said approved layout plan. As per the said approved layout plan, the respondent can sell 862 residential plots and 73 commercial plots/spaces.The respondent be directed to provide the list of hypothecated plots ,which are hypothecated to GMADA, out of the said approved 862 residential and 73 commercial plotsThe respondent be directed to provide the list of hypothected plots already allotted/sold to general public.The respondent be directed to provide the details of funds collected from the general public since 2010 in lieu of the said approved 862 residential plots which are part of approved layout plan and for which the respondent is duly registered under Section 3 of RERA and also, the detail where such amount has been utilized by the respondentThe respondent be directed to provide all the bank details where such amount has been deposited along with the statement of accounts since the year 2010. The respondent be directed to provide the details in respect of number of bookings made by the respondent since the year 2010 for the said 862 residential plots.&nbsp;</p>','1','','2017-03-07 00:00:00','2017-04-28 00:00:00','1370','','',1,1,0,0,'BeeG','2018-12-17 17:24:55.000','BeeG','2018-12-17 17:24:55.000'),(537,1150,'1150',1229,'6166bf56-8baf-4aa7-a05e-6b75f196cc86','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-11-28 20:02:18.000','Ranveer  Sharma','advamitgoyal@hotmail.com',9527700001,0,0,'1003-B, Sterling Seaface, Annie Besant Road, ','Near Poonam Chambers, Worli',21,400,'400018','1','1003-B, Sterling Seaface, Annie Besant Road, ','Near Poonam Chambers, Worli',21,400,'400018','Amit Goyal','advamitgoyal@hotmail.com',9527700001,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0143','Parkwood Glade Tower C ','Parkwood Depelopers Pvt. Ltd.','mail@parkwoodgroup.in',0,1130324952,'M/s Parkwood Developers Pvt. Ltd. ','1001, Hemkunt Chambers, 89 Nehru Place,',10,429,'110019','1','M/s Parkwood Developers Pvt. Ltd. ','1001, Hemkunt Chambers, 89 Nehru Place,',10,429,'110019','1','\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<ol><li style=\"margin: 0cm 0cm 10pt 36pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-ansi-language:EN-US\">Respondents\r\ngave various advertisements &amp; showed a rosy picture about the project.\r\nComplainants relied heavily on these representations &amp;</span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;color:#1A1A1A\"> entered\r\ninto agreement dated 08.12.12 <b>(Annexure C-1)</b> with Respondents for total\r\nconsideration of Rs. </span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">49,97475 for </span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;color:#1A1A1A\">Flat No. C003 Tower C with\r\nSuper Built up Area 1725 sqft.</span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\"> </span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;color:#1A1A1A\">Possession was to be delivered latest by\r\n30.06.15 (clause 19 (a))</span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">.</span></li><li style=\"margin-left: 36pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;color:#1A1A1A\">Complainants\r\nmade initial payment of 300000 (para 6a of agreement). Thereafter payments were\r\nmade as per the demand notes from time to time between Dec 12 &amp; Nov 13.</span></li><li style=\"margin-left: 36pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;color:#1A1A1A\">Next demand\r\nnote was raised by respondent in Feb 16 i.e. after 26 months. Complainants\r\nqueried the Promoter on the status of the project and reminded that in their\r\nprevious site visit </span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n200%;color:#212121\">they found work running&nbsp;behind schedule &amp; therefore\r\nPromoter had no right to raise demand.</span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:\r\n14.0pt;line-height:200%;color:#1A1A1A\"> Complainants sought relevant documents\r\nconfirming progress of work. No response was received.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"margin-left: 36pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;color:#1A1A1A\">Respondent raised\r\nanother demand on 05.04.17 <b>(Annexure C2)</b>. Complainants again queried the\r\nPromoter vide email dated 10.04.17 <b>(Annexure C3)</b> on project progress</span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;color:#212121\">.&nbsp;No\r\nresponse was received. </span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;color:#1A1A1A;mso-bidi-font-style:italic\">This demand note also\r\nsummarised all payments made by Complainants.</span></li><li style=\"margin-left: 36pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;color:#1A1A1A\">Complainants\r\nvisited site in July 17 and again found no progress. Reminder sent to the\r\nPromoter on 01.08.18. Respondents assured they will inform within week but\r\ndidn’t respond despite reminders.</span></li><li style=\"margin-left: 36pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;color:#1A1A1A\">Complainants\r\nlost confidence in the Promoter and in its ability to provide flat within\r\nstipulated time. Complainants therefore sent letter dated 12.03.18 seeking\r\nrefund with interest. Reminder also sent on 12.04.18 <b>(C-4). </b>Promoter\r\ndidn’t respond.</span></li><li style=\"margin-left: 36pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\nCalibri;mso-bidi-font-family:Raavi\">Given the construction status &amp; snail’s\r\npace of work, it is impossible that </span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:\r\n14.0pt;line-height:200%\">respondents</span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:\r\n14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-fareast-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-font-family:\r\nRaavi\"> will deliver possession in near future. T</span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%\">ill date</span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-fareast-font-family:Calibri;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:Raavi\"> no substantial work has been done on site. Actual\r\nvisit will show that only structure has been built (usual practice of all\r\nbuilders). Photographs depicting work as in Nov, 18 are annexed as <b>C-</b></span><b><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%\">5</span></b><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\nCalibri;mso-bidi-font-family:Raavi\">.</span><a name=\"_GoBack\"></a><b><i><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;color:#1A1A1A\"><o:p></o:p></span></i></b></li></ol>','\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<ol><li style=\"margin-left: 18pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;color:#1A1A1A\">Refund of\r\nthe Principal amount paid to date to the Promoter ie INR 42,77,666/-.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"margin: 10pt 0cm 10pt 18pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%\">As per </span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\nCalibri\">clause 2(a) of agreement respondents are charging interest @18% p.a.\r\non account of delay in payment.</span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"> Therefore complainants be also awarded interest at the same\r\nrate-&nbsp;</span>Or- </li><li style=\"margin: 10pt 0cm 10pt 18pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\">Interest as\r\nprovided under <span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">Section 18 and 19(4) of the RERA Act r/w </span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; color: rgb(26, 26, 26);\">Rule 16 of\r\nthe Regulation and Development Rules 2017 on the above Principal amount from\r\nthe respective dates it was paid to the respondent till the date of payment ie\r\nState Bank of India’s (“SBI”) highest Marginal Cost of Lending Rate (“MCLR”)\r\nplus 2%. The current SBI MCLR is 8.50% pa so applicable interest rate for the\r\nrefund is taken as 10.50% pa..</span></li><li style=\"margin-left: 18pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;color:#1A1A1A\">Direct the\r\nrespondent to repay to the complainants the expenses directly incurred by the\r\nComplainants in filing the RERA application ie </span>Litigation\r\nexpenses– for representing the Complainants before this Ld. Authority ie INR\r\n55,000 <b style=\"color: rgb(26, 26, 26); font-size: 14pt;\">(Annexure C-6)</b></li><li style=\"margin: 0cm 0cm 10pt 18pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;color:#1A1A1A\">Compensation for Mental\r\nharassment to the tune of Rs. 1,00,000/- </span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-ansi-language:EN-US\"><o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"margin: 0cm 0cm 10pt 18pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-ansi-language:EN-US\">To impose\r\npenalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 61 of RERA Act\r\nfor contravention of Sections 11(3)(b) and 18 of the RERA Act.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"margin: 0cm 0cm 10pt 18pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-ansi-language:EN-US\">To issue\r\ndirections to make liable every officer concerned i.e. Director, Manager,\r\nSecretary, or any other officer of the respondent’s company at whose instance,\r\nconnivance, acquiescence, neglect any of the offences has been committed as\r\nmentioned in Sec. 69 of RERA Act, 2016 read with Punjab RERA Rules, 2017.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"margin: 0cm 0cm 10pt 18pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-ansi-language:EN-US\">To recommend\r\ncriminal action against the respondents for the criminal offence of cheating,\r\nfraud and criminal breach of trust under section 420, 406 and 409 of the Indian\r\nPenal Code.</span></li><li style=\"margin: 0cm 0cm 10pt 18pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-ansi-language:EN-US\">Any other\r\nrelief which this Hon’ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of the\r\nfacts and circumstances of this complaint.<o:p></o:p></span></li></ol><ol></ol>',4997475.00,4277666.00,'2015-06-30 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:10.0pt;text-align:justify;line-height:\r\n200%\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-ansi-language:\r\nEN-US\">No interim relief is being sought. The complainants only pray that the\r\npromoters be directed to return the amount paid with interest.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','2012-12-08 00:00:00','Village Santemajra, Tehsil Kharar, District S.A.S. Nagar,  Punjab','','',2,0,0,0,'Ranveerneha','2018-12-17 19:16:40.000','Ranveerneha','2018-12-17 19:16:40.000'),(538,1150,'1150',1229,'6166bf56-8baf-4aa7-a05e-6b75f196cc86','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-18 09:43:47.000','Ranveer  Sharma','advamitgoyal@hotmail.com',9527700001,0,0,'1003-B, Sterling Seaface, Annie Besant Road, ','Near Poonam Chambers, Worli',21,400,'400018','1','1003-B, Sterling Seaface, Annie Besa