and for seeking refund of the principal amount paid by the Applicant in respect of the Allotted Unit alongwith interest. Till date,however, the aforesaid demand raised by the Applicant has not been acceded to by the Respondent and thus, vide the instant complaint, the Applicants seek refund of the monies paid by him to the Respondent alongwith interest and compensation.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>x) In spite of the fact that the Applicant had sought refund of the principal amount paid by the Applicants alongwith interest, the Respondents have arbitrarily continued to issue Demand Notices to the Applicant for payment of instalments as per the payment schedule.</p>','<p>i) Refund of an amount of Rs. 86,41,522/- paid by the Applicants alongwith interest (highest marginal cost of lending rate of the State Bank of India + 2%) from the respective dates of deposit till actual realization as per Sections 18 and 19(4) of the Act read with Rule 16 of the Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017.</p><p>ii) Any other relief which the Applicants are entitled for under the Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Act, 2016 and the Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017.&nbsp;</p><div><br></div>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>N.A.</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'Ranjeevrai','2018-12-19 16:04:35.000','Ranjeevrai','2018-12-19 16:04:35.000'),(566,1192,'1192',1254,'f975078e-bd45-46ae-9ad3-968463b14972','FormTypeM',1,1,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Ranjeev  Rai','gaurav.chopra@hotmail.com',9814013127,0,0,'House No. 607','sector 18B',6,128,'160018','1','House No. 607','sector 18B',6,128,'160018','Gaurav Chopra','gaurav.chopra@hotmail.com',9814013127,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0119','Mohali Hills','M/s. EMAAR MGF Land Ltd','sorabh.kakkar@emmarmgf.in',0,0,'EMAAR MGF Land Ltd','40, Ground Floor, Central Plaza, Sector 105',28,507,'140306','1','EMAAR MGF Land Ltd','40, Ground Floor, Central Plaza, Sector 105',28,507,'140306','1','<p>i) Applicant: Ranjeev Singh Rai (name incorrectly stated as Rajeev Singh Rai)&nbsp;</p><p>ii) Application:14.3.2007&nbsp;</p><p>iii) Buyer’s Agreement:1.9.2009&nbsp;</p><p>iv) Construction Linked Installment Plan for total Consideration:Rs. 99,15,199</p><p>v) Amount paid till 21.8.2012:Rs. 86,41,522/-</p><p>vi) As per Clause 21.1 of the Apartment Buyer’s Agreement, the Respondent was under a contractual obligation to handover possession of the Allotted Unit within a period of 36 months from the date of allotment with a further relaxation of 90 days over and above the stipulated time period for the purpose of applying for and obtaining an Occupation Certificate in respect of the Group Housing Complex.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>vii) Date of Possession as per Clause 21.1 of the Agreement r/w Clause 23.1:on or before 1.12.2012.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>viii) Till date, however, despite a lapse of more than 6 years, possession of the Allotted Unit has neither been offered nor handed over to the Applicants and this wilful omission and lapse on the part of the Respondent constitutes a wilful and material breach of the Agreement executed between the parties.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>ix) Aggrieved by the aforesaid omission of the Respondent,the Applicant had written a letter/e-mail dated 9.2.2017 to the Respondent for rescinding the contract and for seeking refund of the principal amount paid by the Applicant in respect of the Allotted Unit alongwith interest. Till date,however, the aforesaid demand raised by the Applicant has not been acceded to by the Respondent and thus, vide the instant complaint, the Applicants seek refund of the monies paid by him to the Respondent alongwith interest and compensation.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>x) In spite of the fact that the Applicant had sought refund of the principal amount paid by the Applicants alongwith interest, the Respondents have arbitrarily continued to issue Demand Notices to the Applicant for payment of instalments as per the payment schedule.</p>','<p>i) Refund of an amount of Rs. 86,41,522/- paid by the Applicants alongwith interest (highest marginal cost of lending rate of the State Bank of India + 2%) from the respective dates of deposit till actual realization as per Sections 18 and 19(4) of the Act read with Rule 16 of the Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017.</p><p>ii) Any other relief which the Applicants are entitled for under the Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Act, 2016 and the Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017.&nbsp;</p><div><br></div>',9915199.00,8641522.00,'2012-12-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>N.A.</p>','1','','2007-03-14 00:00:00','2009-09-01 00:00:00','H3 FPH PH04, TOWER H, THE VIEWS AT MOHALLI HILLS','','',2,0,0,0,'Ranjeevrai','2018-12-19 16:09:21.000','Ranjeevrai','2018-12-19 16:09:21.000'),(567,1152,'1152',1173,'dd2e0667-81c8-4893-b732-43ed1d145484','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-19 16:40:46.000','Atul Mehan','csvedparkash@gmail.com',9815075066,0,0,'Flat No. 1172, Pushpac Society','Sector-49 B, Chandigarh',6,128,'160047','1','Flat No. 1172, Pushpac Society','Sector-49 B, Chandigarh',6,128,'160047','Ved Parkash','csvedparkash@gmail.com',7837223098,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0124','Acme Eden Court','Acme Builders Pvt. Ltd.','contact@acmebuilders.in',8699174000,1724569000,'GH-10, Sector-91','JLPL, Mohali',28,507,'160071','1','GH-10, Sector-91','JLPL, Mohali',28,507,'160071','1','<ul><li>CONCISE STATEMENT OF FACTS AND GROUNDS OF COMPLAINT&nbsp; That the original layout plan of the Äcme Eden Court” is attached at Annexure I.That the applicant booked an apartment in the year 2010 with the respondent&nbsp; vide application for&nbsp; unit No 103, Floor 1, Tower 2 having an approximate super area of 2330 sq.ft. and paid an amount of Rs. 1,00,000/- towards booking amount as per payment receipt attached as Annexure II.The the applicant made additional payment of Rs. 18,00,000/- on 02.04.2013 vide payment receipt attached as Annexure III. The allotment letter was issued to the applicant as attached at Annexure IV. That the respondent signed Builder Buyer Agreement with the applicant on 05.04.2013 attached at Annexure V. The total consideration of the allotted unit was fixed at Rs. 7381250/- and the payment plan was defined in Plan-C of Schedule I referred in clause 2 of the agreement. That despite no progress on construction work at project site, the applicant made payments as requested as per payment receipts dated 5.11.2015 attached as Annexure VI for PLC charges of Rs. 728125 plus service tax and Annexure VII towards construction work of 10% of BSP amounting to Rs. 5,23,169/- plus service tax, That the applicant again cooperated with the respondent and in the hope of getting early possession of the allotted unit, paid additional amount of Rs 22,50,000/- including service tax on 3rd July 2015 as per payment receipts attached at Annexure VIII.The respondent immediately on receipt of 80% of the amount of BSP, sent a reminder on 7th July, 2015 asking for balance payment of BSP, PLC and even the amount payable at the time of possession as attached at Annexed IX which was later kept in abeyance.Thus a total of Rs. 55,50,000/- including service tax of Rs 2,24,793/- has been paid by the applicant up to 03.07.2015. The possession was to be offered on 1.04.2016. The project is registered with PBRERA-SAS81-PR0124. The applicant wishes to withdraw from the project.</li></ul>','<div><br></div><ul><li>In view of the points above, it is clearly established that the respondent has violated the provisions of Section 12, 14, 18 &amp; 19 of Real Estate (Development &amp; Regulations) Act, 2016.</li><li>It, is therefore, humbly prayed that the Hon’ble Adjudicating Officer may consider our submissions and order the respondent to refund our total amount of Rs. 55,50,000/- along with interest as per RERA provisions from the respective dates of payments made to the respondent.</li><li><br></li><li>Place&nbsp;</li><li>Date 28.11.2018<span style=\"white-space:pre\">								</span>Signatures of Atul Mehan</li><li><br></li><li><br></li><li>Through&nbsp;</li><li>Authorized Representative</li><li><br></li><li>(Ved Parkash)</li><li>CS in Practice</li></ul>',7381250.00,5550000.00,'2016-04-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>NA</p>','1','','2013-04-02 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Flat No. 103, Tower-2, First Floor, Acme Eden Court, GH-10, Sector-91, JPL, Mohali','','',1,1,0,0,'atulmehan','2018-12-19 16:40:38.000','atulmehan','2018-12-19 16:40:38.000'),(568,1199,'1199',1284,'354f8531-7e8c-420b-8e3f-36306084d8dc','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Saurabh Sharma','saurabh11nov@gmail.com',9815578420,0,0,'House No 1501, First Floor, ','Phase-10, Mohali',28,507,'160062','1','HOUSE NO 1501 FIRST FLOOR','PHASE 10, Mohali',28,507,'160062','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0090','Sandwoods Infratech Projects Pvt. Ltd.','SK Baagolia','info@sandwoods.com',9501050944,1724634870,'Sandwoods Infratech Projects Pvt. Ltd. (Head Office)','SCO: 222-223 Sector 34-A,',6,128,'160022','1','Sandwoods Infratech Projects Pvt. Ltd. (Head Office)','SCO: 222-223 Sector 34-A,',6,128,'160022','1','<p>Dear Sir,</p><p>We have purchased the flat from Sandwoods Infratech Projects Pvt. Ltd. in the year Nov. 2014 &amp; made the agreement on 26th of Nov. 2014. The details of the apartment are Tower: D3, Apartment No. 109, Floor - 4th, Super Area : 1325 Sq. ft and the basic sale price is Rs. 40,28, 000. The service tax, preferred location charges, Club membership, power backup etc are extra to the basic amount. It was agreed at the time of purchase that Sanwoods will pay the bank loan interest amount until the possession of the apartment</p>','tttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttt',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>ttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttttt</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',1,0,0,0,'Saurabh11nov','2018-12-19 16:47:06.000','Saurabh11nov','2018-12-19 16:47:06.000'),(569,1200,'1200',1272,'51d11184-3a8e-4a16-9673-559a2472f6c0','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-19 17:06:28.000','Rajesh Verma','rajfine123@gmail.com',9991203671,0,0,'Flat no 515 tower b4 The Eminence','Zirakpur, distt s.a.s. nagar',28,507,'140603','1','Dena bank dera bassi','Ambala Chandigarh highway,dera bassi',28,507,'140507','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0396','SUSHMA VALENCIA','SUKSHA DEVELOPERS PVT. LTD.','ankitg@sushmabuildtech.com',0,0,'unit no b-107 business complex at elante mall,first floor','ind. area, phase 1,chandigarh 160009',6,128,'160009','1','unit no b-107 business complex at elante mall,first floor','ind. area, phase 1,chandigarh 160009',6,128,'160009','0','<p>&nbsp;</p><div>\r\n<p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; font-family: roboto; font-size: 14px;\">I have \r\nbooked a flat in feb 2018 in sushma valencia( builder name is SUKSHA DEVELOPERS \r\nPVT. LTD, PBRERA-SAS80-PR0396) at price 62 lakh for which i have paid rs. 620000 \r\nto builder through cheques . I have requested them several times to issue me \r\nreceipts but every time neither they issued receipts nor done any agreement with \r\nme..........After a lot of harassment, i have decided to cancel the flat.for \r\ncancellation, builder issued me their own proforma for flat cancellation. I have \r\nsubmitted the affidavit with clauses (i),(ii) &amp; (iii), but they tampered \r\nthis affidavit and inserted clause (iv) to grab my hard earned money.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; font-family: roboto; font-size: 14px;\">They have \r\nrefunded me rs. 525424/- and refused to pay remaining rs. 94576/- which is \r\ncompletely illegal and lawful...without receipts, without agreement,they should \r\nnot deduct .</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; font-family: roboto; font-size: 14px;\">Please Please&nbsp;\r\nprovide me justice so that i can recover my hard earned money from builder.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; font-family: roboto; font-size: 14px;\">Thanks and \r\nregards.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; font-family: roboto; font-size: 14px;\">Rajesh \r\nverma</p></div>','<p>&nbsp;1. My pending amount 94576 rs.</p><p>2. interest of rs. 620000 which builder has used for more than 8 months till now</p><p>3. mental harassment charges.</p><p>4. legal notice fee 2000 rs.&nbsp;</p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>&nbsp;mentioned in point 5.</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'RAJESHVERMA3671','2018-12-19 16:56:55.000','RAJESHVERMA3671','2018-12-19 16:56:55.000'),(570,1201,'1201',1286,'d5cccd55-ed50-4972-b984-310c180b5690','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Narwar Singh Bhogal','kashika.juneja91@gmail.com',9814013127,0,0,'House No. 607','sector 18B',6,128,'160018','1','House No. 607','sector 18B',6,128,'160018','Gaurav Chopra','gaurav.chopra@hotmail.com',9814013127,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0119','MOHALI HILLS','M/s EMAAR MGF LAND LIMITED','sorabh.kakar@emaarmgf.com',0,0,'M/s. Emaar MGF Land Limited, Office No. 40, Central Plaza, Sector 105','',28,507,'140306','1','M/s. Emaar MGF Land Limited, Office No. 40, Central Plaza, Sector 105','',28,507,'140306','1','<p>i)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Applicants: Narwar Singh Bhogal and Mrs Ajit Kaur Bhogal had</p><p>ii)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Application form: 22.2.2008&nbsp;</p><p>iii)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Allotment Letter: 11.3.2008&nbsp;</p><p>iv)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Buyer’s Agreement: 31.3.2008</p><p>iv)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Vide a letter dated 2.7.2008, the allotted unit, as aforesaid, was changed to TVM-L3-F10-1003&nbsp;</p><p>v)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Total sale price: Rs. 57,01,543/-.&nbsp;</p><p>vi)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Amendment Agreement: 2.12.2013, the Respondent had allotted an alternate unit TVM-L1-F11-1102 ad measuring 1930 sq ft in “The Views” at Mohali Hills in Sector-105, SAS Nagar, District Mohali, Punjab instead of the earlier allotted unit TVM-L3-F10-1003</p><p>vii)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Total sale consideration (revised): Rs. 64,22,558.30/-&nbsp;</p><p>viii)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Co-Applicant i.e. Mrs Ajit Kaur Bhogal has passed away on 7.12.2017 and prior to her death she had executed a registered will dated 22.3.2011 bequeathing her share in the allotted unit to the Applicant.&nbsp;</p><p>ix)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Construction Linked Instalment Plan&nbsp;</p><p>x)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Amount paid upto 8.3.2018: Rs. 66,50,108.51/-&nbsp;</p><p>xi)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That Clause 21.1 of the Agreement read with Clause 23.1 made it abundantly clear that time was the essence of the contract and hence, possession of the Allotted Unit was required to be handed over to the Applicant by the Respondent positively on or before 11.6.2011.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>xii)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Aggrieved by the aforesaid omission and lapse of the Respondent, the Applicant had written a letter/e-mail dated 5.4.2018 to the Respondent for seeking refund of the principal amount paid by the Applicant in respect of the Allotted Unit alongwith interest. The Respondent upon receiving the aforesaid Email/letter, sent a reply dated 13.4.2018 declining the request of the Applicant for refund of the amount paid in respect of the allotted unit. Thus, vide the instant complaint, the Applicant seeks refund of the monies paid by him to the Respondent alongwith interest.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><br></p>','<p>i)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Refund of an amount of Rs. 66,50,108.51/- paid by the Applicant alongwith interest (highest marginal cost of lending rate of the State Bank of India + 2%) from the respective dates of deposit till actual realization as per Sections 18 and 19(4) of the Act read with Rule 16 of the Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017.</p><p>ii)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Any other relief which the Applicant is entitled for under the Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Act, 2016 and the Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p>',6422558.30,6650108.51,'2011-06-11 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','..','1','','2008-03-11 00:00:00','2008-03-31 00:00:00','UNIT NO. TVM L1 F11 1102 \"The Views\" at Mohali Hills','','',2,0,0,0,'Narwarbhogal','2018-12-19 17:01:56.000','Narwarbhogal','2018-12-19 17:01:56.000'),(571,1195,'1195',1285,'16c97337-63b6-4d1f-93b2-1a78bf3f4367','FormTypeM',1,1,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Parshottam Dhillon','gaurav.chopra@hotmail.com',9814013127,0,0,'House No. 607','sector 18B',6,128,'160018','1','House No. 607','sector 18B',6,128,'160018','Gaurav Chopra','gaurav.chopra@hotmail.com',9814013126,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0119','Mohali Hills','Emaar MGF Land Ltd','sorabh.kakar@emaarmgf.com',0,0,'Emaar MGF Land Ltd','40, Central Plaza, Ground Floor, Sector 105 Mohali',28,507,'140306','1','Emaar MGF Land Ltd','40, Central Plaza, Ground Floor, Sector 105 Mohali',28,507,'140306','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">i)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Original Applicants: Mr. Sundeep Singh\r\nPawar and Mrs. Harinder Kaur Pawar <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">ii)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Allotment letter dated 24.4.2007 <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">iii)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Apartment Buyer’s Agreement: 10.4.08 <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">iv)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Allotted Unit No. H1-FPH-PH-01 in ‘The\r\nViews’ at Mohali Hills, Sector-105, SAS Nagar, District Mohali <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">v)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Total sale consideration of Rs.\r\n98,59,200/- <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">vi)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; The Allotted Unit was subsequently\r\ntransferred in the names of Parshottam Dhillon and Gurjeet Kaur Dhillon i.e.\r\nthe Applicants herein vide a letter dated 20.3.09 issued by the\r\nRespondent.&nbsp; The requisite endorsement on\r\nthe Allotment Letter as well as other documents including the Buyer’s Agreement\r\nwas made by the Respondent.&nbsp; <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-32.25pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">vii)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Construction Linked Instalment Plan <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-32.25pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">viii)&nbsp;&nbsp; Amount paid upto 23.8.2013:Rs. 85,06,496/- <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-32.25pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">ix)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;  Clause 21.1 of the Agreement read with\r\nClause 23.1 made it abundantly clear that time was the essence of the contract\r\nand hence, possession of the Allotted Unit was required to be handed over to\r\nthe Applicants by the Respondent positively on or before 24.7.2010.&nbsp; <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-32.25pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">x)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Aggrieved by the aforesaid omission and\r\nlapse of the Respondent, the Applicants had written a letter/e-mail to the\r\nRespondent for rescinding the contract and for seeking refund of the principal\r\namount paid by the Applicants in respect of the Allotted Unit alongwith\r\ninterest.&nbsp; Till date, however, the\r\naforesaid demand raised by the Applicants has not been acceded to by the\r\nRespondent and thus, vide the instant complaint, the Applicants seek refund of\r\nthe monies paid by them to the Respondent alongwith interest.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-32.25pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">xi)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; That it is pertinent to mention herein that\r\nin spite of the fact that the Applicants had sought refund of the principal\r\namount paid by the Applicants alongwith interest, the Respondents have\r\narbitrarily continued to issue Demand Notices to the Applicants for payment of\r\ninstalments as per the payment schedule appended with the Buyer’s agreement.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:1.0in;text-align:justify;text-indent:\r\n-.5in;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n200%;font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">i)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Refund of an amount of Rs. 85,06,496/-\r\npaid by the Applicants alongwith interest (highest marginal cost of lending\r\nrate of the State Bank of India + 2%) from the respective dates of deposit till\r\nactual realization as per Sections 18 and 19(4) of the Act read with Rule 16 of\r\nthe Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:1.0in;text-align:justify;text-indent:\r\n-.5in;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n200%;font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">ii)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Any other relief which the Applicants are\r\nentitled for under the Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Act, 2016 and\r\nthe Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>',