f delay by company in submitting notice of completion beyond 12 months\r\nfrom the end of grace period then the allottee shall become entitled to opt for\r\ntermination.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:\r\njustify;line-height:normal;mso-layout-grid-align:none;text-autospace:none\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial Narrow&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:\r\nVerdana\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:\r\njustify;line-height:normal;mso-layout-grid-align:none;text-autospace:none\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial Narrow&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:\r\nVerdana\">I have made all the payments diligently as and when advised by the\r\ncompany. Till date an amount of Rs 4097341/- has been paid (basic + tax) by me\r\nto the company as per their demand letters received by me but there is no sign\r\nof completion and delivery of the above said unit. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:\r\njustify;line-height:normal;mso-layout-grid-align:none;text-autospace:none\"><span style=\"font-size: 6pt;\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:\r\njustify;line-height:normal;mso-layout-grid-align:none;text-autospace:none\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial Narrow&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:\r\nVerdana\">I had purchased this unit for my son who was to start his career. All\r\nmy hopes have been dashed and we had to invest in making additional\r\nconstruction at my husband’s parental house to create an accommodation for him.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:\r\njustify;line-height:normal;mso-layout-grid-align:none;text-autospace:none\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial Narrow&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:\r\nVerdana\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:\r\njustify;line-height:normal;mso-layout-grid-align:none;text-autospace:none\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial Narrow&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:\r\nVerdana\">You are humbly requested to get my unit cancelled and my money along\r\nwith market rate of interest along with suitable compensation be returned to\r\nme.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','1','','2013-09-11 00:00:00','2013-09-11 00:00:00','X002 C','','',1,1,0,0,'paramkaur','2018-12-20 15:49:32.000','paramkaur','2018-12-20 15:49:32.000'),(585,1209,'1209',1276,'a442c4a5-9b71-4c7a-9da7-d4435d4e0736','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Sarita Singh','calm.rp24@gmail.com',9988539699,0,0,'H. No. 03, Kishore Colony','Bhupindra Road, Patiala',28,454,'147001','1','H. No. 03, Kishore Colony','Bhupindra Road, Patiala',28,454,'147001','Pushpinder Kaushal','dps.legalconsultants@gmail.com',9888104511,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0154','Country Colonizers Private Limited','Country Colonizers Private Limited through its Director/authorized representative','ritu.vansil@waveestate.inPO',0,0,'PO Rayon & Silk Mills Adjoining Coca Cola Depot, Amritsar','',28,39,'143105','1','PO Rayon & Silk Mills Adjoining Coca Cola Depot, Amritsar','',28,39,'143105','1','<p>abc</p>','<p>abc</p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>abc</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'Gurnaam','2018-12-21 11:08:05.000','Gurnaam','2018-12-21 11:08:05.000'),(586,1209,'1209',1276,'a442c4a5-9b71-4c7a-9da7-d4435d4e0736','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Sarita Singh','calm.rp24@gmail.com',9988539699,0,0,'H. No. 03, Kishore Colony','Bhupindra Road, Patiala',28,454,'147001','1','H. No. 03, Kishore Colony','Bhupindra Road, Patiala',28,454,'147001','Pushpinder Kaushal','dps.legalconsultants@gmail.com',9888104511,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0154','Country Colonizers Private Limited','Country Colonizers Private Limited through its Director/authorized representative','ritu.vansil@waveestate.inPO',0,0,'PO Rayon & Silk Mills Adjoining Coca Cola Depot, Amritsar','',28,39,'143105','1','PO Rayon & Silk Mills Adjoining Coca Cola Depot, Amritsar','',28,39,'143105','1','<ol><li>That complainants booked one 3 BHK Apartment with the respondent at their Project “Wave Gardens”, SAS Nagar, Sector 85 and 99, District Mohali, Punjab on 16.10.2012 by paying Rs.5,00,000 vide Receipt No.IR2012000945. Brochure is C1 and Receipt is C2.&nbsp;</li><li>That after passing of three years,&nbsp; provisional allotment was made &amp; Apartment No.0202, J Jasmine, 2nd Floor, Type 3 BHK with Servant Quarter in Group Housing Development named as “Wave Gardens”, SAS Nagar, Sector 85 and 99, District Mohali, having a chargeable super area of approximately 2,283.00 Sq. Feet (212.10 Sq Meters) and having Built up Area 1,932.00 Sq Feet 179.49 Sq Meters was allotted to complainants and in this regard “Apartment Allottee(s) Arrangement” was executed on 19th October, 2015, which is C3.&nbsp;</li><li>That total sale consideration of the Apartment including taxes as provided by respondent is Rs.1,026,69,282, the price details is C4 and the complainants had opted for the “Subvention Payment Linked Plan”, where the payments had to be made as per the Payment Schedule detailed therein, which will be accordingly to progress in the Development of the project. The complainants opted for Preferential Location.&nbsp;</li><li>That the complainants had duly paid an amount of Rs.34,36,440, which was acknowledged by respondents, but inCustomer Statement Account, the respondents had wrongly mentioned as Rs.33,24,040 various receipts are C5 to C7 and Statement is C-8.</li><li>That despite receipt of the said amount, there was no development in the above said project of the respondents till date and the said project is totally in anabandoned condition.&nbsp;</li><li>That the complainants had left with no other option except to seek their refund, which was sought vide e-mails &amp; despite receipt of e-mails, only response was given that “Your request is under process”, but till date refund was not made. E-mails is C9 (Colly. containing pages 1 to 10).</li></ol>','<p>abc</p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>abc</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'Gurnaam','2018-12-21 11:17:29.000','Gurnaam','2018-12-21 11:17:29.000'),(587,1209,'1209',1276,'a442c4a5-9b71-4c7a-9da7-d4435d4e0736','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Sarita Singh','calm.rp24@gmail.com',9988539699,0,0,'H. No. 03, Kishore Colony','Bhupindra Road, Patiala',28,454,'147001','1','H. No. 03, Kishore Colony','Bhupindra Road, Patiala',28,454,'147001','Pushpinder Kaushal','dps.legalconsultants@gmail.com',9888104511,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0154','Country Colonizers Private Limited','Country Colonizers Private Limited through its Director/authorized representative','ritu.vansil@waveestate.inPO',0,0,'PO Rayon & Silk Mills Adjoining Coca Cola Depot, Amritsar','',28,39,'143105','1','PO Rayon & Silk Mills Adjoining Coca Cola Depot, Amritsar','',28,39,'143105','1','<ol><li>That complainants booked one 3 BHK Apartment with the respondent at their Project “Wave Gardens”, SAS Nagar, Sector 85 and 99, District Mohali, Punjab on 16.10.2012 by paying Rs.5,00,000 vide Receipt No.IR2012000945. Brochure is C1 and Receipt is C2.&nbsp;</li><li>That after passing of three years,&nbsp; provisional allotment was made &amp; Apartment No.0202, J Jasmine, 2nd Floor, Type 3 BHK with Servant Quarter in Group Housing Development named as “Wave Gardens”, SAS Nagar, Sector 85 and 99, District Mohali, having a chargeable super area of approximately 2,283.00 Sq. Feet (212.10 Sq Meters) and having Built up Area 1,932.00 Sq Feet 179.49 Sq Meters was allotted to complainants and in this regard “Apartment Allottee(s) Arrangement” was executed on 19th October, 2015, which is C3.&nbsp;</li><li>That total sale consideration of the Apartment including taxes as provided by respondent is Rs.1,026,69,282, the price details is C4 and the complainants had opted for the “Subvention Payment Linked Plan”, where the payments had to be made as per the Payment Schedule detailed therein, which will be accordingly to progress in the Development of the project. The complainants opted for Preferential Location.&nbsp;</li><li>That the complainants had duly paid an amount of Rs.34,36,440, which was acknowledged by respondents, but inCustomer Statement Account, the respondents had wrongly mentioned as Rs.33,24,040 various receipts are C5 to C7 and Statement is C-8.</li><li>That despite receipt of the said amount, there was no development in the above said project of the respondents till date and the said project is totally in anabandoned condition.&nbsp;</li><li>That the complainants had left with no other option except to seek their refund, which was sought vide e-mails &amp; despite receipt of e-mails, only response was given that “Your request is under process”, but till date refund was not made. E-mails is C9 (Colly. containing pages 1 to 10).</li></ol>','<ol><li>That the complainants have been suffering on account of the acts &amp; conduct of the respondents, so the amount deposited by the complainants is liable to be refunded.&nbsp;</li><li>That further as per Clause No.5.1 of the Apartment Allottee Arrangement, the development of the said project and the Apartment was to be completed within 30 months along with an extended period of six months from the date of execution of the Apartment Allottee(s) Arrangement i.e. 19.10.2015 and from the date of start of construction of Group Housing named as “Wave Gardens” whichever is later, however, even the said period has already been elapsed i.e. by 19.10.2018 and by this date, the project as well as the Apartment has to be completed in totality, as per the projections made by the respondents in their Brochures, however, on the other hand, till date, there is no such development, so the amount deposited by the complainants is liable to be refunded. It is also worth mention here that as per Clause 5.5 of the Apartment Allottee(s) Arrangement, in case of delay in construction of the Unit, the delay charges at the rate of Rs.5 per Sq. Feet (super area) per month were payable to the complainants. However, the respondents failed to complete or develop the project, so as to deliver possession of the unit, in question to the complainants within the stipulated period.&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>That due the act and conduct of the respondents, the complainants have been continuously suffering mentally, physically &amp; economically.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Hence, the complainants are seeking the following directions to the respondents:-&nbsp;</li><li>To refund the amount of Rs.34,36,440, alongwith interest at the rate of 18 percent per annum from the respective dates of deposit till realization;</li></ol>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>NIL</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'Gurnaam','2018-12-21 11:25:28.000','Gurnaam','2018-12-21 11:25:28.000'),(588,1209,'1209',1276,'a442c4a5-9b71-4c7a-9da7-d4435d4e0736','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-21 17:24:04.000','Sarita Singh','calm.rp24@gmail.com',9988539699,0,0,'H. No. 03, Kishore Colony','Bhupindra Road, Patiala',28,454,'147001','1','H. No. 03, Kishore Colony','Bhupindra Road, Patiala',28,454,'147001','Pushpinder Kaushal','dps.legalconsultants@gmail.com',9888104511,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0154','Country Colonizers Private Limited','Country Colonizers Private Limited through its Director/authorized representative','ritu.vansil@waveestate.inPO',0,0,'PO Rayon & Silk Mills Adjoining Coca Cola Depot, Amritsar','',28,39,'143105','1','PO Rayon & Silk Mills Adjoining Coca Cola Depot, Amritsar','',28,39,'143105','1','<ol><li>That complainants booked one 3 BHK Apartment with the respondent at their Project “Wave Gardens”, SAS Nagar, Sector 85 and 99, District Mohali, Punjab on 16.10.2012 by paying Rs.5,00,000 vide Receipt No.IR2012000945. Brochure is C1 and Receipt is C2.&nbsp;</li><li>That after passing of three years,&nbsp; provisional allotment was made &amp; Apartment No.0202, J Jasmine, 2nd Floor, Type 3 BHK with Servant Quarter in Group Housing Development named as “Wave Gardens”, SAS Nagar, Sector 85 and 99, District Mohali, having a chargeable super area of approximately 2,283.00 Sq. Feet (212.10 Sq Meters) and having Built up Area 1,932.00 Sq Feet 179.49 Sq Meters was allotted to complainants and in this regard “Apartment Allottee(s) Arrangement” was executed on 19th October, 2015, which is C3.&nbsp;</li><li>That total sale consideration of the Apartment including taxes as provided by respondent is Rs.1,026,69,282, the price details is C4 and the complainants had opted for the “Subvention Payment Linked Plan”, where the payments had to be made as per the Payment Schedule detailed therein, which will be accordingly to progress in the Development of the project. The complainants opted for Preferential Location.&nbsp;</li><li>That the complainants had duly paid an amount of Rs.34,36,440, which was acknowledged by respondents, but inCustomer Statement Account, the respondents had wrongly mentioned as Rs.33,24,040 various receipts are C5 to C7 and Statement is C-8.</li><li>That despite receipt of the said amount, there was no development in the above said project of the respondents till date and the said project is totally in anabandoned condition.&nbsp;</li><li>That the complainants had left with no other option except to seek their refund, which was sought vide e-mails &amp; despite receipt of e-mails, only response was given that “Your request is under process”, but till date refund was not made. E-mails is C9 (Colly. containing pages 1 to 10).</li></ol>','<ol><li>That the complainants have been suffering on account of the acts &amp; conduct of the respondents, so the amount deposited by the complainants is liable to be refunded.&nbsp;</li><li>That further as per Clause No.5.1 of the Apartment Allottee Arrangement, the development of the said project and the Apartment was to be completed within 30 months along with an extended period of six months from the date of execution of the Apartment Allottee(s) Arrangement i.e. 19.10.2015 and from the date of start of construction of Group Housing named as “Wave Gardens” whichever is later, however, even the said period has already been elapsed i.e. by 19.10.2018 and by this date, the project as well as the Apartment has to be completed in totality, as per the projections made by the respondents in their Brochures, however, on the other hand, till date, there is no such development, so the amount deposited by the complainants is liable to be refunded. It is also worth mention here that as per Clause 5.5 of the Apartment Allottee(s) Arrangement, in case of delay in construction of the Unit, the delay charges at the rate of Rs.5 per Sq. Feet (super area) per month were payable to the complainants. However, the respondents failed to complete or develop the project, so as to deliver possession of the unit, in question to the complainants within the stipulated period.&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>That due the act and conduct of the respondents, the complainants have been continuously suffering mentally, physically &amp; economically.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Hence, the complainants are seeking the following directions to the respondents:-&nbsp;</li><li>To refund the amount of Rs.34,36,440, alongwith interest at the rate of 18 percent per annum from the respective dates of deposit till realization;</li></ol>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>NIL</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',1,1,0,0,'Gurnaam','2018-12-21 11:25:45.000','Gurnaam','2018-12-21 11:25:45.000'),(589,1207,'1207',1291,'3eb2066a-1568-4aaa-85a1-53ef2b0ad2ad','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-21 14:47:16.000','Harjinder  kaur','csvedparkash@gmail.com',7837223098,0,0,'#1403-B, Sector-37-B Chandigarh','',6,128,'160037','1','#1403-B, Sector-37-B Chandigarh','',6,128,'160037','Ved Parkash','csvedpakash@gmail.com',7837223098,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0262','M/s Bajwa Developers','M/s Hanumanta Land Promoters Pvt.Ltd','bajwadevelopers@gmail.com',9988888089,0,'Micro Homes, SCO-18-19, Megha Market, Opp.-Naval Air Force group Housing Society, ','Sunny Enclave Sextor-123, Mohali',28,507,'140301','1','Micro Homes, SCO-18-19, Megha Market, Opp.-Naval Air Force group Housing Society, ','Sunny Enclave Sextor-123, Mohali',28,507,'140301','1','<p>CONCISE STATEMENT OF FACTS&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>1. That M/s Bajwa Developers be its head office at __________________ is a pleading developer in Real Estate Projects in Mohali/Kharar area and has also developed more than 50 real estate projectta. That as a part of the overall development plan the respondent developed Sector-123, as per the Layout Plan attached as Annexure I.The respondent has obtained all necessary approvals from competent authorities for the said project.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>2. The Respondent engages developers for constructions of towers within the approved Layout Plan as specified in Annexure I. One of the developers is M/s Hanumanta Land Promoters who has undertaken to develop apartments in area marked in layout plan as above . The registered deed entered into between M/s Bajwa&nbsp; Developers Ltd and M/s Hanumanta Land Promoters Pvt.Ltd attached as Annexure II. &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>3. In view of points (1.) and (2). Above, it is established that both M/s Bajwa Developers and M/s Hanumanta Land Promoters are promoters and co-promoters in this Real Estate Project constructed by M/s Hanumanta Land Promoters. The overall project as per the layout plan is registered with RERA vide RERA No.-_____________.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>4. That the complainant booked Appartment No.- 2 BHK Flat No.- GF(A) in Micro Homes SCO-18-19, Group Housing Society , Sunny Enclave, Sector-123 , Greater Mohali at a consideration of Rs.21,00,000/- as per the Allotment Letter attached as Annexure III.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>5. The Builder Buyer Agreement was signed between the 2 parties is attached as Annexure IV.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>6. That the applicant has made all the payments , the summary of the same is attached as Annexure V.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>7. The Co-Promoter was to give possession&nbsp; of the allotted apartment dated.-______ which has already expired .There is no progress on development of the projectat all and possession is not expected in the near future .&nbsp;<br></p>','<p><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"margin: 0px; line-height: 115%; font-size: 12pt;\"><span style=\"margin: 0px;\"><span style=\'font: 7pt \"Times New Roman\"; margin: 0px; font-size-adjust: none; font-stretch: normal;\'>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; </span></span></span><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"margin: 0px; line-height: 115%; font-size: 12pt;\">Since, there is a delay in handing\r\nover, the complainant wishes to withdraw from the project and seeks refund and\r\ninterest on the amount paid as per RERA Provisions . The overall project is\r\nregistered with RERA by M/s Bajwa Developers and M/s Hanumanta Land Promoters\r\nhas not got its project registered with RERA, both the respondents jointly or\r\nseparately may be directed to pay the amount of refund and interest to the\r\ncomplainant.</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n<b></b><i></i><u></u><sub></sub><sup></sup><strike></strike><font face=\"Times New Roman\"></font><br></p>',2100000.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>NA</p>','1','','2013-08-19 00:00:00','2014-02-07 00:00:00',' 2 BHK Flat No.-23 GF(A)','','',1,0,0,0,'harjinderkaur','2018-12-21 14:47:11.000','harjinderkaur','2018-12-21 14:47:11.000'),(590,1210,'1210',1295,'f7993d00-eee5-49f1-a16c-9e8bc8af7b5a','FormTypeM',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Pardeep Pushap','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9991199955,0,813130859759,'House No197 Sector 14 Urban Estate Karnal Haryana','',13,10,'132001','1','House No197 Sector 14 Urban Estate Karnal Haryana','',13,10,'132001','Kamal Dahiya','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9729902009,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0396','Sushma Valencia','Suksha Developers  Pvt Ltd','bharat@sushmabuildtech.com',9876200054,0,'B 107 First Floor Business Complex at Elante Mall Industrial Area Phase1 Chandigarh','',6,128,'160002','1','B 107 First Floor Business Complex at Elante Mall Industrial Area Phase1 Chandigarh','',6,128,'160002','1','<p>The SUSHMA VALENCIA is a Residential Group Housing Colony Project being developed by the Respondent, situated in Zirakpur, Punjab. The flat was booked in the joint name of the Complainant and his wife Vanita Pushap and they paid Rs 5,00,000/- as a token money, out of which Rs 1,00,000 was paid through&nbsp; vide cheque no. 352596 and Rs 1,00,000 was paid through ICICI Bank credit card ANNEXURE C-1. Further they had paid Rs 3,00,000 in cash to the respondents. The respondents had issued a copy of site plan, Floor Plans, Terrace Plans of the said project to the Complainant ANNEXURE C-2. The Respondent also issued a Payment Plan of the said Project to the Complainant ANNEXURE C-3.The Respondents assured the complainants that the said project is RERA approved and all the necessary documentation are being completed. But after the payment of Rs 5,00,000 by the complainant for the booked flat in the said project, the complainants came to know from their reliable sources that the said project is not RERA approved nor the respondents are complying government rules and regulations regarding this. The Complainant visited so many times in the office of the respondents and asked for the documents or refund of the paid amount and many times, the complainant had the telephonic conversation with them regarding this issue, but neither they showed him the documents of RERA Approval nor refunded his money. The Complainant also had the conversation with Bharat Mittal, Additional Director of the respondent Company vide messenger wherein he was asking for refund but he refused to do help him. The Complainant also explained his issues relating to his father who was admitted in Medanta Gurgaon and requested to transfer his amount of Rs 2,00,000 but he refused him by saying that there is no cancellation policy ANNEXURE C-4.The Complainant had requested the respondent so many times to refund his paid amount of Rs 5,00,000/- but the respondent always denying all the requests.</p><p><br></p>','<p>In view of the facts mentioned in paragraphs above, the complainant prays for the following relief(s):-&nbsp;</p><p>i.To give necessary directions to the respondents for return of the payment made in lieu of the flat with the prescribed rate of interest as per the provisions of Section 18 and 19(4) of the RERA Act.</p><p>ii.To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 60 of RERA Act for willful default committed by them.</p><p>iii.To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 61 of RERA Act for contravention of Sec.12, Sec.14, and Sec. 16 of RERA Act.</p><p>iv.To direct the respondents to pay penalty upto 10% of project cost to the complainant under Sec. 59 of RERA, Act, 2016.</p><p>v.To direct the respondents to refund the amount collected from the complainant in lieu of interest, penalty for delayed payments under Rule 23(3)(c) of Punjab RERA Rules,2017.</p><p>vi.To issue directions to make liable every officer concerned i.e. Director, Manager, Secretary, or any other officer of the respondent’s company at whose instance, connivance, acquiescence, neglect any of the offences has been committed as mentioned in Sec.69 of RERA Act,2016 to be read with Punjab RERA Rules,2017.</p><p>vii.To direct respondent to deliver the flat to the complainant without charging the additional charges for the increased area of the flat.</p><p>viii.To recommend criminal action against the respondents for the criminal offence of cheating, fraud and criminal breach of trust under section 420,406 and 409 of the Indian Penal Code.</p><p>ix.To issue direction to pay the cost of litigation.</p><p>x.Any other relief which this Hon’ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances of this complaint.</p><div><br></div>',0.00,500000.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>i.To direct the respondent not to demand any further amount whatsoever from the complainant.</p><p>ii.The respondent should be restrained from harassing the complainant in any manner whatsoever.</p><p>iii.Any other interim relief which this Hon’ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances of this complaint.</p><div><br></div>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'Pardeep1','2018-12-21 15:42:38.000','Pardeep1','2018-12-21 15:42:38.000'),(591,1201,'1201',1286,'d5cccd55-ed50-4972-b984-310c180b5690','FormTypeM',1,1,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Narwar Singh Bhogal','kashika.juneja91@gmail.com',9814013127,0,0,'House No. 607','sector 18B',6,128,'160018','1','House No. 607','sector 18B',6,128,'160018','Gaurav Chopra','gaurav.chopra@hotmail.com',9814013127,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0119','MOHALI HILLS','M/s EMAAR MGF LAND LIMITED','sorabh.kakar@emaarmgf.com',0,0,'M/s. Emaar MGF Land Limited, Office No. 40, Central Plaza, Sector 105','',28,507,'140306','1','M/s. Emaar MGF Land Limited, Office No. 40, Central Plaza, Sector 105','',28,507,'140306','1','<p>i)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Applicants: Narwar Singh Bhogal and Mrs Ajit Kaur Bhogal had</p><p>ii)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Application form: 22.2.2008&nbsp;</p><p>iii)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Allotment Letter: 11.3.2008&nbsp;</p><p>iv)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Buyer’s Agreement: 31.3.2008</p><p>iv)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Vide a letter dated 2.7.2008, the allotted unit, as aforesaid, was changed to TVM-L3-F10-1003&nbsp;</p><p>v)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Total sale price: Rs. 57,01,543/-.&nbsp;</p><p>vi)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Amendment Agreement: 2.12.2013, the Respondent had allotted an alternate unit TVM-L1-F11-1102 ad measuring 1930 sq ft in “The Views” at Mohali Hills in Sector-105, SAS Nagar, District Mohali, Punjab instead of the earlier allotted unit TVM-L3-F10-1003</p><p>vii)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Total sale consideration (revised): Rs. 64,22,558.30/-&nbsp;</p><p>viii)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Co-Applicant i.e. Mrs Ajit Kaur Bhogal has passed away on 7.12.2017 and prior to her death she had executed a registered will dated 22.3.2011 bequeathing her share in the allotted unit to the Applicant.&nbsp;</p><p>ix)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Construction Linked Instalment Plan&nbsp;</p><p>x)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Amount paid upto 8.3.2018: Rs. 66,50,108.51/-&nbsp;</p><p>xi)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That Clause 21.1 of the Agreement read with Clause 23.1 made it abundantly clear that time was the essence of the contract and hence, possession of the Allotted Unit was required to be handed over to the Applicant by the Respondent positively on or before 11.6.2011.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>xii)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Aggrieved by the aforesaid omission and lapse of the Respondent, the Applicant had written a letter/e-mail dated 5.4.2018 to the Respondent for seeking refund of the principal amount paid by the Applicant in respect of the Allotted Unit alongwith interest. The Respondent upon receiving the aforesaid Email/letter, sent a reply dated 13.4.2018 declining the request of the Applicant for refund of the amount paid in respect of the allotted unit. Thus, vide the instant complaint, the Applicant seeks refund of the monies paid by him to the Respondent alongwith interest.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><br></p>','<p>i)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Refund of an amount of Rs. 66,50,108.51/- paid by the Applicant alongwith interest (highest marginal cost of lending rate of the State Bank of India + 2%) from the respective dates of deposit till actual realization as per Sections 18 and 19(4) of the Act read with Rule 16 of the Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017.</p><p>ii)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Any other relief which the Applicant is entitled for under the Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Act, 2016 and the Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p>',6422558.30,6650108.51,'2011-06-11 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','..','1','','2008-03-11 00:00:00','2008-03-31 00:00:00','UNIT NO. TVM L1 F11 1102 \"The Views\" at Mohali Hills','','',2,0,0,0,'Narwarbhogal','2018-12-21 18:33:56.000','Narwarbhogal','2018-12-21 18:33:56.000'),(592,1197,'1197',1287,'fcebf583-f701-4375-a441-163b29a0faf5','FormTypeM',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Brinder  Singh','kashika.juneja91@gmail.com',9814013127,0,0,'House No. 607','sector 18B',6,128,'160018','1','House No. 607','sector 18B',6,128,'160018','Gaurav Chopra','gaurav.chopra@hotmail.com',9814013125,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0119','Mohali Hills','Emaar MGF Land Ltd','sorabh.kakar@emaarmgf.com',0,0,'Emaar MGF Land Ltd','40, Central Plaza, Ground Floor, Sector 105 Mohali',28,507,'140306','1','Emaar MGF Land Ltd','40, Central Plaza, Ground Floor, Sector 105 Mohali',28,507,'140306','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-indent: -43px; margin-left: 0.5in; line-height: 200%;\"><font face=\"Garamond, serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">i)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That the Applicants had sought allotment of a Residential Apartment in “The Views”, Mohali Hills and were Allotted Unit No. TVM K1-FPH-PH02, Tower K1, ‘The Views’, Mohali Hills, Sector 105, Mohali for which a Buyer’s Agreement 13.6.11 was executed between the Applicants and Respondent.&nbsp;</span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-indent: -43px; margin-left: 0.5in; line-height: 200%;\"><font face=\"Garamond, serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">ii)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That out of the total sale consideration of Rs. 1,04,28,413/-, the amount previously paid by the Applicants in respect of a Built Up Villa No. 10, Sector 106, Mohali, the allotment whereof was cancelled vide a letter dated 25.3.11 issued by the Respondent on mutually accepted terms, was adjusted and over and above the said amount, a further sum of Rs. 15,31,688.13/- was paid by the Applicants upto 27.8.2012 and thus, an amount of Rs. 1,07,66,807/- was paid in respect of the Allotted Unit.</span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-indent: -43px; margin-left: 0.5in; line-height: 200%;\"><font face=\"Garamond, serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">iii)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That the Respondent wilfully defaulted in offering possession of the Allotted Unit by the second quarter of 2012, as assured by the Respondent at the time of migrating the applicants from the Built Up Villa to the Allotted Unit, or within stipulated time period as per Clause 21.1 of the Buyer’s Agreement i.e. 13.12.2014. Consequently, vide an email&nbsp; 20.10.17, the Buyer’s Agreement dated 13.6.11 was rescinded by the Applicants while inter alia calling upon the Respondent to forthwith refund the entire amount paid by them alongwith interest.</span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-indent: -43px; margin-left: 0.5in; line-height: 200%;\"><font face=\"Garamond, serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">iv)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That despite receipt of the aforesaid email 20.10.17, the Respondent offered possession of the Allotted Unit vide its letter dated 28.10.17. The offer of possession given by the Respondent is nothing else but a sham. At the site of the Allotted Unit, the development works were nowhere near completion and the Allotted Unit is also not in any condition whatsoever to be taken&nbsp;</span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-indent: -43px; margin-left: 0.5in; line-height: 200%;\"><font face=\"Garamond, serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">vi)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That failure on the part of the Respondent in handing over possession of the Allotted Unit within the stipulated time period as per Clause 21.1 of the Buyer’s Agreement constitutes a wilful and material breach of the contract executed between the parties.</span></font></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:1.0in;text-align:justify;text-indent:\r\n-.5in;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n200%;font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">i)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Refund of an amount of Rs.\r\n1,02,21,448/-paid by the Applicants alongwith interest (highest marginal cost\r\nof lending rate of the State Bank of India + 2%) from the respective dates of\r\ndeposit till actual realization as per Sections 18 and 19(4) of the Act read\r\nwith Rule 16 of the Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development)\r\nRules, 2017.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:1.0in;text-align:justify;text-indent:\r\n-.5in;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n200%;font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">ii)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Any other relief which the Applicant is\r\nentitled for under the Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Act, 2016 and\r\nthe Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>..</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'brindersingh1','2018-12-21 20:34:59.000','brindersingh1','2018-12-21 20:34:59.000'),(593,1197,'1197',1287,'fcebf583-f701-4375-a441-163b29a0faf5','FormTypeM',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Brinder  Singh','kashika.juneja91@gmail.com',9814013127,0,0,'House No. 607','sector 18B',6,128,'160018','1','House No. 607','sector 18B',6,128,'160018','Gaurav Chopra','gaurav.chopra@hotmail.com',9814013125,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0119','Mohali Hills','Emaar MGF Land Ltd','sorabh.kakar@emaarmgf.com',0,0,'Emaar MGF Land Ltd','40, Central Plaza, Ground Floor, Sector 105 Mohali',28,507,'140306','1','Emaar MGF Land Ltd','40, Central Plaza, Ground Floor, Sector 105 Mohali',28,507,'140306','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-indent: -43px; margin-left: 0.5in; line-height: 200%;\"><font face=\"Garamond, serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">i)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That the Applicants had sought allotment of a Residential Apartment in “The Views”, Mohali Hills and were Allotted Unit No. TVM K1-FPH-PH02, Tower K1, ‘The Views’, Mohali Hills, Sector 105, Mohali for which a Buyer’s Agreement 13.6.11 was executed between the Applicants and Respondent.&nbsp;</span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-indent: -43px; margin-left: 0.5in; line-height: 200%;\"><font face=\"Garamond, serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">ii)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That out of the total sale consideration of Rs. 1,04,28,413/-, the amount previously paid by the Applicants in respect of a Built Up Villa No. 10, Sector 106, Mohali, the allotment whereof was cancelled vide a letter dated 25.3.11 issued by the Respondent on mutually accepted terms, was adjusted and over and above the said amount, a further sum of Rs. 15,31,688.13/- was paid by the Applicants upto 27.8.2012 and thus, an amount of Rs. 1,07,66,807/- was paid in respect of the Allotted Unit.</span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-indent: -43px; margin-left: 0.5in; line-height: 200%;\"><font face=\"Garamond, serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">iii)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That the Respondent wilfully defaulted in offering possession of the Allotted Unit by the second quarter of 2012, as assured by the Respondent at the time of migrating the applicants from the Built Up Villa to the Allotted Unit, or within stipulated time period as per Clause 21.1 of the Buyer’s Agreement i.e. 13.12.2014. Consequently, vide an email&nbsp; 20.10.17, the Buyer’s Agreement dated 13.6.11 was rescinded by the Applicants while inter alia calling upon the Respondent to forthwith refund the entire amount paid by them alongwith interest.</span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-indent: -43px; margin-left: 0.5in; line-height: 200%;\"><font face=\"Garamond, serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">iv)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That despite receipt of the aforesaid email 20.10.17, the Respondent offered possession of the Allotted Unit vide its letter dated 28.10.17. The offer of possession given by the Respondent is nothing else but a sham. At the site of the Allotted Unit, the development works were nowhere near completion and the Allotted Unit is also not in any condition whatsoever to be taken&nbsp;</span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-indent: -43px; margin-left: 0.5in; line-height: 200%;\"><font face=\"Garamond, serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">vi)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That failure on the part of the Respondent in handing over possession of the Allotted Unit within the stipulated time period as per Clause 21.1 of the Buyer’s Agreement constitutes a wilful and material breach of the contract executed between the parties.</span></font></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:1.0in;text-align:justify;text-indent:\r\n-.5in;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n200%;font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">i)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Refund of an amount of Rs.\r\n1,02,21,448/-paid by the Applicants alongwith interest (highest marginal cost\r\nof lending rate of the State Bank of India + 2%) from the respective dates of\r\ndeposit till actual realization as per Sections 18 and 19(4) of the Act read\r\nwith Rule 16 of the Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development)\r\nRules, 2017.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:1.0in;text-align:justify;text-indent:\r\n-.5in;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n200%;font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">ii)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Any other relief which the Applicant is\r\nentitled for under the Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Act, 2016 and\r\nthe Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>',9915199.00,10221448.00,'2014-12-13 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>..</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','2011-06-13 00:00:00','Allotted Unit No. TVM K1-FPH-PH02, Tower K1, ‘The Views’, Mohali Hills','','',2,0,0,0,'brindersingh1','2018-12-21 20:37:46.000','brindersingh1','2018-12-21 20:37:46.000'),(594,1197,'1197',1287,'fcebf583-f701-4375-a441-163b29a0faf5','FormTypeM',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Brinder  Singh','kashika.juneja91@gmail.com',9814013127,0,0,'House No. 607','sector 18B',6,128,'160018','1','House No. 607','sector 18B',6,128,'160018','Gaurav Chopra','gaurav.chopra@hotmail.com',9814013125,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0119','Mohali Hills','Emaar MGF Land Ltd','sorabh.kakar@emaarmgf.com',0,0,'Emaar MGF Land Ltd','40, Central Plaza, Ground Floor, Sector 105 Mohali',28,507,'140306','1','Emaar MGF Land Ltd','40, Central Plaza, Ground Floor, Sector 105 Mohali',28,507,'140306','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-indent: -43px; margin-left: 0.5in; line-height: 200%;\"><font face=\"Garamond, serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">i)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That the Applicants had sought allotment of a Residential Apartment in “The Views”, Mohali Hills and were Allotted Unit No. TVM K1-FPH-PH02, Tower K1, ‘The Views’, Mohali Hills, Sector 105, Mohali for which a Buyer’s Agreement 13.6.11 was executed between the Applicants and Respondent.&nbsp;</span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-indent: -43px; margin-left: 0.5in; line-height: 200%;\"><font face=\"Garamond, serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">ii)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That out of the total sale consideration of Rs. 1,04,28,413/-, the amount previously paid by the Applicants in respect of a Built Up Villa No. 10, Sector 106, Mohali, the allotment whereof was cancelled vide a letter dated 25.3.11 issued by the Respondent on mutually accepted terms, was adjusted and over and above the said amount, a further sum of Rs. 15,31,688.13/- was paid by the Applicants upto 27.8.2012 and thus, an amount of Rs. 1,07,66,807/- was paid in respect of the Allotted Unit.</span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-indent: -43px; margin-left: 0.5in; line-height: 200%;\"><font face=\"Garamond, serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">iii)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That the Respondent wilfully defaulted in offering possession of the Allotted Unit by the second quarter of 2012, as assured by the Respondent at the time of migrating the applicants from the Built Up Villa to the Allotted Unit, or within stipulated time period as per Clause 21.1 of the Buyer’s Agreement i.e. 13.12.2014. Consequently, vide an email&nbsp; 20.10.17, the Buyer’s Agreement dated 13.6.11 was rescinded by the Applicants while inter alia calling upon the Respondent to forthwith refund the entire amount paid by them alongwith interest.</span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-indent: -43px; margin-left: 0.5in; line-height: 200%;\"><font face=\"Garamond, serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">iv)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That despite receipt of the aforesaid email 20.10.17, the Respondent offered possession of the Allotted Unit vide its letter dated 28.10.17. The offer of possession given by the Respondent is nothing else but a sham. At the site of the Allotted Unit, the development works were nowhere near completion and the Allotted Unit is also not in any condition whatsoever to be taken&nbsp;</span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-indent: -43px; margin-left: 0.5in; line-height: 200%;\"><font face=\"Garamond, serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">vi)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That failure on the part of the Respondent in handing over possession of the Allotted Unit within the stipulated time period as per Clause 21.1 of the Buyer’s Agreement constitutes a wilful and material breach of the contract executed between the parties.</span></font></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:1.0in;text-align:justify;text-indent:\r\n-.5in;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n200%;font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">i)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Refund of an amount of Rs.\r\n1,02,21,448/-paid by the Applicants alongwith interest (highest marginal cost\r\nof lending rate of the State Bank of India + 2%) from the respective dates of\r\ndeposit till actual realization as per Sections 18 and 19(4) of the Act read\r\nwith Rule 16 of the Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development)\r\nRules, 2017.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:1.0in;text-align:justify;text-indent:\r\n-.5in;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n200%;font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">ii)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Any other relief which the Applicant is\r\nentitled for under the Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Act, 2016 and\r\nthe Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>',9915199.00,10221448.00,'2014-12-13 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>..</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','2011-06-13 00:00:00','Allotted Unit No. TVM K1-FPH-PH02, Tower K1, ‘The Views’, Mohali Hills','','',2,0,0,0,'brindersingh1','2018-12-21 20:38:01.000','brindersingh1','2018-12-21 20:38:01.000'),(595,1197,'1197',1287,'fcebf583-f701-4375-a441-163b29a0faf5','FormTypeM',1,1,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Brinder  Singh','kashika.juneja91@gmail.com',9814013127,0,0,'House No. 607','sector 18B',6,128,'160018','1','House No. 607','sector 18B',6,128,'160018','Gaurav Chopra','gaurav.chopra@hotmail.com',9814013125,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0119','Mohali Hills','Emaar MGF Land Ltd','sorabh.kakar@emaarmgf.com',0,0,'Emaar MGF Land Ltd','40, Central Plaza, Ground Floor, Sector 105 Mohali',28,507,'140306','1','Emaar MGF Land Ltd','40, Central Plaza, Ground Floor, Sector 105 Mohali',28,507,'140306','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-indent: -43px; margin-left: 0.5in; line-height: 200%;\"><font face=\"Garamond, serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">i)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That the Applicants had sought allotment of a Residential Apartment in “The Views”, Mohali Hills and were Allotted Unit No. TVM K1-FPH-PH02, Tower K1, ‘The Views’, Mohali Hills, Sector 105, Mohali for which a Buyer’s Agreement 13.6.11 was executed between the Applicants and Respondent.&nbsp;</span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-indent: -43px; margin-left: 0.5in; line-height: 200%;\"><font face=\"Garamond, serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">ii)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That out of the total sale consideration of Rs. 1,04,28,413/-, the amount previously paid by the Applicants in respect of a Built Up Villa No. 10, Sector 106, Mohali, the allotment whereof was cancelled vide a letter dated 25.3.11 issued by the Respondent on mutually accepted terms, was adjusted and over and above the said amount, a further sum of Rs. 15,31,688.13/- was paid by the Applicants upto 27.8.2012 and thus, an amount of Rs. 1,07,66,807/- was paid in respect of the Allotted Unit.</span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-indent: -43px; margin-left: 0.5in; line-height: 200%;\"><font face=\"Garamond, serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">iii)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That the Respondent wilfully defaulted in offering possession of the Allotted Unit by the second quarter of 2012, as assured by the Respondent at the time of migrating the applicants from the Built Up Villa to the Allotted Unit, or within stipulated time period as per Clause 21.1 of the Buyer’s Agreement i.e. 13.12.2014. Consequently, vide an email&nbsp; 20.10.17, the Buyer’s Agreement dated 13.6.11 was rescinded by the Applicants while inter alia calling upon the Respondent to forthwith refund the entire amount paid by them alongwith interest.</span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-indent: -43px; margin-left: 0.5in; line-height: 200%;\"><font face=\"Garamond, serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">iv)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That despite receipt of the aforesaid email 20.10.17, the Respondent offered possession of the Allotted Unit vide its letter dated 28.10.17. The offer of possession given by the Respondent is nothing else but a sham. At the site of the Allotted Unit, the development works were nowhere near completion and the Allotted Unit is also not in any condition whatsoever to be taken&nbsp;</span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-indent: -43px; margin-left: 0.5in; line-height: 200%;\"><font face=\"Garamond, serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">vi)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That failure on the part of the Respondent in handing over possession of the Allotted Unit within the stipulated time period as per Clause 21.1 of the Buyer’s Agreement constitutes a wilful and material breach of the contract executed between the parties.</span></font></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:1.0in;text-align:justify;text-indent:\r\n-.5in;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n200%;font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">i)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Refund of an amount of Rs.\r\n1,02,21,448/-paid by the Applicants alongwith interest (highest marginal cost\r\nof lending rate of the State Bank of India + 2%) from the respective dates of\r\ndeposit till actual realization as per Sections 18 and 19(4) of the Act read\r\nwith Rule 16 of the Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development)\r\nRules, 2017.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:1.0in;text-align:justify;text-indent:\r\n-.5in;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n200%;font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">ii)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Any other relief which the Applicant is\r\nentitled for under the Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Act, 2016 and\r\nthe Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>',10428413.00,10766807.00,'2014-12-13 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>..</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','2011-06-13 00:00:00','Allotted Unit No. TVM K1-FPH-PH02, Tower K1, ‘The Views’, Mohali Hills','','',2,0,0,0,'brindersingh1','2018-12-22 10:30:31.000','brindersingh1','2018-12-22 10:30:31.000'),(596,1201,'1201',1286,'d5cccd55-ed50-4972-b984-310c180b5690','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-22 10:32:24.000','Narwar Singh Bhogal','kashika.juneja91@gmail.com',9814013127,0,0,'House No. 607','sector 18B',6,128,'160018','1','House No. 607','sector 18B',6,128,'160018','Gaurav Chopra','gaurav.chopra@hotmail.com',9814013127,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0119','MOHALI HILLS','M/s EMAAR MGF LAND LIMITED','sorabh.kakar@emaarmgf.com',0,0,'M/s. Emaar MGF Land Limited, Office No. 40, Central Plaza, Sector 105','',28,507,'140306','1','M/s. Emaar MGF Land Limited, Office No. 40, Central Plaza, Sector 105','',28,507,'140306','1','<p>i)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Applicants: Narwar Singh Bhogal and Mrs Ajit Kaur Bhogal had</p><p>ii)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Application form: 22.2.2008&nbsp;</p><p>iii)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Allotment Letter: 11.3.2008&nbsp;</p><p>iv)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Buyer’s Agreement: 31.3.2008</p><p>iv)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Vide a letter dated 2.7.2008, the allotted unit, as aforesaid, was changed to TVM-L3-F10-1003&nbsp;</p><p>v)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Total sale price: Rs. 57,01,543/-.&nbsp;</p><p>vi)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Amendment Agreement: 2.12.2013, the Respondent had allotted an alternate unit TVM-L1-F11-1102 ad measuring 1930 sq ft in “The Views” at Mohali Hills in Sector-105, SAS Nagar, District Mohali, Punjab instead of the earlier allotted unit TVM-L3-F10-1003</p><p>vii)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Total sale consideration (revised): Rs. 64,22,558.30/-&nbsp;</p><p>viii)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Co-Applicant i.e. Mrs Ajit Kaur Bhogal has passed away on 7.12.2017 and prior to her death she had executed a registered will dated 22.3.2011 bequeathing her share in the allotted unit to the Applicant.&nbsp;</p><p>ix)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Construction Linked Instalment Plan&nbsp;</p><p>x)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Amount paid upto 8.3.2018: Rs. 66,50,108.51/-&nbsp;</p><p>xi)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That Clause 21.1 of the Agreement read with Clause 23.1 made it abundantly clear that time was the essence of the contract and hence, possession of the Allotted Unit was required to be handed over to the Applicant by the Respondent positively on or before 11.6.2011.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>xii)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Aggrieved by the aforesaid omission and lapse of the Respondent, the Applicant had written a letter/e-mail dated 5.4.2018 to the Respondent for seeking refund of the principal amount paid by the Applicant in respect of the Allotted Unit alongwith interest. The Respondent upon receiving the aforesaid Email/letter, sent a reply dated 13.4.2018 declining the request of the Applicant for refund of the amount paid in respect of the allotted unit. Thus, vide the instant complaint, the Applicant seeks refund of the monies paid by him to the Respondent alongwith interest.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><br></p>','<p>i)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Refund of an amount of Rs. 66,50,108.51/- paid by the Applicant alongwith interest (highest marginal cost of lending rate of the State Bank of India + 2%) from the respective dates of deposit till actual realization as per Sections 18 and 19(4) of the Act read with Rule 16 of the Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017.</p><p>ii)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Any other relief which the Applicant is entitled for under the Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Act, 2016 and the Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p>',6422558.30,6650108.51,'2011-06-11 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','..','1','','2008-03-11 00:00:00','2008-03-31 00:00:00','UNIT NO. TVM L1 F11 1102 \"The Views\" at Mohali Hills','','',1,1,0,0,'Narwarbhogal','2018-12-22 10:31:58.000','Narwarbhogal','2018-12-22 10:31:58.000'),(597,1211,'1211',1301,'99fdf70d-599f-4e41-a773-1804cee1ff27','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-22 15:11:37.000','Ravjot Singh  Gill','gillravjot@yahoo.com',8373900100,1122518435,0,'407 GAGAN VIHAR','',10,189,'110051','1','407 GAGAN VIHAR','',10,189,'110051','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-LDH45-PR0060','IREO WATERFRONT','MADHUKAR TULSI','iwpl@ireo.in',9810237279,0,'SCO 6-8, Sector 9-D','1st & 2nd Floor, Madhya Marg',6,128,'160009','0','C-14, 1ST FLOOR','Malviya Nagar',10,557,'110017','1','<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"3\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n <tbody><tr>\r\n  <td style=\"padding:.75pt .75pt .75pt .75pt\">\r\n  <p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt:auto;margin-bottom:0cm;\r\n  margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial Narrow&quot;,sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n  &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:\r\n  EN-IN\">It is submitted that we had booked an independent floor with the above\r\n  stated company in their project Ireo Waterfront situated at Ludhiana. The application\r\n  for allotment was submitted on 18/02/2013 for Unit no.&nbsp;<b>X006A</b>&nbsp;for\r\n  Ground Floor having super area 1532 square foot in a plot size of 236.80 sq\r\n  yard having proportional rights in the said plot. The agreement was executed\r\n  on 07/10/2013 for this unit. The basic price of unit as per agreement is\r\n  Rs.58,23,722/-. In these years we have visited the site office of the company\r\n  regarding completion of the unit but every time we find a new representative\r\n  from the company side with some false promises of early delivery. Clause no\r\n  12.3 of agreement states that normal period of delivery is 24 months from the\r\n  date of execution of agreement. The company had also asked for a grace period\r\n  of 180 days for delay in delivery. But it has been more than five years from\r\n  date of execution of agreement, but no possession has been offered despite\r\n  major percentage of payment as demanded by the company has been paid. Also,\r\n  please refer to clause 12.5 of agreement which states that in event of delay\r\n  by company in submitting notice of completion beyond 12 months from the end\r\n  of grace period then the allottee shall become entitled to opt for\r\n  termination. We have made all the payments diligently as and when advised by\r\n  the company. Till date an amount of Rs 50,68,232/- has been paid (basic +\r\n  tax) by us to the company as per their demand letters received by us but\r\n  there is no sign of completion and delivery of the above said unit. We had\r\n  purchased this unit for our son who was to start his career. All our hopes\r\n  have been dashed and we had to invest in making additional construction at\r\n  our parental house to create an accommodation for him. You are humbly requested\r\n  to get our unit cancelled and our money along with market rate of interest\r\n  and a suitable amount of compensation be returned to us.</span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n  &quot;Times New Roman&q