&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:\r\n  EN-IN\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n </tr>\r\n</tbody></table><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>','1','','2013-10-07 00:00:00','2013-10-07 00:00:00','X006 A','','',1,0,0,0,'gillravjot','2018-12-22 13:55:49.000','gillravjot','2018-12-22 13:55:49.000'),(598,1190,'1190',1256,'d72e4c4b-b5ec-4480-ad45-a996edad35da','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-23 07:23:34.000','SANJAY NEGI','sanket.dhall@gmail.com',9888159159,0,0,'HOUSE NO 630,PANCHKULA HEIGHTS','PEER MUCHALLA ROAD DHAKAULI ZIRAKPUR',28,507,'140603','1','163 SUNNY ENCLAVE ','ZIRAKPUR',28,507,'160055','SANKET DHALL','sanketdhall@gmail.com',9888159159,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0242','CASA HOMES BY FUTURE CITY DEVELOPERS PVT LTD','BHOLA RAM GOYAL','casahomes2016@gmail.com',8128881288,0,'FUTURE CITY DEVELOPERS PVT LTD,AMARI HEIGHTS','SECTOR-115 KHARAR LANDRAN ROAD MOHALI',28,507,'160055','1','FUTURE CITY DEVELOPERS PVT LTD,AMARI HEIGHTS','SECTOR-115 KHARAR LANDRAN ROAD MOHALI',28,507,'160055','1','<p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">THAT THE COMPLAINANT BOOKED AN APARTMENT AT CASA HOMES A&nbsp; PROJECT WITH FUTURE CITY DEVELOPERS AT SECTOR 115 KHARAR LANDRAN ROAD MOHALI, VIDE AGREEMENT TO SELL DATED 23-12-2017 AND ALLOTMENT LETTER DATED 5-4-2018 IN WHICH THE RESPONDENT HAS PROMISED THE COMPLAINANT THAT HE WILL DELIVER THE POSSESSION OF THE FLAT IN JUNE 2018 AND IF NOT POSSIBLE IN JUNE DUE TO NATURAL CALAMINITY THEN THE POSSESSION WILL BE GIVEN ON OCTOBER 2018,BUT TILL DATE RESPONDENT HAS NOT HANDED OVER THE POSSESSION TO THE COMPLAINANT BECAUSE THE WORK IN THE CASA HOMES PROJECT HAS&nbsp; NOT BEEN COMPLETED AS YET,THEREFORE THE SAID POSSESSION HAS NOT BEEN HANDED OVER AS YET,TO SEE THE DEVELOPMENT WORK AT THE SITE, PHOTOGRAPHS OF THE PROJECT AND MY APARTMENT HAS BEEN ANNEXED WITH THE COMPLAINT.THE TOTAL COST OF THE APARTMENT IS 31,80,800/- AND THE COMPLAINANT HAS PAID RUPEES 190,8480/- LAKH TILL DATE TO THE RESPONDENT VIDE RECEIPT NOS 232 AND 257 DATED 21-4-18 AND 14-5-18.THAT THE COMPLAINANT IS READY TO PAY THE PENDING AMOUNT ALSO BUT THE PROJECT IS NOT READY AND THE MONEY THE COMPLAINANT HAS ALREADY PAID TO THE RESPONDENT IS ALL WASTED BECAUSE THE SAID PROJECT IS NOT READY AND RTESPONDENT IS MAKING FOOL OF THE RESPONDENT A DAY AND THE OTHER. AS IT IS THE HARD EARNED MONEY OF THE COMPLAINANT BECAUSE HE IS DOING A PRIVATE JOB AND HAS TAKEN LOAN FROM THE FINANCE COMPANY AMOUNTING TO RS 31,00,000/-,AND PAYING MONTHLY INSTALLEMENTS TO THE LOAN AGENCY FROM HIS HARD EARNED MONEY BUT THE RESPONDENT IS PLAYING WITH THE HARD EARNED MONEY OF THE COMPLAINANT AND DID NOT DELIVER THE POSSESSION&nbsp; TO THE COMPLAINANT TILL DATE. IT IS THEREFORE PRAYED TAHT KINDLY LOOK INTO THE MATTER IN THE INTEREST OF JUSTICE.</span><br></p>','<p>TO REFUND THE AMOUNT OF RS 1908480/-ALONG WITH INTEREST @24% P.A FROM THE DATE OF BOOKING OF THE SAID FLAT.</p>',3180800.00,1908480.00,'2018-06-30 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>N/A</p>','1','','2018-04-05 00:00:00','2018-12-23 00:00:00','CASA HOMES  F-4,TOWER-F4 ,SECTOR-115,KHARAR LANDRAN ROAD MOHALI','','',1,0,0,0,'sanket.dhall','2018-12-23 06:24:00.000','sanket.dhall','2018-12-23 06:24:00.000');
INSERT INTO `verified_table_tbl_rera_complaint_formm_details` VALUES (599,1210,'1210',1295,'f7993d00-eee5-49f1-a16c-9e8bc8af7b5a','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-23 17:51:58.000','Pardeep Pushap','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9991199955,0,813130859759,'House No197 Sector 14 Urban Estate Karnal Haryana','',13,10,'132001','1','House No197 Sector 14 Urban Estate Karnal Haryana','',13,10,'132001','Kamal Dahiya','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9729902009,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0396','Sushma Valencia','Suksha Developers  Pvt Ltd','bharat@sushmabuildtech.com',9876200054,0,'B 107 First Floor Business Complex at Elante Mall Industrial Area Phase1 Chandigarh','',6,128,'160002','1','B 107 First Floor Business Complex at Elante Mall Industrial Area Phase1 Chandigarh','',6,128,'160002','1','<p>The SUSHMA VALENCIA is a Residential Group Housing Colony Project being developed by the Respondent, situated in Zirakpur, Punjab. The flat was booked in the joint name of the Complainant and his wife Vanita Pushap and they paid Rs 5,00,000/- as a token money, out of which Rs 1,00,000 was paid through&nbsp; vide cheque no. 352596 and Rs 1,00,000 was paid through ICICI Bank credit card ANNEXURE C-1. Further they had paid Rs 3,00,000 in cash to the respondents. The respondents had issued a copy of site plan, Floor Plans, Terrace Plans of the said project to the Complainant ANNEXURE C-2. The Respondent also issued a Payment Plan of the said Project to the Complainant ANNEXURE C-3.The Respondents assured the complainants that the said project is RERA approved and all the necessary documentation are being completed. But after the payment of Rs 5,00,000 by the complainant for the booked flat in the said project, the complainants came to know from their reliable sources that the said project is not RERA approved nor the respondents are complying government rules and regulations regarding this. The Complainant visited so many times in the office of the respondents and asked for the documents or refund of the paid amount and many times, the complainant had the telephonic conversation with them regarding this issue, but neither they showed him the documents of RERA Approval nor refunded his money. The Complainant also had the conversation with Bharat Mittal, Additional Director of the respondent Company vide messenger wherein he was asking for refund but he refused to do help him. The Complainant also explained his issues relating to his father who was admitted in Medanta Gurgaon and requested to transfer his amount of Rs 2,00,000 but he refused him by saying that there is no cancellation policy ANNEXURE C-4.The Complainant had requested the respondent so many times to refund his paid amount of Rs 5,00,000/- but the respondent always denying all the requests.</p><p><br></p>','<p>In view of the facts mentioned in paragraphs above, the complainant prays for the following relief(s):-&nbsp;</p><p>i.To give necessary directions to the respondents for return of the payment made in lieu of the flat with the prescribed rate of interest as per the provisions of Section 18 and 19(4) of the RERA Act.</p><p>ii.To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 60 of RERA Act for willful default committed by them.</p><p>iii.To direct the respondents to refund the amount collected from the complainant in lieu of interest, penalty for delayed payments under Rule 23(3)(c) of Punjab RERA Rules,2017.<br></p><p>iv.To issue direction to pay the cost of litigation.<br></p><p>v.Any other relief which this Hon’ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances of this complaint.</p><div><br></div>',0.00,500000.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>i.To direct the respondent not to demand any further amount whatsoever from the complainant.</p><p>ii.The respondent should be restrained from harassing the complainant in any manner whatsoever.</p><p>iii.Any other interim relief which this Hon’ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances of this complaint.</p><div><br></div>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',1,1,0,0,'Pardeep1','2018-12-23 12:56:04.000','Pardeep1','2018-12-23 12:56:04.000'),(600,1212,'1212',1141,'971b1ae7-f8bc-4323-80a7-088b81f8b7db','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Meenal Lall','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,0,'NA 802, Sapthagiri Splendor','BDM-IV',17,67,'560076','0','253, Sector-4, MDC','Mansa Devi Complex',13,15,'134114','Sanjeev Gupta','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0090','SANDWOODS OPULENCIA','M/s Sandwoods Infratech Private Limited','info@sandwoods.com',0,1725003871,'SCO 222-223','Sector-34',6,128,'160022','1','SCO 222-223','Sector-34',6,128,'160022','1','<p>ABC</p>','<p>ABC</p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>ABC</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'rerafilingformm','2018-12-23 15:31:04.000','rerafilingformm','2018-12-23 15:31:04.000'),(601,1212,'1212',1141,'971b1ae7-f8bc-4323-80a7-088b81f8b7db','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Meenal Lall','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,0,'NA 802, Sapthagiri Splendor','BDM-IV',17,67,'560076','0','253, Sector-4, MDC','Mansa Devi Complex',13,15,'134114','Sanjeev Gupta','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0090','SANDWOODS OPULENCIA','M/s Sandwoods Infratech Private Limited','info@sandwoods.com',0,1725003871,'SCO 222-223','Sector-34',6,128,'160022','1','SCO 222-223','Sector-34',6,128,'160022','1','<p>ABC</p>','<p>ABC</p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>ABC</p>','1','','2014-05-01 00:00:00','2014-05-20 00:00:00','Flat No.50, Tower A, 5th Floor, Type- 3BHK, Super Area 1950 sq ft','','',2,0,0,0,'rerafilingformm','2018-12-23 15:32:45.000','rerafilingformm','2018-12-23 15:32:45.000'),(602,1212,'1212',1141,'971b1ae7-f8bc-4323-80a7-088b81f8b7db','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Meenal Lall','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,0,'NA 802, Sapthagiri Splendor','BDM-IV',17,67,'560076','0','253, Sector-4, MDC','Mansa Devi Complex',13,15,'134114','Sanjeev Gupta','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0090','SANDWOODS OPULENCIA','M/s Sandwoods Infratech Private Limited','info@sandwoods.com',0,1725003871,'SCO 222-223','Sector-34',6,128,'160022','1','SCO 222-223','Sector-34',6,128,'160022','1','<p>Respondent allotted a 3BHK residential apartment No.50, Tower-A, 5th floor, Super Area 1950 sq ft to the complainant.  A brochure (C-1) was given to the complainant mentioning the detail regarding the facilities to be provided. Respondent issued the allotment letter dated 1.5.2014 (C-2). The total sale consideration of unit was fixed as Rs. 5070000.It was agreed at that all the specifications will be provided except Ac’s.Respondent also assured to provide cupboards in all the bedrooms(C-3). Buyer’s agreement (C-4) was signed on 20.5.14, as per which the possession was to be handed over within a period of 36 months with grace period of 6 months. Complainant has paid Rs. 5246662/- (including tax of Rs. 186411/- &amp; EDC of Rs. 243750/-). Out of said amount, she has paid Rs. 4816500/- towards the basic price, out of total sale consideration of Rs. 5070000/-. Receipts of Rs.4629635/- (C-5) Apart from the amount of receipts, an amount of Rs. 264859/- &amp; 352168/- paid on 22/5/16 &amp; 2/9/17, thus totaling Rs. 5246662/-. Vide letter 13.8.18 (C-6), it was informed that unit has reached pre-possession stage &amp; more money was demanded, also that the super area has been increased to 2192 sq ft and demanded Rs. 629200/- in lieu of that. On 17.8.18, complainant took up the matter &amp; asked the reason for not informing her earlier about the increase. On visiting the site, the complainant found the area of flat to be same and no addition was found. Next day, complainant visited the respondent &amp; conveyed it that there is no increase. Then respondent made the reduction of 50% &amp; asked him to pay Rs. 314600. Copy of letter/statement is C-7. Inspite of repeated requests, respondent did not give the detail of increased area.It also started demanding Rs. 78912 towards maintenance advance which it cannot demand. Work has not been completed as per the specifications mentioned in brochure. Apartment is not habitable. Photographs are C-8. Loan document C-9. No completion certificate has been received</p>','<p>ABC</p>',0.00,5246662.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<ol><li>To direct the respondent to complete all the pending work and complete the same as per the specifications as mentioned in the brochure (C-1) &amp; letter (C-3)</li><li>To direct the respondent to provide all the common facilities&nbsp;</li></ol>','1','','2014-05-01 00:00:00','2014-05-20 00:00:00','Flat No.50, Tower A, 5th Floor, Type- 3BHK, Super Area 1950 sq ft','','',2,0,0,0,'rerafilingformm','2018-12-23 15:38:30.000','rerafilingformm','2018-12-23 15:38:30.000'),(603,1212,'1212',1141,'971b1ae7-f8bc-4323-80a7-088b81f8b7db','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Meenal Lall','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,0,'NA 802, Sapthagiri Splendor','BDM-IV',17,67,'560076','0','253, Sector-4, MDC','Mansa Devi Complex',13,15,'134114','Sanjeev Gupta','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0090','SANDWOODS OPULENCIA','M/s Sandwoods Infratech Private Limited','info@sandwoods.com',0,1725003871,'SCO 222-223','Sector-34',6,128,'160022','1','SCO 222-223','Sector-34',6,128,'160022','1','<p>Respondent allotted a 3BHK residential apartment No.50, Tower-A, 5th floor, Super Area 1950 sq ft to the complainant.  A brochure (C-1) was given to the complainant mentioning the detail regarding the facilities to be provided. Respondent issued the allotment letter dated 1.5.2014 (C-2). The total sale consideration of unit was fixed as Rs. 5070000.It was agreed at that all the specifications will be provided except Ac’s.Respondent also assured to provide cupboards in all the bedrooms(C-3). Buyer’s agreement (C-4) was signed on 20.5.14, as per which the possession was to be handed over within a period of 36 months with grace period of 6 months. Complainant has paid Rs. 5246662/- (including tax of Rs. 186411/- &amp; EDC of Rs. 243750/-). Out of said amount, she has paid Rs. 4816500/- towards the basic price, out of total sale consideration of Rs. 5070000/-. Receipts of Rs.4629635/- (C-5) Apart from the amount of receipts, an amount of Rs. 264859/- &amp; 352168/- paid on 22/5/16 &amp; 2/9/17, thus totaling Rs. 5246662/-. Vide letter 13.8.18 (C-6), it was informed that unit has reached pre-possession stage &amp; more money was demanded, also that the super area has been increased to 2192 sq ft and demanded Rs. 629200/- in lieu of that. On 17.8.18, complainant took up the matter &amp; asked the reason for not informing her earlier about the increase. On visiting the site, the complainant found the area of flat to be same and no addition was found. Next day, complainant visited the respondent &amp; conveyed it that there is no increase. Then respondent made the reduction of 50% &amp; asked him to pay Rs. 314600. Copy of letter/statement is C-7. Inspite of repeated requests, respondent did not give the detail of increased area.It also started demanding Rs. 78912 towards maintenance advance which it cannot demand. Work has not been completed as per the specifications mentioned in brochure. Apartment is not habitable. Photographs are C-8. Loan document C-9. No completion certificate has been received</p>','<ol><li>To direct the respondent to handover the possession of the apartment complete in all respect along with the specifications as provided in the brochure (*C-1) &amp; Letter (C-3), along with the interest for the delay in possession, to be calculated w.e.f. 20.05.2017 till the date of actual delivery of possession after obtaining the completion certificate.</li><li>To direct the respondent not to charge Rs. 314000/- towards the enhanced area as there has been no change in the area of the flat.</li><li>To direct the respondent not to charge Rs. 78912/- towards the maintenance advance of two years.</li></ol>',0.00,5246662.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<ol><li>To direct the respondent to complete all the pending work and complete the same as per the specifications as mentioned in the brochure (C-1) &amp; letter (C-3)</li><li>To direct the respondent to provide all the common facilities&nbsp;</li></ol>','1','','2014-05-01 00:00:00','2014-05-20 00:00:00','Flat No.50, Tower A, 5th Floor, Type- 3BHK, Super Area 1950 sq ft','','',2,0,0,0,'rerafilingformm','2018-12-23 15:54:20.000','rerafilingformm','2018-12-23 15:54:20.000'),(604,1212,'1212',1141,'971b1ae7-f8bc-4323-80a7-088b81f8b7db','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Meenal Lall','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,0,'NA 802, Sapthagiri Splendor','BDM-IV',17,67,'560076','0','253, Sector-4, MDC','Mansa Devi Complex',13,15,'134114','Sanjeev Gupta','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0090','SANDWOODS OPULENCIA','M/s Sandwoods Infratech Private Limited','info@sandwoods.com',0,1725003871,'SCO 222-223','Sector-34',6,128,'160022','1','SCO 222-223','Sector-34',6,128,'160022','1','<p>Respondent allotted a 3BHK residential apartment No.50, Tower-A, 5th floor, Super Area 1950 sq ft to the complainant.  A brochure (C-1) was given to the complainant mentioning the detail regarding the facilities to be provided. Respondent issued the allotment letter dated 1.5.2014 (C-2). The total sale consideration of unit was fixed as Rs. 5070000.It was agreed at that all the specifications will be provided except Ac’s.Respondent also assured to provide cupboards in all the bedrooms(C-3). Buyer’s agreement (C-4) was signed on 20.5.14, as per which the possession was to be handed over within a period of 36 months with grace period of 6 months. Complainant has paid Rs. 5246662/- (including tax of Rs. 186411/- &amp; EDC of Rs. 243750/-). Out of said amount, she has paid Rs. 4816500/- towards the basic price, out of total sale consideration of Rs. 5070000/-. Receipts of Rs.4629635/- (C-5) Apart from the amount of receipts, an amount of Rs. 264859/- &amp; 352168/- paid on 22/5/16 &amp; 2/9/17, thus totaling Rs. 5246662/-. Vide letter 13.8.18 (C-6), it was informed that unit has reached pre-possession stage &amp; more money was demanded, also that the super area has been increased to 2192 sq ft and demanded Rs. 629200/- in lieu of that. On 17.8.18, complainant took up the matter &amp; asked the reason for not informing her earlier about the increase. On visiting the site, the complainant found the area of flat to be same and no addition was found. Next day, complainant visited the respondent &amp; conveyed it that there is no increase. Then respondent made the reduction of 50% &amp; asked him to pay Rs. 314600. Copy of letter/statement is C-7. Inspite of repeated requests, respondent did not give the detail of increased area.It also started demanding Rs. 78912 towards maintenance advance which it cannot demand. Work has not been completed as per the specifications mentioned in brochure. Apartment is not habitable. Photographs are C-8. Loan document C-9. No completion certificate has been received</p>','<ol><li>To direct the respondent to handover the possession of the apartment complete in all respect along with the specifications as provided in the brochure (*C-1) &amp; Letter (C-3), along with the interest for the delay in possession, to be calculated w.e.f. 20.05.2017 till the date of actual delivery of possession after obtaining the completion certificate.</li><li>To direct the respondent not to charge Rs. 314000/- towards the enhanced area as there has been no change in the area of the flat.</li><li>To direct the respondent not to charge Rs. 78912/- towards the maintenance advance of two years.</li></ol>',0.00,5246662.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<ol><li>To direct the respondent to complete all the pending work and complete the same as per the specifications as mentioned in the brochure (C-1) &amp; letter (C-3)</li><li>To direct the respondent to provide all the common facilities&nbsp;</li></ol>','1','','2014-05-01 00:00:00','2014-05-20 00:00:00','Flat No.50, Tower A, 5th Floor, Type- 3BHK, Super Area 1950 sq ft','','',2,0,0,0,'rerafilingformm','2018-12-23 15:54:42.000','rerafilingformm','2018-12-23 15:54:42.000'),(605,1213,'1213',1010,'a182232b-88d6-4711-8baa-f8a026fb675f','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-23 16:49:48.000','Raj Kumar and Kuljeet Kaur','lawofficeofhimanshuraj@gmail.com',9988100005,0,999057822446,'#102, Sector 10 A','',6,128,'160011','1','#102, Sector 10 A','',6,128,'160011','HIMANSHU RAJ','lawofficeofhimanshuraj@gmail.com',9988200001,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0005','Josan Heights','JSJ Builders Pvt Ltd','jsjbuilders.in@gmail.com',8699885568,0,'Shop No. 1-3, Josan Heights','Sector 126, Village Chhajumajra, Teh-Kharar',28,507,'140307','1','Shop No. 1-3, Josan Heights','Sector 126, Village Chhajumajra, Teh-Kharar',28,507,'140307','1','<p class=\"Normal2\" style=\"margin-left:36.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-36.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: Thorndale, serif;\">1.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: Thorndale, serif;\">That the complainant is a citizen\r\nof India and is residing at the address<b>&nbsp; House No. &nbsp;<u>1541/2, PAHSE 10, MOHALI, PUNJAB </u></b>.\r\nThe Aadhar card of the complainant is annexed as <b><u>ANNEXURE C 1.</u></b> He has given his hard earned money in the OPs\r\nnew Project <b>Josan Heights</b> situated\r\nin Sector 126, kharar, Mohali, PB for booking of a residential flat.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"Normal2\" style=\"margin-top:10.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:10.0pt;\r\nmargin-left:36.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-36.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nmso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;border:none;mso-padding-alt:31.0pt 31.0pt 31.0pt 31.0pt;\r\nmso-border-shadow:yes\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: Thorndale, serif;\">2.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: Thorndale, serif;\">That the opposite party is a\r\nCompany and has, at all material points of time, been and is still engaged in\r\nthe commercial business of developing and selling housing projects flats and\r\nother construction layouts to various individuals and or others in lieu of\r\nvaluable considerations for profit being their primary objective</span><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: Thorndale, serif;\">. <u><o:p></o:p></u></span></p><p class=\"Normal2\" style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:0cm;\r\nmargin-left:36.0pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-indent:-36.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nborder:none;mso-padding-alt:31.0pt 31.0pt 31.0pt 31.0pt;mso-border-shadow:yes\"><u><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: Thorndale, serif;\"><o:p><span style=\"text-decoration-line: none;\">&nbsp;</span></o:p></span></u></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-indent:-36.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nmso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: Thorndale, serif;\">3.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: Thorndale, serif;\">That the OP Builder Company as part\r\nof their business venture decided to develop a residential space <b>Josan Heights</b> situated in Sector 126,\r\nkharar, Mohali, PB. The OP Builder had published various web and news\r\nadvertisements as well as visual advertisements to attract the public at large\r\nto purchase residential space in the said project. The OP had promised the\r\ncomplainant state of the art residential spaces that are affordable yet modern\r\nand well equipped residential project within a reasonable time period. However,\r\nat the time of selling of the present property to the complainant, the title of\r\nthe land was defective<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"Normal2\" style=\"margin-left:36.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-36.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><br></p>','<p class=\"Normal2CxSpFirst\" style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:\r\n0cm;margin-left:36.0pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;mso-add-space:auto;text-align:\r\njustify;text-indent:-36.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;\r\nborder:none;mso-padding-alt:31.0pt 31.0pt 31.0pt 31.0pt;mso-border-shadow:yes\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: Thorndale, serif;\">(i)<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 13pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: Thorndale, serif;\">To refund the complete amount which\r\nhas been deposited against the residential property so booked by the\r\ncomplainant along with an Interest on the amount from the date of deposit at\r\nthe rate of 28 per cent&nbsp; till the actual\r\nrealization of the complete amount within 90 days according to section 18 1\r\nReal Estate Regulation And Development Act, 2016, Section 19 4 of The Real\r\nEstate Regulation And Development Act, 2016, r w Rule 16 and Rule 17 of Punjab\r\nState Real Estate Regulation and Development Rules, 2017<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"Normal2\" style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:0cm;\r\nmargin-left:36.0pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-36.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;border:none;mso-padding-alt:31.0pt 31.0pt 31.0pt 31.0pt;\r\nmso-border-shadow:yes\"><span style=\"font-size: 13pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: Thorndale, serif;\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p class=\"Normal2CxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:\r\n0cm;margin-left:36.0pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;mso-add-space:auto;text-align:\r\njustify;text-indent:-36.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;\r\ntab-stops:36.0pt;border:none;mso-padding-alt:31.0pt 31.0pt 31.0pt 31.0pt;\r\nmso-border-shadow:yes\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: Thorndale, serif;\">(ii)<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 13pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: Thorndale, serif;\">To direct the Opposite party to pay\r\nRs. 20,00,000&nbsp; for causing mental agony\r\ncaused to the complainant.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"Normal2\" style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:0cm;\r\nmargin-left:36.0pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-indent:-36.0pt;border:none;\r\nmso-padding-alt:31.0pt 31.0pt 31.0pt 31.0pt;mso-border-shadow:yes\"><span style=\"font-size: 13pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Thorndale, serif;\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<span style=\"font-size: 13pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Thorndale, serif;\">To direct the Opposite party to pay Rs. 14,00,000 to\r\nthe complainant as the deficiency in services for keeping the complainant in\r\ndark in regard to the progress of the property.</span><br></p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Not Prayed</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'lawofficeofhimanshuraj','2018-12-23 16:19:41.000','lawofficeofhimanshuraj','2018-12-23 16:19:41.000'),(606,1132,'1132',1193,'109a020f-7ac8-4af7-9194-064fff6a2fe0','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-20 13:56:52.000','Trilok Singh','parveen.ch.2@gmail.com',8882950006,0,0,'Ward No. 10, Balachaur','tehsil Balachaur',28,527,'144521','1','Ward No. 10, Balachaur','tehsil Balachaur',28,527,'144521','PARVEEN CHAUDHARY','parveen.ch.2@gmail.com',8882950006,0,'Allottee','PBRERA-SAS81-PM0010','Industrial knowledge (fashion Technology) Park at sector 90 SAS Nagar','Chandigarh overseas Pvt. Ltd','jbp@j90.in',0,1149879480,'M/s. Chandigarh Overseas Pvt. Ltd., SCO 249, Sector 44-C, Chandigarh.','',6,128,'160047','1','M/s. Chandigarh Overseas Pvt. Ltd., SCO 249, Sector 44-C, Chandigarh.','',6,128,'160047','1','<p>1. That the respondent M/s Chandigarh overseas Pvt. Ltd launched a scheme called “Small Investors Scheme” vide which a share in design studio of an area measuring 100 sq feet on the 4th floors of Industrial Knowledge(Fashion Technology) Park Sector 90, SAS Nagar was offered to the Prospector Buyer(s) on the free hold basis as a co-owner of  Design Studio.\r\n</p><p>2.	That the complainant Trilok Singh submitted application No. 104045 dated 18.01.2008 for purchase of one unit i.e. measuring 100 Sq feet for total consideration of Rs. 6,50,000/- and  again he purchased six more unit @ Rs. 6,50,000/- per unit, vide another Developer Buyer Agreement dated  18.03.2018 and lease deed was executed between complainant and respondent No. 2.  As per above said agreement, complainant paid        Rs. 50,000/- to respondent No. 1 vide receipt dated 18.01.2008 and further sum of Rs. 34,56,000/- was paid to respondent vide receipt dated 18.03.2008.  Further Rs. 5,26,000/- was paid to respondent No. 1 vide receipt dated 19.03.2008.  Complainant had paid sum of                 Rs. 40,32,000/- for purchase of said seven units to respondents.\r\n</p><p>3.	That as per Developer Buyer Agreements the possession was to be delivered after 30 months from the date of start of construction, but till filing of the complaint, respondent has failed to deliver physical possession of said units to complainant.&nbsp; An additional lease agreement was also made as mentioned in para 5th of the developer buyer agreement regarding rent with M/s Green Field Sites Management pvt ltd and no rent has been paid till now as mentioned in the agreement.</p>','<p><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 115%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">It is therefore submitted through this complaint\r\nthat the respondents have failed to comply with the conditions mentioned in the developer buyer agreement so the respondents may be directed to give the possession of units as per the\r\ndeveloper buyer agreements dated 31.01.2008 &amp; 18.03.2008 along with the\r\nrent or the interest as described in the agreements qua and if the respondent\r\ndo not give the possession as per the agreements qua, in that event the amount\r\nof Rs. 40,32,000/- along with the interest @ Rs. 1% per month on the principle\r\namount may be paid to the complainant.</span><br></p>',4550000.00,4032000.00,'2010-07-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;\r\nmso-add-space:auto;text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;text-indent:\r\n-18.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">1.</span><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 14px; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">That\r\nduring the pendency of the complaint the property of respondent may be attached\r\nand amount paid by the complainant to the respondent may be got returned.</span><o:p></o:p></span></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','2008-01-31 00:00:00','floor no. 4, block A2 Industrial Knowledge (fashion Technology) Park, sector 90, SAS Nagar (Punjab)','','',2,0,0,0,'parveenchaudhary','2018-12-23 21:08:29.000','parveenchaudhary','2018-12-23 21:08:29.000'),(607,1132,'1132',1193,'109a020f-7ac8-4af7-9194-064fff6a2fe0','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-23 21:11:38.000','Trilok Singh','parveen.ch.2@gmail.com',8882950006,0,0,'Ward No. 10, Balachaur','tehsil Balachaur',28,527,'144521','1','Ward No. 10, Balachaur','tehsil Balachaur',28,527,'144521','PARVEEN CHAUDHARY','parveen.ch.2@gmail.com',8882950006,0,'Allottee','PBRERA-SAS81-PM0010','Industrial knowledge (fashion Technology) Park at sector 90 SAS Nagar','Chandigarh overseas Pvt. Ltd','jbp@j90.in',0,1149879480,'M/s. Chandigarh Overseas Pvt. Ltd., SCO 249, Sector 44-C, Chandigarh.','',6,128,'160047','1','M/s. Chandigarh Overseas Pvt. Ltd., SCO 249, Sector 44-C, Chandigarh.','',6,128,'160047','1','<p>1. That the respondent M/s Chandigarh overseas Pvt. Ltd launched a scheme called “Small Investors Scheme” vide which a share in design studio of an area measuring 100 sq feet on the 4th floors of Industrial Knowledge(Fashion Technology) Park Sector 90, SAS Nagar was offered to the Prospector Buyer(s) on the free hold basis as a co-owner of  Design Studio.\r\n</p><p>2.	That the complainant Trilok Singh submitted application No. 104045 dated 18.01.2008 for purchase of one unit i.e. measuring 100 Sq feet for total consideration of Rs. 6,50,000/- and  again he purchased six more unit @ Rs. 6,50,000/- per unit, vide another Developer Buyer Agreement dated  18.03.2018 and lease deed was executed between complainant and respondent No. 2.  As per above said agreement, complainant paid        Rs. 50,000/- to respondent No. 1 vide receipt dated 18.01.2008 and further sum of Rs. 34,56,000/- was paid to respondent vide receipt dated 18.03.2008.  Further Rs. 5,26,000/- was paid to respondent No. 1 vide receipt dated 19.03.2008.  Complainant had paid sum of                 Rs. 40,32,000/- for purchase of said seven units to respondents.\r\n</p><p>3.	That as per Developer Buyer Agreements the possession was to be delivered after 30 months from the date of start of construction, but till filing of the complaint, respondent has failed to deliver physical possession of said units to complainant.&nbsp; An additional lease agreement was also made as mentioned in para 5th of the developer buyer agreement regarding rent with M/s Green Field Sites Management pvt ltd and no rent has been paid till now as mentioned in the agreement.</p><p>4. that complainant is filing the complaint through Attorney Bhupinder Singh</p>','<p><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 115%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">It is therefore submitted through this complaint\r\nthat the respondents have failed to comply with the conditions mentioned in the developer buyer agreement so the respondents may be directed to give the possession of units as per the\r\ndeveloper buyer agreements dated 31.01.2008 &amp; 18.03.2008 along with the\r\nrent or the interest as described in the agreements qua and if the respondent\r\ndo not give the possession as per the agreements qua, in that event the amount\r\nof Rs. 40,32,000/- along with the interest @ Rs. 1% per month on the principle\r\namount may be paid to the complainant.</span><br></p>',4550000.00,4032000.00,'2010-07-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;\r\nmso-add-space:auto;text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;text-indent:\r\n-18.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">1.</span><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 14px; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">That\r\nduring the pendency of the complaint the property of respondent may be attached\r\nand amount paid by the complainant to the respondent may be got returned.</span><o:p></o:p></span></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','2008-01-31 00:00:00','floor no. 4, block A2 Industrial Knowledge (fashion Technology) Park, sector 90, SAS Nagar (Punjab)','','',2,0,0,0,'parveenchaudhary','2018-12-23 21:11:35.000','parveenchaudhary','2018-12-23 21:11:35.000'),(608,1212,'1212',1141,'971b1ae7-f8bc-4323-80a7-088b81f8b7db','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Meenal Lall','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,0,'NA 802, Sapthagiri Splendor','BDM-IV',17,67,'560076','0','253, Sector-4, MDC','Mansa Devi Complex',13,15,'134114','Sanjeev Gupta','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0090','SANDWOODS OPULENCIA','M/s Sandwoods Infratech Private Limited','info@sandwoods.com',0,1725003871,'SCO 222-223','Sector-34',6,128,'160022','1','SCO 222-223','Sector-34',6,128,'160022','1','<p>Respondent allotted a 3BHK residential apartment No.50, Tower-A, 5th floor, Super Area 1950 sq ft to the complainant.  A brochure (C-1) was given to the complainant mentioning the detail regarding the facilities to be provided. Respondent issued the allotment letter dated 1.5.2014 (C-2). The total sale consideration of unit was fixed as Rs. 5070000.It was agreed at that all the specifications will be provided except Ac’s.Respondent also assured to provide cupboards in all the bedrooms(C-3). Buyer’s agreement (C-4) was signed on 20.5.14, as per which the possession was to be handed over within a period of 36 months with grace period of 6 months. Complainant has paid Rs. 5246662/- (including tax of Rs. 186411/- &amp; EDC of Rs. 243750/-). Out of said amount, she has paid Rs. 4816500/- towards the basic price, out of total sale consideration of Rs. 5070000/-. Receipts of Rs.4629635/- (C-5) Apart from the amount of receipts, an amount of Rs. 264859/- &amp; 352168/- paid on 22/5/16 &amp; 2/9/17, thus totaling Rs. 5246662/-. Vide letter 13.8.18 (C-6), it was informed that unit has reached pre-possession stage &amp; more money was demanded, also that the super area has been increased to 2192 sq ft and demanded Rs. 629200/- in lieu of that. On 17.8.18, complainant took up the matter &amp; asked the reason for not informing her earlier about the increase. On visiting the site, the complainant found the area of flat to be same and no addition was found. Next day, complainant visited the respondent &amp; conveyed it that there is no increase. Then respondent made the reduction of 50% &amp; asked him to pay Rs. 314600. Copy of letter/statement is C-7. Inspite of repeated requests, respondent did not give the detail of increased area.It also started demanding Rs. 78912 towards maintenance advance which it cannot demand. Work has not been completed as per the specifications mentioned in brochure. Apartment is not habitable. Photographs are C-8. Loan document C-9. No completion certificate has been received</p>','<ol><li>To direct the respondent to handover the possession of the apartment complete in all respect along with the specifications as provided in the brochure (*C-1) &amp; Letter (C-3), along with the interest for the delay in possession, to be calculated w.e.f. 20.05.2017 till the date of actual delivery of possession after obtaining the completion certificate.</li><li>To direct the respondent not to charge Rs. 314000/- towards the enhanced area as there has been no change in the area of the flat.</li><li>To direct the respondent not to charge Rs. 78912/- towards the maintenance advance of two years.</li></ol>',0.00,5246662.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<ol><li>To direct the respondent to complete all the pending work and complete the same as per the specifications as mentioned in the brochure (C-1) &amp; letter (C-3)</li><li>To direct the respondent to provide all the common facilities&nbsp;</li></ol>','1','','2014-05-01 00:00:00','2014-05-20 00:00:00','Flat No.50, Tower A, 5th Floor, Type- 3BHK, Super Area 1950 sq ft','','',2,0,0,0,'rerafilingformm','2018-12-23 21:30:48.000','rerafilingformm','2018-12-23 21:30:48.000'),(609,1212,'1212',1141,'971b1ae7-f8bc-4323-80a7-088b81f8b7db','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Meenal Lall','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,0,'NA 802, Sapthagiri Sp