 5070000.It was agreed at that all the specifications will be provided except Ac’s.Respondent also assured to provide cupboards in all the bedrooms(C-3). Buyer’s agreement (C-4) was signed on 20.5.14, as per which the possession was to be handed over within a period of 36 months. Complainant has paid Rs. 5246662/- (including tax of Rs. 186411/- &amp; EDC of Rs. 243750/-). Out of said amount, she has paid Rs. 4816500/- towards the basic price, out of total sale consideration of Rs. 5070000/-. Receipts of Rs.4629635/- (C-5) Apart from the amount of receipts, an amount of Rs. 264859/- &amp; 352168/- paid on 22/5/16 &amp; 2/9/17, thus totaling Rs. 5246662/-. Vide letter 13.8.18 (C-6), it was informed that unit has reached pre-possession stage &amp; more money was demanded, also that the super area has been increased to 2192 sq ft and demanded Rs. 629200/- in lieu of that. On 17.8.18, complainant took up the matter &amp; asked the reason for not informing her earlier about the increase. On visiting the site, the complainant found the area of flat to be same and no addition was found. Next day, complainant visited the respondent &amp; conveyed it that there is no increase. Then respondent made the reduction of 50% &amp; asked him to pay Rs. 314600. Copy of letter/statement is C-7. Inspite of repeated requests, respondent did not give the detail of increased area.It also started demanding Rs. 78912 towards maintenance advance which it cannot demand. Work has not been completed as per the specifications mentioned in brochure. Apartment is not habitable. Photographs are C-8. Loan document C-9. No completion certificate has been received</p>','<ol><li>To direct the respondent to handover the possession of the apartment complete in all respect along with the specifications as provided in the brochure (C-1) &amp; Letter (C-3), along with the interest for the delay in possession, to be calculated w.e.f. 20.05.2017 till the date of actual delivery of possession after obtaining the completion certificate.</li><li>To direct the respondent not to charge Rs. 314000/- towards the enhanced area as there has been no change in the area of the flat.The respondent has arbitrarily increased the area. Moreover it has never informed the complainant that area will be increased. It is only in August, 2018 vide letter Annexure C-6, it informed that area has been increased.</li><li>To direct the respondent not to charge Rs. 78912/- towards the maintenance advance of two years.</li></ol>',0.00,5246662.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<ol><li>To direct the respondent to complete all the pending work and complete the same as per the specifications as mentioned in the brochure (C-1) &amp; letter (C-3)</li><li>To direct the respondent to provide all the common facilities</li></ol>','1','','2014-05-01 00:00:00','2014-05-20 00:00:00','Flat No.50, Tower A, 5th Floor, Type- 3BHK, Super Area 1950 sq ft','','',2,0,0,0,'rerafilingformm','2018-12-23 21:51:48.000','rerafilingformm','2018-12-23 21:51:48.000'),(613,1212,'1212',1141,'971b1ae7-f8bc-4323-80a7-088b81f8b7db','FormTypeM',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Meenal Lall','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,0,'NA 802, Sapthagiri Splendor','BDM-IV',17,67,'560076','0','253, Sector-4, MDC','Mansa Devi Complex',13,15,'134114','Sanjeev Gupta','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0090','SANDWOODS OPULENCIA','M/s Sandwoods Infratech Private Limited','info@sandwoods.com',0,1725003871,'SCO 222-223','Sector-34',6,128,'160022','1','SCO 222-223','Sector-34',6,128,'160022','1','<p>Respondent allotted a 3BHK residential apartment No.50, Tower-A, 5th floor, Super Area 1950 sq ft to the complainant.  A brochure (C-1) was given to the complainant mentioning the detail regarding the facilities to be provided. Respondent issued the allotment letter dated 1.5.2014 (C-2). The total sale consideration of unit was fixed as Rs. 5070000.It was agreed at that all the specifications w