 Act. This is also borne out by many orders/judgments of\r\nthe Punjab Real Estate Regulatory Authority/Adjudicating Officer.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:6.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:12.0pt;\r\nmargin-left:0cm\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:\r\nEN-IN\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;<b><o:p></o:p></b></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-right:-2.3pt\"><b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%\">a. &nbsp;</span></b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\r\nline-height:115%\">History of the case, event dates and justification for\r\nsubmitting earlier application in Form- N is given in Annexure 10. A perusal of\r\nthis makes it apparent that Complainants are back to square one after about 3\r\nmonths of filing first application due to no fault of theirs.&nbsp; <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-right:-2.3pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\r\nline-height:115%\">Complainants seek expeditious relief and disposal of present complaint\r\nwithin two months as provided for in Section 29 (4), as sacred a section as any\r\nother, of the Act. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-right:-2.3pt\"><b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%\">b. </span></b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%\">&nbsp;The facts given in Para (4) above establish\r\nthat Respondent has failed to deliver possession of the allotted Unit including\r\nCar Parking by the stipulated date in Agreement of Sale. &nbsp;Section 18 of the Act provides that, if the\r\npromoter fails to complete or is unable to give possession by such a date for\r\nany reason and the allottee(s) wishes to withdraw from the project, he shall be\r\nliable 