arking-Rs300000, Due at Possession-Rs 197053. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:6.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:0cm;\r\nmargin-left:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;line-height:normal\"><b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\">b.</span></b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\"> Respondent has committed to hand\r\nover possession of the unit on or before Feb 4, 2017 as per Buyers\r\nAgreement/Agreement of Sale (relevant 3 pages of agreement at Annexure 3) but\r\nhas failed to deliver possession by the stipulated date which is evident from\r\nhis letter dated Feb 7, 2018 (Annexure 4). <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;line-height:\r\nnormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;line-height:\r\nnormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\">The\r\nproject is far from completion. Respondent has provided a copy of so called\r\nCompletion/Occupancy Certificate dated December 14, 2016 (Annexures 5) but it\r\ncertifies neither completion nor fitness for occupancy. It itself admits\r\nincompletion by laying down 7 conditions and subjecting it to obtaining a\r\nnumber of certificates. Furthermore it stipulates that noncompliance of any of\r\nthe conditions will render it redundant. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\">The\r\nbottom line and the relevant fact is that Respondent has failed to complete the\r\nproject and give possession by the date committed in the Agreement for sale.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:\r\n115%\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></b></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:\r\n115%\">c.</span></b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%\">\r\nComplainants have served a Legal Notice dated June 27, 2018 upon Respondent\r\n(Annexure 6). He has been requested to refund the received amount of Rs. 4250362/-\r\nwith interest plus compensation within 30 days of the receipt of the notice.\r\nThe notice was received on July 5, 2018 but there has been no response.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:6.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:12.0pt;\r\nmargin-left:0cm\"><b><span style=\"font-size:\r\n12.0pt;line-height:115%\">d.</span></b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:\r\n115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-language:EN-IN\"> This is an ongoing project and it is now well\r\nsettled law that the Real Estate Act is applicable to such projects as per\r\nBombay High Court Order in WP 2737/2017 and other similar petitions. Any terms\r\nand conditions, which are contrary to express provisions of the Act are invalid\r\nand overridden by the Act. This is also borne out by many orders/judgments of\r\nthe Punjab Real Estate Regulatory Authority/Adjudicating Officer.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:6.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:12.0pt;\r\nmargin-left:0cm\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:\r\nEN-IN\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;<b><o:p></o:p></b></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-right:-2.3pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\r\nline-height:115%\">a<b>. &nbsp;</b>History of the case, event dates and\r\njustification for submitting earlier application in Form- N is given in\r\nAnnexure 10. A perusal of this makes it apparent that Complainants are back to\r\nsquare one after about 3 months of filing first application due to no fault of\r\ntheirs.&nbsp; <o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-right:-2.3pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\r\nline-height:115%\">Complainants seek expeditious relief under Section 18 and\r\ndisposal of the present complaint within two months as provided for in Section\r\n29 (4), as sacred a section as any other, of the Act. <o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-right:-2.3pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\r\nline-height:115%\">b<b>. </b>&nbsp;The facts given in Para (4) above establish\r\nthat Respondent has failed to deliver possession of the allotted Unit including\r\nCar Parking by the stipulated date in Agreement of Sale. &nbsp;Section 18 of the Act provides that, if the\r\npromoter fails to complete or is unable to give possession by such a date for\r\nany reason and the allottee(s) wishes to withdraw from the project, he shall be\r\nliable to return the amount received by him along with interest including\r\ncompensation.<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-right:-2.3pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\r\nline-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\">&nbsp;Complainants are withdrawing from the project\r\nand claiming here the following relief. They will file a separate application\r\nfor compensation with the Adjudicating Officer. <o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:6.0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\r\nline-height:115%\">I. Refund of Amount Received (Annexure2) = </span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\">Rs 4250362.00<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:6.0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\r\nline-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\">II. Payment of Interest: (i) Up to\r\n</span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%\">30.11.2018 (Annexure 2)\r\n= </span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times-Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:Times-Roman\">Rs 2152873.00 <o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:6.0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\r\nline-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times-Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:Times-Roman\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp; (ii) From 01.12.2018 to day of refund, say =\r\nINT</sp