e=\"margin-right:-2.3pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\r\nline-height:115%\">Complainants seek expeditious relief under Section 18 and\r\ndisposal of the present complaint within two months as provided for in Section\r\n29 (4), as sacred a section as any other, of the Act. <o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-right:-2.3pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\r\nline-height:115%\">b<b>. </b>&nbsp;The facts given in Para (4) above establish\r\nthat Respondent has failed to deliver possession of the allotted Unit including\r\nCar Parking by the stipulated date in Agreement of Sale. &nbsp;Section 18 of the Act provides that, if the\r\npromoter fails to complete or is unable to give possession by such a date for\r\nany reason and the allottee(s) wishes to withdraw from the project, he shall be\r\nliable to return the amount received by him along with interest including\r\ncompensation.<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-right:-2.3pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\r\nline-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\">&nbsp;Complainants are withdrawing from the project\r\nand claiming here the following relief. They will file a separate application\r\nfor compensation with the Adjudicating Officer. <o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:6.0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\r\nline-height:115%\">I. Refund of Amount Received (Annexure2) = </span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\">Rs 4250362.00<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:6.0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\r\nline-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\">II. Payment of Interest: (i) Up to\r\n</span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%\">30.11.2018 (Annexure 2)\r\n= </span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times-Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:Times-Roman\">Rs 2152873.00 <o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:6.0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\r\nline-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times-Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:Times-Roman\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp; (ii) From 01.12.2018 to day of refund, say =\r\nINT</span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\"> <o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:6.0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\r\nline-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\">III. Total Claim = Rs 6403235.00\r\n+ INT<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-right:-2.3pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\r\nline-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>',4447415.00,4250362.00,'2017-02-04 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>N.A.</p>','1','','2016-02-05 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','31B, 3rd Floor, Royal Business Park, Chandigarh- Ambala Highway, Zirakpur','','',2,0,0,0,'kssidhu','2018-12-25 19:37:53.000','kssidhu','2018-12-25 19:37:53.000'),(642,1197,'1197',1287,'fcebf583-f701-4375-a441-163b29a0faf5','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-26 09:09:34.000','Brinder  Singh','kashika.juneja91@gmail.com',9814013127,0,0,'House No. 607','sector 18B',6,128,'160018','1','House No. 607','sector 18B',6,128,'160018','Gaurav Chopra','gaurav.chopra@hotmail.com',9814013125,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0119','Mohali Hills','Emaar MGF Land Ltd','sorabh.kakar@emaarmgf.com',0,0,'Emaar MGF Land Ltd','40, Central Plaza, Ground Floor, Sector 105 Mohali',28,507,'140306','1','Emaar MGF Land Ltd','40, Central Plaza, Ground Floor, Sector 105 Mohali',28,507,'140306','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-indent: -43px; margin-left: 0.5in; line-height: 200%;\"><font face=\"Garamond, serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">i)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That the Applicants had sought allotment of a Residential Apartment in “The Views”, Mohali Hills and were Allotted Unit No. TVM K1-FPH-PH02, Tower K1, ‘The Views’, Mohali Hills, Sector 105, Mohali for which a Buyer’s Agreement 13.6.11 was executed between the Applicants and Respondent.&nbsp;</span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-indent: -43px; margin-left: 0.5in; line-height: 200%;\"><font face=\"Garamond, serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">ii)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That out of the total sale consideration of Rs. 1,04,28,413/-, the amount previously paid by the Applicants in respect of a Built Up Villa No. 10, Sector 106, Mohali, the allotment whereof was cancelled vide a letter dated 25.3.11 issued by the Respondent on mutually accepted terms, was adjusted and over and above the said amount, a further sum of Rs. 15,31,688.13/- was paid by the Applicants upto 27.8.2012 and thus, an amount of Rs. 1,07,66,807/- was paid in respect of the Allotted Unit.</span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-indent: -43px; margin-left: 0.5in; line-height: 200%;\"><font face=\"Garamond, serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">iii)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That the Respondent wilfully defaulted in offering possession of the Allotted Unit by the second quarter of 2012, as assured by the Respondent at the time of migrating the applicants from the Built Up Villa to the Allotted Unit, or within stipulated time period as per Clause 21.1 of the Buyer’s Agreement i.e. 13.12.2014. Consequently, vide an email&nbsp; 20.10.17, the Buyer’s Agreement dated 13.6.11 was rescinded by the Applicants while inter alia calling upon the Respondent to forthwith refund the entire amount paid by them alongwith interest.</span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-indent: -43px; margin-left: 0.5in; line-height: 200%;\"><font face=\"Garamond, serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">iv)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That despite receipt of the aforesaid email 20.10.17, the Respondent offered possession of the Allotted Unit vide its letter dated 28.10.17. The offer of possession given by the Respondent is nothing else but a sham. At the site of the Allotted Unit, the development works were nowhere near completion and the Allotted Unit is also not in any condition whatsoever to be taken&nbsp;</span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-indent: -43px; margin-left: 0.5in; line-height: 200%;\"><font face=\"Garamond, serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">vi)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That failure on the part of the Respondent in handing over possession of the Allotted Unit within the stipulated time period as per Clause 21.1 of the Buyer’s Agreement constitutes a wilful and material breach of the contract executed between the parties.</span></font></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:1.0in;text-align:justify;text-indent:\r\n-.5in;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n200%;font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">i)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Refund of an amount of Rs.\r\n1,04,28,413/-paid by the Applicants alongwith interest (highest marginal cost\r\nof lending rate of the State Bank of India + 2%) from the respective dates of\r\ndeposit till actual realization as per Sections 18 and 19(4) of the Act read\r\nwith Rule 16 of the Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development)\r\nRules, 2017.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:1.0in;text-align:justify;text-indent:\r\n-.5in;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n200%;font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">ii)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Any other relief which the Applicant is\r\nentitled for under the Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Act, 2016 and\r\nthe Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>',10428413.00,10766807.00,'2014-12-13 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>..</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','2011-06-13 00:00:00','Allotted Unit No. TVM K1-FPH-PH02, Tower K1, ‘The Views’, Mohali Hills','','',2,0,0,0,'brindersingh1','2018-12-26 09:09:29.000','brindersingh1','2018-12-26 09:09:29.000'),(643,1205,'1205',1042,'ad5aedc0-ba34-46fe-90ba-d852bb0b013c','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Kuljit Sidhu','kssidhuprof@gmail.com',9876831867,0,0,'344 URBAN ESTATE, PHASE 1','Patiala',28,454,'147002','1','344 URBAN ESTATE, PHASE 1','Patiala',28,454,'147002','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PC0001','Royal Business Park','Motia Developers Private Limited','info@motiagroup.com',8558844525,0,'Motia Developers Private Limited','Chandigarh-Ambala Highway, Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','1','Motia Developers Private Limited','Chandigarh-Ambala Highway, Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:6.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:12.0pt;\r\nmargin-left:0cm\"><b><span style=\"font-size:\r\n12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\">a</span></b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\">.\r\nComplainants are husband and wife and joint allottees of the unit 31B-3<sup>rd</sup>\r\nFloor as per Allotment Letter dated Feb 5, 2016 (Annexure 1). They have made\r\nall payments except for 5% due at the time of possession (date wise receipt and\r\nother details in Annexure 2).<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\">Basic\r\nCost of Unit-Rs 3941057, Car Parking-Rs300000, Due at Possession-Rs 197053. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:6.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:0cm;\r\nmargin-left:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;line-height:normal\"><b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\">b.</span></b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\"> Respondent has committed to hand\r\nover possession of the unit on or before Feb 4, 2017 as per Buyers\r\nAgreement/Agreement of Sale (relevant 3 pages of agreement at Annexure 3) but\r\nhas failed to deliver possession by the stipulated date which is evident from\r\nhis letter dated Feb 7, 2018 (Annexure 4). <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;line-height:\r\nnormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;line-height:\r\nnormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\">The\r\nproject is far from completion. Respondent has provided a copy of so called\r\nCompletion/Occupancy Certificate dated December 14, 2016 (Annexures 5) but it\r\ncertifies neither completion nor fitness for occupancy. It itself admits\r\nincompletion by laying down 7 conditions and subjecting it to obtaining a\r\nnumber of certificates. Furthermore it stipulates that noncompliance of any of\r\nthe conditions will render it redundant. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\">The\r\nbottom line and the relevant fact is that Respondent has failed to complete the\r\nproject and give possession by the date committed in the Agreement for sale.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:\r\n115%\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></b></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:\r\n115%\">c.</span></b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%\">\r\nComplainants have served a Legal Notice dated June 27, 2018 upon Respondent\r\n(Annexure 6). He has been requested to refund the received amount of Rs. 4250362/-\r\nwith interest plus compensation within 30 days of the receipt of the notice.\r\nThe notice was received on July 5, 2018 but there has been no response.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:6.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:12.0pt;\r\nmargin-left:0cm\"><b><span style=\"font-size:\r\n12.0pt;line-height:115%\">d.</span></b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:\r\n115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-language:EN-IN\"> This is an ongoing project and it is now well\r\nsettled law that the Real Estate Act is applicable to such projects as per\r\nBombay High Court Order in WP 2737/2017 and other similar petitions. Any terms\r\nand conditions, which are contrary to express provisions of the Act are invalid\r\nand overridden by the Act. This is also borne out by many orders/judgments of\r\nthe Punjab Real Estate Regulatory Authority/Adjudicating Officer.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:6.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:12.0pt;\r\nmargin-left:0cm\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:\r\nEN-IN\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;<b><o:p></o:p></b></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-right:-2.3pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\r\nline-height:115%\">a<b>. &nbsp;</b>History of the case, event dates and\r\njustification for submitting earlier application in Form- N is given in\r\nAnnexure 10. A perusal of this makes it apparent that Complainants are back to\r\nsquare one after about 3 months of filing first application due to no fault of\r\ntheirs.&nbsp; <o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-right:-2.3pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\r\nline-height:115%\">Complainants seek expeditious relief under Section 18 and\r\ndisposal of the present complaint within two months as provided for in Section\r\n29 (4), as sacred a section as any other, of the Act. <o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-right:-2.3pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\r\nline-height:115%\">b<b>. </b>&nbsp;The facts given in Para (4) above establish\r\nthat Respondent has failed to deliver possession of the allotted Unit including\r\nCar Parking by the stipulated date in Agreement of Sale. &nbsp;Section 18 of the Act provides that, if the\r\npromoter fails to complete or is unable to give possession by such a date for\r\nany reason and the allottee(s) wishes to withdraw from the project, he shall be\r\nliable to return the amount received by him along with interest including\r\ncompensation.<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-right:-2.3pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\r\nline-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\">&nbsp;Complainants are withdrawing from the project\r\nand claiming here the following relief. They will file a separate application\r\nfor compensation with the Adjudicating Officer. <o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:6.0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\r\nline-height:115%\">I. Refund of Amount Received (Annexure2) = </span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\">Rs 4250362.00<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:6.0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\r\nline-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\">II. Payment of Interest: (i) Up to\r\n</span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%\">30.11.2018 (Annexure 2)\r\n= </span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times-Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:Times-Roman\">Rs 2152873.00 <o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:6.0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\r\nline-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times-Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:Times-Roman\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp; (ii) From 01.12.2018 to day of refund, say =\r\nINT</span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\"> <o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:6.0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\r\nline-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\">III. Total Claim = Rs 6403235.00\r\n+ INT<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-right:-2.3pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\r\nline-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>',4447415.00,4250362.00,'2017-02-04 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>N.A.</p>','1','','2016-02-05 00:00:00','2016-02-05 00:00:00','31B, 3rd Floor, Royal Business Park, Chandigarh- Ambala Highway, Zirakpur','','',2,0,0,0,'kssidhu','2018-12-26 10:23:06.000','kssidhu','2018-12-26 10:23:06.000'),(644,1205,'1205',1042,'ad5aedc0-ba34-46fe-90ba-d852bb0b013c','FormTypeM',1,1,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Kuljit Sidhu','kssidhuprof@gmail.com',9876831867,0,0,'344 URBAN ESTATE, PHASE 1','Patiala',28,454,'147002','1','344 URBAN ESTATE, PHASE 1','Patiala',28,454,'147002','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PC0001','Royal Business Park','Motia Developers Private Limited','info@motiagroup.com',8558844525,0,'Motia Developers Private Limited','Chandigarh-Ambala Highway, Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','1','Motia Developers Private Limited','Chandigarh-Ambala Highway, Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:6.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:12.0pt;\r\nmargin-left:0cm\"><b><span style=\"font-size:\r\n12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\">a</span></b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\">.\r\nComplainants are husband and wife and joint allottees of the unit 31B-3<sup>rd</sup>\r\nFloor as per Allotment Letter dated Feb 5, 2016 (Annexure 1). They have made\r\nall payments except for 5% due at the time of possession (date wise receipt and\r\nother details in Annexure 2).<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\">Basic\r\nCost of Unit-Rs 3941057, Car Parking-Rs300000, Due at Possession-Rs 197053. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:6.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:0cm;\r\nmargin-left:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;line-height:normal\"><b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\">b.</span></b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\"> Respondent has committed to hand\r\nover possession of the unit on or before Feb 4, 2017 as per Buyers\r\nAgreement/Agreement of Sale (relevant 3 pages of agreement at Annexure 3) but\r\nhas failed to deliver possession by the stipulated date which is evident from\r\nhis letter dated Feb 7, 2018 (Annexure 4). <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;line-height:\r\nnormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;line-height:\r\nnormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\">The\r\nproject is far from completion. Respondent has provided a copy of so called\r\nCompletion/Occupancy Certificate dated December 14, 2016 (Annexures 5) but it\r\ncertifies neither completion nor fitness for occupancy. It itself admits\r\nincompletion by laying down 7 conditions and subjecting it to obtaining a\r\nnumber of certificates. Furthermore it stipulates that noncompliance of any of\r\nthe conditions will render it redundant. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\">The\r\nbottom line and the relevant fact is that Respondent has failed to complete the\r\nproject and give possession by the date committed in the Agreement for sale.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:\r\n115%\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></b></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:\r\n115%\">c.</span></b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%\">\r\nComplainants have served a Legal Notice dated June 27, 2018 upon Respondent\r\n(Annexure 6). He has been requested to refund the received amount of Rs. 4250362/-\r\nwith interest plus compensation within 30 days of the receipt of the notice.\r\nThe notice was received on July 5, 2018 but there has been no response.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:6.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:12.0pt;\r\nmargin-left:0cm\"><b><span style=\"font-size:\r\n12.0pt;line-height:115%\">d.</span></b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:\r\n115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-language:EN-IN\"> This is an ongoing project and it is now well\r\nsettled law that the Real Estate Act is applicable to such projects as per\r\nBombay High Court Order in WP 2737/2017 and other similar petitions. Any terms\r\nand conditions, which are contrary to express provisions of the Act are invalid\r\nand overridden by the Act. This is also borne out by many orders/judgments of\r\nthe Punjab Real Estate Regulatory Authority/Adjudicating Officer.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:6.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:12.0pt;\r\nmargin-left:0cm\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:\r\nEN-IN\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;<b><o:p></o:p></b></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-right:-2.3pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\r\nline-height:115%\">a<b>. &nbsp;</b>History of the case, event dates and\r\njustification for submitting earlier application in Form- N is given in\r\nAnnexure 10. A perusal of this makes it apparent that Complainants are back to\r\nsquare one after about 3 months of filing first application due to no fault of\r\ntheirs.&nbsp; <o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-right:-2.3pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\r\nline-height:115%\">Complainants seek expeditious relief under Section 18 and\r\ndisposal of the present complaint within two months as provided for in Section\r\n29 (4), as sacred a section as any other, of the Act. <o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-right:-2.3pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\r\nline-height:115%\">b<b>. </b>&nbsp;The facts given in Para (4) above establish\r\nthat Respondent has failed to deliver possession of the allotted Unit including\r\nCar Parking by the stipulated date in Agreement of Sale. &nbsp;Section 18 of the Act provides that, if the\r\npromoter fails to complete or is unable to give possession by such a date for\r\nany reason and the allottee(s) wishes to withdraw from the project, he shall be\r\nliable to return the amount received by him along with interest including\r\ncompensation.<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-right:-2.3pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\r\nline-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\">&nbsp;Complainants are withdrawing from the project\r\nand claiming here the following relief. They will file a separate application\r\nfor compensation with the Adjudicating Officer. <o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:6.0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\r\nline-height:115%\">I. Refund of Amount Received (Annexure2) = </span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\">Rs 4250362.00<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:6.0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\r\nline-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\">II. Payment of Interest: (i) Up to\r\n</span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%\">30.11.2018 (Annexure 2)\r\n= </span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times-Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:Times-Roman\">Rs 2152873.00 <o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:6.0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\r\nline-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times-Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:Times-Roman\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp; (ii) From 01.12.2018 to day of refund, say =\r\nINT</span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\"> <o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:6.0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\r\nline-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\">III. Total Claim = Rs 6403235.00\r\n+ INT<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-right:-2.3pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\r\nline-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>',4447415.00,4250362.00,'2017-02-04 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>N.A.</p>','1','','2016-02-05 00:00:00','2016-02-05 00:00:00','31B, 3rd Floor, Royal Business Park, Chandigarh- Ambala Highway, Zirakpur','','',2,0,0,0,'kssidhu','2018-12-26 10:36:58.000','kssidhu','2018-12-26 10:36:58.000'),(645,1216,'1216',1141,'971b1ae7-f8bc-4323-80a7-088b81f8b7db','FormTypeM',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Suparna Randhawa','dpsrandhawa@hotmail.com',9914400088,0,0,'House No.229','Sector-16',6,128,'160015','1','House No. 253','Sector 4, Mansa Devi Complex',13,15,'134114','Sanjeev Gupta','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0093','PALM GARDEN','M/s Manohar Infrastructure & Constructions Pvt Ltd','nbs@manoharrealty.com',0,1725033524,'SCO 139-142','Sector-17C',6,128,'160017','1','SCO 139-142','Sector-17C',6,128,'160017','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:\r\njustify;line-height:200%;mso-layout-grid-align:none;text-autospace:none\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">A\r\nplot measuring 500 sq yards @18500 per sq yards was booked by complainant in\r\nthe project Palm Garden being developed by the respondent,vide application(C-1)dated\r\n18.12.11 &amp; booking amount of Rs. 2775000 i.e. 30% of sale consideration was\r\npaid.Before purchasing the said plot,respondent had assured the complainant\r\nthat it is having all the approvals for the development of project except\r\nlayout plan approval which will be approved within 30 days &amp; possession be\r\ndelivered within 2 years &amp; buyer’s agreement will executed within 3 months.A\r\npayment plan(C-2)was also given to the complainant.An acknowledgment(C-3)dated\r\n2.4.12 was issued.But inspite of repeated requests by the complainant,the respondent\r\nhas failed to issue any allotment letter &amp; execute buyer’s agreement within\r\nthe said period and even till date.Many times complainant visited the office of\r\nrespondent for getting the allotment letter and buyer agreement but to no\r\navail.There was no development on the site &amp; the respondent kept the\r\ncomplainant in dark about the approvals.A legal notice(C-4)dated 30.8.18\r\nwas sent to respondent for refund,in which sequence of events have been duly incorporated,\r\nwhich may kindly be treated as part of pleadings.After that complainant\r\nreceived a call from respondent who invited him to its office for redressal of\r\nhis grievances.Accordingly, complainant went there in 3<sup>rd</sup> week of\r\nOctober,2018,where the respondent assured that allotment letter would be duly\r\nissued &amp; buyer’s agreement would also be executed if the complainant further\r\ndeposit a sum of Rs. 1850000 i.e 20% sale consideration.But the complainant\r\nasked the respondent to first issue the allotment letter &amp; execute the\r\nagreement.Respondent refused to issue the same without getting any further\r\namount.The complainant has been harassed for so many years due to unfair trade\r\npractices on the part of respondent.A list of dates of approvals(C-5) &amp;\r\nimportant approvals as(C-6 &amp;C-7).Complaint for registration of FIR to\r\nvigilance as C-8<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<ol><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">To\r\ndirect the respondent to issue allotment letter in respect of 500 sq yard plot\r\nand execute the buyer’s agreement in compliance with Section 13 of RERA.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">To\r\nhand over the actual physical possession of the plot after issuing the\r\nallotment letter and execution of buyer’s agreement. The complainant is ready\r\nto pay the balance sale consideration. The respondent was not having any\r\nauthority to collect the money from general public before 25.1.2017. <o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">To\r\ndirect the respondent not to charge any other charges from the complainant\r\nexcept EDC and PLC (if any) since the plot was sold to the complainant @Rs18500/-\r\nper sq yards excluding EDC and PLC (if any).<o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">To\r\ndirect the respondent to pay interest at the rate as contemplated under Rule 16\r\nof Punjab RERA Rules, for the period of delay in delivering the possession to\r\nbe calculated from the committed date of possession i.e. 18.12.2013 till the\r\ndate of handing over the actual physical possession after obtaining the\r\ncompletion certificate. <o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">To\r\ntake action against the respondent under Section 61 of RERA for not complying\r\nthe provision of Section 13 which makes it mandatory for a promoter to execute\r\nthe buyer agreement on receiving 10% of sale consideration. Inspite of repeated\r\nrequest the respondent has not offered the buyer’s agreement even after getting itself registered under RERA rather it is\r\ndemanding more money for executing the same which is a clear violation of\r\nSection 13. The respondent was not even having any approval, rather it had not\r\neven applied the necessary permissions when the plot was sold to the\r\ncomplainant. The respondent got the exemption under Section 44 of PAPRA on\r\n25.1.2017. Before the said date it could not collect any money from general\r\npublic. In the present case the respondent collected the money form the\r\ncomplainant in 2011.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">To\r\ntake action against the respondent for collecting the money from the\r\ncomplainant before getting all the approvals and for indulging into unfair\r\ntrade practices<o:p></o:p></span></li></ol><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:150%\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>',9250000.00,2775000.00,'2013-12-18 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<ol><li style=\"margin-left: 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">The\r\nrespondent be directed to issue the allotment letter to the complainant and\r\nexecute the buyer’s agreement in respect of 500 sq yards plot booked by the\r\ncomplainant.</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"margin: 12pt 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">The respondent\r\nbe directed to provide the list of allottees to whom it has allotted/sold the\r\n862 residential plots as per the layout plan approved by GMADA on 6.10.2015 and\r\nfor which it is duly registered under RERA.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"margin: 12pt 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">&nbsp;The respondent be directed to provide the\r\ndetails in respect of funds collected from the general public since 2010 in\r\nlieu of 862 residential plots which are part of approved layout and registered\r\nunder Section 3 of RERA and also, the detail where such amount has been\r\nutilized by the respondent. Also, the respondent be directed to provide all the\r\nbank details where such amount has been deposited along with the statement of\r\naccounts, since the year 2010 and where such amount has been utilized.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"margin: 12pt 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 7pt; line-height: 200%;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">The respondent be\r\ndirected to provide the details in respect of number of bookings done by it\r\nsince the year 2010 for the said 862 residential plots along with the list of\r\napplicants who had applied for booking of plots.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"margin: 12pt 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">The\r\nrespondent be directed to provide the details as regards the criteria adopted\r\nby it for allotting the plot numbers to different applicants through pick and\r\nchoose policy.</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"margin: 12pt 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">The\r\nrespondent be directed to provide the list of total applicants and further, the\r\nlist to whom it has already allotted the plot along with the list of applicants\r\nto whom it has not allotted the plots till date. </span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"margin: 12pt 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">The\r\nrespondent be directed to provide the list of hypothecated plots which are\r\nhypothecated to GMADA, out of the approved 862 residential plots and 73\r\ncommercial plots. Also, the respondent be directed to provide the list of\r\nhypothected plots sold to general public.</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></li></ol><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:12.0pt;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:\r\n0in;margin-left:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:12.0pt;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:\r\n0in;margin-left:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;line-height:200%;\r\nmso-layout-grid-align:none;text-autospace:none\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'rerafilingformm','2018-12-26 11:08:43.000','rerafilingformm','2018-12-26 11:08:43.000'),(646,1216,'1216',1141,'971b1ae7-f8bc-4323-80a7-088b81f8b7db','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-26 15:27:35.000','Suparna Randhawa','dpsrandhawa@hotmail.com',9914400088,0,0,'House No.229','Sector-16',6,128,'160015','1','House No. 253','Sector 4, Mansa Devi Complex',13,15,'134114','Sanjeev Gupta','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0093','PALM GARDEN','M/s Manohar Infrastructure & Constructions Pvt Ltd','nbs@manoharrealty.com',0,1725033524,'SCO 139-142','Sector-17C',6,128,'160017','1','SCO 139-142','Sector-17C',6,128,'160017','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:\r\njustify;line-height:200%;mso-layout-grid-align:none;text-autospace:none\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">A\r\nplot measuring 500 sq yards @18500 per sq yards was booked by complainant in\r\nthe project Palm Garden being developed by the respondent,vide application(C-1)dated\r\n18.12.11 &amp; booking amount of Rs. 2775000 i.e. 30% of sale consideration was\r\npaid.Before purchasing the said plot,respondent had assured the complainant\r\nthat it is having all the approvals for the development of project except\r\nlayout plan approval which will be approved within 30 days &amp; possession be\r\ndelivered within 2 years &amp; buyer’s agreement will executed within 3 months.A\r\npayment plan(C-2)was also given to the complainant.An acknowledgment(C-3)dated\r\n2.4.12 was issued.But inspite of repeated requests by the complainant,the respondent\r\nhas failed to issue any allotment letter &amp; execute buyer’s agreement within\r\nthe said period and even till date.Many times complainant visited the office of\r\nrespondent for getting the allotment letter and buyer agreement but to no\r\navail.There was no development on the site &amp; the respondent kept the\r\ncomplainant in dark about the approvals.A legal notice(C-4)dated 30.8.18\r\nwas sent to respondent for refund,in which sequence of events have been duly incorporated,\r\nwhich may kindly be treated as part of pleadings.After that complainant\r\nreceived a call from respondent who invited him to its office for redressal of\r\nhis grievances.Accordingly, complainant went there in 3<sup>rd</sup> week of\r\nOctober,2018,where the respondent assured that allotment letter would be duly\r\nissued &amp; buyer’s agreement would also be executed if the complainant further\r\ndeposit a sum of Rs. 1850000 i.e 20% sale consideration.But the complainant\r\nasked the respondent to first issue the allotment letter &amp; execute the\r\nagreement.Respondent refused to issue the same without getting any further\r\namount.The complainant has been harassed for so many years due to unfair trade\r\npractices on the part of respondent.A list of dates of approvals(C-5) &amp;\r\nimportant approvals as(C-6 &amp;C-7).Complaint for registration of FIR to\r\nvigilance as C-8<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<ol><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">To\r\ndirect the respondent to issue allotment letter in respect of 500 sq yard plot\r\nand execute the buyer’s agreement in compliance with Section 13 of RERA.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">To\r\nhand over the actual physical possession of the plot after issuing the\r\nallotment letter and execution of buyer’s agreement. The complainant is ready\r\nto pay the balance sale consideration. The respondent was not having any\r\nauthority to collect the money from general public before 25.1.2017. <o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">To\r\ndirect the respondent not to charge any other charges from the complainant\r\nexcept EDC and PLC (if any) since the plot was sold to the complainant @Rs18500/-\r\nper sq yards excluding EDC and PLC (if any).<o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">To\r\ndirect the respondent to pay interest at the rate as contemplated under Rule 16\r\nof Punjab RERA Rules, for the period of delay in delivering the possession to\r\nbe calculated from the committed date of possession i.e. 18.12.2013 till the\r\ndate of handing over the actual physical possession after obtaining the\r\ncompletion certificate. <o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">To\r\ntake action against the respondent under Section 61 of RERA for not complying\r\nthe provision of Section 13 which makes it mandatory for a promoter to execute\r\nthe buyer agreement on receiving 10% of sale consideration.Inspite of repeated\r\nrequest the respondent has not offered the buyer’s agreement even after getting itself registered under RERA rather it is\r\ndemanding more money for executing the same which is a clear violation of\r\nSection 13.The respondent was not even having any approval, rather it had not\r\neven applied the necessary permissions when the plot was sold to the\r\ncomplainant.The respondent got the exemption under Section 44 of PAPRA on\r\n25.1.2017.Before the said date it could not collect any money from general\r\npublic as per Annx C-6 &amp; C-7. In the present case the respondent collected the money from the\r\ncomplainant in 2011-12.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">To\r\ntake action against the respondent for collecting the money from the\r\ncomplainant before getting all the approvals and for indulging into unfair\r\ntrade practices.<o:p></o:p></span></li></ol><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:150%\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>',9250000.00,2775000.00,'2013-12-18 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<ol><li style=\"margin-left: 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">The\r\nrespondent be directed to issue the allotment letter to the complainant and\r\nexecute the buyer’s agreement in respect of 500 sq yards plot booked by the\r\ncomplainant.</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"margin: 12pt 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">The respondent\r\nbe directed to provide the list of allottees to whom it has allotted/sold the\r\n862 residential plots as per the layout plan approved by GMADA on 6.10.2015 and\r\nfor which it is duly registered under RERA.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"margin: 12pt 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">&nbsp;The respondent be directed to provide the\r\ndetails in respect of funds collected from the general public since 2010 in\r\nlieu of 862 residential plots which are part of approved layout and registered\r\nunder Section 3 of RERA and also, the detail where such amount has been\r\nutilized by the respondent. Also, the respondent be directed to provide all the\r\nbank details where such amount has been deposited along with the statement of\r\naccounts, since the year 2010 and where such amount has been utilized.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"margin: 12pt 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 7pt; line-height: 200%;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">The respondent be\r\ndirected to provide the details in respect of number of bookings done by it\r\nsince the year 2010 for the said 862 residential plots along with the list of\r\napplicants who had applied for booking of plots.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"margin: 12pt 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">The\r\nrespondent be directed to provide the details as regards the criteria adopted\r\nby it for allotting the plot numbers to different applicants through pick and\r\nchoose policy.</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"margin: 12pt 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">The\r\nrespondent be directed to provide the list of total applicants and further, the\r\nlist to whom it has already allotted the plot along with the list of applicants\r\nto whom it has not allotted the plots till date. </span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"margin: 12pt 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">The\r\nrespondent be directed to provide the list of hypothecated plots which are\r\nhypothecated to GMADA, out of the approved 862 residential plots and 73\r\ncommercial plots. Also, the respondent be directed to provide the list of\r\nhypothected plots sold to general public.</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></li></ol><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:12.0pt;margin-right:0in;margin-bo