Plot No.\r\n157</b> to the complainant. That on <b>18.12.2014</b>,\r\nOP again failed to complete its legal obligation and hand over the plot to the\r\ncomplainant.<b> </b><o:p></o:p></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"normal\" style=\"tab-stops:211.5pt;border:none;mso-padding-alt:31.0pt 31.0pt 31.0pt 31.0pt;\r\nmso-border-shadow:yes\">Therefore,\r\nthe complainant craves the indulgence of the REAL ESTATE REGULATORY AUTHORITY\r\nto direct the OP to refund the entire amount as per RERA CENTRAL ACT AND RERA STATE\r\nRULES.<o:p></o:p></p>','<p>i<span style=\"white-space: pre;\">	</span>To direct the OP to compensate the complainant in the shape of refund of the complete amount which has been deposited against the residential property so booked by the complainant along with an Interest on the amount from the date of deposit at the rate of 20 per sent&nbsp; till the actual realization of the complete amount within 90 days according to section 18 1 Real Estate Regulation And Development Act 2016 18 2 Real Estate Regulation And Development Act 2016 Section 19 4 of The Real Estate Regulation And Development Act 2016 r w Rule 16 and Rule 17 of Punjab State Real Estate Regulation and Development Rules 2017.<br></p><p>ii<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To direct the OP to pay Rs. 2000000&nbsp; for causing mental agony caused to the complainant.</p><p><br></p><p>iii<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To direct the OP to pay Rs. 1400000 to the complainant as the deficiency in services for keeping the complainant in dark in regard to the progress of the property.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>iv<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span> To direct the OP to pay Rs. 1400000&nbsp; for causing physical harassment caused to the complainant.</p><p><br></p><p>v<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To direct the OP to pay 5% of the total estimated cost of the project under section 61 of Real Estate Regulation and Development Act 2016</p><p><br></p><p>vi<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To revoke the license of the OP under section 7 of the Real Estate Regulation and Development act 2016.</p><p><br></p><p>vii<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Any other relief or claim which the Hon ble Authority deems appropriate.</p><div><br></div>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Not prayed</p>','1','','2009-04-25 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',1,1,0,0,'lawofficeofhimanshuraj','2018-12-27 10:21:57.000','lawofficeofhimanshuraj','2018-12-27 10:21:57.000'),(666,1126,'1126',1010,'a182232b-88d6-4711-8baa-f8a026fb675f','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-27 10:29:53.000','RAGHUNANDAN SATHYANARAYAN RAO','lawofficeofhimanshuraj@gmail.com',9988100005,1724181010,711442413353,'#102, Sector 10 A','',6,128,'160011','1','#102, Sector 10 A','',6,128,'160011','HIMANSHU RAJ','lawofficeofhimanshuraj@gmail.com',9988200001,1724190909,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0013','ATS GOLF MEADOWS 1','ATS ESTATES PRIVATE LIMITED','pradeep.rathee@atsgreens.com',8288033311,0,'ATS TOWER, PLOT NO.16','SECTOR 35, NOIDA',33,216,'201305','1','ATS TOWER, PLOT NO.16','SECTOR 35, NOIDA',33,216,'201305','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: Thorndale, serif;\">The complainant had\r\nbooked a plot measuring <b>500 SQ. YARD </b>at\r\nOPs project <b>ATS GOLF MEADOWS-I</b> in\r\nthe year 2005. That it is pertinent to mention here that OP did not possess any\r\nof the requisite clearances license from the competent authority to develop the\r\nsaid project at that time The complainant has paid the <b>COMPLETE AMOUNT</b> against the said unit to the Opposite Party in the\r\nyear 2005-2006.<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: Thorndale, serif;\">That on <b>25.04.2009, </b>the OP furnished an\r\nALLOTMENT LETTER and allotted a plot to the complainant measuring <b>500 Sq. Yard</b>, indentified by unique No.\r\n<b><u>110 Pocket III</u></b> in the said\r\nproject. That the OP promised through verbal assurance and Verbal Agreement\r\nthat the possession will be handed over to the complainant by <b>25.04.2011</b>, i.e. 2 years from the date\r\nof allotment, but Op failed to do so. That on <b>20.11.2012, </b>Opposite Party demanded EDC against the said plot from the\r\ncomplainant even though the complainant had already paid the complete\r\nconsideration against the said unit to the OP back in the year 2005-2006. The\r\nOP also revised the area of the plot allotted to the complainant from <b>500</b> Sq. Yard. to <b>360</b> Sq. Yard and the complainant was also given a New Plot No. i.e.\r\n<b>94, </b>in OPs project<b> ATS GOLF MEADOWS-I. </b>But only in 7 days\r\ngap from the revision of the area and allotment of new plot Number, Op on <b>27.11.2012 </b>again re-revised the plot\r\narea from 360 Sq. yard to 500 Sq. Yard and re-allotted a new number i.e. <b>Plot No. 253</b> to the complainant and had\r\nagain demanded EDC from the complainant against the said plot. That the OP\r\nagain promised and assured that the possession will be delivered by <b>27.11.2014 </b>i.e. 2 years from the date\r\nof said allotment. But yet again, OP failed to complete its legal obligation\r\nand hand over the plot to the complainant.<b>\r\n<o:p></o:p></b></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"margin-left:0cm;mso-add-space:auto;tab-stops:\r\n211.5pt\"><span style=\"line-height: 200%; font-family: Thorndale, serif;\">Therefore,\r\nthe complainant craves the indulgence of the REAL ESTATE REGULATORY AUTHORITY direct\r\nthe OP to refund of the entire amount as per RERA CENTRAL ACT AND RERA STATE\r\nRULES.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p>i<span style=\"white-space: pre;\">	</span>To direct the OP to compensate the complainant in the shape of refund of the complete amount which has been deposited against the residential property so booked by the complainant along with an Interest on the amount from the date of deposit at the rate of 20 per sent&nbsp; till the actual realization of the complete amount within 90 days according to section 18 1 Real Estate Regulation And Development Act 2016 18 2 Real Estate Regulation And Development Act 2016 Section 19 4 of The Real Estate Regulation And Development Act 2016 r w Rule 16 and Rule 17 of Punjab State Real Estate Regulation and Development Rules 2017<br></p><p>ii<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To direct the OP to pay Rs. 2000000&nbsp; for causing mental agony caused to the complainant.</p><p><br></p><p>iii<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To direct the OP to pay Rs. 1400000 to the complainant as the deficiency in services for keeping the complainant in dark in regard to the progress of the property.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>iv<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span> To direct the OP to pay Rs. 1400000&nbsp; for causing physical harassment caused to the complainant.</p><p><br></p><p>v<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To direct the OP to pay 5 per cent of the total estimated cost of the project under section 61 of Real Estate Regulation and Development Act 2016</p><p><br></p><p>vi<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To revoke the license of the OP under section 7 of the Real Estate Regulation and Development act 2016.</p><p>vii<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Any other relief or claim which the Hon ble Authority deems appropriate.</p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Not Prayed</p>','1','','2009-04-25 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',1,1,0,0,'lawofficeofhimanshuraj','2018-12-27 10:29:47.000','lawofficeofhimanshuraj','2018-12-27 10:29:47.000'),(667,1182,'1182',1010,'a182232b-88d6-4711-8baa-f8a026fb675f','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-27 10:49:18.000','VIKAS MIGLANI and ROHIT MIGLANI ','lawofficeofhimanshuraj@gmail.com',9988100005,1724181010,478144878549,'#102, Sector 10 A','',6,128,'160011','1','#102, Sector 10 A','',6,128,'160011','HIMANSHU RAJ','lawofficeofhimanshuraj@gmail.com',9988200001,1724190909,'Promoter','PBRERA-LDH45-PR0060','IREO WATERFRONT','IREO WATERFRONT PRIVATE LIMITED','iwpl@ireo.in',1613040290,0,'SCO 16-17, BASEMENT, FORTUNE CHAMBERS','OPP. LUDHIANA STOCK EXCHANE, FEROZE GANDHI MARKET, LUDHIANA',28,366,'141001','1','SCO 16-17, BASEMENT, FORTUNE CHAMBERS','OPP. LUDHIANA STOCK EXCHANE, FEROZE GANDHI MARKET, LUDHIANA',28,366,'141001','0','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:\r\njustify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;line-height:200%;tab-stops:0cm\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Thorndale&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:Tahoma\">The complainants are the Residents of India,\r\nresiding at <b>Flat No. 1401, Tower No. 4A,\r\nSuncity Parikrama, Sector 20, Panchkula.</b> They have given their hard earned\r\nmoney for purchasing a residential property in their new project called <b>IREO Waterfront Pvt. Ltd</b>. at Sidhwan\r\nCanal Road, Off Ferozepur Road, Ludhiana, Punjab. The complainants opted for a\r\nResidential property with the super area of <b><u>1600</u></b> Sq.ft. 249.96 sq.yards in the project and booked the\r\nabove mentioned property on <b><u>30.10.2014</u>\r\n</b>at Ludhiana. Subsequently, the complainants got the provisional allotment\r\noffer letter dated <b><u>17.12.2014.</u></b>\r\nIt is pertinent to mention here that the OP entered into a Villa Buyer s\r\nAgreement with the complainants on <b><u>04.03.2015</u></b>\r\nwherein the OP was under the legal obligation to deliver the possession of the\r\nproperty within 24 months from the date of the execution of the said agreement\r\ni.e. by <b><u>04.03.2017</u> </b>but there\r\nis an unfair clause in the Villa Buyer s Agreement which gives the OP an extra\r\n6 months Grace Period after the expiration of the commitment period to hand\r\nover the property due to which the new date of possession was extended to <b><u>04.09.2017</u></b>. The said period of\r\ntwo years has already elapsed and furthermore the grace period of 180 days\r\nafter 24 months has also elapsed on <b><u>04.09.2017</u></b>.\r\nTill date no substantial steps for the possession of the said villa has taken\r\nplace and the complainants have paid a huge amount against the property. The\r\ncomplainants tried to communicate with the OP via personal meetings, telephone\r\nand mail to receive information about the possession of the property but they\r\ngave no/vague answers. Till date the OP has not given any concrete answer about\r\nthe date of possession. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:0cm;\r\nmargin-left:-4.5pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\nline-height:200%;tab-stops:0cm\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Thorndale&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:Tahoma\">Therefore, the\r\ncomplainant craves the indulgence of the Honble RERA authority to direct the Op\r\nto refund the entire amount as per RERA Central act and RERA state rules.</span><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Thorndale&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"normal\" style=\"line-height:200%\"><br></p><p class=\"normalCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:\r\n0cm;margin-left:36.0pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;mso-add-space:auto;text-align:\r\njustify;text-indent:-18.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Thorndale&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:Thorndale;mso-bidi-font-family:Thorndale;color:windowtext\">1.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Thorndale&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:Tahoma;\r\ncolor:windowtext\">To direct the OP to compensate the complainant in the shape\r\nof refund of the complete amount which has been deposited against the\r\nresidential property so booked by the complainant along with an Interest on the\r\namount from the date of deposit at the rate of 20 per cent till the actual\r\nrealization of the complete amount within 90 days according to section 18 1\r\nReal Estate Regulation And Development Act, 2016, 18 2 Real Estate Regulation\r\nAnd Development Act, 2016, Section 19 4 of The Real Estate Regulation And\r\nDevelopment Act, 2016, r w Rule 16 and Rule 17 of Punjab State Real Estate Regulation\r\nand Development Rules, 2017.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"normalCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:\r\n0cm;margin-left:36.0pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;mso-add-space:auto;text-align:\r\njustify;text-indent:-18.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Thorndale&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:Thorndale;mso-bidi-font-family:Thorndale;color:windowtext\">2.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Thorndale&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:Tahoma;\r\ncolor:windowtext\">To direct the Opposite party to reimburse litigation cost of\r\nRs Rs. 2,00,000 two lakhs to the complainants as they were constrained to file\r\nthe same because of the callous and indifferent attitude of the Opposite Party\r\nand the same has been handed over to the lawyer. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"normalCxSpLast\" style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:\r\n0cm;margin-left:36.0pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;mso-add-space:auto;text-align:\r\njustify;text-indent:-18.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Thorndale&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:Thorndale;mso-bidi-font-family:Thorndale;color:windowtext\">3.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Thorndale&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:Tahoma;\r\ncolor:windowtext\">Any other relief or claim which the Hon ble Authority deems\r\nappropriate.<o:p></o:p></span></p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Not Prayed</p>','1','','2014-12-17 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',1,1,0,0,'lawofficeofhimanshuraj','2018-12-27 10:49:15.000','lawofficeofhimanshuraj','2018-12-27 10:49:15.000'),(668,1225,'1225',1223,'9616498a-08f7-4464-9ca8-d1e8ddf49a77','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','RISHI KUMAR GUPTA','agamjund_advocate@yahoo.com',9780269386,0,253992356271,'V & PO MULLANPUR GARIBDASS','NEAR POLICE STATION',28,507,'140901','1','V & PO MULLANPUR GARIBDASS','NEAR POLICE STATION',28,507,'140901','AGAM KUMAR JUND','agamjund_advocate@yahoo.com',9780269387,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0351','SANSKRITI HOMES','SANSKRITI GOLDEN OAK REAL ESTATE PVT. LTD.','info@sanskritihomes.com',7814700800,0,'M/s. Sanskriti Golden Oak Real Estate Pvt. Ltd.,','DLF Pocket R2, New Chandigarh (Mullanpur)',28,39,'140901','1','M/s. Sanskriti Golden Oak Real Estate Pvt. Ltd.,','DLF Pocket R2, New Chandigarh (Mullanpur)',28,39,'140901','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:\r\njustify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi\">Applicant\r\nwas having 45 Bigha 1 Biswa (9 Acres 37 Biswe i.e. 9.385 Acre) ancestral land\r\nat village Devi Nagar, S.A.S Nagar. Respondent had approached the applicant for\r\npurchasing of his land. On being induced by the representation and warranties\r\nof the respondent, Applicant agreed to sell his land at the price of Rs.3 Crore\r\nper Acre. On 21.11.2011, respondent executed one agreement to sell with the\r\napplicant, showing Rs.2 Crore 36 Lakh per Acre, as cost of the land. Further,\r\napplicant was assured that balance amount will be given separately, as\r\nregistered deed has to be executed under value i.e. Rs.2 Crore 36 Lakh per acre.\r\nAccordingly, a separate MOU was prepared by the respondent to adjust the\r\nbalance amount i.e. Rs.6 Crore with the applicant. As per the terms of MOU,<b> </b>applicant\r\nhas to be compensated with four plots of 500 Sq Yd having value of Rs.1 Crore\r\n50 lakh each by the respondent. During the gap period between registry and\r\nAgreement to sell, respondent had allotted four plots No.R-1/C-209, R-1/C-210,\r\nR-1/C-211 &amp; R-1/C-212 to applicant without asking his choice. On\r\n29.05.2012, applicant had executed the registered sale deed of 45 B 1 B land in\r\nfavour of respondent, after receiving Rs 22,14,95,833/- along with confirmation\r\nletter of four plots. </span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:\r\n11.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi\">Respondent had told the\r\napplicant, that to avoid state taxes and to transfer four plots in the name of\r\napplicant as per MOU, respondent shall transfer Rs. 3 Crore 90 Lakh in account\r\nof the applicant; accordingly applicant had to give four cheques of Rs.\r\n92,62,500/- in the name of respondent, So that they can show a valid\r\ntransaction for these four plots. On 28.03.2013, respondent had transferred Rs.\r\n3 Crore 90 Lakh in the account of applicant, i.e. Rs. 97 Lakh 50 Thousand for\r\neach plot. On the same date respondent had encashed the four cheques of Rs.\r\n92,62,500/- taken from the applicant. In this way respondent had taken back Rs.3\r\nCore 70 Lakh 50 Thousand from the applicant. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:\r\njustify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;line-height:200%;tab-stops:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:11.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-bidi-theme-font:\r\nminor-bidi\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">Registration\r\ngranted under section 5 of the Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Act, to\r\nthe respondent may kindly be revoked&nbsp;under Section 7(1)(d) of this\r\nact&nbsp;as the respondent promoter is indulges in unfair and fraudulent\r\npractices&nbsp;by cheating the applicant, after preparing many documents and by\r\nnot providing any clear information to the applicant regarding the\r\npolicy/procedure adopted by the company&nbsp;and had created loss to the state\r\nexchequer by not paying the legal state taxes.&nbsp;Respondent be directed to\r\npay the actual balance amount of land (i.e. Rs. 6 Crore) purchased from the\r\napplicant along with interest, as applicant does not want to take any plot from\r\nthem. Further compensation on account of delaying the payment of the applicant\r\nby preparing false documents just to commit fraud with the applicant and the\r\nstate as per the Rules of Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation and Development)\r\nRules which provides State Bank of India highest marginal cost of lending rate\r\nplus 2% from the respective date of deposit made by the complainants. Further\r\ndirections may please be issued to the respondents to pay Rs. 10,00,000/- for\r\nmental and physical harassment committed upon the applicant by the respondents\r\nand on the account of the deficiency in the services and unfair trade practice\r\ncommitted by the respondents.&nbsp;Further directions may please be issued to\r\nthe respondents to pay Rs. 1,00,000/- on account of litigation charges to the\r\napplicant.&nbsp;It is further prayed that this Hon\'ble Tribunal may grant any\r\nother relief, which it deems fit and proper, in the facts and circumstances of\r\nthe present case, in the interest of justice, equity and fair play.<o:p></o:p></span></p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">Registration\r\ngranted under section 5 of the Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Act, to\r\nthe respondent may kindly be revoked&nbsp;under Section 7(1)(d) of this\r\nact&nbsp;as the respondent promoter is indulges in unfair and fraudulent\r\npractices&nbsp;by cheating the applicant, after preparing many documents and by\r\nnot providing any clear information to the applicant regarding the\r\npolicy/procedure adopted by the company&nbsp;and had created loss to the state\r\nexchequer by not paying the legal state taxes.&nbsp;Respondent be directed to\r\npay the actual balance amount of land (i.e. Rs. 6 Crore) purchased from the\r\napplicant along with interest, as applicant does not want to take any plot from\r\nthem. Further compensation on account of delaying the payment of the applicant\r\nby preparing false documents just to commit fraud with the applicant and the\r\nstate as per the Rules of Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation and Development)\r\nRules which provides State Bank of India highest marginal cost of lending rate\r\nplus 2% from the respective date of deposit made by the complainants. Further\r\ndirections may please be issued to the respondents to pay Rs. 10,00,000/- for\r\nmental and physical harassment committed upon the applicant by the respondents\r\nand on the account of the deficiency in the services and unfair trade practice\r\ncommitted by the respondents.&nbsp;Further directions may please be issued to\r\nthe respondents to pay Rs. 1,00,000/- on account of litigation charges to the\r\napplicant.&nbsp;It is further prayed that this Hon\'ble Tribunal may grant any\r\nother relief, which it deems fit and proper, in the facts and circumstances of\r\nthe present case, in the interest of justice, equity and fair play.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'AGAM','2018-12-27 11:10:35.000','AGAM','2018-12-27 11:10:35.000'),(669,1226,'1226',1308,'1a7482d2-37bb-44bd-bf2e-13a3c485399b','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-27 16:26:09.000','POONAM THAKUR','poonamthakur270@gmail.com',7018363763,0,0,'H. NO. 239','WARD NO. 08 MIDDLE GAURA',14,236,'177001','1','H. NO. 239','WARD NO. 08 MIDDLE GAURA',14,236,'177001','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0069','SBP EXOTIC FLOORS','PRADEEP SHARMA','pradeep375@gmail.com',9216771143,0,'SCO 146-147-148 ','SECTOR 43 B, ',6,128,'160042','1','SCO 146-147-148 ','SECTOR 43 B, ',6,128,'160042','1','<p>THAT AS PER THE TERMS AND CONDITIONS OF THE AGREEMENTS DATED 11-07-2017 WITH SBP, REGARDING ALLOTMENT OF THE FLAT 31-03-2018.</p><p>THAT I HAVE PAID TOTAL 8 LAKHS RS. TILL JANUARY 2018 AND THE CONSTRUCTION WORK HAS NOT BEEN COMPLETED SO FAR. THE COMPLAINT HAVE SUB THE NOTICE DATED 18-05-2018 AND REQUESTED FOR REFUND ALONG WITH INTEREST AND DAMAGES.</p><p>NOT A SINGLE PENNY HAS BEEN REFUNDED THE EMPLOYEES OF THE SAID SBP MR. AMITENDER MISHRA AND PRADEEP ARE HARASSING ME SINCE LONG . THERE FOR IT IS PRAYED THAT THE AMOUNT ALONG WITH INTEREST AND DAMAGES BE REFUNDED FROM THE SBP.</p>','<p>NA</p>',1584900.00,800000.00,'2018-03-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>NOT A SINGLE PENNY HAS BEEN REFUNDED THE EMPLOYEES OF THE SAID SBP MR. AMITENDER MISHRA AND PRADEEP ARE HARASSING ME SINCE LONG . THERE FOR IT IS PRAYED THAT THE AMOUNT ALONG WITH INTEREST AND DAMAGES BE REFUNDED FROM THE SBP.<br></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','2017-07-06 00:00:00','FLAT NO. 114, 1ST FLOOR, SBP EXOTICS','','',1,0,0,0,'POONAMTHAKUR','2018-12-27 14:26:34.000','POONAMTHAKUR','2018-12-27 14:26:34.000'),(670,1188,'1188',1271,'33c16377-7e87-4eb9-827c-5f93f69bf7d5','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-16 17:22:15.000','SUJATA RANA','ranaravi99@yahoo.in',9418488996,0,373687986628,'Flat No. 548, block-24, Sector-3, New Shimla-9','Near Shiv Mandir',14,533,'171009','1','FLAT HO.42, BLOCK NO.1, TYPE-IV','GOVT. COLONY, KASUMPTI SHIMLA-9',14,533,'171009','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0065','Arcadia Country Homes','Primary Estates and Developers Private Limited','primaryestates@gmail.com',9592231111,0,'M/s. Primary Estates and Developers Private Limited, ','SCO 43, Ground Floor, Behind KFC, New Sunny Enclave, Sector 125, SAS Nagar, Mohali.',28,507,'140301','0','Primary Estates & Developers Pvt. Ltd ','Arcadia Park East, SCO No- 4 & 5,  Ludhiana-Chandigarh, NH-95, Besides St.Ezra International School,',28,507,'140301','0','<p>I have to submit that\r\n:</p><p>I have booked an independent floor/Flat No. 1254/SF in Arcadia country homes to with Primary Estates &amp; Developers Pvt. Ltd and have paid Rs.22,00,000/-only until now starting from June, 2016 to June, 2017 against a total agreed value of Rs. 30,00,000/only for the said flat.&nbsp;</p><p>At time of booking I was told that I will get this flat within time limit of 15 months from commencement i.e. June-2016 but the project have been delayed abnormally and final stopped.That many times I found the site deadly locked or find a new face of contractor executing the work saying that the old one had left. This continuous 6th, 7th change of executing contractor or agencies left the quality issues ignored and not attended too till date. One fine morning I was surprised to know that the sale persons have left the organisation and the office have been shifted to new location and I have not been informed.&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>That I latest visited the site as well as your new office on 14/07/2018 and was surprised to see that the position at site is not different to that what was in march-2018. Neither the quality has been improved nor has the progress been geared up. As per the present status of site I am sure to say that it will not be completed even by the end of 2019 that too with very poor quality.\r\n</p><p>Keeping in view the abnormal delay and poor quality of construction, the irresponsible attitude of the company, I requested for refund of my amount as the promoters have not stood by its commitments, neither valued my needs and satisfaction nor its commitment. I have&nbsp;<span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 12pt; text-align: justify;\">written\r\nto the promoters through mail on dated: 17/07/2018; then on 18/08/2018 then on\r\n12/09/2018 but nothing have been heard from the promoters.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0.0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-language:EN-IN;mso-bidi-font-weight:bold;mso-bidi-font-style:italic\">Keeping\r\nin view the abnormal delay and poor quality of construction, irresponsible\r\nattitude of the promoters, in my\r\nopinion they have not stood by its commitments, neither valued my needs\r\nand satisfaction nor its commitment. So feeling aggrieved being cheated I requested&nbsp; to kindly refund my entire amount with all\r\nconsequential benefits/dues.</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0.0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-language:EN-IN;mso-bidi-font-weight:bold;mso-bidi-font-style:italic\"><br></span><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0.0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background-image: initial; background-positio