,0,0,0,'sujatarana','2018-12-27 19:03:22.000','sujatarana','2018-12-27 19:03:22.000'),(678,1205,'1205',1042,'ad5aedc0-ba34-46fe-90ba-d852bb0b013c','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-27 19:16:31.000','Kuljit Sidhu','kssidhuprof@gmail.com',9876831867,0,0,'344 URBAN ESTATE, PHASE 1','Patiala',28,454,'147002','1','344 URBAN ESTATE, PHASE 1','Patiala',28,454,'147002','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PC0001','Royal Business Park','Motia Developers Private Limited','info@motiagroup.com',8558844525,0,'Motia Developers Private Limited','Chandigarh-Ambala Highway, Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','1','Motia Developers Private Limited','Chandigarh-Ambala Highway, Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:6.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:12.0pt;\r\nmargin-left:0cm\"><b><span style=\"font-size:\r\n12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\">a</span></b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\">.\r\nComplainants are husband and wife and joint allottees of the unit 31B-3<sup>rd</sup>\r\nFloor as per Allotment Letter dated Feb 5, 2016 (Annexure 1). They have made\r\nall payments except for 5% due at the time of possession (date wise receipt and\r\nother details in Annexure 2).<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\">Basic\r\nCost of Unit-Rs 3941057, Car Parking-Rs300000, Due at Possession-Rs 197053. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:6.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:0cm;\r\nmargin-left:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;line-height:normal\"><b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\">b.</span></b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\"> Respondent has committed to hand\r\nover possession of the unit on or before Feb 4, 2017 as per Buyers\r\nAgreement/Agreement of Sale (relevant 3 pages of agreement at Annexure 3) but\r\nhas failed to deliver possession by the stipulated date which is evident from\r\nhis letter dated Feb 7, 2018 (Annexure 4). <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;line-height:\r\nnormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;line-height:\r\nnormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\">The\r\nproject is far from completion. Respondent has provided a copy of so called\r\nCompletion/Occupancy Certificate dated December 14, 2016 (Annexures 5) but it\r\ncertifies neither completion nor fitness for occupancy. It itself admits\r\nincompletion by laying down 7 conditions and subjecting it to obtaining a\r\nnumber of certificates. Furthermore it stipulates that noncompliance of any of\r\nthe conditions will render it redundant. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\">The\r\nbottom line and the relevant fact is that Respondent has failed to complete the\r\nproject and give possession by the date committed in the Agreement for sale.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:\r\n115%\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></b></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:\r\n115%\">c.</span></b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%\">\r\nComplainants have served a Legal Notice dated June 27, 2018 upon Respondent\r\n(Annexure 6). He has been requested to refund the received amount of Rs. 4250362/-\r\nwith interest plus compensation within 30 days of the receipt of the notice.\r\nThe notice was received on July 5, 2018 but there has been no response.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:6.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:12.0pt;\r\nmargin-left:0cm\"><b><span style=\"font-size:\r\n12.0pt;line-height:115%\">d.</span></b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:\r\n115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-language:EN-IN\"> This is an ongoing project and it is now well\r\nsettled law that the Real Estate Act is applicable to such projects as per\r\nBombay High Court Order in WP 2737/2017 and other similar petitions. Any terms\r\nand conditions, which are contrary to express provisions of the Act are invalid\r\nand overridden by the Act. This is also borne out by many orders/judgments of\r\nthe Punjab Real Estate Regulatory Authority/Adjudicating Officer.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:6.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:12.0pt;\r\nmargin-left:0cm\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:\r\nEN-IN\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;<b><o:p></o:p></b></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-right:-2.3pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\r\nline-height:115%\">a<b>. &nbsp;</b>History of the case, event dates and\r\njustification for submitting earlier application in Form- N is given in\r\nAnnexure 10. A perusal of this makes it apparent that Complainants are back to\r\nsquare one after about 3 months of filing first application due to no fault of\r\ntheirs.&nbsp; <o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-right:-2.3pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\r\nline-height:115%\">Complainants seek expeditious relief under Section 18 and\r\ndisposal of the present complaint within two months as provided for in Section\r\n29 (4), as sacred a section as any other, of the Act. <o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-right:-2.3pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\r\nline-height:115%\">b<b>. </b>&nbsp;The facts given in Para (4) above establish\r\nthat Respondent has failed to deliver possession of the allotted Unit including\r\nCar Parking by the stipulated date in Agreement of Sale. &nbsp;Section 18 of the Act provides that, if the\r\npromoter fails to complete or is unable to give possession by such a date for\r\nany reason and the allottee(s) wishes to withdraw from the project, he shall be\r\nliable to return the amount received by him along with interest including\r\ncompensation.<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-right:-2.3pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\r\nline-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\">&nbsp;Complainants are withdrawing from the project\r\nand claiming here the following relief. They will file a separate application\r\nfor compensation with the Adjudicating Officer. <o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:6.0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\r\nline-height:115%\">I. Refund of Amount Received (Annexure2) = </span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\">Rs 4250362.00<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:6.0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\r\nline-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\">II. Payment of Interest: (i) Up to\r\n</span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%\">30.11.2018 (Annexure 2)\r\n= </span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times-Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:Times-Roman\">Rs 2152873.00 <o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:6.0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\r\nline-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times-Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:Times-Roman\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp; (ii) From 01.12.2018 to day of refund, say =\r\nINT</span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\"> <o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:6.0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\r\nline-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\">III. Total Claim = Rs 6403235.00\r\n+ INT<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-right:-2.3pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;\r\nline-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>',4447415.00,4250362.00,'2017-02-04 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>N.A.</p>','1','','2016-02-05 00:00:00','2016-02-05 00:00:00','31B, 3rd Floor, Royal Business Park, Chandigarh- Ambala Highway, Zirakpur','','',1,1,0,0,'kssidhu','2018-12-27 19:15:39.000','kssidhu','2018-12-27 19:15:39.000'),(679,1183,'1183',1164,'c03f036c-8689-4b09-adbb-924304b6bb39','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Raman Takiar','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',7018407600,0,0,'House No. 4','Sector-19A',6,128,'160019','1','House No 253','Sector-4,Mansa Devi Complex',13,15,'134114','Sanjeev Gupta','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0093','PALM SPRINGS','M/s Manohar Infrastructure & Constructions Pvt Ltd','nbs@manoharrealty.com',0,1725033524,'SCO 139-142','Sector-17C',6,128,'160017','1','SCO 139-142','Sector-17C',6,128,'160017','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:150%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">Complainant, on 26.02.2011 booked(C-1)a 350 sq\r\nyards plot @ RS.18000 per sq yd (excluding EDC &amp; PLC)from the respondent in\r\nthe project Palm Springs, Mullanpur, Mohali. It was assured&nbsp;by respondent\r\nthat it has received all the approvals except one or two which will be obtained\r\nwithin 2-3 months &amp; the possession of the plot will be delivered in 2\r\nyears.The applicant paid Rs. 1890000 i.e. 30% of total sale\r\nconsideration.Thereafter the applicant chose to have a 250 sq yard plot instead\r\nof 350 sq yard &amp; accordingly requested(C-2) respondent to change the size\r\nof plot. The said request was accepted. Out of the amount of Rs. 1890000, respondent\r\nadjusted Rs. 1350000/- i.e. 30 % sale consideration towards 250 sq yrd plot @\r\nRs 18000 per sq yrd and only refunded Rs. 490000(C-3) instead of Rs. 540000.The\r\nrespondent issued an acknowledgement(C-4) for the 250 sq yards plot wherein it\r\narbitrarily incorporated the condition of paying the IDC which was never agreed\r\nbetween the parties. When resisted by the applicant, the respondent threatened\r\nthe applicant that his money will be forfeited if IDC charges are not paid.\r\nAlso in the said acknowledgment the respondent only acknowledged Rs. 1350000/-\r\ninstead of Rs. 1400000/-. On being confronted,the respondent assured to adjust\r\nremaining 50000/- at the time of agreement.Inspite of number of visits,\r\nrepeated requests and assurances, the respondent did not issue any allotment\r\nletter and execute the buyer’s agreement till date. A legal notice(C-5) was\r\nalso sent to it but to no avail.The respondent has misrepresented the applicant\r\nsince&nbsp;beginning and never informed him about the true picture of the\r\napprovals and the development . It had not even applied the permissions when\r\nthe plot was sold to the applicant. A list of approvals along with the dates\r\nwhen the same were applied and obtained is attached as C-6 and some important\r\napprovals as C-7 &amp; C-8.The respondent was not having approval or sanction\r\nfor collecting money.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.75in; text-align: justify; text-indent: -0.25in; line-height: 15.75pt; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">1.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">Directing the respondent to refund the principle\r\namount i.e. Rs. 1400000 along with interest as contemplated under rule 16 of\r\nThe Punjab RERA Rules, 2017, as the complainant has lost faith in the\r\nrespondent due to misrepresentation by it about the approvals &amp; stages of\r\ndevelopment during all these years ,did not issue any allotment letter &amp;\r\nexecute the agreement till date, failed to develop the project &amp; thus the\r\ncomplainant wish to withdraw from the project. Also the respondent has\r\ncommitted violation of various provisions of PAPRA &amp; conditions of various\r\napprovals granted to it, as it could not collect any amount till the exemption\r\nis received under Section 44 of PAPRA which was granted on 25.1.17.The\r\nrespondent collected the money from the complainant in 2011.The approvals were\r\ngranted to the respondent on the ground that it will not sell any plot &amp;\r\ncollect money from the general public till exemption under Section 44 of PAPRA\r\nis received.Also, inspite of receiving 30% of sale consideration the respondent\r\ndid not execute any agreement &amp; issue a plot number till date &amp; asking\r\nthe complainant to pay more money for getting the allotment letter &amp; execution\r\nof agreement in violation of Section 13 of RERA.</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.75in; text-align: justify; line-height: 15.75pt; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.75in; text-align: justify; text-indent: -0.25in; line-height: 15.75pt; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">2.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">To take action against\r\nrespondent under Section 61 of RERA for constant violation of provision of\r\nSection 13 of RERA as the respondent failed to issue any allotment letter &amp;\r\nexecute the buyer’s agreement till date, inspite of receiving 30% of sale\r\nconsideration&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.5in; text-align: justify; line-height: 15.75pt; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.75in; text-align: justify; text-indent: -0.25in; line-height: 15.75pt; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">3.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">For cancelling the registration of the\r\nrespondent and the extension granted to the respondent for constantly violating\r\nvarious provisions of RERA and for indulging into unfair trade practices.</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>',4500000.00,1400000.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<ol><li style=\"margin: 12pt 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">The respondent be directed to provide the list of allottees to\r\nwhom it has allotted/sold the 862 residential plots as per the layout plan\r\napproved by GMADA on 6.10.2015 and for which it is duly registered under RERA.</span></li><li style=\"margin: 12pt 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">The respondent be directed\r\nto provide the details in respect of funds collected from the general public\r\nsince 2010 in lieu of 862 residential plots which are part of approved layout\r\nand registered under Section 3 of RERA and also, the detail where such amount\r\nhas been utilized by the respondent. Also, the respondent be directed to\r\nprovide all the bank details where such amount has been deposited along with\r\nthe statement of accounts, since the year 2010 and where such amount has been\r\nutilized.</span></li><li style=\"margin: 12pt 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">The respondent be\r\ndirected to provide the details in respect of number of bookings done by it\r\nsince the year 2010 for the said 862 residential plots along with the list of\r\napplicants who had applied for booking of plots.</span></li><li style=\"margin: 12pt 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">The respondent be directed to provide the details as regards the\r\ncriteria adopted by it for allotting the plot numbers to different applicants\r\nthrough pick and choose policy.</span></li><li style=\"margin: 12pt 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">The respondent be directed to provide the list of total applicants\r\nand further, the list to whom it has already allotted the plot along with the\r\nlist of applicants to whom it has not allotted the plots till date.</span></li><li style=\"margin: 12pt 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">The respondent be directed to provide the list of hypothecated\r\nplots which are hypothecated to GMADA, out of the approved 862 residential\r\nplots and 73 commercial plots. Also, the respondent be directed to provide the\r\nlist of hypothected plots sold to general public.</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></li></ol>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:12.0pt;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:\r\n0in;margin-left:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:12.0pt;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:\r\n0in;margin-left:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;line-height:200%;\r\nmso-layout-grid-align:none;text-autospace:none\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'Ramantakiar','2018-12-27 19:57:06.000','Ramantakiar','2018-12-27 19:57:06.000'),(680,1183,'1183',1164,'c03f036c-8689-4b09-adbb-924304b6bb39','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Raman Takiar','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',7018407600,0,0,'House No. 4','Sector-19A',6,128,'160019','1','House No 253','Sector-4,Mansa Devi Complex',13,15,'134114','Sanjeev Gupta','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0093','PALM SPRINGS','M/s Manohar Infrastructure & Constructions Pvt Ltd','nbs@manoharrealty.com',0,1725033524,'SCO 139-142','Sector-17C',6,128,'160017','1','SCO 139-142','Sector-17C',6,128,'160017','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:150%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">Complainant, on 26.02.2011 booked (C-1) a 350 sq\r\nyards plot @ RS.18000 per sq yd (excluding EDC &amp; PLC)from the respondent in\r\nthe project Palm Springs, Mullanpur, Mohali. It was assured&nbsp;by respondent\r\nthat it has received all the approvals except one or two which will be obtained\r\nwithin 2-3 months &amp; the possession of the plot will be delivered in 2\r\nyears.The applicant paid Rs. 1890000 i.e. 30% of total sale\r\nconsideration.Thereafter the applicant chose to have a 250 sq yard plot instead\r\nof 350 sq yard &amp; accordingly requested(C-2) respondent to change the size\r\nof plot. The said request was accepted. Out of the amount of Rs. 1890000, respondent\r\nadjusted Rs. 1350000/- i.e. 30 % sale consideration towards 250 sq yrd plot @\r\nRs 18000 per sq yrd and only refunded Rs. 490000(C-3) instead of Rs. 540000.The\r\nrespondent issued an acknowledgement(C-4) for the 250 sq yards plot wherein it\r\narbitrarily incorporated the condition of paying the IDC which was never agreed\r\nbetween the parties. When resisted by the applicant, the respondent threatened\r\nthe applicant that his money will be forfeited if IDC charges are not paid.\r\nAlso in the said acknowledgment the respondent only acknowledged Rs. 1350000/-\r\ninstead of Rs. 1400000/-. On being confronted,the respondent assured to adjust\r\nremaining 50000/- at the time of agreement.Inspite of number of visits,\r\nrepeated requests and assurances, the respondent did not issue any allotment\r\nletter and execute the buyer’s agreement till date. A legal notice(C-5) was\r\nalso sent to it but to no avail.The respondent has misrepresented the applicant\r\nsince&nbsp;beginning and never informed him about the true picture of the\r\napprovals and the development . It had not even applied the permissions when\r\nthe plot was sold to the applicant. A list of approvals along with the dates\r\nwhen the same were applied and obtained is attached as (C-6) and some important\r\napprovals as (C-7 &amp; C-8).The respondent was not having approval or sanction\r\nfor collecting money.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.75in; text-align: justify; text-indent: -0.25in; line-height: 15.75pt; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">1.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">Directing the respondent to refund the principle\r\namount i.e. Rs. 1400000 along with interest as contemplated under rule 16 of\r\nThe Punjab RERA Rules, 2017, as the complainant has lost faith in the\r\nrespondent due to misrepresentation by it about the approvals &amp; stages of\r\ndevelopment during all these years ,did not issue any allotment letter &amp;\r\nexecute the agreement till date, failed to develop the project &amp; thus the\r\ncomplainant wish to withdraw from the project. Also the respondent has\r\ncommitted violation of various provisions of PAPRA &amp; conditions of various\r\napprovals granted to it, as it could not collect any amount till the exemption\r\nis received under Section 44 of PAPRA which was granted on 25.1.17.The\r\nrespondent collected the money from the complainant in 2011.The approvals were\r\ngranted to the respondent on the ground that it will not sell any plot &amp;\r\ncollect money from the general public till exemption under Section 44 of PAPRA\r\nis received.Also, inspite of receiving 30% of sale consideration the respondent\r\ndid not execute any agreement &amp; issue a plot number till date &amp; asking\r\nthe complainant to pay more money for getting the allotment letter &amp; execution\r\nof agreement in violation of Section 13 of RERA.</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.75in; text-align: justify; line-height: 15.75pt; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.75in; text-align: justify; text-indent: -0.25in; line-height: 15.75pt; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">2.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">To take action against\r\nrespondent under Section 61 of RERA for constant violation of provision of\r\nSection 13 of RERA as the respondent failed to issue any allotment letter &amp;\r\nexecute the buyer’s agreement till date, inspite of receiving 30% of sale\r\nconsideration&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.5in; text-align: justify; line-height: 15.75pt; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initi