08/- on 30.09.2007 and further a sum of Rs.40,49,131/- on 31.10.2007 (Total paid amount : Rs.50,95,339/-.&nbsp;</li><li>That the Claimant was allotted Unit No. L-3/1103 in Tower No. ‘L’ with a total cost of Rs.57,01,543/- in the Project known as ‘The Views’ vide letter dated 23.07.2007 and an Agreement was signed/executed on 11.02.2008 through the Authorized Signatory of the Respondent.</li><li><li>That failure on the part of the Respondent to hand over the possession of the unit on scheduled date and even after lapse of more than 8 years from date of allotment, amounts to deficiency in service.</li><li>That the Applicants have approached the Respondent on various occasions to refund the amount paid along with interest, but the Opposite Parties failed to do so.&nbsp; Further, refusal of the Opposite Parties to refund the amounts deposited by the Applicants</li><li>That as the Applicants have already been defrauded by the Respondent as it has misused the amount deposited, hence, the Respondent is at fault and there was deficiency of service on their part by not offering the possession after the expiry of 36 months i.e. September 2010 and instead offering the same after almost 8 years i.e. on 28.08.2018 without compensating the Applicants.</li></li></ul>','<p>The Applicant prays for the following compensation(s):-</p><p>Refund of an amount of Rs.50,95,339/- paid by the Applicants along with interest (highest marginal cost of lending rate of the State Bank of India+2%) from the respective dates of deposit till actual realization as per Sections 18 and 19(4) of the Act read with Rule 16 of the Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017.</p><p>Any other relief which the Applicants are entitled for under the Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Act, 2016 and the Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017.&nbsp;<br></p><div><br></div>',5701543.00,0.00,'2010-10-05 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<div><br></div><