.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:\r\n115%;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\r\nmso-ansi-language:EN-IN;mso-fareast-language:EN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\">Going\r\nby the facts detailed in para 4 above and the fact that in absence of Completion Certificate/Occupancy Certificate, execution of\r\ntransfer documents for common areas in favor of RWA is not possible.\r\nPending final decision on the requests sought detailed in para 5 the\r\ncomplainant seeks the issuance of the following interim order <i>as per Section 36 of RERA 2016</i>:</span><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">The builder be directed to handover maintenance function of the complex\r\nto the residents’ welfare association, formed by them and registered with the\r\nRegistrar Cooperative Societies, Punjab.</span><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Directing the respondent to ensure continuation\r\nof the services and maintenance, as are being provided by the maintenance\r\nagency SEMS, during intervening period of transfer process, free of cost.The&nbsp;respondent be barred from any further recovery of\r\ncharges on account of services and maintenance from the flat owners.The\r\nrespondent be directed to make payment of the services and maintenance\r\ncharges of unsold flats to RWA.The respondent be\r\ndirected to obtain and furnish Completion Certificate/ Occupancy Certificate\r\nwithin the time specified by the RERA Punjab.</span><br></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'neelam','2018-12-28 15:03:20.000','neelam','2018-12-28 15:03:20.000'),(728,1232,'1232',1302,'d89b0206-2eb1-4682-91b3-2181af1261fa','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','NEELAM PATHAK','n.pathak0312@gmail.com',9888487871,0,598973893949