Punjab\r\nsite nor entered project details, hence allowed to pass time of 3 weeks set by\r\nRERA for this vide cir. dated May 9, 2018, see Annexure I.</span></p><p class=\"paragraph\" style=\"margin:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;\r\nline-height:150%;vertical-align:baseline\"><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\">Documents on Development Plan&nbsp;and&nbsp;Details of Court Cases\r\nsought from AHCL vide Memo No.163 of 21.8.2017 are not available on record see\r\nAnnexure J, notwithstanding claims made in&nbsp;Diary No.1227 dated 01.09.2017\r\nsee Annexure K. Question arises, as to whether the same were ever submitted by\r\nAHCL.</span></p><p class=\"paragraph\" style=\"margin:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;\r\nline-height:150%;vertical-align:baseline\"><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\">RWA is already in place, over 10 years&nbsp;have lapsed\r\nbut&nbsp;completion certificate for the project is pending.&nbsp;State Consumer\r\nForum, Punjab&nbsp;judgement dt. Feb 2, 2018 clearly states:&nbsp;</span><b style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\"><i>The\r\ncompletion certificate is not issued by competent authority because the builder\r\nhas made deviations, violations in construction; it is his duty to rectify\r\nthose deviations or bring the deviations within permissible limits.&nbsp;</i></b><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\">See\r\nAnnexure H.</span></p><p class=\"paragraph\" style=\"margin:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;\r\nline-height:150%;vertical-align:baseline\"><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt;\">A sister concern of AHCL, provides essential services against hefty\r\nmaintenance fees,&nbsp;while delivering poor services. AHCL never responded to\r\nour concerns. Such indifferent&nbsp;attitude forced residents to unanimously\r\nhold back quarterly payment, in protest.&nbsp;Maintenance by builder is allowed\r\nbefore handing over of project to RWA by charging only reasonable charges</span></p><ol><li style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 150%; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Maintenance\r\nby RWA will be exempted vide SN. 77 on page 19 of GST Notification dated June\r\n28, 2017, see Annexure N; and</span></li><li style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 150%; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Maintenance\r\ncharges for unsold flats being borne by the allottees.<o:p></o:p></span></li></ol>\r\n\r\n<span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:Calibri;mso-fareast-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-ansi-language:\r\nEN-IN;mso-fareast-language:EN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\">This is forming approximately\r\n35 percent of the existing charges.</span>','<ol><li><b><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN;mso-fareast-language:\r\nEN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\">Information in contravenes to the Section 4: </span></b><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN;mso-fareast-language:\r\nEN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\">Failure of the promoter to comply with the instruction\r\ngiven in respect of&nbsp; Specific date of\r\ncompletion of the project has been dealt with under Section 60 of the RERA\r\n2016. The RERAPunjab is requested to take a note of failure of the promoter to\r\ncomply with the above instructions and requested to take a view, suitably.</span></li><li><b><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;li