01.09.2017\r\nsee Annexure K. Question arises, as to whether the same were ever submitted by\r\nAHCL.</span></p><p class=\"paragraph\" style=\"margin:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;\r\nline-height:150%;vertical-align:baseline\"><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px;\">RWA is already in place, over 10 years&nbsp;have lapsed\r\nbut&nbsp;completion certificate for the project is pending.&nbsp;State Consumer\r\nForum, Punjab&nbsp;judgement dt. Feb 2, 2018 clearly states:&nbsp;</span><b style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\"><i><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">The\r\ncompletion certificate is not issued by competent authority because the builder\r\nhas made deviations, violations in construction; it is his duty to rectify\r\nthose deviations or bring the deviations within permissible limits.&nbsp;</span></i></b><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px;\">See\r\nAnnexure H.</span></p><p class=\"paragraph\" style=\"margin:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;\r\nline-height:150%;vertical-align:baseline\"><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px;\">A sister concern of AHCL, provides essential services against hefty\r\nmaintenance fees,&nbsp;while delivering poor services. AHCL never responded to\r\nour concerns. Such indifferent&nbsp;attitude forced residents to unanimously\r\nhold back quarterly payment, in protest.&nbsp;Maintenance by builder is allowed\r\nbefore handing over of project to RWA by charging only reasonable charges</span></p><ol><li style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 150%; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px;\">Maintenance\r\nby RWA will be exempted vide SN. 77 on page 19 of GST Notification dated June\r\n28, 2017, see Annexure N; and</span></li><li style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 150%; vertical-align: baseline;\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Maintenance\r\ncharges for unsold flats being borne by the allottees.</span><o:p></o:p></span></li></ol><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">\r\n\r\n</span><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">This is forming approximately\r\n35 percent of the existing charges.</span>','<ol><li><b><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Information in contravenes to the Section 4: </span></b><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Failure of the promoter to comply with the instruction\r\ngiven in respect of&nbsp; Specific date of\r\ncompletion of the project has been dealt with under Section 60 of the RERA\r\n2016. The RERAPunjab is requested to take a note of failure of the promoter to\r\ncomply with the above instructions and requested to take a view, suitably.</span></li><li><b><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Promoter’s obligation of disclosure:&nbsp; </span></b><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Failure of the promoter to comply with the orders for\r\nup loading of information on website within 3 weeks has been dealt with under\r\nSection 63 of the RERA 2016. The RERA Punjab is requested to take a note of\r\nfailure of the promoter to comply its orders and requested to take a view,\r\nsuitably.</span></li><li><b><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Project deficiencies: </span></b><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">In compliance to the obligations, responsibilities and functions as\r\nper section 11.4.a of the Central Real Estate&nbsp;\r\nAct 2016, the builder may kindly