s being borne by the allottees.</span></span></li></ol><p><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">This is forming approximately 35 percent of the existing charges, which\r\nin no way may be considered reasonable.</span><br></span><br></span><br></p>','<ol><li><b><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Information in contravenes to the Section 4:&nbsp;</span></b><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Failure of the promoter to\r\ncomply with the instruction given in respect of&nbsp; Specific date of\r\ncompletion of the project has been dealt with under Section 60 of the RERA\r\n2016. The RERA Punjab is requested to take a note of failure of the promoter to\r\ncomply with the above instructions and on persistence, requested to take a\r\nview, suitably.</span></span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><b><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Promoter’s obligation of disclosure:&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></b><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Failure\r\nof the promoter to comply with the orders for up loading of information on\r\nwebsite within 3 weeks has been dealt with under Section 63 of the RERA 2016. If\r\nthe same still persists, the RERA Punjab is requested to take a note of failure\r\nof the promoter to comply its orders and , requested to take a view, suitably.</span></span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><b><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Project\r\ndeficiencies:&nbsp;</span></b><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">In compliance to the obligations, responsibilities and\r\nfunctions as per section 11.4.a of the Central Real Estate&nbsp; Act 2016, the\r\nbuilder may kindly be directed to complete the shortcomings in respect of the\r\nproject.</span></span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><b><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Completion Certificate</span></b><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">&nbsp;: As per section 11.4.b of the\r\nCentral Real Estate Act 2016 and the Rule 9.1.i of Punjab RERA 2017, the\r\nbuilder may kindly be directed obtain Completion Certificate within the time\r\nspecified by RERA Punjab.</span></span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><b><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Recognition of RWA</span></b><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">:&nbsp; As per section 11.4.e\r\nof the Central Real Estate Act 2016:&nbsp;</span><b><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">&nbsp;The promoter shall be\r\nresponsible for enabling the formation of association, society&nbsp;or coop.\r\nsociety, as the case may be, of&nbsp; allottees or a federation of the same,\r\n........within a period of&nbsp;three months of the majority of allottees have\r\nbooked their plot, apartment.......&nbsp;</span></b><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Hence, the builder may kindly be\r\ndirected to recognize and transfer the project to the already formed RWA.</span></span><br></li></ol>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Going by the facts detailed in para 4 above and the fact that in absence\r\nof Completion Certificate/Occupancy Certificate, execution of transfer\r\ndocuments for common areas in favor of RWA is not possible. Pending final\r\ndecision on the requests sought detailed in para 5 the complainant seeks the\r\nissuance of the following interim order&nbsp;</span><i><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">as per Section 36 of RERA 2016</span></i><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">:</span></span></p><ol><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">The\r\nbuilder be directed to handover maintenance function of the complex to the\r\nresidents’ welfare association, formed by them and registered with the\r\nRegistrar Cooperative Societies, Punjab.</span></span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 115%; font-family: Roboto;\">Directing the respondent to ensure continuation of the\r\nservices and maintenance, as are being provided by the maintenance agency\r\nSunrise Estate Management Services, during intervening period of transfer\r\nprocess, free of cost.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 115%; font-family: Roboto;\">The&nbsp;respondent be barred from any further recovery\r\nof charges on account of services and maintenance from the flat owners.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 115%; font-family: Roboto;\">The\r\nrespondent be directed to make payment of the services and maintenance charges\r\nof unsold flats to RWA.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 115%; font-family: Roboto;\">The respondent be directed to obtain and furnish\r\nCompletion Certificate/ Occupancy Certificate within the time specified by the\r\nRERA Punjab.</span><br></li></ol>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'csbkb','2018-12-30 22:01:43.000','csbkb','2018-12-30 22:01:43.000');
INSERT INTO `verified_table_tbl_rera_complaint_formm_details` VALUES (768,1236,'1236',1312,'6192c304-cccb-4808-870c-b203098a180a','FormTypeM',1,1,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Charanjeet Singh Bagga','csbkb1983@gmail.com',9424492156,0,435060324845,'Juniper 403, Ansal Woodbury Apartments','High Land Marg, Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','1','Juniper 403, Ansal Woodbury Apartments','High Land Marg, Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','Yogesh Pathak','yogeshpathak@hotmail.com',9041639575,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0044','Ansal Woodbury Apartmants','Ansal Housing and Construction Ltd. ','kushagr.ansal@ansals.com',0,0,'15 UGF Indra Prakash','21 Barakhamba Road',10,120,'110001','1','15 UGF Indra Prakash','21 Barakhamba Road',10,120,'110001','1','<p><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Detailed Form M is submitted as Annexure Form M, whereas gist of the\r\nrequest is being submitted here under.</span></p><p><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Project Registration is valid for\r\ncompletion period, declared by the builder in Form B, see Annexure C. AHCL\r\nwillfully omitted project completion date, resulting in:</span></p><ul><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Open registration,\r\nrequiring no further extension of the project.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">RWA is unable to claim the\r\npossession of common areas.</span></li></ul><p><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">After getting login ID, AHCL created neither web\r\npage on RERA Punjab site nor entered project details, hence allowed to pass\r\ntime of 3 weeks set by RERA for this vide cir. dated May 9, 2018, see Annexure\r\nI.</span></p><p><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Documents on Development Plan&nbsp;and&nbsp;Details of Court Cases sought\r\nfrom AHCL vide Memo No.163 of 21.8.2017 are not available on record see Annexure\r\nJ, notwithstanding claims made in&nbsp;Diary No.1227 dated 01.09.2017 see\r\nAnnexure K. Question arises, as to whether the same were ever submitted by\r\nAHCL.</span></p><p><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">RWA is already in place, over 10 years&nbsp;have lapsed\r\nbut&nbsp;completion certificate for the project is pending.&nbsp;State Consumer\r\nForum, Punjab&nbsp;judgment dt. Feb 2, 2018 clearly states:&nbsp;</span></span></span></p><p><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><b><i><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">The\r\ncompletion certificate is not issued by competent authority because the builder\r\nhas made deviations, violations in construction; it is his duty to rectify\r\nthose deviations or bring the deviations within permissible limits.&nbsp;</span></i></b><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">See\r\nAnnexure H.</span></span></span></p><p><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">A sister concern of AHCL, provides essential services against hefty\r\nmaintenance fees,&nbsp;while delivering poor services. AHCL never responded to\r\nour concerns. Such indifferent&nbsp;attitude forced residents to unanimously\r\nhold back quarterly payment, in protest.&nbsp;Maintenance by builder is allowed\r\nbefore handing over of project to RWA by charging only reasonable charges</span></span><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 115%; font-family: Roboto;\">.</span></span></p><ol><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Maintenance by RWA will be exempted vide SN. 77 on page 19 of GST\r\nNotification dated June 28, 2017, see Annexure N; and</span></span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Maintenance charges for\r\nunsold flats being borne by the allottees.</span></span></li></ol><p><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">This is forming approximately 35 percent of the existing charges, which\r\nin no way may be considered reasonable.</span><br></span><br></span><br></p>','<ol><li><b><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Information in contravenes to the Section 4:&nbsp;</span></b><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Failure of the promoter to\r\ncomply with the instruction given in respect of&nbsp; Specific date of\r\ncompletion of the project has been dealt with under Section 60 of the RERA\r\n2016. The RERA Punjab is requested to take a note of failure of the promoter to\r\ncomply with the above instructions and on persistence, requested to take a\r\nview, suitably.</span></span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><b><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Promoter’s obligation of disclosure:&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></b><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Failure\r\nof the promoter to comply with the orders for up loading of information on\r\nwebsite within 3 weeks has been dealt with under Section 63 of the RERA 2016. If\r\nthe same still persists, the RERA Punjab is requested to take a note of failure\r\nof the promoter to comply its orders and , requested to take a view, suitably.</span></span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><b><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Project\r\ndeficiencies:&nbsp;</span></b><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">In compliance to the obligations, responsibilities and\r\nfunctions as per section 11.4.a of the Central Real Estate&nbsp; Act 2016, the\r\nbuilder may kindly be directed to complete the shortcomings in respect of the\r\nproject.</span></span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><b><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Completion Certificate</span></b><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">&nbsp;: As per section 11.4.b of the\r\nCentral Real Estate Act 2016 and the Rule 9.1.i of Punjab RERA 2017, the\r\nbuilder may kindly be directed obtain Completion Certificate within the time\r\nspecified by RERA Punjab.</span></span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><b><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Recognition of RWA</span></b><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">:&nbsp; As per section 11.4.e\r\nof the Central Real Estate Act 2016:&nbsp;</span><b><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">&nbsp;The promoter shall be\r\nresponsible for enabling the formation of association, society&nbsp;or coop.\r\nsociety, as the case may be, of&nbsp; allottees or a federation of the same,\r\n........within a period of&nbsp;three months of the majority of allottees have\r\nbooked their plot, apartment.......&nbsp;</span></b><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Hence, the builder may kindly be\r\ndirected to recognize and transfer the project to the already formed RWA.</span></span><br></li></ol>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Going by the facts detailed in para 4 above and the fact that in absence\r\nof Completion Certificate/Occupancy Certificate, execution of transfer\r\ndocuments for common areas in favor of RWA is not possible. Pending final\r\ndecision on the requests sought detailed in para 5 the complainant seeks the\r\nissuance of the following interim order&nbsp;</span><i><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">as per Section 36 of RERA 2016</span></i><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">:</span></span></p><ol><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">The\r\nbuilder be directed to handover maintenance function of the complex to the\r\nresidents’ welfare association, formed by them and registered with the\r\nRegistrar Cooperative Societies, Punjab.</span></span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 115%; font-family: Roboto;\">Directing the respondent to ensure continuation of the\r\nservices and maintenance, as are being provided by the maintenance agency\r\nSunrise Estate Management Services, during intervening period of transfer\r\nprocess, free of cost.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 115%; font-family: Roboto;\">The&nbsp;respondent be barred from any further recovery\r\nof charges on account of services and maintenance from the flat owners.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 115%; font-family: Roboto;\">The\r\nrespondent be directed to make payment of the services and maintenance charges\r\nof unsold flats to RWA.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 115%; font-family: Roboto;\">The respondent be directed to obtain and furnish\r\nCompletion Certificate/ Occupancy Certificate within the time specified by the\r\nRERA Punjab.</span><br></li></ol>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',1,0,0,0,'csbkb','2018-12-30 22:14:01.000','csbkb','2018-12-30 22:14:01.000'),(769,1235,'1235',1312,'6192c304-cccb-4808-870c-b203098a180a','FormTypeM',1,1,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Charanjeet Singh Bagga','csbkb1983@gmail.com',9424492156,0,435060324845,'Juniper 403, Ansal Woodbury Apartments','High Land Marg, Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','1','Juniper 403, Ansal Woodbury Apartments','High Land Marg, Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','Yogesh Pathak','yogeshpathak@hotmail.com',9041639575,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0044','Ansal Woodbury Apartments ','Ansal Housing and Construction Ltd.','kushagr.ansal@ansals.com',0,0,'15 UGF Indra Prakash','21 Barakhamba Road',10,120,'110001','1','15 UGF Indra Prakash','21 Barakhamba Road',10,120,'110001','1','<p><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Detailed Form M is submitted as Annexure Form M, whereas gist of the\r\nrequest is being submitted here under. Project Registration is valid for\r\ncompletion period, declared by the builder in Form B, see Annexure C. AHCL\r\nwillfully omitted project completion date, resulting in:</span></p><ul><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Open registration,\r\nrequiring no further extension of the project.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">RWA is unable to claim the\r\npossession of common areas.</span></li></ul><p><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">After getting login ID, AHCL