nt, in protest.&nbsp;Maintenance by builder is allowed\r\nbefore handing over of project to RWA by charging only reasonable charges</span><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Roboto;\">.&nbsp;</span></span></p><ol><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Maintenance by RWA will be exempted vide SN. 77 of GST\r\nNotification dated June 28, 2017, see Annexure N; and </span></span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Maintenance charges for\r\nunsold flats presently being borne by the allottees.</span></span></li></ol><p><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">This is forming approximately 36 percent of the existing charges, which in no way may be considered as reasonable.</span><br></span><br></span><br></p>','<ol><li><b><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Information in contravenes to the Section 4:&nbsp;</span></b><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Failure of the promoter to\r\ncomply with the instruction given in respect of&nbsp; Specific date of\r\ncompletion of the project has been dealt with under Section 60 of the RERA\r\n2016. The RERA Punjab is requested to take a note of failure of the promoter to\r\ncomply with the above instructions and on persistence, requested to take a view, suitably.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><b>Promoter’s\r\nobligation of disclosure:&nbsp;&nbsp;</b>Failure of the promoter to comply with\r\nthe orders for up loading of information on website within 3 weeks has been\r\ndealt with under Section 63 of the RERA 2016. If the same still persist, the RERA Punjab is requested to\r\ntake a note of failure of the promoter to comply its orders and requested to\r\ntake a view, suitably.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><b>Project deficiencies:&nbsp;</b>In compliance to the\r\nobligations, responsibilities and functions as per section 11.4.a of the\r\nCentral Real Estate&nbsp; Act 2016, the builder may kindly be directed to\r\ncomplete the shortcomings in respect of the project.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><b>Completion Certificate</b>&nbsp;:\r\nAs per section 11.4.b of the Central Real Estate Act 2016 and the Rule 9.1.i of\r\nPunjab RERA 2017, the builder may kindly be directed obtain Completion Certificate\r\nwithin the time specified by RERA Punjab.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><b>Recognition of RWA</b>:&nbsp; As\r\nper section 11.4.e of the Central Real Estate Act 2016:&nbsp;<b>&nbsp;The\r\npromoter shall be responsible for enabling the formation of association,\r\nsociety&nbsp;or coop. society, as the case may be, of&nbsp; allottees or a\r\nfederation of the same, ........within a period of&nbsp;three months of the\r\nmajority of allottees have booked their plot, apartment.......&nbsp;</b>Hence,\r\nthe builder may kindly be directed to recognize and transfer the project to the\r\nalready formed RWA.</span><br></li></ol>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Going by the facts detailed in para 4 above and the fact that in absence\r\nof Completion Certificate/Occupancy Certificate, execution of transfer\r\ndocuments for common areas in favor of RWA is not possible. Pending final\r\ndecision on the requests sought detailed in para 5 the complainant seeks the\r\nissuance of the following interim order&nbsp;<i>as per Section 36 of RERA 2016</i>:</span></p><ol><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">The\r\nbuilder be directed to handover maintenance function of the complex to the\r\nresidents’ welfare association, formed by them and registered with the\r\nRegistrar Cooperative Societies, Punjab.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Roboto;\">Directing the respondent to ensure continuation of the\r\nservices and maintenance, as are being provided by the maintenance agency\r\nSunrise Estate Management Services, during intervening period of transfer\r\nprocess, free of cost.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Roboto;\">The&nbsp;respondent be barred from any further recovery\r\nof charges on account of services and maintenance from the flat owners.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Roboto;\">The\r\nrespondent be directed to make payment of the services and maintenance charges\r\nof unsold flats to RWA.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Roboto;\">The respondent be directed to obtain and furnish\r\nCompletion Certificate/ Occupancy Certificate within the time specified by the\r\nRERA Punjab.</span><br></li></ol>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'csbkb','2018-12-31 11:06:44.000','csbkb','2018-12-31 11:06:44.000'),(770,1235,'1235',1312,'6192c304-cccb-4808-870c-b203098a180a','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-31 11:12:26.000','Charanjeet Singh Bagga','csbkb1983@gmail.com',9424492156,0,435060324845,'Juniper 403, Ansal Woodbury Apartments','High Land Marg, Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','1','Juniper 403, Ansal Woodbury Apartments','High Land Marg, Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','Yogesh Pathak','yogeshpathak@hotmail.com',9041639575,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0044','Ansal Woodbury Apartments ','Ansal Housing and Construction Ltd.','kushagr.ansal@ansals.com',0,0,'15 UGF Indra Prakash','21 Barakhamba Road',10,120,'110001','1','15 UGF Indra Prakash','21 Barakhamba Road',10,120,'110001','1','<p><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Detailed Form M is submitted as Annexure Form M, whereas gist of the\r\nrequest is being submitted here under. Project Registration is valid for\r\ncompletion period, declared by the builder in Form B, see Annexure C. AHCL\r\nwillfully omitted project completion date, resulting in:</span></p><ul><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Open registration,\r\nrequiring no further extension of the project.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">RWA is unable to claim the\r\npossession of common areas.</span></li></ul><p><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">After getting login ID, AHCL created neither web\r\npage on RERA Punjab website nor entered project details, hence allowed to pass\r\ntime of 3 weeks set by RERA for this vide cir. dated May 9, 2018, see Annexure\r\nI.</span></p><p><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Documents on Development Plan&nbsp;and&nbsp;Details of Court Cases sought\r\nfrom AHCL vide Memo No.163 of 21.8.2017 are not available on record see Annexure\r\nJ, notwithstanding claims made in&nbsp;Diary No.1227 dated 01.09.2017 see\r\nAnnexure K. Question arises, as to whether the same were submitted by\r\nAHCL.</span></p><p><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">RWA is already in place, over 10 years&nbsp;have lapsed\r\nbut&nbsp;completion certificate for the project is pending.&nbsp;State Consumer\r\nForum, Punjab&nbsp;judgment dt. Feb 2, 2018 clearly states:&nbsp;</span></span></p><p><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><b><i>The\r\ncompletion certificate is not issued by competent authority because the builder\r\nhas made deviations, violations in construction; it is his duty to rectify\r\nthose deviations or bring the deviations within permissible limits.&nbsp;</i></b>See\r\nAnnexure H.</span></span></p><p><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">A sister concern of AHCL, provides essential services against hefty\r\nmaintenance fees,&nbsp;while delivering poor services. AHCL never responded to\r\nour concerns. Such indifferent&nbsp;attitude forced residents to unanimously\r\nhold back quarterly payment, in protest.&nbsp;Maintenance by builder is allowed\r\nbefore handing over of project to RWA by charging only reasonable charges</span><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Roboto;\">.&nbsp;</span></span></p><ol><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Maintenance by RWA will be exempted vide SN. 77 of GST\r\nNotification dated June 28, 2017, see Annexure N; and </span></span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Maintenance charges for\r\nunsold flats presently being borne by the allottees.</span></span></li></ol><p><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">This is forming approximately 36 percent of the existing charges, which in no way may be considered as reasonable.</span><br></span><br></span><br></p>','<ol><li><b><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Information in contravenes to the Section 4:&nbsp;</span></b><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Failure of the promoter to\r\ncomply with the instruction given in respect of&nbsp; Specific date of\r\ncompletion of the project has been dealt with under Section 60 of the RERA\r\n2016. The RERA Punjab is requested to take a note of failure of the promoter to\r\ncomply with the above instructions and on persistence, requested to take a view, suitably.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><b>Promoter’s\r\nobligation of disclosure:&nbsp;&nbsp;</b>Failure of the promoter to comply with\r\nthe orders for up loading of information on website within 3 weeks has been\r\ndealt with under Section 63 of the RERA 2016. If the same still persist, the RERA Punjab is requested to\r\ntake a note of failure of the promoter to comply its orders and requested to\r\ntake a view, suitably.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><b>Project deficiencies:&nbsp;</b>In compliance to the\r\nobligations, responsibilities and functions as per section 11.4.a of the\r\nCentral Real Estate&nbsp; Act 2016, the builder may kindly be directed to\r\ncomplete the shortcomings in respect of the project.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><b>Completion Certificate</b>&nbsp;:\r\nAs per section 11.4.b of the Central Real Estate Act 2016 and the Rule 9.1.i of\r\nPunjab RERA 2017, the builder may kindly be directed obtain Completion Certificate\r\nwithin the time specified by RERA Punjab.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><b>Recognition of RWA</b>:&nbsp; As\r\nper section 11.4.e of the Central Real Estate Act 2016:&nbsp;<b>&nbsp;The\r\npromoter shall be responsible for enabling the formation of association,\r\nsociety&nbsp;or coop. society, as the case may be, of&nbsp; allottees or a\r\nfederation of the same, ........within a period of&nbsp;three months of the\r\nmajority of allottees have booked their plot, apartment.......&nbsp;</b>Hence,\r\nthe builder may kindly be directed to recognize and transfer the project to the\r\nalready formed RWA.</span><br></li></ol>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Going by the facts detailed in para 4 above and the fact that in absence\r\nof Completion Certificate/Occupancy Certificate, execution of transfer\r\ndocuments for common areas in favor of RWA is not possible. Pending final\r\ndecision on the requests sought detailed in para 5 the complainant seeks the\r\nissuance of the following interim order&nbsp;<i>as per Section 36 of RERA 2016</i>:</span></p><ol><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">The\r\nbuilder be directed to handover maintenance function of the complex to the\r\nresidents’ welfare association, formed by them and registered with the\r\nRegistrar Cooperative Societies, Punjab.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Roboto;\">Directing the respondent to ensure continuation of the\r\nservices and maintenance, as are being provided by the maintenance agency\r\nSunrise Estate Management Services, during intervening period of transfer\r\nprocess, free of cost.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Roboto;\">The&nbsp;respondent be barred from any further recovery\r\nof charges on account of services and maintenance from the flat owners.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Roboto;\">The\r\nrespondent be directed to make payment of the services and maintenance charges\r\nof unsold flats to RWA.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Roboto;\">The respondent be directed to obtain and furnish\r\nCompletion Certificate/ Occupancy Certificate within the time specified by the\r\nRERA Punjab.</span><br></li></ol>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'csbkb','2018-12-31 11:11:01.000','csbkb','2018-12-31 11:11:01.000'),(771,1234,'1234',1311,'d4bfd6db-9fb2-4eaa-ba16-0539fc46a714','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Gaurav Kumar','gaurav4478@gmail.com',9815978440,0,0,'130, Amrit Colony, Panj Peer Road,','Opposite Dairy Complex, Haibowal Khurd',28,366,'141001','1','130, Amrit Colony, Panj Peer Road,','Opposite Dairy Complex, Haibowal Khurd',28,366,'141001','Prabhjot Singh Sachdeva','prabhjotsinghsachdeva@ymail.com',9988126268,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-LDH45-PR0052','Ireo Waterfront Private Limited','Varun Khanna','varun.khanna@ireo.in',0,0,'Ireo Campus, Archview Drive, Ireo City,','Golf Course Extension Road, Sector 59',13,5,'122101','1','Ireo Campus, Archview Drive, Ireo City,','Golf Course Extension Road, Sector 59',13,5,'122101','1','<p><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font></p><p style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n<br></font></p><p style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\'line-height: 150%; font-family: \"Arial\",\"sans-serif\"; font-size: 14pt;\'>Brief\r\nfacts of the complaint are, Complainants have booked a Built Up <span style=\"mso-spacerun: yes;\">&nbsp;</span>Coral floor situated at Ireo Waterfront Pvt.\r\nLtd., Sidhwan Canal Road, V. Dewatwal, Ludhiana with the respondents in December\r\n2012. The respondents have allotted built up floor no.X012A coral floor having\r\nsuper area of 1532 sq ft., on the plot measuring 236.8 sq yards and the agreement\r\nto the effect was executed on 25.09.2013 (copy enclosed) but latter on\r\nrespondents had changed the same to X26A arbitrarily and without the consent of\r\ncomplainants. In order to buy peace and harmony complainants accepted the same,\r\nafter exchange of several emails, without prejudice to their rights. The complainants\r\nhave made the payments to the respondents and till date</span><span style=\'line-height: 150%; font-family: \"Arial\",\"sans-serif\"; font-size: 14pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 11.0pt;\'> </span><span style=\'line-height: 150%; font-family: \"Arial\",\"sans-serif\"; font-size: 14pt;\'>Rs.53,56,581/- (51,88,041/- for built up\r\nfloor + 1,68,540/- for club membership) have been paid in total. The Complainants\r\nhave also availed a loan of Rs.40 lacs from HDFC Ltd. @ 9.20% for making\r\npayments. <span style=\"mso-spacerun: yes;\">&nbsp;</span>As per the terms of agreement\r\nnotice of completion is to be given by the respondents within the period of 24\r\nmonths + 180 days (Grace Period). But till date i.e. even after the lapse of\r\nmore than five years from the date of execution of agreement, the respondents\r\nhave not delivered the possessions of built up floor. We approached respondents</span><span style=\'line-height: 150%; font-family: \"Arial\",\"sans-serif\"; font-size: 14pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 11.0pt;\'> </span><span style=\'line-height: 150%; font-family: \"Arial\",\"sans-serif\"; font-size: 14pt;\'>number of times but they kept on lingering on\r\nthe matter and also insisted the complainant to take another unit but as and\r\nwhen the complainants intends to accept their offer, then on very next meeting,\r\nthey changed their earlier proposal and offered some another proposal (emails\r\nattached). The respondents are now pressurizing the complainants to get an\r\nalternative unit which is neither agreed between the parties nor\r\nacceptable/feasible to the complainants. Legal notice dated 21.12.2018 was also\r\nserved upon the respondents through counsel, but they failed to do the needful.</span></p><p style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<br></p>','<p><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font></p><p style=\"margin: 0in 0in 10pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><font face=\"Arial\"></font><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n<br></font></p><p style=\"margin: 0in 0in 10pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\'line-height: 150%; font-family: \"Arial\",\"sans-serif\"; font-size: 14pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 11.0pt;\'>It is, therefore, respectfully prayed that the\r\nrespondents may kindly be directed to refund the amount of Rs.53,56,581/- along\r\nwith interest over and above the interest which the complainants are paying to\r\nthe HDFC Ltd. from which they have availed the loan facility for purchase the\r\nproperty, from the date of execution of the agreement till the realization of\r\nthe amount, the complainants are also entitled to get a compensation to the\r\ntune of Rs.5 Lakh on account of mental pain, agony and harassment suffered by\r\nthem as provided U/s 14 (3) and Section 19 of the said Act. </span></p><p style=\"margin: 0in 0in 10pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"></p><span style=\'line-height: 150%; font-family: \"Arial\",\"sans-serif\"; font-size: 14pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 11.0pt;\'><p style=\"margin: 0in 0in 10pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font></p><p style=\"margin: 0in 0in 10pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\'line-height: 150%; font-family: \"Arial\",\"sans-serif\"; font-size: 14pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 11.0pt;\'><span style=\"mso-tab-count: 1;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span>The strict\r\naction U/s 7 &amp; 8 is also required to be taken against the respondents for\r\nviolating the provisions of The Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development Act).</span></p><p style=\"margin: 0in 0in 10pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font></p><p style=\"margin: 0in 0in 10pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\'line-height: 150%; font-family: \"Arial\",\"sans-serif\"; font-size: 14pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 11.0pt;\'><span style=\"mso-tab-count: 2;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span>Any\r\nother relief which the complainants seems entitled to by this Hon\'ble\r\nAuthority, may also be granted to the complainants in the interest of justice\r\nand equity.<br></span></p></span><p style=\"margin: 0in 0in 10pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><br></p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font></p><p style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\'line-height: 150%; font-family: \"Arial\",\"sans-serif\"; font-size: 14pt;\'>The\r\nrespondents may kindly be directed to deposit at least 50% of the amount\r\nalongwith interest as interim relief as a condition precedent before filling\r\ntheir written statement/ defence. <br></span></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'gaurav4478','2018-12-31 16:57:03.000','gaurav4478','2018-12-31 16:57:03.000'),(772,1183,'1183',1164,'c03f036c-8689-4b09-adbb-924304b6bb39','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-01-01 16:21:08.000','Raman Takiar','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',7018407600,0,0,'House No. 4','Sector-19A',6,128,'160019','1','House No 253','Sector-4,Mansa Devi Complex',13,15,'134114','Sanjeev Gupta','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0093','PALM SPRINGS','M/s Manohar Infrastructure & Constructions Pvt Ltd','nbs@manoharrealty.com',0,1725033524,'SCO 139-142','Sector-17C',6,128,'160017','1','SCO 139-142','Sector-17C',6,128,'160017','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:150%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">Complainant, on 26.02.2011 booked (C-1) a 350 sq\r\nyards plot @ RS.18000 per sq yd (excluding EDC &amp; PLC)from the respondent in\r\nthe project Palm Springs, Mullanpur, Mohali. It was assured&nbsp;by respondent\r\nthat it has received all the approvals except one or two which will be obtained\r\nwithin 2-3 months &amp; the possession of the plot will be delivered in 2\r\nyears.The applicant paid Rs. 1890000 i.e. 30% of total sale\r\nconsideration.Thereafter the applicant chose to have a 250 sq yard plot instead\r\nof 350 sq yard &amp; accordingly requested(C-2) respondent to change the size\r\nof plot. The said request was accepted. Out of the amount of Rs. 1890000, respondent\r\nadjusted Rs. 1350000/- i.e. 30 % sale consideration towards 250 sq yrd plot @\r\nRs 18000 per sq yrd and only refunded Rs. 490000(C-3) instead of Rs. 540000.The\r\nrespondent issued an acknowledgement(C-4) for the 250 sq yards plot wherein it\r\narbitrarily incorporated the condition of paying the IDC which was never agreed\r\nbetween the parties. When resisted by the applicant, the respondent threatened\r\nthe applicant that his money will be forfeited if IDC charges are not paid.\r\nAlso in the said acknowledgment the respondent only acknowledged Rs. 1350000/-\r\ninstead of Rs. 1400000/-. On being confronted,the respondent assured to adjust\r\nremaining 50000/- at the time of agreement.Inspite of number of visits,\r\nrepeated requests and assurances, the respondent did not issue any allotment\r\nletter and execute the buyer’s agreement till date. A legal notice(C-5) was\r\nalso sent to it but to no avail.The respondent has misrepresented the applicant\r\nsince&nbsp;beginning and never informed him about the true picture of the\r\napprovals and the development . It had not even applied the permissions when\r\nthe plot was sold to the applicant. A list of approvals along with the dates\r\nwhen the same were applied and obtained is attached as (C-6) and some important\r\napprovals as (C-7 &amp; C-8).The respondent was not having approval or sanction\r\nfor collecting money.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.75in; text-align: justify; text-indent: -0.25in; line-height: 15.75pt; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">1.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">Directing the respondent to refund the principle\r\namount i.e. Rs. 1400000 along with interest as contemplated under rule 16 of\r\nThe Punjab RERA Rules, 2017, as the complainant has lost faith in the\r\nrespondent due to misrepresentation by it about the approvals &amp; stages of\r\ndevelopment during all these years ,did not issue any allotment letter &amp;\r\nexecute the agreement till date, failed to develop the project &amp; thus the\r\ncomplainant wish to withdraw from the project. Also the respondent has\r\ncommitted violation of various provisions of PAPRA &amp; conditions of various\r\napprovals granted to it, as it could not collect any amount till the exemption\r\nis received under Section 44 of PAPRA which was granted on 25.1.17.The\r\nrespondent collected the money from the complainant in 2011.The approvals were\r\ngranted to the respondent on the ground that it will not sell any plot &amp;\r\ncollect money from the general public till exemption under Section 44 of PAPRA\r\nis received.Also, inspite of receiving 30% of sale consideration the respondent\r\ndid not execute any agreement &amp; issue a plot number till date &amp; asking\r\nthe complainant to pay more money for getting the allotment letter &amp; execution\r\nof agreement in violation of Section 13 of RERA.</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.75in; text-align: justify; line-height: 15.75pt; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.75in; text-align: justify; text-indent: -0.25in; line-height: 15.75pt; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">2.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">To take action against\r\nrespondent under Section 61 of RERA for constant violation of provision of\r\nSection 13 of RERA as the respondent failed to issue any allotment letter &amp;\r\nexecute the buyer’s agreement till date, inspite of receiving 30% of sale\r\nconsideration&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.5in; text-align: justify; line-height: 15.75pt; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.75in; text-align: justify; text-indent: -0.25in; line-height: 15.75pt; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">3.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">For cancelling the registration of the\r\nrespondent and the extension granted to the respondent for constantly violating\r\nvarious provisions of RERA and for indulging into unfair trade practices.</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>',4500000.00,1400000.00,'2013-02-26 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<ol><li style=\"margin: 12pt 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">The respondent be directed to provide the list of allottees to\r\nwhom it has allotted/sold the 862 residential plots as per the layout plan\r\napproved by GMADA on 6.10.2015 and for which it is duly registered under RERA.</span></li><li style=\"margin: 12pt 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">The respondent be directed\r\nto provide the details in respect of funds collected from the general public\r\nsince 2010 in lieu of 862 residential plots which are part of approved layout\r\nand registered under Section 3 of RERA and also, the detail where such amount\r\nhas been utilized by the respondent. Also, the respondent be directed to\r\nprovide all the bank details where such amount has been deposited along with\r\nthe statement of accounts, since the year 2010 and where such amount has been\r\nutilized.</span></li><li style=\"margin: 12pt 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">The respondent be\r\ndirected to provide the details in respect of number of bookings done by it\r\nsince the year 2010 for the said 862 residential plots along with the list of\r\napplicants who had applied for booking of plots.</span></li><li style=\"margin: 12pt 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">The respondent be directed to provide the details as regards the\r\ncriteria adopted by it for allotting the plot numbers to different applicants\r\nthrough pick and choose policy.</span></li><li style=\"margin: 12pt 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">The respondent be directed to provide the list of total applicants\r\nand further, the list to whom it has already allotted the plot along with the\r\nlist of applicants to whom it has not allotted the plots till date.</span></li><li style=\"margin: 12pt 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">The respondent be directed to provide the list of hypothecated\r\nplots which are hypothecated to GMADA, out of the approved 862 residential\r\nplots and 73 commercial plots. Also, the respondent be directed to provide the\r\nlist of hypothected plots sold to general public.</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></li></ol>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:12.0pt;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:\r\n0in;margin-left:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:12.0pt;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:\r\n0in;margin-left:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;line-height:200%;\r\nmso-layout-grid-align:none;text-autospace:none\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',1,1,0,0,'Ramantakiar','2018-12-31 19:15:10.000','Ramantakiar','2018-12-31 19:15:10.000'),(773,1234,'1234',1311,'d4bfd6db-9fb2-4eaa-ba16-0539fc46a714','FormTypeM',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Gaurav Kumar','gaurav4478@gmail.com',9815978440,0,0,'130, Amrit Colony, Panj Peer Road,','Opposite Dairy Complex, Haibowal Khurd',28,366,'141001','1','130, Amrit Colony, Panj Peer Road,','Opposite Dairy Complex, Haibowal Khurd',28,366,'141001','Prabhjot Singh Sachdeva','prabhjotsinghsachdeva@ymail.com',9988126268,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-LDH45-PR0052','Ireo Waterfront Private Limited','Varun Khanna','varun.khanna@ireo.in',0,0,'Ireo Campus, Archview Drive, Ireo City,','Golf Course Extension Road, Sector 59',13,5,'122101','1','Ireo Campus, Archview Drive, Ireo City,','Golf Course Extension Road, Sector 59',13,5,'122101','1','<p><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font></p><p style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n<br></font></p><p style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\'line-height: 150%; font-family: \"Arial\",\"sans-serif\"; font-size: 14pt;\'>Brief\r\nfacts of the complaint are, Complainants have booked a Built Up <span style=\"mso-spacerun: yes;\">&nbsp;</span>Coral floor situated at Ireo Waterfront Pvt.\r\nLtd., Sidhwan Canal Road, V. Dewatwal, Ludhiana with the respondents in December\r\n2012. The respondents have allotted built up floor no.X012A coral floor having\r\nsuper area of 1532 sq ft., on the plot measuring 236.8 sq yards and the agreement\r\nto the effect was executed on 25.09.2013 (copy enclosed) but latter on\r\nrespondents had changed the same to X26A arbitrarily and without the consent of\r\ncomplainants. In order to buy peace and harmony complainants accepted the same,\r\nafter exchange of several emails, without prejudice to their rights. The complainants\r\nhave made the payments to the respondents and till date</span><span style=\'line-height: 150%; font-family: \"Arial\",\"sans-serif\"; font-size: 14pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 11.0pt;\'> </span><span style=\'line-height: 150%; font-family: \"Arial\",\"sans-serif\"; font-size: 14pt;\'>Rs.53,56,581/- (51,88,041/- for built up\r\nfloor + 1,68,540/- for club membership) have been paid in total. The Complainants\r\nhave also availed a loan of Rs.40 lacs from HDFC Ltd. @ 9.20% for making\r\npayments. <span style=\"mso-spacerun: yes;\">&nbsp;</span>As per the terms of agreement\r\nnotice of completion is to be given by the respondents within the period of 24\r\nmonths + 180 days (Grace Period). But till date i.e. even after the lapse of\r\nmore than five years from the date of execution of agreement, the respondents\r\nhave not delivered the possessions of built up floor. We approached respondents</span><span style=\'line-height: 150%; font-family: \"Arial\",\"sans-serif\"; font-size: 14pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 11.0pt;\'> </span><span style=\'line-height: 150%; font-family: \"Arial\",\"sans-serif\"; font-size: 14pt;\'>number of times but they kept on lingering on\r\nthe matter and also insisted the complainant to take another unit but as and\r\nwhen the complainants intends to accept their offer, then on very next meeting,\r\nthey changed their earlier proposal and offered some another proposal (emails\r\nattached). The respondents are now pressurizing the complainants to get an\r\nalternative unit which is neither agreed between the parties nor\r\nacceptable/feasible to the complainants. Legal notice dated 21.12.2018 was also\r\nserved upon the respondents through counsel, but they failed to do the needful.</span></p><p style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<br></p>','<p><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font></p><p style=\"margin: 0in 0in 10pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><font face=\"Arial\"></font><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n<br></font></p><p style=\"margin: 0in 0in 10pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\'line-height: 150%; font-family: \"Arial\",\"sans-serif\"; font-size: 14pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 11.0pt;\'>It is, therefore, respectfully prayed that the\r\nrespondents may kindly be directed to refund the amount of Rs.53,56,581/- along\r\nwith interest over and above the interest which the complainants are paying to\r\nthe HDFC Ltd. from which they have availed the loan facility for purchase the\r\nproperty, from the date of execution of the agreement till the realization of\r\nthe amount, the complainants are also entitled to get a compensation to the\r\ntune of Rs.5 Lakh on account of mental pain, agony and harassment suffered by\r\nthem as provided U/s 14 (3) and Section 19 of the said Act. </span></p><p style=\"margin: 0in 0in 10pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"></p><span style=\'line-height: 150%; font-family: \"Arial\",\"sans-serif\"; font-size: 14pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 11.0pt;\'><p style=\"margin: 0in 0in 10pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font></p><p style=\"margin: 0in 0in 10pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\'line-height: 150%; font-family: \"Arial\",\"sans-serif\"; font-size: 14pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 11.0pt;\'><span style=\"mso-tab-count: 1;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span>The strict\r\naction U/s 7 &amp; 8 is also required to be taken against the respondents for\r\nviolating the provisions of The Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development Act).</span></p><p style=\"margin: 0in 0in 10pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font></p><p style=\"margin: 0in 0in 10pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\'line-height: 150%; font-family: \"Arial\",\"sans-serif\"; font-size: 14pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 11.0pt;\'><span style=\"mso-tab-count: 2;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span>Any\r\nother relief which the complainants seems entitled to by this Hon\'ble\r\nAuthority, may also be granted to the complainants in the interest of justice\r\nand equity.<br></span></p></span><p style=\"margin: 0in 0in 10pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><br></p>',6041820.00,5356581.00,'2016-03-24 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font></p><p style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\'line-height: 150%; font-family: \"Arial\",\"sans-serif\"; font-size: 14pt;\'>The\r\nrespondents may kindly be directed to deposit at least 50% of the amount\r\nalongwith interest as interim relief as a condition precedent before filling\r\ntheir written statement/ defence. <br></span></p>','1','','2013-05-15 00:00:00','2013-09-25 00:00:00','X012A Coral Floors, Sidhwan Canal Road, V. Dewatwal, Ludhiana','','',2,0,0,0,'gaurav4478','2019-01-01 15:49:51.000','gaurav4478','2019-01-01 15:49:51.000'),(774,1234,'1234',1311,'d4bfd6db-9fb2-4eaa-ba16-0539fc46a714','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-01-02 19:56:42.000','Gaurav Kumar','gaurav4478@gmail.com',9815978440,0,0,'130, Amrit Colony, Panj Peer Road,','Opposite Dairy Complex, Haibowal Khurd',28,366,'141001','1','130, Amrit Colony, Panj Peer Road,','Opposite Dairy Complex, Haibowal Khurd',28,366,'141001','Prabhjot Singh Sachdeva','prabhjotsinghsachdeva@ymail.com',9988126268,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-LDH45-PR0052','Ireo Waterfront Private Limited','Varun Khanna','varun.khanna@ireo.in',0,0,'Ireo Campus, Archview Drive, Ireo City,','Golf Course Extension Road, Sector 59',13,5,'122101','1','Ireo Campus, Archview Drive, Ireo City,','Golf Course Extension Road, Sector 59',13,5,'122101','1','<p><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font></p><p style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n<br></font></p><p style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\'line-height: 150%; font-family: \"Arial\",\"sans-serif\"; font-size: 14pt;\'>Brief\r\nfacts of the complaint are, Complainants have booked a Built Up <span style=\"mso-spacerun: yes;\">&nbsp;</span>Coral floor situated at Ireo Waterfront Pvt.\r\nLtd., Sidhwan Canal Road, V. Dewatwal, Ludhiana with the respondents in December\r\n2012. The respondents have allotted built up floor no.X012A coral floor having\r\nsuper area of 1532 sq ft., on the plot measuring 236.8 sq yards and the agreement\r\nto the effect was executed on 25.09.2013 (copy enclosed) but latter on\r\nrespondents had changed the same to X26A arbitrarily and without the consent of\r\ncomplainants. In order to buy peace and harmony complainants accepted the same,\r\nafter exchange of several emails, without prejudice to their rights. The complainants\r\nhave made the payments to the respondents and till date</span><span style=\'line-height: 150%; font-family: \"Arial\",\"sans-serif\"; font-size: 14pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 11.0pt;\'> </span><span style=\'line-height: 150%; font-family: \"Arial\",\"sans-serif\"; font-size: 14pt;\'>Rs.53,56,581/- (51,88,041/- for built up\r\nfloor + 1,68,540/- for club membership) have been paid in total. The Complainants\r\nhave also availed a loan of Rs.40 lacs from HDFC Ltd. @ 9.20% for making\r\npayments. <span style=\"mso-spacerun: yes;\">&nbsp;</span>As per the terms of agreement\r\nnotice of completion is to be given by the respondents within the period of 24\r\nmonths + 180 days (Grace Period). But till date i.e. even after the lapse of\r\nmore than five years from the date of execution of agreement, the respondents\r\nhave not delivered the possessions of built up floor. We approached respondents</span><span style=\'line-height: 150%; font-family: \"Arial\",\"sans-serif\"; font-size: 14pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 11.0pt;\'> </span><span style=\'line-height: 150%; font-family: \"Arial\",\"sans-serif\"; font-size: 14pt;\'>number of times but they kept on lingering on\r\nthe matter and also insisted the complainant to take another unit but as and\r\nwhen the complainants intends to accept their offer, then on very next meeting,\r\nthey changed their earlier proposal and offered some another proposal (emails\r\nattached). The respondents are now pressurizing the complainants to get an\r\nalternative unit which is neither agreed between the parties nor\r\nacceptable/feasible to the complainants. Legal notice dated 21.12.2018 was also\r\nserved upon the respondents through counsel, but they failed to do the needful.</span></p><p style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<br></p>','<p><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font></p><p style=\"margin: 0in 0in 10pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><font face=\"Arial\"></font><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n<br></font></p><p style=\"margin: 0in 0in 10pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\'line-height: 150%; font-family: \"Arial\",\"sans-serif\"; font-size: 14pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 11.0pt;\'>It is, therefore, respectfully prayed that the\r\nrespondents may kindly be directed to refund the amount of Rs.53,56,581/- along\r\nwith interest over and above the interest which the complainants are paying to\r\nthe HDFC Ltd. from which they have availed the loan facility for purchase the\r\nproperty, from the date of execution of the agreement till the realization of\r\nthe amount, the complainants are also entitled to get a compensation to the\r\ntune of Rs.5 Lakh on account of mental pain, agony and harassment suffered by\r\nthem as provided U/s 14 (3) and Section 19 of the said Act. </span></p><p style=\"margin: 0in 0in 10pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"></p><span style=\'line-height: 150%; font-family: \"Arial\",\"sans-serif\"; font-size: 14pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 11.0pt;\'><p style=\"margin: 0in 0in 10pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font></p><p style=\"margin: 0in 0in 10pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\'line-height: 150%; font-family: \"Arial\",\"sans-serif\"; font-size: 14pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 11.0pt;\'><span style=\"mso-tab-count: 1;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span>The strict\r\naction U/s 7 &amp; 8 is also required to be taken against the respondents for\r\nviolating the provisions of The Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development Act).</span></p><p style=\"margin: 0in 0in 10pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font></p><p style=\"margin: 0in 0in 10pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\'line-height: 150%; font-family: \"Arial\",\"sans-serif\"; font-size: 14pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 11.0pt;\'><span style=\"mso-tab-count: 2;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span>Any\r\nother relief which the complainants seems entitled to by this Hon\'ble\r\nAuthority, may also be granted to the complainants in the interest of justice\r\nand equity.<br></span></p></span><p style=\"margin: 0in 0in 10pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><br></p>',6041820.00,5356581.00,'2106-03-24 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font></p><p style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\'line-height: 150%; font-family: \"Arial\",\"sans-serif\"; font-size: 14pt;\'>The\r\nrespondents may kindly be directed to deposit at least 50% of the amount\r\nalongwith interest as interim relief as a condition precedent before filling\r\ntheir written statement/ defence. The respondents may also be restrained from changing current allotted coral floor unit X026A to any other coral floor unit during the pendency of proceedings.<br></span></p>','1','','2013-05-15 00:00:00','2013-09-25 00:00:00','X012A Coral Floors, Sidhwan Canal Road, V. Dewatwal, Ludhiana','','',1,1,0,0,'gaurav4478','2019-01-01 16:47:25.000','gaurav4478','2019-01-01 16:47:25.000'),(775,1237,'1237',1307,'8706b2af-2c26-49a1-a6e1-be61b33f0f89','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','ABHISHEK KAPOOR','advocate.abhishekkapoor@gmail.com',9876753879,0,0,'48-B','Udham Singh Nagar',28,366,'141001','1','48-B','Udham Singh Nagar',28,366,'141001','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-LDH45-PR0052','Ireo Waterfront Private Limited','IREO WATERFRONT PRIVATE LIMITED','rajiv.gupta@ireo.in',0,0,'Ireo Waterfront Private Limited','Issewal Deatwal Link Rd',28,366,'141102','1','Ireo Waterfront Private Limited','Issewal Deatwal Link Rd',28,366,'141102','0','<p><span style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: &quot;trebuchet ms&quot;, sans-serif; font-size: large;\">We have paid the full amount of Plot No. X-095 in the name of Abhishek kapoor in the month of February 2016 but still till today they are not getting the conveyance deed done neither they are responding to our e-mails. We want registry of our plot&nbsp;</span><br></p>','<p>We want our Money back amounting to Rs.21.50 Lacs paid to Ireo Waterfront Private Limted&nbsp;</p>',2109800.00,2150917.00,'2015-05-03 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>It is humbly prayed that to please help us in getting our money back or ask the Management of Ireo Waterfront Private Limited to get our conveyance deed registered as already we have suffered a pain and agony because of them .&nbsp;</p>','1','','2015-05-03 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Plot No X-095','','',2,0,0,0,'ABHISHEKKAPOOR','2019-01-01 19:45:12.000','ABHISHEKKAPOOR','2019-01-01 19:45:12.000'),(776,1237,'1237',1307,'8706b2af-2c26-49a1-a6e1-be61b33f0f89','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-01-02 10:07:21.000','ABHISHEK KAPOOR','advocate.abhishekkapoor@gmail.com',9876753879,0,0,'48-B','Udham Singh Nagar',28,366,'141001','1','48-B','Udham Singh Nagar',28,366,'141001','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-LDH45-PR0052','Ireo Waterfront Private Limited','IREO WATERFRONT PRIVATE LIMITED','rajiv.gupta@ireo.in',0,0,'Ireo Waterfront Private Limited','Issewal Deatwal Link Rd',28,366,'141102','1','Ireo Waterfront Private Limited','Issewal Deatwal Link Rd',28,366,'141102','0','<p><span style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: &quot;trebuchet ms&quot;, sans-serif; font-size: large;\">We have paid the full amount of Plot No. X-095 in the name of Abhishek kapoor in the month of February 2016 but still till today they are not getting the conveyance deed done neither they are responding to our e-mails. We want registry of our plot&nbsp;</span><br></p>','<p>We want our Money back amounting to Rs.21.50 Lacs paid to Ireo Waterfront Private Limted&nbsp;</p>',2109800.00,2150917.00,'2015-05-03 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>It is humbly prayed that to please help us in getting our money back or ask the Management of Ireo Waterfront Private Limited to get our conveyance deed registered as already we have suffered a pain and agony because of them .&nbsp;</p>','1','','2015-05-03 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Plot No X-095','','',1,1,0,0,'ABHISHEKKAPOOR','2019-01-01 19:54:14.000','ABHISHEKKAPOOR','2019-01-01 19:54:14.000'),(777,1172,'1172',1078,'d8d4f172-3c37-4e70-b72a-876b113f98f3','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-27 16:01:13.000','Avneet Kaur','vikramsinghchahal@gmail.com',9781750447,0,0,'H.No.28-B, Model Town Phagwara','Punjab',28,300,'144401','1','H.No.28-B, Model Town Phagwara','Punjab',28,300,'144401','Vikram Singh Chahal','vikramsinghchahal@gmail.com',9781750447,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0231','Mohali Hills, M/s EMAAR MGF Land  Pvt. Ltd','EMAAR MGF LAND PVT LTD','feedback@emaar-india.com',0,0,'ECE House, Level-1, 28 Kasturba  Ghandhi Marg','New Delhi  ',10,429,'110001','0','28 KASTURBA GANDHI MARG','',10,429,'110001','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:36.0pt;text-align:justify;line-height:\r\n150%\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:11.0pt;line-height:150%\">Complainant\r\nopted for the purchase of independent plot developed by the respondents and\r\nentered into an agreement dated 04.07.2007 wherein the said plot No 104 measuring\r\n400sq yards in Augusta Green in Sector 109, for the total sale price of Rs.54,00,472/-\r\nand the possession of the said plot as the agreement was to be handed over to\r\nthe complainant on or before 03.07.2010. &nbsp;The complainant made the payment of Rs.53,01,648/-\r\nas per the demand raised by the respondent. The respondent had assured as per\r\nthe agreement that the possession shall be offered on or before July 2010 but\r\nafter the elapse of approximately eight years from the said cutoff date still\r\nthere are no signs of the possession being offered. The complainant has been\r\ncheated by the respondents by not delivering the possession as per the\r\nagreement and further cancelling the allotment of the said plot without\r\ninforming the complainant without any reason. The complainant is concerned\r\nabout the fate of his investment, as such the present complainant seeking the\r\nrefund of the amount deposited by the complainant along with interest and\r\ncompensation.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p><i><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:Calibri;mso-fareast-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-bidi-theme-font:\r\nminor-bidi;mso-ansi-language:EN-US;mso-fareast-language:EN-US;mso-bidi-language:\r\nAR-SA\">Refund of the total amount after deducting Rs.37,55,255/- (the amount\r\ndirectly refunded to the respondent Bank by the respondent no 1 to 3) &nbsp;from Rs 53,01,648 along with interest.&nbsp;</span></i><br></p>',5400472.00,5301648.00,'2010-07-03 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Any relief as it deems fit to the Honorable Authority in the present facts and circumstances of the case in the interest of justice and equity.&nbsp;</p>','1','','2007-07-04 00:00:00','2007-07-04 00:00:00','Plot No 104 measuring 400sq yards in Augusta Green in Sector 109, Mohali','','',2,0,0,0,'P43982017','2019-01-02 11:43:35.000','P43982017','2019-01-02 11:43:35.000'),(778,1186,'1186',1269,'e03c7b9d-d8a0-485d-985d-807b962c7216','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-01-02 11:51:43.000','Rachna  Verma','csvedparkash@gmail.com',9815447788,0,0,'#261, Sector-8, Panchkula','',13,15,'134109','1','#261, Sector-8, Panchkula','',13,15,'134109','Ved Parkash','csvedparkash@gmail.com',7837223098,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PC0006','International Trade Tower','Omaxe Limited','customerrelations_chandigarh@omaxe.com',0,0,'#262, Sector-8, Panchkula','',13,15,'134109','1','#262, Sector-8, Panchkula','',13,15,'134109','1','<p>1. That the complainants applied for allotment of a commercial unit in International Trade Tower situated at Chandigarh promoted by M/s Omaxe in Omaxe township at Mullanpur.&nbsp;</p><p>2. That Omaxe through their Marketting Company M/s Bhanu Infratech Private Limited issued Provisional Allotment of Ommercial Unit-INTT/01/Shop/57 in the International Trade Tower on 30th&nbsp; April, 2017 , after receipt of part of booking amount of Rs.1,00,000/- including Service Tax amount. Total Booking amount payable was Rs.3,00,000/- as per the terms of Contract. Annexure 1.&nbsp;</p><p>3. The Total amount of Consideration of the allotted Commercial unit was Rs.67,46,294/-and&nbsp; All the details of booking amount paid/ payable and total consideration amount are detailed in the Demand letter dated 11.05.2017 of the respondent Company.&nbsp;</p><p>4. That the Respondent company obtained documents from the Complainants for arranging Loan from bank but later on informed that the Loan amount could not be sanctioned for the allotted Commercial Unit.&nbsp;</p><p>5. Accordingly&nbsp; the Complainants requested for refund of the amount immediately and submitted the requisite Documents for processing the refund on 13.07.2017. Annexure II.&nbsp;</p><p>6. That, instead of processing the refund, the Respondent Company sent us a reminder for payment of outstanding amount alongwith and threatened to cancel the allotment in case of Non-Payment by the Applicants on 27.09.2017. Annexure III.&nbsp;</p><p>7. That the Complainants&nbsp; keep on pursuing for refund of the amount and sent reminders of money on 10.10.2017 and 01.11.2017. Annexure IV.&nbsp;</p><p>8. That the respondent company sent a letter dated 15.01.2018 intimating the cancellation of the Allotted unit vide letter dated 06.10.2017 and amount paid has been forfieted. Annexure V&nbsp;</p><p>9. That vide email dated June 16th, 2018, the Respondent Company intimated an amount of Rs.1,40,659.16/- has been paid&nbsp; as Service Tax against the Allotted unit. Annexure VI.</p><p>8.and 9. are contradictory.allotted unit already sold as per details.</p>','<p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 0px 48px; text-indent: -18pt;\"><b style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight:normal\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"margin: 0px; line-height: 115%; font-size: 12pt;\"><span style=\"margin: 0px;\">.<span style=\"font: 7pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; margin: 0px; font-size-adjust: none; font-stretch: normal;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span></span></b><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"margin: 0px; line-height: 115%; font-size: 12pt;\">That the statements made by the\r\nRespondent Company at 8 and 9 are contradictory which shows their malafiding in\r\nnot returning the Booking Amount of the Complainant . And, the Allotted Unit\r\nhas already been sold to as per details complied by the Complainant. <b style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight:normal\"><u>Annexure VII</u></b>.<b style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight:normal\"><u></u></b></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 13.33px 48px;\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"margin: 0px; line-height: 115%; font-size: 12pt;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 13.33px 48px;\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"margin: 0px; line-height: 115%; font-size: 12pt;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 13.33px 48px;\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-bottom: 13.33px; margin-left: 48px; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; background-color: transparent;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 700;\"><u><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 16px; line-height: 18.66px; margin: 0px;\">Prayer:</span></u></span></p><p style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; background-color: transparent;\"></p><p style=\"margin-bottom: 13.33px; margin-left: 48px; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; background-color: transparent;\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 16px; line-height: 18.66px; margin: 0px;\">It is a Registered Project with RERA Registration No.-PBRERA-SAS80-PC0006</span></p><p style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; background-color: transparent;\"></p><p style=\"margin-bottom: 13.33px; margin-left: 48px; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; background-color: transparent;\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 16px; line-height: 18.66px; margin: 0px;\">Respondent Company has violated Section 18 and 19 of the Act. It is respectfully prayed that the Respondent Company may be directed to refund the amount alongwith interest as per RERA Provisions.</span></p><p style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; background-color: transparent;\"></p><p>\r\n\r\n<b></b><i></i><u></u><sub></sub><sup></sup><strike></strike><font face=\"Times New Roman\"></font></p><p style=\"margin-bottom: 13.33px; margin-left: 48px; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; background-color: transparent;\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 16px; line-height: 18.66px; margin: 0px;\">&nbsp;</span></p><div><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 16px; line-height: 18.66px; margin: 0px;\"><br></span></div>',6746294.00,100000.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p style=\"background-color: transparent; box-sizing: border-box; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: roboto; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; letter-spacing: normal; margin: 0px 0px 13.33px 48px; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; word-spacing: 0px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\"><b><u>Not Any</u></b></span></p><p><b></b><i></i><u></u><sub></sub><sup></sup><strike></strike><br></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','INTT/01/Shop/57','','',1,1,0,0,'rachnaverma1','2019-01-02 11:51:41.000','rachnaverma1','2019-01-02 11:51:41.000'),(779,1172,'1172',1078,'d8d4f172-3c37-4e70-b72a-876b113f98f3','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-01-02 12:23:41.000','Avneet Kaur','vikramsinghchahal@gmail.com',9781750447,0,0,'H.No.28-B, Model Town Phagwara','Punjab',28,300,'144401','1','H.No.28-B, Model Town Phagwara','Punjab',28,300,'144401','Vikram Singh Chahal','vikramsinghchahal@gmail.com',9781750447,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0231','Mohali Hills, M/s EMAAR MGF Land  Pvt. Ltd','EMAAR MGF LAND PVT LTD','feedback@emaar-india.com',0,0,'ECE House, Level-1, 28 Kasturba  Ghandhi Marg','New Delhi  ',10,429,'110001','0','28 KASTURBA GANDHI MARG','',10,429,'110001','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:36.0pt;text-align:justify;line-height:\r\n150%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 150%;\">Complainant\r\nopted for the purchase of independent plot developed by the respondents and\r\nentered into an agreement dated 04.07.2007 wherein the said plot No 104 measuring\r\n400sq yards in Augusta Green in Sector 109, for the total sale price of Rs.54,00,472/-\r\nand the possession of the said plot as the agreement was to be handed over to\r\nthe complainant on or before 03.07.2010. Copy of the Buyers agreements is ANNEXURE-C1.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 14px;\">The complaint\r\nhas&nbsp;availed&nbsp;loan from HDFC bank for the payment of the consideration\r\nand despite of 99% payment made by the complainant to the respondent.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">The complainant made the payment of Rs.53,01,648/-\r\nas per the demand raised by the respondent. Copy of the receipts are ANNEXURE-C2 (Colly) and the c</span>opy of the Statement of account is ANNEXURE-C3. The respondent had assured as per\r\nthe agreement that the possession shall be offered on or before July 2010 but\r\nafter the elapse of approximately eight years from the said cutoff date still\r\nthere are no signs of the possession being offered. The complainant has been\r\ncheated by the respondents by not delivering the possession as per the\r\nagreement&nbsp;<span style=\"background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial; line-height: 115%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">Respondent No. 1 to 3\r\nhad already&nbsp;cancelled the allotment and remitted the amount directly to\r\nrespondent No. 4 without any intimation to the complainant and&nbsp;here it is\r\nto be seen that for the plot/land which is not even&nbsp;in the name of the\r\nrespondent No. 1 to 3 till today how the cancellation of that plot can be there\r\nand that too without intimating the complainant.</span>&nbsp;The complainant is concerned\r\nabout the fate of his investment, as such the present complainant seeking the\r\nrefund of the amount deposited by the complainant along with interest and\r\ncompensation.</p>','<p><i><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:Calibri;mso-fareast-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-bidi-theme-font:\r\nminor-bidi;mso-ansi-language:EN-US;mso-fareast-language:EN-US;mso-bidi-language:\r\nAR-SA\">Refund of the total amount after deducting Rs.37,55,255/- (the amount\r\ndirectly refunded to the respondent Bank by the respondent no 1 to 3) &nbsp;from Rs 53,01,648 along with interest and compensation.</span></i><br></p>',5400472.00,5301648.00,'2010-07-03 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Any relief as it deems fit to the Honorable Authority in the present facts and circumstances of the case in the interest of justice and equity.&nbsp;</p>','1','','2007-07-04 00:00:00','2007-07-04 00:00:00','Plot No 104 measuring 400sq yards in Augusta Green in Sector 109, Mohali','','',1,1,0,0,'P43982017','2019-01-02 12:13:07.000','P43982017','2019-01-02 12:13:07.000'),(780,1160,'1160',1221,'371492c6-7a9d-4ed1-b340-1b73bc92dac4','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-01-02 12:51:57.000','AMRINDER KAUR','charanjitpsegs@gmail.com',9888793050,0,0,'2321 C Block 29','Housing Board Flats Sector 63',6,128,'160062','1','House No 1577','Sector 70 Mohali',28,507,'160071','CHARANJIT SINGH','charanjitcan@gmail.com',9888793050,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0367','UNIWORLD CITY MOHALI','M/S UNITECH LIMITED ','sanctions_hry@unitechgroup.com',9821227005,1244835300,'m/s unitech limited','UNITECH HOUSE, L-BLOCK, SOUTH CITY-1',13,5,'122007','1','M/S UNITECH LIMITED','UNITECH HOUSE, L-BLOCK, SOUTH CITY-1',13,5,'122007','1','<p>A.	The complainant purchased a two bedroom flat jointly with her mother in law named Kuldeep Kaur from respondent Unitech Ltd in their project Singleton Floors, Uniworld City Mohali on 26.08.09.The name of my mother in law was deleted on 26.12.11(allotment letter p11).&nbsp;<br></p><p>B.	The agreement was signed with the respondent’s Unitech Ltd. and the Alice developers private Ltd on 12.11.2009(p 12-32).\r\n</p><p>C.	 The cost of the above unit was fixed Rs 2458727/-(p 30).The complainant paid Rs 1978144/(p 36) to respondents till October 2013 on demand. \r\n</p><p>D.	The complainant never delayed the payment or breached any condition of the agreement.\r\n</p><p>E.	 The possession of the flat was to be offered within 36 months I.e is up-to 11.11.2012 by the respondents from the date of signing the agreement i.e. 12.11.2009(p 20,4 a ). However the respondents offered possession on 13.11.2018(p 34)&nbsp; &nbsp;. \r\n</p><p>F.	There is delay of 72 months in offering the possession.\r\n</p><p>G.	The respondents issued a demand notice amounting to Rs 6, 64,288/- to the claimant along with the offer of possession without adjusting the amount of compensation as per agreement(p 36). \r\n</p><p>H.	The cost of the unit was increased to the tune of Rs 93000/- on a/c of revised super area in this aforesaid demand notice(p-35). This was applicable to Uni homes Scheme not to The Singleton Scheme in the same block of units. \r\n</p><p>I.	The final demand notice include a sum of Rs 60000/- club charges whereas no such club is constructed or exists in the aforesaid project. \r\n</p><p>J.	The liability of complainant towards Service Tax/ GST increased due to non-delivery of Unit on time by the respondents(p 36).  \r\n</p><p>K.	The claimant discussed the aforesaid facts   with the representative of respondents Sh. Robin Singh (Mentioned in final notice of possession for contact) who refused to adjust any amount or compensation.\r\n</p><p>L.	The claimant is paying an installment of Rs 4600/- P.M to HDFC on a/c of availed loan as well as family is paying house rent to the tune of   Rs 13500/- P.M.\r\n</p><p><br></p>','<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;\r\nmargin-bottom:0cm;margin-left:70.9pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;mso-add-space:auto;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-indent:-18.0pt;line-height:normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin;\r\nmso-ansi-language:EN-CA\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 14px; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">1.&nbsp;</span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-ansi-language:EN-CA\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">The claimant should be given\r\npossession immediately after payment of external electrification charges and\r\nwater and sewer connection charges.</span></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;\r\nmargin-bottom:0cm;margin-left:70.9pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;mso-add-space:auto;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-indent:-18.0pt;line-height:normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span style=\"text-indent: -18pt;\">2.</span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span style=\"text-indent: -18pt;\">The claimant is filing request\r\nfor compensation in Form N separately.</span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;\r\nmargin-bottom:0cm;margin-left:70.9pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;mso-add-space:auto;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-indent:-18.0pt;line-height:normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-ansi-language:EN-CA\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">3.</span></span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-ansi-language:EN-CA\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">The false increased cost of unit to the tune\r\nof Rs 93000/- should be reduced.</span><o:p></o:p></span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">\r\n\r\n</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">\r\n\r\n</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">\r\n\r\n</span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;\r\nmargin-bottom:0cm;margin-left:70.9pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;mso-add-space:auto;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-indent:-18.0pt;line-height:normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-ansi-language:EN-CA\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">4.</span></span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-ansi-language:EN-CA\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">The club charges to the tune\r\nof Rs. 60000/- should be deducted from the final demand as the respondents have\r\nfailed to start construction of club even after a span of 10 years. The\r\nclaimant has doubt on the integrity of the respondents.</span></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;\r\nmargin-bottom:0cm;margin-left:70.9pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt;mso-add-space:auto;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-indent:-18.0pt;line-height:normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-ansi-language:EN-CA\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">5</span></span>&nbsp; &nbsp; The increased cost of GST due to delayed delivery should be paid by the respondents.</p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<span style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -24px;\">The claimant should be given possession immediately after payment of external electrification charges and water and sewer connection charges.</span>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',1,1,0,0,'lovely','2019-01-02 12:51:19.000','lovely','2019-01-02 12:51:19.000'),(781,1238,'1238',1316,'04ea4248-150e-4148-81b6-34afe1ec1b06','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Kamal Makkar','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9729902009,0,0,'424 Sector 20 Kaithal','',13,9,'136027','1','424 Sector 20 Kaithal','',13,9,'136027','Kamal Dahiya','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9729902009,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0121','Purab Premium Apartments','Greater Mohali Area Development Authority','ce@gmada.gov.in',1722215512,0,'PUDA Bhawan Sector 62 District SAS Nagar Mohali ','',28,507,'160062','1','PUDA Bhawan Sector 62 District SAS Nagar Mohali ','',28,507,'160062','1','<p>NA</p>','<p>NA</p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>NA</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'kamalmakkar1','2019-01-03 12:49:36.000','kamalmakkar1','2019-01-03 12:49:36.000'),(782,1239,'1239',1310,'a760b242-a57c-46e6-a533-2178f2bd8ffe','FormTypeM',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Rakesh Narang','advbswalia@gmail.com',9417374450,1722625384,0,'H.NO. 4/137, SHIVAJI NAGAR','',13,5,'122001','1','H.NO. 4/137, SHIVAJI NAGAR','',13,5,'122001','B. S WALIA','advbswalia@gmail.com',9417374450,1722625384,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0153','WAVES ESTATE ','Wave Estate M/s Country Colonisers Private limited','aditi@waveestate.in',0,0,'Sector 85','',28,507,'160055','1','Sector 85','',28,507,'160055','1','<p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">That the respondent issued\r\nallotment Letter of intent (LOI) to applicant for residential plot no. 63 First floor Sector 99, Mohali dated 14.1.2013 in reference to application form no. 832. That in furtherance\r\nof letter of Intent, allotment letter&nbsp;dated 9-8-2016 was issued to\r\napplicant. The tentative price of the plot is Rs. 11445000/- at the rate of Rs.\r\n21,000/- Rs/Sq. Yard. In pursuance to Allotment Letter, Applicant paid full and\r\nfinal lump sum payment of Rs.1,14,45,000/-.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:\r\njustify;line-height:200%\">\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">Thus, till date Rs.\r\n11445000/- has been paid by Applicant to the respondent as per statement of\r\naccount. As per the Allotment Letter , the possession of the said\r\nplot in question was to be given within 30 months from the date of issuance of\r\nallotment which is already over. Thus, the respondent has failed\r\nto handover possession within the stipulated time as written in the allotment\r\nletter agreed between the parties. The respondent has yet to give reply to\r\nApplicant whether they have got the Occupancy Certificate/Completion\r\nCertificate for the said plot or not? Respondent has been avoiding this\r\nquestion for too long since the Allotment letter was issued. That the said\r\nproject promoted by respondent lacks basic infrastructure like roads, poor\r\nconnectivity, drains, electricity, water supply, green cover and parks, street\r\nlights missing, roads without berm, no provision of security nor any existence\r\nof police post. All these factors further make plot unfit for habitation and\r\nconstruction.&nbsp;Applicant has given a letter on 30-11-2017 regarding\r\npossession of P</span><span style=\"font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">lot no. 63 First floor Sector 99, Mohali</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">. Even today</span><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">,&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">the development works at the said\r\n‘Gateway City’ are not complete, which means the possession of plot is no\r\nsooner expected than 2019 from respondent. Thus, there is a clear delay on the\r\npart of respondent.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:7.5pt;text-align:justify;line-height:\r\n21.0pt\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif;\">In view of the facts mentioned in paragraph 4 above, the\r\napplicant&nbsp;prays for the following compensation(s): -</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: Roboto;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:7.5pt;text-align:justify;line-height:\r\n21.0pt\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif;\">1.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; letter-spacing: 1pt;\">Grant\r\npay 18% interest on the deposited amount of Rs.</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: Roboto;\">&nbsp;11445000</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; letter-spacing: 1pt;\">/-&nbsp;from date of possession.</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: Roboto;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:7.5pt;text-align:justify;line-height:\r\n21.0pt\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:7.5pt;text-align:justify;line-height:\r\n21.0pt\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif;\">2. Any other appropriate remedy or relief which this court may\r\ndeem fit in the present circumstances may also be awarded in the favour of\r\nApplicant.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: Roboto;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>',11445000.00,11445000.00,'2015-07-14 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 7.5pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 21pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif;\">In view of the facts mentioned in paragraph 4 above, the applicant&nbsp;prays for the following compensation(s): -</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: Roboto;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 7.5pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 21pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif;\">1.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; letter-spacing: 1pt;\">Grant pay 18% interest on the deposited amount of Rs.</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: Roboto;\">&nbsp;11445000</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; letter-spacing: 1pt;\">/-&nbsp;from date of possession.</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: Roboto;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 7.5pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 21pt;\"></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 7.5pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 21pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif;\">2. Any other appropriate remedy or relief which this court may deem fit in the present circumstances may also be awarded in the favour of Applicant.&nbsp;</span></p>','1','','2013-01-14 00:00:00','2013-06-06 00:00:00','63 FIRST FLOOR','','',2,0,0,0,'bhupinderwalia','2019-01-03 20:31:48.000','bhupinderwalia','2019-01-03 20:31:48.000'),(783,1239,'1239',1310,'a760b242-a57c-46e6-a533-2178f2bd8ffe','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-01-04 11:49:46.000','Rakesh Narang','advbswalia@gmail.com',9417374450,1722625384,0,'H.NO. 4/137, SHIVAJI NAGAR','',13,5,'122001','1','H.NO. 4/137, SHIVAJI NAGAR','',13,5,'122001','B. S WALIA','advbswalia@gmail.com',9417374450,1722625384,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0153','WAVES ESTATE ','Wave Estate M/s Country Colonisers Private limited','aditi@waveestate.in',0,0,'Sector 85','',28,507,'160055','1','Sector 85','',28,507,'160055','1','<p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">That the respondent issued\r\nallotment Letter of intent (LOI) to applicant for residential plot no. 63 First floor Sector 99, Mohali dated 14.1.2013 in reference to application form no. 832. That in furtherance\r\nof letter of Intent, allotment letter&nbsp;dated 9-8-2016 was issued to\r\napplicant. The tentative price of the plot is Rs. 11445000/- at the rate of Rs.\r\n21,000/- Rs/Sq. Yard. In pursuance to Allotment Letter, Applicant paid full and\r\nfinal lump sum payment of Rs.1,14,45,000/-.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:\r\njustify;line-height:200%\">\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">Thus, till date Rs.\r\n11445000/- has been paid by Applicant to the respondent as per statement of\r\naccount. As per the Allotment Letter , the possession of the said\r\nplot in question was to be given within 30 months from the date of issuance of\r\nallotment which is already over. Thus, the respondent has failed\r\nto handover possession within the stipulated time as written in the allotment\r\nletter agreed between the parties. The respondent has yet to give reply to\r\nApplicant whether they have got the Occupancy Certificate/Completion\r\nCertificate for the said plot or not? Respondent has been avoiding this\r\nquestion for too long since the Allotment letter was issued. That the said\r\nproject promoted by respondent lacks basic infrastructure like roads, poor\r\nconnectivity, drains, electricity, water supply, green cover and parks, street\r\nlights missing, roads without berm, no provision of security nor any existence\r\nof police post. All these factors further make plot unfit for habitation and\r\nconstruction.&nbsp;Applicant has given a letter on 30-11-2017 regarding\r\npossession of P</span><span style=\"font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">lot no. 63 First floor Sector 99, Mohali</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">. Even today</span><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">,&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">the development works at the said\r\n‘Gateway City’ are not complete, which means the possession of plot is no\r\nsooner expected than 2019 from respondent. Thus, there is a clear delay on the\r\npart of respondent.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:7.5pt;text-align:justify;line-height:\r\n21.0pt\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif;\">In view of the facts mentioned in paragraph 4 above, the\r\napplicant&nbsp;prays for the following compensation(s): -</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: Roboto;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:7.5pt;text-align:justify;line-height:\r\n21.0pt\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif;\">1.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; letter-spacing: 1pt;\">Grant\r\npay 18% interest on the deposited amount of Rs.</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: Roboto;\">&nbsp;11445000</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; letter-spacing: 1pt;\">/-&nbsp;from date of possession.</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: Roboto;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:7.5pt;text-align:justify;line-height:\r\n21.0pt\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:7.5pt;text-align:justify;line-height:\r\n21.0pt\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif;\">2. Any other appropriate remedy or relief which this court may\r\ndeem fit in the present circumstances may also be awarded in the favour of\r\nApplicant.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: Roboto;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>',11445000.00,11445000.00,'2015-07-14 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 7.5pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 21pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif;\">In view of the facts mentioned in paragraph 4 above, the applicant&nbsp;prays for the following compensation(s): -</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: Roboto;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 7.5pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 21pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif;\">1.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; letter-spacing: 1pt;\">Grant pay 18% interest on the deposited amount of Rs.</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: Roboto;\">&nbsp;11445000</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; letter-spacing: 1pt;\">/-&nbsp;from date of possession.</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: Roboto;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 7.5pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 21pt;\"></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 7.5pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 21pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif;\">2. Any other appropriate remedy or relief which this court may deem fit in the present circumstances may also be awarded in the favour of Applicant.&nbsp;</span></p>','1','','2013-01-14 00:00:00','2013-06-06 00:00:00','63 FIRST FLOOR','','',2,0,0,0,'bhupinderwalia','2019-01-03 22:54:39.000','bhupinderwalia','2019-01-03 22:54:39.000'),(784,1238,'1238',1316,'04ea4248-150e-4148-81b6-34afe1ec1b06','FormTypeM',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Kamal Makkar','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9729902009,0,358412254419,'424 Sector 20 Kaithal','',13,9,'136027','1','424 Sector 20 Kaithal','',13,9,'136027','Kamal Dahiya','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9729902009,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0121','Purab Premium Apartments','Greater Mohali Area Development Authority','ce@gmada.gov.in',1722215512,0,'PUDA Bhawan Sector 62 District SAS Nagar Mohali ','',28,507,'160062','1','PUDA Bhawan Sector 62 District SAS Nagar Mohali ','',28,507,'160062','1','<p>Respondent opened scheme for public from 12.12.2011 to 12.01.2012 asAnnexureC-1. The depicted salient features asAnnexureC-2. Respondent informed vide letter dated 23.03.2012 that the waiting list no. is 65 and complainant to submit the documents before 23/04/2012AnnexureC-3. Letter of intent for allotment was issued on 21.05.2012 and tentative price was Rs 55,00,000. As per Para 3(II) delivery within a period of 36 months from the date of issuance of the said letter. Possession date was 21.05.2015 i.e. delayed by 3 years and 7 monthsAnnexureC-4. Payment plan B was opted by the complainantAnnexureC-4(Pg 40). Initial amount of INR 11,00,000 paid vide cheque on 16.06.2012AnnexureC-5(Pg41). Total amount paid Rs54, 25,746/- i.e. 98% out of the total consideration till 21.04.2016 AnnexureC-5. After 5 years the complainant was allotted with apartment no.1502, Tower-5, BlockD, Floor14 with 2563.19 sq. ft. area including common stairs and car parking area on 11.10.2017 and the possession was also offeredAnnexureC-6. Thereafter the complainant visited site and found that layout plan has changed without taking the consent of 2/3rd allottees and also found many loopholes in the construction like compromised quality of materials etc. The complainant got the construction inspected by Registered Council of Architecture, New Delhi. Many differences were found as inAnnexureC-7. The complainant intimated such defects to the Estate Officer of GMADA vide letter dated 17.05.2018 and requested for refund of his paid amount but respondent didn’t respondAnnexureC-8. Other allottees also found several defects, deficiencies and deviations in the projectAnnexureC-9(Pg93). Several allottees raised the issues before the press conference(Pg 94-95). The government ordered to remove the defaults but respondent did not comply to repair the faults(Pg 96-97). Fire safety has been expired(Pg 98-99). The lifts are also not safe and stops to work. Many times someone stops in the elevator(Pg 100-102).</p>','<p>In view of the facts mentioned in preceding paragraphs, the complainant prays for the following relief(s):-&nbsp;</p><p>i.To give necessary directions to the respondents for refund the amount paid by the complainant with prescribed interest till realization as per the provisions of Sec. 18 and Sec.19(4)of the RERA Act read with Rule 16 of PSRE(R&amp;D)Rules, 2017.</p><p>ii.To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 60 of RERA Act for willful default committed by them.</p><p>iii.To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 61 of RERA Act for contravention of Sec.12, Sec.14, and Sec. 16 of RERA Act.</p><p>iv.To issue directions to make liable every officer concerned i.e. Director, Manager, Secretary, or any other officer of the respondent’s company at whose instance, connivance, acquiescence, neglect any of the offences has been committed as mentioned in Sec.69 of RERA Act,2016 to be read with Punjab RERA Rules,2017.</p><p>v.To recommend criminal action against the respondents for the criminal offence of cheating, fraud and criminal breach of trust under section 420,406 and 409 of the Indian Penal Code.</p><p>vi.To issue direction to pay the cost of litigation.</p><p>vii.To issue direction to pay the compensation to complainant for compensation for his mental agony, pain and harassment.</p><p>viii.Any other relief which this Hon’ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances of this complaint.</p><div><br></div>',55000.00,5425746.00,'2015-05-21 00:00:00.000','2015-05-21 00:00:00.000','<p>i.To direct the respondent not to demand any further amount whatsoever from the complainant.</p><p>ii.The respondent should be restrained from harassing the complainant in any manner whatsoever.</p><p>iii.Any other interim relief which this Hon’ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances of this complaint.</p><div><br></div>','1','','2017-10-11 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Apartment No 1502 Tower 5 Block D Floor 14 Type 2 Sector 88 Sahibzada Ajit Singh Nagar Punjab 140308','','',2,0,0,0,'kamalmakkar1','2019-01-04 16:23:53.000','kamalmakkar1','2019-01-04 16:23:53.000'),(785,1240,'1240',1317,'d8f8d4fc-24ac-4faa-a9b2-b5ad58a5817a','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Bharat Bhushan Makkar','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9729902009,0,934955777170,'108 Sector 20 Kaithal','',13,9,'136027','1','108 Sector 20 Kaithal','',13,9,'136027','Kamal Dahiya','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9729902009,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0121','Purab Premium Apartments','Greater Mohali Area Development Authority','ce@gmada.gov.in',1722215512,0,'PUDA Bhawan Sector 62 District SAS Nagar Mohali','',28,507,'160062','1','PUDA Bhawan Sector 62 District SAS Nagar Mohali','',28,507,'160062','1','<p>Respondent opened scheme for public from 12.12.2011 to 12.01.2012 asAnnexureC-1. The depicted salient features asAnnexureC-2. Respondent informed vide letter dated 23.03.2012 for the waiting list and complainant to submit the documents before 23/04/2012AnnexureC-3. Letter of intent for allotment was issued on 23.05.2012 and tentative price was Rs 69,00,000 and the flat was allotted with Flat No. 901 in Tower 3, Block E at Type 3 Apartment. As per Para 3(II) delivery within a period of 36 months from the date of issuance of the said letter. Possession date was 23.05.2015 i.e. delayed by 3 years and 7 monthsAnnexureC-4. Payment plan B was opted by the complainantAnnexureC-4(Pg 40). Initial amount of INR 13,80,000 paid vide cheque on 19.06.2012AnnexureC-5(Pg41). Total amount paid Rs68,06,850/- i.e. 99% out of the total considerationAnnexureC-5. Respondent offered the possession vide letter on 10.10.2017. Thereafter the complainant visited site and found that layout plan has changed without taking the consent of 2/3rd allottees and also found many loopholes in the construction like compromised quality of materials etc.Photographs are annexed asAnnexure C-6. The complainant got the construction inspected by Registered Council of Architecture, New Delhi. Many differences were found as inAnnexureC-7. The complainant intimated such defects to the Estate Officer of GMADA vide letter dated 17.05.2018 and requested for refund of his paid amount but respondent didn’t respondAnnexureC-8. Other allottees also found several defects, deficiencies and deviations in the projectAnnexureC-9(Pg104). Several allottees raised the issues before the press conference(Pg 105-106). The government ordered to remove the defaults but respondent did not comply to repair the faults(Pg 107-108). Fire safety has been expired(Pg 109-110). The lifts are also not safe and stops to work. Many times someone stops in the elevator(Pg 111-113).&nbsp;</p><p><br></p>','<p>In view of the facts mentioned in preceding paragraphs, the complainant prays for the following relief(s):-&nbsp;</p><p>i.To give necessary directions to the respondents for refund the amount paid by the complainant with prescribed interest till realization as per the provisions of Sec. 18 and Sec.19(4)of the RERA Act read with Rule 16 of PSRE(R&amp;D)Rules,2017.</p><p>ii.To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 60 of RERA Act for willful default committed by them.</p><p>iii.To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 61 of RERA Act for contravention of Sec.12, Sec.14, and Sec. 16 of RERA Act.</p><p>iv.To issue directions to make liable every officer concerned i.e. Director, Manager, Secretary, or any other officer of the respondent’s company at whose instance, connivance, acquiescence, neglect any of the offences has been committed as mentioned in Sec.69 of RERA Act,2016 to be read with Punjab RERA Rules, 2017.</p><p>v.To recommend criminal action against the respondents for the criminal offence of cheating, fraud and criminal breach of trust under section 420,406 and 409 of the Indian Penal Code.</p><p>vi.To issue direction to pay the cost of litigation.</p><p>vii.To issue direction to pay the compensation to complainant for compensation for his mental agony, pain and harassment.</p><p>viii.Any other relief which this Hon’ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances of this complaint.</p><div><br></div>',69000.00,6806850.00,'2015-05-23 00:00:00.000','2015-05-23 00:00:00.000','<p>i.To direct the respondent not to demand any further amount whatsoever from the complainant.</p><p>ii.The respondent should be restrained from harassing the complainant in any manner whatsoever.</p><p>iii.Any other interim relief which this Hon’ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances of this complaint.</p><div><br></div>','1','','2012-05-23 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Flat No 901 Tower 3 Block E Type 3 Sector 88 Sahibzada Ajit Singh Nagar Punjab 140308','','',2,0,0,0,'Bharatbhushanmakkar','2019-01-04 18:03:53.000','Bharatbhushanmakkar','2019-01-04 18:03:53.000'),(786,1189,'1189',1247,'79ebe07e-2dcd-4db9-b9bf-d83f90187768','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Dhiraj Gurvinder Singh','gurdhiraj@yahoo.co.in',9855578712,0,0,'house no 1083','Phase 9',28,507,'160062','1','house no 1083','Phase 9',28,507,'160062','Amit Sharma','amit@lawyer.com',9878222444,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0086','ATS Casa Espana ','ATS Infrabuild Private Limited','pradeep.rathee@atsgreens.com',0,0,'ATS Casa Espana Street, sector 121','NH 21',28,507,'160055','1','ATS Casa Espana Street, sector 121','NH 21',28,507,'160055','1','<p>1.That the Respondents in the first instance, had launched a Group Housing Project in Mohali, Sector 121, Punjab, under the name and style of “ATS Casa Espana”.&nbsp; The complainant booked an apartment on 28.02.2014.&nbsp; In the interregnum, the Respondents had issued an Allotment Letter dated 20-06-2014 confirming the allotment of a Residential apartment No. 09062, on 6th floor of tower no.9 having super built up area of 222.97 sq.mtr equivalent to 2400 sq.feet, at sector 121 Mohali, Punjab(hereinafter referred to as the “Allotted Unit”).&nbsp; As per the recitals of the aforesaid agreement, the total sale consideration of the Allotted Unit was fixed at Rs. 99,50,000/- which is as per ‘schedule III’ of allotment letter. Allotment Letter dated 20-06-2014 issued by the Respondents is annexed as ANNEXURE C/1 and account statement reflecting the amount of apartment paid is annexed as ANNEXURE C/2</p><p>2.That to the surprise of the complainant, the respondents had issued a demand letter demanding EDC charges dated 07.08.2018 to the tune of 487476/- and now demanding more than 5 lakhs vide subsequent demand letters with interest. It is pertinent to mention here that the EDC charges were promised to be paid by the respondents including change in EDC charges (if any) as already included in the total sale consideration i.e 99,50,000/- and hence, they were specifically deleted from the SCHEDULE III of the Allotment Letter Dated 20.06.2014, so that there is no confusion afterwards. Schedule III is appended with the allotment letter annexed as ANNEXURE C/1 and demand letters are annexed as ANNEXURE C/3.&nbsp;</p><p>3. That even as per the recitals of the allotment letter Annexure C/1, clause 4.1 \"The entire consideration payable by the buyer, towards the absolute purchase of the apartment along with exclusive right to use and occupy the car park space in terms of this agreement, shall be the \'Total Amount Payable\' as mentioned in Schedule III thereto.\' Hence demands for EDC again is illegal as unlawful.</p><p><br></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\">﻿﻿<span style=\"font-family:&quot;roboto&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">That in view of the\r\nfacts and circumstances of the case detailed hereinabove, the Respondent on account\r\nof &nbsp;being deficient in rendering services\r\nto the Complainant and by virtue of having adopting unfair trade practices and\r\nas such, this Hon’ble Authority may be pleased to allow the above mentioned\r\ncomplaint as under:- <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;roboto&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">1.To restrain the\r\nRespondent from demanding the EDC Charges which has already been paid by the\r\nComplainant.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;roboto&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">2.To order the\r\nRespondent from raising any other arbitrary demands and charges which the\r\nComplainant has already paid.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;roboto&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">It is, therefore,\r\nrespectfully prayed that in the light of the facts and circumstances detailed\r\nhereinabove, the instant complaint may kindly be allowed and the relief, as\r\nprayed for in the forgoing paragraph of the instant complaint, may kindly be\r\nawarded in favor of the Complainant and against the Respondent in the interests\r\nof justice, equity and good conscience.</span></p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Notice of motion be issued to the Respondents and stay in favour of the Complainant against the respondent for EDC charges Demands because an interest on the EDC charges are being added in the demand of EDC charges.<br></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'amit.heman@gmail.com','2019-01-04 18:05:27.000','amit.heman@gmail.com','2019-01-04 18:05:27.000'),(787,1189,'1189',1247,'79ebe07e-2dcd-4db9-b9bf-d83f90187768','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Dhiraj Gurvinder Singh','gurdhiraj@yahoo.co.in',9855578712,0,0,'house no 1083','Phase 9',28,507,'160062','1','house no 1083','Phase 9',28,507,'160062','Amit Sharma','amit@lawyer.com',9878222444,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0086','ATS Casa Espana ','ATS Infrabuild Private Limited','pradeep.rathee@atsgreens.com',0,0,'ATS Casa Espana Street, sector 121','NH 21',28,507,'160055','1','ATS Casa Espana Street, sector 121','NH 21',28,507,'160055','1','<p>1.That the Respondents in the first instance, had launched a Group Housing Project in Mohali, Sector 121, Punjab, under the name and style of “ATS Casa Espana”.&nbsp; The complainant booked an apartment on 28.02.2014.&nbsp; In the interregnum, the Respondents had issued an Allotment Letter dated 20-06-2014 confirming the allotment of a Residential apartment No. 09062, on 6th floor of tower no.9 having super built up area of 222.97 sq.mtr equivalent to 2400 sq.feet, at sector 121 Mohali, Punjab(hereinafter referred to as the “Allotted Unit”).&nbsp; As per the recitals of the aforesaid agreement, the total sale consideration of the Allotted Unit was fixed at Rs. 99,50,000/- which is as per ‘schedule III’ of allotment letter. Allotment Letter dated 20-06-2014 issued by the Respondents is annexed as ANNEXURE C/1 and account statement reflecting the amount of apartment paid is annexed as ANNEXURE C/2</p><p>2.That to the surprise of the complainant, the respondents had issued a demand letter demanding EDC charges dated 07.08.2018 to the tune of 487476/- and now demanding more than 5 lakhs vide subsequent demand letters with interest. It is pertinent to mention here that the EDC charges were promised to be paid by the respondents including change in EDC charges (if any) as already included in the total sale consideration i.e 99,50,000/- and hence, they were specifically deleted from the SCHEDULE III of the Allotment Letter Dated 20.06.2014, so that there is no confusion afterwards. Schedule III is appended with the allotment letter annexed as ANNEXURE C/1 and demand letters are annexed as ANNEXURE C/3.&nbsp;</p><p>3. That even as per the recitals of the allotment letter Annexure C/1, clause 4.1 \"The entire consideration payable by the buyer, towards the absolute purchase of the apartment along with exclusive right to use and occupy the car park space in terms of this agreement, shall be the \'Total Amount Payable\' as mentioned in Schedule III thereto.\' Hence demands for EDC again is illegal as unlawful.</p><p><br></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\">﻿﻿<span style=\"font-family:&quot;roboto&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">That in view of the\r\nfacts and circumstances of the case detailed hereinabove, the Respondent on account\r\nof &nbsp;being deficient in rendering services\r\nto the Complainant and by virtue of having adopting unfair trade practices and\r\nas such, this Hon’ble Authority may be pleased to allow the above mentioned\r\ncomplaint as under:- <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;roboto&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">1.To restrain the\r\nRespondent from demanding the EDC Charges which has already been paid by the\r\nComplainant.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;roboto&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">2.To order the\r\nRespondent from raising any other arbitrary demands and charges which the\r\nComplainant has already paid.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;roboto&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">It is, therefore,\r\nrespectfully prayed that in the light of the facts and circumstances detailed\r\nhereinabove, the instant complaint may kindly be allowed and the relief, as\r\nprayed for in the forgoing paragraph of the instant complaint, may kindly be\r\nawarded in favor of the Complainant and against the Respondent in the interests\r\nof justice, equity and good conscience.</span></p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Notice of motion be issued to the Respondents and stay in favour of the Complainant against the respondent for EDC charges Demands because an interest on the EDC charges are being added in the demand of EDC charges.<br></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'amit.heman@gmail.com','2019-01-04 18:19:43.000','amit.heman@gmail.com','2019-01-04 18:19:43.000'),(788,1189,'1189',1247,'79ebe07e-2dcd-4db9-b9bf-d83f90187768','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-01-04 19:02:59.000','Dhiraj Gurvinder Singh','gurdhiraj@yahoo.co.in',9855578712,0,0,'house no 1083','Phase 9',28,507,'160062','1','house no 1083','Phase 9',28,507,'160062','Amit Sharma','amit@lawyer.com',9878222444,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0086','ATS Casa Espana ','ATS Infrabuild Private Limited','pradeep.rathee@atsgreens.com',0,0,'ATS Casa Espana Street, sector 121','NH 21',28,507,'160055','1','ATS Casa Espana Street, sector 121','NH 21',28,507,'160055','1','<p>1.That the Respondents in the first instance, had launched a Group Housing Project in Mohali, Sector 121, Punjab, under the name and style of “ATS Casa Espana”.&nbsp; The complainant booked an apartment on 28.02.2014.&nbsp; In the interregnum, the Respondents had issued an Allotment Letter dated 20-06-2014 confirming the allotment of a Residential apartment No. 09062, on 6th floor of tower no.9 having super built up area of 222.97 sq.mtr equivalent to 2400 sq.feet, at sector 121 Mohali, Punjab(hereinafter referred to as the “Allotted Unit”).&nbsp; As per the recitals of the aforesaid agreement, the total sale consideration of the Allotted Unit was fixed at Rs. 99,50,000/- which is as per ‘schedule III’ of allotment letter. Allotment Letter dated 20-06-2014 issued by the Respondents is annexed as ANNEXURE C/1 and account statement reflecting the amount of apartment paid is annexed as ANNEXURE C/2</p><p>2.That to the surprise of the complainant, the respondents had issued a demand letter demanding EDC charges dated 07.08.2018 to the tune of 487476/- and now demanding more than 5 lakhs vide subsequent demand letters with interest. It is pertinent to mention here that the EDC charges were promised to be paid by the respondents including change in EDC charges (if any) as already included in the total sale consideration i.e 99,50,000/- and hence, they were specifically deleted from the SCHEDULE III of the Allotment Letter Dated 20.06.2014, so that there is no confusion afterwards. Schedule III is appended with the allotment letter annexed as ANNEXURE C/1 and demand letters are annexed as ANNEXURE C/3.&nbsp;</p><p>3. That even as per the recitals of the allotment letter Annexure C/1, clause 4.1 \"The entire consideration payable by the buyer, towards the absolute purchase of the apartment along with exclusive right to use and occupy the car park space in terms of this agreement, shall be the \'Total Amount Payable\' as mentioned in Schedule III thereto.\' Hence demands for EDC again is illegal as unlawful.</p><p><br></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\">﻿﻿<span style=\"font-family:&quot;roboto&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">That in view of the\r\nfacts and circumstances of the case detailed hereinabove, the Respondent on account\r\nof &nbsp;being deficient in rendering services\r\nto the Complainant and by virtue of having adopting unfair trade practices and\r\nas such, this Hon’ble Authority may be pleased to allow the above mentioned\r\ncomplaint as under:- <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;roboto&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">1.To restrain the\r\nRespondent from demanding the EDC Charges which has already been paid by the\r\nComplainant.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;roboto&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">2.To order the\r\nRespondent from raising any other arbitrary demands and charges which the\r\nComplainant has already paid.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;roboto&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">It is, therefore,\r\nrespectfully prayed that in the light of the facts and circumstances detailed\r\nhereinabove, the instant complaint may kindly be allowed and the relief, as\r\nprayed for in the forgoing paragraph of the instant complaint, may kindly be\r\nawarded in favor of the Complainant and against the Respondent in the interests\r\nof justice, equity and good conscience.</span></p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Notice of motion be issued to the Respondents and stay in favour of the Complainant against the respondent for EDC charges Demands because an interest on the EDC charges are being added in the demand of EDC charges.<br></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',1,1,0,0,'amit.heman@gmail.com','2019-01-04 18:23:27.000','amit.heman@gmail.com','2019-01-04 18:23:27.000'),(789,1241,'1241',1141,'971b1ae7-f8bc-4323-80a7-088b81f8b7db','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Navdeep Singh Anand','navee.anand@gmail.com',9814611997,0,0,'19-D, Rajguru Nagar','Ludhiana',28,366,'141002','1','253, Sector 4, MDC','Mansa Devi Complex',13,15,'134114','Sanjeev Gupta','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-LDH45-PR0041','Ireo Waterfront','M/s Ireo Waterfront Pvt. Ltd','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',0,0,'Sidhwan Canal Road',' Opp. Ferozepur Road, ',28,366,'141002','1','Sidhwan Canal Road',' Opp. Ferozepur Road, ',28,366,'141002','1','<p>ABC</p>','<p>ABC</p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>ABC</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'rerafilingformm','2019-01-05 15:34:37.000','rerafilingformm','2019-01-05 15:34:37.000'),(790,1241,'1241',1141,'971b1ae7-f8bc-4323-80a7-088b81f8b7db','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Navdeep Singh Anand','navee.anand@gmail.com',9814611997,0,0,'19-D, Rajguru Nagar','Ludhiana',28,366,'141002','1','253, Sector 4, MDC','Mansa Devi Complex',13,15,'134114','Sanjeev Gupta','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-LDH45-PR0041','Ireo Waterfront','M/s Ireo Waterfront Pvt. Ltd','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',0,0,'Sidhwan Canal Road, Opp. Ferozepur Road, ','Village Dewatwal',28,366,'141002','1','Sidhwan Canal Road, Opp. Ferozepur Road, ','Village Dewatwal',28,366,'141002','1','<p>ABC</p>','<p>ABC</p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>ABC</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'rerafilingformm','2019-01-05 15:35:54.000','rerafilingformm','2019-01-05 15:35:54.000'),(791,1241,'1241',1141,'971b1ae7-f8bc-4323-80a7-088b81f8b7db','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Navdeep Singh Anand','navee.anand@gmail.com',9814611997,0,0,'19-D, Rajguru Nagar','Ludhiana',28,366,'141002','1','253, Sector 4, MDC','Mansa Devi Complex',13,15,'134114','Sanjeev Gupta','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-LDH45-PR0041','Ireo Waterfront','M/s Ireo Waterfront Pvt. Ltd','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',0,0,'Sidhwan Canal Road, Opp. Ferozepur Road, ','Village Dewatwal',28,366,'141002','1','Sidhwan Canal Road, Opp. Ferozepur Road, ','Village Dewatwal',28,366,'141002','1','<p>ABC</p>','<p>ABC</p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>ABC</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'rerafilingformm','2019-01-05 15:38:45.000','rerafilingformm','2019-01-05 15:38:45.000'),(792,1241,'1241',1141,'971b1ae7-f8bc-4323-80a7-088b81f8b7db','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Navdeep Singh Anand','navee.anand@gmail.com',9814611997,0,0,'19-D, Rajguru Nagar','Ludhiana',28,366,'141002','1','253, Sector 4, MDC','Mansa Devi Complex',13,15,'134114','Sanjeev Gupta','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-LDH45-PR0041','Ireo Waterfront','M/s Ireo Waterfront Pvt. Ltd','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',0,0,'Sidhwan Canal Road, Opp. Ferozepur Road, ','Village Dewatwal',28,366,'141002','1','Sidhwan Canal Road, Opp. Ferozepur Road, ','Village Dewatwal',28,366,'141002','1','<p>On 22.9.15, Complainants booked (C-1) a built-up villa, being Type B2, Unit No 104 having 2844 sq ft of built area, to be constructed on 287.04 sq yd plot. Allotment letter was issued to them (C-2). Complainants opted for development linked plan. Total sale consideration including all charges &amp; taxes was fixed as Rs.17000222. Buyer agreement (C-3) was executed on 26.11.15.As per clause 11.3, respondent was bound to handover the possession within 18 months+180 days (grace period) from the date of execution of agreement. Said period has already expired on 25.11.17.The respondent has only completed the plinth level. There is no default on the part of complainants in making the payments. The payments which were due on 28.9.15, 28.10.15 &amp; 27.12.15 were paid by complainants on 22.9.15, 26.11.15 &amp; 18.5.16 respectively. There was no delay attributed to the complainants and thus, no delayed interest was demanded from the complainants since they were not at fault. A communication in this regard is attached as C-4.Thereafter vide demand letter             (C-5) dt 3.9.17, a sum of Rs. 1859828 was demanded, which was duly paid on 30.10.17 &amp; 5.11.17, under protest, since there was dispute about charging of GST &amp; also vide letter dt 9.10.17 &amp; 30.10.17 (C-6 &amp; C-7), it was duly conveyed to respondents but respondent did not send any reply. A sum of Rs. 6001038.30 (receipts &amp; documents C-8) has already been paid by the complainants. The next installment was due on the casting of GF roof slab which has not been done &amp; consequently there has been no demand raised by the respondent. Respondent has also stopped the development work at the site. A letter was also sent to respondent in this regard on 14.12.18 (C-9) &amp; 16.12.18 (C-10) but no reply has been received. Since there has been delay in construction &amp; the respondent was bound to deliver the possession by 25.11.2017, the complainants wishes to withdraw &amp; thus are seeking refund of the amount paid by them along with interest &amp; compensation</p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;line-height:\r\nnormal;mso-layout-grid-align:none;text-autospace:none\"><span style=\"font-family:\r\n&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Relying upon the provision of section 18 RERA, directing the respondent to refund the principle amount\r\ni.e. Rs. 6001038.30 along with interest as&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">contemplated under rule 16 of The Punjab RERA Rules,\r\n2017, as the complainants wishes to withdraw from the project, since the respondent was bound to deliver the possession of the built up villa by 25.11.2017. The respondent has indulged into unfair trade practices by not delivering the possession till date, not doing any development on the project and further it has stopped the development works on the project site and the respondent did not even send any reply to the letters sent by the complainants</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;line-height:\r\nnormal;mso-layout-grid-align:none;text-autospace:none\"><br></p>',17000222.00,6001038.30,'2017-11-25 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>ABC</p>','1','','2015-10-07 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Unit No. 104, Type-B2 Built up villa ','','',2,0,0,0,'rerafilingformm','2019-01-05 16:32:26.000','rerafilingformm','2019-01-05 16:32:26.000'),(793,1241,'1241',1141,'971b1ae7-f8bc-4323-80a7-088b81f8b7db','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Navdeep Singh Anand','navee.anand@gmail.com',9814611997,0,0,'19-D, Rajguru Nagar','Ludhiana',28,366,'141002','1','253, Sector 4, MDC','Mansa Devi Complex',13,15,'134114','Sanjeev Gupta','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-LDH45-PR0041','Ireo Waterfront','M/s Ireo Waterfront Pvt. Ltd','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',0,0,'Sidhwan Canal Road, Opp. Ferozepur Road, ','Village Dewatwal',28,366,'141002','1','Sidhwan Canal Road, Opp. Ferozepur Road, ','Village Dewatwal',28,366,'141002','1','<p>On 22.9.15, Complainants booked (C-1) a built-up villa, being Type B2, Unit No 104 having 2844 sq ft of built area, to be constructed on 287.04 sq yd plot. Allotment letter was issued to them (C-2). Complainants opted for development linked plan. Total sale consideration including all charges &amp; taxes was fixed as Rs.17000222. Buyer agreement (C-3) was executed on 26.11.15.As per clause 11.3, respondent was bound to handover the possession within 18 months+180 days (grace period) from the date of execution of agreement. Said period has already expired on 25.11.17.The respondent has only completed the plinth level. There is no default on the part of complainants in making the payments. The payments which were due on 28.9.15, 28.10.15 &amp; 27.12.15 were paid by complainants on 22.9.15, 26.11.15 &amp; 18.5.16 respectively. There was no delay attributed to the complainants and thus, no delayed interest was demanded from the complainants since they were not at fault. A communication in this regard is attached as C-4.Thereafter vide demand letter             (C-5) dt 3.9.17, a sum of Rs. 1859828 was demanded, which was duly paid on 30.10.17 &amp; 5.11.17, under protest, since there was dispute about charging of GST &amp; also vide letter dt 9.10.17 &amp; 30.10.17 (C-6 &amp; C-7), it was duly conveyed to respondents but respondent did not send any reply. A sum of Rs. 6001038.30 (receipts &amp; documents C-8) has already been paid by the complainants. The next installment was due on the casting of GF roof slab which has not been done &amp; consequently there has been no demand raised by the respondent. Respondent has also stopped the development work at the site. A letter was also sent to respondent in this regard on 14.12.18 (C-9) &amp; 16.12.18 (C-10) but no reply has been received. Since there has been delay in construction &amp; the respondent was bound to deliver the possession by 25.11.2017, the complainants wishes to withdraw &amp; thus are seeking refund of the amount paid by them along with interest &amp; compensation</p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;line-height:\r\nnormal;mso-layout-grid-align:none;text-autospace:none\"><span style=\"font-family:\r\n&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Relying upon the provision of section 18 RERA, directing the respondent to refund the principle amount\r\ni.e. Rs. 6001038.30 along with interest as&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">contemplated under rule 16 of The Punjab RERA Rules,\r\n2017, as the complainants wishes to withdraw from the project, since the respondent was bound to deliver the possession of the built up villa by 25.11.2017. The respondent has indulged into unfair trade practices by not delivering the possession till date, not doing any development on the project and further it has stopped the development works on the project site and the respondent did not even send any reply to the letters sent by the complainants. The respondent have failed to intimate any reason for the delay in development</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;line-height:\r\nnormal;mso-layout-grid-align:none;text-autospace:none\"><br></p>',17000222.00,6001038.30,'2017-11-25 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>To direct the respondent to refund the principal amount of Rs. 6001038.30.</p>','1','','2015-10-07 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Unit No. 104, Type-B2 Built up villa ','','',2,0,0,0,'rerafilingformm','2019-01-05 16:33:59.000','rerafilingformm','2019-01-05 16:33:59.000'),(794,1242,'1242',1255,'9bb53a1d-6d25-411b-98ab-32c07efb3d65','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Gurditt Singh Saini','advocategssaini@gmail.com',9815973578,0,0,'#2240','Sector 45-C',6,128,'160047','1','Chamber No.15','District Courts Sector 43-D',6,128,'160043','Gurditt Singh Saini','advocategssaini@gmail.com',9815973578,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PM0039','Chandigarh Royale City Promoters Pvt. Ltd.','Pardeep Kumar Bansal','chandigarhroyalecity@gmail.com',9217092181,0,'Village Karala','Post office Banur, Tehsil Derabassi',28,507,'140601','1','Village Karala','Post office Banur, Tehsil Derabassi',28,507,'140601','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:12.5pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">sIR,</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:12.5pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">After\r\ngoing through a news item in ‘Hindustan Times’ newspaper dated 4.8.2012,\r\nComplainants applied for 200 Sq. Yds plot in August 2012 @ </span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:12.5pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Rupee Foradian&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:Arial\">` </span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:12.5pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">13750/- per sq. Yds. &amp;\r\npaid an amount of </span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:12.5pt;line-height:\r\n200%;font-family:&quot;Rupee Foradian&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial\">` </span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:12.5pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">7\r\nLac vide cheque on dt 27.8.2012. The Complainants opted for subvention plan of\r\npayment through their approved financial institution i.e. M/S Dewan Housing\r\nFinance corporation Limited(DHFL) vide which loan from one of their approved DHFL\r\nwas being given and the installments of which were initially to be paid by the\r\nRespondents for 18 months or till offer of the possession.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:12.5pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">A\r\nletter dt.5.2.2013 was issued by the Respondents intimating the complainant\r\nabout sanctioning of the lay out plan and the approval of project and demand of\r\npayment due as per schedule given therein which includes EDC being asked and\r\ncomplaints were also asked to enter into the buyer agreement. Thereafter\r\nRespondents issued a provisional allotment dt. 27.9.2013 allotting a Plot\r\nNo.410 measuring 200 sq. yds and complainants had entered into plot buyer\r\nagreement with the Respondents on the same day.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:12.5pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">A\r\nLoan of the Complainants was approved by DHFL for </span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:12.5pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Rupee Foradian&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:Arial\">` </span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:12.5pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">2062000/- and the payments\r\nof </span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:12.5pt;line-height:200%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Rupee Foradian&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial\">` </span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:12.5pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">47100/-\r\n&amp; </span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:12.5pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Rupee Foradian&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial\">` </span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:12.5pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">1692935/-\r\nwere credited into the account of the Respondents on 1.12.2013 &amp; further </span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:12.5pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Rupee Foradian&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:Arial\">` </span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:12.5pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">204710/- on 29.1.2014.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:12.5pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-GB;mso-fareast-language:\r\nEN-GB;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\">There was no progress in the development at site\r\nand its huge delay in the execution of the project. The plot allotted to them\r\nwas neither demarcated nor does any promise given at the time of booking seem to\r\nbe fulfilled in near future. Even respondents are not having all approvals and\r\nsanctions from the competent authorities in respect of the entire 200 acres\r\nproject. None of the promises and assurances of having a smart city seems to\r\nhave been achieved by the Respondents and as such the complainants have been\r\ndeceived by the Respondents. The Respondents with their ulterior motive to\r\navoid the further payment of EMI under the subvention plan, sent an offer of\r\npossession of plot on 7.10.2014 to the complainants</span><br></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:12.5pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">The\r\ncomplainants have been allured and deceived upon by the Respondents while\r\nshattering their dream of a sweet home within the vicinity of Chandigarh. The\r\ncomplainants seek refund of their amount along with other relief inter alia\r\nbased on following grounds:<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:12.5pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">i)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; The Respondents deceived the complainant\r\nby alluring them for depositing an amount of </span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:12.5pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Rupee Foradian&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:Arial\">` </span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:12.5pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">26,44,745/- in their project\r\nwithout having approvals and necessary permissions from the competent\r\nauthorities for such a long time, as such Complainants seeks refund of the\r\namount of <br>\r\n</span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:12.5pt;line-height:200%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Rupee Foradian&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial;background:#F1F1F1\">` </span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:12.5pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">26,44,745/-\r\ntowards the amount deposited in respect of payment of the plot.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:12.5pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">ii)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; The complainants are also entitled for\r\ninterest @18% per annum from the date of its deposit till realization on the\r\namount of refund <br>\r\n</span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:12.5pt;line-height:200%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Rupee Foradian&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial\">` </span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:12.5pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">26,44,745/-.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:12.5pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">iii)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; The complainants are also entitled for </span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:12.5pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Rupee Foradian&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:Arial\">` </span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:12.5pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">50,000/- on account of\r\ndeficiency in service &amp; unfair trade practice on the part of respondents resulting\r\nmonetary loss and for causing physical harassment as well as mental agony to\r\nthe complainants.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:12.5pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">iv)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; The complainants are also entitled for sum\r\nof </span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:12.5pt;line-height:200%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Rupee Foradian&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial\">` </span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:12.5pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">50,000/-\r\ntowards the cost of uncalled and unnecessarily litigation and court fee.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:12.5pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">v)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Any other relief which this Hon’ble Forum\r\nmay deem fit and proper be also granted to the complainants against the\r\nRespondents.<o:p></o:p></span></p>',3276250.00,2644745.00,'2015-09-27 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','No interim relief is claimed.','0','','2013-09-27 00:00:00','2013-09-27 00:00:00','410','','',1,0,0,0,'VakilSaini','2019-01-05 19:34:47.000','VakilSaini','2019-01-05 19:34:47.000'),(795,1243,'1243',1273,'1dbf4637-f288-44fd-b82c-234353e5ccb8','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','ANIL KUMAR GOYAL','advrajivbhatia9@gmail.com',8847215131,0,0,'HO