. Club house as promised by respondent at the time of booking is still not constructed. Further there are no signs of 18 Hole Golf courses as promised by respondent. Revenue Rastas of the villages have not been yet acquired resulting which people of the village roaming within the township  with their cattle as such there are insufficient security arrangements have been made. Respondents were supposed to handover the possession of said plot to complainant till March. 2015 but inspite of the lapse of almost 4 years, there is no development at site. Furter no plot buyer agreement is executed till date.</p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.25in;text-align:justify;text-justify:\r\ninter-ideograph;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:\r\n&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">In view of the factual matrix as mentioned above in\r\npara 4 of this complaint and in view of the facts that despite lapse of 4 years\r\n&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">respondent even failed to get the plot buyer\r\nagreement executed with complainant and further failed to offer possession of the\r\ncomplete project alongwith all basic amenities as per their advertisement and brouchers\r\nand with clear approach from Ludhiana Ferozepur Road, complainant seeks kind indulgence\r\nof this Hon’ble Authority in granting following reliefs: 1. To refund the entire\r\namount paid by complainant i. e. </span></span><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif; font-size: 14px;\">Rs. 23,00,000/- (Rupees Twenty Three Lac\r\nonly)</span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">\r\nalongwith interest @ 18% per annum from the date of respective payments till\r\nthe realization alongwith Rs.5 Lac as compensation for mental harassment\r\nsuffered by complainant and Rs.55,000/- cost of Litigation 2. Any other relief that\r\nthis Hon’ble Authority may deem fit and appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances\r\nof the present complaint.</span><o:p></o:p></span></p>',3530250.00,1800000.00,'2015-05-15 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>NIL</p>','1','','2013-11-15 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Plot no. K-12, The Imperial Golf Estates, Village Mulanpur-Talwandi, Ludhiana.','','',2,0,0,0,'advrajivbhatia9','2019-01-06 09:38:24.000','advrajivbhatia9','2019-01-06 09:38:24.000'),(796,1243,'1243',1273,'1dbf4637-f288-44fd-b82c-234353e5ccb8','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-01-20 21:23:59.000','ANIL KUMAR GOYAL','advrajivbhatia9@gmail.com',8847215131,0,0,'HOUSE NO. 44-45','CENTRAL TOWN, VILLAGE DAAD, POST OFFICE LALTON KALAN, PAKHOWAL ROAD',28,366,'141001','1','HOUSE NO. 44-45','CENTRAL TOWN, VILLAGE DAAD, POST OFFICE LALTON KALAN, PAKHOWAL ROAD',28,366,'141001','RAJIV K. BHATIA, ADVOCATE','advrajivbhatia9@gmail.com',9501814939,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-LDH45-PR0166','THE IMPERIAL GOLF ESTATE','M/s. Emerald Lands (India) Private Limited','ashok.sharma@imperialgolfestate.com',0,1244550340,'Registered office at 2nd Floor, C-8/1-A, Vasant Vihar, New Delhi-110057','',10,120,'110057','1','Registered office at 2nd Floor, C-8/1-A, Vasant Vihar, New Delhi-110057','',10,120,'110057','1','<p>At that time of booking, respondent represented of having all sufficient approvals, clear ownership and clear and well approach from main Ludhiana-Ferozpur Road as per master plan of Glada and is an approachable project to live with 18 Hole Golf Course, 8ft. boundary wall with long trees besides boundary, ultra modern club house with swimming pool and many more facilities would be there. Complainant under their representation got booked a plot no. K-12, measuring 261.50 sq. yards on 30.10.2013  Plot was allotted to complainant by vide Allotment Letter dated 15.11.2013. BSP of the plot was Rs. 35,30,250/- excluding EDC, IFSD,PLC and Golf Club Membership fee. Till date a sum of Rs. 23,00,000/-  has already been paid by complainant which is almost 65% of the BSP. Respondent assured that complainant shall get the possession of the fully developed plot within 18 months from the date of allotment along with the entire basic amenities as per their broachers and advertisement. possession of the&nbsp; plot NOT DELIVERED as per their commitments and as per their promises. No sign of development was observed as promised by respondents. Roads are in pathetic condition, internal roads are still unconstructed, there are no electricity connection arrangements as well as basic amenities such as water, sewerage, park roads, boundary wall is not constructed as yet. Club house as promised by respondent at the time of booking is still not constructed. Further there are no signs of 18 Hole Golf courses as promised by respondent. Revenue Rastas of the villages have not been yet acquired resulting which people of the village roaming within the township  with their cattle as such there are insufficient security arrangements have been made. Respondents were supposed to handover the possession of said plot to complainant till March. 2015 but inspite of the lapse of almost 4 years, there is no development at site. Furter no plot buyer agreement is executed till date.</p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.25in;text-align:justify;text-justify:\r\ninter-ideograph;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:\r\n&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">In view of the factual matrix as mentioned above in\r\npara 4 of this complaint and in view of the facts that despite lapse of 4 years\r\n&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">respondent even failed to get the plot buyer\r\nagreement executed with complainant and further failed to offer possession of the\r\ncomplete project alongwith all basic amenities as per their advertisement and brouchers\r\nand with clear approach from Ludhiana Ferozepur Road, complainant seeks kind indulgence\r\nof this Hon’ble Authority in granting following reliefs: 1. To refund the entire\r\namount paid by complainant i. e. </span></span><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif; font-size: 14px;\">Rs. 23,00,000/- (Rupees Twenty Three Lac\r\nonly)</span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">\r\nalongwith interest @ 18% per annum from the date of respective payments till\r\nthe realization alongwith Rs.5 Lac as compensation for mental harassment\r\nsuffered by complainant and Rs.55,000/- cost of Litigation 2. Any other relief that\r\nthis Hon’ble Authority may deem fit and appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances\r\nof the present complaint.</span><o:p></o:p></span></p>',3530250.00,2300000.00,'2015-05-15 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>NIL</p>','1','','2013-11-15 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Plot no. K-12, The Imperial Golf Estates, Village Mulanpur-Talwandi, Ludhiana.','','',1,1,0,0,'advrajivbhatia9','2019-01-06 09:58:01.000','advrajivbhatia9','2019-01-06 09:58:01.000'),(797,1184,'1184',1250,'bc502035-2e0d-4d0d-ab5b-b3bf8a32e5e8','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-01-06 11:39:12.000','raj kumar chaudhary','mgarg14@gmail.com',9872840114,0,0,'house no. 250, new dashmesh nagar','rama mandi, jalandhar',28,261,'144005','1','house no. 250, new dashmesh nagar','rama mandi, jalandhar',28,261,'144005','Munish Gupta','guptalegal44@gmail.com',9814061084,1724016068,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PM0023','geetu constructions pvt ltd','geetu constructions pvt ltd','info@gcplmohali.com',0,1725032649,'sco 219, 2nd floor','sector 37c',6,128,'160036','1','sco 219, 2nd floor','sector 37c',6,128,'160036','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: roboto, serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">Allured by advertisements and\r\npromises of marketing persons of respondent, in order to have a residential\r\napartment for himself, applicant booked 3BHK apartment in project of\r\nrespondents by paying initial sum of Rs. 1 lakh on 10.09.2012. Total sale consideration\r\nof the unit was fixed as Rs.37,50,000/-. Receipt qua deposit was issued which\r\nis attached. Later as per demands raised telephonically, complainant deposited\r\nRs. 4 lakh vide RTGS on 21.11.2012 and paid another sum of Rs. 1,50,000/- on\r\n11.03.2013 vide Transaction no. 00000869309682A1 from HDFC Bank Jalandhar. All\r\namounts were paid from Account of complainant of HDFC Bank . Statement\r\nreflecting all transactions is attached. Despite receipt of Rs. 6.5 Lakh\r\n(almost 20 % ) , neither allotment letter has been issued , nor any buyers\r\nagreement has been executed , which is violaton of provisions of PAPRA as well\r\nas RERA. Builder has been requested time and again regarding allotment letter,\r\nbuyers agreement and even status of project, but to no use. Complainant is fed\r\nup of the false promises given since 2013 and as such now has decided to\r\nwithdraw from the project. Legal notice dated 23.7.2018 has been served\r\ninforming intention of complainant but to no use and therefore, instant\r\ncomplaint is being filed. Copy of legal notice and postal receipt is attached.</span><o:p></o:p></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: roboto, serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">It is therefore, respectfully\r\nprayed that amount of Rs.6.5 Lakh deposited be ordered to be refunded with\r\ninterest from respective dates of deposits and suitable compensation and\r\nlitigation expenses be also ordered in favour of complainant for mental agony,\r\nharassment caused by respondent.</span></p>',3750000.00,650000.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>respondents bank account be ordered to be attached</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',1,1,0,0,'rajkumarchaudhary4444','2019-01-06 11:32:12.000','rajkumarchaudhary4444','2019-01-06 11:32:12.000'),(798,1244,'1244',1273,'1dbf4637-f288-44fd-b82c-234353e5ccb8','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-01-20 16:58:33.000','ANIL KUMAR GOYAL','advrajivbhatia9@gmail.com',8847215131,0,0,'HOUSE NO. 44-45','CENTRAL TOWN, VILLAGE DAAD, POST OFFICE LALTON KALAN, PAKHOWAL ROAD',28,366,'141001','1','HOUSE NO. 44-45','CENTRAL TOWN, VILLAGE DAAD, POST OFFICE LALTON KALAN, PAKHOWAL ROAD',28,366,'141001','RAJIV K. BHATIA, ADVOCATE','advrajivbhatia9@gmail.com',9501814939,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-LDH45-PR0166','IMPERIAL GOLF ESTATE','M/s. Emerald Lands (India) Private Limited','ashok.sharma@imperialgolfestate.com',0,1244550340,'Registered office at 2nd Floor, C-8/1-A, Vasant Vihar, New Delhi-110057','',10,120,'110057','1','Registered office at 2nd Floor, C-8/1-A, Vasant Vihar, New Delhi-110057','',10,120,'110057','1','<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: roboto, serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">At that time of booking, respondent represented of having all sufficient\r\napprovals, clear ownership and clear and well approach from main\r\nLudhiana-Ferozpur Road as per master plan of Glada and is an approachable\r\nproject to live with 18 Hole Golf Course, 8ft. boundary wall with long trees\r\nbesides boundary, ultra modern club house with swimming pool and many more\r\nfacilities would be there. Complainant under their representation got booked a\r\nplot no. K-13, measuring 261.50 sq. yards on 30.10.2013 Plot was allotted to\r\ncomplainant by vide Allotment Letter dated 15.11.2013. BSP of the plot was Rs.\r\n35,30,250/- excluding EDC, IFSD,PLC and Golf Club Membership fee. Till date a\r\nsum of Rs. 23,00,000/- has already been paid by complainant which is almost 65%\r\nof the BSP. Respondent assured that complainant shall get the possession of the\r\nfully developed plot within 18 months from the date of allotment along with the\r\nentire basic amenities as per their broachers and advertisement. Possession of\r\nthe&nbsp; plot not delivered as per their commitments and as per their\r\npromises. No sign of development was observed as promised by respondents. Roads\r\nare in pathetic condition, internal roads are still unconstructed, there are no\r\nelectricity connection arrangements as well as basic amenities such as water,\r\nsewerage, park roads, boundary wall is not constructed as yet. Club house as\r\npromised by respondent at the time of booking is still not constructed. Further\r\nthere are no signs of 18 Hole Golf courses as promised by respondent. Revenue Rastas\r\nof the villages have not been yet acquired resulting which people of the\r\nvillage roaming within the township with their cattle as such there are\r\ninsufficient security arrangements have been made. Respondents were supposed to\r\nhandover the possession of said plot to complainant till March. 2015 but\r\ninspite of the lapse of almost 4 years, there is no development at site. Further\r\nno plot buyer agreement is executed till date.</span><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.25in;text-align:justify;text-justify:\r\ninter-ideograph;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;font-family:\r\n&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">In view of the factual matrix as mentioned above in\r\npara 4 of this complaint and in view of the facts that despite lapse of 4 years\r\n&nbsp;respondent even failed to get the plot buyer\r\nagreement executed with complainant and further failed to offer possession of the\r\ncomplete project alongwith all basic amenities as per their advertisement and brouchers\r\nand with clear approach from Ludhiana Ferozepur Road, complainant seeks kind indulgence\r\nof this Hon’ble Authority in granting following reliefs: 1. To refund the entire\r\namount paid by complainant i. e. </span><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">Rs.\r\n23,00,000/- (Rupees Twenty Three Lac only)</span><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"> alongwith interest @ 18% per annum\r\nfrom the date of respective payments till the realization alongwith Rs.5 Lac as\r\ncompensation for mental harassment suffered by complainant and Rs.55,000/- cost\r\nof Litigation 2. Any other relief that this Hon’ble Authority may deem fit and appropriate\r\nin view of the facts and circumstances of the present complaint.<o:p></o:p></span></p>',3530250.00,2300000.00,'2015-05-15 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>NIL</p>','1','','2013-11-15 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Plot no. K-13, situated at Maullanpur-Talwandi, Ferozepur road, Ludhiana','','',1,1,0,0,'advrajivbhatia9','2019-01-06 12:03:51.000','advrajivbhatia9','2019-01-06 12:03:51.000'),(799,1181,'1181',1261,'87a17578-cb7d-4b63-b1e8-f97fd8b674d5','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-19 14:34:01.000','Ravikant Sawhney','gaurav.chopra@hotmail.com',9815400414,0,0,'B-XXX-891','near Mothu Ram Pump, sherpur, Sherpur',28,366,'142036','1','B-XXX-891','near Mothu Ram Pump, sherpur, Sherpur',28,366,'142036','Gaurav Chopra','gaurav.chopra@hotmail.com',9814013127,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0119','Mohali Hills (Group Housing)','Emaar MGF Land Ltd','sorabh.kakar@emaarmgf.com',0,0,'40, Ground Floor','Central Plaza, sector 105',28,507,'140306','1','40, Ground Floor','Central Plaza, sector 105',28,507,'140306','1','<p><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">•	Applicant: M/s APS International Pvt Ltd through its Authorized Signatory Sh. Ravikant Sawhney</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">•	Allotment letter : 15.1.2008\r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">•	Allotted Unit: Apartment No. K3-FPH-PH-01 in “The Views” at Mohali Hills in Sector-105, SAS Nagar, District Mohali</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">• Buyer\'s Agreement :29.2.2008\r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">•	Total sale consideration of Rs. 1,10,52,008/- for super area of 3250 sq. ft.   \r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">•	Construction Linked Instalment Plan amount paid till date: Rs. 1,01,71,173/- was paid by the Applicant to the Respondent upto 28.10.2014. \r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">•	As per Clause 21.1 of the Buyer’s Agreement, the Respondent was under a contractual obligation to handover possession of the Allotted Unit within a period of 36 months from the date of allotment with a further relaxation of 90 days over and above the stipulated time period for the purpose of applying for and obtaining an Occupation Certificate in respect of the Group Housing Complex.  \r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">•	That Clause 21.1 of the Agreement read with Clause 23.1 made it abundantly clear that time was the essence of the contract and hence, possession of the Allotted Unit was required to be handed over to the Applicant by the Respondent positively on or before 15.4.2011.  Till date, however, despite a lapse of more than 6 years, possession of the Allotted Unit has not been offered or handed over to the Applicant and this willful omission and lapse on the part of the Respondent constitutes a willful and material breach of the Agreement dated 29.2.2008 executed between the parties.  \r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">•	Aggrieved by the aforesaid omission and lapse of the Respondent, the Applicant had written a letter/e-mail dated 29.9.2017 to the Respondent for rescinding the contract and for seeking refund of the principal amount paid by the Applicant in respect of the Allotted Unit alongwith interest.  Till date, however, the aforesaid demand raised by the Applicant has not been acceded to by the Respondent and thus, vide the instant complaint, the Applicant seek refund of the monies paid by it to the Respondent alongwith interest</span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:1.0in;text-align:justify;text-indent:\r\n-.5in;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n200%;font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">i)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Refund of an amount of Rs. 1,01,71,173/-\r\npaid by the Applicant alongwith interest (highest marginal cost of lending rate\r\nof the State Bank of India + 2%) from the respective dates of deposit till\r\nactual realization as per Sections 18 and 19(4) of the Act read with Rule 16 of\r\nthe Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:1.0in;text-align:justify;text-indent:\r\n-.5in;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n200%;font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">ii)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Any other relief which the Applicant is\r\nentitled for under the Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Act, 2016 and\r\nthe Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017.&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p>',11052008.00,10171173.00,'2011-04-15 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>N.A.</p>','1','','2008-01-15 00:00:00','2008-02-29 00:00:00','K3-FPH-PH-01 “The Views” at Mohali Hills in Sector-105, SAS Nagar, District Mohali','','',2,0,0