 years, possession of the Allotted Unit has not been offered or handed over to the Applicant and this willful omission and lapse on the part of the Respondent constitutes a willful and material breach of the Agreement dated 29.2.2008 executed between the parties.  \r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">•	Aggrieved by the aforesaid omission and lapse of the Respondent, the Applicant had written a letter/e-mail dated 29.9.2017 to the Respondent for rescinding the contract and for seeking refund of the principal amount paid by the Applicant in respect of the Allotted Unit alongwith interest.  Till date, however, the aforesaid demand raised by the Applicant has not been acceded to by the Respondent and thus, vide the instant complaint, the Applicant seek refund of the monies paid by it to the Respondent alongwith interest</span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:1.0in;text-align:justify;text-indent:\r\n-.5in;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n200%;font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">i)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Refund of an amount of Rs. 1,01,71,173/-\r\npaid by the Applicant alongwith interest (highest marginal cost of lending rate\r\nof the State Bank of India + 2%) from the respective dates of deposit till\r\nactual realization as per Sections 18 and 19(4) of the Act read with Rule 16 of\r\nthe Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:1.0in;text-align:justify;text-indent:\r\n-.5in;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n200%;font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">ii)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Any other relief which the Applicant is\r\nentitled for under the Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Act, 2016 and\r\nthe Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017.&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p>',11052008.00,10171173.00,'2011-04-15 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>N.A.</p>','1','','2008-01-15 00:00:00','2008-02-29 00:00:00','K3-FPH-PH-01 “The Views” at Mohali Hills in Sector-105, SAS Nagar, District Mohali','','',2,0,0,0,'APSInternational','2019-01-06 13:23:59.000','APSInternational','2019-01-06 13:23:59.000'),(802,1246,'1246',1273,'1dbf4637-f288-44fd-b82c-234353e5ccb8','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-01-20 17:07:20.000','SANJAY GOYAL','advrajivbhatia9@gmail.com',8847215131,0,0,'HOUSE NO. 44-45','CENTRAL TOWN, VILLAGE DAAD, POST OFFICE LALTON KALAN, PAKHOWAL ROAD',28,366,'141010','1','HOUSE NO. 44-45','CENTRAL TOWN, VILLAGE DAAD, POST OFFICE LALTON KALAN, PAKHOWAL ROAD',28,366,'141010','RAJIV K. BHATIA, ADVOCATE','advrajivbhatia9@gmail.com',9501814939,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-LDH45-PR0166','IMPERIAL GOLF ESTATE','M/s. Emerald Lands (India) Private Limited','ashok.sharma@imperialgolfestate.com',0,1244550340,'Registered office at 2nd Floor, C-8/1-A, Vasant Vihar, New Delhi-110057','',10,120,'110057','1','Registered office at 2nd Floor, C-8/1-A, Vasant Vihar, New Delhi-110057','',10,120,'110057','1','<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: roboto, serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">At that time of booking, respondent represented of having all sufficient\r\napprovals, clear ownership and clear and well approach from main\r\nLudhiana-Ferozpur Road as per master plan of Glada and is an approachable\r\nproject to live with 18 Hole Golf Course, 8ft. boundary wall with long trees\r\nbesides boundary, ultra modern club house with swimming pool and many more\r\nfacilities would be there. Complainant under their representation got booked a\r\nplot no. K-4, measuring 268.26 sq. yards on 30.10.2013 Plot was allotted to\r\ncomplainant by vide Allotment Letter dated 15.11.2013. BSP of the plot was Rs.\r\n36,21,510/- excluding EDC, IFSD,PLC and Golf Club Membership fee. Till date a\r\nsum of Rs. 18,00,000/- has already been paid by complainant which is almost 50%\r\nof the BSP. Respondent assured that complainant shall get the possession of the\r\nfully developed plot within 18 months from the date of allotment along with the\r\nentire basic amenities as per their broachers and advertisement. Possession of\r\nthe&nbsp; plot not delivered as per their commitments and as per their\r\npromises. No sign of development was observed as promised by respondents. Roads\r\nare in pathetic condition, internal roads are still unconstructed, there are no\r\nelectricity connection arrangements as well as basic amenities such as water,\r\nsewerage, park roads, boundary wall is not constructed as yet. Club house as\r\npromised by respondent at the time of booking is still not constructed. Further\r\nthere are no signs of 18 Hole Golf courses as promised by respondent. Revenue Rastas\r\nof the villages have not been yet acquired resulting which people of the\r\nvillage roaming within the township with their cattle as such there are\r\ninsufficient security arrangements have been made. Respondents were supposed to\r\nhandover the possession of said plot to complainant till March. 2015 but\r\ninspite of the lapse of almost 4 years, there is no development at site. Further\r\nno plot buyer agreement is executed till date.</span><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:115%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-theme-font:minor-fareast;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\r\nmso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;mso-ansi-language:EN-US;mso-fareast-language:\r\nEN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\">In view of the factual matrix as mentioned above\r\nin para 4 of this complaint and in view of the facts that despite lapse of 4 years\r\n&nbsp;respondent even failed to get the plot buyer\r\nagreement executed with complainant and further failed to offer possession of the\r\ncomplete project alongwith all basic amenities as per their advertisement and brouchers\r\nand with clear approach from Ludhiana Ferozepur Road, complainant seeks kind indulgence\r\nof this Hon’ble Authority in granting following reliefs: 1. To refund the entire\r\namount paid by complainant i. e. </span><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-theme-font:minor-fareast;mso-bidi-font-family:\r\n&quot;Courier New&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-US;mso-fareast-language:EN-US;mso-bidi-language:\r\nAR-SA\">Rs. 18,00,000/- (Rupees Eighteen Lac only)</span><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-fareast-theme-font:minor-fareast;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;\r\nmso-ansi-language:EN-US;mso-fareast-language:EN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\">\r\nalongwith interest @ 18% per annum from the date of respective payments till\r\nthe realization alongwith Rs.5 Lac as compensation for mental harassment\r\nsuffered by complainant and Rs.55,000/- cost of Litigation 2. Any other relief that\r\nthis Hon’ble Authority may deem fit and appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances\r\nof the present complaint.</span><br></p>',3621510.00,1800000.00,'2015-05-15 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>NIL</p>','1','','2013-11-15 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','PLOT NO. K-4, THE IMPERIAL GOLF ESTATE, LUDHIANA','','',1,1,0,