: initial;\">At that time of booking, respondent represented of having all sufficient\r\napprovals, clear ownership and clear and well approach from main\r\nLudhiana-Ferozpur Road as per master plan of Glada and is an approachable\r\nproject to live with 18 Hole Golf Course, 8ft. boundary wall with long trees\r\nbesides boundary, ultra modern club house with swimming pool and many more\r\nfacilities would be there. Complainant under their representation got booked a\r\nplot no. A-5, measuring 1928.42 sq. yards on 28.04.2013 Plot was allotted to\r\ncomplainant by vide Allotment Letter dated 26.06.2013. BSP of the plot was Rs. 2,60,33,670/-\r\nexcluding EDC, IFSD,PLC and Golf Club Membership fee. Till date a sum of Rs. 2,47,31,987/-\r\nhas already been paid by complainant which is almost 95% of the BSP. Plot buyer\r\nagreement was executed on 17.07.2013. Respondent agreed in clause 12.1 that\r\ncomplainant shall get the possession of the fully developed plot within 24\r\nmonths from the date of agreement along with the entire basic amenities as per\r\ntheir broachers and advertisement. Possession of the&nbsp; plot not delivered\r\nas per their commitments and as per their promises. No sign of development was\r\nobserved as promised by respondents. Roads are in pathetic condition, internal\r\nroads are still unconstructed, there are no electricity connection arrangements\r\nas well as basic amenities such as water, sewerage, park roads, boundary wall\r\nis not constructed as yet. Club house as promised by respondent at the time of\r\nbooking is still not constructed. Further there are no signs of 18 Hole Golf\r\ncourses as promised by respondent. Revenue Rastas of the villages have not been\r\nyet acquired resulting which people of the village roaming within the township\r\nwith their cattle as such there are insufficient security arrangements have\r\nbeen made. Respondents were supposed to handover the possession of said plot to\r\ncomplainant till july. 2015 but inspite of the lapse of almost 4 years, there\r\nis no development at site.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;font-family:\r\n&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.25in;text-align:justify;text-justify:\r\ninter-ideograph;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;font-family:\r\n&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">In view of the factual matrix as mentioned above in\r\npara 4 of this complaint and in view of the facts that despite lapse of 4 years\r\n&nbsp;respondent even failed to get the plot buyer\r\nagreement executed with complainant and further failed to offer possession of the\r\ncomplete project alongwith all basic amenities as per their advertisement and brouchers\r\nand with clear approach from Ludhiana Ferozepur Road, complainant seeks kind indulgence\r\nof this Hon’ble Authority in granting following reliefs: 1. To refund the entire\r\namount paid by complainant i. e. </span><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">Rs.\r\n2,47,31,987/-</span><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">\r\nalongwith interest @ 18% per annum from the date of respective payments till\r\nthe realization alongwith Rs.5 Lac as compensation for mental harassment\r\nsuffered by complainant and Rs.55,000/- cost of Litigation 2. Any other relief that\r\nthis Hon’ble Authority may deem fit and appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances\r\nof the present complaint.<o:p></o:p></span></p>',26033670.00,24731987.00,'2015-07-17 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>nil</p>','1','','2013-06-26 00:00:00','2013-07-17 00:00:00','Plot no. A-5 The Imperial Golf  Estate, Ludhiana.','','',2,0,0,0,'advrajivbhatia9','2019-01-06 14:36:42.000','advrajivbhatia9','2019-01-06 14:36:42.000'),(806,1240,'1240',1317,'d8f8d4fc-24ac-4faa-a9b2-b5ad58a5817a','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Bharat Bhushan Makkar','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9729902009,0,934955777170,'108 Sector 20 Kaithal','',13,9,'136027','1','108 Sector 20 Kaithal','',13,9,'136027','Kamal Dahiya','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9729902009,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0121','Purab Premium Apartments','Greater Mohali Area Development Authority','ce@gmada.gov.in',1722215512,0,'PUDA Bhawan Sector 62 District SAS Nagar Mohali','',28,507,'160062','1','PUDA Bhawan Sector 62 District SAS Nagar Mohali','',28,507,'160062','1','<p>Respondent opened scheme for public from 12.12.2011 to 12.01.2012 asAnnexureC-1. The depicted salient features asAnnexureC-2. Respondent informed vide letter dated 23.03.2012 for the waiting list and complainant to submit the documents before 23/04/2012AnnexureC-3. Letter of intent for allotment was issued on 23.05.2012 and tentative price was Rs 69,00,000 and the flat was allotted with Flat No. 901 in Tower 3, Block E at Type 3 Apartment. As per Para 3(II) delivery within a period of 36 months from the date of issuance of the said letter. Possession date was 23.05.2015 i.e. delayed by 3 years and 7 monthsAnnexureC-4. Payment plan B was opted by the complainantAnnexureC-4(Pg 40). Initial amount of INR 13,80,000 paid vide cheque on 19.06.2012AnnexureC-5(Pg41). Total amount paid Rs68,06,850/- i.e. 99% out of the total considerationAnnexureC-5. Respondent offered the possession vide letter on 10.10.2017. Thereafter the complainant visited site and found that layout plan has changed without taking the consent of 2/3rd allottees and also found many loopholes in the construction like compromised quality of materials etc.Photographs are annexed asAnnexure C-6. The complainant got the construction inspected by Registered Council of Architecture, New Delhi. Many differences were found as inAnnexureC-7. The complainant intimated such defects to the Estate Officer of GMADA vide letter dated 17.05.2018 and requested for refund of his paid amount but respondent didn’t respondAnnexureC-8. Other allottees also found several defects, deficiencies and deviations in the projectAnnexureC-9(Pg104). Several allottees raised the issues before the press conference(Pg 105-106). The government ordered to remove the defaults but respondent did not comply to repair the faults(Pg 107-108). Fire safety has been expired(Pg 109-110). The lifts are also not safe and stops to work. Many times someone stops in the elevator(Pg 111-113).&nbsp;</p><p><br></p>','<p>In view of the facts mentioned in preceding paragraphs, the complainant prays for the following relief(s):-&nbsp;</p><p>i.To give necessary directions to the respondents for refund the amount paid by the complainant with prescribed interest till realization as per the provisions of Sec. 18 and Sec.19(4)of the RERA Act read with Rule 16 of PSRE(R&amp;D)Rules,2017.</p><p>ii.To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 60 of RERA Act for willful default committed by them.</p><p>iii.To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 61 of RERA Act for contravention of Sec.12, Sec.14, and Sec. 16 of RERA Act.</p><p>iv.To issue directions to make liable every officer concerned i.e. Director, Manager, Secretary, or any other officer of the respondent’s company at whose instance, connivance, acquiescence, neglect any of the offences has been committed as mentioned in Sec.69 of RERA Act,2016 to be read with Punjab RERA Rules, 2017.</p><p>v.To recommend criminal action against the respondents for the criminal offence of cheating, fraud and criminal breach of trust under section 420,406 and 409 of the Indian Penal Code.</p><p>vi.To issue direction to pay the cost of litigation.</p><p>vii.To issue direction to pay the compensation to complainant for compensation for his mental agony, pain and harassment.</p><p>viii.Any other relief which this Hon’ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances of this complaint.</p><div><br></div>',69000.00,6806850.00,'2015-05-23 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>i.To direct the respondent not to demand any further amount whatsoever from the complainant.</p><p>ii.The respondent should be restrained from harassing the complainant in any manner whatsoever.</p><p>iii.Any other interim relief which this Hon’ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances of this complaint.</p><div><br></div>','1','','2012-05-23 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Flat No 901 Tower 3 Block E Type 3 Sector 88 Sahibzada Ajit Singh Nagar Punjab 140308','','',2,0,0,0,'Bharatbhushanmakkar','2019-01-06 16:00:36.000','Bharatbhushanmakkar','2019-01-06 16:00:36.000'),(807,1181,'1181',1261,'87a17578-cb7d-4b63-b1e8-f97fd8b674d5','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-01-07 12:17:53.000','Ravikant Sawhney','gaurav.chopra@hotmail.com',9815400414,0,0,'B-XXX-891','near Mothu Ram Pump, sherpur, Sherpur',28,366,'142036','1','B-XXX-891','near Mothu Ram Pump, sherpur, Sherpur',28,366,'142036','Gaurav Chopra','gaurav.chopra@hotmail.com',9814013127,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0119','Mohali Hills (Group Housing)','Emaar MGF Land Ltd','sorabh.kakar@emaarmgf.com',0,0,'40, Ground Floor','Central Plaza, sector 105',28,507,'140306','1','40, Ground Floor','Central Plaza, sector 105',28,507,'140306','1','<p><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">•	Applicant: M/s APS International Pvt Ltd through its Authorized Signatory Sh. Ravikant Sawhney</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">•	Allotment letter : 15.1.2008\r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">•	Allotted Unit: Apartment No. K3-FPH-PH-01 in “The Views” at Mohali Hills in Sector-105, SAS Nagar, District Mohali</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">• Buyer\'s Agreement :29.2.2008\r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">•	Total sale consideration of Rs. 1,10,52,008/- for super area of 3250 sq. ft.   \r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">•	Construction Linked Instalment Plan amount paid till date: Rs. 1,01,71,173/- was paid by the Applicant to the Respondent upto 28.10.2014. \r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">•	As per Clause 21.1 of the Buyer’s Agreement, the Respondent was under a contractual obligation to handover possession of the Allotted Unit within a period of 36 months from the date of allotment with a further relaxation of 90 days over and above the stipulated time period for the purpose of applying for and obtaining an Occupation Certificate in respect of the Group Housing Complex.  \r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">•	That Clause 21.1 of the Agreement read with Clause 23.1 made it abundantly clear that time was the essence of the contract and hence, possession of the Allotted Unit was required to be handed over to the Applicant by the Respondent positively on or before 15.4.2011.  Till date, however, despite a lapse of more than 6 years, possession of the Allotted Unit has not been offered or handed over to the Applicant and this willful omission and lapse on the part of the Respondent constitutes a willful and material breach of the Agreement dated 29.2.2008 executed between the parties.  \r\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">•	Aggrieved by the aforesaid omission and lapse of the Respondent, the Applicant had written a letter/e-mail dated 29.9.2017 to the Respondent for rescinding the contract and for seeking refund of the principal amount paid by the Applicant in respect of the Allotted Unit alongwith interest.  Till date, however, the aforesaid demand raised by the Applicant has not been acceded to by the Respondent and thus, vide the instant complaint, the Applicant seek refund of the monies paid by it to the Respondent alongwith interest</span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:1.0in;text-align:justify;text-indent:\r\n-.5in;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n200%;font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">i)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Refund of an amount of Rs. 1,01,71,173/-\r\npaid by the Applicant alongwith interest (highest marginal cost of lending rate\r\nof the State Bank of India + 2%) from the respective dates of deposit till\r\nactual realization as per Sections 18 and 19(4) of the Act read with Rule 16 of\r\nthe Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:1.0in;text-align:justify;text-indent:\r\n-.5in;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n200%;font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">ii)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Any other relief which the Applicant is\r\nentitled for under the Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Act, 2016 and\r\nthe Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017.&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p>',11052008.00,10171173.00,'2011-04-15 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>N.A.</p>','1','','2008-01-15 00:00:00','2008-02-29 00:00:00','K3-FPH-PH-01 “The Views” at Mohali Hills in Sector-105, SAS Nagar, District Mohali','','',1,1,0,0,'APSInternational','2019-01-07 12:16:57.000','APSInternational','2019-01-07 12:16:57.000'),(808,1193,'1193',1280,'b364f9db-f8bf-4d03-9c07-d43a8d8e4b6f','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-01-07 13:03:51.000','Kamalroop  Sooch','gaurav.chopra@hotmail.com',9814013127,0,0,'House No. 607','Sector 18B Chandigarh',6,128,'160018','1','House No. 607','Sector 18B Chandigarh',6,128,'160018','Gaurav Chopra','gaurav.chopra@hotmail.com',9814013127,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0119','Mohali Hills','Emaar MGF Land Ltd','sorabh.kakar@emaarmgf.com',0,0,'Emaar MGF Land Ltd','40, Central Plaza, Ground Floor, Sector 105 Mohali',28,507,'140306','1','Emaar MGF Land Ltd','40, Central Plaza, Ground Floor, Sector 105 Mohali',28,507,'140306','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">&nbsp;<span lang=\"EN-IN\">i)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Application Form: 14.3.2007<o:p></o:p></span></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">&nbsp;ii)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Allotment\r\nLetter: 30.3.2007 <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">&nbsp;iii)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Apartment\r\nBuyer’s Agreement: 29.2.08<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">&nbsp;iv)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Allotted\r\nUnit No. TVM-H3-F11-1104 in ‘The Views’ at Mohali Hills, Sector-105, SAS Nagar,\r\nDistrict Mohali<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">&nbsp;v) &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Total\r\nsale consideration of Rs. 49,59,650/- <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-32.25pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">vi)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Construction Linked Instalment Plan<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-32.25pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">vii) &nbsp;&nbsp; Amount paid upto 23.8.2012:Rs. 42,71,510/-<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-32.25pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">viii)&nbsp;&nbsp; As per Clause 21.1 of the Agreement read with\r\nClause 23.1 made it abundantly clear that time was the essence of the contract\r\nand hence, possession of the Allotted Unit was required to be handed over to\r\nthe Applicants by the Respondent positively on or before 30.6.2010.&nbsp; <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-32.25pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">v)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Aggrieved by the aforesaid omission and\r\nlapse of the Respondent, the Applicants had written a letter/e-mail to the\r\nRespondent for rescinding the contract and for seeking refund of the principal\r\namount paid by the Applicants in respect of the Allotted Unit alongwith\r\ninterest.&nbsp; Till date, however, the\r\naforesaid demand raised by the Applicants has not been acceded to by the\r\nRespondent and thus, vide the instant complaint, the Applicants seek refund of\r\nthe monies paid by them to the Respondent alongwith interest.&nbsp; <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-32.25pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">vi)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; That it is pertinent to mention herein that\r\nin spite of the fact that the Applicants had sought refund of the principal\r\namount paid by the Applicants alongwith interest, the Respondents have\r\narbitrarily continued to issue Demand Notices to the Applicants for payment of\r\ninstalments as per the payment schedule appended with the Buyer’s agreement.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:1.0in;text-align:justify;text-indent:\r\n-.5in;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n200%;font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">i)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Refund of an amount of Rs. 42,71,510/-\r\npaid by the Applicants alongwith interest (highest marginal cost of lending\r\nrate of the State Bank of India + 2%) from the respective dates of deposit till\r\nactual realization as per Sections 18 and 19(4) of the Act read with Rule 16 of\r\nthe Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:1.0in;text-align:justify;text-indent:\r\n-.5in;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n200%;font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">ii)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Any other relief which the Applicant is\r\nentitled for under the Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Act, 2016 and\r\nthe Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>',4959650.00,4271510.00,'2010-06-30 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>...</p>','1','','2007-03-30 00:00:00','2008-02-29 00:00:00','TVM-H3-F11-1104 in ‘The Views’ at Mohali Hills, Sector-105, SAS Nagar, District Mohali','','',2,0,0,0,'Kamalroopsooch','2019-01-07 13:03:49.000','Kamalroopsooch','2019-01-07 13:03:49.000'),(809,1194,'1194',1281,'ecd6bbdb-27b0-4972-ac46-2f0682f35b3d','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-01-07 13:18:44.000','Sundeep Singh Pawar','gaurav.chopra@hotmail.com',9814013127,0,0,'House No. 607','sector 18B',6,128,'160018','1','House No. 607','sector 18B',6,128,'160018','Gaurav Chopra','gaurav.chopra@hotmail.com',9814013127,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0119','MOHALI HILLs','Emaar MGF Land Ltd','sorabh.kakar@emaarmgf.com',0,0,'Emaar MGF Land Ltd','40, Central Plaza, Ground Floor, Sector 105 Mohali',28,507,'140306','1','Emaar MGF Land Ltd','40, Central Plaza, Ground Floor, Sector 105 Mohali',28,507,'140306','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">i)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Allotment Letter:24.4.07 <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">ii)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Buyer’s Agreement:10.4.08 <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">iii)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Agreement executed between Sundeep Singh\r\nPawar and Mrs. Harinder Kaur Pawar and the Respondent in respect of the Unit\r\nNo. H1-FPH-PH-01 for a total sale consideration of Rs. 98,59,200/- of super\r\narea of 2900 sq. Ft. Subsequently, the Unit was changed TVM-H1-F10-1001.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">iv)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; On the basis of an affidavit sworn by the\r\nCo-Applicant Kamaljit Kaur Pawar, an endorsement dated 10.4.08 was made in the\r\nAgreement dated 10.4.08 whereby the co-allottees of the Allotted Unit No. were\r\nformally recorded as the Applicants herein viz. Sundeep Singh Pawar and\r\nKamaljit Kaur Pawar. Subsequently, the Allotted Unit was changed to\r\nTVM-L2-F12-1202. Further, vide an Addendum, due to modification in the layout\r\nplan, Unit No. TVM-L2-F12-1202, Sector-105, Mohali Hills, Mohali was changed to\r\nUnit No. TVM-L2-F08-802 having a super area of 2600 sq. ft for which the total\r\nsale consideration was fixed at Rs. 83,20,505/- as indicated in the letter\r\ndated 15.9.10 issued by the Respondent. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-32.25pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">v)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Construction Linked Instalment Plan<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-32.25pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">vi) &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Amount paid upto 23.10.13: Rs. 72,61,148/- <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-32.25pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">vii)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; As per Clause 21.1 of the Agreement read\r\nwith Clause 23.1 possession of the Allotted Unit was required to be handed over\r\nto the Applicants by the Respondent positively on or before 24.7.10.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-32.25pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">viii)&nbsp;&nbsp; Aggrieved by the omission of the Respondent,\r\nthe Applicants had written a letter/e-mail to the Respondent for rescinding the\r\ncontract and for seeking refund of the principal amount paid by the Applicants\r\nin respect of the Allotted Unit alongwith interest.&nbsp; Till date, however, the aforesaid demand\r\nraised by the Applicants has not been acceded to by the Respondent.&nbsp; <o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-32.25pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">ix)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; In spite of the fact that the Applicants\r\nhad sought refund of the principal amount alongwith interest, the Respondents\r\nhave arbitrarily continued to issue Demand Notices to the Applicants for\r\npayment of instalments as per the payment schedule appended with the Buyer’s\r\nagreement.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-32.25pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:1.0in;text-align:justify;text-indent:\r\n-.5in;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n200%;font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">i)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Refund of an amount of Rs. 72,61,148/-\r\npaid by the Applicants alongwith interest (highest marginal cost of lending\r\nrate of the State Bank of India + 2%) from the respective dates of deposit till\r\nactual realization as per Sections 18 and 19(4) of the Act read with Rule 16 of\r\nthe Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:1.0in;text-align:justify;text-indent:\r\n-.5in;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n200%;font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">ii)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Any other relief which the Applicants are\r\nentitled for under the Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Act, 2016 and\r\nthe Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-32.25pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>',8320505.00,7261148.00,'2010-07-24 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>..</p>','1','','2007-04-24 00:00:00','2008-04-10 00:00:00','Unit No. TVM-L2-F08-802 ‘The Views’ at Mohali Hills, Sector-105, SAS Nagar, District Mohali, Punjab.','','',2,0,0,0,'sundeepsinghpawar','2019-01-07 13:05:01.000','sundeepsinghpawar','2019-01-07 13:05:01.000'),(810,1250,'1250',1010,'a182232b-88d6-4711-8baa-f8a026fb675f','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-01-08 10:17:05.000','JAGDEEP SINGH and HARJEET KAUR','lawofficeofhimanshuraj@gmail.com',9988100005,0,512717894060,'#102, Sector 10 A','',6,128,'160011','1','#102, Sector 10 A','',6,128,'160011','HIMANSHU RAJ','lawofficeofhimanshuraj@gmail.com',9988200001,1724190909,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0240','MUIRWOODS','Altus Space Builders Private Limited','altusoffice@yahoo.co.in',0,1724003734,'SCO 22','1ST FLOOR, PHASE 10',28,507,'160062','1','SCO 22','1ST FLOOR, PHASE 10',28,507,'160062','1','<p>The complainants booked a plot measuring 250 SQ. YARD at OP No.1s project MUIRWOODS on 24.04.2012 through OP No.1s Channel Partner, AJEET ASSOCIATES i.e. OP no.2. The complainants paid the booking amount to OP no.2 and entered into an AGREEMENT TO SELL but the agreement didnt have any information regarding the date of possession of the unit. That the OP No.1 received CLU for the said project on 25.06.2013 and Layout plan was approved on 08.05.2014 but OP had already demanded and accepted more than 25 per cent of the total consideration without entering into a plot buyer agreement and getting approvals from the authority, which is a direct violation of PAPRA and amounts to unfair trade practice.</p><p>That on 05.09.2014, the OP no.1 executed a PLOT BUYERS AGREEMENT with the complainants and promised that the possession including all the amenities will be handed over to the complainants by 05.09.2017,&nbsp; 30 months plus 6 months from the date of agreement, but OP No.1 failed to do so. That numerous times, OP no.1 demanded money against the said plot from the complainants without achieving any milestones as far as the development of the project is concerned.&nbsp;</p><p>That on 13.10.2017, Op no.1 furnished an Offer of possession letter to the complainants without even completing 10 per cent of the total project. The complainants wrote a letter to Op no.1 against the offer of possession and stated all the shortcomings of the project but OP No.1 just re issued a new offer of possession letter to the complainants without completing its project which is still under developed. That it has been more than 6 YEARS from the date of actual booking of the unit but there is absolutely no sign of development. The complainants have already paid more than the total consideration against the said property.</p><p>Therefore, the complainant craves the indulgence of the Honble RERA authority to hand to direct the OP No.1 and 2 to refund the entire amount as per the RERA CENTRAL ACT AND RERA STATE RULES.</p>','<p>1.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To direct the OP No.1 and Op no.2, being jointly and severally liable to compensate the complainants in the shape of refund of the complete amount which has been deposited against the residential property so booked by the complainants along with an Interest on the amount from the date of deposit at the rate of 20 per cent&nbsp; till the actual realization of the complete amount within 90 days according to section 18 1 Real Estate Regulation And Development Act, 2016, 18 2 Real Estate&nbsp; Regulation And Development Act, 2016, Section 19 4 of The Real Estate Regulation And Development Act, 2016, r w Rule 16 and Rule 17 of Punjab State Real Estate Regulation and Development Rules, 2017</p><p><br></p><p>2.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To direct the OP No.1 and Op no.2, being jointly and severally liable to pay Rs. 20,00,000&nbsp; for causing mental agony caused to the complainants.</p><p><br></p><p>3.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To direct the OP No.1 and Op no.2, being jointly and severally liable to pay Rs. 14,00,000 to the complainants as the deficiency in services for keeping the complainants in dark in regard to the progress of the property.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>4.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To direct the OP No.1 and Op no.2, being jointly and severally liable to pay Rs. 14,00,000&nbsp; for causing physical harassment caused to the complainants.</p><p><br></p><p>5.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To direct the OP No.1 and Op no.2, being jointly and severally liable to pay Rs. 1,00,000 as litigation cost as the complainants were constrained to file the same because of the callous and indifferent attitude of the opposite parties.</p><p>6.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To revoke the license of the OP No.1 under section 7 of the Real Estate Regulation and Development act, 2016.</p><p><br></p><p>7.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To impose heavy penalty on Op no.2 for doing business a Real Estate Agent without getting itself registered with RERA under Section 9 of Real Estate regulation and Development Act, 2016.</p><p><br></p><p>8.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Any other relief or claim which the Honble Authority deems appropriate.</p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Not Prayed</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'lawofficeofhimanshuraj','2019-01-07 13:51:55.000','lawofficeofhimanshuraj','2019-01-07 13:51:55.000'),(811,1251,'1251',1312,'6192c304-cccb-4808-870c-b203098a180a','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Charanjeet Singh Bagga','csbkb1983@gmail.com',9424492156,0,0,'Juniper 403, Ansal Woodbury Apartments','High Land Marg, Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','1','Juniper 403, Ansal Woodbury Apartments','High Land Marg, Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAA79-PR0044','ANDC','WWW','DDD@SSDD.OOO',0,0,'KKK','',10,120,'110001','1','KKK','',10,120,'110001','1','<p><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">Project Registration with RERA U/s 5.3 valid for the period, declared\r\nby the builder U/s 4.2.l.C in Form B. AHCL willfully omitted project completion date, see\r\nAnnexure A; resulting in:Open registration, requiring no further extension of\r\nthe project, and RWA is unable to claim the possession of common areas.After\r\ngetting login ID, AHCL created neither web page on RERA Punjab site nor entered\r\nproject details as sought by RERA in cir. 08 dated May 9, 2018 and notice\r\n09.09.2018.</span><br></p>','<p>www</p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>www</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',1,0,0,0,'csbkb','2019-01-07 16:00:49.000','csbkb','2019-01-07 16:00:49.000'),(812,1252,'1252',1322,'f69298e2-8ace-47aa-9c57-18b058cdc701','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Munish Chajgotra','munishsinghlion@gmail.com',9419118586,0,0,'87/3, sharika vihar, lower roopnagar','Jammu',15,267,'180013','1','87/3, sharika vihar, lower roopnagar','Jammu',15,267,'180013','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0106','MONA CITYHOMES','RENU JASWAL,  KAPIL','renu@mtplgroup.in',7696266800,0,'KL Road,sector 115, Mohali','Punjab',28,507,'140307','1','KL Road,sector 115, Mohali','Punjab',28,507,'140307','1','<p>Dear san,</p><div style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small;\">1.The begining of the deal, on first day when I visited at Monacity homes in the month of July 2018, its in the knowledge of the sales girl(Manpreet) &amp; her Manager( Mr. Mayank)that I am going to finance from canara bank. they said that its their duty to get the tie up with Canara bank and I have to book the flat only. The tie up with the said bank will be in process and get done in next 15 days.I visited two times again at Monacity homes in next 15 days and the topic was same..Tie up with Canara bank.</div><div style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small;\">2. On 19 August, I had called up at Monacity homes for Booking of the Unit. before booking i again take confirmation from Ms. Manpreet/Mr. Mayank regarding the Tie up with the canara bank and the reply was\" AAP BAS BOOKING KARWAO, WOH HAMARA KAAM HAI, WOH HO JAYEGA\" . I booked on the same day with 1,00,000/- transfered to Monacity homes account.&nbsp;</div><div style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small;\">3. On 23 september I had visited Monacity for agreement and submission of balance payment of Rs,2,80,000/-. Before sign of agreement and transfer of balancce 2,80,000/- I again checked for Tie up of canara bank. and I got the same reply from them that it will done in next 15 days. Mr. Kapil offered me the finance facility from Mona end but as already mentioned that my finance from Canara is pre sanctioned.</div><div style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small;\"><div>4. It is since last 3 months the tie up is in process and every time I am getting a new excuse from your end that the tie up is in process.</div><div>5. I had visited 7-8 times at Monacity homes after submission of 3,80,000/- as the possesion date commited by the mona authorities is 20th Nov 2018.</div><div>6. This is almost 2 months passed, I had submitted the sanction letter to your sales persons. but still the tie up is not done.</div><div>7. I had already requested to MTPL authorities for the refund but tey are making excuses.</div><div>8. I was interested to own a flat in Monacity but due to tie up issue its not done, results in a harrasment for me as I am travelling daily Amritsar-Chandigarh-Amritsar since last 45 days due to my job schedule.</div></div>','<p>Dear San,,</p><p>Please help me to get refund of my Booking amount for rs. 3,80,000/- as they are making excuses of 180 days and deduction of charges as there is nothing pending from my end nor any fault from my end.</p><p>I had taken the possesion somewhere else and now am not in position to take a add on flat. so it is requested to the RERA authorities to Please help me . I ned only refund of My booking amount for Rs. 3,80,000/-</p><p><br></p><p><br></p>',3800000.00,380000.00,'2018-11-20 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Refund of money</p>','1','','2019-08-16 00:00:00','2018-09-24 00:00:00','C208, Mona city Homes, sec-115, Mohali','','',1,0,0,0,'Munishchajgotra9','2019-01-07 17:23:16.000','Munishchajgotra9','2019-01-07 17:23:16.000'),(813,1253,'1253',1322,'f69298e2-8ace-47aa-9c57-18b058cdc701','FormTypeM',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Munish Chajgotra','munishsinghlion@gmail.com',9419118586,0,0,'87/3, sharika vihar, lower roopnagar','Jammu',15,267,'180013','1','87/3, sharika vihar, lower roopnagar','Jammu',15,267,'180013','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0106','MONA CITYHOMES','RENU JASWAL,  KAPIL','renu@mtplgroup.in',7696266800,0,'KL Road,sector 115, Mohali','Punjab',28,507,'140307','1','KL Road,sector 115, Mohali','Punjab',28,507,'140307','1','Dear san,\r\n<div>1.The begining of the deal, on first day when I visited at Monacity homes in the month of July 2018, its in the knowledge of the sales girl(Manpreet) &amp; her Manager( Mr. Mayank)that I am going to finance from canara bank. they said that its their duty to get the tie up with Canara bank and I have to book the flat only. The tie up with the said bank will be in process and get done in next 15 days.I visited two times again at Monacity homes in next 15 days and the topic was same..Tie up with Canara bank.\r\n</div><div>2. On 19 August, I had called up at Monacity homes for Booking of the Unit. before booking i again take confirmation from Ms. Manpreet/Mr. Mayank regarding the Tie up with the canara bank and the reply was\" AAP BAS BOOKING KARWAO, WOH HAMARA KAAM HAI, WOH HO JAYEGA\" . I booked on the same day with 1,00,000/- transfered to Monacity homes account. \r\n</div><div>3. On 23 september I had visited Monacity for agreement and submission of balance payment of Rs,2,80,000/-. Before sign of agreement and transfer of balancce 2,80,000/- I again checked for Tie up of canara bank. and I got the same reply from them that it will done in next 15 days. Mr. Kapil offered me the finance facility from Mona end but as already mentioned that my finance from Canara is pre sanctioned.\r\n</div><div>4. It is since last 3 months the tie up is in process and every time I am getting a new excuse from your end that the tie up is in process.\r\n</div><div>5. I had visited 7-8 times at Monacity homes after submission of 3,80,000/- as the possesion date commited by the mona authorities is 20th Nov 2018.\r\n</div><div>6. This is almost 2 months passed, I had submitted the sanction letter to your sales persons. but still the tie up is not done.\r\n</div><div>7. I had already requested to MTPL authorities for the refund but tey are making excuses.\r\n</div><div>8. I was interested to own a flat in Monacity but due to tie up issue its not done,results in a harrasment for me as I am travelling daily Amritsar-Chandigarh-Amritsar since last 45 days due to my job schedule</div>','<p style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0cm\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">Dear San,,<o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin: 0cm 0cm 7.5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">Please\r\nhelp me to get refund of my Booking amount for rs. 3,80,000/- as they are\r\nmaking excuses of 180 days and deduction of charges as there is nothing pending\r\nfrom my end nor any fault from my end.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin: 0cm 0cm 7.5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">I\r\nhad taken the possesion somewhere else and now am not in position to take a add\r\non flat. so it is requested to the RERA authorities to Please help me . I ned\r\nonly refund of My booking amount for Rs. 3,80,000/-<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>',3800000.00,380000.00,'2018-11-20 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Refund of Booking amount</p>','1','','2018-09-19 00:00:00','2018-09-24 00:00:00','C208, mona city homes, sec 115, mohali','','',2,0,0,0,'Munishchajgotra9','2019-01-07 17:35:09.000','Munishchajgotra9','2019-01-07 17:35:09.000'),(814,1254,'1254',1312,'6192c304-cccb-4808-870c-b203098a180a','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Charanjeet Singh Bagga','csbkb1983@gmail.com',9424492156,0,0,'Juniper 403, Ansal Woodbury Apartments','High Land Marg, Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','1','Juniper 403, Ansal Woodbury Apartments','High Land Marg, Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0044','WOODB','ANSALSS','KJSUS@CDDSLS.COM',0,0,'SSSSS','',10,120,'110001','1','SSSSS','',10,120,'110001','1','<p><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:\r\n115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\r\ncolor:#1F497D;mso-themecolor:text2;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN;mso-fareast-language:\r\nEN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\">Project Registration is valid for the period\r\ndeclared by builder in Form B. AHCL wilfully omitted project completion date,\r\nsee Annexure A; resulting in:Open registration, requiring no further extension\r\nof the project, and RWA is unable to claim the possession of common areas.After\r\ngetting login ID, AHCL created neither web page on RERA Punjab site nor entered\r\nproject details as sought by RERA in cir. 08 dated 09/05/18 and notice 09.09.18.</span><br></p>','<p>MMMMMMMMMM</p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>MMMMMMM</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'csbkb','2019-01-07 17:54:38.000','csbkb','2019-01-07 17:54:38.000'),(815,1253,'1253',1322,'f69298e2-8ace-47aa-9c57-18b058cdc701','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-01-07 18:33:02.000','Munish Chajgotra','munishsinghlion@gmail.com',9419118586,0,0,'87/3, sharika vihar, lower roopnagar','Jammu',15,267,'180013','1','87/3, sharika vihar, lower roopnagar','Jammu',15,267,'180013','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0106','MONA CITYHOMES','RENU JASWAL,  KAPIL','renu@mtplgroup.in',7696266800,0,'KL Road,sector 115, Mohali','Punjab',28,507,'140307','1','KL Road,sector 115, Mohali','Punjab',28,507,'140307','1','Dear san,\r\n<div>1.The begining of the deal, on first day when I visited at Monacity homes in the month of July 2018, its in the knowledge of the sales girl(Manpreet) &amp; her Manager( Mr. Mayank)that I am going to finance from canara bank. they said that its their duty to get the tie up with Canara bank and I have to book the flat only. The tie up with the said bank will be in process and get done in next 15 days.I visited two times again at Monacity homes in next 15 days and the topic was same..Tie up with Canara bank.\r\n</div><div>2. On 19 August, I had called up at Monacity homes for Booking of the Unit. before booking i again take confirmation from Ms. Manpreet/Mr. Mayank regarding the Tie up with the canara bank and the reply was\" AAP BAS BOOKING KARWAO, WOH HAMARA KAAM HAI, WOH HO JAYEGA\" . I booked on the same day with 1,00,000/- transfered to Monacity homes account. \r\n</div><div>3. On 23 september I had visited Monacity for agreement and submission of balance payment of Rs,2,80,000/-. Before sign of agreement and transfer of balancce 2,80,000/- I again checked for Tie up of canara bank. and I got the same reply from them that it will done in next 15 days. Mr. Kapil offered me the finance facility from Mona end but as already mentioned that my finance from Canara is pre sanctioned.\r\n</div><div>4. It is since last 3 months the tie up is in process and every time I am getting a new excuse from your end that the tie up is in process.\r\n</div><div>5. I had visited 7-8 times at Monacity homes after submission of 3,80,000/- as the possesion date commited by the mona authorities is 20th Nov 2018.\r\n</div><div>6. This is almost 2 months passed, I had submitted the sanction letter to your sales persons. but still the tie up is not done.\r\n</div><div>7. I had already requested to MTPL authorities for the refund but tey are making excuses.\r\n</div><div>8. I was interested to own a flat in Monacity but due to tie up issue its not done,results in a harrasment for me as I am travelling daily Amritsar-Chandigarh-Amritsar since last 45 days due to my job schedule</div>','<p style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0cm\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">Dear San,,<o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin: 0cm 0cm 7.5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">Please\r\nhelp me to get refund of my Booking amount for rs. 3,80,000/- as they are\r\nmaking excuses of 180 days and deduction of charges as there is nothing pending\r\nfrom my end nor any fault from my end.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin: 0cm 0cm 7.5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">I\r\nhad taken the possesion somewhere else and now am not in position to take a add\r\non flat. so it is requested to the RERA authorities to Please help me . I ned\r\nonly refund of My booking amount for Rs. 3,80,000/-<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>',3800000.00,380000.00,'2018-11-20 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Refund of Booking amount</p>','1','','2018-09-19 00:00:00','2018-09-24 00:00:00','C208, mona city homes, sec 115, mohali','','',2,0,0,0,'Munishchajgotra9','2019-01-07 17:58:03.000','Munishchajgotra9','2019-01-07 17:58:03.000'),(816,1254,'1254',1312,'6192c304-cccb-4808-870c-b203098a180a','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Charanjeet Singh Bagga','csbkb1983@gmail.com',9424492156,0,0,'Juniper 403, Ansal Woodbury Apartments','High Land Marg, Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','1','Juniper 403, Ansal Woodbury Apartments','High Land Marg, Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0044','WOODB','ANSALSS','KJSUS@CDDSLS.COM',0,0,'SSSSS','',10,120,'110001','1','SSSSS','',10,120,'110001','1','<p><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:\r\n115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\r\ncolor:#1F497D;mso-themecolor:text2;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN;mso-fareast-language:\r\nEN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\">Project Registration is valid for the period\r\ndeclared by builder in Form B. AHCL willfully omitted project completion date,\r\nsee Annexure A; resulting in:Open registration, requiring no further extension\r\nof the project, and RWA is unable to claim the possession of common areas.After\r\ngetting login ID, AHCL created neither web page on RERA Punjab site nor entered\r\nproject details as sought by RERA in cir. 08 dt. 09/05/18 and notice 09.09.18.</span></p><p><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:\r\n115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\r\ncolor:#1F497D;mso-themecolor:text2;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN;mso-fareast-language:\r\nEN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 115%;\">Possession\r\ngranted to buyers on the pretext that all approvals and clearances are in\r\nplace.By&nbsp;</span><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 115%;\">claiming project completion in 2012, it also secured\r\nHigh Court order for issuance of completion certificate expeditiously see\r\nannexure D. Deviations observed in its letter DTP.SS14/1204 dt. 14.07.14 by Town Planning Wing, Local Bodies Dept. while RWA letter No. 52\r\ndt. 31.10.18 forwarded by it to MC Zirakpur, reveals violation of Supreme\r\nCourt Order in Civil Appeal No. 2544 of 2010 page 14 para 39:\r\n…<b><i>.\r\nstilt parking space/s being part of ‘common areas\'… Such stilt parking space….\r\nis not sellable at all</i></b>. &nbsp;See Annexure E, F and G, respectively.Consumer Forum, Punjab&nbsp;judgement dt. Feb 2,\r\n2018 states:&nbsp;<b><i>The completion certificate is not issued by competent\r\nauthority because the builder has made deviations, violations in construction;\r\nit is his duty to rectify those deviations or bring the deviations within\r\npermissible limits.&nbsp;</i></b>See Annexure H. A sister concern of AHCL,\r\nprovides essential services against hefty maintenance fees,&nbsp;while\r\ndelivering poor services. AHCL never responded to our concerns. Such\r\nindifferent&nbsp;attitude forced residents to unanimously hold back quarterly\r\npayment, in protest.&nbsp;Maintenance by builder is allowed by RERA before\r\nhanding over of project to RWA by charging only reasonable charges.Maintenance\r\nby RWA will be exempted vide SN. 77, page 19 of GST Notification dated June 28,\r\n2017, see Annexure N; andMaintenance charges for unsold flats presently being\r\nborne by the allottees.</span><br></span><br></p>','<p>MMMMMMMMMM</p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>MMMMMMM</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',1,0,0,0,'csbkb','2019-01-07 18:00:29.000','csbkb','2019-01-07 18:00:29.000'),(817,1255,'1255',1312,'6192c304-cccb-4808-870c-b203098a180a','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Charanjeet Singh Bagga','csbkb1983@gmail.com',9424492156,0,0,'Juniper 403, Ansal Woodbury Apartments','High Land Marg, Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','1','Juniper 403, Ansal Woodbury Apartments','High Land Marg, Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0044','ANSALA','ANSALS','KUSHAGR@ANSAL.COM',0,0,'SSAKAKS','',10,120,'110001','1','SSAKAKS','',10,120,'110001','1','<p><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:\r\n115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:Calibri;\r\nmso-fareast-theme-font:minor-latin;color:#1F497D;mso-themecolor:text2;\r\nmso-ansi-language:EN-IN;mso-fareast-language:EN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\">Possession\r\ngranted to buyers on the pretext that all approvals and clearances are in\r\nplace. By</span><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\r\ncolor:#1F497D;mso-themecolor:text2;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN;mso-fareast-language:\r\nEN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\"> claiming project completion in 2012, it also secured\r\nHigh Court order for issuance of completion certificate expeditiously see\r\nannexure D. Certain deviations observed in its letter DTP.SS14/1204 dated\r\n14.07.14 by Town Planning Wing, Local Bodies Dept. while RWA letter No. 52\r\ndated 31.10.18 forwarded by it to MC Zirakpur, reveals violation of Supreme\r\nCourt Order in Civil Appeal No. 2544 of 2010 on Common Areas on page 14 para 39:\r\n…<b><i>.\r\nstilt parking space/s being part of ‘common areas\'… Such stilt parking space….\r\nis not sellable at all</i></b>. &nbsp;See Annexures\r\nE, F and G, respectively.&nbsp;Consumer Forum, Punjab&nbsp;judgement dt. Feb 2,\r\n2018 states:&nbsp;<b><i>The completion certificate is not issued by competent\r\nauthority because the builder has made deviations, violations in construction;\r\nit is his duty to rectify those deviations or bring the deviations within\r\npermissible limits.&nbsp;</i></b>See Annexure H.</span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<br></p>','<p>MMMMM&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>MMMMMMMM</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'csbkb','2019-01-07 20:10:24.000','csbkb','2019-01-07 20:10:24.000'),(818,1255,'1255',1312,'6192c304-cccb-4808-870c-b203098a180a','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Charanjeet Singh Bagga','csbkb1983@gmail.com',9424492156,0,0,'Juniper 403, Ansal Woodbury Apartments','High Land Marg, Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','1','Juniper 403, Ansal Woodbury Apartments','High Land Marg, Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0044','ANSALA','ANSALS','KUSHAGR@ANSAL.COM',0,0,'SSAKAKS','',10,120,'110001','1','SSAKAKS','',10,120,'110001','1','<p><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:\r\n115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:Calibri;\r\nmso-fareast-theme-font:minor-latin;color:#1F497D;mso-themecolor:text2;\r\nmso-ansi-language:EN-IN;mso-fareast-language:EN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\">Possession\r\ngranted to buyers on the pretext that all approvals and clearances are in\r\nplace. By</span><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\r\ncolor:#1F497D;mso-themecolor:text2;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN;mso-fareast-language:\r\nEN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\"> claiming project completion in 2012, it also secured\r\nHigh Court order for issuance of completion certificate expeditiously see\r\nannexure D. Certain deviations observed in its letter DTP.SS14/1204 dt. 14.07.14 by Town Planning Wing, Local Bodies Dept. while RWA letter No. 52\r\ndated 31.10.18 forwarded by it to MC Zirakpur, reveals violation of Supreme\r\nCourt Order in Civil Appeal No. 2544 of 2010 on Common Areas on page 14 para 39:\r\n…<b><i>.\r\nstilt parking space/s being part of ‘common areas\'… Such stilt parking space….\r\nis not sellable at all</i></b>. &nbsp;See Annexures\r\nE, F and G, respectively.&nbsp;Consumer Forum, Punjab&nbsp;judgement dt. 02/2/18 states:&nbsp;<b><i>The completion certificate is not issued by competent\r\nauthority because the builder has made deviations, violations in construction;\r\nit is his duty to rectify those deviations or bring the deviations within\r\npermissible limits.&nbsp;</i></b>See Annexure H.</span><span style=\"color: rgb(31, 73, 125); font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 12pt;\">Its sister concern provides essential services\r\nagainst hefty maintenance fees,&nbsp;while delivering poor services. AHCL never\r\nresponded to our concerns. Such indifferent&nbsp;attitude forced residents to\r\nunanimously hold back quarterly payment, in protest.&nbsp;Maintenance by\r\nbuilder is allowed by charging only reasonable charges.Maintenance by RWA will\r\nbe exempted vide SN. 77, page 19 of GST Notification dt. 28/06/17, see Annexure\r\nN; andMaintenance charges for unsold flats presently being borne by the\r\nallottees.</span><span style=\"color: rgb(31, 73, 125); font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 12pt;\">This is forming approximately 35 percent of the\r\nexisting charges, which in no way may be considered reasonable.</span>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</p>','<p>MMMMM&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>MMMMMMMM</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'csbkb','2019-01-07 20:16:59.000','csbkb','2019-01-07 20:16:59.000'),(819,1255,'1255',1312,'6192c304-cccb-4808-870c-b203098a180a','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Charanjeet Singh Bagga','csbkb1983@gmail.com',9424492156,0,0,'Juniper 403, Ansal Woodbury Apartments','High Land Marg, Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','1','Juniper 403, Ansal Woodbury Apartments','High Land Marg, Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0044','ANSALA','ANSALS','KUSHAGR@ANSAL.COM',0,0,'SSAKAKS','',10,120,'110001','1','SSAKAKS','',10,120,'110001','1','<p><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:\r\n115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:Calibri;\r\nmso-fareast-theme-font:minor-latin;color:#1F497D;mso-themecolor:text2;\r\nmso-ansi-language:EN-IN;mso-fareast-language:EN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\">Possession\r\ngranted to buyers on the pretext that all approvals and clearances are in\r\nplace. By</span><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New