round-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">I booked a residential flat\r\n(Flat No. WG/H/0502) in Wave Garden, Sector 85, Mohali as per allotment letter\r\nDtd. 24/11/2012. As per Clause 5.1 of the allotment letter, possession of the\r\nflat was to be given by the builder within 36 months of the allotment i.e. upto\r\nNovember 2015. I have made total payment of Rs. 79,85,207/- towards the cost of\r\nFlat as per the demand of the builder. I wrote various letters, mails and had\r\ntelephonic conversation time to time to the company staff, to know about the\r\nstatus of the project. Company never responded and also never confirmed the\r\ndate of possession. Even after lapse of 6 years, project is still incomplete.\r\nFinally I vide my registered letter Dtd 26/07/2018, requested the company to\r\ncancel my flat booking and refund the total amount paid by me with interest but\r\nthe company is neither responding nor refunding the money.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">1) Refund of\r\ntotal money deposited/paid by me to the Company against booking of Flat No.\r\nWG/H/0502.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">2) Payment of\r\nInterest @ 24% p.a. on the amount deposited/paid by me to the Company.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">3) Payment of\r\ncompensation as per RERA Rules.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">4) Any other\r\nrelief as the Honourable Regulatory authority deem fit.&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p>',8786975.00,7985207.00,'2015-11-24 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: roboto, serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">As per reliefs sought in Point\r\nNo 5 above.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','1','','2012-11-24 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','WG/H/0502, Wave Garden, SAS Nagar, Mohali','','',2,0,0,0,'PravinAgrawal','2019-01-12 12:02:10.000','PravinAgrawal','2019-01-12 12:02:10.000'),(847,1238,'1238',1316,'04ea4248-150e-4148-81b6-34afe1ec1b06','FormTypeM',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Kamal Makkar','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9729902009,0,358412254419,'424 Sector 20 Kaithal','',13,9,'136027','1','424 Sector 20 Kaithal','',13,9,'136027','Kamal Dahiya','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9729902009,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0121','Purab Premium Apartments','Greater Mohali Area Development Authority','ce@gmada.gov.in',1722215512,0,'PUDA Bhawan Sector 62 District SAS Nagar Mohali ','',28,507,'160062','1','PUDA Bhawan Sector 62 District SAS Nagar Mohali ','',28,507,'160062','1','<p>Respondent opened scheme for public from 12.12.2011 to 12.01.2012 asAnnexureC-1. The depicted salient features asAnnexureC-2. Respondent informed vide letter dated 23.03.2012 that the waiting list no. is 65 and complainant to submit the documents before 23/04/2012AnnexureC-3. Letter of intent for allotment was issued on 21.05.2012 and tentative price was Rs 55,00,000. As per Para 3(II) delivery within a period of 36 months from the date of issuance of the said letter. Possession date was 21.05.2015 i.e. delayed by 3 years and 7 monthsAnnexureC-4. Payment plan B was opted by the complainantAnnexureC-4(Pg 40). Initial amount of INR 11,00,000 paid vide cheque on 16.06.2012AnnexureC-5(Pg41). Total amount paid Rs54, 25,746/- i.e. 98% out of the total consideration till 21.04.2016 AnnexureC-5. After 5 years the complainant was allotted with apartment no.1502, Tower-5, BlockD, Floor14 with 2563.19 sq. ft. area including common stairs and car parking area on 11.10.2017 and the possession was also offeredAnnexureC-6. Thereafter the complainant visited site and found that layout plan has changed without taking the consent of 2/3rd allottees and also found many loopholes in the construction like compromised quality of materials etc. The complainant got the construction inspected by Registered Council of Architecture, New Delhi. Many differences were found as inAnnexureC-7. The complainant intimated such defects to the Estate Officer of GMADA vide letter dated 17.05.2018 and requested for refund of his paid amount but respondent didn’t respondAnnexureC-8. Other allottees also found several defects, deficiencies and deviations in the projectAnnexureC-9(Pg93). Several allottees raised the issues before the press conference(Pg 94-95). The government ordered to remove the defaults but respondent did not comply to repair the faults(Pg 96-97). Fire safety has been expired(Pg 98-99). The lifts are also not safe and stops to work. Many times someone stops in the elevator(Pg 100-102).</p>','<p>In view of the facts mentioned in preceding paragraphs, the complainant prays for the following relief(s):-&nbsp;</p><p>i.To give necessary directions to the respondents for refund the amount paid by the complainant with prescribed interest till realization as per the provisions of Sec. 18 and Sec.19(4)of the RERA Act read with Rule 16 of PSRE(R&amp;D)Rules, 2017.</p><p>ii.To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 60 of RERA Act for willful default committed by them.</p><p>iii.To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 61 of RERA Act for contravention of Sec.12, Sec.14, and Sec. 16 of RERA Act.</p><p>iv.To issue directions to make liable every officer concerned i.e. Director, Manager, Secretary, or any other officer of the respondent’s company at whose instance, connivance, acquiescence, neglect any of the offences has been committed as mentioned in Sec.69 of RERA Act,2016 to be read with Punjab RERA Rules,2017.</p><p>v.To recommend criminal action against the respondents for the criminal offence of cheating, fraud and criminal breach of trust under section 420,406 and 409 of the Indian Penal Code.</p><p>vi.To issue direction to pay the cost of litigation.</p><p>vii.To issue direction to pay the compensation to complainant for compensation for his mental agony, pain and harassment.</p><p>viii.Any other relief which this Hon’ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances of this complaint.</p><div><br></div>',55000.00,5425746.00,'2015-05-21 00:00:00.000','2015-05-21 00:00:00.000','<p>i.To direct the respondent not to demand any further amount whatsoever from the complainant.</p><p>ii.The respondent should be restrained from harassing the complainant in any manner whatsoever.</p><p>iii.Any other interim relief which this Hon’ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances of this complaint.</p><div><br></div>','1','','2017-10-11 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Apartment No 1502 Tower 5 Block D Floor 14 Type 2 Sector 88 Sahibzada Ajit Singh Nagar Punjab 140308','','',2,0,0,0,'kamalmakkar1','2019-01-12 12:25:04.000','kamalmakkar1','2019-01-12 12:25:04.000'),(848,1235,'1235',1312,'6192c304-cccb-4808-870c-b203098a180a','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-31 11:12:26.000','Charanjeet Singh Bagga','csbkb1983@gmail.com',9424492156,0,435060324845,'Juniper 403, Ansal Woodbury Apartments','High Land Marg, Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','1','Juniper 403, Ansal Woodbury Apartments','High Land Marg, Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','Yogesh Pathak','yogeshpathak@hotmail.com',9041639575,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0044','Ansal Woodbury Apartments ','Ansal Housing and Construction Ltd.','kushagr.ansal@ansals.com',0,0,'15 UGF Indra Prakash','21 Barakhamba Road',10,120,'110001','1','15 UGF Indra Prakash','21 Barakhamba Road',10,120,'110001','1','<p><font face=\"Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.6667px;\">As per the rules, registration of a Project with RERA expires on the date, which a builder declares for completion in Form B. In our case, the builder i.e. AHCL wilfully omitted the completion date twice, see Appendix I.A and I.B; resulting in ‘Open Registration’ needing no further extension and also leaving no scope for RWA for claiming the possession of common areas.</span></font></p><p><font face=\"Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.6667px;\">Even after getting login ID, AHCL did not create any web page on PB RERA site, hence kept away from entering project details thereon; despite PB RERA reminders vide cir. No.08 dt. 09.05.18 and notice dt. 09.09.18.</span></font></p><p><font face=\"Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.6667px;\">The builder granted possession of flats to buyers, pretending that all approvals are in place. Also, by claiming that project got completed in 2012, it secured High Court orders for issuance of completion certificate, expeditiously; see Appendix II. On the contrary, Punjab Urban Local Bodies Directorate, Chandigarh pointed out several deviations/violations from original plan. Various court judgements/orders including those of Supreme Court of India and State Consumer Forum, Punjab support their contention, see appendix III, IV, V and VI.&nbsp;</span></font></p><p><font face=\"Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.6667px;\">Neither the AHCL nor its sister concern, which is providing the essential services in our complex, respond to our complaints, made repeatedly against highly poor services. Such an indifferent attitude forced the residents to unanimously decide for holding of quarterly payment, in protest. Reasonable maintenance amount is allowed to be charged by the builder during intervening period. However, the most unfortunate part in our case is that the allottees are paying the maintenance for even the unsold flats for several years. While this is also a point to be noted that amount incurred by RWA in hiring maintenance services are exempted from GST vide Notification of 28.06.17, see Appendix VII. Aggregate of above said maintenance and instance of GST, is forming approximately 35.0 percent of the current charges.</span></font></p><div><br></div>','<ol><li><b><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Information in contravenes to the Section 4:&nbsp;</span></b><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Failure of the promoter to\r\ncomply with the instruction given in respect of&nbsp; Specific date of\r\ncompletion of the project has been dealt with under Section 60 of the RERA\r\n2016. The RERA Punjab is requested to take a note of failure of the promoter to\r\ncomply with the above instructions and on persistence, requested to take a view, suitably.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><b>Promoter’s\r\nobligation of disclosure:&nbsp;&nbsp;</b>Failure of the promoter to comply with\r\nthe orders for up loading of information on website within 3 weeks has been\r\ndealt with under Section 63 of the RERA 2016. If the same still persist, the RERA Punjab is requested to\r\ntake a note of failure of the promoter to comply its orders and requested to\r\ntake a view, suitably.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><b>Project deficiencies:&nbsp;</b>In compliance to the\r\nobligations, responsibilities and functions as per section 11.4.a of the\r\nCentral Real Estate&nbsp; Act 2016, the builder may kindly be directed to\r\ncomplete the shortcomings in respect of the project.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><b>Completion Certificate</b>&nbsp;:\r\nAs per section 11.4.b of the Central Real Estate Act 2016 and the Rule 9.1.i of\r\nPunjab RERA 2017, the builder may kindly be directed obtain Completion Certificate\r\nwithin the time specified by RERA Punjab.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><b>Recognition of RWA</b>:&nbsp; As\r\nper section 11.4.e of the Central Real Estate Act 2016:&nbsp;<b>&nbsp;The\r\npromoter shall be responsible for enabling the formation of association,\r\nsociety&nbsp;or coop. society, as the case may be, of&nbsp; allottees or a\r\nfederation of the same, ........within a period of&nbsp;three months of the\r\nmajority of allottees have booked their plot, apartment.......&nbsp;</b>Hence,\r\nthe builder may kindly be directed to recognize and transfer the project to the\r\nalready formed RWA.</span><br></li></ol>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Going by the facts detailed in para 4 above and the fact that in absence\r\nof Completion Certificate/Occupancy Certificate, execution of transfer\r\ndocuments for common areas in favor of RWA is not possible. Pending final\r\ndecision on the requests sought detailed in para 5 the complainant seeks the\r\nissuance of the following interim order&nbsp;<i>as per Section 36 of RERA 2016</i>:</span></p><ol><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">The\r\nbuilder be directed to handover maintenance function of the complex to the\r\nresidents’ welfare association, formed by them and registered with the\r\nRegistrar Cooperative Societies, Punjab.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Roboto;\">Directing the respondent to ensure continuation of the\r\nservices and maintenance, as are being provided by the maintenance agency\r\nSunrise Estate Management Services, during intervening period of transfer\r\nprocess, free of cost.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Roboto;\">The&nbsp;respondent be barred from any further recovery\r\nof charges on account of services and maintenance from the flat owners.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Roboto;\">The\r\nrespondent be directed to make payment of the services and maintenance charges\r\nof unsold flats to RWA.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Roboto;\">The respondent be directed to obtain and furnish\r\nCompletion Certificate/ Occupancy Certificate within the time specified by the\r\nRERA Punjab.</span><br></li></ol>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'csbkb','2019-01-12 16:39:11.000','csbkb','2019-01-12 16:39:11.000'),(849,1267,'1267',1338,'a14a6627-fb57-4589-90fb-ac52fbab3bc2','FormTypeM',1,1,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','PRAVIN AGRAWAL','pravin_baa@yahoo.com',9648227755,0,0,'15/79(2)','CIVIL LINES',33,297,'208001','1','15/79(2)','CIVIL LINES',33,297,'208001','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0154','WAVE ESTATE, GROUP HOUSING 2 ','COUNTRY COLONISERS PVT LTD','rera@waveestate.in',7290015352,0,'P.O. Rayon and Silk Mills, adjoining Coca Cola Depot','GT Road, Chheharta',28,39,'143105','0','Sector 85','SAS Nagar',28,507,'160062','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: roboto, serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">I booked a residential flat\r\n(Flat No. WG/H/0502) in Wave Garden, Sector 85, Mohali as per allotment letter\r\nDtd. 24/11/2012. As per Clause 5.1 of the allotment letter, possession of the\r\nflat was to be given by the builder within 36 months of the allotment i.e. upto\r\nNovember 2015. I have made total payment of Rs. 79,85,207/- towards the cost of\r\nFlat as per the demand of the builder. I wrote various letters, mails and had\r\ntelephonic conversation time to time to the company staff, to know about the\r\nstatus of the project. Company never responded and also never confirmed the\r\ndate of possession. Even after lapse of 6 years, project is still incomplete.\r\nFinally I vide my registered letter Dtd 26/07/2018, requested the company to\r\ncancel my flat booking and refund the total amount paid by me with interest but\r\nthe company is neither responding nor refunding the money.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">1) Refund of\r\ntotal money deposited/paid by me to the Company against booking of Flat No.\r\nWG/H/0502.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">2) Payment of\r\nInterest @ 24% p.a. on the amount deposited/paid by me to the Company.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">3) Payment of\r\ncompensation as per RERA Rules.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">4) Any other\r\nrelief as the Honourable Regulatory authority deem fit.&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p>',8786975.00,7985207.00,'2015-11-24 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: roboto, serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">As per reliefs sought in Point\r\nNo 5 above.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','1','','2012-11-24 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','WG/H/0502, Wave Garden, SAS Nagar, Mohali','','',2,0,0,0,'PravinAgrawal','2019-01-12 16:42:22.000','PravinAgrawal','2019-01-12 16:42:22.000'),(850,1235,'1235',1312,'6192c304-cccb-4808-870c-b203098a180a','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-31 11:12:26.000','Charanjeet Singh Bagga','csbkb1983@gmail.com',9424492156,0,435060324845,'Juniper 403, Ansal Woodbury Apartments','High Land Marg, Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','1','Juniper 403, Ansal Woodbury Apartments','High Land Marg, Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','Yogesh Pathak','yogeshpathak@hotmail.com',9041639575,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0044','Ansal Woodbury Apartments ','Ansal Housing and Construction Ltd.','kushagr.ansal@ansals.com',0,0,'15 UGF Indra Prakash','21 Barakhamba Road',10,120,'110001','1','15 UGF Indra Prakash','21 Barakhamba Road',10,120,'110001','1','<p><font face=\"Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.6667px;\">As per the rules, registration of a Project with RERA expires on the date, which a builder declares for completion in Form B. In our case, the builder i.e. AHCL wilfully omitted the completion date twice, see Appendix I.A and I.B; resulting in ‘Open Registration’ needing no further extension and also leaving no scope for RWA for claiming the possession of common areas.</span></font></p><p><font face=\"Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.6667px;\">Even after getting login ID, AHCL did not create any web page on PB RERA site, hence kept away from entering project details thereon; despite PB RERA reminders vide cir. No.08 dt. 09.05.18 and notice dt. 09.09.18.</span></font></p><p><font face=\"Arial, sans-serif\"><spa