on of the\r\nresidents’ welfare association therein, which has already been formed and registered with the\r\nRegistrar Cooperative Societies, Punjab.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Roboto;\">Directing the respondent to ensure continuation of the\r\nservices and maintenance, as are being provided by the maintenance agency viz. Sunrise Estate Management Services, during intervening period of transfer\r\nprocess, free of cost.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Roboto;\">The&nbsp;respondent be barred from any further recovery\r\nof charges on account of services and maintenance from the flat owners.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Roboto;\">The\r\nrespondent be directed to make payment of the services and maintenance charges for unsold flats to the said agency with RWA representation therein.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Roboto;\">The Municipal Council, Zirakpur be directed to get removal of violations and completion of mandatory items within given time frame and furnish\r\nCompletion Certificate/ Occupancy Certificate to builder within the time specified by the\r\nRERA Punjab.</span><br></li></ol>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'csbkb','2019-01-12 18:41:28.000','csbkb','2019-01-12 18:41:28.000'),(855,1235,'1235',1312,'6192c304-cccb-4808-870c-b203098a180a','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-31 11:12:26.000','Charanjeet Singh Bagga','csbkb1983@gmail.com',9424492156,0,435060324845,'Juniper 403, Ansal Woodbury Apartments','High Land Marg, Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','1','Juniper 403, Ansal Woodbury Apartments','High Land Marg, Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','Yogesh Pathak','yogeshpathak@hotmail.com',9041639575,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0044','Ansal Woodbury Apartments ','Ansal Housing and Construction Ltd.','kushagr.ansal@ansals.com',0,0,'15 UGF Indra Prakash','21 Barakhamba Road',10,120,'110001','1','15 UGF Indra Prakash','21 Barakhamba Road',10,120,'110001','1','<p><font face=\"Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.6667px;\">As per the rules, registration of a Project with RERA expires on the date, which a builder declares for completion in Form B. In our case, the builder i.e. AHCL wilfully omitted the completion date twice, see Appendix I.A and I.B; resulting in ‘Open Registration’ needing no further extension and also leaving no scope for RWA for claiming the possession of common areas.</span></font></p><p><font face=\"Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.6667px;\">Even after getting login ID, AHCL did not create any web page on PB RERA site, hence kept away from entering project details thereon; despite PB RERA reminders vide cir. No.08 dt. 09.05.18 and notice dt. 09.09.18.</span></font></p><p><font face=\"Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.6667px;\">The builder granted possession of flats to buyers, pretending that all approvals are in place. Also, by claiming that project got completed in 2012, it secured High Court orders for issuance of completion certificate, expeditiously; see Appendix II. On the contrary, Punjab Urban Local Bodies Directorate, Chandigarh pointed out several deviations/violations from original plan. Various court judgements/orders including those of Supreme Court of India and State Consumer Forum, Punjab support their contention, see appendix III, IV, V and VI.&nbsp;</span></font></p><p><font face=\"Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.6667px;\">Neither the AHCL nor its sister concern, which is providing the essential services in our complex, respond to our complaints, made repeatedly against highly poor services. Such an indifferent attitude forced the residents to unanimously decide for holding of quarterly payment, in protest. Reasonable maintenance amount is allowed to be charged by the builder during intervening period. However, the most unfortunate part in our case is that the allottees are paying the maintenance for even the unsold flats for several years. While this is also a point to be noted that amount incurred by RWA in hiring maintenance services are exempted from GST vide Notification of 28.06.17, see Appendix VII. Aggregate of above said maintenance charges and instance of GST, is forming approximately 35.0 percent of the current charges.</span></font></p><div><br></div>','<ol><li><b><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Information in contravenes to the Section 4:&nbsp;</span></b><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Failure of the promoter to\r\ncomply with the instruction given in respect of&nbsp; Specific date of\r\ncompletion of the project has been dealt with under Section 60 of the RERA\r\n2016. The RERA Punjab is requested to take a note of failure of the promoter to\r\ncomply with the above instructions and on persistence, requested to take a view, suitably.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><b>Promoter’s\r\nobligation of disclosure:&nbsp;&nbsp;</b>Failure of the promoter to comply with\r\nthe orders for up loading of information on website has been\r\ndealt with under Section 63 of the RERA 2016. The RERA Punjab is requested to\r\ntake a note of failure of the promoter to comply its orders and hence requested to\r\ntake a view, suitably.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><b>Project deficiencies:&nbsp;</b>In compliance to the\r\nobligations, responsibilities and functions as per section 11.4.a of the\r\nCentral Real Estate&nbsp; Act 2016, the builder may kindly be directed to\r\ncomplete the shortcomings in respect of the project within the prescribed time by it.&nbsp;</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><b>Completion Certificate</b>&nbsp;:\r\nAs per section 11.4.b of the Central Real Estate Act 2016 and the Rule 9.1.i of\r\nPunjab RERA 2017, the builder, in addition to the orders in other judgments,&nbsp; may kindly be directed obtain Completion Certificate\r\nwithin the time specified by RERA Punjab.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><b>Recognition of RWA</b>:&nbsp; As\r\nper section 11.4.e of the Central Real Estate Act 2016:&nbsp;<b>&nbsp;The\r\npromoter shall be responsible for enabling the formation of association,\r\nsociety&nbsp;or coop. society, as the case may be, of&nbsp; allottees or a\r\nfederation of the same, ........within a period of&nbsp;three months of the\r\nmajority of allottees have booked their plot, apartment.......&nbsp;</b>Hence,\r\nthe builder may kindly be directed to recognize and transfer the project to the\r\nalready formed RWA.</span><br></li></ol>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Going by the facts detailed in para 4 above and the fact that in absence\r\nof Completion Certificate/Occupancy Certificate, execution of transfer\r\ndocuments for common areas in favor of RWA is not possible. Pending final\r\ndecision on the requests sought detailed in para 5 the complainant seeks the\r\nissuance of the following interim order&nbsp;<i>as per Section 36 of RERA 2016</i>:</span></p><ol><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">The\r\nbuilder please be directed to handover maintenance function of the complex to an independent agency ordered by it along with representation of the\r\nresidents’ welfare association therein, which has already been formed and registered with the\r\nRegistrar Cooperative Societies, Punjab.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Roboto;\">Directing the respondent to ensure continuation of the\r\nservices and maintenance, as are being provided by the maintenance agency viz. Sunrise Estate Management Services, during intervening period of transfer\r\nprocess, free of cost.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Roboto;\">The&nbsp;respondent be barred from any further recovery\r\nof charges on account of services and maintenance from the flat owners.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Roboto;\">The\r\nrespondent be directed to make payment of the services and maintenance charges for unsold flats to the said agency with RWA representation therein.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Roboto;\">The Municipal Council, Zirakpur be directed to get removal of violations and completion of mandatory items within given time frame from builder and furnish\r\nCompletion Certificate/ Occupancy Certificate to builder within the time specified by the\r\nRERA Punjab.</span><br></li></ol>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'csbkb','2019-01-12 18:42:24.000','csbkb','2019-01-12 18:42:24.000'),(856,1235,'1235',1312,'6192c304-cccb-4808-870c-b203098a180a','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-31 11:12:26.000','Charanjeet Singh Bagga','csbkb1983@gmail.com',9424492156,0,435060324845,'Juniper 403, Ansal Woodbury Apartments','High Land Marg, Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','1','Juniper 403, Ansal Woodbury Apartments','High Land Marg, Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','Yogesh Pathak','yogeshpathak@hotmail.com',9041639575,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0044','Ansal Woodbury Apartments ','Ansal Housing and Construction Ltd.','kushagr.ansal@ansals.com',0,0,'15 UGF Indra Prakash','21 Barakhamba Road',