&nbsp;:\r\nAs per section 11.4.b of the Central Real Estate Act 2016 and the Rule 9.1.i of\r\nPunjab RERA 2017, the builder, in addition to the orders in other judgments,&nbsp; may kindly be directed obtain Completion Certificate\r\nwithin the time specified by RERA Punjab.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><b>Recognition of RWA</b>:&nbsp; As\r\nper section 11.4.e of the Central Real Estate Act 2016:&nbsp;<b>&nbsp;The\r\npromoter shall be responsible for enabling the formation of association,\r\nsociety&nbsp;or coop. society, as the case may be, of&nbsp; allottees or a\r\nfederation of the same, ........within a period of&nbsp;three months of the\r\nmajority of allottees have booked their plot, apartment.......&nbsp;</b>Hence,\r\nthe builder may kindly be directed to recognize and transfer the project to the\r\nalready formed RWA.</span><br></li></ol>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Going by the facts detailed in para 4 above and the fact that in absence\r\nof Completion Certificate/Occupancy Certificate, execution of transfer\r\ndocuments for common areas in favor of RWA is not possible. Pending final\r\ndecision on the requests sought detailed in para 5 the complainant seeks the\r\nissuance of the following interim order&nbsp;<i>as per Section 36 of RERA 2016</i>:</span></p><ol><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">The\r\nbuilder please be directed to handover maintenance function of the complex to an independent agency ordered by it along with representation of the\r\nresidents’ welfare association therein, which has already been formed and registered with the\r\nRegistrar Cooperative Societies, Punjab.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Roboto;\">Directing the respondent to ensure continuation of the\r\nservices and maintenance, as are being provided by the maintenance agency viz. Sunrise Estate Management Services, during intervening period of transfer\r\nprocess, free of cost.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Roboto;\">The&nbsp;respondent be barred from any further recovery\r\nof charges on account of services and maintenance from the flat owners.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Roboto;\">The\r\nrespondent be directed to make payment of the services and maintenance charges for unsold flats to the said agency with RWA representation therein.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Roboto;\">The Municipal Council, Zirakpur be directed to get removal of violations and completion of mandatory items within given time frame from builder and furnish\r\nCompletion Certificate/ Occupancy Certificate to builder within the time specified by the\r\nRERA Punjab.</span><br></li></ol>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'csbkb','2019-01-12 18:51:54.000','csbkb','2019-01-12 18:51:54.000'),(858,1240,'1240',1317,'d8f8d4fc-24ac-4faa-a9b2-b5ad58a5817a','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-01-13 11:45:38.000','Bharat Bhushan Makkar','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9729902009,0,934955777170,'108 Sector 20 Kaithal','',13,9,'136027','1','108 Sector 20 Kaithal','',13,9,'136027','Kamal Dahiya','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9729902009,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0121','Purab Premium Apartments','Greater Mohali Area Development Authority','ce@gmada.gov.in',1722215512,0,'PUDA Bhawan Sector 62 District SAS Nagar Mohali','',28,507,'160062','1','PUDA Bhawan Sector 62 District SAS Nagar Mohali','',28,507,'160062','1','<p>Respondent opened scheme for public from 12.12.11 to 12.01.12 as Annexure C-1. The depicted salient features were as AnnexureC-2. Respondent informed vide letter dated 23.03.12 of the waiting list and complainant to submit the documents before 23.04.12 as Annexure C-3. Letter of intent for allotment was issued on 23.05.2012 and tentative price was Rs 69,00,000 and the flat was allotted with Flat No. 901 in Tower 3, Block E at Type 3 Apartment. As per Para 3(II) delivery was to be within a period of 36 months from the date of issuance of the said letter. Possession date was 23.05.2015 i.e. delay is of 3 years and 7 months as AnnexureC-4. Payment plan B was opted by the complainant as AnnexureC-4 (Pg 40). Initial amount of INR 13,80,000 paid vide cheque on 19.06.12 as AnnexureC-5 (Pg41). Total amount paid is Rs 68,06,850/- i.e. 99% out of the total consideration as AnnexureC-5 (colly). Respondent offered the possession vide letter on 10.10.2017. Thereafter the complainant visited site and found that layout plan has changed without taking the consent of 2/3rd allottees and also found many loopholes in the construction like compromised quality of materials etc. Photographs are annexed as Annexure C-6. The complainant got the construction inspected by Registered Council of Architecture, New Delhi. Many differences were found as in Annexure C-7. The complainant intimated such defects to the Estate Officer of GMADA vide letter dated 17.05.18 and requested for refund of his paid amount but respondent didn’t respond AnnexureC-8. Other allottees also found several defects, deficiencies and deviations in the project AnnexureC-9 (Pg104). Several allottees raised the issues before the press conference(Pg 105-106). The government ordered to remove the defaults but respondent did not comply to repair the faults (Pg 107-108). Fire safety has been expired (Pg 109-110). The lifts are also not safe at all for females and stops to work (Pg 111-113).</p>','<p>In view of the facts mentioned in preceding paragraphs, the complainant prays for the following relief(s):-&nbsp;</p><p>i.To give necessary directions to the respondents for refund the amount paid by the complainant with prescribed interest till realization as per the provisions of Sec. 18 and Sec.19(4)of the RERA Act read with Rule 16 of PSRE(R&amp;D)Rules,2017.</p><p>ii.To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 60 of RERA Act for willful default committed by them.</p><p>iii.To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 61 of RERA Act for contravention of Sec.12, Sec.14, and Sec. 16 of RERA Act.</p><p>iv.To issue directions to make liable every officer concerned i.e. Director, Manager, Secretary, or any other officer of the respondent’s company at whose instance, connivance, acquiescence, neglect any of the offences has been committed as mentioned in Sec.69 of RERA Act,2016 to be read with Punjab RERA Rules, 2017.</p><p>v.To recommend criminal action against the respondents for the criminal offence of cheating, fraud and criminal breach of trust under section 420,406 and 409 of the Indian Penal Code.</p><p>vi.To issue direction to pay the cost of litigation.</p><p>vii.To issue direction to pay the compensation to complainant for compensation for his mental agony, pain and harassment.</p><p>viii.Any other relief which this Hon’ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances of this complaint.</p>',69000.00,6806850.00,'2015-05-23 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>i.To direct the respondent not to demand any further amount whatsoever from the complainant.</p><p>ii.The respondent should be restrained from harassing the complainant in any manner whatsoever.</p><p>iii.Any other interim relief which this Hon’ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances of this complaint.</p><div><br></div>','1','','2012-05-23 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Flat No 901 Tower 3 Block E Type 3 Sector 88 Sahibzada Ajit Singh Nagar Punjab 140308','','',2,0,0,0,'Bharatbhushanmakkar','2019-01-13 11:42:30.000','Bharatb