 the project Annexure C-9 (Pg93). Several allottees raised the issues before the press conference (Pg 94-95). The government ordered to remove the defaults but respondent did not comply to repair the faults (Pg 96-97). Fire safety has been expired (Pg 98-99). The lifts are also not at all safe for females and stops to work (Pg 100-103).<br></p>','<p>In view of the facts mentioned in preceding paragraphs, the complainant prays for the following relief(s):-&nbsp;</p><p>i.To give necessary directions to the respondents for refund the amount paid by the complainant with prescribed interest till realization as per the provisions of Sec. 18 and Sec.19(4)of the RERA Act read with Rule 16 of PSRE(R&amp;D)Rules, 2017.</p><p>ii.To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 60 of RERA Act for willful default committed by them.</p><p>iii.To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 61 of RERA Act for contravention of Sec.12, Sec.14, and Sec. 16 of RERA Act.</p><p>iv.To issue directions to make liable every officer concerned i.e. Director, Manager, Secretary, or any other officer of the respondent’s company at whose instance, connivance, acquiescence, neglect any of the offences has been committed as mentioned in Sec.69 of RERA Act,2016 to be read with Punjab RERA Rules,2017.</p><p>v.To recommend criminal action against the respondents for the criminal offence of cheating, fraud and criminal breach of trust under section 420,406 and 409 of the Indian Penal Code.</p><p>vi.To issue direction to pay the cost of litigation.</p><p>vii.To issue direction to pay the compensation to complainant for compensation for his mental agony, pain and harassment.</p><p>viii.Any other relief which this Hon’ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances of this complaint.</p><div><br></div>',55000.00,5425746.00,'2015-05-21 00:00:00.000','2015-05-21 00:00:00.000','<p>i.To direct the respondent not to demand any further amount whatsoever from the complainant.</p><p>ii.The respondent should be restrained from harassing the complainant in any manner whatsoever.</p><p>iii.Any other interim relief which this Hon’ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances of this complaint.</p><div><br></div>','1','','2017-10-11 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Apartment No 1502 Tower 5 Block D Floor 14 Type 2 Sector 88 Sahibzada Ajit Singh Nagar Punjab 140308','','',2,0,0,0,'kamalmakkar1','2019-01-13 13:16:19.000','kamalmakkar1','2019-01-13 13:16:19.000'),(862,1268,'1268',1334,'d2ee06f3-c476-4a55-a3b3-19a64b5572f1','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Rishi Malhotra','fortunateme2@gmail.com',9971705420,0,0,'B105 SAINIK NAGAR','UTTAM NAGAR',10,628,'110059','1','T1D403, OMAXE PALM GREEN','Sector MU',33,216,'201310','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0106','MTPL FTP90 CHANDIGARH OVERSEAS PVT. LTD.','Sumesh Chawala','roc@monatownships.com',8088098809,0,' MCH, Sector 115, Kharar - Landran Road, Kharar, 140603','',28,507,'140603','1',' MCH, Sector 115, Kharar - Landran Road, Kharar, 140603','',28,507,'140603','1','<p>I have booked 100 sqft. commercial space in year 2006 in a project called fashion technology park greater mohali sector 90 with a builder called chandigarh overseas private limited. We have booked and made payments in their New Delhi connaught place office at that time.&nbsp; Builder has promised to deliver the project in 3 years but till now the project is not complete and builder has refused to return our hard earned money. we have tried to recover our money on multiple occasions that includes visiting project site office several times, visiting booking office old and changed ones, written multiple mails, and tried to put pressure on builder through several several telephone calls at that time.&nbsp;</p><p>Builder has also promised to pay fine if the project is not complete on time which is also denied by the builder on several occasions.&nbsp;</p><p>During this tenure from 2006 to 2019 builder has collaborated with different investors to complete the project without informing or intimating us. Also i have not received any relevant communication about the project status except their false assurances over phone. I have not received any written committed communication about delivery of project as it was very uncertain from the builder\'s side, hence the builder did not commit.</p><p><br></p><p>Me and my family members have been mentally tortured throughout this long journey of recovery of our hard earned money but till now there is no result.</p><p><br></p><p>I need money back with interest, fine.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>&nbsp;</p>','<p>No relief till now except little part of fine paid by the builder.</p>',500000.00,475000.00,'2009-06-18 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Not applicable.</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','2006-12-18 00:00:00','Block A2, design studio number 16, 5th floor, Sector 90, Sahibzada Ajit Singh Nagar, Punjab 140607','','',1,0,0,0,'fortunateme2','2019-01-14 15:23:19.000','fortunateme2','2019-01-14 15:23:19.000'),(863,1267,'1267',1338,'a14a6627-fb57-4589-90fb-ac52fbab3bc2','FormTypeM',1,1,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','PRAVIN AGRAWAL','pravin_baa@yahoo.com',9648227755,0,0,'15/79(2)','CIVIL LINES',33,297,'208001','1','15/79(2)','CIVIL LINES',33,297,'208001','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0154','WAVE ESTATE, GROUP HOUSING 2 ','COUNTRY COLONISERS PVT LTD','rera@waveestate.in',7290015352,0,'P.O. Rayon and Silk Mills, adjoining Coca Cola Depot','GT Road, Chheharta',28,39,'143105','0','Sector 85','SAS Nagar',28,507,'160062','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: roboto, serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">I booked a residential flat\r\n(Flat No. WG/H/0502) in Wave Garden, Sector 85, Mohali as per allotment letter\r\nDtd. 24/11/2012. As per Clause 5.1 of the allotment letter, possession of the\r\nflat was to be given by the builder within 36 months of the allotment i.e. upto\r\nNovember 2015. I have made total payment of Rs. 79,85,207/- towards the cost of\r\nFlat as per the demand of the builder. I wrote various letters, mails and had\r\ntelephonic conversation time to time to the company staff, to know about the\r\nstatus of the project. Company never responded and also never confirmed the\r\ndate of possession. Even after lapse of 6 years, project is still incomplete.\r\nFinally I vide my registered letter Dtd 26/07/2018, requested the company to\r\ncancel my flat booking and refund the total amount paid by me with interest but\r\nthe company is neither responding nor refunding the money. </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: roboto, serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">That as per provisions of Section 18 of RERA Act, 2016 if promoter fails to complete or is unable to give possession of an apartment, plot, or building in accordance with terms of agreement for sale then he shall be liable to return the amount received along with interest (as per RERA Rules). As in our case promoter has violated the provisions of Section 18 and 19 of RERA Act 2016, hence he is liable to refund the amount received along with interest and penal provisions are also applicable on him.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">1) Refund of\r\ntotal money deposited/paid by me to the Company against booking of Flat No.\r\nWG/H/0502.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0in;margi