ial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">That as per provisions of Section 18 of RERA Act, 2016 if promoter fails to complete or is unable to give possession of an apartment, plot, or building in accordance with terms of agreement for sale then he shall be liable to return the amount received along with interest (as per RERA Rules). As in our case promoter has violated the provisions of Section 18 and 19 of RERA Act 2016, hence he is liable to refund the amount received along with interest and penal provisions are also applicable on him.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">1) Refund of\r\ntotal money deposited/paid by me to the Company against booking of Flat No.\r\nWG/H/0502.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">2) Payment of\r\nInterest @ 24% p.a. on the amount deposited/paid by me to the Company.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p>3) Payment of Penalty upto 5% of the estimated cost of the Real estate Project (as per Section 61 of RERA Act, 2016)</o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">4) Payment of\r\ncompensation as per RERA Rules.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">5) Any other\r\nrelief as the Honourable Regulatory authority deem fit.&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p>',8786975.00,7941247.00,'2015-11-24 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: roboto, serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">As per reliefs sought in Point\r\nNo 5 above.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','1','','2012-11-24 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','WG/H/0502, Wave Garden, SAS Nagar, Mohali','','',1,1,0,0,'PravinAgrawal','2019-01-15 11:51:01.000','PravinAgrawal','2019-01-15 11:51:01.000'),(870,1235,'1235',1312,'6192c304-cccb-4808-870c-b203098a180a','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-01-12 18:52:02.000','Charanjeet Singh Bagga','csbkb1983@gmail.com',9424492156,0,435060324845,'Juniper 403, Ansal Woodbury Apartments','High Land Marg, Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','1','Juniper 403, Ansal Woodbury Apartments','High Land Marg, Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','Yogesh Pathak','yogeshpathak@hotmail.com',9041639575,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0044','Ansal Woodbury Apartments ','Ansal Housing and Construction Ltd.','kushagr.ansal@ansals.com',0,0,'15 UGF Indra Prakash','21 Barakhamba Road',10,120,'110001','1','15 UGF Indra Prakash','21 Barakhamba Road',10,120,'110001','1','<p><font face=\"Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.6667px;\">As per the rules, registration of a Project with RERA expires on the date, which a builder declares for completion in Form B. In our case, the builder i.e. AHCL wilfully omitted the completion date twice, see Appendix I.A and I.B; resulting in ‘Open Registration’ needing no further extension and also leaving no scope for RWA for claiming the possession of common areas.</span></font></p><p><font face=\"Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.6667px;\">Even after getting login ID, AHCL did not create any web page on PB RERA site, hence kept away from entering project details thereon; despite PB RERA reminders vide cir. No.08 dt. 09.05.18 and notice dt. 09.09.18.</span></font></p><p><font face=\"Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.6667px;\">The builder granted possession of flats to buyers, pretending that all approvals are in place. Also, by claiming that project got completed in 2012, it secured High Court orders for issuance of completion certificate, expeditiously; see Appendix II. On the contrary, Punjab Urban Local Bodies Directorate, Chandigarh pointed out several deviations/violations from original plan. Various court judgements/orders including those of Supreme Court of India and State Consumer Forum, Punjab support their contention, see appendix III, IV, V and VI.&nbsp;</span></font></p><p><font face=\"Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.6667px;\">Neither the AHCL nor its sister concern, which is providing the essential services in our complex, respond to our complaints, made repeatedly against highly poor services. Such an indifferent attitude forced the residents to unanimously decide for holding of quarterly payment, in protest. Reasonable maintenance amount is allowed to be charged by the builder during intervening period. However, the most unfortunate part in our case is that the allottees are paying the maintenance for even the unsold flats for several years. While this is also a point to be noted that amount incurred by RWA in hiring maintenance services are exempted from GST vide Notification of 28.06.17, see Appendix VII. Aggregate of above said maintenance charges and instance of GST, is forming approximately 35.0 percent of the current charges.</span></font></p><div><br></div>','<ol><li><b><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Information in contravenes to the Section 4:&nbsp;</span></b><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Failure of the promoter to\r\ncomply with the instruction given in respect of&nbsp; Specific date of\r\ncompletion of the project has been dealt with under Section 60 of the RERA\r\n2016. The RERA Punjab is requested to take a note of failure of the promoter to\r\ncomply with the above instructions and on persistence, requested to take a view, suitably.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><b>Promoter’s\r\nobligation of disclosure:&nbsp;&nbsp;</b>Failure of the promoter to comply with\r\nthe orders for up loading of information on website has been\r\ndealt with under Section 63 of the RERA 2016. The RERA Punjab is requested to\r\ntake a note of failure of the promoter to comply its orders and hence requested to\r\ntake a view, suitably.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><b>Project deficiencies:&nbsp;</b>In compliance to the\r\nobligations, responsibilities and functions as per section 11.4.a of the\r\nCentral Real Estate&nbsp; Act 2016, the builder may kindly be directed to\r\ncomplete the shortcomings in respect of the project within the prescribed time by it.&nbsp;</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><b>Completion Certificate</b>&nbsp;:\r\nAs per section 11.4.b of the Central Real Estate Act 2016 and the Rule 9.1.i of\r\nPunjab RERA 2017, the builder, in addition to the orders in other judgments,&nbsp; may kindly be directed obtain Completion Certificate\r\nwithin the time specified by RERA Punjab.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><b>Recognition of RWA</b>:&nbsp; As\r\nper section 11.4.e of the Central Real Estate Act 2016:&nbsp;<b>&nbsp;The\r\npromoter shall be responsible for enabling the formation of association,\r\nsociety&nbsp;or coop. society, as the case may be, of&nbsp; allottees or a\r\nfederation of the same, ........within a period of&nbsp;three months of the\r\nmajority of allottees have booked their plot, apartment.......&nbsp;</b>Hence,\r\nthe builder may kindly be directed to recognize and transfer the project to the\r\nalready formed RWA.</span><br></li></ol>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Going by the facts detailed in para 4 above and the fact that in absence\r\nof Completion Certificate/Occupancy Certificate, execution of transfer\r\ndocuments for common areas in favor of RWA is not possible. Pending final\r\ndecision on the requests sought detailed in para 5 the complainant seeks the\r\nissuance of the following interim order&nbsp;<i>as per Section 36 of RERA 2016</i>:</span></p><ol><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">The\r\nbuilder please be directed to handover maintenance function of the complex to an independent agency ordered by it along with representation of the\r\nresidents’ welfare association therein, which has already been formed and registered with the\r\nRegistrar Cooperative Societies, Punjab.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Roboto;\">Directing the respondent to ensure continuation of the\r\nservices and maintenance, as are being provided by the maintenance agency viz. Sunrise Estate Management Services, during intervening period of transfer\r\nprocess, free of cost.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Roboto;\">The&nbsp;respondent be barred from any further recovery\r\nof charges on account of services and maintenance from the flat owners.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Roboto;\">The\r\nrespondent be directed to make payment of the services and maintenance charges for unsold flats to the said agency with RWA representation therein.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Roboto;\">The Municipal Council, Zirakpur be directed to get removal of violations and completion of mandatory items within given time frame from builder and furnish\r\nCompletion Certificate/ Occupancy Certificate to builder within the time specified by the\r\nRERA Punjab.</span><br></li></ol>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'csbkb','2019-01-15 13:37:22.000','csbkb','2019-01-15 13:37:22.000'),(871,1235,'1235',1312,'6192c304-cccb-4808-870c-b203098a180a','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-01-15 13:40:28.000','Charanjeet Singh Bagga','csbkb1983@gmail.com',9424492156,0,435060324845,'Juniper 403, Ansal Woodbury Apartments','High Land Marg, Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','1','Juniper 403, Ansal Woodbury Apartments','High Land Marg, Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','Yogesh Pathak','yogeshpathak@hotmail.com',9041639575,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0044','Ansal Woodbury Apartments ','Ansal Housing and Construction Ltd.','kushagr.ansal@ansals.com',0,0,'15 UGF Indra Prakash','21 Barakhamba Road',10,120,'110001','1','15 UGF Indra Prakash','21 Barakhamba Road',10,120,'110001','1','<p><font face=\"Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.6667px;\">As per the rules, registration of a Project with RERA expires on the date, which a builder declares for completion in Form B. In our case, the builder i.e. AHCL wilfully omitted the completion date twice, see Appendix I.A and I.B; resulting in ‘Open Registration’ needing no further extension and also leaving no scope for RWA for claiming the possession of common areas.</span></font></p><p><font face=\"Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.6667px;\">Even after getting login ID, AHCL did not create any web page on PB RERA site, hence kept away from entering project details thereon; despite PB RERA reminders vide cir. No.08 dt. 09.05.18 and notice dt. 09.09.18.</span></font></p><p><font face=\"Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.6667px;\">The builder granted possession of flats to buyers, pretending that all approvals are in place. Also, by claiming that project got completed in 2012, it secured High Court orders for issuance of completion certificate, expeditiously; see Appendix II. On the contrary, Punjab Urban Local Bodies Directorate, Chandigarh pointed out several deviations/violations from original plan. Various court judgements/orders including those of Supreme Court of India and State Consumer Forum, Punjab support their contention, see appendix III, IV, V and VI.&nbsp;</span></font></p><p><font face=\"Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.6667px;\">Neither the AHCL nor its sister concern, which is providing the essential services in our complex, respond to our complaints, made repeatedly against highly poor services. Such an indifferent attitude forced the residents to unanimously decide for holding of quarterly payment, in protest. Reasonable maintenance amount is allowed to be charged by the builder during intervening period. However, the most unfortunate part in our case is that the allottees are paying the maintenance for even the unsold flats for several years. While this is also a point to be noted that amount incurred by RWA in hiring maintenance services are exempted from GST vide Notification of 28.06.17, see Appendix VII. Aggregate of above said maintenance charges and instance of GST, is forming approximately 35.0 percent of the current charges.</span></font></p><div><br></div>','<ol><li><b><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Information in contravenes to the Section 4:&nbsp;</span></b><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Failure of the promoter to\r\ncomply with the instruction given in respect of&nbsp; Specific date of\r\ncompletion of the project has been dealt with under Section 60 of the RERA\r\n2016. The RERA Punjab is requested to take a note of failure of the promoter to\r\ncomply with the above instructions and on persistence, requested to take a view, suitably.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><b>Promoter’s\r\nobligation of disclosure:&nbsp;&nbsp;</b>Failure of the promoter to comply with\r\nthe orders for up loading of information on website has been\r\ndealt with under Section 63 of the RERA 2016. The RERA Punjab is requested to\r\ntake a note of failure of the promoter to comply its orders and hence requested to\r\ntake a view, suitably.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><b>Project deficiencies:&nbsp;</b>In compliance to the\r\nobligations, responsibilities and functions as per section 11.4.a of the\r\nCentral Real Estate&nbsp; Act 2016, the builder may kindly be directed to\r\ncomplete the shortcomings in respect of the project within the prescribed time by it.&nbsp;</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><b>Completion Certificate</b>&nbsp;:\r\nAs per section 11.4.b of the Central Real Estate Act 2016 and the Rule 9.1.i of\r\nPunjab RERA 2017, the builder, in addition to the orders in other judgments,&nbsp; may kindly be directed obtain Completion Certificate\r\nwithin the time specified by RERA Punjab.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"><b>Recognition of RWA</b>:&nbsp; As\r\nper section 11.4.e of the Central Real Estate Act 2016:&nbsp;<b>&nbsp;The\r\npromoter shall be responsible for enabling the formation of association,\r\nsociety&nbsp;or coop. society, as the case may be, of&nbsp; allottees or a\r\nfederation of the same, ........within a period of&nbsp;three months of the\r\nmajority of allottees have booked their plot, apartment.......&nbsp;</b>Hence,\r\nthe builder may kindly be directed to recognize and transfer the project to the\r\nalready formed RWA.</span><br></li></ol>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Going by the facts detailed in para 4 above and the fact that in absence\r\nof Completion Certificate/Occupancy Certificate, execution of transfer\r\ndocuments for common areas in favor of RWA is not possible. Pending final\r\ndecision on the requests sought detailed in para 5 the complainant seeks the\r\nissuance of the following interim order&nbsp;<i>as per Section 36 of RERA 2016</i>:</span></p><ol><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">The\r\nbuilder please be directed to handover maintenance function of the complex to an independent agency ordered by it along with representation of the\r\nresidents’ welfare association therein, which has already been formed and registered with the\r\nRegistrar Cooperative Societies, Punjab.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Roboto;\">Directing the respondent to ensure continuation of the\r\nservices and maintenance, as are being provided by the maintenance agency viz. Sunrise Estate Management Services, during intervening period of transfer\r\nprocess, free of cost.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Roboto;\">The&nbsp;respondent be barred from any further recovery\r\nof charges on account of services and maintenance from the flat owners.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Roboto;\">The\r\nrespondent be directed to make payment of the services and maintenance charges for unsold flats to the said agency with RWA representation therein.</span></li><li><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 8pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Roboto;\">The Municipal Council, Zirakpur be directed to get removal of violations and completion of mandatory items within given time frame from builder and furnish\r\nCompletion Certificate/ Occupancy Certificate to builder within the time specified by the\r\nRERA Punjab.</span><br></li></ol>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',1,1,0,0,'csbkb','2019-01-15 13:40:24.000','csbkb','2019-01-15 13:40:24.000'),(872,1269,'1269',1158,'0c27aca9-8cc5-4938-a0f5-138a7568230c','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-01-16 19:04:24.000','Naveen  Walia','vdharmani@gmail.com',9780041313,0,0,'R/O 24 Milk ','Milk (Part)(307)',13,1,'134203','1','534','Sector-10-D',6,128,'160011','Mukesh Pandit','mukeshpanditlawyer@gmail.com',8968334555,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0292','Palm Heights','M/s Palm Heights Private Limited','gmdb@ubbergroup.com',0,0,'SCO-5','Madanpura, Sector-54',28,39,'160055','0','Haibatpur Road',' Dera Bassi',28,507,'140201','1','<p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0cm\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\'margin: 0px; color: black; font-family: \"Arial\",\"sans-serif\";\'>Complainant&nbsp;</span><span style=\'margin: 0px; color: black; font-family: \"Arial\",\"sans-serif\";\'>paid the booking amount of Rs. 64,500&nbsp;by way of post dated\r\ncheque and cash.Thereafter,&nbsp;issued an allotment\r\nletter.Subsequently,&nbsp;an Apartment Buyers Agreement dated 20.02.2016 was\r\nexecuted bearing Flat No. 631, Third Floor proposed to be constructed at Tower\r\nSixth (T-6), super area 525 Sq. Ft. 1BHK&nbsp;for a total sale consideration of\r\nRs.12, 90,000/- inclusive of club house, IFMS, power back-up and service tax\r\netc.</span><span style=\'margin: 0px; color: black; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\";\'></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0cm\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\'margin: 0px; color: black; font-family: \"Arial\",\"sans-serif\";\'>However, pertinently as on today the construction of Tower 6 of the\r\nproject has not even started and the same is already marred by inordinate delay\r\nand even as on date, no work is going on and furthermore the development work\r\nof other facilities other than flats are also marred by inordinate delay.</span><span style=\'margin: 0px; color: black; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\";\'></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0cm\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\'margin: 0px; color: black; font-family: \"Arial\",\"sans-serif\";\'>The Complainant sought financial assistance to the tune of Rs.\r\n11,72,989/- from&nbsp;</span><span style=\'margin: 0px; color: black; font-family: \"Arial\",\"sans-serif\";\'>DHFL. After due execution of the loan documents including a\r\ntripartite agreement between DHFL, Complainant &nbsp;and the\r\nRespondent,&nbsp;&nbsp;the bank sanctioned loan in favour of the Complainants\r\nfor a tune of Rs.11,72,989/- from which an amount of Rs. 8,44,039/- as sale\r\nconsideration has already been disbursed to the Respondent by the DHFL in lieu\r\nof the mortgage deed being executed between the NBFC and Complainant. Since\r\nthereon, the Complainant is regularly paying the EMI to the Bank as per the\r\nloan documents.</span><span style=\'margin: 0px; color: black; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\";\'></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0cm\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\'margin: 0px; color: black; font-family: \"Arial\",\"sans-serif\";\'>Pertinently, as per Clause 4 of the said agreement the Respondent was\r\nunder legal obligation to deliver the possession of the said flat to the\r\ncomplainant on or before<b><u>&nbsp;August, 2016.</u></b></span><span style=\'margin: 0px; color: black; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\";\'></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n<b></b><i></i><u></u><sub></sub><sup></sup><strike></strike><font face=\"Times New Roman\"></font><br></p>','<p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0cm\"><span style=\'margin: 0px; color: black; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 10.5pt;\'>1.&nbsp;\r\n&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\'margin: 0px; color: black; font-family: \"Arial\",\"sans-serif\";\'>Refund of principle amount i.e. Rs.&nbsp;<u>8,32,050</u>/-\r\nalongwith the payments of EMI\'s paid to the financial Institution as per\r\ntripartite Agreement.</span></b><span style=\'margin: 0px; color: black; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\";\'></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0cm\"><b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\'margin: 0px; color: black; font-family: \"Arial\",\"sans-serif\";\'>Further, The Respondent shall be held liable for:</span></b><span style=\'margin: 0px; color: black; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\";\'></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0cm\"><b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\'margin: 0px; color: black; font-family: \"Arial\",\"sans-serif\";\'>2.</span></b><span style=\'margin: 0px; color: black; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 10.5pt;\'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span style=\'margin: 0px; color: black; font-family: \"Arial\",\"sans-serif\";\'>The guilty for non disclosure of the status report of the ongoing\r\nproject as per Section 4 of The Punjab State Real Estate&nbsp;(regulation and\r\nDevelopment) Act, 2017.&nbsp;</span><span style=\'margin: 0px; color: black; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\";\'></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0cm\"><span style=\'margin: 0px; color: black; font-family: \"Arial\",\"sans-serif\";\'>3.</span><span style=\'margin: 0px; color: black; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 10.5pt;\'>&nbsp;\r\n&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span style=\'margin: 0px; color: black; font-family: \"Arial\",\"sans-serif\";\'>&nbsp;Failed\r\nto discharge various functions and duties as enumerated in Section 11 Real\r\nEstate (Regulation and Development ) Act, 2016.</span><span style=\'margin: 0px; color: black; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\";\'></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0cm\"><span style=\'margin: 0px; color: black; font-family: \"Arial\",\"sans-serif\";\'>4.&nbsp;</span><span style=\'margin: 0px; color: black; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 10.5pt;\'>&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span style=\'margin: 0px; color: black; font-family: \"Arial\",\"sans-serif\";\'>The&nbsp; guilty for</span><span style=\'margin: 0px; color: black; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\"; font-size: 10.5pt;\'>&nbsp;</span><span style=\'margin: 0px; color: black; font-family: \"Arial\",\"sans-serif\";\'>misrepresenting the\r\napplicants through the said prospectus/ broucher for non approval of the\r\nstatutory&nbsp;compliances&nbsp;and the time period of possession and thus it\r\nhas committed violation of Section 12 of Real Estate (regulation and\r\nDevelopment) Act, 2016.</span><span style=\'margin: 0px; color: black; font-family: \"roboto\",\"serif\";\'></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n<b></b><i></i><u></u><sub></sub><sup></sup><strike></strike><font face=\"Times New Roman\"></font><br></p>',1290000.00,832050.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p><br></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','631 3rd Floor Palm Heights','','',1,1,0,0,'MukeshPandit','2019-01-15 15:57:55.000','MukeshPandit','2019-01-15 15:57:55.000'),(873,1270,'1270',1119,'dae2bb68-2fa2-473d-a49d-c15de93bd3da','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Manshinderjit','advravinder@gmail.com',9815700280,0,0,'1821 Phase 5 ','Mohali',28,507,'160059','1','ZIrakpur','Mohali',28,507,'140604','Ravinderpal Singh','advravinder@gmail.com',9815700280,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PM0010','FASHION TECHNOLOGY PARK','CHANDIGARH OVERSEAS PVT. LTD.','jbp@j90.in',0,0,'SCO 249 backside  Sector 44 C ','Chandigarh',6,128,'160047','0','Fashion Technology Park, Next to BSF Housing Complex','Sector 90 Mohali',28,507,'160055','1','<p>Respondent came up with project FASHION TECHNOLOGY PARK, selling office spaces (known as Design Studios) measuring 100/125 sq. ft. at a price of Rs.5,00,000/- each (5000 per sq. ft.). Construction of the project was started on 19.07.2007. Complainant applied for a unit no. 13, Block A-2, measuring 125 sq. ft. at 6th floor @ Rs.5,00,000/- Out of which Rs.4,75,000/- was paid. Rest was to be paid at the time of offer of possession. Buyer\'s Agreement was executed on 21.12.2006 along with one Lease Agreement with its sister concern Greenfield Sites management Pvt. Ltd.  Complainant initially paid Rs.1,25,000/- on 05.09.2006, thereafter Rs.1,25,000/- on 04.11.2006, thereafter Rs.1,25,000/- on 19.12.2006, Rs.50,000/- on 25.8.2007 and lastly Rs.50,000/- on 06.11.2007. As per Clause 28 possession of the unit was to be handed over within a period of 30 months from the date of start of construction failing which developer shall pay Rs.50/- per sq. ft. per month to the allottee. The time has already expired on 19.01.2010. Till date neither construction got completed nor amount is refunded. Respondent paid Rs.1,46,371/- Compensation from 19.01.2010 to 31.12.2011 thereafter stopped paying the same. Respondent also offered to the complainant to Buy Back the unit @ Rs.7,50,000/- if applied by the complainant within 30 months from start of construction. Since construction activities were very slow, complainant applied for the same on 10.12.2009 as well as reminder on 16.07.2011. Respondent has acknowledged the same vide their letter dated 13.01.2010 and promised to honour the Buy Back amount of Rs.7,50,000/- by 30.06.2010. There was no force majeur circumstances communicated to the complainant till date. Non payment of agreed amount under the agreement is violation of RERA. Therefore complainant is filing the present complaint seeking Buy Back amount and payment of Rs.6250 per month w.e.f. 01.01.2012 till payment of Buy Back Amount as confirmed vide letter dated 29.06.2010. Hence,&nbsp;</p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" align=\"left\" style=\"margin-bottom: 7.5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: roboto, serif;\">SEEKING REFUND OF RS.7,50,000/- ALONG WITH INTEREST\r\n@ 18% P.A. W.E.F. 30.06.2010 TILL REALIZATION<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" align=\"left\" style=\"margin-bottom: 7.5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: roboto, serif;\">ASSURED RETURN AMOUNTING TO RS.5,25,000/- DUE\r\nW.E.F. 01.01.2012 TILL PAYMENT OF BUY BACK AMOUNT (RS.5,25,000/- CALCULATED\r\nTILL 31.12.2018)<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" align=\"left\" style=\"margin-bottom: 7.5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: roboto, serif;\">RS,1,10,000/- AS COST OF LITIGATION.&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p>',500000.00,475000.00,'2010-01-19 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Respondent may be directed to deposit/ pay Rs.5,25,000/- as assured return/ compensation for delay in payment of Buy back / payment of delayed possession compensation due w.e.f. 01.01.2012 to 31.12.2018.</p>','1','','2006-12-04 00:00:00','2006-12-21 00:00:00','Design Studio No. 13, Block A-2, 6th Floor, FTP, Sector 90 Mohali','','',2,0,0,0,'advravinder','2019-01-16 10:39:13.000','advravinder','2019-01-16 10:39:13.000'),(874,1270,'1270',1119,'dae2bb68-2fa2-473d-a49d-c15de93bd3da','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-01-16 19:42:32.000','Manshinderjit','advravinder@gmail.com',9815700280,0,0,'1821 Phase 5 ','Mohali',28,507,'160059','1','ZIrakpur','Mohali',28,507,'140604','Ravinderpal Singh','advravinder@gmail.com',9815700280,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PM0010','FASHION TECHNOLOGY PARK','CHANDIGARH OVERSEAS PVT. LTD.','jbp@j90.in',0,0,'SCO 249 backside  Sector 