=\"background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><span lang=\"EN\" style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:\r\nRoboto;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial;color:#333333;mso-ansi-language:EN\">I) To\r\ndirect the respondent not to demand nay further amount what so ever from the\r\ncomplainant.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><span lang=\"EN\" style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:\r\nRoboto;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial;color:#333333;mso-ansi-language:EN\">ii)&nbsp;\r\nThe respondent should be restrained form harassing the complainant in any\r\nmanner whatsoever.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><span lang=\"EN\" style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:\r\nRoboto;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial;color:#333333;mso-ansi-language:EN\">iii) Any\r\nother interim relief which this Hon\'ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in\r\nview of the facts and circumstance of the present compliant.&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',1,1,0,0,'SANCHITPUNIA','2019-01-17 22:52:30.000','SANCHITPUNIA','2019-01-17 22:52:30.000'),(887,1125,'1125',1191,'16dedd0c-2e6f-4eb1-85bb-f16106f43c42','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-01-19 15:43:08.000','Nitin Jindal','nitin.email2me@gmail.com',8800669083,0,0,'D2 065 DLF NEW TOWN','Westend heights begur',17,67,'560068','1','D2 065 DLF NEW TOWN','Westend heights begur',17,67,'560068','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0084','Sushma Crescent ','BHARAT MITTAL','bharat@sushmabuildtech.com',0,0,'B-107, First Floor',', Business Complex at Elante Mall, Industrial Area - 1 ',6,128,'160002','1','B-107, First Floor',', Business Complex at Elante Mall, Industrial Area - 1 ',6,128,'160002','1','<p>1. Delay in Possession (Section 18): My possession date as per agreement is 31-Mar, 2015 and had paid about 85% of amount till Jul, 2014 (Rs 42,32,843). This year builder had further demand – one in September (for flooring work) and final demand on offer the possession on 11 Dec, 2018 (that too without sharing occupancy certificate).<br></p><p>2. Multiple changes in Specification without information (Under section 19): Rights and Duties of Allottees, Builder had changes the layout and specification without any notification and also not ready to share the details (moreover provided incorrect information that they have not made any changes). One example is the change in location of the swimming pool, now constructed in front of my tower (instead originally not proposed at that location). This is unacceptable.</p><p>3. Not sharing information (Under section 19): Builder is not ready to share the specification details and also partial occupancy certificate. But forcing me to pay the final demand for offer of possession (applies 24% interest penalty). </p><p>4. Not delivered as promised at the time of sale (Section 12 &amp; 14): As the time of sale builder promised to provide covered car parking, but now providing open parking</p>','<p>As per section 18 ,&nbsp;<span style=\"font-family: Calibri, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt;\">in\r\ncase of delay the promoter has to pay the interest (State bank of India highest\r\nmarginal cost of lending rate plus two percent) or refund the complete amount paid with the penalty interest.</span></p>',5053900.00,5006075.00,'2015-03-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>I have asked for compensation as per form N as well. AsC No 10522018</p>','1','','2011-11-05 00:00:00','2012-03-21 00:00:00','704, Tower F, Sushma Crescent, Sushma square','','',2,0,0,0,'Nitinjindal0505','2019-01-18 11:40:16.000','Nitinjindal0505','2019-01-18 11:40:16.000'),(888,1273,'1273',1223,'9616498a-08f7-4464-9ca8-d1e8ddf49a77','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','RISHI KUMAR GUPTA','agamjund_advocate@yahoo.com',9780269386,0,253992356271,'V & PO MULLANPUR GARIBDASS','NEAR POLICE STATION',28,507,'140901','1','V & PO MULLANPUR GARIBDASS','NEAR POLICE STATION',28,507,'140901','AGAM KUMAR JUND','agamjund_advocate@yahoo.com',9780269387,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0351','SANSKRITI HOMES (DLF HYDE PARK)','DLF UNIVERSAL LTD. & SANSKRITI GOLDEN OAK REAL ESTATE PVT. LTD.','info@sanskritihomes.com',7814700800,0,'M/s. Sanskriti Golden Oak Real Estate Pvt. Ltd.,','DLF Pocket R-2, New Chandigarh Mullanpur',28,507,'140901','0','DLF Universal Ltd. ','SCO 190,191,192  Sector 8-C',6,128,'160017','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:13.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:Mangal;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi\">Applicant had (9\r\nAcres 37 Biswe i.e. 9.385 Acre) ancestral land at village Devi Nagar, S.A.S\r\nNagar. Respondent approached applicant for purchasing land. On being induced by\r\nthe representation of respondent, Applicant agreed to sell his land at Rs.3\r\nCrore per Acre. Agreement to sell @ 2 Crore 36 Lakh per Acre was signed between\r\nparties on 21.11.11. Respondent assured that balance amount will be given separately;\r\nas registered deed has to be executed under value to avoid state taxes i.e.\r\nRs.2 Crore 36 Lakh per acre. A separate MOU was prepared to adjust balance\r\namount of Rs.6 Crore of applicant. As per MOU,<b> </b>respondent had to give four plots of 500 Sq Yd of Rs.1 Crore 50\r\nlakh each to applicant. During gap period, without asking choice, respondent\r\nallotted four plots No.R-1/C-209, R-1/C-210, R-1/C-211 &amp; R-1/C-212 to\r\napplicant. On 29.05.12, applicant executed registered sale deed of 9.385 Acre land\r\nin favour of respondent, after receiving Rs 22,14,95,833/- along with\r\nconfirmation letter of four plots. For transferring plots in name of applicant\r\nas per MOU and to show a valid transaction for these four plots, on 28.03.13,\r\nrespondent had transferred Rs. 3 Cr 90 Lakh in account of applicant, i.e. Rs.\r\n97 Lakh 50 Thousand for each plot. Accordingly four cheques of Rs. 92,62,500/- each\r\nwere taken from the applicant by respondent. In this way respondent had taken\r\nback Rs.3,70,50,000/- from applicant. On 27.12.13, plot buyer’s agreement for\r\nfour plots separately were signed between applicant and respondent. Respondent\r\nissued demand notices of Rs.2,51,044 on 15.10.13 and of Rs.1,05,82,129.60 on\r\n15.11.14. </span><span style=\"font-size:13.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Instead of paying actual balance amount of Rs.6 Crore to\r\napplicant, respondent has cheated applicant with Rs. 2 Crore 99 lakh. Till date\r\nplots possession has not been delivered and whole land of applicant has been\r\nutilized by respondent. Copy of representation/notice dated 22.12.2018 may\r\nkindly be read as facts of the case.</span><span style=\"font-size:13.0pt;\r\nline-height:115%\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size: 13pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">Registration granted under section 5 of the Real\r\nEstate (Regulation and Development) Act, to the respondent may kindly be\r\nrevoked&nbsp;under Section 7(1) (d) of this act&nbsp;as the respondent promoter\r\nis indulges in unfair and fraudulent practices&nbsp;by cheating the applicant,\r\nafter preparing many documents and by not providing any clear information to\r\nthe applicant regarding the policy/procedure adopted by the company&nbsp;and\r\nhad created loss to the state exchequer by not paying the legal state\r\ntaxes.&nbsp;Respondent be directed to pay the actual balance amount of land\r\n(i.e. Rs. 6 Crore) purchased from the applicant along with interest, as\r\napplicant does not want to take any plot from them. Further compensation on\r\naccount of delaying the payment of the applicant by preparing false documents\r\njust to commit fraud with the applicant and the state as per the Rules of\r\nPunjab State Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Rules which provides\r\nState Bank of India highest marginal cost of lending rate plus 2% from the\r\nrespective date of deposit made by the complainants. Further directions may\r\nkindly be issued to the respondents to pay Rs. 10 Lacs to the applicant for\r\nmental and physical harassment and on the account of the deficiency in the\r\nservices and unfair trade practice committed by the respondents.&nbsp;Further\r\ndirections may kindly be issued to the respondents to pay Rs. 1,00,000/- on\r\naccount of litigation charges to the applicant.&nbsp;It is further prayed that\r\nthis Hon\'ble Tribunal may grant any other relief, which it deems fit and\r\nproper, in the facts and circumstances of the present case, in the interest of\r\njustice, equity and fair play.<o:p></o:p></span></p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:13.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Bank\r\nAccounts of the Respondent may kindly be freezed during the pendency of present\r\npetition.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:13.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Sale\r\nand purchase of Plots/Flats constructed therein the project of the respondent may\r\nkindly be stopped.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:13.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Respondent\r\nmay kindly be directed not to alter in the land or may be stopped from creating\r\nany third party right over the land in dispute.</span><span style=\"font-size:\r\n13.0pt;line-height:115%\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>','1','','2012-05-29 00:00:00','2011-11-21 00:00:00','R-1/C/209,R-1/C/210,R-1/C/211,R-1/C/212 DLF HYDE PARK, ESTATE PROJECT, NEW CHANDIGARH','','',2,0,0,0,'AGAM','2019-01-20 11:41:48.000','AGAM','2019-01-20 11:41:48.000'),(889,1273,'1273',1223,'9616498a-08f7-4464-9ca8-d1e8ddf49a77','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-01-20 16:05:07.000','RISHI KUMAR GUPTA','agamjund_advocate@yahoo.com',9780269386,0,253992356271,'V & PO MULLANPUR GARIBDASS','NEAR POLICE STATION',28,507,'140901','1','V & PO MULLANPUR GARIBDASS','NEAR POLICE STATION',28,507,'140901','AGAM KUMAR JUND','agamjund_advocate@yahoo.com',9780269387,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0351','SANSKRITI HOMES (DLF HYDE PARK)','DLF UNIVERSAL LTD. & SANSKRITI GOLDEN OAK REAL ESTATE PVT. LTD.','info@sanskritihomes.com',7814700800,0,'M/s. Sanskriti Golden Oak Real Estate Pvt. Ltd.,','DLF Pocket R-2, New Chandigarh Mullanpur',28,507,'140901','0','DLF Universal Ltd. ','SCO 190,191,192  Sector 8-C',6,128,'160017','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:13.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:Mangal;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi\">Applicant had (9\r\nAcres 37 Biswe i.e. 9.385 Acre) ancestral land at village Devi Nagar, S.A.S\r\nNagar. Respondent approached applicant for purchasing land. On being induced by\r\nthe repre