O/38/2018 before adjudicating office which was ordered to be returned to the complainant vide order dated 27.11.2018 (A-8) in view of the circular dated 9.10.18 &amp; 21.11.18.</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><br></p>',5747919.00,1336820.00,'2015-02-22 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>To direct the respondent to furnish details regarding the group housing project and the reason for not starting the construction of group housing flats</p>','1','','2013-11-25 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','CG-T3-02-203','','',2,0,0,0,'rerafilingformm','2019-01-30 12:16:42.000','rerafilingformm','2019-01-30 12:16:42.000'),(953,1286,'1286',1141,'971b1ae7-f8bc-4323-80a7-088b81f8b7db','FormTypeM',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Harjinder Singh Kohli','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.comm',9814257243,0,0,'1191','Sector-42D',6,128,'160036','1','House No. 253','Sector 4, Mansa Devi Complex',13,15,'134114','Sanjeev Gupta','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-LDH45-PR0004','Ireo Waterfront','Ireo waterfront Private Limited','iwpl@ireo.in',0,1613040290,'Ireo Waterfront, Sidhwan Canal Road','Opp Ferozpur Road, Village Dewatwal',28,366,'141001','0','SCO 16-17, Fortune Chambers','Opposite Ludhiana Stock Exchange',28,366,'141001','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">Complainant booked a residential flat bearing No. CC-T3-02-203,Type-H measuring 1306 sq ft(121.33 sq mtr)for total sale consideration of Rs.5747919/-. Complainant has paid Rs.1336820 till date but till today neither buyer’s agreement has been executed nor did the respondent start any development of group housing. Respondent acknowledged the receipt of application dated 22.2.13 and receipt of Rs. 3 lacs vide A-1 and further demanded Rs. 234728/- by 24.3.13 and Rs. 802092/- by 23.5.13,which was duly paid by the complainant(Ann A-2 &amp; A-3).A provisional allotment letter was issued and flat No. CG-T3-02-203 was provisionally allotted(A-4).Respondent had assured to deliver the possession within 2 years.Respondent failed to mail the buyer agreement as promised.Inspite of repeated requests, the buyer agreement was not executed. In June,2014 a request was made through email to refund the amount with interest since there was no development. Complainant received a letter vide(A-5)which it was informed that development work is progressing well but infact there was no development. Complainant also called for refund and it was assured that his request for refund will be processed shortly.Thereafter many times request for refund was made but to no avail. Respondent failed to start the construction of group housing.Email was also sent on 9.4.2015(A-6)and a call was also made to Amrik Singh,on 1.10.2015 but to avail.A letter dated 21.7.2017(A-7)was also sent to respondent for refund but there was response from respondent.Since there is no development and construction activity of group housing in which the flat of complainant is located, and considerable time has also passed,the complainant does not wish to have a flat and thus wish to withdraw from the project.The respondent has indulged into unfair trade practices by not informing about the progress of project and it even failed to start the construction of group housing and kept the complainant in loop for many years.Order (A-8)</span></font></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">To direct the\r\nrespondent to refund the principal amount of Rs. 1336820/- as per Section 18 of\r\nRERA along with interest as prescribed under rule 16 of Punjab RERA Rules, since\r\nthe respondent has failed to start any construction of group housing and consequently\r\nhas failed to handover the possession and thus the complainant wishes to\r\nwithdraw from the project and therefore is seeking refund of the amount paid by\r\nhim along with interest. The complainant will file separate complaint for\r\nclaiming compensation. The complainant earlier filed the complaint in Form N i.e. AO/38/2018 before adjudicating office which was ordered to be returned to the complainant vide order dated 27.11.2018 (A-8) in view of the circular dated 9.10.18 &amp; 21.11.18.</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><br></p>',5747919.00,1336820.00,'2015-02-22 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>To direct the respondent to furnish details regarding the group housing project and the reason for not starting the construction of group housing flats</p>','1','','2013-11-25 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','CG-T3-02-203','','',2,0,0,0,'rerafilingformm','2019-01-30 12:18:05.000','rerafilingformm','2019-01-30 12:18:05.000'),(954,1286,'1286',1141,'971b1ae7-f8bc-4323-80a7-088b81f8b7db','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-01-30 15:40:40.000','Harjinder Singh Kohli','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.comm',9814257243,0,0,'1191','Sector-42D',6,128,'160036','1','House No. 253','Sector 4, Mansa Devi Complex',13,15,'134114','Sanjeev Gupta','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-LDH45-PR0004','Ireo Waterfront','Ireo waterfront Private Limited','iwpl@ireo.in',0,1613040290,'Ireo Waterfront, Sidhwan Canal Road','Opp Ferozpur Road, Village Dewatwal',28,366,'141001','0','SCO 16-17, Fortune Chambers','Opposite Ludhiana Stock Exchange',28,366,'141001','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">Complainant booked a residential flat bearing No. CC-T3-02-203,Type-H measuring 1306 sq ft(121.33 sq mtr)for total sale consideration of Rs.5747919/-. Complainant has paid Rs.1336820 till date but till today neither buyer’s agreement has been executed nor did the respondent start any development of group housing. Respondent acknowledged the receipt of application dated 22.2.13 and receipt of Rs. 3 lacs vide A-1 and further demanded Rs. 234728/- by 24.3.13 and Rs. 802092/- by 23.5.13,which was duly paid by the complainant(Ann A-2 &amp; A-3).Respondent had assured to deliver the possession within 2 years.A provisional allotment letter was issued and flat No. CG-T3-02-203 was provisionally allotted(A-4).Respondent failed to mail the buyer agreement as promised.Inspite of repeated requests, the buyer agreement was not executed. In June,2014 a request was made through email to refund the amount with interest since there was no development. Complainant received a letter vide(A-5)which it was informed that development work is progressing well but infact there was no development. Complainant also called for refund and it was assured that his request for refund will be processed shortly.Thereafter many times request for refund was made but to no avail. Respondent failed to start the construction of group housing.Email was also sent on 9.4.2015(A-6)and a call was also made to Amrik Singh,on 1.10.2015 but to avail.A letter dated 21.7.2017(A-7)was also sent to respondent for refund but there was response from respondent.Since there is no development and construction activity of group housing in which the flat of complainant is located, and considerable time has also passed,the complainant does not wish to have a flat and thus wish to withdraw from the project.The respondent has indulged into unfair trade practices by not informing about the progress of project and it even failed to start the construction of group housing and kept the complainant in loop for many years.Order (A-8)</span></font></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">To direct the\r\nrespondent to refund the principal amount of Rs. 1336820/- as per Section 18 of\r\nRERA along with interest as prescribed under rule 16 of Punjab RERA Rules, since\r\nthe respondent has failed to start any construction of group housing and consequently\r\nhas failed to handover the possession and thus the complainant wishes to\r\nwithdraw from the project and therefore is seeking refund of the amount paid by\r\nhim along with interest. The complainant will file separate complaint for\r\nclaiming compensation. The complainant earlier filed the complaint in Form N i.e. AO/38/2018 before adjudicating office which was ordered to be returned to the complainant vide order dated 27.11.2018 (A-8) in view of the circular dated 9.10.18 &amp; 21.11.18.</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><br></p>',5747919.00,1336820.00,'2015-02-22 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>To direct the respondent to furnish details regarding the group housing project and the reason for not starting the construction of group housing flats</p>','1','','2013-11-25 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','CG-T3-02-203','','',1,1,0,0,'rerafilingformm','2019-01-30 12:27:39.000','rerafilingformm','2019-01-30 12:27:39.000'),(955,1212,'1212',1141,'971b1ae7-f8bc-4323-80a7-088b81f8b7db','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-24 15:32:20.000','Meenal Lall','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,0,'NA 802, Sapthagiri Splendor','BDM-IV',17,67,'560076','0','253, Sector-4, MDC','Mansa Devi Complex',13,15,'134114','Sanjeev Gupta','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0090','SANDWOODS OPULENCIA','M/s Sandwoods Infratech Private Limited','info@sandwoods.com',0,1725003871,'SCO 222-223','Sector-34',6,128,'160022','1','SCO 222-223','Sector-34',6,128,'160022','1','<p>Respondent allotted a 3BHK residential apartment No.50,TowerA,5th floor,Super Area 1950 sq ft to the complainant.A brochure (C-1) was given to the complainant mentioning the detail regarding the facilities to be provided.Respondent issued the allotment letter dated 1.5.2014 (C-2).The total sale consideration of unit was fixed as Rs. 5070000.It was agreed at that all the specifications will be provided except Ac’s.Respondent also assured to provide cupboards in all the bedrooms(C-3). Buyer’s agreement (C-4) was signed on 20.5.14,as per which the possession was to be handed over within a period of 36 months.Complainant has paid Rs. 5246662(including tax of Rs. 186411&amp; EDC of Rs. 243750)Out of said amount, she has paid Rs. 4816500/- towards the basic price, out of total sale consideration of Rs. 5070000/-. Receipts of Rs.4629635/- (C-5) Apart from the amount of receipts, an amount of Rs. 264859/- &amp; 352168/- paid on 22/5/16 &amp; 2/9/17, thus totaling Rs. 5246662/-. Vide letter 13.8.18 (C-6), it was informed that unit has reached pre-possession stage &amp; more money was demanded, also that the super area has been increased to 2192 sq ft and demanded Rs. 629200/- in lieu of that. On 17.8.18, complainant took up the matter &amp; asked the reason for not informing her earlier about the increase. On visiting the site, the complainant found the area of flat to be same and no addition was found. Next day, complainant visited the respondent &amp; conveyed it that there is no increase. Then respondent made the reduction of 50% &amp; asked him to pay Rs. 314600. Copy of letter/statement is C-7.Inspite of repeated requests, respondent did not give the detail of increased area.It also started demanding Rs. 78912 towards maintenance advance which it cannot demand.Work has not been completed as per the specifications mentioned in brochure.Apartment is not habitable. Photographs are C-8. Loan document C-9.No completion certificate has been received.Order dated 19.11.2018 by SCDRC,Chandigarh as C-10</p>','<ol><li>To direct the respondent to handover the possession of the apartment complete in all respect along with the specifications as provided in the brochure (C-1) &amp; Letter (C-3), along with the interest for the delay in possession, to be calculated w.e.f. 20.05.2017 till the date of actual delivery of possession after obtaining the completion certificate.</li><li>To direct the respondent not to charge Rs. 314000/- towards the enhanced area as there has been no change in the area of the flat.The respondent has arbitrarily increased the area. Moreover it has never informed the complainant that area will be increased. It is only in August, 2018 vide letter Annexure C-6, it informed that area has been increased.</li><li>To direct the respondent not to charge Rs. 78912/- towards the maintenance advance of two years.</li></ol>',0.00,5246662.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<ol><li>To direct the respondent to complete all the pending work and complete the same as per the specifications as mentioned in the brochure (C-1) &amp; letter (C-3)</li><li>To direct the respondent to provide all the common facilities</li></ol>','1','','2014-05-01 00:00:00','2014-05-20 00:00:00','Flat No.50, Tower A, 5th Floor, Type- 3BHK, Super Area 1950 sq ft','','',2,0,0,0,'rerafilingformm','2019-01-30 12:35:53.000','rerafilingformm','2019-01-30 12:35:53.000'),(956,1132,'1132',1193,'109a020f-7ac8-4af7-9194-064fff6a2fe0','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-23 21:11:38.000','Trilok Singh','parveen.ch.2@gmail.com',8882950006,0,0,'Ward No. 10, Balachaur','tehsil Balachaur',28,527,'144521','1','Ward No. 10, Balachaur','tehsil Balachaur',28,527,'144521','PARVEEN CHAUDHARY','parveen.ch.2@gmail.com',8882950006,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PM0010','Industrial knowledge (fashion Technology) Park at sector 90 SAS Nagar','Chandigarh overseas Pvt. Ltd','jbp@j90.in',0,1149879480,'M/s. Chandigarh Overseas Pvt. Ltd., SCO 249, Sector 44-C, Chandigarh.','',6,128,'160047','1','M/s. Chandigarh Overseas Pvt. Ltd., SCO 249, Sector 44-C, Chandigarh.','',6,128,'160047','1','<p>1. That the respondent M/s Chandigarh overseas Pvt. Ltd launched a scheme called “Small Investors Scheme” vide which a share in design studio of an area measuring 100 sq feet on the 4th floors of Industrial Knowledge(Fashion Technology) Park Sector 90, SAS Nagar was offered to the Prospector Buyer(s) on the free hold basis as a co-owner of  Design Studio.\r\n</p><p>2.	That the complainant Trilok Singh submitted application No. 104045 dated 18.01.2008 for purchase of one unit i.e. measuring 100 Sq feet for total consideration of Rs. 6,50,000/- and  again he purchased six more unit @ Rs. 6,50,000/- per unit, vide another Developer Buyer Agreement dated  18.03.2018 and lease deed was executed between complainant and respondent No. 2.  As per above said agreement, complainant paid        Rs. 50,000/- to respondent No. 1 vide receipt dated 18.01.2008 and further sum of Rs. 34,56,000/- was paid to respondent vide receipt dated 18.03.2008.  Further Rs. 5,26,000/- was paid to respondent No. 1 vide receipt dated 19.03.2008.  Complainant had paid sum of                 Rs. 40,32,000/- for purchase of said seven units to respondents.\r\n</p><p>3.	That as per Developer Buyer Agreements the possession was to be delivered after 30 months from the date of start of construction, but till filing of the complaint, respondent has failed to deliver physical possession of said units to complainant.&nbsp; An additional lease agreement was also made as mentioned in para 5th of the developer buyer agreement regarding rent with M/s Green Field Sites Management pvt ltd and no rent has been paid till now as mentioned in the agreement.</p><p>4. that complainant is filing the complaint through Attorney Bhupinder Singh</p>','<p><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 115%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">It is therefore submitted through this complaint\r\nthat the respondents have failed to comply with the conditions mentioned in the developer buyer agreement so the respondents may be directed to give the possession of units as per the\r\ndeveloper buyer agreements dated 31.01.2008 &amp; 18.03.2008 along with the\r\nrent or the interest as described in the agreements qua and if the respondent\r\ndo not give the possession as per the agreements qua, in that event the amount\r\nof Rs. 40,32,000/- along with the interest @ Rs. 1% per month on the principle\r\namount may be paid to the complainant.</span><br></p>',4550000.00,4032000.00,'2010-07-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;\r\nmso-add-space:auto;text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;text-indent:\r\n-18.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">1.</span><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 14px; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">That\r\nduring the pendency of the complaint the property of respondent may be attached\r\nand amount paid by the complainant to the respondent may be got returned.</span><o:p></o:p></span></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','2008-01-31 00:00:00','floor no. 4, block A2 Industrial Knowledge (fashion Technology) Park, sector 90, SAS Nagar (Punjab)','','',2,0,0,0,'parveenchaudhary','2019-01-30 14:21:51.000','parveenchaudhary','2019-01-30 14:21:51.000'),(957,1132,'1132',1193,'109a020f-7ac8-4af7-9194-064fff6a2fe0','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-02-04 10:39:08.000','Trilok Singh','parveen.ch.2@gmail.com',8882950006,0,0,'Ward No. 10, Balachaur','tehsil Balachaur',28,527,'144521','1','Ward No. 10, Balachaur','tehsil Balachaur',28,527,'144521','PARVEEN CHAUDHARY','parveen.ch.2@gmail.com',8882950006,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PM0010','Industrial knowledge (fashion Technology) Park at sector 90 SAS Nagar','Chandigarh overseas Pvt. Ltd','jbp@j90.in',0,1149879480,'M/s. Chandigarh Overseas Pvt. Ltd., SCO 249, Sector 44-C, Chandigarh.','',6,128,'160047','1','M/s. Chandigarh Overseas Pvt. Ltd., SCO 249, Sector 44-C, Chandigarh.','',6,128,'160047','1','<p>1. That the respondent M/s Chandigarh overseas Pvt. Ltd launched a scheme called “Small Investors Scheme” vide which a share in design studio of an area measuring 100 sq feet on the 4th floors of Industrial Knowledge(Fashion Technology) Park Sector 90, SAS Nagar was offered to the Prospector Buyer(s) on the free hold basis as a co-owner of  Design Studio.\r\n</p><p>2.	That the complainant Trilok Singh submitted application No. 104045 dated 18.01.2008 for purchase of one unit i.e. measuring 100 Sq feet for total consideration of Rs. 6,50,000/- and  again he purchased six more unit @ Rs. 6,50,000/- per unit, vide another Developer Buyer Agreement dated  18.03.2018 and lease deed was executed between complainant and respondent No. 2.  As per above said agreement, complainant paid        Rs. 50,000/- to respondent No. 1 vide receipt dated 18.01.2008 and further sum of Rs. 34,56,000/- was paid to respondent vide receipt dated 18.03.2008.  Further Rs. 5,26,000/- was paid to respondent No. 1 vide receipt dated 19.03.2008.  Complainant had paid sum of                 Rs. 40,32,000/- for purchase of said seven units to respondents.\r\n</p><p>3.	That as per Developer Buyer Agreements the possession was to be delivered after 30 months from the date of start of construction, but till filing of the complaint, respondent has failed to deliver physical possession of said units to complainant.&nbsp; An additional lease agreement was also made as mentioned in para 5th of the developer buyer agreement regarding rent with M/s Green Field Sites Management pvt ltd and no rent has been paid till now as mentioned in the agreement.</p><p>4. that complainant is filing the complaint through Attorney Bhupinder Singh</p>','<p><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 115%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">It is therefore submitted through this complaint\r\nthat the respondents have failed to comply with the conditions mentioned in the developer buyer agreement so the respondents may be directed to give the possession of units as per the\r\ndeveloper buyer agreements dated 31.01.2008 &amp; 18.03.2008 along with the\r\nrent or the interest as described in the agreements qua and if the respondent\r\ndo not give the possession as per the agreements qua, in that event the amount\r\nof Rs. 40,32,000/- along with the interest @ Rs. 1% per month on the principle\r\namount may be paid to the complainant.</span><br></p>',4550000.00,4032000.00,'2010-07-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;\r\nmso-add-space:auto;text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;text-indent:\r\n-18.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">1.</span><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 14px; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">That\r\nduring the pendency of the complaint the property of respondent may be attached\r\nand amount paid by the complainant to the respondent may be got returned.</span><o:p></o:p></span></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','2008-01-31 00:00:00','floor no. 4, block A2 Industrial Knowledge (fashion Technology) Park, sector 90, SAS Nagar (Punjab)','','',1,1,0,0,'parveenchaudhary','2019-01-30 14:22:14.000','parveenchaudhary','2019-01-30 14:22:14.000'),(958,1288,'1288',1369,'0e157dcb-4e45-4c7a-a3cd-d4664ae34cf8','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Uniroyal Industries Limited through Akhil Mahajan','csvedparkash@gmail.com',9876011456,0,0,'Plot No. 365, Insdustral Area','Phase-II, Pachkula',13,15,'134113','1','Plot No. 365, Insdustral Area','Phase-II, Pachkula',13,15,'134113','Ved Parkash','csvedparkash@gmail.com',7837223098,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0124','Acme Eden Court','Acme Builders Pvt. Ltd','contact@acmebuilders.in',8592122888,1724625000,'GH-10, JLPL','Sector-91 Mohali',28,507,'160032','1','GH-10, JLPL','Sector-91 Mohali',28,507,'160032','1','<p>aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa</p>','<p>bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb</p>',9087212.00,8609752.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa</p>','1','','2012-12-15 00:00:00','2012-12-13 00:00:00','Flat No. 1002, 10th Floor, Tower-1, Acme Eden Court, GH-10, JLPL Sector-90-91, Mohali','','',2,0,0,0,'uniroyalindustries','2019-01-30 15:14:08.000','uniroyalindustries','2019-01-30 15:14:08.000'),(959,1168,'1168',1233,'d2a1f0ed-7a16-44e8-9590-5e568e27fcb7','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-01-30 15:30:09.000','Malkit Singh','malkit.singh@nabard.org',6239648955,1722972303,0,'Flat no. B 303 ','NABARD Vihar',28,507,'160062','1','Flat no. B 303 ','NABARD Vihar',28,507,'160062','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0255','Sunny Enclave - Chando Gobindgarg','J S Bajwa','bajwadeveloperltd@gmail.com',9814014381,1605035000,'Bajwa Developers Ltd., Sunny Business Centre','5th Floor, New Sunny Enclave, Kharar, Mohali',28,507,'140301','1','Bajwa Developers Ltd., Sunny Business Centre','5th Floor, New Sunny Enclave, Kharar, Mohali',28,507,'140301','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span lang=\"EN-ZW\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Georgia&quot;,serif\">I ,\r\nMalkit Singh alongwith my wife Mrs . Namarta Singh had purchased a 200 sq&nbsp; yards plot number 2225 in Sector 123 Jandpur\r\n, Kharar , Distt. Mohali on 31.12.2013. <o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span lang=\"EN-ZW\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Georgia&quot;,serif\">At the\r\ntime of purchase in addition to consideration of Rs. 17.00 Lakh given for purchase,\r\nRs. 1.70 Lakh was incurred as registry charges &amp; Rs. 10000 as transfer charges,\r\nI was also made to pay Rs. 3.80 Lakhs as External Development Charges (EDC)\r\nwith a commitment to develop the roads &amp; provide other basic amenities within a year with further grace period of three months from the date of sale deed. But respondent failed to deliver possession of the plot and also develop the project with promised facilities and amenities.&nbsp; The respondent has not demarcated the plot and only certificate of possession was incorporated in the sale deed. No development work has been&nbsp; done at the spot and its also not possible to identify the said plot at the site.<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span lang=\"EN-ZW\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Georgia&quot;,serif\">Sir , a\r\nperiod of nearly 5 years have since lapsed , the said plot till date doesn’t\r\nhave access to pucca road in absence of which we are neither able to construct\r\nhouse for self-living. We\r\nhave been visiting the developer from time to time but no attention has been\r\npaid in this regard.&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><span lang=\"EN-ZW\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Georgia&quot;,serif;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-language:EN-ZW\">The developer may kindly be directed to provide all amenities &amp; facilities as promised and get the plot demarcated at the spot to be identifiable and to develop\r\nthe road immediately to enable us to construct the house.\r\nDelayed development has deprived us to construct our house. Our valuable hard earned is blocked and we are suffering losses as construction cost is increasing day by day. Apart from it, our plans to shift to the residential unit have been shattered. We are entitled to get interest as prescribed under RERA for the delayed period as no facility or amenities as promised have been provided at spot by the respondent.<o:p></o:p></span></p>',2260000.00,2260000.00,'2014-12-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><span lang=\"EN-ZW\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Georgia&quot;,serif;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-language:EN-ZW\">Till the time development is done, developer may\r\nkindly be directed to pay interest @18% or as prescribed under RERA on all the expenses incurred in this\r\nregard i.e. on Rs. 22.60 Lakhs (details as above ) from the date of purchase of\r\nthe said plot i.e. 31.12.2013 as an opportunity cost of all options lost during\r\nthe period of 5 years.&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p>','1','','2013-12-31 00:00:00','2013-12-31 00:00:00','Plot no not allotted','','',2,0,0,0,'malkit.singh@nabard.org','2019-01-30 15:29:28.000','malkit.singh@nabard.org','2019-01-30 15:29:28.000'),(960,1289,'1289',1367,'5dd7625b-2bb2-4b5e-8466-b20eef3fe061','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Rupinder  Kaur Narang','sanjeevangrish@gmail.com',9915511386,0,0,'hno.2 north east bibi wala road  ','',28,84,'151001','1','386','sector15',13,15,'134113','Sanjeev Sharma','sanjeevangrish@gmail.com',9915511386,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PM0084','Country colonisers pvt ltd','country colonisers pvt ltd','estate@thewavegroup.com',0,0,'Rayon Silk Mills  adjoining coca cola depot g.t. road Chhehtra ','',28,39,'143105','1','Rayon Silk Mills  adjoining coca cola depot g.t. road Chhehtra ','',28,39,'143105','1','<p>That Expression of Interest was signed on 16.10.2012. Copy of application form is annexed as ANNEXURE C-1. \r\n</p><p>\r\n That the complainants entered into an Apartment Allottee Arrangement dated 17.07.2013 . copy of the said Apartment Allottee Arrangement is annexed as ANNEXURE C-2.&nbsp;</p><p>\r\n</p><p>&nbsp;That    the complainants  were allotted    duplex    in  Group   Housing Development named Wave Estate. The    Apartment    Number    as    per    the    agreement was Wave   Garden   Tower    Bougainvillea,   Type : Duplex,    at   Ground Floor    at  (Wave Estates)    Sector 85,    Mohali,           having chargeable super area of approximately 3275 sq. Ft. And having built up area of 2603.8 Sq. Ft.&nbsp;</p><p>That it was agreed upon in the agreement as per clause 5.1 that the possession shall be handed over by the respondent complete in all respect within 36 months from the date of signing of the agreement , resultantly the possession of the flat was to be offered by  16th July 2016. \r\n</p><p>That the  complainants as such till date has made a payment of total sum of Rs.13,393,760 /- as  demanded by the respondents and copy of statement of account is annexed as ANNEXURE C-3. \r\n However the possession has not been offered till date . so refund is prayed for</p><p>	\r\n</p><p><br></p>','<p><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:Calibri;\r\nmso-fareast-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN;mso-fareast-language:\r\nEN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\">refund of deposited amount ie 13,393,761/ along\r\nwith interest at the rate of 18% p.a. besides compensation/damages of\r\nRs.10,00,000/- and Rs.1,10,000/- as cost of litigation as the developer has failed to offer possession so in terms of section 18 of The Real Estate (Regulation and development) Act, 2016 refund be allowed and interest be awarded as per section 16 of The Punjab&nbsp;</span><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">Real Estate (Regulation and development) Act, 2017.</span></font></p>',14448325.00,13393761.00,'2016-07-16 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">That\r\nRespondents be restrained from issuing any fresh demands or cancelling the\r\napartment as complainants are seeking refund of their amount.&nbsp; &nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','2013-07-17 00:00:00','001, Ground Floor, Sector 85, Mohali, Tower  Bougainvillea at wave garden','','',2,0,0,0,'rajinder112','2019-01-30 18:29:42.000','rajinder112','2019-01-30 18:29:42.000'),(961,1290,'1290',1370,'ffcfd84d-7b8f-405c-8938-659860f80b71','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Satwant kaur sangha','mandeepkhuranj@gmail.com',9417422227,0,0,'Income Tax Office Sangha Complex','Mr. Ambadkar Nagar, Batala Road',28,232,'143001','1','Income Tax Office Sangha Complex','Mr. Ambadkar Nagar, Batala Road',28,232,'143001','Amarbir Dhaliwal','amarbir67@hotmai