text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\">The &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Apartment &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Number&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; as&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;per&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; the&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; agreement was &nbsp;01 at Wave&nbsp;&nbsp; Garden&nbsp;&nbsp; Tower&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;Bougainvillea,&nbsp;&nbsp; Type : Duplex, &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;at&nbsp;&nbsp; Ground Floor&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; at&nbsp; (Wave Estates) &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Sector 85,&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Mohali,&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; having chargeable super area of approximately 3275 sq. Ft. it was agreed upon in the agreement as per clause 5.1 that the possession shall be handed over by the respondent complete in all respect within 36 months from the date of signing of the agreement ie 16.07.2016</span></p><p style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 16px; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: 22.08px; margin-bottom: 13.33px; margin-top: 0px; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-decoration: none; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; word-spacing: 0px;\" dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;; font-size: 18.66px; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: 400; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\">complainants as such till date has made a payment of total sum of Rs.13,393,760 /-</span></p><p><br style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 16px; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-decoration: none; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; word-spacing: 0px;\"></p><p style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 16px; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: 22.08px; margin-bottom: 13.33px; margin-top: 0px; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-decoration: none; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; word-spacing: 0px;\" dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;; font-size: 18.66px; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: 400; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\">That the complainants cannot wait indefinitely for the possession to be offered and complainant has taken loan also</span></p><p><br style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 16px; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-decoration: none; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; word-spacing: 0px;\"><b></b><i></i><u></u><sub></sub><sup></sup><strike></strike><br></p>','<br id=\"docs-internal-guid-7b04df0e-7fff-eabc-df9a-e24ac9d76690\" style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 16px; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-decoration: none; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; word-spacing: 0px;\"><p style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 16px; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: 22.08px; margin-bottom: 13.33px; margin-top: 0px; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-decoration: none; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; word-spacing: 0px;\" dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;; font-size: 18.66px; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: 400; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\">In view of the facts mentioned in paragraph 4 above, the complainant prays for the following relief(s) That the respondents have failed to complete the project and have defaulted in their obligations as such the complainants are entitled for filing of the present complaint for the refund of the amount deposited by the complainants as per section 18 and 19 of The Real Estate (development and regulation ) act, 2016 and section 16 of The Punjab Real Estate (development and regulation ) act, 2017.</span></p><br style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 16px; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-decoration: none; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; word-spacing: 0px;\">',0.00,13393760.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p><br></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','apartment no.1 BOUGAINVILLEA GROUND FLOOR ','','',1,0,0,0,'rajinder112','2019-01-31 13:57:57.000','rajinder112','2019-01-31 13:57:57.000'),(964,1289,'1289',1367,'5dd7625b-2bb2-4b5e-8466-b20eef3fe061','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-02-15 20:42:40.000','Rupinder  Kaur Narang','sanjeevangrish@gmail.com',9915511386,0,0,'hno.2 north east bibi wala road  ','',28,84,'151001','1','386','sector15',13,15,'134113','Sanjeev Sharma','sanjeevangrish@gmail.com',9915511386,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PM0084','Country colonisers pvt ltd','country colonisers pvt ltd','estate@thewavegroup.com',0,0,'Rayon Silk Mills  adjoining coca cola depot g.t. road Chhehtra ','',28,39,'143105','1','Rayon Silk Mills  adjoining coca cola depot g.t. road Chhehtra ','',28,39,'143105','1','<p>That Expression of Interest was signed on 16.10.2012. Copy of application form is annexed as ANNEXURE C-1. \r\n</p><p>\r\n That the complainants entered into an Apartment Allottee Arrangement dated 17.07.2013 . copy of the said Apartment Allottee Arrangement is annexed as ANNEXURE C-2.&nbsp;</p><p>\r\n</p><p>&nbsp;That    the complainants  were allotted    duplex    in  Group   Housing Development named Wave Estate. The    Apartment    Number    as    per    the    agreement was Wave   Garden   Tower    Bougainvillea,   Type : Duplex,    at   Ground Floor    at  (Wave Estates)    Sector 85,    Mohali,           having chargeable super area of approximately 3275 sq. Ft. And having built up area of 2603.8 Sq. Ft.&nbsp;</p><p>That it was agreed upon in the agreement as per clause 5.1 that the possession shall be handed over by the respondent complete in all respect within 36 months from the date of signing of the agreement , resultantly the possession of the flat was to be offered by  16th July 2016. \r\n</p><p>That the  complainants as such till date has made a payment of total sum of Rs.13,393,760 /- as  demanded by the respondents and copy of statement of account is annexed as ANNEXURE C-3. \r\n However the possession has not been offered till date . so refund is prayed for</p><p>	\r\n</p><p><br></p>','<p><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:Calibri;\r\nmso-fareast-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN;mso-fareast-language:\r\nEN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\">refund of deposited amount ie 13,393,761/ along\r\nwith interest at the rate of 18% p.a. besides compensation/damages of\r\nRs.10,00,000/- and Rs.1,10,000/- as cost of litigation as the developer has failed to offer possession so in terms of section 18 of The Real Estate (Regulation and development) Act, 2016 refund be allowed and interest be awarded as per section 16 of The Punjab&nbsp;</span><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">Real Estate (Regulation and development) Act, 2017.</span></font></p>',14448325.00,13393761.00,'2016-07-16 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">That\r\nRespondents be restrained from issuing any fresh demands or cancelling the\r\napartment as complainants are seeking refund of their amount.&nbsp; &nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','2013-07-17 00:00:00','001, Ground Floor, Sector 85, Mohali, Tower  Bougainvillea at wave garden','','',1,1,0,0,'rajinder112','2019-01-31 17:36:03.000','rajinder112','2019-01-31 17:36:03.000'),(965,1194,'1194',1281,'ecd6bbdb-27b0-4972-ac46-2f0682f35b3d','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-01-07 13:18:44.000','Sundeep Singh Pawar','gaurav.chopra@hotmail.com',9814013127,0,0,'House No. 360','Phase IV ',28,507,'160059','0','House No. 607','sector 18B',6,128,'160018','Gaurav Chopra','gaurav.chopra@hotmail.com',9814013127,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0119','MOHALI HILLs','Emaar MGF Land Ltd','sorabh.kakar@emaarmgf.com',0,0,'Emaar MGF Land Ltd','40, Central Plaza, Ground Floor, Sector 105 Mohali',28,507,'140306','1','Emaar MGF Land Ltd','40, Central Plaza, Ground Floor, Sector 105 Mohali',28,507,'140306','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">i)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Allotment Letter:24.4.07 <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">ii)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Buyer’s Agreement:10.4.08 <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">iii)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Agreement executed between Sundeep Singh\r\nPawar and Mrs. Harinder Kaur Pawar and the Respondent in respect of the Unit\r\nNo. H1-FPH-PH-01 for a total sale consideration of Rs. 98,59,200/- of super\r\narea of 2900 sq. Ft. Subsequently, the Unit was changed TVM-H1-F10-1001.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">iv)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; On the basis of an affidavit sworn by the\r\nCo-Applicant Kamaljit Kaur Pawar, an endorsement dated 10.4.08 was made in the\r\nAgreement dated 10.4.08 whereby the co-allottees of the Allotted Unit No. were\r\nformally recorded as the Applicants herein viz. Sundeep Singh Pawar and\r\nKamaljit Kaur Pawar. Subsequently, the Allotted Unit was changed to\r\nTVM-L2-F12-1202. Further, vide an Addendum, due to modification in the layout\r\nplan, Unit No. TVM-L2-F12-1202, Sector-105, Mohali Hills, Mohali was changed to\r\nUnit No. TVM-L2-F08-802 having a super area of 2600 sq. ft for which the total\r\nsale consideration was fixed at Rs. 83,20,505/- as indicated in the letter\r\ndated 15.9.10 issued by the Respondent. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-32.25pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">v)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Construction Linked Instalment Plan<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-32.25pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">vi) &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Amount paid upto 23.10.13: Rs. 72,61,148/- <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-32.25pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">vii)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; As per Clause 21.1 of the Agreement read\r\nwith Clause 23.1 possession of the Allotted Unit was required to be handed over\r\nto the Applicants by the Respondent positively on or before 24.7.10.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-32.25pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">viii)&nbsp;&nbsp; Aggrieved by the omission of the Respondent,\r\nthe Applicants had written a letter/e-mail to the Respondent for rescinding the\r\ncontract and for seeking refund of the principal amount paid by the Applicants\r\nin respect of the Allotted Unit alongwith interest.&nbsp; Till date, however, the aforesaid demand\r\nraised by the Applicants has not been acceded to by the Respondent.&nbsp; <o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-32.25pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">ix)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; In spite of the fact that the Applicants\r\nhad sought refund of the principal amount alongwith interest, the Respondents\r\nhave arbitrarily continued to issue Demand Notices to the Applicants for\r\npayment of instalments as per the payment schedule appended with the Buyer’s\r\nagreement.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-32.25pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:1.0in;text-align:justify;text-indent:\r\n-.5in;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n200%;font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">i)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Refund of an amount of Rs. 72,61,148/-\r\npaid by the Applicants alongwith interest (highest marginal cost of lending\r\nrate of the State Bank of India + 2%) from the respective dates of deposit till\r\nactual realization as per Sections 18 and 19(4) of the Act read with Rule 16 of\r\nthe Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:1.0in;text-align:justify;text-indent:\r\n-.5in;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n200%;font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">ii)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Any other relief which the Applicants are\r\nentitled for under the Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Act, 2016 and\r\nthe Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-32.25pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>',8320505.00,7261148.00,'2010-07-24 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>..</p>','1','','2007-04-24 00:00:00','2008-04-10 00:00:00','Unit No. TVM-L2-F08-802 ‘The Views’ at Mohali Hills, Sector-105, SAS Nagar, District Mohali, Punjab.','','',2,0,0,0,'sundeepsinghpawar','2019-01-31 20:04:30.000','sundeepsinghpawar','2019-01-31 20:04:30.000'),(966,1194,'1194',1281,'ecd6bbdb-27b0-4972-ac46-2f0682f35b3d','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-01-07 13:18:44.000','Sundeep Singh Pawar','gaurav.chopra@hotmail.com',9814013127,0,0,'House No. 360','Phase IV ',28,507,'160059','0','House No. 607','sector 18B',6,128,'160018','Gaurav Chopra','gaurav.chopra@hotmail.com',9814013127,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0119','MOHALI HILLs','Emaar MGF Land Ltd','sorabh.kakar@emaarmgf.com',0,0,'Emaar MGF Land Ltd','40, Central Plaza, Ground Floor, Sector 105 Mohali',28,507,'140306','1','Emaar MGF Land Ltd','40, Central Plaza, Ground Floor, Sector 105 Mohali',28,507,'140306','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">i)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Allotment Letter:24.4.07 <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">ii)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Buyer’s Agreement:10.4.08 <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">iii)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Agreement executed between Sundeep Singh\r\nPawar and Mrs. Harinder Kaur Pawar and the Respondent in respect of the Unit\r\nNo. H1-FPH-PH-01 for a total sale consideration of Rs. 98,59,200/- of super\r\narea of 2900 sq. Ft. Subsequently, the Unit was changed TVM-H1-F10-1001.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">iv)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; On the basis of an affidavit sworn by the\r\nCo-Applicant Kamaljit Kaur Pawar, an endorsement dated 10.4.08 was made in the\r\nAgreement dated 10.4.08 whereby the co-allottees of the Allotted Unit No. were\r\nformally recorded as the Applicants herein viz. Sundeep Singh Pawar and\r\nKamaljit Kaur Pawar. Subsequently, the Allotted Unit was changed to\r\nTVM-L2-F12-1202. Further, vide an Addendum, due to modification in the layout\r\nplan, Unit No. TVM-L2-F12-1202, Sector-105, Mohali Hills, Mohali was changed to\r\nUnit No. TVM-L2-F08-802 having a super area of 2600 sq. ft for which the total\r\nsale consideration was fixed at Rs. 83,20,505/- as indicated in the letter\r\ndated 15.9.10 issued by the Respondent. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-32.25pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">v)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Construction Linked Instalment Plan<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-32.25pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">vi) &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Amount paid upto 23.10.13: Rs. 72,61,148/- <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-32.25pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">vii)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; As per Clause 21.1 of the Agreement read\r\nwith Clause 23.1 possession of the Allotted Unit was required to be handed over\r\nto the Applicants by the Respondent positively on or before 24.7.10.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-32.25pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">viii)&nbsp;&nbsp; Aggrieved by the omission of the Respondent,\r\nthe Applicants had written a letter/e-mail to the Respondent for rescinding the\r\ncontract and for seeking refund of the principal amount paid by the Applicants\r\nin respect of the Allotted Unit alongwith interest.&nbsp; Till date, however, the aforesaid demand\r\nraised by the Applicants has not been acceded to by the Respondent.&nbsp; <o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-32.25pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">ix)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; In spite of the fact that the Applicants\r\nhad sought refund of the principal amount alongwith interest, the Respondents\r\nhave arbitrarily continued to issue Demand Notices to the Applicants for\r\npayment of instalments as per the payment schedule appended with the Buyer’s\r\nagreement.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-32.25pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:1.0in;text-align:justify;text-indent:\r\n-.5in;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n200%;font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">i)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Refund of an amount of Rs. 72,61,148/-\r\npaid by the Applicants alongwith interest (highest marginal cost of lending\r\nrate of the State Bank of India + 2%) from the respective dates of deposit till\r\nactual realization as per Sections 18 and 19(4) of the Act read with Rule 16 of\r\nthe Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:1.0in;text-align:justify;text-indent:\r\n-.5in;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n200%;font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">ii)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Any other relief which the Applicants are\r\nentitled for under the Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Act, 2016 and\r\nthe Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-32.25pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>',8320505.00,7261148.00,'2010-07-24 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>..</p>','1','','2007-04-24 00:00:00','2008-04-10 00:00:00','Unit No. TVM-L2-F08-802 ‘The Views’ at Mohali Hills, Sector-105, SAS Nagar, District Mohali, Punjab.','','',2,0,0,0,'sundeepsinghpawar','2019-01-31 20:05:42.000','sundeepsinghpawar','2019-01-31 20:05:42.000'),(967,1192,'1192',1254,'f975078e-bd45-46ae-9ad3-968463b14972','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-19 18:18:30.000','Ranjeev  Rai','gaurav.chopra@hotmail.com',9814013127,0,0,'House No. 360','Phase IV ',28,507,'160059','1','House No. 607','sector 18B',6,128,'160018','Gaurav Chopra','gaurav.chopra@hotmail.com',9814013127,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0119','Mohali Hills','M/s. EMAAR MGF Land Ltd','sorabh.kakkar@emmarmgf.in',0,0,'EMAAR MGF Land Ltd','40, Ground Floor, Central Plaza, Sector 105',28,507,'140306','1','EMAAR MGF Land Ltd','40, Ground Floor, Central Plaza, Sector 105',28,507,'140306','1','<p>i) Applicant: Ranjeev Singh Rai (name incorrectly stated as Rajeev Singh Rai)&nbsp;</p><p>ii) Application:14.3.2007&nbsp;</p><p>iii) Buyer’s Agreement:1.9.2009&nbsp;</p><p>iv) Construction Linked Installment Plan for total Consideration:Rs. 99,15,199</p><p>v) Amount paid till 21.8.2012:Rs. 86,41,522/-</p><p>vi) As per Clause 21.1 of the Apartment Buyer’s Agreement, the Respondent was under a contractual obligation to handover possession of the Allotted Unit within a period of 36 months from the date of allotment with a further relaxation of 90 days over and above the stipulated time period for the purpose of applying for and obtaining an Occupation Certificate in respect of the Group Housing Complex.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>vii) Date of Possession as per Clause 21.1 of the Agreement r/w Clause 23.1:on or before 1.12.2012.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>viii) Till date, however, despite a lapse of more than 6 years, possession of the Allotted Unit has neither been offered nor handed over to the Applicants and this wilful omission and lapse on the part of the Respondent constitutes a wilful and material breach of the Agreement executed between the parties.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>ix) Aggrieved by the aforesaid omission of the Respondent,the Applicant had written a letter/e-mail dated 9.2.2017 to the Respondent for rescinding the contract and for seeking refund of the principal amount paid by the Applicant in respect of the Allotted Unit alongwith interest. Till date,however, the aforesaid demand raised by the Applicant has not been acceded to by the Respondent and thus, vide the instant complaint, the Applicants seek refund of the monies paid by him to the Respondent alongwith interest and compensation.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>x) In spite of the fact that the Applicant had sought refund of the principal amount paid by the Applicants alongwith interest, the Respondents have arbitrarily continued to issue Demand Notices to the Applicant for payment of instalments as per the payment schedule.</p>','<p>i) Refund of an amount of Rs. 86,41,522/- paid by the Applicants alongwith interest (highest marginal cost of lending rate of the State Bank of India + 2%) from the respective dates of deposit till actual realization as per Sections 18 and 19(4) of the Act read with Rule 16 of the Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017.</p><p>ii) Any other relief which the Applicants are entitled for under the Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Act, 2016 and the Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017.&nbsp;</p><div><br></div>',9915199.00,8641522.00,'2012-12-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>N.A.</p>','1','','2007-03-14 00:00:00','2009-09-01 00:00:00','H3 FPH PH04, TOWER H, THE VIEWS AT MOHALLI HILLS','','',2,0,0,0,'Ranjeevrai','2019-01-31 20:10:05.000','Ranjeevrai','2019-01-31 20:10:05.000'),(968,1200,'1200',1272,'51d11184-3a8e-4a16-9673-559a2472f6c0','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-02-01 11:53:54.000','Rajesh Verma','rajfine123@gmail.com',9991203671,0,0,'Flat no 515 tower b4 The Eminence','Zirakpur, distt s.a.s. nagar',28,507,'140603','1','Dena bank dera bassi','Ambala Chandigarh highway,dera bassi',28,507,'140507','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0396','SUSHMA VALENCIA','SUKSHA DEVELOPERS PVT. LTD.','ankitg@sushmabuildtech.com',0,0,'unit no b-107 business complex at elante mall,first floor','ind. area, phase 1,chandigarh 160009',6,128,'160009','1','unit no b-107 business complex at elante mall,first floor','ind. area, phase 1,chandigarh 160009',6,128,'160009','1','<p>&nbsp;</p><div>\r\n<p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; font-family: roboto; font-size: 14px;\">I have \r\nbooked a flat in feb 2018 in sushma valencia( builder name is SUKSHA DEVELOPERS \r\nPVT. LTD, PBRERA-SAS80-PR0396) at price 62 lakh for which i have paid rs. 620000 \r\nto builder through cheques . I have requested them several times to issue me \r\nreceipts but every time neither they issued receipts nor done any agreement with \r\nme..........After a lot of harassment, i have decided to cancel the flat.for \r\ncancellation, builder issued me their own proforma for flat cancellation. I have \r\nsubmitted the affidavit with clauses (i),(ii) &amp; (iii), but they tampered \r\nthis affidavit and inserted clause (iv) to grab my hard earned money.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; font-family: roboto; font-size: 14px;\">They have \r\nrefunded me rs. 525424/- and refused to pay remaining rs. 94576/- which is \r\ncompletely illegal and lawful...without receipts, without agreement,they should \r\nnot deduct .</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; font-family: roboto; font-size: 14px;\">Please Please&nbsp;\r\nprovide me justice so that i can recover my hard earned money from builder.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; font-family: roboto; font-size: 14px;\">Thanks and \r\nregards.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 10px; font-family: roboto; font-size: 14px;\">Rajesh \r\nverma</p></div>','<p>&nbsp;1. My pending amount 94576 rs.</p><p>2. interest of rs. 620000 which builder has used for more than 8 months till now</p><p>3. mental harassment charges.</p><p>4. legal notice fee 2000 rs.&nbsp;</p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>&nbsp;mentioned in point 5.</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',1,1,0,0,'RAJESHVERMA3671','2019-02-01 11:53:45.000','RAJESHVERMA3671','2019-02-01 11:53:45.000'),(969,1168,'1168',1233,'d2a1f0ed-7a16-44e8-9590-5e568e27fcb7','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-02-01 12:25:39.000','Malkit Singh','malkit.singh@nabard.org',6239648955,1722972303,0,'Flat no. B 303 ','NABARD Vihar',28,507,'160062','1','Flat no. B 303 ','NABARD Vihar',28,507,'160062','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0255','Sunny Enclave ','J S Bajwa','bajwadeveloperltd@gmail.com',9814014381,1605035000,'Sunny Enclave ','5th Floor, New Sunny Enclave, Kharar, Mohali',28,507,'140301','1','Bajwa Developers Ltd., Sunny Business Centre','5th Floor, New Sunny Enclave, Kharar, Mohali',28,507,'140301','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span lang=\"EN-ZW\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Georgia&quot;,serif\">I ,\r\nMalkit Singh alongwith my wife Mrs . Namarta Singh had purchased a 200 sq&nbsp; yards plot number 2225 in Sector 123 Jandpur\r\n, Kharar , Distt. Mohali on 31.12.2013. <o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span lang=\"EN-ZW\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Georgia&quot;,serif\">At the\r\ntime of purchase in addition to consideration of Rs. 17.00 Lakh given for purchase,\r\nRs. 1.70 Lakh was incurred as registry charges &amp; Rs. 10000 as transfer charges,\r\nI was also made to pay Rs. 3.80 Lakhs as External Development Charges (EDC)\r\nwith a commitment to develop the roads &amp; provide other basic amenities within a year with further grace period of three months from the date of sale deed. But respondent failed to deliver possession of the plot and also develop the project with promised facilities and amenities.&nbsp; The respondent has not demarcated the plot and only certificate of possession was incorporated in the sale deed. No development work has been&nbsp; done at the spot and its also not possible to identify the said plot at the site.<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span lang=\"EN-ZW\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Georgia&quot;,serif\">Sir , a\r\nperiod of nearly 5 years have since lapsed , the said plot till date doesn’t\r\nhave access to pucca road in absence of which we are neither able to construct\r\nhouse for self-living. We\r\nhave been visiting the developer from time to time but no attention has been\r\npaid in this regard.&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><span lang=\"EN-ZW\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Georgia&quot;,serif;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-language:EN-ZW\">The developer may kindly be directed to provide all amenities &amp; facilities as promised and get the plot demarcated at the spot to be identifiable and to develop\r\nthe road immediately to enable us to construct the house.\r\nDelayed development has deprived us to construct our house. Our valuable hard earned is blocked and we are suffering losses as construction cost is increasing day by day. Apart from it, our plans to shift to the residential unit have been shattered. We are entitled to get interest as prescribed under RERA for the delayed period as no facility or amenities as promised have been provided at spot by the respondent.<o:p></o:p></span></p>',2260000.00,2260000.00,'2014-12-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><span lang=\"EN-ZW\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Georgia&quot;,serif;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-language:EN-ZW\">Till the time development is done, developer may\r\nkindly be directed to pay interest @18% or as prescribed under RERA on all the expenses incurred in this\r\nregard i.e. on Rs. 22.60 Lakhs (details as above ) from the date of purchase of\r\nthe said plot i.e. 31.12.2013 as an opportunity cost of all options lost during\r\nthe period of 5 years.&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p>','1','','2013-12-31 00:00:00','2013-12-31 00:00:00','Plot no not allotted','','',1,1,0,0,'malkit.singh@nabard.org','2019-02-01 12:25:35.000','malkit.singh@nabard.org','2019-02-01 12:25:35.000'),(970,1292,'1292',1376,'0b9fb8a5-aba9-44ae-8b2e-dee11afdaf7d','FormTypeM',1,1,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Anaesthetic Gases P Ltd  Through Surinder Singh Virdi Managing Director','agplho22@gmail.com',9417004482,0,0,'SCO-841-842, IInd floor, Sector-22 A ','',6,128,'160022','1','SCO-841-842, IInd floor, Sector-22 A ','',6,128,'160022','Ved Parkash','csvedparkash@gmail.com',7837223098,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PC0006','International Trade Tower','M/s Omaxe Chandigarh Extension Developers P Ltd ','syediqbal@omaxe.com',8054002819,0,'Plot no.-6, Omaxe Sales office , Chandigarh Baddi Road, Mullanpur','',6,128,'140901','1','Plot no.-6, Omaxe Sales office , Chandigarh Baddi Road, Mullanpur','',6,128,'140901','1','<p>&nbsp;\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:6.8pt;margin-left:0cm;&#10;text-align:justify\"><b><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:9.5pt;font-family:&#10;Roboto;color:black;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">BRIEF FACTS OF THE CASE.</span></b><span style=\"box-sizing: border-box\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:9.5pt;&#10;font-family:Roboto;color:black;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">That initially,\r\nSurinder Singh Virdhi S/o Shri Man Singh, R/o House No. 199, Sector 16,\r\nChandigarh, booked Unit No 401-B, Fourth Floor, at India Trade Tower, located\r\nat Mullanpur, SAS Nagar, Mohali, Punjab on 06.01.2011 on the basis of\r\nrepresentations, warranties and commercial details shown in the Brochure of the\r\nM/s Omaxe Limited (hereinafter referred to as Respondent Company). A copy of\r\nBrochure and payment plan of the respondent company are attached as Annexure\r\nC/1.That Mr. Surinder Singh made initial booking and two other payments as per\r\nPayment Plan offered by the respondent company, amounting to Rs. 21.71,190/- as\r\ndetailed in Annexure C/2.The said office/unit was endorsed in the name of M/s\r\nAnaesthetic Gases Pvt. Limited (hereinafter referred to as the Complainant) by\r\nSurinder Singh Virdhi on 05.7.2011 as per document attached as Annexure C/3.The\r\nComplaint made further construction linked payments as per the demand notices\r\nissued from time to time by the respondent company amounting to Rs. 37,82,644/-\r\nas per details attached as Annexure C/4.The respondent company entered into\r\nagreement of sale (Annexed as C/5) with the applicant 03.06.2013 at a total\r\nconsideration of Rs. 77,33,504/- inclusive of PLC, Maintenance Security and\r\nAdditional cost. The allotted unit measured 135.83 sq. meters with a corner\r\nlocation as depicted in Brochure annexed above as C/1. That as per clause 26(a)\r\nof the said allotment letter/agreement for sale, the respondent company was to\r\noffer possession within 30 months from the start of construction i.e. thirty\r\nmonths from 21.05.2011 which arrives at 20.11.2013.Upon receipt of further\r\ndemand notices, the applicant/complainant made further payments amounting to\r\nRs. 7,53,336.35 as per details attached at Annexure C/6.The respondent company\r\nintimated the status of the project vide its letter dated 3.09.2015 attached as\r\nAnnexure C/7.</span></span><span style=\"font-size:9.5pt;font-family:Roboto;&#10;color:black\"></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:6.8pt;margin-left:0cm;&#10;text-align:justify;box-sizing: border-box;orphans: 2;-webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px;&#10;word-spacing:0px\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:9.5pt;font-family:Roboto;&#10;color:black;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\"><span style=\"box-sizing: border-box\">&nbsp;</span></span><span style=\"font-size:9.5pt;font-family:Roboto;color:black\"></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:6.8pt;margin-left:0cm;&#10;text-align:justify;box-sizing: border-box;orphans: 2;-webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px;&#10;word-spacing:0px\"><span style=\"font-size:9.5pt;font-family:Roboto;color:black\">&nbsp;</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\">&nbsp;</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><b></b><br></p><p><br></p>','<p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\">The respondent\r\ncompany offered fit out possession of the office/unit vide its letter dated\r\n28.03.2018 attached as Annexure C/8. The offer of possession was fit out and\r\ntentative in nature, without obtaining occupancy/completion certificate.\r\nMoreover, the area of the office/unit has been reduced to 101.81 sq. meters\r\nfrom 135.83 sq. meters and also changed the location of the allotted unit\r\nwithout the consent of the complainant.The complainant objected to the fit out offer\r\nof possession through its letters dated 30.03.2018 and 10.04.2018 attached as\r\nAnnexure C/9, but no reply has been received from the respondent company. The complainant\r\nhad filed a complaint before the State Consumer Disputes Redressal Commission,\r\nPunjab, Chandigarh attached as Annexure C/10, which was withdrawn by the\r\napplicant/complainant on technical grounds.That the above project of the\r\nrespondent is registered with RERA with Registration Number PBRERA-SAS80-PC0007being an ongoing project. The project is already delayed by more than 5 years\r\nand 2 months.&nbsp;</span><br></p><p><span lang=\"EN-IN\">In view of the\r\nabove facts, the respondent has violated the provisions mentioned u/s 12, 14, 18\r\nand 19 of the Act. The complainant wishes to withdraw from the project on\r\naccount of delayed possessions and major reduction in the unit area offered as\r\nagainst the area specified in the agreement for sale.It is most respectfully prayed\r\nthat the respondent be directed to refund the entire amount paid to the\r\nrespondent along with interest as per provisions of the Act.</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\">For M/s\r\nAnaesthetic Gases Pvt. Limited</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:&#10;justify\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\">Surinder Singh Virdhi</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:&#10;justify\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\">Authorized Signatory</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:&#10;justify\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\">&nbsp;</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:&#10;justify\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\">Through Counsel</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:&#10;justify\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\">&nbsp;</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\">Manju Goyal, Advocate\r\n(P/1682/2015)</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\">Ved Parkash, PCS\r\n-15927(F-3880)</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\">&nbsp;</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n<b></b><i></i><u></u><sub></sub><sup></sup><strike></strike><br></p>',7733504.00,3782644.00,'2013-11-20 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>NIL</p>','1','','2011-05-21 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Unit- 401 B, IVFloor','','',2,0,0,0,'surindervirdi','2019-02-01 15:24:05.000','surindervirdi','2019-02-01 15:24:05.000'),(971,1194,'1194',1281,'ecd6bbdb-27b0-4972-ac46-2f0682f35b3d','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-02-01 18:33:10.000','Sundeep Singh Pawar','gaurav.chopra@hotmail.com',9814013127,0,0,'House No. 360','Phase IV ',28,507,'160059','0','House No. 607','sector 18B',6,128,'160018','Gaurav Chopra','gaurav.chopra@hotmail.com',9814013127,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0119','MOHALI HILLs','Emaar MGF Land Ltd','sorabh.kakar@emaarmgf.com',0,0,'Emaar MGF Land Ltd','40, Central Plaza, Ground Floor, Sector 105 Mohali',28,507,'140306','1','Emaar MGF Land Ltd','40, Central Plaza, Ground Floor, Sector 105 Mohali',28,507,'140306','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">i)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Allotment Letter:24.4.07 <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">ii)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Buyer’s Agreement:10.4.08 <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">iii)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Agreement executed between Sundeep Singh\r\nPawar and Mrs. Harinder Kaur Pawar and the Respondent in respect of the Unit\r\nNo. H1-FPH-PH-01 for a total sale consideration of Rs. 98,59,200/- of super\r\narea of 2900 sq. Ft. Subsequently, the Unit was changed TVM-H1-F10-1001.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">iv)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; On the basis of an affidavit sworn by the\r\nCo-Applicant Kamaljit Kaur Pawar, an endorsement dated 10.4.08 was made in the\r\nAgreement dated 10.4.08 whereby the co-allottees of the Allotted Unit No. were\r\nformally recorded as the Applicants herein viz. Sundeep Singh Pawar and\r\nKamaljit Kaur Pawar. Subsequently, the Allotted Unit was changed to\r\nTVM-L2-F12-1202. Further, vide an Addendum, due to modification in the layout\r\nplan, Unit No. TVM-L2-F12-1202, Sector-105, Mohali Hills, Mohali was changed to\r\nUnit No. TVM-L2-F08-802 having a super area of 2600 sq. ft for which the total\r\nsale consideration was fixed at Rs. 83,20,505/- as indicated in the letter\r\ndated 15.9.10 issued by the Respondent. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-32.25pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">v)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Construction Linked Instalment Plan<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-32.25pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">vi) &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Amount paid upto 23.10.13: Rs. 72,61,148/- <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-32.25pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">vii)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; As per Clause 21.1 of the Agreement read\r\nwith Clause 23.1 possession of the Allotted Unit was required to be handed over\r\nto the Applicants by the Respondent positively on or before 24.7.10.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-32.25pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">viii)&nbsp;&nbsp; Aggrieved by the omission of the Respondent,\r\nthe Applicants had written a letter/e-mail to the Respondent for rescinding the\r\ncontract and for seeking refund of the principal amount paid by the Applicants\r\nin respect of the Allotted Unit alongwith interest.&nbsp; Till date, however, the aforesaid demand\r\nraised by the Applicants has not been acceded to by the Respondent.&nbsp; <o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-32.25pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">ix)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; In spite of the fact that the Applicants\r\nhad sought refund of the principal amount alongwith interest, the Respondents\r\nhave arbitrarily continued to issue Demand Notices to the Applicants for\r\npayment of instalments as per the payment schedule appended with the Buyer’s\r\nagreement.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-32.25pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:1.0in;text-align:justify;text-indent:\r\n-.5in;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n200%;font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">i)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Refund of an amount of Rs. 72,61,148/-\r\npaid by the Applicants alongwith interest (highest marginal cost of lending\r\nrate of the State Bank of India + 2%) from the respective dates of deposit till\r\nactual realization as per Sections 18 and 19(4) of the Act read with Rule 16 of\r\nthe Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:1.0in;text-align:justify;text-indent:\r\n-.5in;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n200%;font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">ii)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Any other relief which the Applicants are\r\nentitled for under the Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Act, 2016 and\r\nthe Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-32.25pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>',8320505.00,7261148.00,'2010-07-24 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>..</p>','1','','2007-04-24 00:00:00','2008-04-10 00:00:00','Unit No. TVM-L2-F08-802 ‘The Views’ at Mohali Hills, Sector-105, SAS Nagar, District Mohali, Punjab.','','',1,1,0,0,'sundeepsinghpawar','2019-02-01 18:33:07.000','sundeepsinghpawar','2019-02-01 18:33:07.000'),(972,1192,'1192',1254,'f975078e-bd45-46ae-9ad3-968463b14972','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-02-01 18:36:47.000','Ranjeev  Rai','gaurav.chopra@hotmail.com',9814013127,0,0,'House No. 360','Phase IV ',28,507,'160059','0','House No. 607','sector 18B',6,128,'160018','Gaurav Chopra','gaurav.chopra@hotmail.com',9814013127,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0119','Mohali Hills','M/s. EMAAR MGF Land Ltd','sorabh.kakkar@emmarmgf.in',0,0,'EMAAR MGF Land Ltd','40, Ground Floor, Central Plaza, Sector 105',28,507,'140306','1','EMAAR MGF Land Ltd','40, Ground Floor, Central Plaza, Sector 105',28,507,'140306','1','<p>i) Applicant: Ranjeev Singh Rai (name incorrectly stated as Rajeev Singh Rai)&nbsp;</p><p>ii) Application:14.3.2007&nbsp;</p><p>iii) Buyer’s Agreement:1.9.2009&nbsp;</p><p>iv) Construction Linked Installment Plan for total Consideration:Rs. 99,15,199</p><p>v) Amount paid till 21.8.2012:Rs. 86,41,522/-</p><p>vi) As per Clause 21.1 of the Apartment Buyer’s Agreement, the Respondent was under a contractual obligation to handover possession of the Allotted Unit within a period of 36 months from the date of allotment with a further relaxation of 90 days over and above the stipulated time period for the purpose of applying for and obtaining an Occupation Certificate in respect of the Group Housing Complex.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>vii) Date of Possession as per Clause 21.1 of the Agreement r/w Clause 23.1:on or before 1.12.2012.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>viii) Till date, however, despite a lapse of more than 6 years, possession of the Allotted Unit has neither been offered nor handed over to the Applicants and this wilful omission and lapse on the part of the Respondent constitutes a wilful and material breach of the Agreement executed between the parties.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>ix) Aggrieved by the aforesaid omission of the Respondent,the Applicant had written a letter/e-mail dated 9.2.2017 to the Respondent for rescinding the contract and for seeking refund of the principal amount paid by the Applicant in respect of the Allotted Unit alongwith interest. Till date,however, the aforesaid demand raised by the Applicant has not been acceded to by the Respondent and thus, vide the instant complaint, the Applicants seek refund of the monies paid by him to the Respondent alongwith interest and compensation.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>x) In spite of the fact that the Applicant had sought refund of the principal amount paid by the Applicants alongwith interest, the Respondents have arbitrarily continued to issue Demand Notices to the Applicant for payment of instalments as per the payment schedule.</p>','<p>i) Refund of an amount of Rs. 86,41,522/- paid by the Applicants alongwith interest (highest marginal cost of lending rate of the State Bank of India + 2%) from the respective dates of deposit till actual realization as per Sections 18 and 19(4) of the Act read with Rule 16 of the Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017.</p><p>ii) Any other relief which the Applicants are entitled for under the Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Act, 2016 and the Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017.&nbsp;</p><div><br></div>',9915199.00,8641522.00,'2012-12-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>N.A.</p>','1','','2007-03-14 00:00:00','2009-09-01 00:00:00','H3 FPH PH04, TOWER H, THE VIEWS AT MOHALLI HILLS','','',1,1,0,0,'Ranjeevrai','2019-02-01 18:36:43.000','Ranjeevrai','2019-02-01 18:36:43.000'),(973,1193,'1193',1280,'b364f9db-f8bf-4d03-9c07-d43a8d8e4b6f','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-02-01 18:38:09.000','Kamalroop  Sooch','gaurav.chopra@hotmail.com',9814013127,0,0,'House No. 360','Phase IV ',28,507,'160059','0','House No. 607','sector 18B',6,128,'160018','Gaurav Chopra','gaurav.chopra@hotmail.com',9814013127,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0119','Mohali Hills','Emaar MGF Land Ltd','sorabh.kakar@emaarmgf.com',0,0,'Emaar MGF Land Ltd','40, Central Plaza, Ground Floor, Sector 105 Mohali',28,507,'140306','1','Emaar MGF Land Ltd','40, Central Plaza, Ground Floor, Sector 105 Mohali',28,507,'140306','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">&nbsp;<span lang=\"EN-IN\">i)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Application Form: 14.3.2007<o:p></o:p></span></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">&nbsp;ii)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Allotment\r\nLetter: 30.3.2007 <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">&nbsp;iii)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Apartment\r\nBuyer’s Agreement: 29.2.08<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">&nbsp;iv)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Allotted\r\nUnit No. TVM-H3-F11-1104 in ‘The Views’ at Mohali Hills, Sector-105, SAS Nagar,\r\nDistrict Mohali<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">&nbsp;v) &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Total\r\nsale consideration of Rs. 49,59,650/- <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-32.25pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">vi)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Construction Linked Instalment Plan<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-32.25pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">vii) &nbsp;&nbsp; Amount paid upto 23.8.2012:Rs. 42,71,510/-<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-32.25pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">viii)&nbsp;&nbsp; As per Clause 21.1 of the Agreement read with\r\nClause 23.1 made it abundantly clear that time was the essence of the contract\r\nand hence, possession of the Allotted Unit was required to be handed over to\r\nthe Applicants by the Respondent positively on or before 30.6.2010.&nbsp; <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-32.25pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">v)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Aggrieved by the aforesaid omission and\r\nlapse of the Respondent, the Applicants had written a letter/e-mail to the\r\nRespondent for rescinding the contract and for seeking refund of the principal\r\namount paid by the Applicants in respect of the Allotted Unit alongwith\r\ninterest.&nbsp; Till date, however, the\r\naforesaid demand raised by the Applicants has not been acceded to by the\r\nRespondent and thus, vide the instant complaint, the Applicants seek refund of\r\nthe monies paid by them to the Respondent alongwith interest.&nbsp; <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-32.25pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">vi)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; That it is pertinent to mention herein that\r\nin spite of the fact that the Applicants had sought refund of the principal\r\namount paid by the Applicants alongwith interest, the Respondents have\r\narbitrarily continued to issue Demand Notices to the Applicants for payment of\r\ninstalments as per the payment schedule appended with the Buyer’s agreement.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:1.0in;text-align:justify;text-indent:\r\n-.5in;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n200%;font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">i)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Refund of an amount of Rs. 42,71,510/-\r\npaid by the Applicants alongwith interest (highest marginal cost of lending\r\nrate of the State Bank of India + 2%) from the respective dates of deposit till\r\nactual realization as per Sections 18 and 19(4) of the Act read with Rule 16 of\r\nthe Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:1.0in;text-align:justify;text-indent:\r\n-.5in;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n200%;font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">ii)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Any other relief which the Applicant is\r\nentitled for under the Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Act, 2016 and\r\nthe Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>',4959650.00,4271510.00,'2010-06-30 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>...</p>','1','','2007-03-30 00:00:00','2008-02-29 00:00:00','TVM-H3-F11-1104 in ‘The Views’ at Mohali Hills, Sector-105, SAS Nagar, District Mohali','','',1,1,0,0,'Kamalroopsooch','2019-02-01 18:38:06.000','Kamalroopsooch','2019-02-01 18:38:06.000'),(974,1292,'1292',1376,'0b9fb8a5-aba9-44ae-8b2e-dee11afdaf7d','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-02-03 11:27:21.000','Anaesthetic Gases P Ltd  Through Surinder Singh Virdi Managing Director','agplho22@gmail.com',9417004482,0,0,'SCO-841-842, IInd floor, Sector-22 A ','',6,128,'160022','1','SCO-841-842, IInd floor, Sector-22 A ','',6,128,'160022','Ved Parkash','csvedparkash@gmail.com',7837223098,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PC0006','International Trade Tower','M/s Omaxe Chandigarh Extension Developers P Ltd ','syediqbal@omaxe.com',8054002819,0,'Plot no.-6, Omaxe Sales office , Chandigarh Baddi Road, Mullanpur','',6,128,'140901','1','Plot no.-6, Omaxe Sales office , Chandigarh Baddi Road, Mullanpur','',6,128,'140901','1','<p>&nbsp;\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:6.8pt;margin-left:0cm;&#10;text-align:justify\"><b><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:9.5pt;font-family:&#10;Roboto;color:black;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">BRIEF FACTS OF THE CASE.</span></b><span style=\"box-sizing: border-box\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:9.5pt;&#10;font-family:Roboto;color:black;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">That initially,\r\nSurinder Singh Virdhi S/o Shri Man Singh, R/o House No. 199, Sector 16,\r\nChandigarh, booked Unit No 401-B, Fourth Floor, at India Trade Tower, located\r\nat Mullanpur, SAS Nagar, Mohali, Punjab on 06.01.2011 on the basis of\r\nrepresentations, warranties and commercial details shown in the Brochure of the\r\nM/s Omaxe Limited (hereinafter referred to as Respondent Company). A copy of\r\nBrochure and payment plan of the respondent company are attached as Annexure\r\nC/1.That Mr. Surinder Singh made initial booking and two other payments as per\r\nPayment Plan offered by the respondent company, amounting to Rs. 21.71,190/- as\r\ndetailed in Annexure C/2.The said office/unit was endorsed in the name of M/s\r\nAnaesthetic Gases Pvt. Limited (hereinafter referred to as the Complainant) by\r\nSurinder Singh Virdhi on 05.7.2011 as per document attached as Annexure C/3.The\r\nComplaint made further construction linked payments as per the demand notices\r\nissued from time to time by the respondent company amounting to Rs. 37,82,644/-\r\nas per details attached as Annexure C/4.The respondent company entered into\r\nagreement of sale (Annexed as C/5) with the applicant 03.06.2013 at a total\r\nconsideration of Rs. 77,33,504/- inclusive of PLC, Maintenance Security and\r\nAdditional cost. The allotted unit measured 135.83 sq. meters with a corner\r\nlocation as depicted in Brochure annexed above as C/1. That as per clause 26(a)\r\nof the said allotment letter/agreement for sale, the respondent company was to\r\noffer possession within 30 months from the start of construction i.e. thirty\r\nmonths from 21.05.2011 which arrives at 20.11.2013.Upon receipt of further\r\ndemand notices, the applicant/complainant made further payments amounting to\r\nRs. 7,53,336.35 as per details attached at Annexure C/6.The respondent company\r\nintimated the status of the project vide its letter dated 3.09.2015 attached as\r\nAnnexure C/7.</span></span><span style=\"font-size:9.5pt;font-family:Roboto;&#10;color:black\"></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:6.8pt;margin-left:0cm;&#10;text-align:justify;box-sizing: border-box;orphans: 2;-webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px;&#10;word-spacing:0px\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:9.5pt;font-family:Roboto;&#10;color:black;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\"><span style=\"box-sizing: border-box\">&nbsp;</span></span><span style=\"font-size:9.5pt;font-family:Roboto;color:black\"></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:6.8pt;margin-left:0cm;&#10;text-align:justify;box-sizing: border-box;orphans: 2;-webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px;&#10;word-spacing:0px\"><span style=\"font-size:9.5pt;font-family:Roboto;color:black\">&nbsp;</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\">&nbsp;</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><b></b><br></p><p><br></p>','<p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\">The respondent\r\ncompany offered fit out possession of the office/unit vide its letter dated\r\n28.03.2018 attached as Annexure C/8. The offer of possession was fit out and\r\ntentative in nature, without obtaining occupancy/completion certificate.\r\nMoreover, the area of the office/unit has been reduced to 101.81 sq. meters\r\nfrom 135.83 sq. meters and also changed the location of the allotted unit\r\nwithout the consent of the complainant.The complainant objected to the fit out offer\r\nof possession through its letters dated 30.03.2018 and 10.04.2018 attached as\r\nAnnexure C/9, but no reply has been received from the respondent company. The complainant\r\nhad filed a complaint before the State Consumer Disputes Redressal Commission,\r\nPunjab, Chandigarh attached as Annexure C/10, which was withdrawn by the\r\napplicant/complainant on technical grounds.That the above project of the\r\nrespondent is registered with RERA with Registration Number PBRERA-SAS80-PC0007being an ongoing project. The project is already delayed by more than 5 years\r\nand 2 months.&nbsp;</span><br></p><p><span lang=\"EN-IN\">In view of the\r\nabove facts, the respondent has violated the provisions mentioned u/s 12, 14, 18\r\nand 19 of the Act. The complainant wishes to withdraw from the project on\r\naccount of delayed possessions and major reduction in the unit area offered as\r\nagainst the area specified in the agreement for sale.It is most respectfully prayed\r\nthat the respondent be directed to refund the entire amount paid to the\r\nrespondent along with interest as per provisions of the Act.</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\">For M/s\r\nAnaesthetic Gases Pvt. Limited</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:&#10;justify\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\">Surinder Singh Virdhi</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:&#10;justify\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\">Authorized Signatory</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:&#10;justify\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\">&nbsp;</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:&#10;justify\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\">Through Counsel</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:&#10;justify\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\">&nbsp;</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\">Manju Goyal, Advocate\r\n(P/1682/2015)</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\">Ved Parkash, PCS\r\n-15927(F-3880)</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\">&nbsp;</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n<b></b><i></i><u></u><sub></sub><sup></sup><strike></strike><br></p>',7733504.00,3782644.00,'2013-11-20 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>NIL</p>','1','','2011-05-20 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Unit- 401 B, IVFloor','','',1,1,0,0,'surindervirdi','2019-02-03 11:27:16.000','surindervirdi','2019-02-03 11:27:16.000'),(975,1293,'1293',1377,'51ea772d-c350-4740-acaa-bf08ceacf9f6','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-02-04 10:07:18.000','Harish  Kumar','harishkumar1967@yahoo.co.in',7015859185,0,0,'H.no-494, maroo Mohalla, P.o-Dagshal','Solan',14,551,'173210','1','H.no-494, maroo Mohalla, P.o-Dagshal','Solan',14,551,'173210','Ved Parkash','csvedparkash@gmail.com',7837223098,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0046','Imperial County','M/s WWICS Estates Pvt Ltd','info@wwicsestates.com',9357993579,1726663600,'A-12, Industrial Area,Phase VI, Mohali','',28,507,'160059','1','A-12, Industrial Area,Phase VI, Mohali','',28,507,'160059','1','<p>BRIEF FACTS OF THE CASE • That the Complainant, Shri Harish Kumar S/o Shri Tulsi Ram, resident of House No 494, Maroo Mohalla, Nahesh (69/819), Dagshai&nbsp; Solan, Himachal Pradesh applied for a residential plot in the township project known as “Imperial County” situated at Kurali-Siswan Road, Kurali (Punjab) promoted by M/s WWICS Estates Pvt. Ltd, the Respondent No 1. • That the Respondent No 1 issued advertisement in newspapers inviting applications for allotment of residential plots highlighting the features of the project. One of the features was that the home loans are available with all leading banks. A copy of the advertisement is attached as Annexure C/1. That the complainant applied for allotment of plot through Mr. Vikrant Sood, Authorized Dealer for the project, now Respondent No 2, and was allotted a plot measuring 138.89 sq.yards (WEIC-P-154) at a total consideration of Rs. 19,05,015/- based on the payment plan annexed as C/2. That the complainant made payments amounting to Rs. 1,66,668/- as per payment plan to the respondent No 1,&nbsp; as annexed at&nbsp; C/3 (Colly).&nbsp; That the complainant applied for home loan to HDFC, SBI, PNB and other banks for the allotted plot but the home loan application was not considered as it was not a registered project with them eligible for home loan. The complainant intimated the status of home loan to the respondent No 1 and requested for refund of the booking amount showing his inability to arrange funds for the total consideration of the plot.&nbsp; The complainant’s communication in this regard is annexed as C/4.&nbsp; • That the respondent no 1 directed the complainant to approach the respondent No 2 for refund.&nbsp; The complainant kept on following with the respondent No 1 &amp; 2 and finally the complainant was asked to sign an affidavit cum undertaking that the booking amount may be assigned to the account of Lalita Kaushal w/o Vinay Kumar Kaushal, resident of Trinity House, Kelston Estate, Shimla on the promise that the respondent No 2 would</p>','<p>on the promise that the respondent No 2 would pay the amount to the complainant. A copy of affidavit cum undertaking is annexed as C/5.&nbsp;</p><p>• That subsequent to signing of affidavit cum undertaking&nbsp; by the complainant as annexed at C/5 above, a Credit Note was issued by respondent No 1 to Vijay Kumar Kaushal for an amount of Rs. 1,67,000/- in lieu of the complainant’s assigning his rights on allotted unit in the name of Lalita Kaushal&nbsp; W/o Vijay Kumar Kaushal. The said credit note is annexed as C/6. • That the respondent No 2 issued a Self Cheque No 030860 dated 25.03.2018 of Bank of India, Shimla Branch, to the complainant annexed as C/7. The Complainant visited bank of the respondent No 2 number of times but owing to insufficient balance, the cheque could not be realized. The complainant has been writing to both the respondent no 1 and 2 through mails annexed as C/8, but of no available. That the said plot now stands allotted in the name of Dheeraj Kumar S/o Shri Vinay Kumar Kaushal. The letters dated 6.6.2018 and 6.09.2018 annexed as C/9 (Colly) addressed to Dheeraj Kumar asking for maintenance charges by respondent No 1 confirm the allotment of plot in the name of Dheeraj Kumar.&nbsp; That the “Imperial County” is a registered project with the Authority with Regn No PBRERA-SAS80-PR0046, as an ongoing project. That the complainant was being harassed by the respondent no 1 &amp; 2&nbsp; for a long period of time and finally approached RERA on 10.8.2018, but the complaint was dismissed on 12.11.2018 by Shri J.S. Khushdil, Hon’ble Member, RERA, Punjab on the ground that the complainant did not appear on the appointed date.&nbsp; A copy of the Orders dated 12.11.2018 is annexed as C/10.&nbsp; That the complainant’s absence in the Hon’ble Court was not intentional but was caused due to the death of his close relative.&nbsp; The respondent No 1 &amp; 2 have violated the provisions of Section 12 of the Act which entitle the complainant to seek refund of booking amount.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p></p><p></p>',1905015.00,166668.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;&#10;text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:Symbol;&#10;mso-fareast-font-family:Symbol;mso-bidi-font-family:Symbol;mso-ansi-language:&#10;EN-IN\"><span style=\"mso-list:Ignore\">·<span style=\'font:7.0pt \"Times New Roman\"\'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span></span><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;&#10;line-height:115%;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">That the title of the allotted unit\r\nhas been transferred from the complainant in the name of third party with the\r\ncollusion of both respondent No 1 &amp; 2.</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;&#10;line-height:115%;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">&nbsp;</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:&#10;inter-ideograph\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;&#10;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">&nbsp;</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;&#10;text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:Symbol;&#10;mso-fareast-font-family:Symbol;mso-bidi-font-family:Symbol;mso-ansi-language:&#10;EN-IN\"><span style=\"mso-list:Ignore\">·<span style=\'font:7.0pt \"Times New Roman\"\'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span></span><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;&#10;line-height:115%;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">It is therefore, most respectfully\r\nprayed that the respondent No 1 &amp; 2 may be directed to refund the amount of\r\nRs. 1,66,668 to the complainant, along with interest from the respective dates\r\nof payments as per provisions of the Act, Rules.</span><br></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"margin-left:36.0pt;text-align:justify;text-justify:&#10;inter-ideograph\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;&#10;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">Harish Kumar, Complainant</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"margin-left:36.0pt;text-align:justify;text-justify:&#10;inter-ideograph\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;&#10;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">&nbsp;</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"margin-left:36.0pt;text-align:justify;text-justify:&#10;inter-ideograph\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;&#10;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">Through Counsel</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"margin-left:36.0pt;text-align:justify;text-justify:&#10;inter-ideograph\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;&#10;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">Adv Manju Goyal,</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"margin-left:36.0pt;text-align:justify;text-justify:&#10;inter-ideograph\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;&#10;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">Ved Parkash, AR</span></p><p>Interim Prayed - NIL</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','WEIC-P-154','','',1,1,0,0,'harishkumar.1','2019-02-03 15:30:44.000','harishkumar.1','2019-02-03 15:30:44.000'),(976,1250,'1250',1010,'a182232b-88d6-4711-8baa-f8a026fb675f','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-02-03 19:13:59.000','JAGDEEP SINGH and HARJEET KAUR','lawofficeofhimanshuraj@gmail.com',9988100005,0,512717894060,'#2870-B, SECTOR 42-C','',6,128,'160036','0','#102, Sector 10 A','',6,128,'160011','HIMANSHU RAJ','lawofficeofhimanshuraj@gmail.com',9988200001,1724190909,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0240','MUIRWOODS','Altus Space Builders Private Limited','altusoffice@yahoo.co.in',0,1724003734,'SCO 22','1ST FLOOR, PHASE 10',28,507,'160062','1','SCO 22','1ST FLOOR, PHASE 10',28,507,'160062','1','<p>The complainants booked a plot measuring 250 SQ. YARD at OP No.1s project MUIRWOODS on 24.04.2012 through OP No.1s Channel Partner, AJEET ASSOCIATES i.e. OP no.2. The complainants paid the booking amount to OP no.2 and entered into an AGREEMENT TO SELL but the agreement didnt have any information regarding the date of possession of the unit. That the OP No.1 received CLU for the said project on 25.06.2013 and Layout plan was approved on 08.05.2014 but OP had already demanded and accepted more than 25 per cent of the total consideration without entering into a plot buyer agreement and getting approvals from the authority, which is a direct violation of PAPRA and amounts to unfair trade practice.</p><p>That on 05.09.2014, the OP no.1 executed a PLOT BUYERS AGREEMENT with the complainants and promised that the possession including all the amenities will be handed over to the complainants by 05.09.2017,&nbsp; 30 months plus 6 months from the date of agreement, but OP No.1 failed to do so. That numerous times, OP no.1 demanded money against the said plot from the complainants without achieving any milestones as far as the development of the project is concerned.&nbsp;</p><p>That on 13.10.2017, Op no.1 furnished an Offer of possession letter to the complainants without even completing 10 per cent of the total project. The complainants wrote a letter to Op no.1 against the offer of possession and stated all the shortcomings of the project but OP No.1 just re issued a new offer of possession letter to the complainants without completing its project which is still under developed. That it has been more than 6 YEARS from the date of actual booking of the unit but there is absolutely no sign of development. The complainants have already paid more than the total consideration against the said property.</p><p>Therefore, the complainant craves the indulgence of the Honble RERA authority to hand to direct the OP No.1 and 2 to refund the entire amount as per the RERA CENTRAL ACT AND RERA STATE RULES.</p>','<p>1.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To direct the OP No.1 and Op no.2, being jointly and severally liable to compensate the complainants in the shape of refund of the complete amount which has been deposited against the residential property so booked by the complainants along with an Interest on the amount from the date of deposit at the rate of 20 per cent&nbsp; till the actual realization of the complete amount within 90 days according to section 18 1 Real Estate Regulation And Development Act, 2016, 18 2 Real Estate&nbsp; Regulation And Development Act, 2016, Section 19 4 of The Real Estate Regulation And Development Act, 2016, r w Rule 16 and Rule 17 of Punjab State Real Estate Regulation and Development Rules, 2017</p><p><br></p><p>2.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To direct the OP No.1 and Op no.2, being jointly and severally liable to pay Rs. 20,00,000&nbsp; for causing mental agony caused to the complainants.</p><p><br></p><p>3.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To direct the OP No.1 and Op no.2, being jointly and severally liable to pay Rs. 14,00,000 to the complainants as the deficiency in services for keeping the complainants in dark in regard to the progress of the property.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>4.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To direct the OP No.1 and Op no.2, being jointly and severally liable to pay Rs. 14,00,000&nbsp; for causing physical harassment caused to the complainants.</p><p><br></p><p>5.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To direct the OP No.1 and Op no.2, being jointly and severally liable to pay Rs. 1,00,000 as litigation cost as the complainants were constrained to file the same because of the callous and indifferent attitude of the opposite parties.</p><p>6.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To revoke the license of the OP No.1 under section 7 of the Real Estate Regulation and Development act, 2016.</p><p><br></p><p>7.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To impose heavy penalty on Op no.2 for doing business a Real Estate Agent without getting itself registered with RERA under Section 9 of Real Estate regulation and Development Act, 2016.</p><p><br></p><p>8.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Any other relief or claim which the Honble Authority deems appropriate.</p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Not Prayed</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',1,1,0,0,'lawofficeofhimanshuraj','2019-02-03 19:13:55.000','lawofficeofhimanshuraj','2019-02-03 19:13:55.000'),(977,1294,'1294',1001,'abcbc615-56f0-487c-bd5a-d97762a711d4','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Desh Raj Sharma','deva_2406@yahoo.co.in',9463087206,0,601475614290,'test data 76','test data 89',28,507,'111111','1','test data 76','test data 89',28,507,'111111','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PM0089','Aeropolis City (formerly known as Yellowstone Landmark Infocity)','Aeropolis Infrastructure Pvt. Ltd.','tejindersbhatia@gmail.com',9592969696,0,'M/s. Aeropolis Infrastructure Pvt. Ltd.,','Aeropolis City, Sector 66-A, S.A.S. Nagar,',28,507,'160062','1','M/s. Aeropolis Infrastructure Pvt. Ltd.,','Aeropolis City, Sector 66-A, S.A.S. Nagar,',28,507,'160062','1','<p>1.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span> Mega IT Project of M/s Aeropolis Infrastructure Pvt. Ltd. (formerly known as M/s Sukhm Infrastructure pvt. Ltd.) Namely AEROPOLIS CITY (Formerly known as YELLOWSTONE LAND MARK INFOCITY), SECTOR 66A, Mohali, approved by the state Government was launched in the market in the year 2009.&nbsp; Promoters issued Misleading and False adds in the Media or otherwise using names of Big Corporate Houses such as MukeshAmbani led Reliance group, The Dalmias, Bergruen( US ) and Yellow stone Chandigarh based firm.</p><p>2.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>On 17th Feb. 2010, Sukhm issued the Allotment letter in which it is on record and mentioned that “THAT ALLOTMENT LETTER IS SUBJECT TO SIGNING OF THE BUYER/SELLER AGREEMENT WITHIN 60 DAYS FROM THE ISSUANCE OF THIS LETTER.</p><p>3.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>But M/s Sukhm has issued the BUYER/SELLER AGREEMENT in August 2013, In Buyer/Seller Agreement Clause 7 (a) read as ( Development of the said IT/Industrial Plots is likely to be completed within a tentative period of 18 months from the date of this Agreement.)</p><p>4.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>We have paid under pressure up to 65% of the BSP.</p><p>5.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>On 26.09.2018, M/s Sukham Infrastructures Pvt. Ltd. has signed Joint Development Agreement with GBP Group.</p><p>6.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>ON PAYMENT OF PLC, THE PLOTS ALLOTED TO US BY M/S SUKHM, IN THE LAND, WHICH TILL DATE, DOES NOT BELONG TO SUKHM.</p><p>7.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>M/s Sukhm does not respond to our letter or e mails and also do not answer our phone calls.</p><p>8.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>As on date the status at the site of the project is as follows.</p><p>a)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Development work is insignificant, which can be verified.</p><p>b)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>No demarcation of plots.</p><p>c)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>No services are available.</p><p>d)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Patches of land which are shown on their approved maps, still not owned/ bought by them.</p><p>9.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>As on date we strongly believe that promoters :-</p><p>a)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Does not have the approved layout plan from the competent Authority BEING DEFAULTER IN PAYMENT OF EDC.</p><p>b)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>May not have valid agreement with State Govt. as on date.</p><p>c)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>May have not acquired/purchased land which is part of promoters approved maps.</p>','<p>In view of the facts stated above , when promoters have failed on all fronts to give possession of plots even after 9 years of our investment,&nbsp; We request your honor as under to save us as we have invested all our life’s savings in this project.</p><p>a.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Direct the promoters and Govt. Authorities concerned to develop the Project immediately and give possession of plots to us.</p><p>b.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Payment of interest on the amount paid @ 18% p.a. (compounded) for the delay in giving the possession of plots.</p><p>c.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Pay compensation for mental harassment and agony suffered by us as per Seller/Buyers Agreement.</p><p>Any other relief which RERA may feel appropriate.</p>',7095726.00,4967690.00,'2015-02-08 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>a.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Payment of interest on the&nbsp; amount paid @ 18% (compound) for the delay in giving possession of plots.</p><p>b.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Pay compensation for the mental harassment and agony suffered by us so long.</p><p>c.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Any other relief which RERA may feel appropriate.</p><p>d.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Direct the promoters and Govt. Authorities concerned to develop the Project immediately and give possession of plots to us.</p>','1','','2010-02-17 00:00:00','2013-08-08 00:00:00','Plot Number IT/P/MS/05 M/s. Aeropolis Infrastructure Pvt. Ltd., Aeropolis City, Sector 66-A, S.A.S. Nagar, Mohali-160062','','',1,0,0,0,'testdata34','2019-02-04 11:24:47.000','testdata34','2019-02-04 11:24:47.000'),(978,1295,'1295',1374,'82227358-6d09-4a12-8b11-de1e75c71cac','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Dev Raj Sharma','deva_2406@yahoo.co.in',9463087206,0,601475614290,'H.No. 306','Sector - 35A, Chandigarh',6,128,'160017','1','H.No. 306','Sector - 35A, Chandigarh',6,128,'160017','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PM0089','Aeropolis City (formerly known as Yellowstone Landmark Infocity)','Aeropolis Infrastructure Pvt. Ltd.','tejindersbhatia@gmail.com',9592969696,0,'M/s. Aeropolis Infrastructure Pvt. Ltd.,','Aeropolis City, Sector 66-A, S.A.S. Nagar,',28,507,'160062','1','M/s. Aeropolis Infrastructure Pvt. Ltd.,','Aeropolis City, Sector 66-A, S.A.S. Nagar,',28,507,'160062','1','<p>1.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span> Mega IT Project of M/s Aeropolis Infrastructure Pvt. Ltd. (formerly known as M/s Sukhm Infrastructure pvt. Ltd.) Namely AEROPOLIS CITY (Formerly known as YELLOWSTONE LAND MARK INFOCITY), SECTOR 66A, Mohali, approved by the state Government was launched in the market in the year 2009.&nbsp; Promoters issued Misleading and False adds in the Media or otherwise using names of Big Corporate Houses such as MukeshAmbani led Reliance group, The Dalmias, Bergruen( US ) and Yellow stone Chandigarh based firm.</p><p>2.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>On 17th Feb. 2010, Sukhm issued the Allotment letter in which it is on record and mentioned that “THAT ALLOTMENT LETTER IS SUBJECT TO SIGNING OF THE BUYER/SELLER AGREEMENT WITHIN 60 DAYS FROM THE ISSUANCE OF THIS LETTER.</p><p>3.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>But M/s Sukhm has issued the BUYER/SELLER AGREEMENT in August 2013, In Buyer/Seller Agreement Clause 7 (a) read as ( Development of the said IT/Industrial Plots is likely to be completed within a tentative period of 18 months from the date of this Agreement.)</p><p>4.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>We have paid under pressure up to 65% of the BSP.</p><p>5.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>On 26.09.2018, M/s Sukham Infrastructures Pvt. Ltd. has signed Joint Development Agreement with GBP Group.</p><p>6.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>ON PAYMENT OF PLC, THE PLOTS ALLOTED TO US BY M/S SUKHM, IN THE LAND, WHICH TILL DATE, DOES NOT BELONG TO SUKHM.</p><p>7.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>M/s Sukhm does not respond to our letter or e mails and also do not answer our phone calls.</p><p>8.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>As on date the status at the site of the project is as follows.</p><p>a)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Development work is insignificant, which can be verified.</p><p>b)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>No demarcation of plots.</p><p>c)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>No services are available.</p><p>d)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Patches of land which are shown on their approved maps, still not owned/ bought by them.</p><p>9.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>As on date we strongly believe that promoters :-</p><p>a)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Does not have the approved layout plan from the competent Authority BEING DEFAULTER IN PAYMENT OF EDC.</p><p>b)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>May not have valid agreement with State Govt. as on date.</p><p>c)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>May have not acquired/purchased land which is part of promoters approved maps.</p>','<p>In view of the facts stated above , when promoters have failed on all fronts to give possession of plots even after 9 years of our investment,&nbsp; We request your honor as under to save us as we have invested all our life’s savings in this project.</p><p>a.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Direct the promoters and Govt. Authorities concerned to develop the Project immediately and give possession of plots to us.</p><p>b.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Payment of interest on the amount paid @ 18% p.a. (compounded) for the delay in giving the possession of plots.</p><p>c.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Pay compensation for mental harassment and agony suffered by us as per Seller/Buyers Agreement.</p><p>Any other relief which RERA may feel appropriate.</p>',7095726.00,4967690.00,'2015-02-08 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>a.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Payment of interest on the&nbsp; amount paid @ 18% (compound) for the delay in giving possession of plots.</p><p>b.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Pay compensation for the mental harassment and agony suffered by us so long.</p><p>c.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Any other relief which RERA may feel appropriate.</p><p>d.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Direct the promoters and Govt. Authorities concerned to develop the Project immediately and give possession of plots to us.</p>','1','','2010-02-17 00:00:00','2013-08-08 00:00:00','Plot Number IT/P/MS/05, M/s. Aeropolis Infrastructure Pvt. Ltd., Aeropolis City, Sector 66-A, S.A.S. Nagar, Mohali-160062','','',2,0,0,0,'devraj306','2019-02-04 11:51:26.000','devraj306','2019-02-04 11:51:26.000'),(979,1277,'1277',1022,'33a0ed60-04ed-4ddd-b47a-6c6e5113bf37','FormTypeM',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Nikhil Juneja','nikhil_sp1@yahoo.com',8699499940,0,0,'128, Shakti Nagar','',28,261,'144001','1','128, Shakti Nagar','',28,261,'144001','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-JAL33-PM0077','Old Jail Site, Jalandhar','PUNJAB URBAN PLANNING AND DEVELOPMENT AUTHORITY','ca@puda.gov.in',0,0,'PUDA BHAWAN SECTOR- 62','SAS NAGAR MOHALI',28,507,'160062','1','PUDA BHAWAN SECTOR- 62','SAS NAGAR MOHALI',28,507,'160062','1','<p>\r\n		\r\n	\r\n	\r\n		</p><div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 2\">\r\n			<div class=\"layoutArea\">\r\n				<div class=\"column\">\r\n					<p><font face=\"Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt;\">I purchased plot number 65-C at Old Jail site (As known as PUDA SPORTS ENCLAVE), Jalandhar on\r\n22/04/2016 via PUDA auction. The plot was purchased for Rs 1,14,02,358 excluding the cess. The cess\r\namount paid was Rs 2,28,047. The size of the plot is 222.92 sq. mtrs. On 17/08/2016 I received the Allotment letter (Annexure A) in Clause 4 sub clause (i) it is mentioned that the possession shall be handed\r\nover within 1 year of the Auction, after completion of development works. Details of the instalments made\r\nby me are attached in Annexure B (Payment Schedule for Plot 65 C Old Jail Site Jalandhar). All the\r\npayments except TDS deposited amount Rs 48,866.97 on 14/04/2018 Annexure C (Form 16B) are also\r\nshown in the Ledger downloaded from PUDA/JDA website (Annexure D). The possession was delayed by\r\nover 2 years and 3 months. I was offered possession on 02/07/2018. Attached is the possession letter\r\n(Annexure E). I would like to keep the plot and not withdraw from the project. On 14/04/2018 I made lump\r\nsum payment of the plot by taking a loan from Punjab National Bank&nbsp; and availed 5% discount on the balance payment. After making lump sum payment I applied for No Due Certificate on 02/05/2018 and its been almost 9 months and I have still not </span><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px;\">received</span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt;\">&nbsp;the No Due Certificate. Now as I haven\'t got the No Due Certificate the bank is not willing to lend me any funds for construction. According to clause 6 (iii) of the allotment letter if the construction is not done within 3 years of </span><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px;\">possession</span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt;\">&nbsp;there will be Non Construction charges.&nbsp; I have also attached </span><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px;\">Brochure</span><span style=\"font-size: 11pt;\">&nbsp;given at the time of auction (Annexure F).</span></font></p>\r\n				</div>\r\n			</div>\r\n		</div>','<p>\r\n		\r\n	\r\n	\r\n		</p><div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 2\">\r\n			<div class=\"layoutArea\">\r\n				<div class=\"column\">\r\n					<p><span style=\"font-size: 11.000000pt; font-family: \'Helvetica\'\">I seek relief of interest on principal amount paid by me for delay in the possession @18% PA on the\r\nmonthly compounding basis. This delay has put me in significant financial constraints, physical and\r\nmental stress. I also seek compensation of Rs 5 Lakh for Physical and metal stress for being dragged in\r\nthe litigation to seek re