white-space:pre\">	</span>The complainant got the home loan approval from the PNB Housing Finance Limited for an amount of Rs. 61,30,443/-. Out of the said home loan approval account, an amount of Rs. 55,63,515/- has been paid to the respondent as per details annexed as C/7.</p><p>•<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Thus total payments made by the complainant to the respondent amount to Rs. 86,09,752/- as per Statement of Account annexed as C/8.</p><p>•<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That the residential project is still not complete and the development of common areas is very low. Being an ongoing project, the said project is registered with RERA vide Registration No PBRERA-SAS81-PR0124.&nbsp;</p><p>•<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That the above project of the respondent is registered with RERA with Registration Number PBRERA-SAS80-PC0007, being an ongoing project.&nbsp;</p><p>•<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>The project is already delayed by more than 2 years and 8 months where the respondent received majority of the payments between 2011 and 2014 suggesting diversion of funds by the respondent. The complainant has lost faith that the respondent would be able to offer early possession after obtaining completion/occupancy certificate from the competent authorities.</p><p>•<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>In view of the above facts, the respondent has violated the provisions mentioned u/s 12, 18 and 19 of the Act.&nbsp;</p><p>•<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>The complainant wishes to withdraw from the project on account of delayed possession of the allocated unit.&nbsp;</p><p>•<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>It is most respectfully prayed that the respondent be directed to refund the entire amount paid to the respondent along with interest as per provisions of the Act.</p><div><br></div>',9087212.00,8609752.00,'2016-06-13 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Not Applicable</p>','1','','2012-12-15 00:00:00',