INSERT INTO `verified_table_tbl_rera_complaint_formm_details` VALUES (991,1288,'1288',1369,'0e157dcb-4e45-4c7a-a3cd-d4664ae34cf8','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-02-06 17:06:00.000','Uniroyal Industries Limited through Akhil Mahajan','csvedparkash@gmail.com',9876011456,0,0,'Plot No. 365, Insdustral Area','Phase-II, Pachkula',13,15,'134113','1','Plot No. 365, Insdustral Area','Phase-II, Pachkula',13,15,'134113','Ved Parkash','csvedparkash@gmail.com',7837223098,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0124','Acme Eden Court','Acme Builders Pvt. Ltd','contact@acmebuilders.in',8592122888,1724625000,'GH-10, JLPL','Sector-91 Mohali',28,507,'160032','1','GH-10, JLPL','Sector-91 Mohali',28,507,'160032','1','<div>•<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That M/s Uniroyal Industries Limited with its Corporate Office at Plot No 365, Industrial Estate, Phase II, Panchkula-134113, the Complainant, booked a Flat No T1/1002, Sector 91, Acme Eden Court, Mohali (Punjab)-141001 on 11.05.2011 from M/s Acme Builders Private Limited with its Corporate Office at SCO 2449-50, First Floor, Sector 22-C, Chandigarh, the Respondent. A copy of the brochure, commercial details and advance registration form are attached as Annexure C/1(Colly).</div><div>•<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That the complainant&nbsp; made initial booking amount of 24,50,0000/- along with advance registration form and one more payment amounting to Rs. 1,17,775/- as per details annexed as C/2.</div><div>•<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>The respondent issued allotment letter for the allotted unit on 15.12.2012 attached as C/3.</div><div>•<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>The respondent entered into Builder Buyer Agreement (Annexed as C/4) with the complainant 13.12.2012 at a total consideration of Rs. 90,87,212/- inclusive of PLC, Maintenance Security etc. The allotted unit measured super area of 2345 sq.ft. That as per clause 15 of the said builder buyer agreement, the respondent was to offer possession within 42 months from the date of the said agreement, which arrives at 13.06.2016.</div><div>•<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That the complainant opted for subvention payment plan annexed to the agreement which was later on converted into CLP vide amendment date 31.12.2012 to the said agreement, annexed as C/5.</div><div>•<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>The complainant made additional payments amounting to Rs. 3,19,773/- and Rs. 158,689/- from their own account as per details annexed as C/6.</div><div>•<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>The complainant got the home loan approval from the PNB Housing Finance Limited for an amount of Rs. 61,30,443/-. Out of the said home loan approval account, an amount of Rs. 55,63,515/- has been paid to the respondent as per details annexed as C/7.<br></div>','<p>•<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>The complainant got the home loan approval from the PNB Housing Finance Limited for an amount of Rs. 61,30,443/-. Out of the said home loan approval account, an amount of Rs. 55,63,515/- has been paid to the respondent as per details annexed as C/7.</p><p>•<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Thus total payments made by the complainant to the respondent amount to Rs. 86,09,752/- as per Statement of Account annexed as C/8.</p><p>•<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That the residential project is still not complete and the development of common areas is very low. Being an ongoing project, the said project is registered with RERA vide Registration No PBRERA-SAS81-PR0124.&nbsp;</p><p>•<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That the above project of the respondent is registered with RERA with Registration Number PBRERA-SAS80-PC0007, being an ongoing project.&nbsp;</p><p>•<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>The project is already delayed by more than 2 years and 8 months where the respondent received majority of the payments between 2011 and 2014 suggesting diversion of funds by the respondent. The complainant has lost faith that the respondent would be able to offer early possession after obtaining completion/occupancy certificate from the competent authorities.</p><p>•<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>In view of the above facts, the respondent has violated the provisions mentioned u/s 12, 18 and 19 of the Act.&nbsp;</p><p>•<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>The complainant wishes to withdraw from the project on account of delayed possession of the allocated unit.&nbsp;</p><p>•<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>It is most respectfully prayed that the respondent be directed to refund the entire amount paid to the respondent along with interest as per provisions of the Act.</p><div><br></div>',9087212.00,8609752.00,'2016-06-13 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Not Applicable</p>','1','','2012-12-15 00:00:00','2012-12-13 00:00:00','Flat No. 1002, 10th Floor, Tower-1, Acme Eden Court, GH-10, JLPL Sector-90-91, Mohali','','',1,1,0,0,'uniroyalindustries','2019-02-06 16:50:22.000','uniroyalindustries','2019-02-06 16:50:22.000'),(992,1297,'1297',1380,'8534ccb5-71b6-42a7-a6ae-bb6958ca02ae','FormTypeM',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Richa Tandon','amit_tandon1in@yahoo.co.in',9876594454,9878848595,944715970921,'Flat No - A4/403 Nirmal Chhaya Towers','VIP Road, Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','1','Flat No - A4/403 Nirmal Chhaya Towers','VIP Road, Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','AMIT TANDON','richa_tandon10@yahoo.co.in',9878848595,9876594454,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PC0010','M/s CITI CENTRE DEVELOPERS','Mrs. NEHA AGGARWAL','neha@chandigarhciticenter.in',8699026543,7087722229,'Chandigarh Citi Center, VIP Road','Near Metro Cash and Carry, VIP Road, Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','1','Chandigarh Citi Center, VIP Road','Near Metro Cash and Carry, VIP Road, Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','1','<ul><li><p class=\"MsoNormal\">19 July 2018 </p>\r\n\r\n<ol><li>Submitted all documents to CCC Builders after clearing\r\nall dues for transfer (purhcased on resale).</li></ol>\r\n\r\n<ol><li>Signed all possession related documents with comments to\r\npending jobs related to showroom and to our Block - A. CCC builders refused to\r\nsign. Documents changed and signed - \'\'CLEANED\'\' as CCC Builders promised\r\ntimely completion of pending jobs as agreed and signed seperately.</li></ol></li></ul><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><ul><li>20.July.2018 - Showroom transferred on my name.</li></ul><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><ul><li>26.July.2018 - Registration of showroom done</li></ul><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><ul><li>20.July.2018 to 05.Feb.2019 - continuous reminder to CCC\r\nbuilder to complete the pending jobs related to my showroom as per list signed\r\nand agreed on 19.July.2018 and handing over of Showroom.</li></ul>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><ol><li>All pending jobs related to my showroom and to my block\r\nto be completed as soon as possible.</li><li>Delay of over 6.5 months for handing over of showroom as\r\nagreed ( pending jobs lists dated 19.July.18), caused loss of rental\r\nincome&nbsp; 40000 rs / month, Relief Request\r\n-&nbsp; 2.6 lakhs.</li><li>Maintenance to start from day you complete all pending\r\njobs as agreed and all pending jobs related to Block-A related to parking area,\r\nroad and ramp between Block A&amp; D, lifts, common washroom, completion of\r\nconstruction / labour movement on 3rd, 4th floor and roof of Block A, all\r\nfirefighting equips operational for block A and false ceiling completed for\r\ncommon corridor of 2nd floor of Block A. (expected by 01.Sept.2019)</li><li>Maintenance charges are 13.10 rs / sq ft / month (for our\r\nshowroom - 12050 rs / month).However presently project is incomplete (another about 2 yrs\r\nto complete 100%). Maintenance charges to be reduced to basis actual costs.Presently seems like builder is charging excessive\r\nmaintenance charges to complete the construction of remaining project.</li><li>Loss in earning if my Husband need to stay at home further\r\nto settle this case.&nbsp; ( husband earnings\r\n- 9.8 lakhs/Month + tax liability if his NRI Status not maintained for year\r\n2019-20).<br></li></ol>',3159204.00,3159204.00,'2018-07-26 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<ol><li>All pending jobs related to my showroom and to my block to be completed as soon as possible.</li><li>Maintenance to start from day you complete all pending jobs as agreed and all pending jobs related to Block-A related to parking area, road and ramp between Block A&amp; D, lifts, common washroom, completion of construction / labour movement on 3rd, 4th floor and roof of Block A, all firefighting equips operational for block A and false ceiling completed for common corridor of 2nd floor of Block A. (expected by 01.Sept.2019)</li><li><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p>Maintenance charges are 13.10 rs / sq ft / month (for our showroom - 12050 rs / month). However presently project is incomplete (another about 2 yrs to complete 100%). Maintenance charges to be reduced to basis actual costs.</li></ol>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','2018-07-20 00:00:00','SCO NO. 15 SECOND FLOOR, BLOCK A, CHANDIGARH CITI CENTER, VIP ROAD, ZIRAKPUR, MOHALI, PUNJAB','','',2,0,0,0,'amit2008','2019-02-06 21:38:44.000','amit2008','2019-02-06 21:38:44.000'),(993,1297,'1297',1380,'8534ccb5-71b6-42a7-a6ae-bb6958ca02ae','FormTypeM',1,1,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Richa Tandon','amit_tandon1in@yahoo.co.in',9876594454,9878848595,944715970921,'Flat No - A4/403 Nirmal Chhaya Towers','VIP Road, Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','1','Flat No - A4/403 Nirmal Chhaya Towers','VIP Road, Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','AMIT TANDON','richa_tandon10@yahoo.co.in',9878848595,9876594454,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PC0010','M/s CITI CENTRE DEVELOPERS','Mrs. NEHA AGGARWAL','neha@chandigarhciticenter.in',8699026543,7087722229,'Chandigarh Citi Center, VIP Road','Near Metro Cash and Carry, VIP Road, Z