Agreement.)</p><p>4.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>We have paid under pressure up to 61.5% of the BSP.</p><p>5.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>On 26.09.2018, M/s Sukham Infrastructures Pvt. Ltd. has signed Joint Development Agreement with GBP Group.</p><p>6.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>M/s Sukhm does not respond to our letter or e mails and also do not answer our phone calls.</p><p>7.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>As on date the status at the site of the project is as follows.</p><p>a)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Development work is insignificant, which can be verified.</p><p>b)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>No demarcation of plots.</p><p>c)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>No services are available.</p><p>d)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Patches of land which are shown on their approved maps, still not owned/ bought by them.</p><p>8.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>As on date we strongly believe that promoters :-</p><p>a)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Does not have the approved layout plan from the competent Authority BEING DEFAULTER IN PAYMENT OF EDC.</p><p>b)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>May not have valid agreement with State Govt. as on date.</p><p>c)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>May have not acquired/purchased land which is part of promoters approved maps.</p>','<p>In view of the facts stated above , when promoters have failed on all fronts to give possession of plots even after 9 years of our investment,&nbsp; We request your honor as under to save us as we have invested all our life’s savings in this project.</p><p>a.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Direct the promoters and Govt. Authorities concerned to develop the Project immediately and give possession of plots to us.</p><p>b.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Payment of interest on the amount paid @ 18% p.a. (compounded) for the delay in giving the possession of plots.</p><p>c.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Pay compensation&nbsp; as per Seller/Buyers Agreement.</p><p>Any other relief which RERA may feel appropriate.</p>',7095726.00,4369778.00,'2015-02-08 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>a.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Payment of interest on the&nbsp; amount paid @ 18% (compound) for the delay in giving possession of plots.</p><p>b.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Pay compensation for the mental harassment and agony suffered by us so long.</p><p>c.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Any other relief which RERA may feel appropriate.</p><p>d.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Direct the promoters and Govt. Authorities concerned to develop the Project immediately and give possession of plots to us.</p>','1','','2010-02-17 00:00:00','2013-08-08 00:00:00','Plot Number IT/P/MS/05, M/s. Aeropolis Infrastructure Pvt. Ltd., Aeropolis City, Sector 66-A, S.A.S. Nagar, Mohali-160062','','',2,0,0,0,'devraj306','2019-02-08 14:08:41.000','devraj306','2019-02-08 14:08:41.000'),(1000,1298,'1298',1078,'d8d4f172-3c37-4e70-b72a-876b113f98f3','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Jasneet Kaur','vikramsinghchahal@gmail.com',9417545867,0,0,'House no 159, Teg Colony, Patiala','Patiala',28,454,'147001','1','House no 159, Teg Colony, Patiala','Patiala',28,454,'147001','vikram singh chahal','vikramsinghchahal@gmail.com',9781750447,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0022','GATEWAY CITY SECTOR 118-119, SAS NAGAR MOHALI ','Chief Administrator, PUDA','se@puda.gov.in',1725063022,0,'PUDA Bhawan','Sector 62, SAS Nagar',28,507,'160063','1','PUDA Bhawan','Sector 62, SAS Nagar',28,507,'160063','1','<p>1.	That the complainant/allottee after shown rosy picture and wide claims by the respondents decided to buy the residential plot in GATEWAY CITY SECTOR 118-119, SAS NAGAR MOHALI which was widely advertised by the respondents. The complainant filed the form along with prescribed fee for the allotment of residential plot in the GATEWAY CITY SECTOR 118-119, SAS NAGAR MOHALI. \r\n</p><p>2.	That the complainant on being successful in draw of plots was elated that her dream of owning a house in Mohali is going to be realized soon. The respondents issued a letter of Intent (LOI) vide no 22294 dated 10.06.2015 (ANNEXURE-C001) and made a demand of Rs 8,06,400 and Rs 1,07,520  which was paid by the complainant vide receipts dated 09.07.2015 (ANNEXURE-C002 Colly).&nbsp;</p><p>3.	That the respondents thereafter issued an allotment letter(ANNEXURE-C003) vide letter no 45219 dated 27.09.2016 in which the respondents allotted Plot no 600 measuring 283.88sq.yards in Sector 118-119, Gateway City at the rate of Rs 21,000/- per Sq.yd for the total consideration of Rs 59,61,480/-(Fifty Nine Lac Sixty One Thousand Four Hundred Eighty).&nbsp;</p><p>4.	That thereafter going through the layout plan issued by the respondents, the complainant deems it proper to physically verify the allotted plot at the site of the project but to her utter surprise, no demarcation was done of the plot  and after lot of efforts and struggle, the complainant spotted her allotted plot no 600 and to the utter shock her allotted plot is adjoining to the sewage treatment plant (STP) and the area is filled with bad odour from the STP and in addition to that the high voltage electricity wires and electricity pillars are next to the said plot making it inhabitable and dangerous. The dreams of the complainant shattered therein on seeing the conditions prevailing in the project and complainant moved representation (ANNEXURE-C004) to the respondent dated&nbsp;<span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">07.11.2016 for the\r\nre-allotment of some alternate plot taking the objections</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">.</span></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\ntext-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">1.</span><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 14px; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">That as per the clause 4 of the allotment letter </span><b><i><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">the\r\npossession of the said plot shall be handed over to the allottee after the completion\r\nof the development works at the site or 18 months from the date of issuance of\r\nthe allotment letter whichever is earlier</span></i></b><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">. The respondents have failed\r\nto offer possession to the allottees and paid fraud and used the payments accumulated\r\nfrom the allottees and yielding interest thereon.&nbsp;</span></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\ntext-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><br></span><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 14px;\">That the complainant\r\nhave lost all hopes of getting a owning a dream house in Mohali and no more\r\ninterested in the project as the development of the project is pathetically\r\nslow and despite of the lapse of the promised possession date (28.03.2018) the\r\nrespondents have miserably failed to develop the project in a time bound manner.</span><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 14px; text-indent: -0.25in;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\ntext-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 14px; text-indent: -0.25in;\">T</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">&nbsp; That the respondents allotted the unfeasible plot to the complainant which is at no stretch of imagination would be acceptable to any reasonable person taking into account the adjoining STP and High Voltage wires and Electricity Pillars. The Respondents failed in re-allotting any alternate plot in time bound manner and shattered the dreams of the complainant to own a house in Mohali.</span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\ntext-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 14pt; text-indent: -0.25in;\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\ntext-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Therefore, the complainant\r\nprays before this Hon’ble Authority to direct the respondents to refund of the\r\nhard earned money of Rs 14,90,370(</span><b><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Fourteen\r\nLac Ninety Thousand Three Hundred Seventy</span></b><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">) along with interest @18% p.a. in\r\nthe interest of justice and equity.</span></span><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 14pt; text-indent: -0.25in;\"><br></span></p>',5961480.00,0.00,'2018-03-26 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Any interim relief which this Hon\'ble Authority deems proper in the facts and circumstances of the case.&nbsp;</p>','1','','2016-09-27 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Plot No 600, Gateway City Mohali Sector 118-19','','',2,0,0,0,'P43982017','2019-02-08 14:19:36.000','P43982017','2019-02-08 14:19:36.000'),(1001,1298,'1298',1078,'d8d4f172-3c37-4e70-b72a-876b113f98f3','FormTypeM',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Jasneet Kaur','vikramsinghchahal@gmail.com',9417545867,0,0,'House no 159, Teg Colony, Patiala','Patiala',28,454,'147001','1','House no 159, Teg Colony, Patiala','Patiala',28,454,'147001','vikram singh chahal','vikramsinghchahal@gmail.com',9781750447,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0022','GATEWAY CITY SECTOR 118-119, SAS NAGAR MOHALI ','Chief Administrator, PUDA','se@puda.gov.in',1725063022,0,'PUDA Bhawan','Sector 62, SAS Nagar',28,507,'160063','1','PUDA Bhawan','Sector 62, SAS Nagar',28,507,'160063','1','<p>1. That the present complaint is being filed by Paramjit Kaur who is the lawful GPA of Jasneet Kaur hereinafter the complainant.Copy of the GPA is ANNEXURE-C001.</p><p>2.	That the complainant filed the form along with prescribed fee for the allotment of residential plot in the GATEWAY CITY SECTOR 118-119, SAS NAGAR MOHALI and on being successful in draw of plots was elated that her dream of owning a house in Mohali is going to be realized soon. The respondents issued a letter of Intent (LOI) vide no 22294 dated 10.06.2015 (ANNEXURE-C002) and made a demand of Rs 8,06,400 and Rs 1,07,520  which was paid by the complainant vide receipts dated 09.07.2015 (ANNEXURE-C003 Colly).&nbsp;</p><p>3.	That the respondents thereafter issued an allotment letter(ANNEXURE-C004) vide letter no 45219 dated 27.09.2016 in which the respondents allotted Plot no 600 measuring 283.88sq.yards in Sector 118-119, Gateway City at the rate of Rs 21,000/- per Sq.yd for the total consideration of Rs 59,61,480/-(Fifty Nine Lac Sixty One Thousand Four Hundred Eighty). 4.	That thereafter going through the layout plan issued by the respondents, the complainant deems it proper to physically verify the allotted plot at the site of the project but to her utter surprise, no demarcation was done of the plot  and after lot of efforts and struggle, the complainant spotted her allotted plot no 600 and to the utter shock her allotted plot is adjoining to the sewage treatment plant (STP) and the area is filled with bad odour from the STP and in addition to that the high voltage electricity wires and electricity pillars are next to the said plot making it inhabitable and dangerous. The dreams of the complainant shattered therein on seeing the conditions prevailing in the project and complainant moved representation (ANNEXURE-C005) to the respondent dated&nbsp;<span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">07.11.2016 for the\r\nre-allotment of some alternate plot taking the objections</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">.</span></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\ntext-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">1.</span><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 14px; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">That as per the clause 4 of the allotment letter </span><b><i><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">the\r\npossession of the said plot shall be handed over to the allottee after the completion\r\nof the development works at the site or 18 months from the date of issuance of\r\nthe allotment letter whichever is earlier</span></i></b><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">. The respondents have failed\r\nto offer possession to the allottees and paid fraud and used the payments accumulated\r\nfrom the allottees and yielding interest thereon.&nbsp;</span></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\ntext-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><br></span><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 14px;\">That the complainant\r\nhave lost all hopes of getting a owning a dream house in Mohali and no more\r\ninterested in the project as the development of the project is pathetically\r\nslow and despite of the lapse of the promised possession date (28.03.2018) the\r\nrespondents have miserably failed to develop the project in a time bound manner.</span><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 14px; text-indent: -0.25in;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\ntext-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 14px; text-indent: -0.25in;\">T</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">&nbsp; That the respondents allotted the unfeasible plot to the complainant which is at no stretch of imagination would be acceptable to any reasonable person taking into account the adjoining STP and High Voltage wires and Electricity Pillars. The Respondents failed in re-allotting any alternate plot in time bound manner and shattered the dreams of the complainant to own a house in Mohali.</span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\ntext-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 14pt; text-indent: -0.25in;\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\ntext-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Therefore, the complainant\r\nprays before this Hon’ble Authority to direct the respondents to refund of the\r\nhard earned money of Rs 14,90,370(</span><b><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Fourteen\r\nLac Ninety Thousand Three Hundred Seventy</span></b><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">) along with interest @18% p.a. in\r\nthe interest of justice and equity.</span></span><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 14pt; text-indent: -0.25in;\"><br></span></p>',5961480.00,0.00,'2018-03-26 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Any interim relief which this Hon\'ble Authority deems proper in the facts and circumstances of the case.&nbsp;</p>','1','','2016-09-27 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Plot No 600, Gateway City Mohali Sector 118-19','','',2,0,0,0,'P43982017','2019-02-08 14:25:56.000','P43982017','2019-02-08 14:25:56.000'),(1002,1299,'1299',1387,'409dd6e7-281c-4e0a-b00e-646b90d3edc0','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-03-08 15:19:29.000','Dewan  Bal Krishan','nehadewan86@gmail.com',8288927636,0,705137822724,'H. no.111, Model Town, Narwana (Haryana)','',13,8,'126116','1','H. no.111, Model Town, Narwana (Haryana)','',13,8,'126116','Rachit Kaushal','rkaushal009@gmail.com',9464500303,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0282','Opera Garden 1 and Opera garden 2','Ajai Veer Sehgal','operahomes@gmail.com',9316500005,0,'SCO 36, Sector 3','',13,15,'134109','1','SCO 36, Sector 3','',13,15,'134109','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:150%\"><font face=\"Tahoma, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 17.3333px;\">1. That Respondent no 1 has got approved projects from RERA on the land having khasra numbers 284/42(1-1), 288/43(2-0), 28(4-0),29 (4-0),30(4-0),31(4-0),266/32(1-0) of Registration no PBRERA-SAS79-PR0232 and Khasra no 265/32(3-0),33(4-0),36(4-0),34(1-0)267/37(0-2)269/38(3-18), 265/32,33,34, 47(4-0) and 46(4-0) in registration no PBRERA-SAS79-PR0282 as per the sale deeds annexed with the file of RERA of Respondents.&nbsp;</span></font><span style=\"font-size: 17.3333px; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif;\">That the land on which the project is made was under litigation since 1990 so the title of the Respondent no 1 was defective at the time of approval of the said project.&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:150%\"><font face=\"Tahoma, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 17.3333px;\">2. That during the pendency of the aforesaid civil suits,&nbsp; Respondent no 1 and his family member Sheila Rani Seghal (mother of Respondent no 1) purchased the land under litigation in their own names and in the name of their company\r\n.&nbsp;</span></font><span style=\"font-size: 17.3333px; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif;\">That the Civil Suits were decreed in favour of vendors of the Complainant and the said decree was affirmed upto the Hon’ble High Court, thereby conferring the title of the project land on the Complainant jointly with 10 other persons, which did not include the Respondents or their Company.&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:150%\"><font face=\"Tahoma, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 17.3333px;\">3. That the Sale Deeds have been executed and the mutation of the project land is recorded in favour of the Complainant jointly with 10 other persons, and the respondent has constructed the project on the land of the Complainant without having any title to the same.\r\n&nbsp;</span></font><span style=\"font-size: 17.3333px; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif;\">The registration of both the projects was applied by showing themselves to be the exclusive owner of the land, which is actually co-owned &amp; jointly possessed by the complainant &amp; ot</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">﻿</span><span style=\"font-size: 17.3333px; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif;\">her 10 persons. The Respondent no 1 and Respondent no 2 with dishonest intention and to deceive/cheat the complainant &amp; other co-owners applied to get the projects passed on the land owned by complainant and others.&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:150%\"><font face=\"Tahoma, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 17.3333px;\">In this way RERA officials did not even verify the Revenue Record on the land on which they were passing the above projects. Hence this Complaint.</span></font></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:150%\"><span style=\"font-size:13.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">In\r\nview of the facts mentioned in paragraph 4 above, the complainants prays for\r\nthe following relief(s) :-<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-indent:.5in;line-height:150%\"><span style=\"font-size:13.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">It\r\nis therefore prayed that in view of the submissions made above, the approval/license\r\ngranted to both the projects to the respondents may please be cancelled/revoked\r\nforthwith in order to save innocent people and the banks from fraud and the\r\nrespondents be further directed to return the money of buyers. It is further\r\nrequested that an FIR may kindly be lodged against Respondent No 1, 2 &amp; 5 </span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:13.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">under section 420, 467, 471, 120 B of the IPC against the\r\nerring respondents, immediately in order to save RERA officials from criminal\r\nprosecution.</span><b><span style=\"font-size:13.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;\r\ncolor:red\"><o:p></o:p></span></b></p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:150%\"><span style=\"font-size:13.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Pending\r\nfinal decision on the complaint the complainant seeks issue of the following\r\ninterim order: <o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n<span style=\"font-size:13.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:Calibri;mso-ansi-language:EN-US;mso-fareast-language:\r\nEN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\">Respondents be restrained from selling/booking,\r\nconstructing, advertising etc of any flat constructed on the land of the\r\ncomplainant mentioned in para no. 5 of the complaint, to any person.&nbsp;</span><br></p>','0','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',1,1,0,0,'dewanbalkrishan','2019-02-08 20:25:29.000','dewanbalkrishan','2019-02-08 20:25:29.000'),(1003,1298,'1298',1078,'d8d4f172-3c37-4e70-b72a-876b113f98f3','FormTypeM',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Jasneet Kaur','vikramsinghchahal@gmail.com',9417545867,0,0,'House no 159, Teg Colony, Patiala','Patiala',28,454,'147001','1','House no 159, Teg Colony, Patiala','Patiala',28,454,'147001','vikram singh chahal','vikramsinghchahal@gmail.com',9781750447,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0022','GATEWAY CITY SECTOR 118-119, SAS NAGAR MOHALI ','Chief Administrator, PUDA','se@puda.gov.in',1725063022,0,'PUDA Bhawan','Sector 62, SAS Nagar',28,507,'160063','1','PUDA Bhawan','Sector 62, SAS Nagar',28,507,'160063','1','<p>1. That the present complaint is being filed by Paramjit Kaur who is the lawful GPA of Jasneet Kaur hereinafter the complainant.Copy of the GPA is ANNEXURE-C001.</p><p>2.	That the complainant filed the form along with prescribed fee for the allotment of residential plot in the GATEWAY CITY SECTOR 118-119, SAS NAGAR MOHALI and on being successful in draw of plots was elated that her dream of owning a house in Mohali is going to be realized soon. The respondents issued a letter of Intent (LOI) vide no 22294 dated 10.06.2015 (ANNEXURE-C002) and made a demand of Rs 8,06,400 and Rs 1,07,520  which was paid by the complainant vide receipts dated 09.07.2015 (ANNEXURE-C003 Colly).&nbsp;</p><p>3.	That the respondents thereafter issued an allotment letter(ANNEXURE-C004) vide letter no 45219 dated 27.09.2016 in which the respondents allotted Plot no 600 measuring 283.88sq.yards in Sector 118-119, Gateway City at the rate of Rs 21,000/- per Sq.yd for the total consideration of Rs 59,61,480/-(Fifty Nine Lac Sixty One Thousand Four Hundred Eighty). 4.	That thereafter going through the layout plan issued by the respondents, the complainant deems it proper to physically verify the allotted plot at the site of the project but to her utter surprise, no demarcation was done of the plot  and after lot of efforts and struggle, the complainant spotted her allotted plot no 600 and to the utter shock her allotted plot is adjoining to the sewage treatment plant (STP) and the area is filled with bad odour from the STP which is&nbsp; nuisance to the allottee and in addition to that the high voltage electricity wires and electricity pillars are next to the said plot making it inhabitable and dangerous. The dreams of the complainant shattered therein on seeing the conditions prevailing in the project and complainant moved representation (ANNEXURE-C005) to the respondent dated&nbsp;<span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 14pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">07.11.2016 for the\r\nre-allotment of some alternate plot taking the objections</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">.</span></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\ntext-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">1.</span><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 14px; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">That as per the clause 4 of the allotment letter </span><b><i><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">the\r\npossession of the said plot shall be handed over to the allottee after the completion\r\nof the development works at the site or 18 months from the date of issuance of\r\nthe allotment letter whichever is earlier</span></i></b><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">. The respondents have failed\r\nto offer possession to the allottee and paid fraud and used the payments accumulated\r\nfrom the allottee and yielding interest thereon.&nbsp;</span></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\ntext-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><br></span><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 14px;\">That the complainant\r\nhave lost all hopes of getting a owning a dream house in Mohali and no more\r\ninterested in the project as the development of the project is pathetically\r\nslow and despite of the lapse of the promised possession date (28.03.2018) the\r\nrespondents have miserably failed to develop the project in a time bound manner and failed in giving possession</span><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 14px; text-indent: -0.25in;\">&nbsp; of the said plot.</span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\ntext-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 14px; text-indent: -0.25in;\">T</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">&nbsp; That the respondents allotted the unfeasible plot to the complainant which is at no stretch of imagination would be acceptable to any reasonable person taking into account the adjoining STP and High Voltage wires and Electricity Pillars which are nuisance to the allottee. The Respondents failed in re-allotting any alternate plot in time bound manner and shattered the dreams of the complainant to own a house in Mohali.</span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\ntext-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 14pt; text-indent: -0.25in;\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\ntext-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Therefore, the complainant\r\nprays before this Hon’ble Authority to direct the respondents to refund of the\r\nhard earned money of Rs 14,90,370(</span><b><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Fourteen\r\nLac Ninety Thousand Three Hundred Seventy</span></b><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">) along with interest @18% p.a. in\r\nthe interest of justice and equity.</span></span><span style=\"font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 14pt; text-indent: -0.25in;\"><br></span></p>',5961480.00,0.00,'2018-03-26 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Any interim relief which this Hon\'ble Authority deems proper in the facts and circumstances of the case.&nbsp;</p>','1','','2016-09-27 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Plot No 600, Gateway City Mohali Sector 118-19','','',2,0,0,0,'P43982017','2019-02-08 22:24:51.000','P43982017','2019-02-08 22:24:51.000'),(1004,1298,'1298',1078,'d8d4f172-3c37-4e70-b72a-876b113f98f3','FormTypeM',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Jasneet Kaur Chahal','vikramsinghchahal@gmail.com',9781750447,0,0,'House no 159, Teg Colony, Patiala','Patiala',28,454,'147001','1','House no 159, Teg Colony, Patiala','Patiala',28,454,'147001','vikram singh chahal','vikramsinghchahal@gmail.com',9781750447,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0022','GATEWAY CITY SECTOR