ken to pay the maintenance charges after taking over possession of the\r\nsaid apartment and had also undertaken to enter into a maintenance agreement. The respondent had\r\nthereafter, entered into a maintenance agreement dated 06.11.2015 with the complainant no. 2. That the\r\nrespondents despite been in possession of the said apartment, has not been paying the maintenance\r\ncharges fixed as per the maintenance agreement and is enjoying all the services free of cost. It is further\r\npertinent to mention here that a number of public notices has been got attached in the society whereby\r\nthe respondent was called upon various times for payment of the maintenance charges but no heed was\r\npaid to the said notices by the respondents.<br></p>','<p>&nbsp;Directing the respondent to pay the amount of Rs. 34,727/- due towards the maintenance charges.\r\nDirecting the respondent to pay compensation of Rs. 25,000/- to the complainants<br></p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Directing the respondents to pay interest on the due amount as mentioned in the maintenance agreement\r\ntill the pendency of the present complaint till actual payment.&nbsp;<br></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'BeeG','2019-02-15 13:26:44.000','BeeG','2019-02-15 13:26:44.000'),(1050,1295,'1295',1374,'82227358-6d09-4a12-8b11-de1e75c71cac','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-02-08 20:24:03.000','Dev Raj Sharma , Satya Devi Sharma , Ranjan Sharma , Jyoti Sharma','deva_2406@yahoo.co.in',9463087206,0,601475614290,'H.No. 306','Sector - 35A, Chandigarh',6,128,'160017','1','H.No. 306','Sector - 35A, Chandigarh',6,128,'160017','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PM0089','GBP Aeropolis City (formerly known as Yellowstone Landmark Infocity)','Mr.  TS Bhatia(MD)  Mr. Aprajit Sachdev(GM) Mr. Anupam Gupta, Director – GBP Group.','tejindersbhatia@gmail.com',9592969696,9814412946,'M/s. Aeropolis Infrastructure Pvt. Ltd.,','Aeropolis City, Sector 66-A, S.A.S. Nagar,',28,507,'160062','1','M/s. Aeropolis Infrastructure Pvt. Ltd.,','Aeropolis City, Sector 66-A, S.A.S. Nagar,',28,507,'160062','1','<p>1.<span style=\"white-space: pre;\">	</span> Mega IT Project of M/s Aeropolis Infrastructure Pvt. Ltd. (formerly known as M/s Sukhm Infrastructure pvt. Ltd.) Project: AEROPOLIS CITY (Formerly known as YELLOWSTONE LAND MARK INFOCITY), SECTOR 66A, Mohali, approved by the state Government was launched in the market in the year 2009.&nbsp; Promoters issued Misleading and False adds in the Media or otherwise using names of Big Corporate Houses such as MukeshAmbani led Reliance group, The Dalmias, Bergruen( US ) and Yellow stone Chandigarh based firm.</p><p>2.<span style=\"white-space: pre;\">	</span>On 17th Feb. 2010, Sukhm issued the Allotment letter in which it is on record and mentioned that “THAT ALLOTMENT LETTER IS SUBJECT TO SIGNING OF THE BUYER/SELLER AGREEMENT WITHIN 60 DAYS FROM THE ISSUANCE OF THIS LETTER.</p><p>3.<span style=\"white-space: pre;\">	</span>But M/s Sukhm has issued the BUYER/SELLER AGREEMENT in August 2013, In Buyer/Seller Agreement Clause 7 (a) read as ( Development of the said IT/Industrial Plots is likely to be completed within a tentative period of 18 months from the date of this Agreement.)</p><p>4.<span style=\"white-space: pre;\">	</span>We have paid under pressure up to 65% of the BSP.</p><p>5.<span style=\"white-space: pre;\">	</span>On 26.09.2018, M/s Sukham Infrastructures Pvt. Ltd. has signed Joint Development Agreement with GBP Group.</p><p>6.<span style=\"white-space: pre;\">	</span>As on date the status at the site of the project is as follows.</p><p>a)<span style=\"white-space: pre;\">	</span>Development work is insignificant, which can be verified.</p><p>b)<span style=\"white-space: pre;\">	</span>No demarcation of plots.</p><p>c)<span style=\"white-space: pre;\">	</span>No services are available.</p><p>d)<span style=\"white-space: pre;\">	</span>Patches of land which are shown on their approved maps, still not owned/ bought by them.</p><p>7.<span style=\"white-space: pre;\">	</span>As on date we strongly believe that promoters :-</p><p>a)<span style=\"white-space: pre;\">	</span>Does not have the approved layout plan from the competent Authority BEING DEFAULTER IN PAYMENT OF EDC.</p><p>b)<span style=\"white-space: pre;\">	</span>May not have valid agreement with State Govt. as on date.</p><p>c)<span style=\"white-space: pre;\">	</span>May have not acquired/purchased land which is part of promoters approved maps.</p>','<p>In view of the facts stated above , when promoters have failed on all fronts to give possession of plots even after 9 years of our investment,&nbsp; We request your honor as under to save us as we have invested all our life’s savings in this project.</p><p><br></p><p>a.<span style=\"white-space: pre;\">	</span>Direct the promoters and Govt. Authorities concerned to develop the Project immediately and give possession of plots to us.</p><p><br></p><p>b.<span style=\"white-space: pre;\">	</span>Payment of interest on the amount paid @ 18% p.a. (compounded) for the delay in giving the possession of plots.</p><p><br></p><p>c.<span style=\"white-space: pre;\">	</span>Pay compensation&nbsp; as per Seller/Buyers Agreement.</p><p>Any other relief which RERA may feel appropriate.</p>',15840000.00,10451397.00,'2015-08-08 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>a.<span style=\"white-space: pre;\">	</span>Payment of interest on the&nbsp; amount paid @ 18% (compound) for the delay in giving possession of plots.</p><p>b.<span style=\"white-space: pre;\">	</span>Pay compensation&nbsp;as per seller-Buyer agreement&nbsp;and mental harassment and agony suffered by us so long.</p><p>c.<span style=\"white-space: pre;\">	</span>Any other relief which RERA may feel appropriate.</p><p>d.<span style=\"white-space: pre;\">	</span>Direct the promoters and Govt. Authorities concerned to develop the Project immediately and give possession of plots to us.</p>','1','','2010-02-17 00:00:00','2013-08-08 00:00:00','Plot Number IT/P/MS/05 , IT/P/MS/06 M/s. Aeropolis Infrastructure Pvt. Ltd., Aeropolis City, Sector 66-A, S.A.S. Nagar, Mohali-160062','','',2,0,0,0,'devraj306','2019-02-15 18:48:24.000','devraj306','2019-02-15 18:48:24.000'),(1051,1323,'1323',1249,'633d568c-6bc4-4a67-ac48-2650be8f8a83','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-02-15 20:40:35.000','Harish Minocha','kangan_1993@yahoo.in',9810617548,0,0,'E-3, Lajpat Nagar-III','2nd Floor, Delhi-24',10,557,'110024','1','E-3, Lajpat Nagar-III','2nd Floor, Delhi-24',10,557,'110024','Baani Chhibber','baanichbr@gmail.com',9876658773,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PM0010','Industrial Knowledge (Fashion Technology) Park at Sector-90, SAS Nagar, Mohali, Punjab','M/s Chandigarh Overseas Pvt. Ltd. ','chdoverseas@rediffmail.com',0,0,'SCO 249','Sector 44-C',6,128,'160047','0','SCO 196-197, Top Floor','Sector 34-A',6,128,'160032','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:\r\njustify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;line-height:200%;mso-layout-grid-align:\r\nnone;text-autospace:none\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n200%;font-family:&quot;Cambria&quot;,serif;mso-ascii-theme-font:major-latin;mso-hansi-theme-font:\r\nmajor-latin;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial\">The complainant booked a space/unit of\r\nSuper area of 125 Sq. ft. in Design Studio No. 11, Floor No. 6, Block A1 in\r\nIndustrial Knowledge (Fashion Technology) Park, Sector 90, SAS Nagar, Mohali\r\nfor total amount of Rs. 5,00,000/- vide Application Form No. 104077 dt.\r\n25.03.2007. Complainant &amp; respondent had executed Developer Buyer Agreement\r\ndt. 24.12.2007. The complainant has made a total payment of Rs. 4,75,000/- till\r\ndate &amp; balance was to be made at the time of possession. Also, the\r\ncomplainant had purchased two units from the respondent &amp; separate\r\ncomplaint has been filed for other unit. The Complainant was promised the\r\ndelivery of possession within the period of 30 months from the date of start of\r\nconstruction but the possession of the said unit has not been delivered to the complainant\r\nso far. The construction of the project was delayed and by the promised date\r\ni.e. the end of 2009 &amp; till now the construction of the said project is\r\nincomplete due to which the complainant had suffered immense mental &amp;\r\nphysical harassment. That as per the agreement, the complainant was entitled to\r\nreceive Rs. 50 per square feet per month as delay charges which amounts to Rs.\r\n6250/- p.m., if the possession was not delivered at the agreed time. The said\r\ndelay charges were also paid by the respondent from 26.03.2010 till 02.01.2012\r\nonly amounting to Rs. 3,30,242/- for two units and thereafter no delay charges\r\nhave been paid to the complainant. The act of the respondent is in clear\r\nviolation of provisions of RERA Act &amp; Rules. Section 18 of the RERA Act\r\nmandates a promoter to return the amount received in respect of a plot with interest\r\nat the prescribed rate and compensation at the wish of the buyer in case the\r\npromoter fails to give possession. If the buyer wishes to continue &amp; get\r\nthe possession of plot then the promoter shall pay monthly interest on delay of\r\neach month and handover the possession. The documents annexed herewith may be\r\nread as part &amp; parcel of the complainant.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:36.0pt;text-align:justify;line-height:\r\n200%\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif\">In view of the\r\nfacts mentioned in paragraph 4 above, the Complainant prays for the following relief:<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:36.0pt;text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"margin-left:90.0pt;text-align:justify;\r\ntext-indent:-54.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:Arial\">(i)<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-weight: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span></b><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif\">Pass\r\nan order/direction to the respondent to deliver the possession of the units as\r\nper the Developer Buyer Agreement, alongwith interest @10.15 % p.a. i,e prevailing\r\napplicable State Bank of India Highest Marginal Cost of Lending Rate plus two\r\npercent from the date of payments till the date of possession of the units\r\n&amp; accept the balance payment.&nbsp; <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"margin-left:90.0pt;text-align:justify\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"margin-left:90.0pt;text-align:justify;\r\ntext-indent:-54.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:Arial\">(ii)<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-weight: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span></b><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif\">Levy\r\na penalty of 5% of the estimated cost of the real estate project for breach of\r\nits obligation to deliver possession on time under the Act.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"margin-left:90.0pt;text-align:justify;\r\ntext-indent:-54.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:Arial\">(iii)<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-weight: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span></b><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif\">Pass\r\nan order/direction to the respondent to pay an amount of Rs.12,500/- (Rupees\r\nTen Lakh Fifty Thousand only) p.m for both the units as delay charges from the\r\nperiod starting from 01.02.2012 till actual realization to the complainant, alongwith\r\nthe interest @ 10.15% p.a i,e prevailing applicable State Bank of India Highest\r\nMarginal Cost of Lending Rate plus two percent. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"margin-left:90.0pt;text-align:justify;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"margin-left:90.0pt;text-align:justify;\r\ntext-indent:-54.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:Arial\">(iv)<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-weight: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span></b><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif\">If\r\nthe Respondent is not able to give the possession of the units as per the\r\nagreement then in the alternative, direction to the Respondent to return the\r\namounts paid with interest from the date of payment till the actual realization\r\nas per the RERA Rule 15 with the prevailing applicable State Bank of India\r\nHighest Marginal Cost of Lending Rate plus two percent i.e. 10.15%<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"margin-left:90.0pt;text-align:justify;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"margin-left:90.0pt;text-align:justify;\r\ntext-indent:-54.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:Arial\">(v)<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-weight: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span></b><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif\">Pass\r\nany other order/direction in favor of the complainant &amp; against the\r\nrespondent as deem fit by the authority.<o:p></o:p></span></p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:36.0pt;text-align:justify;line-height:\r\n200%\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif\">Pending final\r\ndecision on the complaint the complainant seeks issue of&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; text-indent: -36pt;\">direction to the Respondent not to\r\nsell/transfer/allot the units to any third person.</span></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',1,1,0,0,'BaaniChhibber','2019-02-15 20:08:14.000','BaaniChhibber','2019-02-15 20:08:14.000'),(1052,1320,'1320',1112,'29af80b1-85ed-4b88-8344-b429d2f24eca','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Bee Gee Builtech','savindersinghgill@gmail.com',9988861126,0,0,'SCF 44-45, Ist Floor','Sector-9',13,15,'134108','1','SCF 44-45, Ist Floor','Sector-9',13,15,'134108','Savinder Singh Gill','savindersinghgill@gmail.com',9988861126,0,'Allottee','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0103','Palm Village','Kusum Kaushal','sahil_kaushal@rediffmail.com',9878687838,0,'D-301, 3rd floor, Tower-D, Palm Village','Village-Desumajra, Sector-126',28,507,'140301','1','D-301, 3rd floor, Tower-D, Palm Village','Village-Desumajra, Sector-126',28,507,'140301','1','<p>That the complainant no. 1 is the promoter having RERA registration no. PBRERA-SAS80-PR0103, has\r\ndeveloped project under the name and style of “PALM VILLAGE”, located in Sector-126, NH-21, S.A.S.\r\nNagar, Mohali. The complainant no. 2 is a maintenance agency which has been entrusted upon with the\r\nmaintenance of the project of the complainant no. 1. It is pertinent to mention here that both the\r\ncomplainants have entered into an agreement for the said reason. That the respondents are allottees of\r\nthe complainant no. 1 who had applied for an apartment measuring 2180 sq. ft. (Approximate Super Area)\r\non 09.09.2012 in the abovementioned project and in pursuance of the said booking, they were allotted flat\r\nno. D-301 on 3rd Floor in Tower D vide allotment letter dated 30.10.2012. That a buyer’s agreement\r\nwas signed between the complainant no. 1 and the respondents on 30.10.2012. The respondents were\r\nthereafter offered possession of the said apartment and the possession was taken over by the\r\nrespondents on 11.09.2015. Further it is pertinent to mention here that in the possession handing over\r\nletter, the respondents had undertaken to pay the maintenance charges after taking over possession of\r\nthe said apartment and had also undertaken to enter into a maintenance agreement. The respondents\r\nthereafter, entered into a maintenance agreement dated 11.09.2015 with the complainant no. 2. That the\r\nrespondents despite been in possession of the said apartment, has not been paying the maintenance\r\ncharges fixed as per the maintenance agreement and is enjoying all the services free of cost. It is further\r\npertinent to mention here that a number of public notices has been got attached in the society whereby\r\nthe respondents were called upon various times for payment of the maintenance charges but no heed\r\nwas paid to the said notices by the respondents.&nbsp;<br></p>','<p>Directing the respondents to pay the amount of Rs. 34,727/- due towards the maintenance charges.\r\nDirecting the respondent to pay compensation of Rs. 25,000/- to the complainants&nbsp;<br></p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Directing the respondents to pay interest on the due amount as mentioned in the maintenance agreement\r\ntill the pendency of the present complaint till actual payment.<br></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'BeeG','2019-02-16 09:56:22.000','BeeG','2019-02-16 09:56:22.000'),(1053,1320,'1320',1112,'29af80b1-85ed-4b88-8344-b429d2f24eca','FormTypeM',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Bee Gee Builtech','savindersinghgill@gmail.com',9988861126,0,0,'SCF 44-45, Ist Floor','Sector-9',13,15,'134108','1','SCF 44-45, Ist Floor','Sector-9',13,15,'134108','Savinder Singh Gill','savindersinghgill@gmail.com',9988861126,0,'Allottee','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0103','Palm Village','Kusum Kaushal','sahil_kaushal@rediffmail.com',9878687838,0,'D-301, 3rd floor, Tower-D, Palm Village','Village-Desumajra, Sector-126',28,507,'140301','1','D-301, 3rd floor, Tower-D, Palm Village','Village-Desumajra, Sector-12