t of Rs. 34,727/- due towards the maintenance charges.\r\nDirecting the respondent to pay compensation of Rs. 25,000/- to the complainants&nbsp;<br></p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Directing the respondents to pay interest on the due amount as mentioned in the maintenance agreement\r\ntill the pendency of the present complaint till actual payment.<br></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'BeeG','2019-02-16 09:59:50.000','BeeG','2019-02-16 09:59:50.000'),(1054,1321,'1321',1112,'29af80b1-85ed-4b88-8344-b429d2f24eca','FormTypeM',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Bee Gee Builtech','savindersinghgill@gmail.com',9988861126,0,0,'SCF 44-45, Ist Floor','Sector-9',13,15,'134108','1','SCF 44-45, Ist Floor','Sector-9',13,15,'134108','Savinder Singh Gill','savindersinghgill@gmail.com',9988861126,0,'Allottee','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0103','Palm Village','Anita Sharma','anitaisnow@rediffmail.com',9872856212,0,'House No.- 523, 2nd floor, ','sector-10 D',6,128,'160011','1','House No.- 523, 2nd floor, ','sector-10 D',6,128,'160011','1','<p>That the complainant no. 1 is the promoter having RERA registration no. PBRERA-SAS80-PR0103, has\r\ndeveloped project under the name and style of “PALM VILLAGE”, located in Sector-126, NH-21, S.A.S.\r\nNagar, Mohali. The complainant no. 2 is a maintenance agency which has been entrusted upon with the\r\nmaintenance of the project of the complainant no. 1. It is pertinent to mention here that both the\r\ncomplainants have entered into an agreement for the said reason. That the respondent is allottee of\r\nthe complainant no. 1 who had applied for an apartment measuring 2180 sq. ft. (Approximate Super Area)\r\non 24.06.2014 in the abovementioned project and in pursuance of the said booking, they were allotted flat\r\nno. D-1202 on 12th Floor in Tower D vide allotment letter dated 10.08.2014. That a buyer’s agreement\r\nwas signed between the complainant no. 1 and the respondent on 10.08.2014. The respondent was thereafter offered possession of the said apartment and the possession was taken over by the\r\nrespondents on 30.01.2016. Further it is pertinent to mention here that in the possession handing over\r\nletter, the respondent had undertaken to pay the maintenance charges after taking over possession of\r\nthe said apartment and had also undertaken to enter into a maintenance agreement. The respondent thereafter, entered into a maintenance agreement dated 30.01.2016 with the complainant no. 2. That the\r\nrespondent despite been in possession of the said apartment, has not been paying the maintenance\r\ncharges fixed as per the maintenance agreement and is enjoying all the services free of cost. It is further\r\npertinent to mention here that a number of public notices has been got attached in the society whereby\r\nthe respondent were called upon various times for payment of the maintenance charges but no heed\r\nwas paid to the said notices by the respondent.&nbsp;<br></p>','<p>Directing the respondent to pay the amount of Rs. 46,304/- due towards the maintenance charges.\r\nDirecting the respondent to pay compensation of Rs. 25,000/- to the complainants<br></p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Directing the respondent to pay interest on the due amount as mentioned in the maintenance agreement\r\ntill the pendency of the present complaint till actual payment.<br></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'BeeG','2019-02-16 10:37:46.000','BeeG','2019-02-16 10:37:46.000'),(1055,1322,'1322',1112,'29af80b1-85ed-4b88-8344-b429d2f24eca','FormTypeM',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Bee Gee Builtech','savindersinghgill@gmail.com',9988861126,0,0,'SCF 44-45, Ist Floor','Sector-9',13,15,'134108','1','SCF 44-45, Ist Floor','Sector-9',13,15,'134108','Savinder Singh Gill','savindersinghgill@gmail.com',9988861126,0,'Allottee','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0103','Palm Village','Karamjeet Singh','singhkarma662@gmail.com',9417155388,0,'# 244, Namdev Nagar, Near Khalsa School,','BTI Road, Shri Muktsar Sahib',28,399,'152026','1','# 244, Namdev Nagar, Near Khalsa School,','BTI Road, Shri Muktsar Sahib',28,399,'152026','1','<p>That the complainant no. 1 is the promoter having RERA registration no. PBRERA-SAS80-PR0103, has\r\ndeveloped project under the name and style of “PALM VILLAGE”, located in Sector-126, NH-21, S.A.S.\r\nNagar, Mohali. The complainant no. 2 is a maintenance agency which has been entrusted upon with the\r\nmaintenance of the project of the complainant no. 1. It is pertinent to mention here that both the\r\ncomplainants have entered into an agreement for the said reason. That the respondent is an allottee of\r\nthe complainant no. 1 who had applied for an apartment measuring 2180 sq. ft. (Approximate Super Area)\r\non 16.06.2011 in the abovementioned project and in pursuance of the said booking, he was allotted flat\r\nno. B-202 on 2rd Floor in Tower B vide allotment letter dated 13.09.2011. That a buyer’s agreement was\r\nsigned between the complainant no. 1 and the respondent. The respondent was thereafter\r\noffered possession of the said apartment on 13.07.2015 and the possession of the said apartment was\r\ntaken over by the respondent. Further it is pertinent to mention here that in the possession handing over\r\nletter, the respondent had undertaken to pay the maintenance charges after taking over possession of the\r\nsaid apartment and had also undertaken to enter into a maintenance agreement. The respondent had\r\nthereafter, entered into a maintenance agreement dated 13.07.2015 with the complainant no. 2. That the\r\nrespondent despite been in possession of the said apartment, has not been paying the maintenance\r\ncharges fixed as per the maintenance agreement and is enjoying all the services free of cost. It is further\r\npertinent to mention here that a number of public notices has been got attached in the society whereby\r\nthe respondent was called upon various times for payment of the maintenance charges but no heed was\r\npaid to the said notices by the respondent&nbsp;<br></p>','<p>&nbsp;Directing the respondent to pay the amount of Rs. 34,727/- due towards the maintenance charges.\r\nDirecting the respondent to pay compensation of Rs. 25,000/- to the complainants<br></p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Directing the respondent to pay interest on the due amount as mentioned in the maintenance agreement\r\ntill the pendency of the present complaint till actual payment.&nbsp;<br></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'BeeG','2019-02-16 11:09:59.000','BeeG','2019-02-16 11:09:59.000'),(1056,1309,'1309',1112,'29af80b1-85ed-4b88-8344-b429d2f24eca','FormTypeM',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Bee Gee Builtech','savindersinghgill@gmail.com',9988861126,0,0,'SCF 44-45, Ist Floor','Sector-9',13,15,'134108','1','SCF 44-45, Ist Floor','Sector-9',13,15,'134108','Savinder Singh Gill','savindersinghgill@gmail.com',9988861126,0,'Allottee','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0103','Palm Village','Rajni Rani','ashwanianeja1973@gmail.com',9781200007,0,'B-201, 2nd floor, Tower-B, Palm Village,','Village-Desumajra, Sector-126,',28,507,'140301','1','B-201, 2nd floor, Tower-B, Palm Village,','Village-Desumajra, Sector-126,',28,507,'140301','1','<p>That the complainant no. 1 is the promoter having RERA registration no. PBRERA-SAS80-PR0103, has\r\ndeveloped project under the name and style of “PALM VILLAGE”, located in Sector-126, NH-21, S.A.S.\r\nNagar, Mohali. The complainant no. 2 is a maintenance agency which has been entrusted upon with the\r\nmaintenance of the project of the complainant no. 1. It is pertinent to mention here that both the\r\ncomplainants have entered into an agreement for the said reason. That the respondents are allottees of\r\nthe complainant no. 1 who had applied for an apartment measuring 2180 sq. ft. (Approximate Super Area)\r\non 25.08.2011 in the abovementioned project and in pursuance of the said booking, they were allotted flat\r\nno. B-201 on 2nd Floor in Tower-B vide allotment letter dated 13.09.2011. That a buyer’s agreement was\r\nsigned between the complainant no. 1 and the respondents. The respondents were thereafter\r\noffered possession of the said apartment on 06.11.2015 and the possession of the said apartment was\r\ntaken over by the respondents. Further it is pertinent to mention here that in the possession handing over\r\nletter, the respondent had undertaken to pay the maintenance charges after taking over possession of the\r\nsaid apartment and had also undertaken to enter into a maintenance agreement. The respondent had\r\nthereafter, entered into a maintenance agreement dated 06.11.2015 with the complainant no. 2. That the\r\nrespondents despite been in possession of the said apartment, has not been paying the maintenance\r\ncharges fixed as per the maintenance agreement and is enjoying all the services free of cost. It is further\r\npertinent to mention here that a number of public notices has been got attached in the society whereby\r\nthe respondent was called upon various times for payment of the maintenance charges but no heed was\r\npaid to the said notices by the respondents.<br></p>','<p>&nbsp;Directing the respondent to pay the amount of Rs. 34,727/- due towards the maintenance charges.\r\nDirecting the respondent to pay compensation of Rs. 25,000/- to the complainants<br></p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Directing the respondents to pay interest on the due amount as mentioned in the maintenance agreement\r\ntill the pendency of the present complaint till actual payment.&nbsp;<br></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'BeeG','2019-02-16 11:15:48.000','BeeG','2019-02-16 11:15:48.000'),(1057,1324,'1324',1388,'9f925b8d-3343-4247-ac11-f438350e37ab','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Vijesh Jaiswal','vijesh44@gmail.com',9416001990,0,0,'D-44, Bawa Vihar','Sector-9',13,1,'134003','1','F-112, Orbit Apartments','VIP Road, Adjacent Metro Wholesale',28,507,'140603','Ashutosh Vig','SARassociates1211@gmail.com',9915882345,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0085','SUSHMA CHANDIGARH GRANDE','Sh. Binder Pal Mittal, Chairman, M/s Sushma Buildtech Limited','bhupinder@sushmabuildtech.com',0,0,'Unit No.B-107, Business Complex, 1st Floor','Industrial Area-1, Elante Mall',6,128,'160055','1','Unit No.B-107, Business Complex, 1st Floor','Industrial Area-1, Elante Mall',6,128,'160055','1','<p>1.	That as the son of the applicants was suffering from celiac disease and for easy access to the good hospitals in Tricity, the applicants purchased Apartment No. G-1203 in Tower-G for a sale consideration of Rs. 45,77,100/- (Annexure A-2). Later on, the applicants requested the respondents to change the Apartment and the respondent allotted Apartment No. G-403 on 4th Floor in “G” Tower vide allotment letter dated 15.09.2016 (Annexure A-1) in exchange of G-1203 and adjusted the above-payment in G-403. The applicants paid full payment of the apartment i.e. G-1203 on 04.07.2016. \r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>2.	That as per the terms and condition of the agreement dated 15.09.2016 (Annexure A-3), the respondents were bound to deliver the possession within 12 months from the date of execution of Annexure A-3 but the respondents failed to deliver the actual physical possession of the Apartment by the due date. The relevant clause regarding the possession is reproduced hereunder:- \r\n</p><p>“14.	POSSESSION :\r\n</p><p>&nbsp;(d)	The Developer shall endeavor to give possession of the said unit to the buyer within a period of Twelve (12) months from the date of execution of this Agreement unless and until restrained by circumstances beyond its contemplation and control and subject to timely payment by the allottee. Besides, the Developer can take six months grace period for completing and handing over the said unit to the buyer.”\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>3.	That being aggrieved from the act and conduct of the respondents, the applicants made numerous representations (Annexure A-4) for delivering the possession of the apartment but to no effect. \r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>4.	Rule 16 of Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Rules provides for Interest payable by the promoter and the allottee for delay in delivery of possession to the allottess, which is reproduced hereunder for the ready reference to this Hon’ble Tribunal :-\r\n</p><p>“Rule 16- Interest payable by the promoter and the allottee –The rate of interest payable by the promoter to the allottee or b</p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:0in;\r\nmargin-left:1.0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:11.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\">(i)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Respondents be directed to pay Interest on\r\naccount of delay in handing over the possession of the Apartment as per Rule 16\r\nof Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Rules which provides\r\nState Bank of India highest marginal cost of lending rate plus 2% from the\r\nrespective date of deposit made by the complainants. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:0in;\r\nmargin-left:1.0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:11.0pt;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:0in;\r\nmargin-left:1.0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:11.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\">(ii)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; It is further prayed that this Hon\'ble\r\nTribunal may grant any other relief, which it deems fit and proper, in the\r\nfacts and circumstances of the present case, in the interest of justice, equity\r\nand fair play.<o:p></o:p></span></p>',4577100.00,4577100.00,'2017-09-14 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Respondent be restrained from floating any other project, till the claim of the applicants for delivery of possession and for compensation, is settled.&nbsp;</p>','1','','2016-09-15 00:00:00','2016-09-15 00:00:00','G-403 on 4th Floor in “G”  \r\nTower, Village : Bishangarh and Bishanpura, Zirakpur, Tehsil : Derabassi, District : S.A.S. Nagar','','',2,0,0,0,'VijeshJaiswal','2019-02-16 14:35:00.000','VijeshJaiswal','2019-02-16 14:35:00.000'),(1058,1324,'1324',1388,'9f925b8d-3343-4247-ac11-f438350e37ab','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-03-11 17:42:52.000','Vijesh Jaiswal','vijesh44@gmail.com',9416001990,0,0,'D-44, Bawa Vihar','Sector-9',13,1,'134003','1','F-112, Orbit Apartments','VIP Road, Adjacent Metro Wholesale',28,507,'140603','Ashutosh Vig','SARassociates1211@gmail.com',9915882345,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0085','SUSHMA CHANDIGARH GRANDE','Sh. Binder Pal Mittal, Chairman, M/s Sushma Buildtech Limited','bhupinder@sushmabuildtech.com',0,0,'Unit No.B-107, Business Complex, 1st Floor','Industrial Area-1, Elante Mall',6,128,'160055','1','Unit No.B-107, Business Complex, 1st Floor','Industrial Area-1, Elante Mall',6,128,'160055','1','<p>1.	That as the son of the applicants was suffering from celiac disease and for easy access to the good hospitals in Tricity, the applicants purchased Apartment No. G-1203 in Tower-G for a sale consideration of Rs. 45,77,100/- (Annexure A-2). Later on, the applicants requested the respondents to change the Apartment and the respondent allotted Apartment No. G-403 on 4th Floor in “G” Tower vide allotment letter dated 15.09.2016 (Annexure A-1) in exchange of G-1203 and adjusted the above-payment in G-403. The applicants paid full payment of the apartment i.e. G-1203 on 04.07.2016. \r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>2.	That as per the terms and condition of the agreement dated 15.09.2016 (Annexure A-3), the respondents were bound to deliver the possession within 12 months from the date of execution of Annexure A-3 but the respondents failed to deliver the actual physical possession of the Apartment by the due date. The relevant clause regarding the possession is reproduced hereunder:- \r\n</p><p>“14.	POSSESSION :\r\n</p><p>&nbsp;(d)	The Developer shall endeavor to give possession of the said unit to the buyer within a period of Twelve (12) months from the date of execution of this Agreement unless and until restrained by circumstances beyond its contemplation and control and subject to timely payment by the allottee. Besides, the Developer can take six months grace period for completing and handing over the said unit to the buyer.”\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>3.	That being aggrieved from the act and conduct of the respondents, the applicants made numerous representations (Annexure A-4) for delivering the possession of the apartment but to no effect. \r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>4.	Rule 16 of Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Rules provides for Interest payable by the promoter and the allottee for delay in delivery of possession to the allottess, which is reproduced hereunder for the ready reference to this Hon’ble Tribunal :-\r\n</p><p>“Rule 16- Interest payable by the promoter and the allottee –The rate of interest payable by the promoter to the allottee or b</p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:0in;\r\nmargin-left:1.0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:11.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\">(i)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Respondents be directed to pay Interest on\r\naccount of delay in handing over the possession of the Apartment as per Rule 16\r\nof Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Rules which provides\r\nState Bank of India highest marginal cost of lending rate plus 2% from the\r\nrespective date of deposit made by the complainants. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:0in;\r\nmargin-left:1.0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:11.0pt;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:0in;\r\nmargin-left:1.0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:11.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\">(ii)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; It is further prayed that this Hon\'ble\r\nTribunal may grant any other relief, which it deems fit and proper, in the\r\nfacts and circumstances of the present case, in the interest of justice, equity\r\nand fair play.<o:p></o:p></span></p>',4577100.00,4577100.00,'2017-09-14 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Respondent be restrained from floating any other project, till the claim of the applicants for delivery of possession and for compensation, is settled.&nbsp;</p>','1','','2016-09-15 00:00:00','2016-09-15 00:00:00','G-403 on 4th Floor in “G”  \r\nTower, Village : Bishangarh and Bishanpura, Zirakpur, Tehsil : Derabassi, District : S.A.S. Nagar','','',1,0,0,0,'VijeshJaiswal','2019-02-16 14:36:29.000','VijeshJaiswal','2019-02-16 14:36:29.000'),(1059,1295,'1295',1374,'82227358-6d09-4a12-8b11-de1e75c71cac','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-02-25 20:26:50.000','Dev Raj Sharma , Satya Devi Sharma , Ranjan Sharma , Jyoti Sharma','deva_2406@yahoo.co.in',9463087206,0,601475614290,'H.No. 306','Sector - 35A, Chandigarh',6,128,'160017','1','H.No. 306','Sector - 35A, Chandigarh',6,128,'160017','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PM0089','GBP Aeropolis City (formerly known as Yellowstone Landmark Infocity)','Mr.  TS Bhatia(MD)  Mr. Aprajit Sachdev(GM) Mr. Anupam Gupta, Director – GBP Group.','tejindersbhatia@gmail.com',9592969696,9814412946,'M/s. Aeropolis Infrastructure Pvt. Ltd.,','Aeropolis City, Sector 66-A, S.A.S. Nagar,',28,507,'160062','1','M/s. Aeropolis Infrastructure Pvt. Ltd.,','Aeropolis City, Sector 66-A, S.A.S. Nagar,',28,507,'160062','1','<p>1.<span style=\"white-space: pre;\">	</span> Mega IT Project of M/s Aeropolis Infrastructure Pvt. Ltd. (formerly known as M/s Sukhm Infrastructure pvt. Ltd.) Project: AEROPOLIS CITY (Formerly known as YELLOWSTONE LAND MARK INFOCITY), SECTOR 66A, Mohali, approved by the state Government was launched in the market in the year 2009.&nbsp; Promoters issued Misleading and False adds in the Media or otherwise using names of Big Corporate Houses such as MukeshAmbani led Reliance group, The Dalmias, Bergruen( US ) and Yellow stone Chandigarh based firm.</p><p>2.<span style=\"white-space: pre;\">	</span>On 17th Feb. 2010, Sukhm issued the Allotment letter in which it is on record and mentioned that “THAT ALLOTMENT LETTER IS SUBJECT TO SIGNING OF THE BUYER/SELLER AGREEMENT WITHIN 60 DAYS FROM THE ISSUANCE OF THIS LETTER.</p><p>3.<span style=\"white-space: pre;\">	</span>But M/s Sukhm has issued the BUYER/SELLER AGREEMENT in August 2013, In Buyer/Seller Agreement Clause 7 (a) read as ( Development of the said IT/Industrial Plots is likely to be completed within a tentative period of 18 months from the date of this Agreement.)</p><p>4.<span style=\"white-space: pre;\">	</span>We have paid under pressure up to 65% of the BSP.</p><p>5.<span style=\"white-space: pre;\">	</span>On 26.09.2018, M/s Sukham Infrastructures Pvt. Ltd. has signed Joint Development Agreement with GBP Group.</p><p>6.<span style=\"white-space: pre;\">	</span>As on date the status at the site of the project is as follows.</p><p>a)<span style=\"white-space: pre;\">	</span>Development work is insignificant, which can be verified.</p><p>b)<span style=\"white-space: pre;\">	</span>No demarcation of plots.</p><p>c)<span style=\"white-space: pre;\">	</span>No services are available.</p><p>d)<span style=\"white-space: pre;\">	</span>Patches of land which are shown on their approved maps, still not owned/ bought by them.</p><p>7.<span style=\"white-space: pre;\">	</span>As on date we strongly believe that promoters :-</p><p>a)<span style=\"white-space: pre;\">	</span>Does not have the approved layout plan from the competent Authority BEING DEFAULTER IN PAYMENT OF EDC.</p><p>b)<span style=\"white-space: pre;\">	</span>May not have valid agreement with State Govt. as on date.</p><p>c)<span style=\"white-space: pre;\">	</span>May have not acquired/purchased land which is part of promoters approved maps.</p>','<p>In view of the facts stated above , when promoters have failed on all fronts to give possession of plots even after 9 years of our investment,&nbsp; We request your honor as under to save us as we have invested all our life’s savings in this project.</p><p><br></p><p>a.<span style=\"white-space: pre;\">	</span>Direct the promoters and Govt. Authorities concerned to develop the Project immediately and give possession of plots to us.</p><p><br></p><p>b.<span style=\"white-space: pre;\">	</span>Payment of interest on the amount paid @ 18% p.a. (compounded) for the delay in giving the possession of plots.</p><p><br></p><p>c.<span style=\"white-space: pre;\">	</span>Pay compensation&nbsp; as per Seller/Buyers Agreement.</p><p>Any other relief which RERA may feel appropriate.</p>',15840000.00,10451397.00,'2015-08-08 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>a.<span style=\"white-space: pre;\">	</span>Payment of interest on the&nbsp; amount paid @ 18% (compound) for the delay in giving possession of plots.</p><p>b.<span style=\"white-space: pre;\">	</span>Pay compensation&nbsp;as per seller-Buyer agreement&nbsp;and mental harassment and agony suffered by us so long.</p><p>c.<span style=\"white-space: pre;\">	</span>Any other relief which RERA may feel appropriate.</p><p>d.<span style=\"white-space: pre;\">	</span>Direct the promoters and Govt. Authorities concerned to develop the Project immediately and give possession of plots to us.</p>','1','','2010-02-17 00:00:00','2013-08-08 00:00:00','Plot Number IT/P/MS/05 , IT/P/MS/06 M/s. Aeropolis Infrastructure Pvt. Ltd., Aeropolis City, Sector 66-A, S.A.S. Nagar, Mohali-160062','','',2,0,0,0,'devraj306','2019-02-17 15:02:50.000','devraj306','2019-02-17 15:02:50.000'),(1060,1213,'1213',1010,'a182232b-88d6-4711-8baa-f8a026fb675f','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-23 16:49:48.000','Raj Kumar and Kuljeet Kaur','lawofficeofhimanshuraj@gmail.com',9988100005,0,999057822446,'#102, Sector 10 A','',6,128,'160011','1','#102, Sector 10 A','',6,128,'160011','HIMANSHU RAJ','lawofficeofhimanshuraj@gmail.com',9988200001,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0005','Josan Heights','JSJ Builders Pvt Ltd','jsjbuilders.in@gmail.com',8699885568,0,'Shop No. 1-3, Josan Heights','Sector 126, Village Chhajumajra, Teh-Kharar',28,507,'140307','1','Shop No. 1-3, Josan Heights','Sector 126, Village Chhajumajra, Teh-Kharar',28,507,'140307','1','<font face=\"Thorndale, serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">The complainants had booked a unit with super area measuring 1423 Sq. Ft. at OPs project JOSAN HEIGHTS on 04.10.2016. That on 04.10.2016, the OP furnished an Allotment letter against the unit and allotted UNIT NO. 402, BLOCK C, MEASURING 1423 SQ. FT in OPs project JOSAN HEIGHTS. It was stated in the Allotment letter that the possession will be handed over by 25.10.2016.\r\n</span></font><div><font face=\"Thorndale, serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">That on 04.10.2016, the OP executed a BUILDER BUYERS AGREEMENT with the complainants and assured promised to hand over the possession including all the amenities as per the brochure of the unit. That on 25.10.2016, OP offered the possession of the unit to the complainant. That it is pertinent to mention here that neither did OP have the completion certificate for the project nor had the occupation certificate before offering possession to the complainants in 2016, meaning thereby no possession in the eyes of law.\r\n</span></font></div><div><font face=\"Thorndale, serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">That the OP directed the complainants to execute the sale deed against the said unit and the same was executed, under coercion and duress. That the OP received the PARTIAL COMPLETION CERTIFICATE on 14.12.2017 i.e. 12 months from the date of possession and OP has yet to receive Occupation certificate for the project and has offered possession of the unit without possessing OCCUPATION CERTIFICATE.\r\n</span></font></div><div><font face=\"Thorndale, serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">That it is pertinent to mention here that OP has installed Mobile Towers above complainants building without approvals which causes serious health hazard. That OP has failed to completely develop the project as per the brochure and has taken complete consideration against the unit from the complainants and has offered possession of the unit without possessing occupancy certificate. Therefore, the complainants craves the indulgence of the HONBLE RERA AUTHORITY PUNJAB to direct the OP to hand over the interest from the deemed date of possession till actual offer of possession according to the Real Estate Regulation and Development Act, 2016 and Punjab Real Estate Regulation and Development Rules, 20</span></font></div>','<pre class=\"aLF-aPX-K0-aPE\" style=\"user-select: text; font-family: &quot;Courier New&quot;, Courier, monospace, arial, sans-serif; margin-bottom: 0px; white-space: pre-wrap; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px;\">i	To direct the OP to compensate the complainant in the shape of compensation against the residential property so booked by the complainant for delayed possession from the deeded date of possession i.e. 25.10.2016 till grant of Occupancy certificate from the concerned authority according to section 18 Real Estate (Regulation And Development) Act, 2016, r/w Rule 16 of Punjab Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Rules, 2017.\r\n\r\nii	To direct the OP to remove the MOBILE Towers Installed above the residential Towers and pay compensation of Rs.5,00,000 (FIVE LAKS) for causing serious health hazard by installing the same.\r\n\r\niii	To direct the OP to pay Rs. 2,00,000  for causing mental agony caused to the complainants.\r\n\r\niv	To direct the OP to pay Rs. 14,00,000 to the complainants as the deficiency in services for not completing the project as per brochure &amp; commitments made to the RERA AUTHORITY, especially Gym, Swimming Pool, Club House etc. , till date under Section 12 of the Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Act, 2016\r\n\r\nv	 To direct the OP to pay Rs. 1,40,000  for causing physical harassment caused to the complainants.\r\n\r\nvi	To direct the OP to complete all the infractions committed by the OP as per the brochure as soon as possible\r\n\r\nvii	To direct the respondent to pay Rs. 1,00,000 as litigation cost as the complainants was constrained to file the same because of the callous and indifferent attitude of the opposite party.\r\n\r\nviii	To revoke the license of the OP under section 7 of the Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) act, 2016.\r\n\r\nix	Any other relief or claim which the HON’BLE RERA AUTHORITY deems appropriate.</pre>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Not Prayed</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'lawofficeofhimanshuraj','2019-02-18 15:37:08.000','lawofficeofhimanshuraj','2019-02-18 15:37:08.000'),(1061,1213,'1213',1010,'a182232b-88d6-4711-8baa-f8a026fb675f','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-23 16:49:48.000','Raj Kumar and Kuljeet Kaur','lawofficeofhimanshuraj@gmail.com',9988100005,0,999057822446,'#102, Sector 10 A','',6,128,'160011','1','#102, Sector 10 A','',6,128,'160011','HIMANSHU RAJ','lawofficeofhimanshuraj@gmail.com',9988200001,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0005','Josan Heights','JSJ Builders Pvt Ltd','jsjbuilders.in@gmail.com',8699885568,0,'Shop No. 1-3, Josan Heights','Sector 126, Village Chhajumajra, Teh-Kharar',28,507,'140307','1','Shop No. 1-3, Josan Heights','Sector 126, Village Chhajumajra, Teh-Kharar',28,507,'140307','1','<font face=\"Thorndale, serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">The complainants had booked a unit with super area measuring 1423 Sq. Ft. at OPs project JOSAN HEIGHTS on 04.10.2016. That on 04.10.2016, the OP furnished an Allotment letter against the unit and allotted UNIT NO. 402, BLOCK C, MEASURING 1423 SQ. FT in OPs project JOSAN HEIGHTS. It was stated in the Allotment letter that the possession will be handed over by 25.10.2016.\r\n</span></font><div><font face=\"Thorndale, serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">That on 04.10.2016, the OP executed a BUILDER BUYERS AGREEMENT with the complainants and assured promised to hand over the possession including all the amenities as per the brochure of the unit. That on 25.10.2016, OP offered the possession of the unit to the complainant. That it is pertinent to mention here that neither did OP have the completion certificate for the project nor had the occupation certificate before offering possession to the complainants in 2016, meaning thereby no possession in the eyes of law.\r\