onospace, arial, sans-serif; margin-bottom: 0px; white-space: pre-wrap; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px;\">i	To direct the OP to compensate the complainant in the shape of compensation against the residential property so booked by the complainant for delayed possession from the deeded date of possession i.e. 25.10.2016 till grant of Occupancy certificate from the concerned authority according to section 18 Real Estate (Regulation And Development) Act, 2016, r/w Rule 16 of Punjab Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Rules, 2017.\r\n\r\nii	To direct the OP to remove the MOBILE Towers Installed above the residential Towers and pay compensation of Rs.5,00,000 (FIVE LAKS) for causing serious health hazard by installing the same.\r\n\r\niii	To direct the OP to pay Rs. 2,00,000  for causing mental agony caused to the complainants.\r\n\r\niv	To direct the OP to pay Rs. 14,00,000 to the complainants as the deficiency in services for not completing the project as per brochure &amp; commitments made to the RERA AUTHORITY, especially Gym, Swimming Pool, Club House etc. , till date under Section 12 of the Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Act, 2016\r\n\r\nv	 To direct the OP to pay Rs. 1,40,000  for causing physical harassment caused to the complainants.\r\n\r\nvi	To direct the OP to complete all the infractions committed by the OP as per the brochure as soon as possible\r\n\r\nvii	To direct the respondent to pay Rs. 1,00,000 as litigation cost as the complainants was constrained to file the same because of the callous and indifferent attitude of the opposite party.\r\n\r\nviii	To revoke the license of the OP under section 7 of the Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) act, 2016.\r\n\r\nix	Any other relief or claim which the HON’BLE RERA AUTHORITY deems appropriate.</pre>',3000000.00,3000000.00,'2016-10-25 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Not Prayed</p>','1','','2016-10-04 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',1,1,0,0,'lawofficeofhimanshuraj','2019-02-18 15:45:46.000','lawofficeofhimanshuraj','2019-02-18 15:45:46.000'),(1064,1318,'1318',1112,'29af80b1-85ed-4b88-8344-b429d2f24eca','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-04-02 17:01:31.000','Bee Gee Builtech','savindersinghgill@gmail.com',9988861126,0,0,'SCF 44-45, Ist Floor','Sector-9',13,15,'134108','1','SCF 44-45, Ist Floor','Sector-9',13,15,'134108','Savinder Singh Gill','savindersinghgill@gmail.com',9988861126,0,'Allottee','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0103','Palm Village','Mamta Handa','strikerbrother@gmail.com',9816070090,0,'# 91, sector-3, Roura','Bilaspur',14,106,'174001','1','# 91, sector-3, Roura','Bilaspur',14,106,'174001','1','<p>That the complainant no. 1 is the promoter having RERA registration no. PBRERA-SAS80-PR0103, has\r\ndeveloped project under the name and style of “PALM VILLAGE”, located in Sector-126, NH-21, S.A.S.\r\nNagar, Mohali. The complainant no. 2 is a maintenance agency which has been entrusted upon with the\r\nmaintenance of the project of the complainant no. 1. It is pertinent to mention here that both the\r\ncomplainants have entered into an agreement for the said reason. That the respondent is allottee of\r\nthe complainant no. 1 who had applied for an apartment measuring 2180 sq. ft. (Approximate Super Area)\r\non 02.05.2014 in the abovementioned project and in pursuance of the said booking, they were allotted flat\r\nno. B-1201 on 12th Floor in Tower-B vide allotment letter dated 02.05.2014. That a buyer’s agreement\r\nwas signed between the complainant no. 1 and the respondent on 02.05.2014. The respondent was thereafter offered possession of the said apartment and the possession was taken over by the\r\nrespondent on 22.04.2015. Further it is pertinent to mention here that in the possession handing over\r\nletter, the respondent had undertaken to pay the maintenance charges after taking over possession of\r\nthe said apartment and had also undertaken to enter into a maintenance agreement. The respondent the