cate also but it also goes in vain and got no response from them.</p><p>8. Kindly help me either to takeover possession of my Plots which have been allotted by them. If they fail to do so then please fine them litigation fees and harassment/ mentally torture charge of Rs 2 lac alingwith Refund of my Amount Rs 1319360 with interest till date.</p><p>9. I shall be thankful to you for this act of kindness.</p>','<p>Sir,&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>I want relief for mentally torture and harassment ie Rs 100000.</p><p>I want &nbsp;litigation fees of Rs 100000.</p><p><br></p><p>The total relief Rs 200000 along with refund of my Amount Rs 1319360 plus interest till date.</p>',4750000.00,1319360.00,'2018-04-16 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Sir,&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>I want relief for mentally torture and harassment ie Rs 100000.</p><p>I want &nbsp;litigation fees of Rs 100000.</p><p><br></p><p>The total relief Rs 200000 along with refund of my Amount Rs 1319360 plus interest till date.</p>','1','','2017-07-03 00:00:00','2017-08-19 00:00:00','Plot no 158 and 124,\r\nPosh City\r\nSector 92, Mohali','','',1,1,0,0,'HSToor','2019-02-19 22:35:09.000','HSToor','2019-02-19 22:35:09.000'),(1081,1325,'1325',1112,'29af80b1-85ed-4b88-8344-b429d2f24eca','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Bee Gee Builtech','savindersinghgill@gmail.com',9988861126,0,0,'SCF 44-45, Ist Floor','Sector-9',13,15,'134108','1','SCF 44-45, Ist Floor','Sector-9',13,15,'134108','Savinder Singh Gill','savindersinghgill@gmail.com',9988861126,0,'Allottee','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0103','Palm Village','Varinder Singh Jawanda','varinders@milleniumsystem.com',9810093075,0,'#-231-E, Greater Kailash Part-1','New Delhi',10,429,'110048','1','#-231-E, Greater Kailash Part-1','New Delhi',10,429,'110048','0','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: roboto, serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">That\r\nthe complainant no. 1 is a promoter having RERA registration no.\r\nPBRERA-SAS80-PR0103, which has developed project under the name and style of\r\n“PALM VILLAGE”, located in Sector-126, NH-21, S.A.S. Nagar, Mohali. The\r\ncomplainant no. 2 is a maintenance agency which has been entrusted upon with\r\nthe maintenance of the project of the complainant no. 1. It is pertinent to\r\nmention here that both the complainants have entered into an agreement for the\r\nsaid reason. That the respondent is allottee of the complainant no. 1 who\r\nhad purchased an apartment measuring 2180 sq. ft. (Approximate Super Area) in\r\nresale on 16.03.2016 in the abovementioned project and he was allotted flat\r\nno. D-1001 on 10th Floor in Tower-D vide re-allotment letter dated 29.04.2016.\r\nThat a buyer’s agreement was signed between the complainant no. 1 and the\r\noriginal allotees on 24.10.2014. The respondent was thereafter offered\r\npossession of the said apartment and the possession was taken over by the\r\noriginal allottees on 02.09.2015. The said agreement was endorsed in the name of\r\nrespondent after resale of the said apartment and all the rights and\r\nliabilities were undertaken by the respondent as they had stepped into the\r\nshoes of the original allottees.&nbsp; It is pertinent to mention here that in the\r\npossession handing over letter, the respondent had undertaken to pay the\r\nmaintenance charges after taking over possession of the said apartment and had\r\nalso undertaken to enter into a maintenance agreement. The original allottees thereafter, entered into a maintenance agreement dated 02.09.2015 with the\r\ncomplainant no. 2. That the respondent despite been in possession of the said\r\napartment, has not been paying the maintenance charges fixed as per the\r\nmaintenance agreement and is enjoying all the services free of cost.</span><o:p></o:p></p>','<p>&nbsp;Directing the respondent to pay the amount of Rs. 46,304/- due towards the maintenance charges.\r\nDirecting the respondent to pay compensation of Rs. 25,000/- to the complainants<br></p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Directing the respondent to pay interest on the due amount as mentioned in the maintenance agreement\r\ntill the pendency of the present complaint till actual payment.&nbsp;<br></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'BeeG','2019-02-20 09:31:57.000','BeeG','2019-02-20 09:31:57.000'),(1082,1325,'1325',1112,'29af80b1-85ed-4b88-8344-b429d2f24eca','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-02-23 10:23:44.000','Bee Gee Builtech','savindersinghgill@gmail.com',9988861126,0,0,'SCF 44-45, Ist Floor','Sector-9',13,15,'134108','1','SCF 44-45, Ist Floor','Sector-9',13,15,'134108','Savinder Singh Gill','savindersinghgill@gmail.com',9988861126,0,'Allottee','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0103','Palm Village','Varinder Singh Jawanda','varinders@milleniumsystem.com',9810093075,0,'#-231-E, Greater Kailash Part-1','New Delhi',10,429,'110048','1','#-231-E, Greater Kailash Part-1','New Delhi',10,429,'110048','0','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: roboto, serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">That\r\nthe complainant no. 1 is a promoter having RERA registration no.\r\nPBRERA-SAS80-PR0103, which has developed project under the name and style of\r\n“PALM VILLAGE”, located in Sector-126, NH-21, S.A.S. Nagar, Mohali. The\r\ncomplainant no. 2 is a maintenance agency which has been entrusted upon with\r\nthe maintenance of the project of the complainant no. 1. It is pertinent to\r\nmention here that both the complainants have entered into an agreement for the\r\nsaid reason. That the respondent is allottee of the complainant no. 1 who\r\nhad purchased an apartment measuring 2180 sq. ft. (Approximate Super Area) in\r\nresale on 16.03.2016 in the abovementioned project and he was allotted flat\r\nno. D-1001 on 10th Floor in Tower-D vide re-allotment letter dated 29.04.2016.\r\nThat a buyer’s agreement was signed between the complainant no. 1 and the\r\noriginal allotees on 24.10.2014. The respondent was thereafter offered\r\npossession of the said apartment and the possession was taken over by the\r\noriginal allottees on 02.09.2015. The said agreement was endorsed in the name of\r\nrespondent after resale of the said apartment and all the rights and\r\nliabilities were undertaken by the respondent as they had stepped into the\r\nshoes of the original allottees.&nbsp; It is pertinent to mention here that in the\r\npossession handing over letter, the respondent had undertaken to pay the\r\nmaintenance charges after taking over possession of the said apartment and had\r\nalso undertaken to enter into a maintenance agreement. The original allottees thereafter, entered into a maintenance agreement dated 02.09.2015 with the\r\ncomplainant no. 2. That the respondent despite been in possession of the said\r\napartment, has not been paying the maintenance charges fixed as per the\r\nmaintenance agreement and is enjoying all the services free of cost.</span><o:p></o:p></p>','<p>&nbsp;Directing the respondent to pay the amount of Rs. 46,304/- due towards the maintenance charges.\r\nDirecting the respondent to pay compensation of Rs. 25,000/- to the complainants<br></p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Directing the respondent to pay interest on the due amount as mentioned in the maintenance agreement\r\ntill the pendency of the present complaint till actual payment.&nbsp;<br></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'BeeG','2019-02-20 09:33:49.000','BeeG','2019-02-20 09:33:49.000'),(1083,1330,'1330',1112,'29af80b1-85ed-4b88-8344-b429d2f24eca','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Bee Gee Builtech','savindersinghgill@gmail.com',9988861126,0,0,'SCF 44-45, Ist Floor','Sector-9',13,15,'134108','1','SCF 44-45, Ist Floor','Sector-9',13,15,'134108','Savinder Singh Gill','savindersinghgill@gmail.com',9988861126,0,'Allottee','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0103','Palm Village','Manoj Kumar Arora','mka150266@gmaik.com',9958115380,0,'hh','',6,128,'160011','1','hh','',6,128,'160011','0','<p>d</p>','<p>d</p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>d</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'BeeG','2019-02-20 09:41:19.000','BeeG','2019-02-20 09:41:19.000'),(1084,1175,'1175',1239,'d25b078a-2844-47e7-9d66-87c143312e53','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-28 10:16:49.000','LEENA KUMARI','cmavishal85@gmail.com',8968318866,0,0,'Flat No .226, Ground Floor, Noor Homes','Kharar Landranroad, Sector 111, Mohali',28,507,'160055','1','Flat No .226, Ground Floor, Noor Homes','Kharar Landranroad, Sector 111, Mohali',28,507,'160055','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0219','M/S. GGP BUILDTECH PRIVATE LIMITED','M/S. GGP BUILDTECH PRIVATE LIMITED','ajayguptaggp@gmail.com',9815990640,0,'Mr. Ajay Gupta, # 402, Shivalik City, Sector 127','Kharar, SAS Nagar, Mohali',28,507,'160055','1','Mr. Ajay Gupta, # 402, Shivalik City, Sector 127','Kharar, SAS Nagar, Mohali',28,507,'160055','1','<p>That the project named Noor Homes is currently being promoted/developed by GGP Buildtech Pvt Limited. The Promoters of M/s GGP BUILDTECH PVT LTD started their business initially with a Partnership firm M/s Singla Builders &amp; Promoters in which Sh. Ajay Gupta and Sh. Amandeep Singla were partners. That the Project Named Noor Homes is launched by GGP Buildtech Pvt Limited in February 2014. That the Builder (GGP Buildtech Pvt Limited) had come up with advertisement/public offer to sell 1, 2, 3 BHK Apartments &amp; 3 BHK Villas to be constructed at Sector 115, Village Sante Majra, Tehsil Kharar, District Mohali with a construction target to be completed in 2017. That the Complainants (society members) start booking flats from Builder from 2014. That to some Complainants the flats were forcefully handed over by builder in incomplete stage. That some Complainants were forced to pay 100% payment to Builder for incomplete flats by threatening them from goons hired by builders. That Some Complainants were forced to execute sale deed for less price paying money in cash or for shell companies (Daya Infra) and thus frauding with GST and service tax.That These flats are incomplete to such extent that there is no permanent water connection,internal roads, electricity, sewerage connections, Sewerage treatment plant, staircase, streetlights, fire protection system etc.That these flats are handed over without obtaining occupancy certificate from MC khararThat Builder was approached time to time and several MOM’s were signed but till date.That MOM is attached as Annexure-1, where in Builder has initially agreed to complete the project by 31-March 2016.That vide MOM dated 30-April-2017 Builder agreed to complete the project by 31-Jan-2018. That again MOM vide 18.09.2017 Builder agreed to complete project in next 6 months i.e Mar-2018.&nbsp; That status of project is same&nbsp; as mentioned in point No.9</p><div><br></div>','<p>a. Direct PSPCL for permanent electricity connections for the 65 families (Complainant).Direct MC kharar for permanent water and sewerage connections to the society.Direct Inquiry against involvement of Municipal Corporation with Builder in cheating the Public by allowing sale deed to be executed without issuing occupancy certificate.Direct Inquiry against Builder regarding diversion of project funds to other shell companies.Action against Builder for non completion of Project.Direct Inquiry against Builder regarding theft of GST.Pledge/Stay on&nbsp; selling if the Properties of Builder, Promoters, Directors with immediate effect to avoid misuse of diverted funds.Pass any other order/orders which PBRERA may deem fit in the facts and circumstances of the case.</p><p>b. As we are facing mentally, physically, socially and financially&nbsp; due to the non availability of electricity at our residence and the following financial relief is sought.</p><p>1. During the visit and meeting with the builder on dated 5th Nov 2018 our parents faced medical emergency and we have to rush to the hospital and till date he is under treatment and suffering. An amount of Rs. 5,00,000/- as&nbsp; claim may be consider for the health loss and mental stress to the family.</p><p>2. Due to non availability of electricity&nbsp; for the last and two and half month which cause social defamation.&nbsp;&nbsp;An amount of&nbsp; Rs. 3,00,000/- as&nbsp; claim may be consider.</p><p>3.&nbsp; As we are providing freelancer financial services which badly effected by the non availability of electricity which cause financial loss to the tune of Rs. 2,00,000/-&nbsp;</p><p>4. Litigation and RERA application as per actual estimated to the tune of Rs. 50,000/-</p><p>c. The final we pray that as alternative the complete amount as consideration of the flat along with the interest.</p><p><br></p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>a. Direct PSPCL for permanent electricity connections for the 65 families (Complainant).Direct MC kharar for permanent water and sewerage connections to the society.Direct Inquiry against involvement of Municipal Corporation with Builder in cheating the Public by allowing sale deed to be executed without issuing occupancy certificate.Direct Inquiry against Builder regarding diversion of project funds to other shell companies.Action against Builder for non completion of Project.Direct Inquiry against Builder regarding theft of GST.Pledge/Stay on&nbsp; selling if the Properties of Builder, Promoters, Directors with immediate effect to avoid misuse of diverted funds.Pass any other order/orders which PBRERA may deem fit in the facts and circumstances of the case.</p><p>b. As we are facing mentally, physically, socially and financially&nbsp; due to the non availability of electricity at our residence and the following financial relief is sought.</p><p>1. During the visit and meeting with the builder on dated 5th Nov 2018 our parents faced medical emergency and we have to rush to the hospital and till date he is under treatment and suffering. An amount of Rs. 5,00,000/- as&nbsp; claim may be consider for the health loss and mental stress to the family.</p><p>2. Due to non availability of electricity&nbsp; for the last and two and half month which cause social defamation.&nbsp;&nbsp;An amount of&nbsp; Rs. 3,00,000/- as&nbsp; claim may be consider.</p><p>3.&nbsp; As we are providing freelancer financial services which badly effected by the non availability of electricity which cause financial loss to the tune of Rs. 2,00,000/-&nbsp;</p><p>4. Litigation and RERA application as per actual estimated to the tune of Rs. 50,000/-</p><p>c. The final we pray that as alternative the complete amount as consideration of the flat along with the interest.</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'LeenaKumari','2019-02-20 15:53:42.000','LeenaKumari','2019-02-20 15:53:42.000'),(1085,1175,'1175',1239,'d25b078a-2844-47e7-9d66-87c143312e53','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-02-20 16:24:58.000','LEENA KUMARI','cmavishal85@gmail.com',8968318866,0,0,'Flat No .226, Ground Floor, Noor Homes','Kharar Landranroad, Sector 111, Mohali',28,507,'160055','1','Flat No .226, Ground Floor, Noor Homes','Kharar Landranroad, Sector 111, Mohali',28,507,'160055','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0219','M/S. GGP BUILDTECH PRIVATE LIMITED','M/S. GGP BUILDTECH PRIVATE LIMITED','ajayguptaggp@gmail.com',9815990640,0,'Mr. Ajay Gupta, # 402, Shivalik City, Sector 127','Kharar, SAS Nagar, Mohali',28,507,'160055','1','Mr. Ajay Gupta, # 402, Shivalik City, Sector 127','Kharar, SAS Nagar, Mohali',28,507,'160055','1','<p>That the project named Noor Homes is currently being promoted/developed by GGP Buildtech Pvt Limited. The Promoters of M/s GGP BUILDTECH PVT LTD started their business initially with a Partnership firm M/s Singla Builders &amp; Promoters in which Sh. Ajay Gupta and Sh. Amandeep Singla were partners. That the Project Named Noor Homes is launched by GGP Buildtech Pvt Limited in February 2014. That the Builder (GGP Buildtech Pvt Limited) had come up with advertisement/public offer to sell 1, 2, 3 BHK Apartments &amp; 3 BHK Villas to be constructed at Sector 115, Village Sante Majra, Tehsil Kharar, District Mohali with a construction target to be completed in 2017. That the Complainants (society members) start booking flats from Builder from 2014. That to some Complainants the flats were forcefully handed over by builder in incomplete stage. That some Complainants were forced to pay 100% payment to Builder for incomplete flats by threatening them from goons hired by builders. That Some Complainants were forced to execute sale deed for less price paying money in cash or for shell companies (Daya Infra) and thus frauding with GST and service tax.That These flats are incomplete to such extent that there is no permanent water connection,internal roads, electricity, sewerage connections, Sewerage treatment plant, staircase, streetlights, fire protection system etc.That these flats are handed over without obtaining occupancy certificate from MC khararThat Builder was approached time to time and several MOM’s were signed but till date.That MOM is attached as Annexure-1, where in Builder has initially agreed to complete the project by 31-March 2016.That vide MOM dated 30-April-2017 Builder agreed to complete the project by 31-Jan-2018. That again MOM vide 18.09.2017 Builder agreed to complete project in next 6 months i.e Mar-2018.&nbsp; That status of project is same&nbsp; as mentioned in point No.9</p><div><br></div>','<p>a. Direct PSPCL for permanent electricity connections for the 65 families (Complainant).Direct MC kharar for permanent water and sewerage connections to the society.Direct Inquiry against involvement of Municipal Corporation with Builder in cheating the Public by allowing sale deed to be executed without issuing occupancy certificate.Direct Inquiry against Builder regarding diversion of project funds to other shell companies.Action against Builder for non completion of Project.Direct Inquiry against Builder regarding theft of GST.Pledge/Stay on&nbsp; selling if the Properties of Builder, Promoters, Directors with immediate effect to avoid misuse of diverted funds.Pass any other order/orders which PBRERA may deem fit in the facts and circumstances of the case.</p><p>b. As we are facing mentally, physically, socially and financially&nbsp; due to the non availability of electricity at our residence and the following financial relief is sought.</p><p>1. During the visit and meeting with the builder on dated 5th Nov 2018 our parents faced medical emergency and we have to rush to the hospital and till date he is under treatment and suffering. An amount of Rs. 5,00,000/- as&nbsp; claim may be consider for the health loss and mental stress to the family.</p><p>2. Due to non availability of electricity&nbsp; for the last and two and half month which cause social defamation.&nbsp;&nbsp;An amount of&nbsp; Rs. 3,00,000/- as&nbsp; claim may be consider.</p><p>3.&nbsp; As we are providing freelancer financial services which badly effected by the non availability of electricity which cause financial loss to the tune of Rs. 2,00,000/-&nbsp;</p><p>4. Litigation and RERA application as per actual estimated to the tune of Rs. 50,000/-</p><p>c. The final we pray that as alternative the complete amount as consideration of the flat along with the interest.</p><p><br></p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>a. Direct PSPCL for permanent electricity connections for the 65 families (Complainant).Direct MC kharar for permanent water and sewerage connections to the society.Direct Inquiry against involvement of Municipal Corporation with Builder in cheating the Public by allowing sale deed to be executed without issuing occupancy certificate.Direct Inquiry against Builder regarding diversion of project funds to other shell companies.Action against Builder for non completion of Project.Direct Inquiry against Builder regarding theft of GST.Pledge/Stay on&nbsp; selling if the Properties of Builder, Promoters, Directors with immediate effect to avoid misuse of diverted funds.Pass any other order/orders which PBRERA may deem fit in the facts and circumstances of the case.</p><p>b. As we are facing mentally, physically, socially and financially&nbsp; due to the non availability of electricity at our residence and the following financial relief is sought.</p><p>1. During the visit and meeting with the builder on dated 5th Nov 2018 our parents faced medical emergency and we have to rush to the hospital and till date he is under treatment and suffering. An amount of Rs. 5,00,000/- as&nbsp; claim may be consider for the health loss and mental stress to the family.</p><p>2. Due to non availability of electricity&nbsp; for the last and two and half month which cause social defamation.&nbsp;&nbsp;An amount of&nbsp; Rs. 3,00,000/- as&nbsp; claim may be consider.</p><p>3.&nbsp; As we are providing freelancer financial services which badly effected by the non availability of electricity which cause financial loss to the tune of Rs. 2,00,000/-&nbsp;</p><p>4. Litigation and RERA application as per actual estimated to the tune of Rs. 50,000/-</p><p>c. The final we pray that as alternative the complete amount as consideration of the flat along with the interest.</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',1,1,0,0,'LeenaKumari','2019-02-20 15:54:08.000','LeenaKumari','2019-02-20 15:54:08.000'),(1086,1253,'1253',1322,'f69298e2-8ace-47aa-9c57-18b058cdc701','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-02-20 16:08:54.000','Munish Chajgotra','munishsinghlion@gmail.com',9419118586,0,0,'87/3, sharika vihar, lower roopnagar','Jammu',15,267,'180013','1','87/3, sharika vihar, lower roopnagar','Jammu',15,267,'180013','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0106','MONA CITYHOMES (MTPL)','MONACITY HOMES(MTPL), VIKAS MADAAN, AAKASH SETHIA,RENU JASWAL,  KAPIL','renu@mtplgroup.in',7696266800,0,'KL Road,sector 115, Mohali','Punjab',28,507,'140307','1','KL Road,sector 115, Mohali','Punjab',28,507,'140307','1','Dear san,\r\n<div>1.The begining of the deal, on first day when I visited at Monacity homes in the month of July 2018, its in the knowledge of the sales girl(Manpreet) &amp; her Manager( Mr. Mayank)that I am going to finance from canara bank. they said that its their duty to get the tie up with Canara bank and I have to book the flat only. The tie up with the said bank will be in process and get done in next 15 days.I visited two times again at Monacity homes in next 15 days and the topic was same..Tie up with Canara bank.\r\n</div><div>2. On 19 August, I had called up at Monacity homes for Booking of the Unit. before booking i again take confirmation from Ms. Manpreet/Mr. Mayank regarding the Tie up with the canara bank and the reply was\" AAP BAS BOOKING KARWAO, WOH HAMARA KAAM HAI, WOH HO JAYEGA\" . I booked on the same day with 1,00,000/- transfered to Monacity homes account. \r\n</div><div>3. On 23 september I had visited Monacity for agreement and submission of balance payment of Rs,2,80,000/-. Before sign of agreement and transfer of balancce 2,80,000/- I again checked for Tie up of canara bank. and I got the same reply from them that it will done in next 15 days. Mr. Kapil offered me the finance facility from Mona end but as already mentioned that my finance from Canara is pre sanctioned.\r\n</div><div>4. It is since last 3 months the tie up is in process and every time I am getting a new excuse from your end that the tie up is in process.\r\n</div><div>5. I had visited 7-8 times at Monacity homes after submission of 3,80,000/- as the possesion date commited by the mona authorities is 20th Nov 2018.\r\n</div><div>6. This is almost 2 months passed, I had submitted the sanction letter to your sales persons. but still the tie up is not done.\r\n</div><div>7. I had already requested to MTPL authorities for the refund but tey are making excuses.\r\n</div><div>8. I was interested to own a flat in Monacity but due to tie up issue its not done,results in a harrasment for me as I am travelling daily Amritsar-Chandigarh-Amritsar since last 45 days due to my job schedule</div>','<p style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0cm\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">Dear San,,<o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin: 0cm 0cm 7.5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">Please\r\nhelp me to get refund of my Booking amount for rs. 3,80,000/- as they are\r\nmaking excuses of 180 days and deduction of charges as there is nothing pending\r\nfrom my end nor any fault from my end.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin: 0cm 0cm 7.5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">I\r\nhad taken the possesion somewhere else and now am not in position to take a add\r\non flat. so it is requested to the RERA authorities to Please help me . I ned\r\nonly refund of My booking amount for Rs. 3,80,000/-<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>',3800000.00,380000.00,'2018-11-20 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Refund of Booking amount</p>','1','','2018-09-19 00:00:00','2018-09-24 00:00:00','C208, mona city homes, sec 115, mohali','','',1,1,0,0,'Munishchajgotra9','2019-02-20 16:01:04.000','Munishchajgotra9','2019-02-20 16:01:04.000'),(1087,1330,'1330',1112,'29af80b1-85ed-4b88-8344-b429d2f24eca','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Bee Gee Builtech','savindersinghgill@gmail.com',9988861126,0,0,'SCF 44-45, Ist Floor','Sector-9',13,15,'134108','1','SCF 44-45, Ist Floor','Sector-9',13,15,'134108','Savinder Singh Gill','savindersinghgill@gmail.com',9988861126,0,'Allottee','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0103','Palm Village','Manoj Kumar Arora','mka150266@gmaik.com',9958115380,0,'B-1102, 11th Floor, Tower-B, Palm Village ','Village-Desumajra, Sector-126',28,507,'140301','1','B-1102, 11th Floor, Tower-B, Palm Village ','Village-Desumajra, Sector-126',28,507,'140301','0','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: roboto, serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">That\r\nthe complainant no. 1 is a promoter having RERA registration no.\r\nPBRERA-SAS80-PR0103, which has developed project under the name and style of\r\n“PALM VILLAGE”, located in Sector-126, NH-21, S.A.S. Nagar, Mohali. The\r\ncomplainant no. 2 is a maintenance agency which has been entrusted upon with\r\nthe maintenance of the project of the complainant no. 1. It is pertinent to\r\nmention here that both the complainants have entered into an agreement for the\r\nsaid reason. That the respondents are allottees of the complainant no. 1 who\r\nhad purchased an apartment measuring 2180 sq. ft. (Approximate Super Area) in\r\nresale on 17.05.2016 in the abovementioned project and they were allotted flat\r\nno. B-1102 on 11th Floor in Tower-B vide re-allotment letter dated 19.05.2016.\r\nThat a buyer’s agreement was signed between the complainant no. 1 and the\r\noriginal allotees on 17.09.2012. The respondents were thereafter offered\r\npossession of the said apartment and the possession was taken over by the\r\noriginal allottee on 20.04.2016. The said agreement was endorsed in the name of\r\nrespondents after resale of the said apartment and all the rights and\r\nliabilities were undertaken by the respondents as they had stepped into the\r\nshoes of the original allottee.&nbsp; It is pertinent to mention here that in\r\nthe possession handing over letter, the respondents had undertaken to pay the\r\nmaintenance charges after taking over possession of the said apartment and had\r\nalso undertaken to enter into a maintenance agreement. The original allottees\r\nthereafter, entered into a maintenance agreement dated 20.04.2016 with the\r\ncomplainant no. 2. That the respondents despite been in possession of the said\r\napartment, has not been paying the maintenance charges fixed as per the maintenance\r\nagreement and is enjoying all the services free of cost.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p>&nbsp;Directing the respondents to pay the amount of Rs. 34,727/- due towards the maintenance charges.\r\nDirecting the respondents to pay compensation of Rs. 25,000/- to the complainants<br></p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Directing the respondents to pay interest on the due amount as mentioned in the maintenance agreement\r\ntill the pendency of the present complaint till actual payment.&nbsp;<br></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'BeeG','2019-02-20 16:38:22.000','BeeG','2019-02-20 16:38:22.000'),(1088,1330,'1330',1112,'29af80b1-85ed-4b88-8344-b429d2f24eca','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-02-21 18:31:41.000','Bee Gee Builtech','savindersinghgill@gmail.com',9988861126,0,0,'SCF 44-45, Ist Floor','Sector-9',13,15,'134108','1','SCF 44-45, Ist Floor','Sector-9',13,15,'134108','Savinder Singh Gill','savindersinghgill@gmail.com',9988861126,0,'Allottee','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0103','Palm Village','Manoj Kumar Arora','mka150266@gmaik.com',9958115380,0,'B-1102, 11th Floor, Tower-B, Palm Village ','Village-Desumajra, Sector-126',28,507,'140301','1','B-1102, 11th Floor, Tower-B, Palm Village ','Village-Desumajra, Sector-126',28,507,'140301','0','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: roboto, serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">That\r\nthe complainant no. 1 is a promoter having RERA registration no.\r\nPBRERA-SAS80-PR0103, which has developed project under the name and style of\r\n“PALM VILLAGE”, located in Sector-126, NH-21, S.A.S. Nagar, Mohali. The\r\ncomplainant no. 2 is a maintenance agency which has been entrusted upon with\r\nthe maintenance of the project of the complainant no. 1. It is pertinent to\r\nmention here that both the complainants have entered into an agreement for the\r\nsaid reason. That the respondents are allottees of the complainant no. 1 who\r\nhad purchased an apartment measuring 2180 sq. ft. (Approximate Super Area) in\r\nresale on 17.05.2016 in the abovementioned project and they were allotted flat\r\nno. B-1102 on 11th Floor in Tower-B vide re-allotment letter dated 19.05.2016.\r\nThat a buyer’s agreement was signed between the complainant no. 1 and the\r\noriginal allotees on 17.09.2012. The respondents were thereafter offered\r\npossession of the said apartment and the possession was taken over by the\r\noriginal allottee on 20.04.2016. The said agreement was endorsed in the name of\r\nrespondents after resale of the said apartment and all the rights and\r\nliabilities were undertaken by the respondents as they had stepped into the\r\nshoes of the original allottee.&nbsp; It is pertinent to mention here that in\r\nthe possession handing over letter, the respondents had undertaken to pay the\r\nmaintenance charges after taking over possession of the said apartment and had\r\nalso undertaken to enter into a maintenance agreement. The original allottees\r\nthereafter, entered into a maintenance agreement dated 20.04.2016 with the\r\ncomplainant no. 2. That the respondents despite been in possession of the said\r\napartment, has not been paying the maintenance charges fixed as per the maintenance\r\nagreement and is enjoying all the services free of cost.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p>&nbsp;Directing the respondents to pay the amount of Rs. 34,727/- due towards the maintenance charges.\r\nDirecting the respondents to pay compensation of Rs. 25,000/- to the complainants<br></p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Directing the respondents to pay interest on the due amount as mentioned in the maintenance agreement\r\ntill the pendency of the present complaint till actual payment.&nbsp;<br></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'BeeG','2019-02-20 16:42:03.000','BeeG','2019-02-20 16:42:03.000'),(1089,1198,'1198',1283,'a69593cc-e858-492f-ab4c-c34fdd75b5d8','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-19 18:20:06.000','Harinder Dhillon','gaurav.chopra@hotmail.com',9814013127,0,0,'House No. 360','Phase IV ',28,507,'160059','1','House No. 607','Sector 18B Chandigarh',6,128,'160018','Gaurav Chopra','gaurav.chopra@hotmail.com',9814013125,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0119','MOHALI HILLS','Emaar MGF Land Ltd','sorabh.kakar@emaarmgf.com',0,0,'Emaar MGF Land Ltd','40, Central Plaza, Ground Floor, Sector 105 Mohali',28,507,'140306','1','Emaar MGF Land Ltd','40, Central Plaza, Ground Floor, Sector 105 Mohali',28,507,'140306','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">i)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Allotment letter: 24.4.2007 <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">ii)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Apartment Buyer’s Agreement: 12.12.08 <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">iii)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Unit No. L3-F12-1203 in ‘The Views’ at\r\nMohali Hills<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">iv)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Amendment Agreement dated 27.8.2015 was\r\nexecuted between the Applicants and the Respondent whereby, while retaining all\r\nother clauses and provisions of the Buyer’s Agreement dated 12.12.2008, Unit\r\nNo. TVM-L2-F11-1101 having a super area of 2600 sq. Ft was allotted to the\r\nApplicants at the rate of Rs. 2950/- per sq. foot and consequently, the total\r\nsale consideration payable in respect of the Allotted Unit was revised from Rs.\r\n62,72,558/- to Rs. 83,40,000/-.&nbsp; <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-32.25pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">v)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Construction Linked Instalment Plan<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-32.25pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">vi)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Amount paid upto 7.2.2014: Rs. 72,96,406/- <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-32.25pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">vi)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; As per Clause 21.1 of the Apartment Buyer’s\r\nAgreement, the Respondent was under a contractual obligation to handover\r\npossession of the Allotted Unit within a period of 36 months from the date of\r\nallotment with a further relaxation of 90 days over.&nbsp; Hence, possession of the Allotted Unit was\r\nrequired to be handed over to the Applicants by the Respondent positively on or\r\nbefore 24.7.2010 <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-32.25pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">vii)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Aggrieved by the aforesaid omission and\r\nlapse of the Respondent, the Applicants had written a letter/e-mail to the\r\nRespondent for rescinding the contract and for seeking refund of the principal\r\namount paid by the Applicants in respect of the Allotted Unit alongwith\r\ninterest.&nbsp; Till date, however, the\r\naforesaid demand raised by the Applicants has not been acceded to by the\r\nRespondent and thus, vide the instant complaint, the Applicants seek refund of\r\nthe monies paid by them to the Respondent alongwith interest. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-32.25pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">viii)&nbsp;&nbsp; That it is pertinent to mention herein that\r\nin spite of the fact that the Applicants had sought refund of the principal\r\namount paid by the Applicants alongwith interest, the Respondents have\r\narbitrarily continued to issue Demand Notices to the Applicants for payment of\r\ninstalments as per the payment schedule appended with the Buyer’s agreement.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:1.0in;text-align:justify;text-indent:\r\n-.5in;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n200%;font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">i)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Refund of an amount of Rs. 72,96,406/-\r\npaid by the Applicants alongwith interest (highest marginal cost of lending\r\nrate of the State Bank of India + 2%) from the respective dates of deposit till\r\nactual realization as per Sections 18 and 19(4) of the Act read with Rule 16 of\r\nthe Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:1.0in;text-align:justify;text-indent:\r\n-.5in;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n200%;font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">ii)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Any other relief which the Applicant is\r\nentitled for under the Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Act, 2016 and\r\nthe Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>',8340000.00,7296406.00,'2010-07-24 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>..</p>','1','','2008-11-04 00:00:00','2008-12-12 00:00:00','UNIT NO. TVM-L2-F11-1101, TOWER NO. L, \'The Views\' at Mohali Hills','','',2,0,0,0,'Harinderdhillon','2019-02-20 19:50:37.000','Harinderdhillon','2019-02-20 19:50:37.000'),(1090,1331,'1331',1160,'09581713-6148-49dc-9291-17a00d6bad73','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Sweety Sharma ','adv.karanjindal@gmail.com',9876111762,0,0,'house no 118','sector-70',28,507,'160071','1','house no 118','sector-70',28,507,'160071','J P Singla and Karan Jindal  ','jpsingladdld@gmail.com',9815482240,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0147','wave estate sector-85, SAS nagar Mohali','Country colonisers pvt ltd ','rera@waveestate.in',7290015352,0,'country colonisers pvt ltd','Sector 85, SAS Nagar Mohali',28,507,'160071','1','country colonisers pvt ltd','Sector 85, SAS Nagar Mohali',28,507,'140071','0','<p style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0cm\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">1.That the\r\ncomplainant has booked a unit no 190/ff in block A, Wave estate , sector 85 SAS\r\nnagar Mohali for a total sum of Rs. 63,50,000 (Sixty Three Lakhs Fifty thousand\r\nonly)<o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin: 0cm 0cm 7.5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">2.That the\r\ncomplainant&nbsp; paid an amount of Rs.500000 (five lakh only) as booking\r\namount vide cheque no 182051 dated 5.7.2014 of oriental bank of commerce,\r\nsector 33 chandigarh.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin: 0cm 0cm 7.5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">3. That the complainant further paid Rs.481932 (Four lakh eighty one thousand nine\r\nhundered thirty two only) vide cheque no 182053 of Oriental Bank of commerce\r\nsector 33 chandigarh.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin: 0cm 0cm 7.5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">4.\r\nThat, an agreement to that effect was executed on 1.12.2014. as per clause 5.1\r\nof the agreement the possession of the unit/flat was to be delivered on or\r\nbefore 1.12.2016 with an extended period of six months i.e on or before\r\n30.5.2017<o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin: 0cm 0cm 7.5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">5.\r\nThat the complainant has further arranged a loan of Rs.48,50,000 (Fourty eight\r\nlakhs fifty thousand only) from HDFC and the said financial institution has\r\ndisbursed Rs.45,32,500 (Fourty five lakhs thirty two thousand five hundered\r\nonly) to the developer i.e Country Colonisers pvt ltd. In this way the\r\ncomplainant has paid a total sum of Rs.55,14,432 (Fifty five lakhs fourteen\r\nthousand four hundered thirty two only) against a total price of Rs.63,50,000\r\n(sixty three lakhs fifty thousand only).&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin: 0cm 0cm 7.5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">6.\r\nThat the complainant was shocked to see that the developer has not completed\r\nthe project as per agreement and the work was going on at a slow pace. So, the\r\ncomplainant has stopped the balance payment against the total sum of\r\nRs.63,50,000 (Sixty Three Lakhs Fifty thousand only).&nbsp;&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"margin: 0cm 0cm 7.5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">7.That\r\nthe complainant has a dream to live in her own house but her dream to live in\r\nher own house was shattered because of the non fullfillment of the commitment of\r\nthe developer to deliver possession on or before 1.12.2016.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0cm\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">1. The\r\ncomplainant has lost the faith in the developer and is no more interested to\r\nretain herself with the project and hence wants to take her money back along\r\nwith the interest and Rs.2,00,000 (Two lakhs only) for mental agony which she\r\nhas suffered from the developer and Rs.1,00,000 One Lakh only as litigation\r\ncost which the complainant has to suffer on account of the developer.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0cm\"><br></p>',6350000.00,5514432.00,'2016-12-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0cm\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">The developer\r\nshould be ordered not to issue any further notice for the recovery of any\r\namount as the same irritates her which effects the health of the complainant.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Flat no 190 F.f Block A wave estate Sector 85, SAS nagar Mohali','','',2,0,0,0,'adv.karanjindal','2019-02-20 20:44:53.000','adv.karanjindal','2019-02-20 20:44:53.000'),(1091,1331,'1331',1160,'09581713-6148-49dc-9291-17a00d6bad73','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Sweety Sharma ','adv.karanjindal@gmail.com',9876111762,0,0,'house no 118','sector-70',28,507,'160071','1','house no 118','sector-70',28,507,'160071','J P Singla and Karan Jindal  ','jpsingladdld@gmail.com',9815482240,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0147','wave estate sector-85, SAS nagar Mohali','Country colonisers pvt ltd ','rera@waveestate.in',7290015352,0,'country colonisers pvt ltd','Sector 85, SAS Nagar Mohali',28,507,'160071','1','country colonisers pvt ltd','Sector 85, SAS Nagar Mohali',28,507,'140071','0','<p style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0cm\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">1.That the\r\ncomplainant has booked a unit no 190/ff in block A, Wave estate , sector 85 SAS\r\nnagar Mohali for a total sum of Rs. 63,50,000 (Sixty Three Lakhs Fifty thousand\r\nonly)<o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin: 0cm 0cm 7.5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">2.That the\r\ncomplainant&nbsp; paid an amount of Rs.500000 (five lakh only) as booking\r\namount vide cheque no 182051 dated 5.7.2014 of oriental bank of commerce,\r\nsector 33 chandigarh.<o: