khs. After taking all the factors into\r\nconsideration the interest amount for 48 months comes down to Rs. 6.78 Lakhs. The\r\nagreement also suggests that possession can only be taken after <span style=\"margin: 0px;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;</span>clearance of account. Balance amount now payable\r\nis Rs. -5.51 Lakhs (1.27 lakhs - 6.78 lakhs). </span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"background: white; margin: 0px 0px 0px 75.6px; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\'margin: 0px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: \"Verdana\",\"sans-serif\";\'>&nbsp;</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"background: white; margin: 0px 0px 0px 75.6px; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\'margin: 0px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: \"Verdana\",\"sans-serif\";\'>In view of the facts mentioned in\r\npara 4,I, Suman Dhaundiyal, prays for the compensation of Rs.<b style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight:normal\">6.78 Lakhs and reversal of legal notice\r\nnumber 3 (cancellation of said property)</b></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"background: white; margin: 0px 0px 0px 75.6px; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\'margin: 0px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: \"Verdana\",\"sans-serif\";\'>&nbsp;</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"background: white; margin: 0px 0px 0px 75.6px; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\'margin: 0px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: \"Verdana\",\"sans-serif\";\'>&nbsp;</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n<b></b><i></i><u></u><sub></sub><sup></sup><strike></strike><font face=\"Times New Roman\"></font><br></p>',2550000.00,2422000.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>CANCELLATION OF LEGAL NOTICE NUMBER -03 WHICH WAS ISSUED BY THE ADVOCATE OF THE BUILDER FOR CANCELLATION OF THE ABOVE MENTIONED PROPERTY</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','FLAT NUMBER -950,FLOOR-09 TOWER-04 IN SBP HOUSING PARK AT VILLAGE RAUNI,TEHSIL DERABASSI, DISTT. MOHALI PUNJAB','','',1,0,0,0,'sumandhaundiyal','2019-02-25 10:52:40.000','sumandhaundiyal','2019-02-25 10:52:40.000'),(1104,1197,'1197',1287,'fcebf583-f701-4375-a441-163b29a0faf5','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-26 09:09:34.000','Brinder  Singh','kashika.juneja91@gmail.com',9814013127,0,0,'Hamilton Brook, London road, Sunningdale,','Ascot, Berkshire, SL5 9RY, England',36,2023,'000000','1','House No. 607','sector 18B',6,128,'160018','Gaurav Chopra','gaurav.chopra@hotmail.com',9814013125,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0119','Mohali Hills','Emaar MGF Land Ltd','sorabh.kakar@emaarmgf.com',0,0,'Emaar MGF Land Ltd','40, Central Plaza, Ground Floor, Sector 105 Mohali',28,507,'140306','1','Emaar MGF Land Ltd','40, Central Plaza, Ground Floor, Sector 105 Mohali',28,507,'140306','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-indent: -43px; margin-left: 0.5in; line-height: 200%;\"><font face=\"Garamond, serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">i)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That the Applicants had sought allotment of a Residential Apartment in “The Views”, Mohali Hills and were Allotted Unit No. TVM K1-FPH-PH02, Tower K1, ‘The Views’, Mohali Hills, Sector 105, Mohali for which a Buyer’s Agreement 13.6.11 was executed between the Applicants and Respondent.&nbsp;</span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-indent: -43px; margin-left: 0.5in; line-height: 200%;\"><font face=\"Garamond, serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">ii)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That out of the total sale consideration of Rs. 1,04,28,413/-, the amount previously paid by the Applicants in respect of a Built Up Villa No. 10, Sector 106, Mohali, the allotment whereof was cancelled vide a letter dated 25.3.11 issued by the Respondent on mutually accepted terms, was adjusted and over and above the said amount, a further sum of Rs. 15,31,688.13/- was paid by the Applicants upto 27.8.2012 and thus, an amount of Rs. 1,07,66,807/- was paid in respect of the Allotted Unit.</span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-indent: -43px; margin-left: 0.5in; line-height: 200%;\"><font face=\"Garamond, serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">iii)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That the Respondent wilfully defaulted in offering possession of the Allotted Unit by the second quarter of 2012, as assured by the Respondent at the time of migrating the applicants from the Built Up Villa to the Allotted Unit, or within stipulated time period as per Clause 21.1 of the Buyer’s Agreement i.e. 13.12.2014. Consequently, vide an email&nbsp; 20.10.17, the Buyer’s Agreement dated 13.6.11 was rescinded by the Applicants while inter alia calling upon the Respondent to forthwith refund the entire amount paid by them alongwith interest.</span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-indent: -43px; margin-left: 0.5in; line-height: 200%;\"><font face=\"Garamond, serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">iv)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That despite receipt of the aforesaid email 20.10.17, the Respondent offered possession of the Allotted Unit vide its letter dated 28.10.17. The offer of possession given by the Respondent is nothing else but a sham. At the site of the Allotted Unit, the development works were nowhere near completion and the Allotted Unit is also not in any condition whatsoever to be taken&nbsp;</span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-indent: -43px; margin-left: 0.5in; line-height: 200%;\"><font face=\"Garamond, serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">vi)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That failure on the part of the Respondent in handing over possession of the Allotted Unit within the stipulated time period as per Clause 21.1 of the Buyer’s Agreement constitutes a wilful and material breach of the contract executed between the parties.</span></font></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:1.0in;text-align:justify;text-indent:\r\n-.5in;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n200%;font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">i)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Refund of an amount of Rs.\r\n1,04,28,413/-paid by the Applicants alongwith interest (highest marginal cost\r\nof lending rate of the State Bank of India + 2%) from the respective dates of\r\ndeposit till actual realization as per Sections 18 and 19(4) of the Act read\r\nwith Rule 16 of the Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development)\r\nRules, 2017.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:1.0in;text-align:justify;text-indent:\r\n-.5in;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n200%;font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">ii)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Any other relief which the Applicant is\r\nentitled for under the Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Act, 2016 and\r\nthe Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>',10428413.00,10766807.00,'2014-12-13 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>..</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','2011-06-13 00:00:00','Allotted Unit No. TVM K1-FPH-PH02, Tower K1, ‘The Views’, Mohali Hills','','',2,0,0,0,'brindersingh1','2019-02-25 12:43:23.000','brindersingh1','2019-02-25 12:43:23.000'),(1105,1197,'1197',1287,'fcebf583-f701-4375-a441-163b29a0faf5','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-02-25 12:44:04.000','Brinder  Singh','kashika.juneja91@gmail.com',9814013127,0,0,'Hamilton Brook, London road, Sunningdale,','Ascot, Berkshire, SL5 9RY, England',36,2023,'000000','1','House No. 607','sector 18B',6,128,'160018','Gaurav Chopra','gaurav.chopra@hotmail.com',9814013127,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0119','Mohali Hills','Emaar MGF Land Ltd','sorabh.kakar@emaarmgf.com',0,0,'Emaar MGF Land Ltd','40, Central Plaza, Ground Floor, Sector 105 Mohali',28,507,'140306','1','Emaar MGF Land Ltd','40, Central Plaza, Ground Floor, Sector 105 Mohali',28,507,'140306','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-indent: -43px; margin-left: 0.5in; line-height: 200%;\"><font face=\"Garamond, serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">i)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That the Applicants had sought allotment of a Residential Apartment in “The Views”, Mohali Hills and were Allotted Unit No. TVM K1-FPH-PH02, Tower K1, ‘The Views’, Mohali Hills, Sector 105, Mohali for which a Buyer’s Agreement 13.6.11 was executed between the Applicants and Respondent.&nbsp;</span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-indent: -43px; margin-left: 0.5in; line-height: 200%;\"><font face=\"Garamond, serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">ii)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That out of the total sale consideration of Rs. 1,04,28,413/-, the amount previously paid by the Applicants in respect of a Built Up Villa No. 10, Sector 106, Mohali, the allotment whereof was cancelled vide a letter dated 25.3.11 issued by the Respondent on mutually accepted terms, was adjusted and over and above the said amount, a further sum of Rs. 15,31,688.13/- was paid by the Applicants upto 27.8.2012 and thus, an amount of Rs. 1,07,66,807/- was paid in respect of the Allotted Unit.</span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-indent: -43px; margin-left: 0.5in; line-height: 200%;\"><font face=\"Garamond, serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">iii)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That the Respondent wilfully defaulted in offering possession of the Allotted Unit by the second quarter of 2012, as assured by the Respondent at the time of migrating the applicants from the Built Up Villa to the Allotted Unit, or within stipulated time period as per Clause 21.1 of the Buyer’s Agreement i.e. 13.12.2014. Consequently, vide an email&nbsp; 20.10.17, the Buyer’s Agreement dated 13.6.11 was rescinded by the Applicants while inter alia calling upon the Respondent to forthwith refund the entire amount paid by them alongwith interest.</span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-indent: -43px; margin-left: 0.5in; line-height: 200%;\"><font face=\"Garamond, serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">iv)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That despite receipt of the aforesaid email 20.10.17, the Respondent offered possession of the Allotted Unit vide its letter dated 28.10.17. The offer of possession given by the Respondent is nothing else but a sham. At the site of the Allotted Unit, the development works were nowhere near completion and the Allotted Unit is also not in any condition whatsoever to be taken&nbsp;</span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-indent: -43px; margin-left: 0.5in; line-height: 200%;\"><font face=\"Garamond, serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">vi)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That failure on the part of the Respondent in handing over possession of the Allotted Unit within the stipulated time period as per Clause 21.1 of the Buyer’s Agreement constitutes a wilful and material breach of the contract executed between the parties.</span></font></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:1.0in;text-align:justify;text-indent:\r\n-.5in;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n200%;font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">i)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Refund of an amount of Rs.\r\n1,04,28,413/-paid by the Applicants alongwith interest (highest marginal cost\r\nof lending rate of the State Bank of India + 2%) from the respective dates of\r\ndeposit till actual realization as per Sections 18 and 19(4) of the Act read\r\nwith Rule 16 of the Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development)\r\nRules, 2017.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:1.0in;text-align:justify;text-indent:\r\n-.5in;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n200%;font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">ii)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Any other relief which the Applicant is\r\nentitled for under the Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Act, 2016 and\r\nthe Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>',10428413.00,10766807.00,'2014-12-13 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>..</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','2011-06-13 00:00:00','Allotted Unit No. TVM K1-FPH-PH02, Tower K1, ‘The Views’, Mohali Hills','','',1,1,0,0,'brindersingh1','2019-02-25 12:43:56.000','brindersingh1','2019-02-25 12:43:56.000'),(1106,1198,'1198',1283,'a69593cc-e858-492f-ab4c-c34fdd75b5d8','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2018-12-19 18:20:06.000','Harinder Dhillon','gaurav.chopra@hotmail.com',9814013127,0,0,'House No. 360','Phase IV ',28,507,'160059','1','House No. 607','Sector 18B Chandigarh',6,128,'160018','Gaurav Chopra','gaurav.chopra@hotmail.com',9814013127,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0119','MOHALI HILLS','Emaar MGF Land Ltd','sorabh.kakar@emaarmgf.com',0,0,'Emaar MGF Land Ltd','40, Central Plaza, Ground Floor, Sector 105 Mohali',28,507,'140306','1','Emaar MGF Land Ltd','40, Central Plaza, Ground Floor, Sector 105 Mohali',28,507,'140306','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">i)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Allotment letter: 24.4.2007 <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">ii)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Apartment Buyer’s Agreement: 12.12.08 <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">iii)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Unit No. L3-F12-1203 in ‘The Views’ at\r\nMohali Hills<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">iv)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Amendment Agreement dated 27.8.2015 was\r\nexecuted between the Applicants and the Respondent whereby, while retaining all\r\nother clauses and provisions of the Buyer’s Agreement dated 12.12.2008, Unit\r\nNo. TVM-L2-F11-1101 having a super area of 2600 sq. Ft was allotted to the\r\nApplicants at the rate of Rs. 2950/- per sq. foot and consequently, the total\r\nsale consideration payable in respect of the Allotted Unit was revised from Rs.\r\n62,72,558/- to Rs. 83,40,000/-.&nbsp; <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-32.25pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">v)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Construction Linked Instalment Plan<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-32.25pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">vi)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Amount paid upto 7.2.2014: Rs. 72,96,406/- <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-32.25pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">vi)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; As per Clause 21.1 of the Apartment Buyer’s\r\nAgreement, the Respondent was under a contractual obligation to handover\r\npossession of the Allotted Unit within a period of 36 months from the date of\r\nallotment with a further relaxation of 90 days over.&nbsp; Hence, possession of the Allotted Unit was\r\nrequired to be handed over to the Applicants by the Respondent positively on or\r\nbefore 24.7.2010 <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-32.25pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">vii)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Aggrieved by the aforesaid omission and\r\nlapse of the Respondent, the Applicants had written a letter/e-mail to the\r\nRespondent for rescinding the contract and for seeking refund of the principal\r\namount paid by the Applicants in respect of the Allotted Unit alongwith\r\ninterest.&nbsp; Till date, however, the\r\naforesaid demand raised by the Applicants has not been acceded to by the\r\nRespondent and thus, vide the instant complaint, the Applicants seek refund of\r\nthe monies paid by them to the Respondent alongwith interest. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-32.25pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">viii)&nbsp;&nbsp; That it is pertinent to mention herein that\r\nin spite of the fact that the Applicants had sought refund of the principal\r\namount paid by the Applicants alongwith interest, the Respondents have\r\narbitrarily continued to issue Demand Notices to the Applicants for payment of\r\ninstalments as per the payment schedule appended with the Buyer’s agreement.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:1.0in;text-align:justify;text-indent:\r\n-.5in;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n200%;font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">i)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Refund of an amount of Rs. 72,96,406/-\r\npaid by the Applicants alongwith interest (highest marginal cost of lending\r\nrate of the State Bank of India + 2%) from the respective dates of deposit till\r\nactual realization as per Sections 18 and 19(4) of the Act read with Rule 16 of\r\nthe Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:1.0in;text-align:justify;text-indent:\r\n-.5in;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n200%;font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">ii)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Any other relief which the Applicant is\r\nentitled for under the Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Act, 2016 and\r\nthe Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>',8340000.00,7296406.00,'2010-07-24 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>..</p>','1','','2008-11-04 00:00:00','2008-12-12 00:00:00','UNIT NO. TVM-L2-F11-1101, TOWER NO. L, \'The Views\' at Mohali Hills','','',2,0,0,0,'Harinderdhillon','2019-02-25 12:45:41.000','Harinderdhillon','2019-02-25 12:45:41.000'),(1107,1198,'1198',1283,'a69593cc-e858-492f-ab4c-c34fdd75b5d8','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-02-25 12:46:13.000','Harinder Dhillon','gaurav.chopra@hotmail.com',9814013127,0,0,'House No. 360','Phase IV ',28,507,'160059','1','House No. 607','Sector 18B Chandigarh',6,128,'160018','Gaurav Chopra','gaurav.chopra@hotmail.com',9814013127,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0119','MOHALI HILLS','Emaar MGF Land Ltd','sorabh.kakar@emaarmgf.com',0,0,'Emaar MGF Land Ltd','40, Central Plaza, Ground Floor, Sector 105 Mohali',28,507,'140306','1','Emaar MGF Land Ltd','40, Central Plaza, Ground Floor, Sector 105 Mohali',28,507,'140306','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">i)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Allotment letter: 24.4.2007 <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">ii)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Apartment Buyer’s Agreement: 12.12.08 <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">iii)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Unit No. L3-F12-1203 in ‘The Views’ at\r\nMohali Hills<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">iv)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Amendment Agreement dated 27.8.2015 was\r\nexecuted between the Applicants and the Respondent whereby, while retaining all\r\nother clauses and provisions of the Buyer’s Agreement dated 12.12.2008, Unit\r\nNo. TVM-L2-F11-1101 having a super area of 2600 sq. Ft was allotted to the\r\nApplicants at the rate of Rs. 2950/- per sq. foot and consequently, the total\r\nsale consideration payable in respect of the Allotted Unit was revised from Rs.\r\n62,72,558/- to Rs. 83,40,000/-.&nbsp; <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-32.25pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">v)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Construction Linked Instalment Plan<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-32.25pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">vi)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Amount paid upto 7.2.2014: Rs. 72,96,406/- <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-32.25pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">vi)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; As per Clause 21.1 of the Apartment Buyer’s\r\nAgreement, the Respondent was under a contractual obligation to handover\r\npossession of the Allotted Unit within a period of 36 months from the date of\r\nallotment with a further relaxation of 90 days over.&nbsp; Hence, possession of the Allotted Unit was\r\nrequired to be handed over to the Applicants by the Respondent positively on or\r\nbefore 24.7.2010 <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-32.25pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">vii)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Aggrieved by the aforesaid omission and\r\nlapse of the Respondent, the Applicants had written a letter/e-mail to the\r\nRespondent for rescinding the contract and for seeking refund of the principal\r\namount paid by the Applicants in respect of the Allotted Unit alongwith\r\ninterest.&nbsp; Till date, however, the\r\naforesaid demand raised by the Applicants has not been acceded to by the\r\nRespondent and thus, vide the instant complaint, the Applicants seek refund of\r\nthe monies paid by them to the Respondent alongwith interest. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-32.25pt;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">viii)&nbsp;&nbsp; That it is pertinent to mention herein that\r\nin spite of the fact that the Applicants had sought refund of the principal\r\namount paid by the Applicants alongwith interest, the Respondents have\r\narbitrarily continued to issue Demand Notices to the Applicants for payment of\r\ninstalments as per the payment schedule appended with the Buyer’s agreement.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:1.0in;text-align:justify;text-indent:\r\n-.5in;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n200%;font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">i)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Refund of an amount of Rs. 72,96,406/-\r\npaid by the Applicants alongwith interest (highest marginal cost of lending\r\nrate of the State Bank of India + 2%) from the respective dates of deposit till\r\nactual realization as per Sections 18 and 19(4) of the Act read with Rule 16 of\r\nthe Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:1.0in;text-align:justify;text-indent:\r\n-.5in;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n200%;font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">ii)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Any other relief which the Applicant is\r\nentitled for under the Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Act, 2016 and\r\nthe Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>',8340000.00,7296406.00,'2010-07-24 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>..</p>','1','','2008-11-04 00:00:00','2008-12-12 00:00:00','UNIT NO. TVM-L2-F11-1101, TOWER NO. L, \'The Views\' at Mohali Hills','','',1,1,0,0,'Harinderdhillon','2019-02-25 12:46:10.000','Harinderdhillon','2019-02-25 12:46:10.000'),(1108,1336,'1336',1361,'a52599d4-e47a-4877-8e30-d95c9ef9cf7f','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','SUMAN DHAUNDIYAL','kailashicwai@gmail.com',9818401409,0,0,'D-102,ARYA SAMAJ ROAD','UTTAM NAGAR',10,628,'110059','1','D-102,ARYA SAMAJ ROAD','UTTAM NAGAR',10,628,'110059','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0096','SBP HOUSING PARK','AMAN SINGLA','info@sbpgroup.in',9316004240,0,'SCO146-148','1st Floor sector-43B',6,128,'160043','1','SCO146-148','1st Floor sector-43B',6,128,'160043','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.75in; text-align: justify; line-height: 12.65pt; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial;\r\ncolor:#222222;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\">On 20<sup>th</sup>&nbsp;January 2013\r\nthe undersigned underwent an agreement (Copy enclosed) with the said builder &nbsp;for purchase of apartment for &nbsp;approximately 1130 sq feet in the complex\r\ncalled SBP Housing Park for a total value of Rs.25,50,000/-. All the payment\r\nhas been made (down payment + home loan) except for Rs.1, 27,499/- , which is\r\nthe last instalment due <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.75in; text-align: justify; line-height: 12.65pt; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial;\r\ncolor:#222222;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt 56.7pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial;\r\ncolor:#222222;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\">In Dec18 and Jan19, 3 numbers of\r\nlegal notices were received from their advocate. The first 2 notices (copy\r\nenclosed) demanded the payment of the last instalment. Despite our response to\r\nfirst 2 notices (copy enclosed) and earlier communication, another legal notice\r\nhas been received from their advocate which says our allotment has been\r\ncancelled and that we should now proceed for refund of amount paid by us&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt 56.7pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial;\r\ncolor:#222222;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\">As per article 4(possession) <b>(copy enclosed)</b> of the agreement, the\r\nflat should have been handed over on or before 31<sup>st</sup>&nbsp;December\r\n2014.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt 56.7pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial;\r\ncolor:#222222;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\">As a compensation for non-compliance\r\nof the same, simple interest at the rate equivalent to rate of fixed deposit\r\noffered by SBI would be charged for the gap period (for the amount paid).&nbsp;\r\n<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt 56.7pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial;\r\ncolor:#222222;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt 56.7pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial;\r\ncolor:#222222;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\">Assuming the work is now over &amp;\r\nthe flat is ready for possession in Jan 19, there is &nbsp;&nbsp;a gap of approximately 48 months (Dec 2014 to\r\nJan 19) and current rate of interest offered by SBI is approximately 7.00%.\r\nTotal amount paid till date is 24.22 Lakhs. After taking all the factors into\r\nconsideration the interest amount for 48 months comes down to Rs. 6.78 Lakhs. The\r\nagreement also suggests that possession can only be taken after &nbsp;&nbsp;clearance of account. Balance amount now payable\r\nis Rs. -5.51 Lakhs (1.27 lakhs - 6.78 lakhs). <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt 56.7pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial;\r\ncolor:#222222;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt 56.7pt; text-align: justify; line-height: normal; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial;\r\ncolor:#222222;mso-fareast-language:EN-IN\">In view of the facts mentioned in\r\npara 4,I, Suman Dhaundiyal, prays for the compensation of Rs.<b>6.78 Lakhs and reversal of legal notice\r\nnumber 3 (cancellation of said property)<o:p></o:p></b></span></p>',2550000.00,2422000.00,'2014-12-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>CANCELLATION OF 3rd LEGAL NOTICE REGARDING CANCELLATION OF THE ALLOTMENT OF THE PROPERTY</p>','1','','2013-01-20 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','FLAT NUMBER-950, FLOOR NUMBER-09  TOWER-04 IN SBP HOUSING PARK AT VILLAGE RAUNI ,TEHSIL DERABASSI DISSTT, MOHALI PUNJAB','','',1,0,0,0,'sumandhaundiyal','2019-02-25 16:05:50.000','sumandhaundiyal','2019-02-25 16:05:50.000'),(1109,1264,'1264',1010,'a182232b-88d6-4711-8baa-f8a026fb675f','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-01-14 13:39:24.000','SUNDAR KRISHNAN','lawofficeofhimanshuraj@gmail.com',9988100005,1724181010,434498329217,'Tower 6, Flat 62, Godrej Garden Enclave, ','Opp. Godrej Memorial Hospital, Vikroli East, Mumbai',21,400,'400079','0','#102, Sector 10 A','',6,128,'160011','HIMANSHU RAJ','lawofficeofhimanshuraj@gmail.com',9988200001,1724190909,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0013','ATS GOLF MEADOWS-I','ATS ESTATES PRIVATE LIMITED','pradeep.rathee@atsgreens.com',8288033311,0,'711/92, DEEPALI','NEHRU PLACE, NEW DELHI',10,429,'110019','1','711/92, DEEPALI','NEHRU PLACE, NEW DELHI',10,429,'110019','1','<p>The complainant had booked a plot measuring 350 SQ. YARD at OPs project ATS GOLF MEADOWS I in the year 2005. That it is pertinent to mention here that OP did not possess any of the requisite clearances license from the competent authority to develop the said project at that time The complainant has paid the COMPLETE AMOUNT against the said unit to the Opposite Party in the year 2005.&nbsp;</p><p>That on 03.11.2009 the OP furnished an ALLOTMENT LETTER and allotted a plot to the complainant measuring 388.11 Sq. Yard, indentified by unique No. 120 in the said project. That it is pertinent to mention here that the OP had arbitrarily reduced the area of the plot which was booked. That the OP promised through verbal assurance and Verbal Agreement that the possession will be handed over to the complainant by 03.11.2011, i.e. 2 years from the date of allotment, but Op failed to do so. That the OP had raised a Demand for EDC from the complainant at exorbitant rate after the expiry of deemed date of possession 8 years after the date of booking. That OP had threatened to cancel the allotment and deduct the Earnest money if the demanded EDC is not paid. The complainant complied with the demands of OP and deposited the amount against EDC but till date the possession of the unit has not been handed over.&nbsp;</p><p>Therefore, the complainant craves the indulgence of the Honble RERA authority to hand to direct the OP to refund the entire amount as per the RERA CENTRAL ACT AND RERA STATE RULES.</p>','<p>1.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To direct the OP to compensate the complainant in the shape of refund the complete amount which has been deposited against the residential property so booked by the complainant along with an Interest on the amount from the date of deposit at the rate of 20 per cent&nbsp; till the actual realization of the complete amount within 90 days according to section 18 1 Real Estate Regulation And Development Act, 2016, 18 2 Real Estate Regulation And Development Act, 2016, Section 19 4 of The Real Estate Regulation And Development Act, 2016, r w Rule 16 and Rule 17 of Punjab State Real Estate Regulation and Development Rules, 2017</p><p><br></p><p>2.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To direct the OP to pay Rs. 20,00,000&nbsp; for causing mental agony caused to the complainant.</p><p><br></p><p>3.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To direct the OP to pay Rs. 14,00,000 to the complainant as the deficiency in services for keeping the complainant in dark in regard to the progress of the property.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>4.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span> To direct the OP to pay Rs. 14,00,000&nbsp; for causing physical harassment caused to the complainant.</p><p><br></p><p>5.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To direct the OP to pay 5 per cent of the total estimated cost of the project under section 61 of Real Estate Regulation and Development Act, 2016</p><p><br></p><p>6.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To revoke the license of the OP under section 7 of the Real Estate Regulation and Development act, 2016.</p><p><br></p><p>Any other relief or claim which the Honble Authority deems appropriate.</p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Not Prayed</p>','1','','2009-11-03 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'lawofficeofhimanshuraj','2019-02-26 13:05:25.000','lawofficeofhimanshuraj','2019-02-26 13:05:25.000'),(1110,1264,'1264',1010,'a182232b-88d6-4711-8baa-f8a026fb675f','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-01-14 13:39:24.000','SUNDAR KRISHNAN','lawofficeofhimanshuraj@gmail.com',9988100005,1724181010,434498329217,'Tower 6, Flat 62, Godrej Garden Enclave, ','Opp. Godrej Memorial Hospital, Vikroli East, Mumbai',21,400,'400079','0','#102, Sector 10 A','',6,128,'160011','HIMANSHU RAJ','lawofficeofhimanshuraj@gmail.com',9988200001,1724190909,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0013','ATS GOLF MEADOWS-I','ATS ESTATES PRIVATE LIMITED','pradeep.rathee@atsgreens.com',8288033311,0,'711/92, DEEPALI','NEHRU PLACE, NEW DELHI',10,429,'110019','1','711/92, DEEPALI','NEHRU PLACE, NEW DELHI',10,429,'110019','1','<p>The complainant had booked a plot measuring 350 SQ. YARD at OPs project ATS GOLF MEADOWS I in the year 2005. That it is pertinent to mention here that OP 