<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:.25pt;margin-bottom:0in;\r\nmargin-left:.5in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size:13.5pt;line-height:200%;font-family:\r\nGaramond;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial\">To refund the amount of Rs.<i>85,62,767</i>/- along with 18% interest from\r\nthe date of deposit till the date of actual &nbsp;realization of amount &nbsp;as per RERA Act.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:.25pt;margin-bottom:0in;\r\nmargin-left:.5in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size:13.5pt;line-height:200%;font-family:\r\nGaramond;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial\">B.&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Litigation expenses of Rs.75,000/<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-right:.25pt;text-align:justify;line-height:\r\n200%\"><span style=\"font-size:13.5pt;line-height:200%;font-family:Garamond;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:Arial\">Or any other order which this respected authority deems\r\nfit in the interest of justice.<o:p></o:p></span></p>',0.00,0.00,'2018-01-26 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-right:.25pt;text-align:justify;line-height:\r\n200%\"><span style=\"font-size:13.5pt;line-height:200%;font-family:Garamond;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:Arial\">1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; That\r\nis request to the respected authority to direct the respondent -1 to pay\r\nPre-Emi interest to the respondent-2 which has failed to pay by respondent 1 as\r\nper clause 3 of tripartite agreement from date of failure to pay &nbsp;Emi till 26 Jan 2018.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','2015-01-27 00:00:00','Wave Gardens, Apartment No. 1101, F Freesia, 11th Floor, Type 3 BHK, Sector 85 & 89 District S.A.S Nagar, Punjab, Pin -140308','','',1,0,0,0,'advkulwindersingh','2019-03-01 12:48:07.000','advkulwindersingh','2019-03-01 12:48:07.000'),(1132,1239,'1239',1310,'a760b242-a57c-46e6-a533-2178f2bd8ffe','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-03-19 20:18:42.000','Rakesh Narang','advbswalia@gmail.com',9417374450,1722625384,0,'H.NO. 4/137, SHIVAJI NAGAR','',13,5,'122001','1','H.NO. 4/137, SHIVAJI NAGAR','',13,5,'122001','B. S WALIA','advbswalia@gmail.com',9417374450,1722625384,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0153','WAVES ESTATE ','Wave Estate M/s Country Colonisers Private limited','aditi@waveestate.in',0,0,'Sector 85','',28,507,'160055','1','Sector 85','',28,507,'160055','1','<p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">That the respondent issued\r\nallotment Letter of intent (LOI) to applicant for residential plot no. 63 First floor Sector 99, Mohali dated 14.1.2013 in reference to application form no. 832. That in furtherance\r\nof letter of Intent, allotment letter&nbsp;dated 9-8-2016 was issued to\r\napplicant. The tentative price of the plot is Rs. 11445000/- at the rate of Rs.\r\n21,000/- Rs/Sq. Yard. In pursuance to Allotment Letter, Applicant paid full and\r\nfinal lump sum payment of Rs.1,14,45,000/-.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:\r\njustify;line-height:200%\">\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">Thus, till date Rs.\r\n11445000/- has been paid by Applicant to the respondent as per statement of\r\naccount. As per the Allotment Letter , the possession of the said\r\nplot in question was to be given within 30 months from the date of issuance of\r\nallotment which is already over. Thus, the respondent has failed\r\nto handover possession within the stipulated time as written in the allotment\r\nletter agreed between the parties. The respondent has yet to give reply to\r\nApplicant whether they have got the Occupancy Certificate/Completion\r\nCertificate for the said plot or not? Respondent has been avoiding this\r\nquestion for too long since the Allotment letter was issued. That the said\r\nproject promoted by respondent lacks basic infrastructure like roads, poor\r\nconnectivity, drains, electricity, water supply, green cover and parks, street\r\nlights missing, roads without berm, no provision of security nor any existence\r\nof police post. All these factors further make plot unfit for habitation and\r\nconstruction.&nbsp;Applicant has given a letter on 30-11-2017 regarding\r\npossession of P</span><span style=\"font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">lot no. 63 First floor Sector 99, Mohali</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">. Even today</span><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">,&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;\">the development works at the said\r\n‘Gateway City’ are not complete, which means the possession of plot is no\r\nsooner expected than 2019 from respondent. Thus, there is a clear delay on the\r\npart of respondent.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:7.5pt;text-align:justify;line-height:\r\n21.0pt\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif;\">In view of the facts mentioned in paragraph 4 above, the\r\napplicant&nbsp;prays for the following compensation(s): -</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: Roboto;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:7.5pt;text-align:justify;line-height:\r\n21.0pt\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif;\">1.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; letter-spacing: 1pt;\">Grant\r\npay 18% interest on the deposited amount of Rs.</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: Roboto;\">&nbsp;11445000</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; letter-spacing: 1pt;\">/-&nbsp;from date of possession.</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: Roboto;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:7.5pt;text-align:justify;line-height:\r\n21.0pt\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:7.5pt;text-align:justify;line-height:\r\n21.0pt\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif;\">2. Any other appropriate remedy or relief which this court may\r\ndeem fit in the present circumstances may also be awarded in the favour of\r\nApplicant.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: Roboto;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>',11445000.00,11445000.00,'2015-07-14 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 7.5pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 21pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif;\">In view of the facts mentioned in paragraph 4 above, the applicant&nbsp;prays for the following compensation(s): -</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: Roboto;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 7.5pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 21pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif;\">1.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; letter-spacing: 1pt;\">Grant pay 18% interest on the deposited amount of Rs.</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: Roboto;\">&nbsp;11445000</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; letter-spacing: 1pt;\">/-&nbsp;from date of possession.</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: Roboto;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 7.5pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 21pt;\"></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 7.5pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 21pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: &quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;, serif;\">2. Any other appropriate remedy or relief which this court may deem fit in the present circumstances may also be awarded in the favour of Applicant.&nbsp;</span></p>','1','','2013-01-14 00:00:00','2013-06-06 00:00:00','63 FIRST FLOOR','','',1,1,0,0,'bhupinderwalia','2019-03-01 14:32:14.000','bhupinderwalia','2019-03-01 14:32:14.000'),(1133,1345,'1345',1422,'734523d9-57e4-48b1-9b68-dd6258678e15','FormTypeM',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Aman Kumar Sharma','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9729902009,0,0,'D-73, Spangle Condos','Gazipur, Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','1','D-73, Spangle Condos','Gazipur, Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','Kamaljeet Dahiya','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9729902009,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0084','SUSHMA CRESCENT','SUSHMA BUILDTECH LIMITED','customercare@sushmabuildtech.com',0,0,'Unit No. B-107, Business Complex Elante Mall, 1st Floor, Industrial Area, Phase-I, Chandigarh','',6,128,'160002','1','Unit No. B-107, Business Complex Elante Mall, 1st Floor, Industrial Area, Phase-I, Chandigarh','',6,128,'160002','1','<p>Complainants had filed the complaint bearing no.ADCNo10162018 titled Aman Kumar&amp;Anr. v. Sushma Buildtech Ltd. on 31.08.18 before the Hon’ble Adjudicating Officer,RERA Punjab which was returned to the Complainants vide order dated 06.12.18 &amp; granted them liberty to file a fresh complaint before this Hon’ble Authority. But in the meantime after the pronouncement of order, the respondent cancelled the allotted unit on 31.01.19(C-1) &amp; again sent an Intimation Letter for the same on 16.02.19(C-2) which is illegal i.e. null &amp; void as this act of respondent is against the settled principle of law and natural justice. Complainants had been allotted with Duplex Apartment no.A-1103, area 2380 sq. ft, 11th Floor in TowerA. ABA executed 18.02.13AnnexureC-3.Total consideration Rs66,60,000 excluding other statutory charges.Complainants paid total Rs68,88,605(95%) (C-4). Due date of possession-18.02.16 &amp; with 6 months grace period-18.07.16(clause14(d)ABA).Respondent offered possession vide email12.04.18(C-5). Complainants replied vide email 19.04.18 &amp; raised queries that whether Occupany Certificate or Completion Certificate has been procured by the respondent before making offer of possession or not(C-6) but no reply. It means that they offered the possession without having the approvals &amp; Occupation or Completion Certificate.Complainants sent various reminder emails but all in vain(C-7). Certain deficiencies or snags reported by the Complainants after the site visit &amp; they prepared a snag list(C-8).But it was not removed till date.Complainants requested the respondent vide various emails to remove such snags but all in vain(C-9,Pg27).Respondent assured the Complainants vide email 16.06.2018(Pg28).Complainants expresses their displeasure vide email(Pg29-30) and raised their objections vide email(Pg31).Respondent again invited the Complainants to visit the project site vide email(Pg32).Complainants again expressed their displeasure and requested for refund vide emails(Pg33-34)<br></p>','<p>i.To give necessary directions to the respondents for refund the amount paid by the Complainants with prescribed interest till realization as per the provisions of Sec. 18 and Sec.19(4)of the RERA Act read with Rule 16 of PSRE(R&amp;D)Rules,2017.</p><p>ii.To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 60 of RERA Act for willful default committed by them.</p><p>iii.To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 61 of RERA Act for contravention of Sec.12, Sec.14, and Sec. 16 of RERA Act.</p><p>iv.To issue directions to make liable every officer concerned i.e. Director, Manager, Secretary, or any other officer of the respondent’s company at whose instance, connivance, acquiescence, neglect any of the offences has been committed as mentioned in Sec.69 of RERA Act,2016 to be read with Punjab RERA Rules, 2017.</p><p>v.To recommend criminal action against the respondents for the criminal offence of cheating, fraud and criminal breach of trust under section 420,406 and 409 of the Indian Penal Code.</p><p>vi.To issue direction to pay the cost of litigation.</p><p>vii.Any other relief which this Hon’ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances of this complaint.</p><div><br></div>',6660000.00,6888605.00,'2016-02-18 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>i.To direct the respondent not to demand any further amount whatsoever from the Complainants.</p><p>ii.The respondent should be restrained from harassing the Complainants in any manner whatsoever.</p><p>iii.Any other interim relief which this Hon’ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances of this complaint.</p><div><br></div>','1','','2012-08-08 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','A-1103, Sushma Crescent, Zirakpur, Punjab','','',2,0,0,0,'AmanKumar','2019-03-01 18:00:56.000','AmanKumar','2019-03-01 18:00:56.000'),(1134,1340,'1340',1245,'3f889bdc-3ee0-4229-87d4-71be8592f729','FormTypeM',1,1,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Prashant Gajanan Pathak','advamitgoyal@hotmail.com',9527700001,0,0,'Flat no. 603, Lotus Tower, Bollywood Heights,','Near sector-20 Panchkula Peer Machalla, Dhakoli, ',28,507,'140603','1','Flat no. 603, Lotus Tower, Bollywood Heights,','Near sector-20 Panchkula Peer Machalla, Dhakoli, ',28,507,'140603','Amit Goyal','advamitgoyal@hotmail.com',9527700001,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0086','ATS CASA ESPANA','ATS INFRABUILD PVT. LTD','email@atsgreens.com',0,1203811500,'ATS CASA ESPANA ','Village Bad Majra, Sector 121 SAS Nagar',28,507,'140307','1','ATS CASA ESPANA ','Village Bad Majra, Sector 121 SAS Nagar',28,507,'140307','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%\">Complainants relied on\r\nfalse promises &amp; signed </span><b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">Application\r\nfor Allotment </span></b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">on 10.12.17<b>(C1)</b>. Paid Rs 100,000\r\nas <b>booking amount(C2)</b>. Asked to pay 928,280 as installment. Complainant asked\r\nfor <b>Agreement To Sell</b> &amp; T&amp;C.\r\nThey said formalities could be done later. Installment paid on 02.01.18 <b>(C3).</b>They\r\nasked further payments. Complainant asked for agreement. But no response.\r\nComplainants requested them to execute agreement- they kept prolonging –didn’t\r\neven show agreement- therefore we were unable to raise loan.On 12.02.18\r\ncomplainant called to sign agreement. Advance copy not given. went to their\r\noffice on 17.02.18. shocked on reading agreement. No exit clause for allotee. Promoter\r\nhad option of leaving project mid-way at his discretion. Could change site plan/dimensions\r\nwithout intimation. No remedy for delay in possession. Late payments charged at\r\n18%. These terms were unacceptable &amp; asked for change. All terms were in their\r\nfavour. Sanctioned/ layout plan/ stage wise schedule not given.On 18.02.18 Complainant\r\ndecided to cancel allotment citing these reasons.they requested this will send\r\nbad name to project &amp; requested to cite other reason &amp; they will refund\r\nin full. They typed a letter in office citing reason as professional-\r\ncomplainant constrained to sign<b>(C4)</b>.They said they will issue cheque in\r\nname of Prashant &amp; sought email from Shilpa. Sent<b>(C5).</b> But no\r\nrefund.Complainant visited them many times for refund. They assured full return\r\nbut did not.No loss to them. When we requested them to give booked flat back,\r\nthey said sold &amp; is no longer available<b>(C6)</b>.Can keep nominal amount.\r\nNot whole. At best respondents can forfeit only part of booking/earnest amount of\r\n100,000. Not whole 1028000.Unilateral agreement- not signed by respondents-hence\r\ncannot be termed agreement.Written in their application that Receipt of\r\napplication &amp; booking Does not confirm allotment. Meaning, allotment not\r\nmade till then.Hard earned money of complainants. Respondents cannot be allowed\r\nto usurp.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"margin-left:72.0pt;mso-add-space:\r\nauto;text-align:justify;text-indent:-72.0pt;mso-text-indent-alt:-36.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-US\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</span>1.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-US\">Unilateral\r\nagreement- not signed by respondents- hence cannot be termed as agreement.<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-left:72.0pt;mso-add-space:\r\nauto;text-align:justify;text-indent:-72.0pt;mso-text-indent-alt:-36.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-US\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span>2.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-US\">Written\r\nin their application that Receipt of application &amp; acceptance of booking Does\r\nnot confirm allotment. Meaning, allotment not made till that time &amp; never\r\ncommunicated to us.<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"margin-left:72.0pt;mso-add-space:auto;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-indent:-72.0pt;mso-text-indent-alt:-36.0pt;line-height:\r\n200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-US\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span>3.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-US\">Hard\r\nearned money of complainants. Respondents cannot be allowed to usurp.<o:p></o:p></span></p>',11125760.00,1028000.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>abcd</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Apartment 9012 Building no. 9','','',2,0,0,0,'Prashantshilpa','2019-03-01 18:39:06.000','Prashantshilpa','2019-03-01 18:39:06.000'),(1135,1340,'1340',1245,'3f889bdc-3ee0-4229-87d4-71be8592f729','FormTypeM',1,1,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Prashant Gajanan Pathak','advamitgoyal@hotmail.com',9527700001,0,0,'Flat no. 603, Lotus Tower, Bollywood Heights,','Near sector-20 Panchkula Peer Machalla, Dhakoli, ',28,507,'140603','1','Flat no. 603, Lotus Tower, Bollywood Heights,','Near sector-20 Panchkula Peer Machalla, Dhakoli, ',28,507,'140603','Amit Goyal','advamitgoyal@hotmail.com',9527700001,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0086','ATS CASA ESPANA','ATS INFRABUILD PVT. LTD','email@atsgreens.com',0,1203811500,'ATS CASA ESPANA ','Village Bad Majra, Sector 121 SAS Nagar',28,507,'140307','1','ATS CASA ESPANA ','Village Bad Majra, Sector 121 SAS Nagar',28,507,'140307','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%\">Complainants relied on\r\nfalse promises &amp; signed </span><b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">Application\r\nfor Allotment </span></b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">on 10.12.17<b>(C1)</b>. Paid Rs 100,000\r\nas <b>booking amount(C2)</b>. Asked to pay 928,280 as installment. Complainant asked\r\nfor <b>Agreement To Sell</b> &amp; T&amp;C.\r\nThey said formalities could be done later. Installment paid on 02.01.18 <b>(C3).</b>They\r\nasked further payments. Complainant asked for agreement. But no response.\r\nComplainants requested them to execute agreement- they kept prolonging –didn’t\r\neven show agreement- therefore we were unable to raise loan.On 12.02.18\r\ncomplainant called to sign agreement. Advance copy not given. went to their\r\noffice on 17.02.18. shocked on reading agreement. No exit clause for allotee. Promoter\r\nhad option of leaving project mid-way at his discretion. Could change site plan/dimensions\r\nwithout intimation. No remedy for delay in possession. Late payments charged at\r\n18%. These terms were unacceptable &amp; asked for change. All terms were in their\r\nfavour. Sanctioned/ layout plan/ stage wise schedule not given.On 18.02.18 Complainant\r\ndecided to cancel allotment citing these reasons.they requested this will send\r\nbad name to project &amp; requested to cite other reason &amp; they will refund\r\nin full. They typed a letter in office citing reason as professional-\r\ncomplainant constrained to sign<b>(C4)</b>.They said they will issue cheque in\r\nname of Prashant &amp; sought email from Shilpa. Sent<b>(C5).</b> But no\r\nrefund.Complainant visited them many times for refund. They assured full return\r\nbut did not.No loss to them. When we requested them to give booked flat back,\r\nthey said sold &amp; is no longer available<b>(C6)</b>.Can keep nominal amount.\r\nNot whole. At best respondents can forfeit only part of booking/earnest amount of\r\n100,000. Not whole 1028000.Unilateral agreement- not signed by respondents-hence\r\ncannot be termed agreement.Written in their application that Receipt of\r\napplication &amp; booking Does not confirm allotment. Meaning, allotment not\r\nmade till then.Hard earned money of complainants. Respondents cannot be allowed\r\nto usurp.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"margin-left:72.0pt;mso-add-space:\r\nauto;text-align:justify;text-indent:-72.0pt;mso-text-indent-alt:-36.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-US\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</span>1.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-US\">Unilateral\r\nagreement- not signed by respondents- hence cannot be termed as agreement.<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle\" style=\"margin-left:72.0pt;mso-add-space:\r\nauto;text-align:justify;text-indent:-72.0pt;mso-text-indent-alt:-36.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-US\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span>2.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-US\">Written\r\nin their application that Receipt of application &amp; acceptance of booking Does\r\nnot confirm allotment. Meaning, allotment not made till that time &amp; never\r\ncommunicated to us.<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpLast\" style=\"margin-left:72.0pt;mso-add-space:auto;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-indent:-72.0pt;mso-text-indent-alt:-36.0pt;line-height:\r\n200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-US\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span>3.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-US\">Hard\r\nearned money of complainants. Respondents cannot be allowed to usurp.<o:p></o:p></span></p>',11125760.00,1028000.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-ansi-language:EN-US\">No\r\ninterim relief is being sought. The complainants only pray that the promoters\r\nbe directed to return the amount paid with interest.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Apartment 9012 Building no. 9','','',2,0,0,0,'Prashantshilpa','2019-03-01 18:45:02.000','Prashantshilpa','2019-03-01 18:45:02.000'),(1136,1340,'1340',1245,'3f889bdc-3ee0-4229-87d4-71be8592f729','FormTypeM',1,1,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Prashant Gajanan Pathak','advamitgoyal@hotmail.com',9527700001,0,0,'Flat no. 603, Lotus Tower, Bollywood Heights,','Near sector-20 Panchkula Peer Machalla, Dhakoli, ',28,507,'140603','1','Flat no. 603, Lotus Tower, Bollywood Heights,','Near sector-20 Panchkula Peer Machalla, Dhakoli, ',28,507,'140603','Amit Goyal','advamitgoyal@hotmail.com',9527700001,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0086','ATS CASA ESPANA','ATS INFRABUILD PVT. LTD','email@atsgreens.com',0,1203811500,'ATS CASA ESPANA ','Village Bad Majra, Sector 121 SAS Nagar',28,507,'140307','1','ATS CASA ESPANA ','Village Bad Majra, Sector 121 SAS Nagar',28,507,'140307','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%\">Complainants relied on\r\nfalse promises &amp; signed </span><b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">Application\r\nfor Allotment </span></b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">on 10.12.17<b>(C1)</b>. Paid Rs 100,000\r\nas <b>booking amount(C2)</b>. Asked to pay 928,280 as installment. Complainant asked\r\nfor <b>Agreement To Sell</b> &amp; T&amp;C.\r\nThey said formalities could be done later. Installment paid on 02.01.18 <b>(C3).</b>They\r\nasked further payments. Complainant asked for agreement. But no response.\r\nComplainants requested them to execute agreement- they kept prolonging –didn’t\r\neven show agreement- therefore we were unable to raise loan.On 12.02.18\r\ncomplainant called to sign agreement. Advance copy not given. went to their\r\noffice on 17.02.18. shocked on reading agreement. No exit clause for allotee. Promoter\r\nhad option of leaving project mid-way at his discretion. Could change site plan/dimensions\r\nwithout intimation. No remedy for delay in possession. Late payments charged at\r\n18%. These terms were unacceptable &amp; asked for change. All terms were in their\r\nfavour. Sanctioned/ layout plan/ stage wise schedule not given.On 18.02.18 Complainant\r\ndecided to cancel allotment citing these reasons.they requested this will send\r\nbad name to project &amp; requested to cite other reason &amp; they will refund\r\nin full. They typed a letter in office citing reason as professional-\r\ncomplainant constrained to sign<b>(C4)</b>.They said they will issue cheque in\r\nname of Prashant &amp; sought email from Shilpa. Sent<b>(C5).</b> But no\r\nrefund.Complainant visited them many times for refund. They assured full return\r\nbut did not.No loss to them. When we requested them to give booked flat back,\r\nthey said sold &amp; is no longer available<b>(C6)</b>.Can keep nominal amount.\r\nNot whole. At best respondents can forfeit only part of booking/earnest amount of\r\n100,000. Not whole 1028000.Unilateral agreement- not signed by respondents-hence\r\ncannot be termed agreement.Written in their application that Receipt of\r\napplication &amp; booking Does not confirm allotment. Meaning, allotment not\r\nmade till then.Hard earned money of complainants. Respondents cannot be allowed\r\nto usurp.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"margin-left:1.0cm;mso-add-space:auto;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-indent:-1.0cm;mso-text-indent-alt:-35.45pt;line-height:\r\n200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-US\">The\r\ncomplainant has suffered losses by reason of false and incorrect commitment\r\nmade by the respondents. Thus, the respondents are liable to cancel the booking\r\nof the flat and return the amount of ₹ 10,28,280 along with interest.</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;</span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; color: rgb(26, 26, 26);\">Interest as provided under </span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">Section\r\n18 and 19(4) of the RERA Act r/w </span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; color: rgb(26, 26, 26);\">Rule 16 of the Regulation and Development Rules\r\n2017 on the above Principal amount from the respective dates it was paid to the\r\nrespondent till the date of payment ie State Bank of India’s (“SBI”) highest\r\nMarginal Cost of Lending Rate (“MCLR”) plus 2%. The current SBI MCLR is 8.50%\r\npa so applicable interest rate for the refund is taken as 10.50% pa.</span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(26, 26, 26);\">Compensation\r\nfor Mental harassment to the tune of Rs. 1,00,000/-</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">To\r\nissue direction to pay the cost of litigation ie ₹ 44,000/-.</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</span></span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">To\r\nimpose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 60 of RERA\r\nAct for willful default committed by them.</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;</span></span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">To\r\nimpose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 61 of RERA\r\nAct for contravention of Sec.12, Sec.14, and Sec. 16 of RERA Act.</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;</span></span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">To\r\nissue directions to make liable every officer concerned i.e. Director, Manager,\r\nSecretary, or any other officer of the respondent’s company at whose instance,\r\nconnivance, acquiescence, neglect any of the offences has been committed as\r\nmentioned in Sec.69 of RERA Act, 2016 to be read with Punjab RERA Rules, 2017.</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;</span></span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">To\r\nrecommend criminal action against the respondents for the criminal offence of\r\ncheating, fraud and criminal breach of trust under section 420, 406 and 409 of\r\nthe Indian Penal Code.</span><span style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Any\r\nother relief which this Hon’ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of\r\nthe facts and circumstances of this complaint.</span></p>',11125760.00,1028000.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-ansi-language:EN-US\">No\r\ninterim relief is being sought. The complainants only pray that the promoters\r\nbe directed to return the amount paid with interest.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Apartment 9012 Building no. 9','','',2,0,0,0,'Prashantshilpa','2019-03-01 18:52:12.000','Prashantshilpa','2019-03-01 18:52:12.000'),(1137,1340,'1340',1245,'3f889bdc-3ee0-4229-87d4-71be8592f729','FormTypeM',1,1,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Prashant Gajanan Pathak','advamitgoyal@hotmail.com',9527700001,0,0,'Flat no. 603, Lotus Tower, Bollywood Heights,','Near sector-20 Panchkula Peer Machalla, Dhakoli, ',28,507,'140603','1','Flat no. 603, Lotus Tower, Bollywood Heights,','Near sector-20 Panchkula Peer Machalla, Dhakoli, ',28,507,'140603','Amit Goyal','advamitgoyal@hotmail.com',9527700001,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0086','ATS CASA ESPANA','ATS INFRABUILD PVT. LTD','email@atsgreens.com',0,1203811500,'ATS CASA ESPANA ','Village Bad Majra, Sector 121 SAS Nagar',28,507,'140307','1','ATS CASA ESPANA ','Village Bad Majra, Sector 121 SAS Nagar',28,507,'140307','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%\">Complainants relied on\r\nfalse promises &amp; signed </span><b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">Application\r\nfor Allotment </span></b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">on 10.12.17<b>(C1)</b>. Paid Rs 100,000\r\nas <b>booking amount(C2)</b>. Asked to pay 928,280 as installment. Complainant asked\r\nfor <b>Agreement To Sell</b> &amp; T&amp;C.\r\nThey said formalities could be done later. Installment paid on 02.01.18 <b>(C3).</b>They\r\nasked further payments. Complainant asked for agreement. But no response.\r\nComplainants requested them to execute agreement- they kept prolonging –didn’t\r\neven show agreement- therefore we were unable to raise loan.On 12.02.18\r\ncomplainant called to sign agreement. Advance copy not given. went to their\r\noffice on 17.02.18. shocked on reading agreement. No exit clause for allotee. Promoter\r\nhad option of leaving project mid-way at his discretion. Could change site plan/dimensions\r\nwithout intimation. No remedy for delay in possession. Late payments charged at\r\n18%. These terms were unacceptable &amp; asked for change. All terms were in their\r\nfavour. Sanctioned/ layout plan/ stage wise schedule not given.On 18.02.18 Complainant\r\ndecided to cancel allotment citing these reasons.they requested this will send\r\nbad name to project &amp; requested to cite other reason &amp; they will refund\r\nin full. They typed a letter in office citing reason as professional-\r\ncomplainant constrained to sign<b>(C4)</b>.They said they will issue cheque in\r\nname of Prashant &amp; sought email from Shilpa. Sent<b>(C5).</b> But no\r\nrefund.Complainant visited them many times for refund. They assured full return\r\nbut did not.No loss to them. When we requested them to give booked flat back,\r\nthey said sold &amp; is no longer available<b>(C6)</b>.Can keep nominal amount.\r\nNot whole. At best respondents can forfeit only part of booking/earnest amount of\r\n100,000. Not whole 1028000.Unilateral agreement- not signed by respondents-hence\r\ncannot be termed agreement.Written in their application that Receipt of\r\napplication &amp; booking Does not confirm allotment. Meaning, allotment not\r\nmade till then.Hard earned money of complainants. Respondents cannot be allowed\r\nto usurp.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"margin-left:1.0cm;mso-add-space:auto;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-indent:-1.0cm;mso-text-indent-alt:-35.45pt;line-height:\r\n200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-US\">The\r\ncomplainant has suffered losses by reason of false and incorrect commitment\r\nmade by the respondents. Thus, the respondents are liable to cancel the booking\r\nof the flat and return the amount of ₹ 10,28,280 along with interest.</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;</span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; color: rgb(26, 26, 26);\">Interest as provided under </span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">Section\r\n18 and 19(4) of the RERA Act r/w </span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; color: rgb(26, 26, 26);\">Rule 16 of the Regulation and Development Rules\r\n2017 on the above Principal amount from the respective dates it was paid to the\r\nrespondent till the date of payment ie State Bank of India’s (“SBI”) highest\r\nMarginal Cost of Lending Rate (“MCLR”) plus 2%. The current SBI MCLR is 8.50%\r\npa so applicable interest rate for the refund is taken as 10.50% pa.&nbsp;</span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(26, 26, 26);\">Compensation\r\nfor Mental harassment to the tune of Rs. 1,00,000/-</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">To\r\nissue direction to pay the cost of litigation ie ₹ 44,000/-.</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</span></span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">To\r\nimpose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 60 of RERA\r\nAct for willful default committed by them.</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;</span></span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">To\r\nimpose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 61 of RERA\r\nAct for contravention of Sec.12, Sec.14, and Sec. 16 of RERA Act.</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;</span></span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">To\r\nissue directions to make liable every officer concerned i.e. Director, Manager,\r\nSecretary, or any other officer of the respondent’s company at whose instance,\r\nconnivance, acquiescence, neglect any of the offences has been committed as\r\nmentioned in Sec.69 of RERA Act, 2016 to be read with Punjab RERA Rules, 2017.</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;</span></span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">To\r\nrecommend criminal action against the respondents for the criminal offence of\r\ncheating, fraud and criminal breach of trust under section 420, 406 and 409 of\r\nthe Indian Penal Code.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Any\r\nother relief which this Hon’ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of\r\nthe facts and circumstances of this complaint.</span></p>',11125760.00,1028000.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-ansi-language:EN-US\">No\r\ninterim relief is being sought. The complainants only pray that the promoters\r\nbe directed to return the amount paid with interest.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Apartment 9012 Building no. 9','','',2,0,0,0,'Prashantshilpa','2019-03-01 18:53:07.000','Prashantshilpa','2019-03-01 18:53:07.000'),(1138,1340,'1340',1245,'3f889bdc-3ee0-4229-87d4-71be8592f729','FormTypeM',1,1,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Prashant Gajanan Pathak','advamitgoyal@hotmail.com',9527700001,0,0,'Flat no. 603, Lotus Tower, Bollywood Heights,','Near sector-20 Panchkula Peer Machalla, Dhakoli, ',28,507,'140603','1','Flat no. 603, Lotus Tower, Bollywood Heights,','Near sector-20 Panchkula Peer Machalla, Dhakoli, ',28,507,'140603','Amit Goyal','advamitgoyal@hotmail.com',9527700001,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0086','ATS CASA ESPANA','ATS INFRABUILD PVT. LTD','email@atsgreens.com',0,1203811500,'ATS CASA ESPANA ','Village Bad Majra, Sector 121 SAS Nagar',28,507,'140307','1','ATS CASA ESPANA ','Village Bad Majra, Sector 121 SAS Nagar',28,507,'140307','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%\">Complainants relied on\r\nfalse promises &amp; signed </span><b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">Application\r\nfor Allotment </span></b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">on 10.12.17<b>(C1)</b>. Paid Rs 100,000\r\nas <b>booking amount(C2)</b>. Asked to pay 928,280 as installment. Complainant asked\r\nfor <b>Agreement To Sell</b> &amp; T&amp;C.\r\nThey said formalities could be done later. Installment paid on 02.01.18 <b>(C3).</b>They\r\nasked further payments. Complainant asked for agreement. But no response.\r\nComplainants requested them to execute agreement- they kept prolonging –didn’t\r\neven show agreement- therefore we were unable to raise loan.On 12.02.18\r\ncomplainant called to sign agreement. Advance copy not given. went to their\r\noffice on 17.02.18. shocked on reading agreement. No exit clause for allotee. Promoter\r\nhad option of leaving project mid-way at his discretion. Could change site plan/dimensions\r\nwithout intimation. No remedy for delay in possession. Late payments charged at\r\n18%. These terms were unacceptable &amp; asked for change. All terms were in their\r\nfavour. Sanctioned/ layout plan/ stage wise schedule not given.On 18.02.18 Complainant\r\ndecided to cancel allotment citing these reasons.they requested this will send\r\nbad name to project &amp; requested to cite other reason &amp; they will refund\r\nin full. They typed a letter in office citing reason as professional-\r\ncomplainant constrained to sign<b>(C4)</b>.They said they will issue cheque in\r\nname of Prashant &amp; sought email from Shilpa. Sent<b>(C5).</b> But no\r\nrefund.Complainant visited them many times for refund. They assured full return\r\nbut did not.No loss to them. When we requested them to give booked flat back,\r\nthey said sold &amp; is no longer available<b>(C6)</b>.Can keep nominal amount.\r\nNot whole. At best respondents can forfeit only part of booking/earnest amount of\r\n100,000. Not whole 1028000.Unilateral agreement- not signed by respondents-hence\r\ncannot be termed agreement.Written in their application that Receipt of\r\napplication &amp; booking Does not confirm allotment. Meaning, allotment not\r\nmade till then.Hard earned money of complainants. Respondents cannot be allowed\r\nto usurp.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"margin-left:1.0cm;mso-add-space:auto;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-indent:-1.0cm;mso-text-indent-alt:-35.45pt;line-height:\r\n200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-US\">The\r\ncomplainant has suffered losses by reason of false and incorrect commitment\r\nmade by the respondents. Thus, the respondents are liable to cancel the booking\r\nof the flat and return the amount of ₹ 10,28,280 along with interest.</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;</span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; color: rgb(26, 26, 26);\">Interest as provided under </span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">Section\r\n18 and 19(4) of the RERA Act r/w </span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; color: rgb(26, 26, 26);\">Rule 16 of the Regulation and Development Rules\r\n2017 on the above Principal amount from the respective dates it was paid to the\r\nrespondent till the date of payment ie State Bank of India’s (“SBI”) highest\r\nMarginal Cost of Lending Rate (“MCLR”) plus 2%. The current SBI MCLR is 8.50%\r\npa so applicable interest rate for the refund is taken as 10.50% pa.&nbsp;</span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(26, 26, 26);\">Compensation\r\nfor Mental harassment to the tune of Rs. 1,00,000/-</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">To\r\nissue direction to pay the cost of litigation ie ₹ 44,000/-.</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</span></span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">To\r\nimpose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 60 of RERA\r\nAct for willful default committed by them.</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;</span></span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">To\r\nimpose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 61 of RERA\r\nAct for contravention of Sec.12, Sec.14, and Sec. 16 of RERA Act.</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;</span></span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">To\r\nissue directions to make liable every officer concerned i.e. Director, Manager,\r\nSecretary, or any other officer of the respondent’s company at whose instance,\r\nconnivance, acquiescence, neglect any of the offences has been committed as\r\nmentioned in Sec.69 of RERA Act, 2016 to be read with Punjab RERA Rules, 2017.</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;</span></span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">To\r\nrecommend criminal action against the respondents for the criminal offence of\r\ncheating, fraud and criminal breach of trust under section 420, 406 and 409 of\r\nthe Indian Penal Code.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Any\r\nother relief which this Hon’ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of\r\nthe facts and circumstances of this complaint.</span></p>',11125760.00,1028000.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-ansi-language:EN-US\">No\r\ninterim relief is being sought. The complainants only pray that the promoters\r\nbe directed to return the amount paid with interest.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Apartment 9012 Building no. 9','','',2,0,0,0,'Prashantshilpa','2019-03-01 18:53:45.000','Prashantshilpa','2019-03-01 18:53:45.000'),(1139,1346,'1346',1406,'66159cde-d904-4355-a1f0-5ee347b0773b','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Varinder Mohan Garg','princegoyal1316@gmail.com',9216790493,0,0,'Ahata Kheta Mal Ramji Dass','Railway Road, Bathinda',28,84,'151001','0','H.NO. 311, SECTOR 79, AIRPORT ROAD','Mohali',28,507,'140308','MUNISH BANSAL & PRINCE GOYAL','mbansal.ind@gmail.com',9872029475,7888910080,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0093','The Palm (Palm Springs/Palm Eco/Palm Garden/Villas)',' Manohar Infrastructure and Constructions Private Limited ','manohargroupchd@gmail.com',1725033524,1725033526,'M/s. Manohar Infrastructure and Constructions Private Limited','SCO- 139 - 141, Sector 17-C, Chandigarh ',6,128,'160017','1','M/s. Manohar Infrastructure and Constructions Private Limited','SCO- 139 - 141, Sector 17-C, Chandigarh ',6,128,'160017','1','<p>1.	That the respondent in 2011 widely advertised its project \'Palm Garden\' situated at Mullanpur (New Chandigarh) and allured by advertisement, complainant booked a plot for his personal use measuring 250 Sq. Yards @ Rs. 18,500/Sq. Yards in above said project. \r\n</p><p>2.	That it was advertised that all the necessary permissions for the project have already been obtained by the respondent and the possession of the developed plot shall be handed over within a period of 3 years from the payment of booking amount. \r\n</p><p>3.	That Complainant on 09.04.2012 paid booking amount of 13,87,500/- vide cheque dt. 31.03.2012. Copy of Application Acknowledgement dated 31.03.2012 is Annex-A.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>4.	That, thereafter on subsequent demand of the respondent, the complainant further made a payment of Rs. 9,25,000/-.Copy of the receipt is Annex-B. \r\n</p><p>5.	That complainant had till date made a total payment of Rs. 23,12,500/-(50% of the BSP) on the demands raised by the respondent and the payment has been duly acknowledged by the respondent vide Statement of Account(Annex-C). \r\n</p><p>6.	That respondent has failed to execute any agreement/allotment letter in favor of the complaint till date but&nbsp;only issued registration No: PG/2132 on dated 29.06.2013.Copies of said documents are Annex-D. \r\n</p><p>7.	That despite receiving such a huge amount from complainant with a promise to deliver the fully developed plot by 31.03.2015, nothing matured and not even a draw for allotment of any plot in favor of complainant had been carried out (even till date of today). \r\n</p><p>8.	That on 06.08.2018, respondent further raised a demand for the balance 50% payment illegally without any actual development on the spot.The latest photographs of site are Annex-E.\r\n</p><p>9.	That the complainant has served legal notice(Annex–F) dt 03.10.2018 to the respondent to refund the hard earned money of complainant along with interest, but respondent failed to reply even to said legal notice, thereby admitting the averments of legal notice.</p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:6.9pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size: 9.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">That since there has been a false advertisement\r\nat the time of marketing of the project that the project has all the necessary\r\napprovals, whereas in actuality the project was not approved from all the\r\ncompetent authorities, as such the respondent failed to fulfill his obligation\r\nunder Section 12 of the RERA, 2016.</span><span style=\"font-size: 9.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:6.9pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size: 9.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">That the respondent had also taken/ accepted\r\namount of Rs 23,12,500/-(50% of the BSP), without entering into any formal\r\nagreement to sell, thus violating the provisions of Section 13 of the RERA,\r\n2016 and Section 6 of the PAPRA, 1995.</span><span style=\"font-size: 9.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:6.9pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size: 9.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">That since the respondent has failed to hand\r\nover the possession of the plot in the stipulated time period i.e 31.03.2015\r\nand further even till date, possession has not been delivered to the\r\nComplainant, as such the complainant is entitled to return of amount and\r\ncompensation.</span><span style=\"font-size: 9.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:6.9pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size: 9.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">In view of the above,&nbsp;It is therefore, most\r\nrespectfully&nbsp;</span><a href=\"prayed:-\"><span style=\"font-size: 9.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">prayed</span><span style=\"font-size: 9.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">:-</span></a><span style=\"font-size: 9.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:6.9pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size: 9.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 9.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">To&nbsp;refund the whole\r\namount paid by complainant&nbsp;i.e. Rs. 26,25,000/- alongwith interest @ 18 %\r\nw.e.f. the date of deposit with the opposite party till the same is paid to the\r\ncomplainant.</span><span style=\"font-size: 9.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:6.9pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size: 9.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 9.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">To pay an amount of Rs.\r\n2,50,000/- on account of monetary losses, mental as well as physical harassment\r\nto the complainant.</span><span style=\"font-size: 9.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:6.9pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size: 9.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 9.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">To pay Rs. 1,00,000/-\r\ntowards the litigation charges and counsel fees.</span><span style=\"font-size: 9.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<span style=\"font-size: 9.5pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: roboto, serif;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 9.5pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Any other relief which this\r\nHon’ble Commission deems fit and appropriate in facts and circumstances of the\r\npresent case.<br>\r\n<!--[if !supportLineBreakNewLine]--><br>\r\n<!--[endif]--></span></p>',4625000.00,2312500.00,'2015-03-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p><span style=\"font-size: 9.5pt; line-height: 14.5667px; font-family: roboto, serif;\">&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 9.5pt; line-height: 14.5667px; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Any interim relief which this Hon’ble Commission deems fit and appropriate in facts and circumstances of the present case.</span><br></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','NOT GIVEN.','','',2,0,0,0,'princegoyal2840','2019-03-01 20:37:05.000','princegoyal2840','2019-03-01 20:37:05.000'),(1140,1216,'1216',1141,'971b1ae7-f8bc-4323-80a7-088b81f8b7db','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-03-02 10:13:31.000','Suparna Randhawa','dpsrandhawa@hotmail.com',9914400088,0,0,'House No.229','Sector-16',6,128,'160015','1','House No. 253','Sector 4, Mansa Devi Complex',13,15,'134114','Sanjeev Gupta','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0093','PALM GARDEN','M/s Manohar Infrastructure & Constructions Pvt Ltd','nbs@manoharrealty.com',0,1725033524,'SCO 139-142','Sector-17C',6,128,'160017','1','SCO 139-142','Sector-17C',6,128,'160017','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:\r\njustify;line-height:200%;mso-layout-grid-align:none;text-autospace:none\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">A\r\nplot measuring 500 sq yards @18500 per sq yards was booked by complainant in\r\nthe project Palm Garden being developed by the respondent,vide application(C-1)dated\r\n18.12.11 &amp; booking amount of Rs. 2775000 i.e. 30% of sale consideration was\r\npaid.Before purchasing the said plot,respondent had assured the complainant\r\nthat it is having all the approvals for the development of project except\r\nlayout plan approval which will be approved within 30 days &amp; possession be\r\ndelivered within 2 years &amp; buyer’s agreement will executed within 3 months.A\r\npayment plan(C-2)was also given to the complainant.An acknowledgment(C-3)dated\r\n2.4.12 was issued.But inspite of repeated requests by the complainant,the respondent\r\nhas failed to issue any allotment letter &amp; execute buyer’s agreement within\r\nthe said period and even till date.Many times complainant visited the office of\r\nrespondent for getting the allotment letter and buyer agreement but to no\r\navail.There was no development on the site &amp; the respondent kept the\r\ncomplainant in dark about the approvals.A legal notice(C-4)dated 30.8.18\r\nwas sent to respondent for refund,in which sequence of events have been duly incorporated,\r\nwhich may kindly be treated as part of pleadings.After that complainant\r\nreceived a call from respondent who invited him to its office for redressal of\r\nhis grievances.Accordingly, complainant went there in 3<sup>rd</sup> week of\r\nOctober,2018,where the respondent assured that allotment letter would be duly\r\nissued &amp; buyer’s agreement would also be executed if the complainant further\r\ndeposit a sum of Rs. 1850000 i.e 20% sale consideration.But the complainant\r\nasked the respondent to first issue the allotment letter &amp; execute the\r\nagreement.Respondent refused to issue the same without getting any further\r\namount.The complainant has been harassed for so many years due to unfair trade\r\npractices on the part of respondent.A list of dates of approvals(C-5) &amp;\r\nimportant approvals as(C-6 &amp;C-7).Complaint for registration of FIR to\r\nvigilance as C-8<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<ol><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">To\r\ndirect the respondent to issue allotment letter in respect of 500 sq yard plot\r\nand execute the buyer’s agreement in compliance with Section 13 of RERA.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">To\r\nhand over the actual physical possession of the plot after issuing the\r\nallotment letter and execution of buyer’s agreement. The complainant is ready\r\nto pay the balance sale consideration. The respondent was not having any\r\nauthority to collect the money from general public before 25.1.2017. <o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">To\r\ndirect the respondent not to charge any other charges from the complainant\r\nexcept EDC and PLC (if any) since the plot was sold to the complainant @Rs18500/-\r\nper sq yards excluding EDC and PLC (if any).<o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">To\r\ndirect the respondent to pay interest at the rate as contemplated under Rule 16\r\nof Punjab RERA Rules, for the period of delay in delivering the possession to\r\nbe calculated from the committed date of possession i.e. 18.12.2013 till the\r\ndate of handing over the actual physical possession after obtaining the\r\ncompletion certificate. or in alternative to refund the amount with interest &amp; Compensation from the respective date of deposits.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">To\r\ntake action against the respondent under Section 61 of RERA for not complying\r\nthe provision of Section 13.Inspite of repeated\r\nrequest the respondent has not offered the buyer’s agreement even after getting itself registered under RERA rather it is\r\ndemanding more money for executing the same which is a clear violation of\r\nSection 13.The respondent was not even having any approval, rather it had not\r\neven applied the necessary permissions when the plot was sold to the\r\ncomplainant.The respondent got the exemption under Section 44 of PAPRA on\r\n25.1.2017.Before the said date it could not collect any money from general\r\npublic as per Annx C-6 &amp; C-7. In the present case the respondent collected the money from the\r\ncomplainant in 2011-12.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">To\r\ntake action against the respondent for collecting the money from the\r\ncomplainant before getting all the approvals and for indulging into unfair\r\ntrade practices.<o:p></o:p></span></li></ol><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:150%\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>',9250000.00,2775000.00,'2013-12-18 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<ol><li style=\"margin-left: 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">The\r\nrespondent be directed to issue the allotment letter to the complainant and\r\nexecute the buyer’s agreement in respect of 500 sq yards plot booked by the\r\ncomplainant.</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"margin: 12pt 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">The respondent\r\nbe directed to provide the list of allottees to whom it has allotted/sold the\r\n862 residential plots as per the layout plan approved by GMADA on 6.10.2015 and\r\nfor which it is duly registered under RERA.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"margin: 12pt 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">&nbsp;The respondent be directed to provide the\r\ndetails in respect of funds collected from the general public since 2010 in\r\nlieu of 862 residential plots which are part of approved layout and registered\r\nunder Section 3 of RERA and also, the detail where such amount has been\r\nutilized by the respondent. Also, the respondent be directed to provide all the\r\nbank details where such amount has been deposited along with the statement of\r\naccounts, since the year 2010 and where such amount has been utilized.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"margin: 12pt 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 7pt; line-height: 200%;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">The respondent be\r\ndirected to provide the details in respect of number of bookings done by it\r\nsince the year 2010 for the said 862 residential plots along with the list of\r\napplicants who had applied for booking of plots.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"margin: 12pt 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">The\r\nrespondent be directed to provide the details as regards the criteria adopted\r\nby it for allotting the plot numbers to different applicants through pick and\r\nchoose policy.</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"margin: 12pt 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">The\r\nrespondent be directed to provide the list of total applicants and further, the\r\nlist to whom it has already allotted the plot along with the list of applicants\r\nto whom it has not allotted the plots till date. </span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"margin: 12pt 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">The\r\nrespondent be directed to provide the list of hypothecated plots which are\r\nhypothecated to GMADA, out of the approved 862 residential plots and 73\r\ncommercial plots. Also, the respondent be directed to provide the list of\r\nhypothected plots sold to general public.</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></li></ol><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:12.0pt;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:\r\n0in;margin-left:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:12.0pt;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:\r\n0in;margin-left:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;line-height:200%;\r\nmso-layout-grid-align:none;text-autospace:none\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'rerafilingformm','2019-03-02 10:13:24.000','rerafilingformm','2019-03-02 10:13:24.000'),(1141,1347,'1347',1119,'dae2bb68-2fa2-473d-a49d-c15de93bd3da','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-03-02 13:46:11.000','Sundeep Singh Kajla','advravinder@gmail.com',9815700280,0,0,'VPO Juglan, Distt. Hisar','ZIrakpur',13,6,'125001','0','D-711, Ravindra Apartments, Ravindra Enclave, Baltana','ZIrakpur',28,507,'140604','Ravinder Pal Singh','advravinder@gmail.com',9815700280,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0155','GOLF LINKS - I','ANSAL PROPERTIES AND INFRASTRUCTURE LTD','customercare@ansalapi.com',0,0,'SCO 183-184, First Floor, Sector 9 Chandigarh','',6,128,'160009','0','Showroom No. 12A, Ground Floor, Citi Centre','Sector 115, Kharar-Landran Road, Mohali',28,507,'140307','1','<p>Complainant is an Army Personnel and is presently serving at Ferozepur Cant as Major. For his and his families own residential purposes, complainant decided to purchase a 3BHK Flat at the Golf Link-I project of Opposite Parties in the year 2010 with a hope that possession of the apartment shall be given within a period of 24-30 months in view of Clause 12 of the agreement dated 25.10.2010. Price of the Flat No. 917-FF measuring 1299 sq. ft. agreed at Rs.28,20,129/- besides PLC Charges Rs.1,00,000/- and&nbsp; Rs.1,50,515 as EDC. Thus the price of flat was Rs.30,70,644/-. Since the construction was badly delayed and there was no construction till 2015, therefore, complainant requested the Opposite Parties to shift him some other block where construction is in advance stage. Therefore, he was shifted to Flat bearing no. 933SF on 24.04.2015 whose price was agreed as Rs.32,65,097/- and the super area increased from 1299 to 1389 however, there was no increase in the carpet area of flat as to earlier. Till date complainant has paid Rs.32,09,499/- which is about 98% of the total price value, but still the possession of the flat has not been offered to the complainant till date. Comlpainat has also taken a loan of Rs.25,00,000/- against the said flat from HDFC. Recently, on 25.02.2019, complainant visited the site and found the flat in a very miserable condition. There are seepage in the whole staircase area from ground floor till top floor. No development is going on, It appears that Opposite Parties have dumped the project after receiving almost all the money from him. Thus violating the provisions of RERA by not handing over possession despite a lapse of more than 8 years. Therefore, complainant has decided to seek refund from the Opposite Parties. Thereafter, he visited their office at #12A, Sector 115 Mohali seeking refund of the deposited amount. Thereupon they flatly refused to refund the amount. Therefore complainant is filing the instant complaint seeking refund.</p>','<p>Opposite party may kindly be directed to refund deposited amount of Rs.32,09,499/- along with interest as per RERA Act and Cost of present litigation Rs.1,00,000/-.</p>',3265097.00,3209499.00,'2013-02-25 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Opposite Party may be directed to deposit Rs.32,09,499/- before this Hon\'ble Authority during the pendency of the present complaint.</p>','1','','2010-10-25 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','933 SF, Golf Links - I, Sector 114, Mohali','','',1,1,0,0,'advravinder','2019-03-02 12:50:53.000','advravinder','2019-03-02 12:50:53.000'),(1142,1345,'1345',1422,'734523d9-57e4-48b1-9b68-dd6258678e15','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-03-02 14:24:53.000','Aman Kumar Sharma','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9729902009,0,0,'D-73, Spangle Condos','Gazipur, Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','1','D-73, Spangle Condos','Gazipur, Zirakpur',28,507,'140603','Kamaljeet Dahiya','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9729902009,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0084','SUSHMA CRESCENT','SUSHMA BUILDTECH LIMITED','customercare@sushmabuildtech.com',0,0,'Unit No. B-107, Business Complex Elante Mall, 1st Floor, Industrial Area, Phase-I, Chandigarh','',6,128,'160002','1','Unit No. B-107, Business Complex Elante Mall, 1st Floor, Industrial Area, Phase-I, Chandigarh','',6,128,'160002','1','<p>Complainants had filed the complaint bearing no.ADCNo10162018 titled Aman Kumar&amp;Anr. v. Sushma Buildtech Ltd. on 31.08.18 before the Ld. Adjudicating Officer,RERA Punjab which was returned to the Complainants vide order dated 06.12.18 by putting reliance on the circular of Ld. Authority dated 21.11.18(C-1) &amp; granted them liberty to file a fresh complaint before this Hon’ble Authority. But in the meantime after the pronouncement of order, respondent cancelled the allotted unit 31.01.19 &amp; again sent an Intimation Letter for the same on16.02.19(C-2) which is illegal i.e. null &amp; void as this act of respondent is against the settled principle of law &amp; natural justice. Complainants had been allotted with Duplex Apartment no.A-1103, area 2380sq.ft, 11thFloor,TowerA. ABA executed18.02.13(C-3).Total consideration Rs66,60,000 excluding other statutory charges.Complainants paid total Rs68,88,605(95%)(C-4). Due date of possession-18.02.16 &amp; with 6 months grace period-18.07.16(clause14(d)ABA).Respondent offered possession vide email12.04.18(C-5).Complainants replied vide email19.04.18 &amp; raised queries that whether Occupany Certificate or Completion Certificate has been procured by the respondent before making offer of possession or not(C-6) but no reply. It means that they offered the possession without having the approvals &amp; Occupation or Completion Certificate.Complainants sent various reminder emails but all in vain(C-7). Certain deficiencies or snags reported by the Complainants after site visit &amp; they prepared a snag list(C-8).But was not removed till date.Complainants requested the respondent vide various emails to remove such snags but all in vain(C-9,Pg32).Respondent assured Complainants vide email 16.06.2018(Pg33).Complainants expresses their displeasure &amp; raised objections vide email(Pg34-36).Respondent again invited the Complainants to visit the project site vide email(Pg37).Complainants again expressed their displeasure &amp; requested for refund vide emails(Pg38-39)<br></p>','<p>i.To give necessary directions to the respondents for refund the amount paid by the Complainants with prescribed interest till realization as per the provisions of Sec. 18 and Sec.19(4)of the RERA Act read with Rule 16 of PSRE(R&amp;D)Rules,2017.</p><p>ii.To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 60 of RERA Act for willful default committed by them.</p><p>iii.To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 61 of RERA Act for contravention of Sec.12, Sec.14, and Sec. 16 of RERA Act.</p><p>iv.To issue directions to make liable every officer concerned i.e. Director, Manager, Secretary, or any other officer of the respondent’s company at whose instance, connivance, acquiescence, neglect any of the offences has been committed as mentioned in Sec.69 of RERA Act,2016 to be read with Punjab RERA Rules, 2017.</p><p>v.To recommend criminal action against the respondents for the criminal offence of cheating, fraud and criminal breach of trust under section 420,406 and 409 of the Indian Penal Code.</p><p>vi.To issue direction to pay the cost of litigation.</p><p>vii.Any other relief which this Hon’ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances of this complaint.</p><div><br></div>',6660000.00,6888605.00,'2016-02-18 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>i.To direct the respondent not to demand any further amount whatsoever from the Complainants.</p><p>ii.The respondent should be restrained from harassing the Complainants in any manner whatsoever.</p><p>iii.Any other interim relief which this Hon’ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances of this complaint.</p><div><br></div>','1','','2012-08-08 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','A-1103, Sushma Crescent, Zirakpur, Punjab','','',1,1,0,0,'AmanKumar','2019-03-02 13:14:36.000','AmanKumar','2019-03-02 13:14:36.000'),(1143,1348,'1348',1017,'c5979978-7e2d-4b44-85f9-d7153801dae4','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-03-05 13:38:09.000','PARIKA GANERIWAL','Kanisth@ganeriwala.co.in',9814048883,1724654850,0,'H NO 323, ADVOCATES ENCLAVE','SECTOR 49A',6,128,'160047','1','H NO 323, ADVOCATES ENCLAVE','SECTOR 49A',6,128,'160047','DN GANERIWALA','devki@ganeriwala.co.in',9814004850,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0090','SANDWOODS OPULENCIA, INFRATECH PROJECTS PRIVATE LIMITED','SANDWOODS INFRATECH PROJECTS PVT. LTD','info@sandwoods.com',0,0,'Regd Office. 1108, Arunachal Building','19 Barakhamba Road',10,120,'110001','0','SCO 222-223, 3rd Floor','Sector 34 A',6,128,'160034','1','<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"margin-top:12.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:\r\n8.0pt;margin-left:72.0pt;mso-add-space:auto;text-align:justify;line-height:\r\n200%\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: roboto, serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">The complainant executed Buyer\r\nAgreement on 27.05.2014 for the Unit against BSP of Rs. 4180000. The Builder\r\nfailed to deliver the possession on 27.05.2017 as per Clause 6(a) of Buyer\r\nAgreement which states that Builder shall offer the possession of Unit to the\r\nBuyer within 36 months from date of Agreement. The Builder sent letter\r\n05.09.2017 stating that it is offering possession of the Unit soon and on this\r\npretext stopped discharging their liabilities. The complainant was compelled to\r\nforeclose the loan on 27.12.2017. After more than 1 year from letter dated\r\n05.09.2017 had lapsed a complaint no. GC No.1048 of 2018 claiming refund under\r\nSection 18 was filed before RERA. Thereafter, Builder issued ante-dated letter\r\n13.09.2018 sent through postal receipt 01.10.2018, received on 04.10.2018. In\r\nhead note of letter ‘offer of possession’ is claimed whereas inside it is\r\nmentioned that Unit is in ‘pre-possession stage’ and getting ready for\r\npossession. The Builder misrepresented through its letter which was misconceived\r\nunder the garb of ‘offer of possession’ since it had neither applied nor\r\nobtained Occupation Certificate and Completion Certificate. This was proved\r\nfrom the RTI response from GMADA which was placed on record after having the\r\napproval of legal advisor on 26.12.2018. Its copy was also sent to counsel for\r\nopposite party under registered speed post on 26.12.2018. It shows fraud and\r\nsham by the Builder which speaks volumes of the delay and conduct of the\r\nBuilder which requires to be dealt strictly. The complaint has not received any\r\nintimation for handing over of actual possession along Completion Certificate\r\nand Occupation Certificate. The complainant has made timely payments of Rs.\r\n4398288 till 26.12.2017 which is more than the BSP. As per Clause (6)a of Agreement\r\nthe possession was to be handed over till 27.05.2017. In view of order\r\n08.01.2019, Builder failed to hand over the possession even till 28.02.2019,\r\npresent complaint has been filed for refund.</span><o:p></o:p></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:12.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:\r\n8.0pt;margin-left:72.0pt;text-align:justify;line-height:21.0pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">In view of the order\r\ndated 08.01.2019 passed in Complaint No. GC1048 of 2018 by the Chairperson,\r\nRERA, Punjab that “it is made clear that if possession is not handed over by\r\nend of February, 2019, the complainants would be entitled to move this forum\r\nafresh for refund of the amount deposited by them.”</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:12.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:\r\n8.0pt;margin-left:72.0pt;text-align:justify;line-height:21.0pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:12.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:\r\n8.0pt;margin-left:72.0pt;text-align:justify;line-height:21.0pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Therefore, the\r\ncomplainant claims the refund for all the amounts paid under Section 18 of RERA\r\nAct along with interest at the prescribed rate under Rule 16 of the Punjab\r\nState Real Estate Rules, 2017. The Builder may set off the interest amounts\r\nalready paid it to the financial institution under the subvention scheme\r\nagainst the interest amount now payable towards refund.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>',4180000.00,4398288.00,'2017-05-27 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>As this Hon\'ble Forum may deem fit under the circumstances of the case.&nbsp;</p>','1','','2014-05-28 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Unit No. 172, Tower D4, Sandwoods Opulencia, Sector 110, Landran Road, SAS Nagar','','',1,1,0,0,'Saloney','2019-03-03 11:26:00.000','Saloney','2019-03-03 11:26:00.000'),(1144,1349,'1349',1017,'c5979978-7e2d-4b44-85f9-d7153801dae4','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','KANISTH GANERIWALA','Kanisth@ganeriwala.co.in',9814048883,1724654850,0,'H NO 323, ADVOCATES ENCLAVE','SECTOR 49A',6,128,'160047','1','H NO 323, ADVOCATES ENCLAVE','SECTOR 49A',6,128,'160047','DN GANERIWALA','devki@ganeriwala.co.in',9814004850,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0090','SANDWOODS OPULENCIA, INFRATECH PROJECTS PRIVATE LIMITED','SANDWOODS INFRATECH PROJECTS PVT. LTD','info@sandwoods.com',0,0,'Regd Office. 1108, Arunachal Building','19 Barakhamba Road',10,120,'110001','0','SCO 222-223, 3rd Floor','Sector 34 A',6,128,'160034','1','<p>The complainant executed Buyer Agreement on 27.10.2014 for the Unit against BSP of Rs. 4180000. The Builder failed to deliver the possession on 26.10.2017 as per Clause 6(a) of Buyer Agreement which states that Builder shall offer the possession of Unit to the Buyer within 36 months from date of Agreement. The Builder sent letter 05.09.2017 stating that it is offering possession of the Unit soon and on this pretext stopped discharging their liabilities. After more than 1 year from letter dated 05.09.2017 had lapsed a complaint no. GC No.1049 of 2018 claiming refund under Section 18 was filed before RERA. Thereafter, Builder issued ante-dated letter 13.09.2018 sent through postal receipt 01.10.2018, received on 04.10.2018. In head note of letter ‘offer of possession’ is claimed whereas inside it is mentioned that Unit is in ‘pre-possession stage’ and getting ready for possession. The Builder misrepresented through its letter which was misconceived under the garb of ‘offer of possession’ since it had neither applied nor obtained Occupation Certificate and Completion Certificate. This was proved from the RTI response from GMADA which was placed on record after having the approval of legal advisor on 26.12.2018. Its copy was also sent to counsel for opposite party under registered speed post on 26.12.2018. It shows fraud and sham by the Builder and admittedly on the face of it, it speaks volumes of the delay and conduct of Builder which requires to be dealt strictly with heavy hands. The complaint has not received any intimation for handing over of actual possession along Completion Certificate and Occupation Certificate. The complainant has made timely payments of Rs. 4290666 till 26.12.2017 which is more than the BSP. As per Clause (6)a of Agreement the possession was required to be handed over till 26.10.2017. In view of order 08.01.2019 Builder failed to hand over the possession even till 28.02.2019, the present complaint has been filed seeking refund with interest.</p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:12.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:\r\n8.0pt;margin-left:72.0pt;text-align:justify;line-height:21.0pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">In view of the order\r\ndated 08.01.2019 passed in Complaint No. GC1049 of 2018 by the Chairperson,\r\nRERA, Punjab that “it is made clear that if possession is not handed over by\r\nend of February, 2019, the complainants would be entitled to move this forum\r\nafresh for refund of the amount deposited by them.”</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:12.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:\r\n8.0pt;margin-left:72.0pt;text-align:justify;line-height:21.0pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:12.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:\r\n8.0pt;margin-left:72.0pt;text-align:justify;line-height:21.0pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Therefore, the\r\ncomplainant claims the refund for all the amounts paid under Section 18 of RERA\r\nAct along with interest at the prescribed rate under Rule 16 of the Punjab\r\nState Real Estate Rules, 2017. The Builder may set off the interest amounts\r\nalready paid it to the financial institution under the subvention scheme\r\nagainst the interest amount now payable towards refund.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>',4180000.00,4290666.00,'2017-10-26 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>As this Hon\'ble Forum deems fit under the facts and circumstances of the case.</p>','1','','2014-10-27 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Unit No. 169, Tower D4, Sandwoods Opulencia, Sector 110, Landran Road, SAS Nagar','','',2,0,0,0,'Saloney','2019-03-03 13:26:36.000','Saloney','2019-03-03 13:26:36.000'),(1145,1349,'1349',1017,'c5979978-7e2d-4b44-85f9-d7153801dae4','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','KANISTH GANERIWALA','Kanisth@ganeriwala.co.in',9814048883,1724654850,0,'H NO 323, ADVOCATES ENCLAVE','SECTOR 49A',6,128,'160047','1','H NO 323, ADVOCATES ENCLAVE','SECTOR 49A',6,128,'160047','DN GANERIWALA','devki@ganeriwala.co.in',9814004850,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PR0090','SANDWOODS OPULENCIA, INFRATECH PROJECTS PRIVATE LIMITED','SANDWOODS INFRATECH PROJECTS PVT. LTD','info@sandwoods.com',0,0,'Regd Office. 1108, Arunachal Building','19 Barakhamba Road',10,120,'110001','0','SCO 222-223, 3rd Floor','Sector 34 A',6,128,'160034','1','<p>The complainant executed Buyer Agreement on 27.10.2014 for the Unit against BSP of Rs. 4180000. The Builder failed to deliver the possession on 26.10.2017 as per Clause 6(a) of Buyer Agreement which states that Builder shall offer the possession of Unit to the Buyer within 36 months from date of Agreement. The Builder sent letter 05.09.2017 stating that it is offering possession of the Unit soon and on this pretext stopped discharging their liabilities. After more than 1 year from letter dated 05.09.2017 had lapsed a complaint no. GC No.1049 of 2018 claiming refund under Section 18 was filed before RERA. Thereafter, Builder issued ante-dated letter 13.09.2018 sent through postal receipt 01.10.2018, received on 04.10.2018. In head note of letter ‘offer of possession’ is claimed whereas inside it is mentioned that Unit is in ‘pre-possession stage’ and getting ready for possession. The Builder misrepresented through its letter which was misconceived under the garb of ‘offer of possession’ since it had neither applied nor obtained Occupation Certificate and Completion Certificate. This was proved from the RTI response from GMADA which was placed on record after having the approval of legal advisor on 26.12.2018. Its copy was also sent to counsel for opposite party under registered speed post on 26.12.2018. It shows fraud and sham by the Builder and admittedly on the face of it, it speaks volumes of the delay and conduct of Builder which requires to be dealt strictly with heavy hands. The complaint has not received any intimation for handing over of actual possession along Completion Certificate and Occupation Certificate. The complainant has made timely payments of Rs. 4290666 till 26.12.2017 which is more than the BSP. As per Clause (6)a of Agreement the possession was required to be handed over till 26.10.2017. In view of order 08.01.2019 Builder failed to hand over the possession even till 28.02.2019, the present complaint has been filed seeking refund with interest.</p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:12.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:\r\n8.0pt;margin-left:72.0pt;text-align:justify;line-height:21.0pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">In view of the order\r\ndated 08.01.2019 passed in Complaint No. GC1049 of 2018 by the Chairperson,\r\nRERA, Punjab that “it is made clear that if possession is not handed over by\r\nend of February, 2019, the complainants would be entitled to move this forum\r\nafresh for refund of the amount deposited by them.”</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:12.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:\r\n8.0pt;margin-left:72.0pt;text-align:justify;line-height:21.0pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:12.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:\r\n8.0pt;margin-left:72.0pt;text-align:justify;line-height:21.0pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Therefore, the\r\ncomplainant claims the refund for all the amounts paid under Section 18 of RERA\r\nAct along with interest at the prescribed rate under Rule 16 of the Punjab\r\nState Real Estate Rules, 2017. The Builder may set off the interest amounts\r\nalready paid it to the financial institution under the subvention scheme\r\nagainst the interest amount now payable towards refund.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>',4180000.00,4290666.00,'2017-10-26 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>The Builder may be directed to pay the pre-EMI to the bank in view of the undertaking dated 26.07.2014 which the Builder has stopped paying since from October 2017.</p>','1','','2014-10-27 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Unit No. 169, Tower D4, Sandwoods Opulencia, Sector 110, Landran Road, SAS Nagar','','',2,0,0,0,'Saloney','