00 sq yards plot\r\nbooked by the complainant.</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"margin: 12pt 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">The respondent be directed to provide the list of allottees to whom\r\nit has allotted/sold the 862 residential plots as per the layout plan approved\r\nby GMADA on 6.10.2015 and for which it is duly registered under RERA. The fact is that the respondent has overbooked the plot. It has collected money from around 3000 people.As per the layout plan approved in 2015, it is having only 862 plot.&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"margin: 12pt 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">&nbsp;The respondent be directed\r\nto provide the details in respect of funds collected from the general public\r\nsince 2010 in lieu of 862 residential plots which are part of approved layout\r\nand registered under Section 3 of RERA and also, the detail where such amount\r\nhas been utilized by the respondent. Also, the respondent be directed to\r\nprovide all the bank details where such amount has been deposited along with\r\nthe statement of accounts, since the year 2010 and where such amount has been\r\nutilized.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"margin: 12pt 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 7pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">The respondent be\r\ndirected to provide the details in respect of number of bookings done by it\r\nsince the year 2010 for the said 862 residential plots along with the list of\r\napplicants who had applied for booking of plots.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"margin: 12pt 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">The respondent be directed to provide the details as regards the\r\ncriteria adopted by it for allotting the plot numbers to different applicants\r\nthrough pick and choose policy.</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"margin: 12pt 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">The respondent be directed to provide the list of total applicants\r\nand further, the list to whom it has already allotted the plot along with the list\r\nof applicants to whom it has not allotted the plots till date. </span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"margin: 12pt 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">The respondent be directed to provide the list of hypothecated\r\nplots which are hypothecated to GMADA, out of the approved 862 residential\r\nplots and 73 commercial plots. Also, the respondent be directed to provide the\r\nlist of hypothected plots sold to general public.</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></li></ol><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:12.0pt;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:\r\n0in;margin-left:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:12.0pt;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:\r\n0in;margin-left:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;line-height:200%;\r\nmso-layout-grid-align:none;text-autospace:none\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'rerafilingformm','2019-03-04 14:25:36.000','rerafilingformm','2019-03-04 14:25:36.000'),(1156,1241,'1241',1141,'971b1ae7-f8bc-4323-80a7-088b81f8b7db','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Navdeep Singh Anand','navee.anand@gmail.com',9814611997,0,0,'19-D, Rajguru Nagar','Ludhiana',28,366,'141002','1','253, Sector 4, MDC','Mansa Devi Complex',13,15,'134114','Sanjeev Gupta','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-LDH45-PR0041','Ireo Waterfront','M/s Ireo Waterfront Pvt. Ltd','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',0,0,'Sidhwan Canal Road, Opp. Ferozepur Road, ','Village Dewatwal',28,366,'141002','1','Sidhwan Canal Road, Opp. Ferozepur Road, ','Village Dewatwal',28,366,'141002','1','<p>abc</p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;line-height:\r\nnormal;mso-layout-grid-align:none;text-autospace:none\"><span style=\"font-family:\r\n&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Relying upon the provision of section 18 RERA, directing the respondent to refund the principle amount\r\ni.e. Rs. 6001038.30 along with interest as&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">contemplated under rule 16 of The Punjab RERA Rules,\r\n2017, as the complainants wishes to withdraw from the project, since the respondent was bound to deliver the possession of the built up villa by 25.11.2017. The respondent has indulged into unfair trade practices by not delivering the possession till date, not doing any development on the project and further it has stopped the development works on the project site and the respondent did not even send any reply to the letters sent by the complainants. The respondent have failed to intimate any reason for the delay in development</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;line-height:\r\nnormal;mso-layout-grid-align:none;text-autospace:none\"><br></p>',17000222.00,6001038.30,'2017-11-25 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>To direct the respondent to refund the principal amount of Rs. 6001038.30.</p>','1','','2015-10-07 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Unit No. 104, Type-B2 Built up villa ','','',1,0,0,0,'rerafilingformm','2019-03-04 17:02:26.000','rerafilingformm','2019-03-04 17:02:26.000'),(1157,1350,'1350',1010,'a182232b-88d6-4711-8baa-f8a026fb675f','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-03-08 10:36:51.000','MONIKA TAKKAR','lawofficeofhimanshuraj@gmail.com',8622000001,1724181010,457308216625,'RZ 63, GALI NO.-2','MAIN ROAD, PALAM PURAN NAGAR, PALAM COLONY, PALAM VILLAGE',10,562,'110045','0','#102, Sector 10 A','',6,128,'160011','HIMANSHU RAJ','lawofficeofhimanshuraj@gmail.com',9988200001,1724190909,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PC0029','ANSAL GOLF LINKS','ANSAL PROPERTIES AND INFRASTRUCTURE LIMITED ','customercare@ansalapi.com',1725035035,0,'115, ANSAL BHAWAN ','K G MARG, NEW DELHI',10,429,'110001','1','115, ANSAL BHAWAN ','K G MARG, NEW DELHI',10,429,'110001','1','<p>That the original allottee had booked a plot on 11.12.2010 for shop cum office SCO in OPs project ANSAL GOLF LINKS situated around village kailon on kharar-landran road, Mohali, Punjab. That on 12.10.2010, the Op allotted Plot No. 47 E measuring 33.33 Sq. Yard in the said Project and it was assured that the possession of the plot will be delivered by 31.12.2011. Allotment letter is annexed as ANNEXURE C-1</p><p>That on 10.02.2011, the complainant, aadhar card annexed as ANNEXURE C-2, had purchased the said plot from the original allottee vide transfer application annexed as ANENXURE C-3 COLLY. That the OP continuously demanded amount from the complainant without even having necessary approvals from the competent authority. Demand notices is annexed as ANNEXURE C-4. That the complainant had paid the complete amount along with delayed interest 18 per cent to the OP but OP failed to hand over the possession of the unit by 31.12.2011. Total amount paid by complainant is annexed as ANNEXURE C-5 COLLY.</p><p>That the complainant tried to contact the OP numerous times regarding the status of the unit but no response was given. Being aggrieved the complainant issued Legal notice but no response was given. Legal Notice is annexed as ANNEXURE C-6. The complainant had also lodged a complaint against OP in Police station Hari Nagar. New delhi under Section 420 of IPC 1806 on 20.02.2016. Police complaint is annexed as ANNEXURE C-7.</p><p>That on 10.09.2018, OP unilaterally and arbitrarily relocated the plot of the complainant from 47 E to 54 E, the letter is annexed as ANENXURE C-8, but has failed to hand over the possession of the unit. That the OP has even failed to upload the requite documents in RERA’s website, till date. That the complainant had even filed a complaint with NCDRC but the same is to be withdrawn by the complainants.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>','<p>1.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To direct the OP to hand over the complete amount along with 18 per cent interest according to Section 2 za i of Real Estate Regulation and Development Act, 2016, as the same was demanded and accepted by OP from the complainant for delayed payments.</p><p>2.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To direct the OP to pay Rs.10,000 per month from the committed date of possession till the filing of the present petition,&nbsp; for causing mental agony caused to the complainants.</p><p>3.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To direct the OP to pay Rs.10,000 per month from the committed date of possession till the filing of the present petition, to the complainants as the deficiency in services for keeping the complainants in dark in regard to the progress of the property.</p><p>4.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To direct the OP to pay Rs.10,000 per month from the committed date of possession till the filing of the present petition, for causing physical harassment caused to the complainants.</p><p>5.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To direct the OP to hand upload all the requiste documents in RERA Haryana website i.e. CLU, License to develop, Environmental clearance etc&nbsp; and furnish the complainant with the same.</p><p>6.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Any other relief or claim which the Honble Authority deems appropriate.</p>',1499850.00,1589708.00,'2011-12-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Not Prayed</p>','1','','2010-11-12 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Earlier Allotted Unit No. 47 E, Revised Allotted Unit No. 54 E, Sector-114, Golf Links-I, Mohali','','',2,0,0,0,'lawofficeofhimanshuraj','2019-03-04 19:52:24.000','lawofficeofhimanshuraj','2019-03-04 19:52:24.000'),(1158,1351,'1351',1301,'99fdf70d-599f-4e41-a773-1804cee1ff27','FormTypeM',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Ravjot Singh  Gill','gillravjot@yahoo.com',8373900100,1122518435,0,'407 GAGAN VIHAR','',10,189,'110051','1','407 GAGAN VIHAR','',10,189,'110051','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-LDH45-PR0060','Ireo Waterfront Pvt. Ltd.','MADHUKAR TULSI','iwpl@ireo.in',9810237279,0,'SCO 6-8, Sector 9-D','1st & 2nd Floor, Madhya Marg',6,128,'160009','0','C-14, 1ST FLOOR','Malviya Nagar',10,557,'110017','1','<p>It is submitted that we had booked an independent floor with the above stated company in their project</p><p>Ireo Waterfront situated at Ludhiana. The application for allotment was submitted on 18/02/2013 for Unit</p><p>no. X006A for Ground Floor having super area 1532 square foot in a plot size of 236.80 sq yard having</p><p>proportional rights in the said plot. The agreement was executed on 07/10/2013 for this unit. The basic</p><p>price of unit as per agreement is Rs.58,23,722/-. In these years we have visited the site office of the</p><p>company regarding completion of the unit but every time we find a new representative from the company</p><p>side with some false promises of early delivery. Clause no 12.3 of agreement states that normal period of</p><p>delivery is 24 months from the date of execution of agreement. The company had also asked for a grace</p><p>period of 180 days for delay in delivery. But it has been more than five years from date of execution of</p><p>agreement, but no possession has been offered despite major percentage of payment as demanded by</p><p>the company has been paid. Also, please refer to clause 12.5 of agreement which states that in event of</p><p>delay by company in submitting notice of completion beyond 12 months from the end of grace period then</p><p>the allottee shall become entitled to opt for termination. We have made all the payments diligently as and</p><p>when advised by the company. Till date an amount of Rs 50,68,232/- has been paid (basic + tax) by us to</p><p>the company as per their demand letters received by us but there is no sign of completion and delivery of</p><p>the above said unit. We had purchased this unit for our son who was to start his career. All our hopes</p><p>have been dashed and we had to invest in making additional construction at our parental house to create</p><p>an accommodation for him. You are humbly requested to get our unit cancelled and our money along with</p><p>market rate of interest and a suitable amount of compensation be returned to us.</p>','<p>It is submitted that we had booked an independent floor with the above stated company in their project</p><p>Ireo Waterfront situated at Ludhiana. The application for allotment was submitted on 18/02/2013 for Unit</p><p>no. X006A for Ground Floor having super area 1532 square foot in a plot size of 236.80 sq yard having</p><p>proportional rights in the said plot. The agreement was executed on 07/10/2013 for this unit. The basic</p><p>price of unit as per agreement is Rs.58,23,722/-. In these years we have visited the site office of the</p><p>company regarding completion of the unit but every time we find a new representative from the company</p><p>side with some false promises of early delivery. Clause no 12.3 of agreement states that normal period of</p><p>delivery is 24 months from the date of execution of agreement. The company had also asked for a grace</p><p>period of 180 days for delay in delivery. But it has been more than five years from date of execution of</p><p>agreement, but no possession has been offered despite major percentage of payment as demanded by</p><p>the company has been paid. Also, please refer to clause 12.5 of agreement which states that in event of</p><p>delay by company in submitting notice of completion beyond 12 months from the end of grace period then</p><p>the allottee shall become entitled to opt for termination. We have made all the payments diligently as and</p><p>when advised by the company. Till date an amount of Rs 50,68,232/- has been paid (basic + tax) by us to</p><p>the company as per their demand letters received by us but there is no sign of completion and delivery of</p><p>the above said unit. We had purchased this unit for our son who was to start his career. All our hopes</p><p>have been dashed and we had to invest in making additional construction at our parental house to create</p><p>an accommodation for him. You are humbly requested to get our unit cancelled and our money along with</p><p>market rate of interest and a suitable amount of compensation be returned to us.</p>',5823722.00,5068232.00,'2015-10-06 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>It is submitted that we had booked an independent floor with the above stated company in their project</p><p>Ireo Waterfront situated at Ludhiana. The application for allotment was submitted on 18/02/2013 for Unit</p><p>no. X006A for Ground Floor having super area 1532 square foot in a plot size of 236.80 sq yard having</p><p>proportional rights in the said plot. The agreement was executed on 07/10/2013 for this unit. The basic</p><p>price of unit as per agreement is Rs.58,23,722/-. In these years we have visited the site office of the</p><p>company regarding completion of the unit but every time we find a new representative from the company</p><p>side with some false promises of early delivery. Clause no 12.3 of agreement states that normal period of</p><p>delivery is 24 months from the date of execution of agreement. The company had also asked for a grace</p><p>period of 180 days for delay in delivery. But it has been more than five years from date of execution of</p><p>agreement, but no possession has been offered despite major percentage of payment as demanded by</p><p>the company has been paid. Also, please refer to clause 12.5 of agreement which states that in event of</p><p>delay by company in submitting notice of completion beyond 12 months from the end of grace period then</p><p>the allottee shall become entitled to opt for termination. We have made all the payments diligently as and</p><p>when advised by the company. Till date an amount of Rs 50,68,232/- has been paid (basic + tax) by us to</p><p>the company as per their demand letters received by us but there is no sign of completion and delivery of</p><p>the above said unit. We had purchased this unit for our son who was to start his career. All our hopes</p><p>have been dashed and we had to invest in making additional construction at our parental house to create</p><p>an accommodation for him. You are humbly requested to get our unit cancelled and our money along with</p><p>market rate of interest and a suitable amount of compensation be returned to us.</p>','1','','2013-10-07 00:00:00','2013-10-07 00:00:00','X006 A','','',2,0,0,0,'gillravjot','2019-03-06 14:43:23.000','gillravjot','2019-03-06 14:43:23.000'),(1159,1216,'1216',1141,'971b1ae7-f8bc-4323-80a7-088b81f8b7db','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-03-02 10:13:31.000','Suparna Randhawa','dpsrandhawa@hotmail.com',9914400088,0,0,'House No.229','Sector-16',6,128,'160015','1','House No. 253','Sector 4, Mansa Devi Complex',13,15,'134114','Sanjeev Gupta','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0093','PALM GARDEN','M/s Manohar Infrastructure & Constructions Pvt Ltd','nbs@manoharrealty.com',0,1725033524,'SCO 139-142','Sector-17C',6,128,'160017','1','SCO 139-142','Sector-17C',6,128,'160017','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:\r\njustify;line-height:200%;mso-layout-grid-align:none;text-autospace:none\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">A\r\nplot measuring 500 sq yards @18500 per sq yards was booked by complainant in\r\nthe project Palm Garden being developed by the respondent,vide application(C-1)dated\r\n18.12.11 &amp; booking amount of Rs. 2775000 i.e. 30% of sale consideration was\r\npaid.Before purchasing the said plot,respondent had assured the complainant\r\nthat it is having all the approvals for the development of project except\r\nlayout plan approval which will be approved within 30 days &amp; possession be\r\ndelivered within 2 years &amp; buyer’s agreement will executed within 3 months.An acknowledgment(C-2)dated\r\n2.4.12 was issued.But inspite of repeated requests by the complainant,the respondent\r\nhas failed to issue any allotment letter &amp; execute buyer’s agreement within\r\nthe said period and even till date.Many times complainant visited the office of\r\nrespondent for getting the allotment letter and buyer agreement but to no\r\navail.There was no development on the site &amp; the respondent kept the\r\ncomplainant in dark about the approvals.A legal notice(C-3)dated 30.8.18\r\nwas sent to respondent for refund,in which sequence of events have been duly incorporated,\r\nwhich may kindly be treated as part of pleadings.After that complainant\r\nreceived a call from respondent who invited him to its office for redressal of\r\nhis grievances.Accordingly, complainant went there in 3<sup>rd</sup> week of\r\nOctober,2018,where the respondent assured that allotment letter would be duly\r\nissued &amp; buyer’s agreement would also be executed if the complainant further\r\ndeposit a sum of Rs. 1850000 i.e 20% sale consideration.But the complainant\r\nasked the respondent to first issue the allotment letter &amp; execute the\r\nagreement.Respondent refused to issue the same without getting any further\r\namount.The complainant has been harassed for so many years due to unfair trade\r\npractices on the part of respondent.A list of dates of approvals(C-4) &amp;\r\nimportant approvals as(C-5 &amp;C-6).Complaint for registration of FIR to\r\nvigilance as C-7<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<ol><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">To\r\ndirect the respondent to issue allotment letter in respect of 500 sq yard plot\r\nand execute the buyer’s agreement in compliance with Section 13 of RERA.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">To\r\nhand over the actual physical possession of the plot after issuing the\r\nallotment letter and execution of buyer’s agreement. The complainant is ready\r\nto pay the balance sale consideration. The respondent was not having any\r\nauthority to collect the money from general public before 25.1.2017. <o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">To\r\ndirect the respondent not to charge any other charges from the complainant\r\nexcept EDC and PLC (if any) since the plot was sold to the complainant @Rs18500/-\r\nper sq yards excluding EDC and PLC (if any).<o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">To\r\ndirect the respondent to pay interest at the rate as contemplated under Rule 16\r\nof Punjab RERA Rules, for the period of delay in delivering the possession to\r\nbe calculated from the committed date of possession i.e. 18.12.2013 till the\r\ndate of handing over the actual physical possession after obtaining the\r\ncompletion certificate. or in alternative to refund the amount with interest &amp; Compensation from the respective date of deposits.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">To\r\ntake action against the respondent under Section 61 of RERA for not complying\r\nthe provision of Section 13.Inspite of repeated\r\nrequest the respondent has not offered the buyer’s agreement even after getting itself registered under RERA rather it is\r\ndemanding more money for executing the same which is a clear violation of\r\nSection 13.The respondent was not even having any approval, rather it had not\r\neven applied the necessary permissions when the plot was sold to the\r\ncomplainant.The respondent got the exemption under Section 44 of PAPRA on\r\n25.1.2017.Before the said date it could not collect any money from general\r\npublic as per Annx C-6 &amp; C-7. In the present case the respondent collected the money from the\r\ncomplainant in 2011-12.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">To\r\ntake action against the respondent for collecting the money from the\r\ncomplainant before getting all the approvals and for indulging into unfair\r\ntrade practices.<o:p></o:p></span></li></ol><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:150%\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>',9250000.00,2775000.00,'2013-12-18 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<ol><li style=\"margin-left: 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">The\r\nrespondent be directed to issue the allotment letter to the complainant and\r\nexecute the buyer’s agreement in respect of 500 sq yards plot booked by the\r\ncomplainant.</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"margin: 12pt 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">The respondent\r\nbe directed to provide the list of allottees to whom it has allotted/sold the\r\n862 residential plots as per the layout plan approved by GMADA on 6.10.2015 and\r\nfor which it is duly registered under RERA.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"margin: 12pt 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">&nbsp;The respondent be directed to provide the\r\ndetails in respect of funds collected from the general public since 2010 in\r\nlieu of 862 residential plots which are part of approved layout and registered\r\nunder Section 3 of RERA and also, the detail where such amount has been\r\nutilized by the respondent. Also, the respondent be directed to provide all the\r\nbank details where such amount has been deposited along with the statement of\r\naccounts, since the year 2010 and where such amount has been utilized.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"margin: 12pt 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 7pt; line-height: 200%;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">The respondent be\r\ndirected to provide the details in respect of number of bookings done by it\r\nsince the year 2010 for the said 862 residential plots along with the list of\r\napplicants who had applied for booking of plots.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"margin: 12pt 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">The\r\nrespondent be directed to provide the details as regards the criteria adopted\r\nby it for allotting the plot numbers to different applicants through pick and\r\nchoose policy.</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"margin: 12pt 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">The\r\nrespondent be directed to provide the list of total applicants and further, the\r\nlist to whom it has already allotted the plot along with the list of applicants\r\nto whom it has not allotted the plots till date. </span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"margin: 12pt 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">The\r\nrespondent be directed to provide the list of hypothecated plots which are\r\nhypothecated to GMADA, out of the approved 862 residential plots and 73\r\ncommercial plots. Also, the respondent be directed to provide the list of\r\nhypothected plots sold to general public.</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></li></ol><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:12.0pt;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:\r\n0in;margin-left:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:12.0pt;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:\r\n0in;margin-left:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;line-height:200%;\r\nmso-layout-grid-align:none;text-autospace:none\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'rerafilingformm','2019-03-06 17:42:27.000','rerafilingformm','2019-03-06 17:42:27.000'),(1160,1216,'1216',1141,'971b1ae7-f8bc-4323-80a7-088b81f8b7db','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-03-02 10:13:31.000','Suparna Randhawa','dpsrandhawa@hotmail.com',9914400088,0,0,'House No.229','Sector-16',6,128,'160015','1','House No. 253','Sector 4, Mansa Devi Complex',13,15,'134114','Sanjeev Gupta','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0093','PALM GARDEN','M/s Manohar Infrastructure & Constructions Pvt Ltd','nbs@manoharrealty.com',0,1725033524,'SCO 139-142','Sector-17C',6,128,'160017','1','SCO 139-142','Sector-17C',6,128,'160017','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:\r\njustify;line-height:200%;mso-layout-grid-align:none;text-autospace:none\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6667px;\">Plot measuring 500 sq yards@18500 per sq yards was booked by complainant in Palm Garden being developed by the respondent,vide application(C-1)dated 18.12.11 &amp; booking amount of Rs. 2775000 i.e. 30% of sale consideration was paid.Before purchasing the said plot,respondent had assured the complainant that it is having all the approvals for the development of project except layout plan approval which will be approved within 30 days &amp; possession be delivered within 2 years &amp; buyer’s agreement will executed within 3 months.It was assured that next installment would be demanded at the time of starting of development.Acknowledgment(C-2)dated 2.4.12 was issued.But inspite of repeated requests by the complainant,the respondent has failed to issue any allotment letter &amp; execute buyer’s agreement within the said period &amp; even till date.Many times complainant visited the office of respondent for getting the allotment letter &amp; buyer agreement but to no avail.There was no development on the site &amp; the respondent kept the complainant in dark about the approvals.Legal notice(C-3)dated 30.8.18 was sent to respondent for refund,in which sequence of events have been duly incorporated, which may kindly be treated as part of pleadings.After that complainant received a call from respondent who invited him to its office for redressal of his grievances.Accordingly, complainant went there in 3rd week of October,2018,where the respondent assured that allotment letter would be duly issued &amp; buyer’s agreement would also be executed if the complainant further deposit a sum of Rs. 1850000 i.e 20% sale consideration.But the complainant asked the respondent to first issue the allotment letter &amp; execute the agreement.Respondent refused to issue the same without getting any further amount.The complainant has been harassed for so many years due to unfair trade practices on the part of respondent.A list of dates of approvals(C-4)&amp; important approvals as(C-5 &amp;C-6).Complaint to vigilance for FIR as C-7</span></font></p>','<ol><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">To\r\ndirect the respondent to issue allotment letter in respect of 500 sq yard plot\r\nand execute the buyer’s agreement in compliance with Section 13 of RERA.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">To\r\nhand over the actual physical possession of the plot after issuing the\r\nallotment letter and execution of buyer’s agreement. The complainant is ready\r\nto pay the balance sale consideration. The respondent was not having any\r\nauthority to collect the money from general public before 25.1.2017. <o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">To\r\ndirect the respondent not to charge any other charges from the complainant\r\nexcept EDC and PLC (if any) since the plot was sold to the complainant @Rs18500/-\r\nper sq yards excluding EDC and PLC (if any).<o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">To\r\ndirect the respondent to pay interest at the rate as contemplated under Rule 16\r\nof Punjab RERA Rules, for the period of delay in delivering the possession to\r\nbe calculated from the committed date of possession i.e. 18.12.2013 till the\r\ndate of handing over the actual physical possession after obtaining the\r\ncompletion certificate. or in alternative to refund the amount with interest &amp; Compensation from the respective date of deposits.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">To\r\ntake action against the respondent under Section 61 of RERA for not complying\r\nthe provision of Section 13.Inspite of repeated\r\nrequest the respondent has not offered the buyer’s agreement even after getting itself registered under RERA rather it is\r\ndemanding more money for executing the same which is a clear violation of\r\nSection 13.The respondent was not even having any approval, rather it had not\r\neven applied the necessary permissions when the plot was sold to the\r\ncomplainant.The respondent got the exemption under Section 44 of PAPRA on\r\n25.1.2017.Before the said date it could not collect any money from general\r\npublic as per Annx C-5 &amp; C-6. In the present case the respondent collected the money from the\r\ncomplainant in 2011-12.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">To\r\ntake action against the respondent for collecting the money from the\r\ncomplainant before getting all the approvals and for indulging into unfair\r\ntrade practices.<o:p></o:p></span></li></ol><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:150%\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>',9250000.00,2775000.00,'2013-12-18 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<ol><li style=\"margin-left: 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">The\r\nrespondent be directed to issue the allotment letter to the complainant and\r\nexecute the buyer’s agreement in respect of 500 sq yards plot booked by the\r\ncomplainant.</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"margin: 12pt 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 20