r\nof 6 month from the date of execution of agreement the maximum period on or\r\nbefore i.e. 26-Jan-2018 but the respondent-1 failed to deliver the possession\r\ntill date even after taking the hefty amount from complainant of Rs.</span><span style=\"font-size:13.5pt;font-family:Garamond;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial\">85,62,767/-\r\nand also failed to pay &nbsp;the\r\npre-possession Emi to the respondent-2.</span><span style=\"font-size:13.5pt;\r\nmso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;font-family:Garamond\"> &nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:13.5pt;\r\nmso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;font-family:Garamond\">4.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; That the complainants approached several a times to the\r\nrespondent-1 to hand over the possession of the flat but respondent-1 failed to\r\nhand it over till date, and it is further submitted that project is not in\r\ncondition to hand over to the allottee in the absence of completion/occupation\r\ncertificate.<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:13.5pt;\r\nmso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;font-family:Garamond\">5. That having no other option the\r\ncomplainants are compelled to approach respected authority for getting refund\r\ntheir hard earned money along with interest as per norms of RERA.<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-family: Garamond; font-size: 13.5pt;\">&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size:13.5pt;\r\nmso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;font-family:Garamond\">&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:.25pt;margin-bottom:0in;\r\nmargin-left:.5in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size:12.5pt;line-height:200%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Calisto MT&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial\">A&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; To\r\nrefund the amount of Rs.</span><span style=\"font-size:13.5pt;line-height:200%;\r\nfont-family:Garamond;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial\">85,62,767</span><span style=\"font-size:12.5pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Calisto MT&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:\r\nArial\">/- along with 12% interest from the date of deposit till the date of\r\nrealization as per PAPRA Act.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:.25pt;margin-bottom:0in;\r\nmargin-left:.5in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size:12.5pt;line-height:200%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Calisto MT&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial\">B &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; To\r\nPay Rs5,00,000/- for deficiency and suffering of pain and mental harassment. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-right:.25pt;text-align:justify;line-height:\r\n200%\"><span style=\"font-size:12.5pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Calisto MT&quot;;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:Arial\">C&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; To\r\npay Rs 55,000/- as litigation charges.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-right:.25pt;text-align:justify;line-height:\r\n200%\"><span style=\"font-size:13.5pt;line-height:200%;font-family:Garamond;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:Arial\">Or any other order which this respected authority deems\r\nfit in the interest of justice.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:.25pt;margin-bottom:0in;\r\nmargin-left:.5in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;\r\nline-height:200%\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-right:.25pt;text-align:justify;line-height:\r\n200%\"><span style=\"font-size:13.5pt;line-height:200%;font-family:Garamond;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:Arial\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>',9374837.00,8562767.00,'2018-01-26 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-right:.25pt;text-align:justify;line-height:\r\n200%\"><span style=\"font-size:13.5pt;line-height:200%;font-family:Garamond;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:Arial\">1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; That\r\nis request to the respected&nbsp; authority to direct the respondent -1\r\nto pay Pre-Emi interest to the respondent-2 which was not paid by respondent 1 as\r\nper clause 3 of tripartite agreement from date of failure to pay &nbsp;&nbsp;till 26 Jan 2018.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','2015-01-27 00:00:00','Wave Gardens, Apartment No. 1101, F Freesia, 11th Floor, Type 3 BHK, Sector 85 & 89 District S.A.S Nagar, Punjab, Pin -140308','','',1,1,0,0,'advkulwindersingh','2019-03-07 13:12:04.000','advkulwindersingh','2019-03-07 13:12:04.000'),(1170,1352,'1352',1396,'01b8ddba-9dff-412e-8389-ef5e70711838','FormTypeM',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','SATISH SHARMA','SKSHARMAMOHALI@GMAIL.COM',9814536789,9814536789,562993606375,'859,GILLCO PALM,LANDRA KHARAR ROAD,MOHALI','NEAR NULIFE HOSPITAL',28,507,'140307','1','859,GILLCO PALM,LANDRA KHARAR ROAD,MOHALI','NEAR NULIFE HOSPITAL',28,507,'140307','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0067','Singla Builders and Promoters Limited','Raman Singla','raman@sbpgroup.in',9316004242,0,'Singla Builders and Promoters Limited SCO 146-148,','1st Floor, Sector 43-B,',6,128,'160022','1','Singla Builders and Promoters Limited SCO 146-148,','1st Floor, Sector 43-B,',6,128,'160022','1','<p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Dear Rera Seniors,</p><p>Greetings !</p><p>I have booked two flats i.e Flat no 619 &amp; 618 )in the name of Satish Kumar Sharma (Self) &amp; Kusum Sharma (Spouse) in Project&nbsp; SBP city of dreams ( RERA number –SAS 80-PR0067) , Landran Kharar Highway, Sector 116, Sahibzada Ajit Singh Nagar,Punjab. We have done total Rs. 4,65,800 payments of both flats through NEFT mode. (Receipts are attached).</p><p>I had to join a new company in the end of June 2018, Due to unavoidable circumstances, I could not join and then we had showed our disinterest to SBP sales team within 40-44 days i.e on 24th July,2018 in buying the property. ( All our mails &amp; SBP replies are attached herewith)</p><p>We have asked our refund but they have asked us to wait for further three months &amp; they (Sales head Mr.Amitendra Mishra &amp; Mr.Lovepret Singh –Sales Mgr ) have assured us to refund the amount, which we even took in our written mail. But now they are not showing interest in refunding our money.</p><p>In my recent visits, GM Sales Mr. Raman Singla is trying to behave smartly &amp; he asked me to meet his Sales head Amitendra Mishra . He is passing his responsibility to his employee because he was unable to give the reply. During meeting with SBP sales head Mr. Amitendra Mishra, he has told me when I was sitting in his cabin that he can throw me out of SBP office when I have asked him to return my hard earned money. He also warned me that he would call his legal team if I will further cross question for my money refund!! .He is therefore in the process of threatening the customers of the dire consequences.</p><p>Customer has the right to question regularly if he does not receive his/ her money!! This is the condition of SBP Sales head &amp; Real Estate Refund process in now days</p><p>It seems that this has become the new way of revenue generation in Real estate industry</p>','<p>Also, I want to share about this real estate industry working style. That Real Estate has a very good behavior only at the time of Sales but very rude &amp; unattended behavior during refund of money. Real estate has enough money for brunch activities &amp; also has enough money for refund cases but they have no time for refund processing. They feel confidence in their rudeness during customer‘s money refund queries.&nbsp;</p><p>In our case they were asking us to submit the bank statement again and again while we have already shown the disinterest in buying the property.</p><p>Please intervene in this long long pending case &amp; make immediate refund arrangement &amp; give&nbsp; them instructions to refund my money i.e&nbsp; Rs. 4,65,800 in a single go including&nbsp; interest for causing the mental&nbsp; harassment ( 15 visits in SBP 116 office from 20.06.2018 to 20 .2.2019), others&nbsp; as per Rera Act. We immediately required the money to pay our dues &amp; child fees. My account details are:</p><p>Satish Kumar Sharma</p><p>A/c no 00351050126867</p><p>Hdfc Bank,SCO 371-372 ,Sec 35B,Chandigarh</p><p>IFSC code HDFC0000035</p><p><br></p><p>Regards</p><p>Satish Sharma &amp; Kusum Sharma</p><p>Mohali&nbsp;</p><p>Mob 9814536789, 7009830848</p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Also, I want to share about this real estate industry working style. That Real Estate has a very good behavior only at the time of Sales but very rude &amp; unattended behavior during refund of money. Real estate has enough money for brunch activities &amp; also has enough money for refund cases but they have no time for refund processing. They feel confidence in their rudeness during customer‘s money refund queries.&nbsp;</p><p>In our case they were asking us to submit the bank statement again and again while we have already shown the disinterest in buying the property.</p><p>Please intervene in this long long pending case &amp; make immediate refund arrangement &amp; give&nbsp; them instructions to refund my money i.e&nbsp; Rs. 4,65,800 in a single go including&nbsp; interest for causing the mental&nbsp; harassment ( 15 visits in SBP 116 office from 20.06.2018 to 20 .2.2019), others&nbsp; as per Rera Act. We immediately required the money to pay our dues &amp; child fees. My account details are:</p><p>Satish Kumar Sharma</p><p>A/c no 00351050126867</p><p>Hdfc Bank,SCO 371-372 ,Sec 35B,Chandigarh</p><p>IFSC code HDFC0000035</p><p><br></p><p>Regards</p><p>Satish Sharma &amp; Kusum Sharma</p><p>Mohali&nbsp;</p><p>Mob 9814536789, 7009830848</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'SKSHARMAMOHALI','2019-03-07 16:20:40.000','SKSHARMAMOHALI','2019-03-07 16:20:40.000'),(1171,1353,'1353',1426,'c52fa8fb-ca9e-4d5d-9572-49b22b4f0748','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Puneet Bedi','adv.amansingla@yahoo.com',9915344358,0,0,'House No. 224','Sector 2',13,15,'134109','1','House No. 224','Sector 2',13,15,'134109','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-PTL65-PM0108','Parsavnath king Citi','Parsavnath Developer Limited','mail@parsavnath.com',0,0,'Parsvnath Tower, ','Near Shahdara Metro Station, Shahdara, Delhi ',10,436,'110032','1','Parsvnath Tower, ','Near Shahdara Metro Station, Shahdara, Delhi ',10,436,'110032','1','<p>abc</p>','<p>abc</p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>abc</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'Amansingla','2019-03-08 11:30:29.000','Amansingla','2019-03-08 11:30:29.000'),(1172,1353,'1353',1426,'c52fa8fb-ca9e-4d5d-9572-49b22b4f0748','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Puneet Bedi','adv.amansingla@yahoo.com',9915344358,0,0,'House No. 224','Sector 2',13,15,'134109','1','House No. 224','Sector 2',13,15,'134109','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-PTL65-PM0108','Parsavnath king Citi','Parsavnath Developer Limited','mail@parsavnath.com',0,0,'Parsvnath Tower, ','Near Shahdara Metro Station, Shahdara, Delhi ',10,436,'110032','1','Parsvnath Tower, ','Near Shahdara Metro Station, Shahdara, Delhi ',10,436,'110032','1','<p>1. One plot for a sale price of Rs. 21,27,102.50/- purchased from respondent no.1. As per the Plot Buyer Agreement dated 2.4.2007 the maintenance and upkeep of common areas and facilities will only be done by respondent no.1 or by nominee of respondent no.1 till the same is handed over to authority/local body. Respondent no.1 nominated and assigned the maintenance work of common areas and facilities to respondent no.2 and got executed an agreement regarding this on 8.4.2008.</p><p>2. Conveyance Deed executed 1.8.2008 in it is wrongly mentioned that physical, peaceful and vacant possession of the plot has been handed over to complainants. Physical and vacant possession of plot is not handed over to the complainants as no demarcation of plot in project done and complainants have no knowledge about whereabouts of their plot.</p><p>3. Respondent no.1 was liable to maintain the project itself and pay for all the outgoings till transferring possession of plots to allottee/allottees after proper demarcation. Respondent no.1 has transferred his liability of maintaining the project upon respondent no.2 so now respondent no. 2 shall also be treated as promoter of the project as per law.</p><p>4. The maintenance agreement was executed for 5 years which has expired in the year 2013 and thereafter the maintenance agreement has not been renewed till date.</p><p>5. The project has been stalled since long and no construction and maintenance work has been done on the project since long. Essential services and basic necessities which are essential for human habitat is not provided in the project. Respondents haven\'t spent a single penny on development, maintenance and upkeep of the project till date and the project bears a deserted look. No periphery wall of the project has been erected till date.</p><p>6. Respondent No.2 raising illegal demand for maintenance of project as complainants have not received physical possession and the agreement has expired.<br></p>','<p>In view of the facts mentioned in paragraph 4 above, the complainant prays for the following relief(s):</p><p><br></p><p>(a)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Stay of illegal demand notices for maintenance and upkeep charges by respondent no. 2;</p><p>(b)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Respondent No. 1 and Respondent No. 2 be restrained from charging maintenance and upkeep charges from the complainants till the completion of project, completion and occupancy certificate is provided to complainants, demarcation of plots are done in the project and physical and vacant possession of plot no. 549 is handed over to complainants;</p><p>(c)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Respondents be directed to provide Sold and Unsold inventories to the complainants;</p><p>(d)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Respondents be directed to provide Internal Development work which is Annexure II of Plot Buyer Agreement dated 02.04.2007 to the complainants;</p><p>(e)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Respondents be directed to provide Initial Layout Plans of the Project which is Annexure IV of Plot Buyer Agreement dated 02.04.2007 to the complainants;</p><p>(f)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Respondents be directed to place on record Initial Prospectus/Brochure/ Launching Advertisement;</p><p>(g)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Litigation costs of Rs. 51,000/-.</p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Pending final decision on the complaint the complainant seeks issue of the following interim order:</p><p>(a)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Interim Stay of illegal demand notices for maintenance and upkeep charges by respondent no. 2.</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'Amansingla','2019-03-08 11:36:01.000','Amansingla','2019-03-08 11:36:01.000'),(1173,1352,'1352',1396,'01b8ddba-9dff-412e-8389-ef5e70711838','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-03-10 12:13:54.000','SATISH SHARMA','SKSHARMAMOHALI@GMAIL.COM',9814536789,9814536789,562993606375,'859,GILLCO PALM,LANDRA KHARAR ROAD,MOHALI','NEAR NULIFE HOSPITAL',28,507,'140307','1','859,GILLCO PALM,LANDRA KHARAR ROAD,MOHALI','NEAR NULIFE HOSPITAL',28,507,'140307','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0067','Singla Builders and Promoters Limited','Raman Singla','raman@sbpgroup.in',9316004242,0,'Singla Builders and Promoters Limited SCO 146-148,','1st Floor, Sector 43-B,',6,128,'160022','1','Singla Builders and Promoters Limited SCO 146-148,','1st Floor, Sector