stry working style. That Real Estate has a very good behavior only at the time of Sales but very rude &amp; unattended behavior during refund of money. Real estate has enough money for brunch activities &amp; also has enough money for refund cases but they have no time for refund processing. They feel confidence in their rudeness during customer‘s money refund queries.&nbsp;</p><p>In our case they were asking us to submit the bank statement again and again while we have already shown the disinterest in buying the property.</p><p>Please intervene in this long long pending case &amp; make immediate refund arrangement &amp; give&nbsp; them instructions to refund my money i.e&nbsp; Rs. 4,65,800 in a single go including&nbsp; interest for causing the mental&nbsp; harassment ( 15 visits in SBP 116 office from 20.06.2018 to 20 .2.2019), others&nbsp; as per Rera Act. We immediately required the money to pay our dues &amp; child fees. My account details are:</p><p>Satish Kumar Sharma</p><p>A/c no 00351050126867</p><p>Hdfc Bank,SCO 371-372 ,Sec 35B,Chandigarh</p><p>IFSC code HDFC0000035</p><p><br></p><p>Regards</p><p>Satish Sharma &amp; Kusum Sharma</p><p>Mohali&nbsp;</p><p>Mob 9814536789, 7009830848</p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Also, I want to share about this real estate industry working style. That Real Estate has a very good behavior only at the time of Sales but very rude &amp; unattended behavior during refund of money. Real estate has enough money for brunch activities &amp; also has enough money for refund cases but they have no time for refund processing. They feel confidence in their rudeness during customer‘s money refund queries.&nbsp;</p><p>In our case they were asking us to submit the bank statement again and again while we have already shown the disinterest in buying the property.</p><p>Please intervene in this long long pending case &amp; make immediate refund arrangement &amp; give them instructions to refund or money i.e&nbsp; Rs. 4,65,800 in a single go including&nbsp; interest@ 24 % &amp; also 1 lac for causing the mental&nbsp; harassment ( 15 visits in SBP 116 office from 20.06.2018 to 20 .2.2019), others&nbsp; as per Rera Act. We immediately required the money to pay our dues &amp; child fees. My account details are:</p><p>Satish Kumar Sharma</p><p>A/c no 00351050126867</p><p>Hdfc Bank,SCO 371-372 ,Sec 35B,Chandigarh</p><p>IFSC code HDFC0000035</p><p><br></p><p>Regards</p><p>Satish Sharma &amp; Kusum Sharma</p><p>Mohali&nbsp;</p><p>Mob 9814536789, 7009830848</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',1,1,0,0,'SKSHARMAMOHALI','2019-03-08 19:31:22.000','SKSHARMAMOHALI','2019-03-08 19:31:22.000'),(1174,1223,'1223',1299,'f05423d6-8aeb-41cc-9669-749a50a90d4d','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-02-20 16:50:30.000','VICKY  FRANCIS','vf18jan@gmail.com',9996767263,0,0,'217 Rajesh Colony','Near old court',13,21,'135003','1','253','Sector 4, Mansa Devi Complex',13,1,'134114','Sanjeev Gupta','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PM0004','Falcon View Apartments','Janta Land Promoters Pvt. Ltd.','janta@jantahousing.com',0,0,'SCO 39-42','Sector 82 JLPL',28,507,'140306','1','SCO 39-42','Sector 82 JLPL',28,507,'140306','1','<p>The complainants agreed to purchase the Apartment No. E-1402, Facing Green in Wing “E” at 14th Floor in (Super Mega) Falcon View, Phase-1, Sector 66-A, Mohali for an amount of Rs. 96,92,942/-. Annexure C-1 Allotment letter \r\n</p><p>After the authorized representatives of the respondent builder committed that they will complete and handover the apartment within 18 months and there is also possibility that they will hand over prior to the committed date.\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>And thereafter the complainants paid the booking amount of Rs. 11,00,000/- to the respondent on 23.06.2015 vide receipt no. 3055. The copy of the receipt dated 23.06.2015 is appended herewith as Annexure C-2. \r\n</p><p>The complainants chose the Down Payment Plan . The payment plan is reproduced here as under for the kind perusal of this Hon’ble Court:\r\n</p><p>S. No.	Due Dates	Payment\r\n</p><p>1	17.08.2015	Rs. 81,17,540/- (BSP) + Rs. 2,00,000/- (Car Parking Charges) + applicable service tax on date\r\n</p><p>2.	On the delivery of possession	Rs. 5,19,140/- (Balance 5% BSP) + Rs. 1,50,650/- (IFMS) + Rs. 1,80,780/- (Club Charges) + 45,195/- (Power backup) + applicable service tax on date\r\n</p><p>&nbsp;G. Total	Rs. 86,36,680/- (Basic) + Rs. 5,76,625/- (Other Charges) + along with applicable service tax on date\r\n</p><p>\r\nThat it is the admitted fact that the complainants had made the payment of Rs. 86,86,477/- BSP along with all the applicable taxes on 27.08.2015. The copy of the receipts dated 27.08.2015 is appended herewith as Annexure C-3.&nbsp;</p><p>That it is submitted that as per the clause 2.24 of the allotment letter, the respondent was to deliver the possession of the apartment within 18 months from the date of issue of allotment letter i.e. on or before 22.12.2016. \r\n</p><p>The contentions of the complainant is that despite having paid 95% of the BSP and additional Rs 2000,00 as car parking charges along with the applicable service charges i.e Total of Rs 97,86,477 well within time, He has still not been offered possession of the flat which was to be completed by 23.12.2016</p>','<ul><li>To direct the respondent to complete the development&nbsp; &nbsp;of project and construction of the apartment and deliver the possession of it along with all the facilities.</li><li>Interest on the payment paid by the complainant till the date of delivery of possession of the apartment as prescribed by the act.</li><li>A compensation of Rs 500.000 for the inconvenience caused and the the mental agony faced</li></ul>',10268967.00,9786477.00,'2016-12-22 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<ul><li>To direct the respondent to complete the development&nbsp; &nbsp;of project and construction of the apartment and deliver the possession of it along with all the facilities.</li></ul>','1','','2018-06-23 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','1402 E Wing Falcon View\r\nSector 66-A Mohali','','',2,0,0,0,'vf18jan','2019-03-08 20:03:05.000','vf18jan','2019-03-08 20:03:05.000'),(1175,1223,'1223',1299,'f05423d6-8aeb-41cc-9669-749a50a90d4d','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-02-20 16:50:30.000','VICKY  FRANCIS','vf18jan@gmail.com',9996767263,0,0,'217 Rajesh Colony','Near old court',13,21,'135003','1','253','Sector 4, Mansa Devi Complex',13,1,'134114','Sanjeev Gupta','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PM0004','Falcon View Apartments','Janta Land Promoters Pvt. Ltd.','janta@jantahousing.com',0,0,'SCO 39-42','Sector 82 JLPL',28,507,'140306','1','SCO 39-42','Sector 82 JLPL',28,507,'140306','1','<p>The complainants agreed to purchase the Apartment No. E-1402, Facing Green in Wing “E” at 14th Floor in (Super Mega) Falcon View, Phase-1, Sector 66-A, Mohali for an amount of Rs. 96,92,942/-. Annexure C-1 Allotment letter \r\n</p><p>After the authorized representatives of the respondent builder committed that they will complete and handover the apartment within 18 months and there is also possibility that they will hand over prior to the committed date.\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>And thereafter the complainants paid the booking amount of Rs. 11,00,000/- to the respondent on 23.06.2015 vide receipt no. 3055. The copy of the receipt dated 23.06.2015 is appended herewith as Annexure C-2. \r\n</p><p>The complainants chose the Down Payment Plan . The payment plan is reproduced here as under for the kind perusal of this Hon’ble Court:\r\n</p><p>S. No.	Due Dates	Payment\r\n</p><p>1	17.08.2015	Rs. 81,17,540/- (BSP) + Rs. 2,00,000/- (Car Parking Charges) + applicable service tax on date\r\n</p><p>2.	On the delivery of possession	Rs. 5,19,140/- (Balance 5% BSP) + Rs. 1,50,650/- (IFMS) + Rs. 1,80,780/- (Club Charges) + 45,195/- (Power backup) + applicable service tax on date\r\n</p><p>&nbsp;G. Total	Rs. 86,36,680/- (Basic) + Rs. 5,76,625/- (Other Charges) + along with applicable service tax on date\r\n</p><p>\r\nThat it is the admitted fact that the complainants had made the payment of Rs. 86,86,477/- BSP along with all the applicable taxes on 27.08.2015. The copy of the receipts dated 27.08.2015 is appended herewith as Annexure C-3.&nbsp;</p><p>That it is submitted that as per the clause 2.24 of the allotment letter, the respondent was to deliver the possession of the apartment within 18 months from the date of issue of allotment letter i.e. on or before 22.12.2016. \r\n</p><p>The contentions of the complainant is that despite having paid 95% of the BSP and additional Rs 2000,00 as car parking charges along with the applicable service charges i.e Total of Rs 97,86,477 well within time, He has still not been offered possession of the flat which was to be completed by 23.12.2016</p>','<ul><li>To direct the respondent to handover the actual physical possession of the said apartment complete in all aspects, after obtaining the occupancy certificate.</li><li>To direct the respondent to complete the development&nbsp; of project and construction of the apartment and deliver the possession of it along with all the facilities.</li><li>Interest on the payment paid by the complainant till the date of delivery of possession of the apartment as prescribed by the act.</li><li>A compensation of Rs 500.000 for the inconvenience caused and the the mental agony faced</li></ul>',10268967.00,9786477.00,'2016-12-22 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<ul><li>To direct the respondent to complete the development&nbsp; &nbsp;of project and construction of the apartment and deliver the possession of it along with all the facilities.</li></ul>','1','','2018-06-23 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','1402 E Wing Falcon View\r\nSector 66-A Mohali','','',2,0,0,0,'vf18jan','2019-03-08 20:05:50.000','vf18jan','2019-03-08 20:05:50.000'),(1176,1223,'1223',1299,'f05423d6-8aeb-41cc-9669-749a5