roject mid-way on discretion. Could change\r\nsite plan/dimensions without intimation. No remedy for delay in possession.\r\nLate payments charged at 18%. These terms were unacceptable &amp; asked for\r\nchange. All terms were in their favour. Sanctioned/ layout plan/ stage wise\r\nschedule not given.On 18.02.18 Complainant decided to cancel allotment citing\r\nthese reasons.they requested this will send bad name to project &amp; requested\r\nto cite other reason &amp; they will refund in full. They typed a letter in\r\noffice citing reason as professional- complainant constrained to sign<b>(C4)</b>.They\r\nsaid they will issue cheque in name of Prashant &amp; sought email from Shilpa.\r\nSent<b>(C5).</b> But no refund.Complainant visited them many times for refund.\r\nThey assured full return but did not.No loss to them. When we requested them to\r\ngive booked flat back, they said sold &amp; is no longer available<b>(C6)</b>.Cannot\r\nforfeit whole amount of 1028000. At best respondents can forfeit only part of booking/earnest\r\namount of 100,000.Unilateral agreement- not signed by respondents-hence cannot\r\nbe termed agreement.Written in their application that Receipt of application &amp;\r\nbooking Does not confirm allotment. Meaning, allotment not made till then.Hard earned\r\nmoney of complainants. Respondents cannot be allowed to usurp.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"margin-left:1.0cm;mso-add-space:auto;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-indent:-1.0cm;mso-text-indent-alt:-35.45pt;line-height:\r\n200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-US\">The\r\ncomplainant has suffered losses by reason of false and incorrect commitment\r\nmade by the respondents. Thus, the respondents are liable to cancel the booking\r\nof the flat and return the amount of ₹ 10,28,280 along with interest.</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;</span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; color: rgb(26, 26, 26);\">Interest as provided under </span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">Section\r\n18 and 19(4) of the RERA Act r/w </span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; color: rgb(26, 26, 26);\">Rule 16 of the Regulation and Development Rules\r\n2017 on the above Principal amount from the respective dates it was paid to the\r\nrespondent till the date of payment ie State Bank of India’s (“SBI”) highest\r\nMarginal Cost of Lending Rate (“MCLR”) plus 2%. The current SBI MCLR is 8.50%\r\npa so applicable interest rate for the refund is taken as 10.50% pa.&nbsp;</span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(26, 26, 26);\">Compensation\r\nfor Mental harassment to the tune of Rs. 1,00,000/-</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">To\r\nissue direction to pay the cost of litigation ie ₹ 44,000/-.</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</span></span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">To\r\nimpose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 60 of RERA\r\nAct for willful default committed by them.</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;</span></span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">To\r\nimpose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 61 of RERA\r\nAct for contravention of Sec.12, Sec.14, and Sec. 16 of RERA Act.</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;</span></span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">To\r\nissue directions to make liable every officer concerned i.e. Director, Manager,\r\nSecretary, or any other officer of the respondent’s company at whose instance,\r\nconnivance, acquiescence, neglect any of the offences has been committed as\r\nmentioned in Sec.69 of RERA Act, 2016 to be read with Punjab RERA Rules, 2017.</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;</span></span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">To\r\nrecommend criminal action against the respondents for the criminal offence of\r\ncheating, fraud and criminal breach of trust under section 420, 406 and 409 of\r\nthe Indian Penal Code.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Any\r\nother relief which this Hon’ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of\r\nthe facts and circumstances of this complaint.</span></p>',11125760.00,1028000.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-ansi-language:EN-US\">No\r\ninterim relief is being sought. The complainants only pray that the promoters\r\nbe directed to return the amount paid with interest.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Apartment 9012 Building no. 9','','',2,0,0,0,'Prashantshilpa','2019-03-11 15:28:22.000','Prashantshilpa','2019-03-11 15:28:22.000'),(1188,1353,'1353',1426,'c52fa8fb-ca9e-4d5d-9572-49b22b4f0748','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-03-11 16:08:01.000','Puneet Bedi','adv.amansingla@yahoo.com',9915344358,0,0,'House No. 224','Sector 2',13,15,'134109','1','House No. 224','Sector 2',13,15,'134109','Aman Singla','adv.amansingla@yahoo.com',9915344358,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-PTL65-PM0108','Parsavnath king Citi','Parsavnath Developer Limited','mail@parsavnath.com',9560110741,0,'Parsvnath Tower, ','Near Shahdara Metro Station, Shahdara, Delhi ',10,436,'110032','1','Parsvnath Tower, ','Near Shahdara Metro Station, Shahdara, Delhi ',10,436,'110032','1','<p>1. One plot for a sale price of Rs. 21,27,102.50/- purchased from respondent no.1. As per the Plot Buyer Agreement dated 2.4.2007 the maintenance and upkeep of common areas and facilities will only be done by respondent no.1 or by nominee of respondent no.1 till the same is handed over to authority/local body. Respondent no.1 nominated and assigned the maintenance work of common areas and facilities to respondent no.2 (formerly known as M/s Basundra Properties Pvt. Ltd.) and got executed an agreement regarding this on 8.4.2008.</p><p>2. Conveyance Deed executed 1.8.2008 in it is wrongly mentioned that physical, peaceful and vacant possession of the plot has been handed over to complainants. Physical and vacant possession of plot is not handed over to the complainants as no demarcation of plot in project done and complainants have no knowledge about whereabouts of their plot.</p><p>3. Respondent no.1 was liable to maintain the project itself and pay for all the outgoings till transferring possession of plots to allottee/allottees after proper demarcation. Respondent no.1 has transferred his liability of maintaining the project upon respondent no.2 so now respondent no. 2 shall also be treated as promoter of the project as per law.</p><p>4. The maintenance agreement was executed for 5 years which has expired in the year 2013 and thereafter the maintenance agreement has not been renewed till date.</p><p>5. The project has been stalled since long and no construction and maintenance work has been done on the project since long. Essential services and basic necessities which are essential for human habitat is not provided in the project. Respondents haven\'t spent a single penny on development, maintenance and upkeep of the project till date and the project bears a deserted look. No periphery wall of the project has been erected till date.</p><p>6. Respondent No.2 raising illegal demand for maintenance of project as complainants have not received physical possession and the agreement has expired.<br></p>','<p>In view of the facts mentioned in paragraph 4 above, the complainant prays for the following relief(s):</p><p><br></p><p>(a)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Stay of illegal demand notices for maintenance and upkeep charges by respondent no. 2;</p><p>(b)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Respondent No. 1 and Respondent No. 2 be restrained from charging maintenance and upkeep charges from the complainants till the completion of project, completion and occupancy certificate is provided to complainants, demarcation of plots are done in the project and physical and vacant possession of plot no. 549 is handed over to complainants;</p><p>(c)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Respondents be directed to provide Sold and Unsold inventories to the complainants;</p><p>(d)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Respondents be directed to provide Internal Development work which is Annexure II of Plot Buyer Agreement dated 02.04.2007 to the complainants;</p><p>(e)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Respondents be directed to provide Initial Layout Plans of the Project which is Annexure IV of Plot Buyer Agreement dated 02.04.2007 to the complainants;</p><p>(f)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Respondents be directed to place on record Initial Prospectus/Brochure/ Launching Advertisement;</p><p>(g)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Litigation costs of Rs. 51,000/-.</p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Pending final decision on the complaint the complainant seeks issue of the following interim order:</p><p>(a)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Interim Stay of illegal demand notices for maintenance and upkeep charges by respondent no. 2.</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'Amansingla','2019-03-11 16:07:36.000','Amansingla','2019-03-11 16:07:36.000'),(1189,1340,'1340',1245,'3f889bdc-3ee0-4229-87d4-71be8592f729','FormTypeM',1,1,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Prashant Gajanan Pathak','advamitgoyal@hotmail.com',9527700001,0,0,'Flat no. 603, Lotus Tower, Bollywood Heights,','Near sector-20 Panchkula Peer Machalla, Dhakoli, ',28,507,'140603','1','Flat no. 603, Lotus Tower, Bollywood Heights,','Near sector-20 Panchkula Peer Machalla, Dhakoli, ',28,507,'140603','Amit Goyal','advamitgoyal@hotmail.com',9527700001,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0086','ATS CASA ESPANA','ATS INFRABUILD PVT. LTD','email@atsgreens.com',0,1203811500,'ATS CASA ESPANA ','Village Bad Majra, Sector 121 SAS Nagar',28,507,'140307','1','ATS CASA ESPANA ','Village Bad Majra, Sector 121 SAS Nagar',28,507,'140307','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%\">Complainants relied on\r\nfalse promises &amp; signed </span><b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">Application\r\nfor Allotment </span></b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">on 10.12.17<b>(C1)</b>. Paid Rs 100,000\r\nas <b>booking amount(C2)</b>. Asked to pay 928,280 as installment. Complainant asked\r\nfor <b>Agreement To Sell</b> &amp; T&amp;C.\r\nThey said formalities could be done later. Installment paid on 02.01.18 <b>(C3).</b>They\r\nasked further payments. Complainant asked for agreement. But no response.\r\nComplainants requested them to execute agreement- they kept prolonging –didn’t\r\neven show agreement- therefore we were unable to raise loan.On 12.02.18\r\ncomplainant called to sign agreement. Advance copy not given. went to their\r\noffice on 17.02.18. shocked on reading agreement. Not as per RERA. No exit\r\nclause for allotee. Promoter could leave project mid-way on discretion. Could change\r\nsite plan/dimensions without intimation. No remedy for delay in possession.\r\nLate payments charged at 18%. These terms were unacceptable &amp; asked for\r\nchange. All terms were in their favour. Sanctioned/ layout plan/ stage wise\r\nschedule not given.On 18.02.18 Complainant decided to cancel allotment citing\r\nthese reasons.they requested this will send bad name to project &amp; requested\r\nto cite other reason &amp; they will refund in full. They typed a letter in\r\noffice citing reason as professional- complainant constrained to sign<b>(C4)</b>.They\r\nsaid they will issue cheque in name of Prashant &amp; sought email from Shilpa.\r\nSent<b>(C5).</b> But no refund.Complainant visited them many times for refund.\r\nThey assured full return but did not.No loss to them. When we requested them to\r\ngive booked flat back, they said sold &amp; is no longer available<b>(C6)</b>.Cannot\r\nforfeit whole amount of 1028000. At best respondents can forfeit only part of booking/earnest\r\namount of 100,000.Unilateral agreement- not signed by respondents-hence cannot\r\nbe termed agreement.Written in their application that Receipt of application &amp;\r\nbooking Does not confirm allotment. Meaning, allotment not made till then.Hard earned\r\nmoney of complainants. Respondents cannot be allowed to usurp.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"margin-left:1.0cm;mso-add-space:auto;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-indent:-1.0cm;mso-text-indent-alt:-35.45pt;line-height:\r\n200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-US\">The\r\ncomplainant has suffered losses by reason of false and incorrect commitment\r\nmade by the respondents. Thus, the respondents are liable to cancel the booking\r\nof the flat and return the amount of ₹ 10,28,280 along with interest.</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;</span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; color: rgb(26, 26, 26);\">Interest as provided under </span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">Section\r\n18 and 19(4) of the RERA Act r/w </span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; color: rgb(26, 26, 26);\">Rule 16 of the Regulation and Development Rules\r\n2017 on the above Principal amount from the respective dates it was paid to the\r\nrespondent till the date of payment ie State Bank of India’s (“SBI”) highest\r\nMarginal Cost of Lending Rate (“MCLR”) plus 2%. The current SBI MCLR is 8.50%\r\npa so applicable interest rate for the refund is taken as 10.50% pa.&nbsp;</span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(26, 26, 26);\">Compensation\r\nfor Mental harassment to the tune of Rs. 1,00,000/-</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">To\r\nissue direction to pay the cost of litigation ie ₹ 44,000/-.</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</span></span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">To\r\nimpose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 60 of RERA\r\nAct for willful default committed by them.</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;</span></span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">To\r\nimpose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 61 of RERA\r\nAct for contravention of Sec.12, Sec.14, and Sec. 16 of RERA Act.</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;</span></span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">To\r\nissue directions to make liable every officer concerned i.e. Director, Manager,\r\nSecretary, or any other officer of the respondent’s company at whose instance,\r\nconnivance, acquiescence, neglect any of the offences has been committed as\r\nmentioned in Sec.69 of RERA Act, 2016 to be read with Punjab RERA Rules, 2017.</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;</span></span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">To\r\nrecommend criminal action against the respondents for the criminal offence of\r\ncheating, fraud and criminal breach of trust under section 420, 406 and 409 of\r\nthe Indian Penal Code.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Any\r\nother relief which this Hon’ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of\r\nthe facts and circumstances of this complaint.</span></p>',11125760.00,1028000.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-ansi-language:EN-US\">No\r\ninterim relief is being sought. The complainants only pray that the promoters\r\nbe directed to return the amount paid with interest.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Apartment 9012 Building no. 9','','',2,0,0,0,'Prashantshilpa','2019-03-11 17:44:46.000','Prashantshilpa','2019-03-11 17:44:46.000'),(1190,1340,'1340',1245,'3f889bdc-3ee0-4229-87d4-71be8592f729','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-03-11 17:48:51.000','Prashant Gajanan Pathak','advamitgoyal@hotmail.com',9527700001,0,0,'Flat no. 603, Lotus Tower, Bollywood Heights,','Near sector-20 Panchkula Peer Machalla, Dhakoli, ',28,507,'140603','1','Flat no. 603, Lotus Tower, Bollywood Heights,','Near sector-20 Panchkula Peer Machalla, Dhakoli, ',28,507,'140603','Amit Goyal','advamitgoyal@hotmail.com',9527700001,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0086','ATS CASA ESPANA','ATS INFRABUILD PVT. LTD','email@atsgreens.com',0,1203811500,'ATS CASA ESPANA ','Village Bad Majra, Sector 121 SAS Nagar',28,507,'140307','1','ATS CASA ESPANA ','Village Bad Majra, Sector 121 SAS Nagar',28,507,'140307','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%\">Complainants relied on\r\nfalse promises &amp; signed </span><b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">Application\r\nfor Allotment </span></b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:\r\n200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">on 10.12.17<b>(C1)</b>. Paid Rs 100,000\r\nas <b>booking amount(C2)</b>. Asked to pay 928,280 as installment. Complainant asked\r\nfor <b>Agreement To Sell</b> &amp; T&amp;C.\r\nThey said formalities could be done later. Installment paid on 02.01.18 <b>(C3).</b>They\r\nasked further payments. Complainant asked for agreement. But no response.\r\nComplainants requested them to execute agreement- they kept prolonging –didn’t\r\neven show agreement- therefore we were unable to raise loan.On 12.02.18\r\ncomplainant called to sign agreement. Advance copy not given. went to their\r\noffice on 17.02.18. shocked on reading agreement. Not as per RERA. No exit\r\nclause for allotee. Promoter could leave project mid-way on discretion. Could change\r\nsite plan/dimensions without intimation. No remedy for delay in possession.\r\nLate payments charged at 18%. These terms were unacceptable &amp; asked for\r\nchange. All terms were in their favour. Sanctioned/ layout plan/ stage wise\r\nschedule not given.On 18.02.18 Complainant decided to cancel allotment citing\r\nthese reasons.they requested this will send bad name to project &amp; requested\r\nto cite other reason &amp; they will refund in full. They typed a letter in\r\noffice citing reason as professional- complainant constrained to sign<b>(C4)</b>.They\r\nsaid they will issue cheque in name of Prashant &amp; sought email from Shilpa.\r\nSent<b>(C5).</b> But no refund.Complainant visited them many times for refund.\r\nThey assured full return but did not.No loss to them. When we requested them to\r\ngive booked flat back, they said sold &amp; is no longer available<b>(C6)</b>.Cannot\r\nforfeit whole amount of 1028000. At best respondents can forfeit only part of booking/earnest\r\namount of 100,000.Unilateral agreement- not signed by respondents-hence cannot\r\nbe termed agreement.Written in their application that Receipt of application &amp;\r\nbooking Does not confirm allotment. Meaning, allotment not made till then.Hard earned\r\nmoney of complainants. Respondents cannot be allowed to usurp.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"margin-left:1.0cm;mso-add-space:auto;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-indent:-1.0cm;mso-text-indent-alt:-35.45pt;line-height:\r\n200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-ansi-language:EN-US\">The\r\ncomplainant has suffered losses by reason of false and incorrect commitment\r\nmade by the respondents. Thus, the respondents are liable to cancel the booking\r\nof the flat and return the amount of ₹ 10,28,280 along with interest.</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;</span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; color: rgb(26, 26, 26);\">Interest as provided under </span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">Section\r\n18 and 19(4) of the RERA Act r/w </span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; color: rgb(26, 26, 26);\">Rule 16 of the Regulation and Development Rules\r\n2017 on the above Principal amount from the respective dates it was paid to the\r\nrespondent till the date of payment ie State Bank of India’s (“SBI”) highest\r\nMarginal Cost of Lending Rate (“MCLR”) plus 2%. The current SBI MCLR is 8.50%\r\npa so applicable interest rate for the refund is taken as 10.50% pa.&nbsp;</span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(26, 26, 26);\">Compensation\r\nfor Mental harassment to the tune of Rs. 1,00,000/-</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">To\r\nissue direction to pay the cost of litigation ie ₹ 44,000/-.</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</span></span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">To\r\nimpose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 60 of RERA\r\nAct for willful default committed by them.</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;</span></span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">To\r\nimpose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 61 of RERA\r\nAct for contravention of Sec.12, Sec.14, and Sec. 16 of RERA Act.</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;</span></span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">To\r\nissue directions to make liable every officer concerned i.e. Director, Manager,\r\nSecretary, or any other officer of the respondent’s company at whose instance,\r\nconnivance, acquiescence, neglect any of the offences has been committed as\r\nmentioned in Sec.69 of RERA Act, 2016 to be read with Punjab RERA Rules, 2017.</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;</span></span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">To\r\nrecommend criminal action against the respondents for the criminal offence of\r\ncheating, fraud and criminal breach of trust under section 420, 406 and 409 of\r\nthe Indian Penal Code.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"text-indent: -1cm; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; font-size: 14pt;\">Any\r\nother relief which this Hon’ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of\r\nthe facts and circumstances of this complaint.</span></p>',11125760.00,1028000.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;mso-ansi-language:EN-US\">No\r\ninterim relief is being sought. The complainants only pray that the promoters\r\nbe directed to return the amount paid with interest.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Apartment 9012 Building no. 9','','',1,1,0,0,'Prashantshilpa','2019-03-11 17:48:11.000','Prashantshilpa','2019-03-11 17:48:11.000'),(1191,1280,'1280',1253,'70b12b4c-e79c-4d06-9369-5f060352ed65','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-01-28 20:05:38.000','Tejbir Singh Sawhney','tssawhney@yahoo.com',9876604020,0,0,'Flat No 2302, Wing A, Ajmera Zeon','Ajmera I-Land, Bhakti Park, Anik Wadala Link Road, Wadala East',21,400,'400037','1','Flat No 2302, Wing A, Ajmera Zeon','Ajmera I-Land, Bhakti Park, Anik Wadala Link Road, Wadala East',21,400,'400037','Ankit Chowdhri','ankit_chowdhri@hotmail.com',9814433585,1724630585,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PM0004','Falcon View Apartments \r\nTower C','Janta Land Promoters Pvt Ltd ','janta@jantahousing.com',0,0,'SCO 39 - 42 , Sector 82 ','SAS Nagar , Mohali ',28,507,'140306','1','SCO 39 - 42 , Sector 82 ','SAS Nagar , Mohali ',28,507,'140306','1','<p>i)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That the Respondent was engaged in the development of the Super Mega Mixed Use Integrated Industrial Park Project of 263.38 acre of land in sector 66 – A,82 and 83, Mohali.&nbsp;</p><p>ii)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That the Applicant had applied for allotment of one 4 BHk flat in the above sated project vide application form dated 01.06.2013 which is annexed herewith as Annexure C-1.</p><p>iii)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That in reference thereof the applicant was allotted a Unit No./ Apartment No. C-901 in the above-mentioned project along with a construction linked plan vide an allotment letter 27.04.2013 which is annexed herewith as Annexure C-2.</p><p>iv)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>The as per the Construction Linked Installment Plan appended to the aforesaid Agreement in pursuance wherein the applicant was required to pay Rs.1,08,43,200/- out of which the complainant had already paid Rs.27,94,563/- (Principal Rs.26,94,595/- and Service Tax of Rs.99,968/-) vide receipts Nos. 4422 and 4889 dated 01.06.2013 and 18.07.2013 respectively.&nbsp; An amount of Rs.10,934,794.00/- was paid by the Applicant to the Respondent upto 21.02.2018 as reflected in the flat holders card annexed herewith as Annexure C-3.</p><p>v)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That the respondent was to hand over possession within 30 months from date of allotment As per Clause 2.24 of Annexure C-2 which has not been complied with till date despite repeated reminders.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>vi)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That finally reminder dated 02.10.2018 vide email is annexed herewith as Annexure C-4 to no avail.</p><p>vii)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That aggrieved therewith the applicant seeks to invoke the jurisdiction of this Hon’ble forum for relief as the provisions of RERA have been violated owing to undue delay in delivery of possession of the flat to the complainant.&nbsp;</p><div><br></div>','<p>i)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To direct the respondent to deliver the flat to the complainant immediately without any increased charges.</p><p>ii)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To direct the respondent to pay interest on the Amount of Rs.1,09,34,794/- i.e. the payment made by the applicant till date as prescribed by the Act and the Rules framed there under.&nbsp;</p><p>iii)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To waive off GST applicable on the outstanding amount.</p><p>iv)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To issue directions to pay cost of litigation so incurred by the complainant to the tune of Rs.2,00,000/-.</p><p>v)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To issue direction to pay compensation to the complainant for the compensation for his mental agony, pain and harassment to the tune of Rs.5,00,000/-.&nbsp;</p><p>vi)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Any other relief which the Applicant is entitled for under the Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Act, 2016 and the Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017.&nbsp;</p><div><br></div>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>To direct the respondent to deliver the flat to the complainant immediately without any increased charges.</p><p><br></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'AnkitChowdhri','2019-03-12 18:00:20.000','AnkitChowdhri','2019-03-12 18:00:20.000'),(1192,1280,'1280',1253,'70b12b4c-e79c-4d06-9369-5f060352ed65','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-01-28 20:05:38.000','Tejbir Singh Sawhney','tssawhney@yahoo.com',9876604020,0,0,'Flat No 2302, Wing A, Ajmera Zeon','Ajmera I-Land, Bhakti Park, Anik Wadala Link Road, Wadala East',21,400,'400037','1','Flat No 2302, Wing A, Ajmera Zeon','Ajmera I-Land, Bhakti Park, Anik Wadala Link Road, Wadala East',21,400,'400037','Ankit Chowdhri','ankit_chowdhri@hotmail.com',9814433585,1724630585,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PM0004','Falcon View Apartments \r\nTower C','Janta Land Promoters Pvt Ltd ','janta@jantahousing.com',0,0,'SCO 39 - 42 , Sector 82 ','SAS Nagar , Mohali ',28,507,'140306','1','SCO 39 - 42 , Sector 82 ','SAS Nagar , Mohali ',28,507,'140306','1','<p>i)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That the Respondent was engaged in the development of the Super Mega Mixed Use Integrated Industrial Park Project of 263.38 acre of land in sector 66 – A,82 and 83, Mohali.&nbsp;</p><p>ii)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That the Applicant had applied for allotment of one 4 BHk flat in the above sated project vide application form dated 01.06.2013 which is annexed herewith as Annexure C-1.</p><p>iii)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That in reference thereof the applicant was allotted a Unit No./ Apartment No. C-901 in the above-mentioned project along with a construction linked plan vide an allotment letter 27.04.2013 which is annexed herewith as Annexure C-2.</p><p>iv)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>The as per the Construction Linked Installment Plan appended to the aforesaid Agreement in pursuance wherein the applicant was required to pay Rs.1,08,43,200/- out of which the complainant had already paid Rs.27,94,563/- (Principal Rs.26,94,595/- and Service Tax of Rs.99,968/-) vide receipts Nos. 4422 and 4889 dated 01.06.2013 and 18.07.2013 respectively.&nbsp; An amount of Rs.10,934,794.00/- was paid by the Applicant to the Respondent upto 21.02.2018 as reflected in the flat holders card annexed herewith as Annexure C-3.</p><p>v)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That the respondent was to hand over possession within 30 months from date of allotment As per Clause 2.24 of Annexure C-2 which has not been complied with till date despite repeated reminders.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>vi)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That finally reminder dated 02.10.2018 vide email is annexed herewith as Annexure C-4 to no avail.</p><p>vii)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That aggrieved therewith the applicant seeks to invoke the jurisdiction of this Hon’ble forum for relief as the provisions of RERA have been violated owing to undue delay in delivery of possession of the flat to the complainant.&nbsp;</p><div><br></div>','<p>i)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To direct the respondent to deliver the flat to the complainant immediately without any increased charges.</p><p>ii)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To direct the respondent to pay interest on the Amount of Rs.1,09,34,794/- i.e. the payment made by the applicant till date as prescribed by the Act and the Rules framed there under.&nbsp;</p><p>iii)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To waive off GST applicable on the outstanding amount.</p><p>iv)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To issue directions to pay cost of litigation so incurred by the complainant to the tune of Rs.2,00,000/-.</p><p>v)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To issue direction to pay compensation to the complainant for the compensation for his mental agony, pain and harassment to the tune of Rs.5,00,000/-.&nbsp;</p><p>vi)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Any other relief which the Applicant is entitled for under the Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Act, 2016 and the Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017.&nbsp;</p><div><br></div>',0.00,10934794.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>To direct the respondent to deliver the flat to the complainant immediately without any increased charges.</p><p><br></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00',' C-901','','',2,0,0,0,'AnkitChowdhri','2019-03-12 18:02:25.000','AnkitChowdhri','2019-03-12 18:02:25.000'),(1193,1357,'1357',1431,'0787530d-1e75-4c59-a072-b71ad9aa4a1f','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Anuradha Sharma','radha.anu12175@gmail.com',9988802712,0,0,'27 E, New Kitchlu Nagar','Opposite Radha Swami Satsang Ghar',28,366,'141001','1','27 E, New Kitchlu Nagar','Opposite Radha Swami Satsang Ghar',28,366,'141001','prabhjot Singh Sachdeva','',9988126268,1615009615,'Promoter','PBRERA-LDH45-PR0052','Ireo Waterfront Pvt. Ltd.','Varun Khanna','varun.khanna@ireo.in',0,0,'Ireo Campus, Archview Drive, Ireo City','Golf Course Extension Road, Sector 59',13,5,'122101','1','Ireo Campus, Archview Drive, Ireo City','Golf Course Extension Road, Sector 59',13,5,'122101','1','<p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:150%\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\'font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:\"Arial\",\"sans-serif\"\'>Brief\r\nfacts of the complaint are, Complainants had booked a Plot with the respondents\r\nin November 2013. The respondents had allotted Plot Type-T-Plot-X122 having\r\narea of 126.05 sq yards and the agreement to the effect was executed on\r\n26.09.2014 (copy enclosed). Total sale consideration of the said plot is\r\nRs.27,76,145/- The complainants had made the payments, by availing bank loan of\r\nRs.17,66,512/- lacs @ 8.80%, as and when demanded <span style=\"mso-spacerun:yes\">&nbsp;</span>by the respondents and till\r\ndateRs.26,06,301/-<span style=\"mso-spacerun:yes\">&nbsp; </span>had been paid in\r\ntotal (Annexure and relevant documents enclosed). As per the terms of agreement\r\nnotice of completion is to be given by the respondents within the period of 24\r\nmonths + 180 days (Grace Period) i.e. by 25.03.2017. But till date i.e. more\r\nthan four years from the date of execution of agreement respondents had not\r\ndelivered the possession of plot. We approached respondents number of times but\r\nthey kept on lingering on the matter on one pretext or the other by making\r\nwhimsical or illogical excuses and also insisted the complainant to take\r\nanother plot/unit but as and when the complainants intends to accept their\r\noffer, then on very next meeting, they changed their earlier proposal and\r\noffered some another proposal (emails attached). The respondents are pressurizing\r\nthe complainants to get an alternative plot/unit which is neither agreed\r\nbetween the parties nor acceptable/feasible to the complainants.</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n<b></b><i></i><u></u><sub></sub><sup></sup><strike></strike><br></p>','<p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:150%\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\'font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:11.0pt;line-height:150%;&#10;font-family:\"Arial\",\"sans-serif\"\'>It is, therefore, respectfully prayed that\r\nthe respondents may kindly be directed to refund the amount of Rs.26,06,301/-\r\nalong with interest over and above the interest which the complainants are\r\npaying to the HDFC bank from which they have availed the loan facility for\r\npurchase the property, from the date of execution of the agreement till the\r\nrealization of the amount, the complainants are also entitled to get a\r\ncompensation to the tune of Rs.5 Lakh on account of mental pain, agony and\r\nharassment suffered by them as provided U/s 14 (3) and Section 19 of the said\r\nAct. </span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:150%\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\'font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:11.0pt;line-height:150%;&#10;font-family:\"Arial\",\"sans-serif\"\'><span style=\"mso-tab-count:1\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span>The\r\nstrict action U/s 7 &amp; 8 is also required to be taken against the\r\nrespondents for violating the provisions of The Real Estate (Regulation &amp;\r\nDevelopment Act).</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\'font-family:\"Arial\",\"sans-serif\"\'></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:150%\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\'font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:11.0pt;line-height:150%;&#10;font-family:\"Arial\",\"sans-serif\"\'><span style=\"mso-tab-count:2\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span>Any\r\nother relief which the complainants seems entitled to by this Hon\'ble\r\nAuthority, may also be granted to the complainants in the interest of justice\r\nand equity. </span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\'font-family:\"Arial\",\"sans-serif\"\'></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:150%\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">&nbsp;</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n<b></b><i></i><u></u><sub></sub><sup></sup><strike></strike><br></p>',2776145.00,2606301.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p><br></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'radha.anu12175','2019-03-13 08:02:31.000','radha.anu12175','2019-03-13 08:02:31.000'),(1194,1238,'1238',1316,'04ea4248-150e-4148-81b6-34afe1ec1b06','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-01-13 13:18:02.000','Kamal Makkar','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9729902009,0,358412254419,'424 Sector 20 Kaithal','',13,9,'136027','1','424 Sector 20 Kaithal','',13,9,'136027','Kamal Dahiya','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9729902009,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PMO121_','Purab Premium Apartments','Greater Mohali Area Development Authority','ce@gmada.gov.in',0,1722215512,'PUDA Bhawan Sector 62 District SAS Nagar Mohali ','',28,507,'160062','1','PUDA Bhawan Sector 62 District SAS Nagar Mohali ','',28,507,'160062','1','<p>Respondent opened scheme for public from 12.12.11 to 12.01.12 as Annexure C-1. The depicted salient features were as Annexure C-2. Respondent informed vide letter dated 23.03.2012 of the waiting list no. 65 &amp; complainant to submit the documents before 23.04.12 as Annexure C-3. Letter of intent for allotment was issued on 21.05.12 and tentative price was Rs 55,00,000. As per Para 3(II) delivery was to be within a period of 36 months from the date of issuance of the said letter. Possession date was 21.05.15 i.e. delay is more than 3 years &amp; 7 months as per Annexure C-4. Payment plan B was opted as per AnnexureC-4 (Pg 40). Initial amount of INR 11,00,000 paid vide cheque on 16.06.12 as Annexure C-5 (Pg41). Total amount paid Rs54,25,746/- ie 98% out of the total consideration till 21.04.16 as Annexure C-5(colly). After 5 years the complainant was allotted with apartment no.1502, Tower-5, Block D, Floor 14 with 2563.19 sq ft area including common stairs &amp; car parking area on 11.10.17 &amp; the possession was also offered as Annexure C-6. Thereafter the complainant visited site &amp; found that layout plan has changed without taking consent of 2/3rd allottees &amp; found many loopholes in the construction like compromised quality of materials etc. The complainant got the construction inspected by Registered Council of Architecture, New Delhi. Many differences were found as in Annexure C-7. The complainant intimated such defects to the E.O. of GMADA vide letter dated 17.05.218 and requested for refund of his paid amount but respondent didn’t respond as Annexure C-8. Other allottees also found several defects, deficiencies &amp; deviations in the project Annexure C-9 (Pg93). Several allottees raised the issues before the press conference (Pg 94-95). The government ordered to remove the defaults but respondent did not comply to repair the faults (Pg 96-97). Fire safety has been expired (Pg 98-99). The lifts are also not at all safe for females and stops to work (Pg 100-103).<br></p>','<p>In view of the facts mentioned in preceding paragraphs, the complainant prays for the following relief(s):-&nbsp;</p><p>i.To give necessary directions to the respondents for refund the amount paid by the complainant with prescribed interest till realization as per the provisions of Sec. 18 and Sec.19(4)of the RERA Act read with Rule 16 of PSRE(R&amp;D)Rules, 2017.</p><p>ii.To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 60 of RERA Act for willful default committed by them.</p><p>iii.To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 61 of RERA Act for contravention of Sec.12, Sec.14, and Sec. 16 of RERA Act.</p><p>iv.To issue directions to make liable every officer concerned i.e. Director, Manager, Secretary, or any other officer of the respondent’s company at whose instance, connivance, acquiescence, neglect any of the offences has been committed as mentioned in Sec.69 of RERA Act,2016 to be read with Punjab RERA Rules,2017.</p><p>v.To recommend criminal action against the respondents for the criminal offence of cheating, fraud and criminal breach of trust under section 420,406 and 409 of the Indian Penal Code.</p><p>vi.To issue direction to pay the cost of litigation.</p><p>vii.To issue direction to pay the compensation to complainant for compensation for his mental agony, pain and harassment.</p><p>viii.Any other relief which this Hon’ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances of this complaint.</p><div><br></div>',55000.00,5425746.00,'2015-05-21 00:00:00.000','2015-05-21 00:00:00.000','<p>i.To direct the respondent not to demand any further amount whatsoever from the complainant.</p><p>ii.The respondent should be restrained from harassing the complainant in any manner whatsoever.</p><p>iii.Any other interim relief which this Hon’ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances of this complaint.</p><div><br></div>','1','','2017-10-11 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Apartment No 1502 Tower 5 Block D Floor 14 Type 2 Sector 88 Sahibzada Ajit Singh Nagar Punjab 140308','','',2,0,0,0,'kamalmakkar1','2019-03-13 18:09:36.000','kamalmakkar1','2019-03-13 18:09:36.000'),(1195,1238,'1238',1316,'04ea4248-150e-4148-81b6-34afe1ec1b06','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-01-13 13:18:02.000','Kamal Makkar','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9729902009,0,358412254419,'424 Sector 20 Kaithal','',13,9,'136027','1','424 Sector 20 Kaithal','',13,9,'136027','Kamal Dahiya','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9729902009,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PM0121','Purab Premium Apartments','Greater Mohali Area Development Authority','ce@gmada.gov.in',0,1722215512,'PUDA Bhawan Sector 62 District SAS Nagar Mohali ','',28,507,'160062','1','PUDA Bhawan Sector 62 District SAS Nagar Mohali ','',28,507,'160062','1','<p>Respondent opened scheme for public from 12.12.11 to 12.01.12 as Annexure C-1. The depicted salient features were as Annexure C-2. Respondent informed vide letter dated 23.03.2012 of the waiting list no. 65 &amp; complainant to submit the documents before 23.04.12 as Annexure C-3. Letter of intent for allotment was issued on 21.05.12 and tentative price was Rs 55,00,000. As per Para 3(II) delivery was to be within a period of 36 months from the date of issuance of the said letter. Possession date was 21.05.15 i.e. delay is