nexure C-9 (Pg93). Several allottees raised the issues before the press conference (Pg 94-95). The government ordered to remove the defaults but respondent did not comply to repair the faults (Pg 96-97). Fire safety has been expired (Pg 98-99). The lifts are also not at all safe for females and stops to work (Pg 100-103).<br></p>','<p>In view of the facts mentioned in preceding paragraphs, the complainant prays for the following relief(s):-&nbsp;</p><p>i.To give necessary directions to the respondents for refund the amount paid by the complainant with prescribed interest till realization as per the provisions of Sec. 18 and Sec.19(4)of the RERA Act read with Rule 16 of PSRE(R&amp;D)Rules, 2017.</p><p>ii.To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 60 of RERA Act for willful default committed by them.</p><p>iii.To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 61 of RERA Act for contravention of Sec.12, Sec.14, and Sec. 16 of RERA Act.</p><p>iv.To issue directions to make liable every officer concerned i.e. Director, Manager, Secretary, or any other officer of the respondent’s company at whose instance, connivance, acquiescence, neglect any of the offences has been committed as mentioned in Sec.69 of RERA Act,2016 to be read with Punjab RERA Rules,2017.</p><p>v.To recommend criminal action against the respondents for the criminal offence of cheating, fraud and criminal breach of trust under section 420,406 and 409 of the Indian Penal Code.</p><p>vi.To issue direction to pay the cost of litigation.</p><p>vii.To issue direction to pay the compensation to complainant for compensation for his mental agony, pain and harassment.</p><p>viii.Any other relief which this Hon’ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances of this complaint.</p><div><br></div>',55000.00,5425746.00,'2015-05-21 00:00:00.000','2015-05-21 00:00:00.000','<p>i.To direct the respondent not to demand any further amount whatsoever from the complainant.</p><p>ii.The respondent should be restrained from harassing the complainant in any manner whatsoever.</p><p>iii.Any other interim relief which this Hon’ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances of this complaint.</p><div><br></div>','1','','2017-10-11 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Apartment No 1502 Tower 5 Block D Floor 14 Type 2 Sector 88 Sahibzada Ajit Singh Nagar Punjab 140308','','',1,1,0,0,'kamalmakkar1','2019-03-13 18:12:22.000','kamalmakkar1','2019-03-13 18:12:22.000'),(1197,1240,'1240',1317,'d8f8d4fc-24ac-4faa-a9b2-b5ad58a5817a','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-03-13 18:16:14.000','Bharat Bhushan Makkar','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9729902009,0,934955777170,'108 Sector 20 Kaithal','',13,9,'136027','1','108 Sector 20 Kaithal','',13,9,'136027','Kamal Dahiya','jurisaxisrera@gmail.com',9729902009,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PM0121','Purab Premium Apartments','Greater Mohali Area Development Authority','ce@gmada.gov.in',1722215512,0,'PUDA Bhawan Sector 62 District SAS Nagar Mohali','',28,507,'160062','1','PUDA Bhawan Sector 62 District SAS Nagar Mohali','',28,507,'160062','1','<p>Respondent opened scheme for public from 12.12.11 to 12.01.12 as Annexure C-1. The depicted salient features were as AnnexureC-2. Respondent informed vide letter dated 23.03.12 of the waiting list and complainant to submit the documents before 23.04.12 as Annexure C-3. Letter of intent for allotment was issued on 23.05.2012 and tentative price was Rs 69,00,000 and the flat was allotted with Flat No. 901 in Tower 3, Block E at Type 3 Apartment. As per Para 3(II) delivery was to be within a period of 36 months from the date of issuance of the said letter. Possession date was 23.05.2015 i.e. delay is of 3 years and 7 months as AnnexureC-4. Payment plan B was opted by the complainant as AnnexureC-4 (Pg 40). Initial amount of INR 13,80,000 paid vide cheque on 19.06.12 as AnnexureC-5 (Pg41). Total amount paid is Rs 68,06,850/- i.e. 99% out of the total consideration as AnnexureC-5 (colly). Respondent offered the possession vide letter on 10.10.2017. Thereafter the complainant visited site and found that layout plan has changed without taking the consent of 2/3rd allottees and also found many loopholes in the construction like compromised quality of materials etc. Photographs are annexed as Annexure C-6. The complainant got the construction inspected by Registered Council of Architecture, New Delhi. Many differences were found as in Annexure C-7. The complainant intimated such defects to the Estate Officer of GMADA vide letter dated 17.05.18 and requested for refund of his paid amount but respondent didn’t respond AnnexureC-8. Other allottees also found several defects, deficiencies and deviations in the project AnnexureC-9 (Pg104). Several allottees raised the issues before the press conference(Pg 105-106). The government ordered to remove the defaults but respondent did not comply to repair the faults (Pg 107-108). Fire safety has been expired (Pg 109-110). The lifts are also not safe at all for females and stops to work (Pg 111-113).</p>','<p>In view of the facts mentioned in preceding paragraphs, the complainant prays for the following relief(s):-&nbsp;</p><p>i.To give necessary directions to the respondents for refund the amount paid by the complainant with prescribed interest till realization as per the provisions of Sec. 18 and Sec.19(4)of the RERA Act read with Rule 16 of PSRE(R&amp;D)Rules,2017.</p><p>ii.To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 60 of RERA Act for willful default committed by them.</p><p>iii.To impose penalty upon the respondents as per the provisions of Section 61 of RERA Act for contravention of Sec.12, Sec.14, and Sec. 16 of RERA Act.</p><p>iv.To issue directions to make liable every officer concerned i.e. Director, Manager, Secretary, or any other officer of the respondent’s company at whose instance, connivance, acquiescence, neglect any of the offences has been committed as mentioned in Sec.69 of RERA Act,2016 to be read with Punjab RERA Rules, 2017.</p><p>v.To recommend criminal action against the respondents for the criminal offence of cheating, fraud and criminal breach of trust under section 420,406 and 409 of the Indian Penal Code.</p><p>vi.To issue direction to pay the cost of litigation.</p><p>vii.To issue direction to pay the compensation to complainant for compensation for his mental agony, pain and harassment.</p><p>viii.Any other relief which this Hon’ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances of this complaint.</p>',69000.00,6806850.00,'2015-05-23 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>i.To direct the respondent not to demand any further amount whatsoever from the complainant.</p><p>ii.The respondent should be restrained from harassing the complainant in any manner whatsoever.</p><p>iii.Any other interim relief which this Hon’ble Authority deem fit and appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances of this complaint.</p><div><br></div>','1','','2012-05-23 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Flat No 901 Tower 3 Block E Type 3 Sector 88 Sahibzada Ajit Singh Nagar Punjab 140308','','',1,1,0,0,'Bharatbhushanmakkar','2019-03-13 18:16:05.000','Bharatbhushanmakkar','2019-03-13 18:16:05.000'),(1198,1353,'1353',1426,'c52fa8fb-ca9e-4d5d-9572-49b22b4f0748','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-03-11 16:08:01.000','Puneet Bedi','adv.amansingla@yahoo.com',9915344358,0,0,'House No. 224','Sector 2',13,15,'134109','1','House No. 224','Sector 2',13,15,'134109','Aman Singla','adv.amansingla@yahoo.com',9915344358,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-PTL65-PM0108','Parsavnath king Citi','Parsavnath Developer Limited','mail@parsavnath.com',9560110741,0,'Parsvnath Tower, ','Near Shahdara Metro Station, Shahdara, Delhi ',10,436,'110032','1','Parsvnath Tower, ','Near Shahdara Metro Station, Shahdara, Delhi ',10,436,'110032','1','<p>1. One plot for a sale price of Rs. 21,27,102.50/- purchased from respondent no.1. As per the Plot Buyer Agreement dated 2.4.2007 the maintenance and upkeep of common areas and facilities will only be done by respondent no.1 or by nominee of respondent no.1 till the same is handed over to authority/local body. Respondent no.1 nominated and assigned the maintenance work of common areas and facilities to respondent no.2 (formerly known as M/s Basundra Properties Pvt. Ltd.) and got executed an agreement regarding this on 8.4.2008.</p><p>2. Conveyance Deed executed 1.8.2008 in it is wrongly mentioned that physical, peaceful and vacant possession of the plot has been handed over to complainants. Physical and vacant possession of plot is not handed over to the complainants as no demarcation of plot in project done and complainants have no knowledge about whereabouts of their plot.</p><p>3. Respondent no.1 was liable to maintain the project itself and pay for all the outgoings till transferring possession of plots to allottee/allottees after proper demarcation. Respondent no.1 has transferred his liability of maintaining the project upon respondent no.2 so now respondent no. 2 shall also be treated as promoter of the project as per law.</p><p>4. The maintenance agreement was executed for 5 years which has expired in the year 2013 and thereafter the maintenance agreement has not been renewed till date.</p><p>5. The project has been stalled since long and no construction and maintenance work has been done on the project since long. Essential services and basic necessities which are essential for human habitat is not provided in the project. Respondents haven\'t spent a single penny on development, maintenance and upkeep of the project till date and the project bears a deserted look. No periphery wall of the project has been erected till date.</p><p>6. Respondent No.2 raising illegal demand for maintenance of project as complainants have not received physical possession and the agreement has expired.<br></p>','<p>In view of the facts mentioned in paragraph 4 above, the complainant prays for the following relief(s):</p><p><br></p><p>(a)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Stay of illegal demand notices for maintenance and upkeep charges by respondent no. 2;</p><p>(b)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Respondent No. 1 and Respondent No. 2 be restrained from charging maintenance and upkeep charges from the complainants till the completion of project, completion and occupancy certificate is provided to complainants, demarcation of plots are done in the project and physical and vacant possession of plot no. 549 is handed over to complainants;</p><p>(c)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Respondents be directed to provide Sold and Unsold inventories to the complainants;</p><p>(d)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Respondents be directed to provide Internal Development work which is Annexure II of Plot Buyer Agreement dated 02.04.2007 to the complainants;</p><p>(e)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Respondents be directed to provide Initial Layout Plans of the Project which is Annexure IV of Plot Buyer Agreement dated 02.04.2007 to the complainants;</p><p>(f)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Respondents be directed to place on record Initial Prospectus/Brochure/ Launching Advertisement;</p><p>(g)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Litigation costs of Rs. 51,000/-.</p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Pending final decision on the complaint the complainant seeks issue of the following interim order:</p><p>(a)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Interim Stay of illegal demand notices for maintenance and upkeep charges by respondent no. 2.</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'Amansingla','2019-03-13 22:51:51.000','Amansingla','2019-03-13 22:51:51.000'),(1199,1353,'1353',1426,'c52fa8fb-ca9e-4d5d-9572-49b22b4f0748','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-03-11 16:08:01.000','Puneet Bedi','adv.amansingla@yahoo.com',991534435