ssential services and basic necessities which are essential for human habitat is not provided in the project. Respondents haven\'t spent a single penny on development, maintenance and upkeep of the project till date and the project bears a deserted look. No periphery wall of the project has been erected till date.</p><p>6. Respondent No.2 raising illegal demand for maintenance of project as complainants have not received physical possession and the agreement has expired.<br></p>','<p>In view of the facts mentioned in paragraph 4 above, the complainant prays for the following relief(s):</p><p><br></p><p>(a)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Stay of illegal demand notices for maintenance and upkeep charges by respondent no. 2;</p><p>(b)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Respondent No. 1 and Respondent No. 2 be restrained from charging maintenance and upkeep charges from the complainants till the completion of project, completion and occupancy certificate is provided to complainants, demarcation of plots are done in the project and physical and vacant possession of plot no. 549 is handed over to complainants;</p><p>(c)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Respondents be directed to provide Sold and Unsold inventories to the complainants;</p><p>(d)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Respondents be directed to provide Internal Development work which is Annexure II of Plot Buyer Agreement dated 02.04.2007 to the complainants;</p><p>(e)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Respondents be directed to provide Initial Layout Plans of the Project which is Annexure IV of Plot Buyer Agreement dated 02.04.2007 to the complainants;</p><p>(f)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Respondents be directed to place on record Initial Prospectus/Brochure/ Launching Advertisement;</p><p>(g)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Litigation costs of Rs. 51,000/-.</p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Pending final decision on the complaint the complainant seeks issue of the following interim order:</p><p>(a)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Interim Stay of illegal demand notices for maintenance and upkeep charges by respondent no. 2.</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'Amansingla','2019-03-13 23:08:35.000','Amansingla','2019-03-13 23:08:35.000'),(1200,1353,'1353',1426,'c52fa8fb-ca9e-4d5d-9572-49b22b4f0748','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-03-13 23:09:05.000','Puneet Bedi','adv.amansingla@yahoo.com',9915344358,0,0,'House No. 224','Sector 2',13,15,'134109','1','House No. 224','Sector 2',13,15,'134109','Aman Singla','adv.amansingla@yahoo.com',9915344358,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-PTL65-PM0108','Parsavnath king Citi','Parsavnath Developer Limited','mail@parsavnath.com',9560110741,0,'Parsvnath Tower, ','Near Shahdara Metro Station, Shahdara, Delhi ',10,436,'110032','1','Parsvnath Tower, ','Near Shahdara Metro Station, Shahdara, Delhi ',10,436,'110032','1','<p>1. One plot for a sale price of Rs. 21,27,102.50/- purchased from respondent no.1. As per the Plot Buyer Agreement dated 2.4.2007 the maintenance and upkeep of common areas and facilities will only be done by respondent no.1 or by nominee of respondent no.1 till the same is handed over to authority/local body. Respondent no.1 nominated and assigned the maintenance work of common areas and facilities to respondent no.2 (formerly known as M/s Basundra Properties Pvt. Ltd.) and got executed an agreement regarding this on 8.4.2008.</p><p>2. Conveyance Deed executed 1.8.2008 in it is wrongly mentioned that physical, peaceful and vacant possession of the plot has been handed over to complainants. Physical and vacant possession of plot is not handed over to the complainants as no demarcation of plot in project done and complainants have no knowledge about whereabouts of their plot.</p><p>3. Respondent no.1 was liable to maintain the project itself and pay for all the outgoings till transferring possession of plots to allottee/allottees after proper demarcation. Respondent no.1 has transferred his liability of maintaining the project upon respondent no.2 so now respondent no. 2 shall also be treated as promoter of the project as per law.</p><p>4. The maintenance agreement was executed for 5 years which has expired in the year 2013 and thereafter the maintenance agreement has not been renewed till date.</p><p>5. The project has been stalled since long and no construction and maintenance work has been done on the project since long. Essential services and basic necessities which are essential for human habitat is not provided in the project. Respondents haven\'t spent a single penny on development, maintenance and upkeep of the project till date and the project bears a deserted look. No periphery wall of the project has been erected till date.</p><p>6. Respondent No.2 raising illegal demand for maintenance of project as complainants have not received physical possession and the agreement has expired.<br></p>','<p>In view of the facts mentioned in paragraph 4 above, the complainant prays for the following relief(s):</p><p><br></p><p>(a)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Stay of illegal demand notices for maintenance and upkeep charges by respondent no. 2;</p><p>(b)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Respondent No. 1 and Respondent No. 2 be restrained from charging maintenance and upkeep charges from the complainants till the completion of project, completion and occupancy certificate is provided to complainants, demarcation of plots are done in the project and physical and vacant possession of plot no. 549 is handed over to complainants;</p><p>(c)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Respondents be directed to provide Sold and Unsold inventories to the complainants;</p><p>(d)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Respondents be directed to provide Internal Development work which is Annexure II of Plot Buyer Agreement dated 02.04.2007 to the complainants;</p><p>(e)<span style=\"