plainant, he can transfer the LOI on\r\npaying the 2.5% of price of plot, which was fixed by GMADA @25,000/- per sq.\r\nYds. (C/3) Complainant purchased the Plot from Balwinder Singh etc. vide\r\ntransfer letter dated 15/11/2013, after paying Rs.315250 as transfer fee(C/4).\r\norally GMADA have promised that they will develop land in 1.5 to 2 years.\r\nHowever now on 28/1/2019 they have issued allotment letter and offer\r\npossession, without completing the development on the spot. They have also\r\ndemanded extra amount for facing park and corner, which was not mention either\r\nin award or policy of land pooling or in LOI. Possession also offered without\r\ncompleting the development work. Even in High Court in CWP No.398/2016, EO has\r\nstated that they will complete development work by 30/11/2018. But to develop\r\nthe parks they have issued the tenders only on 8/2/2019 to be completed in 8\r\nMonths. Although some development work is going but same is not completed. No street\r\nlight was working. Sewerage System was lying open. Even development of Parks\r\nhas not been started yet. Roads are only half done. So there is no question of\r\nthe handing over the possession. There is a huge delay in handing over the\r\npossession, whereas they have developed the area for private builder in 2016\r\nitself.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin: 0cm 0cm 7.5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: Roboto;\">Further even\r\ndemand for extra amount for Corner with facing park is also not justified, as\r\nNothing such condition in Award, or in Policy or in Original LOI. Further in\r\nECO City matter also in case of Land pooling scheme, GMADA has itself withdrawn\r\nsuch charges, when people approached HIGH COURT by way of CWP No.25715/15.</span></p>','<p>1.&nbsp; &nbsp; Prayer for issuance of direction to the Respondent to handover the possession of the Plot after completion of the Development work, as defined under Section 2(t), 2(w), 2(zb) of the The Real Estate (Reg. and Development), Act 2006.</p><p>2.&nbsp; &nbsp; To Pay interest @18% p.a.&nbsp;for delayed period of Possession, from the date of issuance of LOI till handing over the actual possession, after completing the development work.&nbsp;</p><p>3.&nbsp; &nbsp; Not to charge any extra amount on account of Preferential Location Charges, being beyond the Scope of LOI, Award and Land acquisition Policy and in view of withdrawal of such charges by themselves in ECO City.&nbsp;</p><p>4.&nbsp; &nbsp;This Hon\'ble Court may grant any other relief, which this Hon\'ble Court may deem fit and proper in the peculiar facts and circumstances of the present case.&nbsp;</p>',12687500.00,12687500.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>For issuance of direction to the Respondents not to charge any amount on account of PLC, during the pendency of the present complaint and also not to cancel/Resume the plot during the pendency of the present complaint.&nbsp;</p>','1','','2019-01-28 00:00:00','2013-09-30 00:00:00','Plot No.3021, Sector 88, Block D, SAS Nagar, Mohali','','',2,0,0,0,'harish635','2019-03-14 15:45:45.000','harish635','2019-03-14 15:45:45.000'),(1202,1358,'1358',1393,'d33e1b7d-de22-43e0-97c8-115b8ed3d62e','FormTypeM',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Ravinder Goyal','harish635@rediffmail.com',9815072433,0,932801396199,'#2231, Phase 7, ','SAS Nagar, Mohali',28,507,'160062','1','#2231, Phase 7, ','SAS Nagar, Mohali',28,507,'160062','Harish Goyal','harish635@rediffmail.com',9815628635,1722217635,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PM0121','Sector 88 and 89 including Purab Premium Apartments','Estate Officer GMADA','eo@gmada.gov.in',0,1722213535,'PUDA Bhawan','Sector 62',28,507,'160062','0','EO GMADA, PUDA Bhawan','Sector 62',28,507,'160062','1','<p style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0cm;\r\ntext-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: Roboto;\">Respondents acquired land vide award dated 15/11/11. In lieu of\r\ncompensation GMADA has given land pooling scheme, according to which owner will\r\nget developed land in lieu of his acquired land. Neither land owner required to\r\npay anything nor GMADA has to pay anything for the same(Anne C/2). As per LOI dated\r\n30/9/13, issued to the vendor of the complainant, he can transfer the LOI on\r\npaying the 2.5% of price of plot, which was fixed by GMADA @25,000/- per sq.\r\nYds. (Ann C/3). Complainant purchased the Plot from Balwinder Singh etc. vide\r\ntransfer letter dated 15/11/2013, after paying Rs.315250 as transfer fee (Ann C/4). Orally GMADA have promised that they will develop land in 1.5 to 2 years.\r\nHowever now on 28/1/2019 they have issued allotment letter and offer of possession, without completing the development on the spot(Ann C/5). They have also\r\ndemanded extra amount for facing park and corner, which was not mention either\r\nin award or policy of land pooling or in LOI. Possession also offered without\r\ncompleting the development work. Even in High Court in CWP No.398/2016, EO has\r\nstated that they will complete development work by 30/11/2018. But to develop\r\nthe parks they have issued the tenders only on 8/2/2019 to be completed in 8\r\nMonths. Although some development work is going but same is not completed. No street\r\nlight was working. Sewerage System was lying open. Even development of Parks\r\nhas not been started yet. Roads are only half done. So there is no question of\r\nthe handing over the possession. There is a huge delay in handing over the\r\npossession, whereas they have developed the area for private builder in 2016\r\nitself.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin: 0cm 0cm 7.5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: Roboto;\">Further even\r\ndemand for extra amount for Corner with facing park is also not justified, as\r\nNothing such condition in Award, or in Policy or in Original LOI. Further in\r\nECO City matter also in case of Land pooling scheme, GMADA has itself withdrawn\r\nsuch charges, when people approached HIGH COURT by way of CWP No.25715/15.</span></p>','<p>1.&nbsp; &nbsp; Prayer for issuance of direction to the Respondent to handover the possession of the Plot after completion of the Development work, as defined under Section 2(t), 2(w), 2(zb) of the The Real Estate (Reg. and Development), Act 2006, as allotment letter issued on 28/1/2019, where as till date development work is not complete. Roads are not complete, street lights are not working, even for parks, they have issued tenders just on 8/2/2019, after issuance of allotment letter.&nbsp;</p><p>2.&nbsp; &nbsp; To Pay interest @18% p.a. (or as per the provisions of the Act) for delayed period of Possession, from the date of issuance of LOI till handing over the actual possession, after completing the development work, since entire consideration has already paid to them, in lieu of land. Further they have developed the land for the private builder Hero Homes, within 6 months in the year 2016, development for the common people only started after intervention of the Hon\'ble High Court in CWP No.398 of 2016. Further even allotment letters are issued only to show in the Hon\'ble High Court, otherwise development is still in complete. There is a huge delay of 6 years in handing over the possession. They have violated the various provisions of the RERA Act.&nbsp;</p><p>3.&nbsp; &nbsp; Not to charge any extra amount on account of Preferential Location Charges, being beyond the Scope of LOI, Award and Land acquisition Policy and in view of withdrawal of such charges by themselves in ECO City. In the LOI no such condition was mentioned. Now they can not of there own, could start charging extra amount as per their own whim and caprice.&nbsp;</p><p>4.&nbsp; &nbsp;This Hon\'ble Court may grant any other relief, which this Hon\'ble Court may deem fit and proper in the peculiar facts and circumstances of the present case.&nbsp;</p>',12687500.00,12687500.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>For issuance of direction to the Respondents not to charge any amount on account of PLC, during the pendency of the present complaint and also not to cancel/Resume the plot during the pendency of the present complaint.&nbsp;</p>','1','','2019-01-28 00:00:00','2013-09-30 00:00:00','Plot No.3021, Sector 88, Block D, SAS Nagar, Mohali','','',2,0,0,0,'harish635','2019-03-14 16:32:26.000','harish635','2019-03-14 16:32:26.000'),(1203,1358,'1358',1393,'d33e1b7d-de22-43e0-97c8-115b8ed3d62e','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-03-14 18:11:30.000','Ravinder Goyal','harish635@rediffmail.com',9815072433,0,932801396199,'#2231, Phase 7, ','SAS Nagar, Mohali',28,507,'160062','1','#2231, Phase 7, ','SAS Nagar, Mohali',28,507,'160062','Harish Goyal','harish635@rediffmail.com',9815628635,1722217635,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PM0121','Sector 88 and 89 including Purab Premium Apartments','Estate Officer GMADA','eo@gmada.gov.in',0,1722213535,'PUDA Bhawan','Sector 62',28,507,'160062','0','EO GMADA, PUDA Bhawan','Sector 62',28,507,'160062','1','<p style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0cm;\r\ntext-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: Roboto;\">Respondents acquired land vide award dated 15/11/11. In lieu of\r\ncompensation GMADA has given land pooling scheme, according to which owner will\r\nget developed land in lieu of his acquired land. Neither land owner required to\r\npay anything nor GMADA has to pay anything for the same(Anne C/2). As per LOI dated\r\n30/9/13, issued to the vendor of the complainant, he can transfer the LOI on\r\npaying the 2.5% of price of plot, which was fixed by GMADA @25,000/- per sq.\r\nYds. (Ann C/3). Complainant purchased the Plot from Balwinder Singh etc. vide\r\ntransfer letter dated 15/11/2013, after paying Rs.315250 as transfer fee (Ann C/4). Orally GMADA have promised that they will develop land in 1.5 to 2 years.\r\nHowever now on 28/1/2019 they have issued allotment letter and offer of possession, without completing the development on the spot(Ann C/5). They have also\r\ndemanded extra amount for facing park and corner, which was not mention either\r\nin award or policy of land pooling or in LOI. Possession also offered without\r\ncompleting the development work. Even in High Court in CWP No.398/2016, EO has\r\nstated that they will complete development work by 30/11/2018. But to develop\r\nthe parks they have issued the tenders only on 8/2/2019 to be completed in 8\r\nMonths. Although some development work is going but same is not completed. No street\r\nlight was working. Sewerage System was lying open. Even development of Parks\r\nhas not been started yet. Roads are only half done. So there is no question of\r\nthe handing over the possession. There is a huge delay in handing over the\r\npossession, whereas they have developed the area for private builder in 2016\r\nitself.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin: 0cm 0cm 7.5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: Roboto;\">Further even\r\ndemand for extra amount for Corner with facing park is also not justified, as\r\nNothing such condition in Award, or in Policy or in Original LOI. Further in\r\nECO City matter also in case of Land pooling scheme, GMADA has itself withdrawn\r\nsuch charges, when people approached HIGH COURT by way of CWP No.25715/15.</span></p>','<p>1.&nbsp; &nbsp; Prayer for issuance of direction to the Respondent to handover the possession of the Plot after completion of the Development work, as defined under Section 2(t), 2(w), 2(zb) of the The Real Estate (Reg. and Development), Act 2006, as allotment letter issued on 28/1/2019, where as till date development work is not complete. Roads are not complete, street lights are not working, even for parks, they have issued tenders just on 8/2/2019, after issuance of allotment letter.&nbsp;</p><p>2.&nbsp; &nbsp; To Pay interest @18% p.a. (or as per the provisions of the Act) for delayed period of Possession, from the date of issuance of LOI till handing over the actual possession, after completing the development work, since entire consideration has already paid to them, in lieu of land. Further they have developed the land for the private builder Hero Homes, within 6 months in the year 2016, development for the common people only started after intervention of the Hon\'ble High Court in CWP No.398 of 2016. Further even allotment letters are issued only to show in the Hon\'ble High Court, otherwise development is still in complete. There is a huge delay of 6 years in handing over the possession. They have violated the various provisions of the RERA Act.&nbsp;</p><p>3.&nbsp; &nbsp; Not to charge any extra amount on account of Preferential Location Charges, being beyond the Scope of LOI, Award and Land acquisition Policy and in view of withdrawal of such charges by themselves in ECO City. In the LOI no such condition was mentioned. Now they can not of there own, could start charging extra amount as per their own whim and caprice.&nbsp;</p><p>4.&nbsp; &nbsp;This Hon\'ble Court may grant any other relief, which this Hon\'ble Court may deem fit and proper in the peculiar facts and circumstances of the present case.&nbsp;</p>',12687500.00,12687500.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>For issuance of direction to the Respondents not to charge any amount on account of PLC, during the pendency of the present complaint and also not to cancel/Resume the plot during the pendency of the present complaint.&nbsp;</p>','1','','2019-01-28 00:00:00','2013-09-30 00:00:00','Plot No.3021, Sector 88, Block D, SAS Nagar, Mohali','','',1,1,0,0,'harish635','2019-03-14 16:35:07.000','harish635','2019-03-14 16:35:07.000'),(1204,1359,'1359',1437,'45fd2620-aaa7-4466-8edd-d5a9ee5044c7','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-03-16 17:35:16.000','MANOJ  SOOD','imanojsood@gmail.com',9592222222,9592122222,648610011991,'HOUSE NO 473, NEAR KRISHNA MANDIR ','WARD NO 5, MOHALLA DADPURA',28,507,'140507','1','HOUSE NO 473, NEAR KRISHNA MANDIR ','WARD NO 5, MOHALLA DADPURA',28,507,'140507','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PC0021','GBP CENTRUM','PARDEEP KUMAR','sales@gbpgroup.in',9815895724,9569545454,'GUPTA BUILDERS AND PROMOTERS PVT. LTD.','SCO 64-65, SECTOR 17-A, CHANDIGARH',6,128,'160017','1','GUPTA BUILDERS AND PROMOTERS PVT. LTD.','SCO 64-65, SECTOR 17-A, CHANDIGARH',6,128,'160017','1','<p>ON 17-05-2017, I MADE FULL PAYMENT RS. 54,40,182.00 FOR TWO UNDER CONSTRUCTION COMMERCIAL UNITS FOR WHICH I HAVE PAID UP FULL PAYMENTS AND GET MONTHLY INTEREST ON MY PAYMENT VIA PDC ON EVERY 17TH. WHICH POSSESSION IS DUE ON 17-05-2021.</p><p>BUT I DONT NEED MONTHLY INTEREST . I WANT TO CANCEL THESE ALLOTMENTS AND WANT MY PAYMENT BACK.</p><p><br></p><p>THE BUILDER HAS DENIED THAT PAYMENT WILL NOT PAID BACK UNDER NO CIRCUMSTANCES. HE IS PRESSURIZING ME TO RETAIN THE UNITS. SAYING ITS&nbsp; A APPROVED PROJECT. YOU CAN NOT CANCEL IT.</p><p>PLEASE HELP ME TO CANCEL THESE ALLOTMENTS AND REFUND MY HARD EARNED MONEY BACK VERY SOON.</p><p>LOOKING FORWARDS TO AN EARLY HEAR PLEASE.</p>','<p>CANCEL THE ALLOTMENTS OF BOTH UNITS AND REFUND MY PAYMENT BACK AT THE EARLIEST POSSIBLE.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p>',4911232.00,5440182.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>CANCEL BOTH ALLOTMENTS OF UNITS AND REFUND MY HARD EARNED MONEY BACK AT THE EARLIEST POSSIBLE TIMELINE.</p><p>REQUESTED.</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','1.  COMMERCIAL SPACE NO. 637 ON 6TH FLOOR ADMEASURING SUPER AREA 493.29 SQ. FT. TYPE STUDIO CUM OFFICE : RS. 3201452.00\r\n\r\n2. COMMERCIAL SPACE NO. 28 ON 7TH FLOOR ADMEASURING SUPER AREA 187.25 SQ. FT. TYPE OFFICE CUM CABIN : RS. 1709780.00\r\n\r\nTOTAL 4911232.00\r\n BOTH UNITS IN GBP CENTRUM, VILLAGE SINGHPURA, ZIRAKPUR, DISTT. SAS NAGAR (MOHALI).','','',1,1,0,0,'MANOJSOOD','2019-03-16 16:41:53.000','MANOJSOOD','2019-03-16 16:41:53.000'),(1205,1357,'1357',1431,'0787530d-1e75-4c59-a072-b71ad9aa4a1f','FormTypeM',1,1,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Anuradha Sharma','radha.anu12175@gmail.com',9988802712,0,0,'27 E, New Kitchlu Nagar','Opposite Radha Swami Satsang Ghar',28,366,'141001','1','27 E, New Kitchlu Nagar','Opposite Radha Swami Satsang Ghar',28,366,'141001','prabhjot Singh Sachdeva','',9988126268,1615009615,'Promoter','PBRERA-LDH45-PR0052','Ireo Waterfront Pvt. Ltd.','Varun Khanna','varun.khanna@ireo.in',0,0,'Ireo Campus, Archview Drive, Ireo City','Golf Course Extension Road, Sector 59',13,5,'122101','1','Ireo Campus, Archview Drive, Ireo City','Golf Course Extension Road, Sector 59',13,5,'122101','1','<p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:150%\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\'font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:\"Arial\",\"sans-serif\"\'>Brief\r\nfacts of the complaint are, Complainants had booked a Plot with the respondents\r\nin November 2013. The respondents had allotted Plot Type-T-Plot-X122 having\r\narea of 126.05 sq yards and the agreement to the effect was executed on\r\n26.09.2014 (copy enclosed). Total sale consideration of the said plot is\r\nRs.27,76,145/- The complainants had made the payments, by availing bank loan of\r\nRs.17,66,512/- lacs @ 8.80%, as and when demanded <span style=\"mso-spacerun:yes\">&nbsp;</span>by the respondents and till\r\ndateRs.26,06,301/-<span style=\"mso-spacerun:yes\">&nbsp; </span>had been paid in\r\ntotal (Annexure and relevant documents enclosed). As per the terms of agreement\r\nnotice of completion is to be given by the respondents within the period of 24\r\nmonths + 180 days (Grace Period) i.e. by 25.03.2017. But till date i.e. more\r\nthan four years from the date of execution of agreement respondents had not\r\ndelivered the possession of plot. We approached respondents number of times but\r\nthey kept on lingering on the matter on one pretext or the other by making\r\nwhimsical or illogical excuses and also insisted the complainant to take\r\nanother plot/unit but as and when the complainants intends to accept their\r\noffer, then on very next meeting, they changed their earlier proposal and\r\noffered some another proposal (emails attached). The respondents are pressurizing\r\nthe complainants to get an alternative plot/unit which is neither agreed\r\nbetween the parties nor acceptable/feasible to the complainants.</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n<b></b><i></i><u></u><sub></sub><sup></sup><strike></strike><br></p>','<p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:150%\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\'font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:11.0pt;line-height:150%;&#10;font-family:\"Arial\",\"sans-serif\"\'>It is, therefore, respectfully prayed that\r\nthe respondents may kindly be directed to refund the amount of Rs.26,06,301/-\r\nalong with interest over and above the interest which the complainants are\r\npaying to the HDFC bank from which they have availed the loan facility for\r\npurchase the property, from the date of execution of the agreement till the\r\nrealization of the amount, the complainants are also entitled to get a\r\ncompensation to the tune of Rs.5 Lakh on account of mental pain, agony and\r\nharassment suffered by them as provided U/s 14 (3) and Section 19 of the said\r\nAct. </span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:150%\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\'font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:11.0pt;line-height:150%;&#10;font-family:\"Arial\",\"sans-serif\"\'><span style=\"mso-tab-count:1\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span>The\r\nstrict action U/s 7 &amp; 8 is also required to be taken against the\r\nrespondents for violating the provisions of The Real Estate (Regulation &amp;\r\nDevelopment Act).</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\'font-family:\"Arial\",\"sans-serif\"\'></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:150%\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\'font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:11.0pt;line-height:150%;&#10;font-family:\"Arial\",\"sans-serif\"\'><span style=\"mso-tab-count:2\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span>Any\r\nother relief which the complainants seems entitled to by this Hon\'ble\r\nAuthority, may also be granted to the complainants in the interest of justice\r\nand equity. </span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\'font-family:\"Arial\",\"sans-serif\"\'></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:150%\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">&nbsp;</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n<b></b><i></i><u></u><sub></sub><sup></sup><strike></strike><br></p>',2776145.00,2606301.00,'2017-03-25 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p><br></p>','1','','2014-08-12 00:00:00','2014-09-26 00:00:00','Plot No. X122, Type -T, Ireo Waterfront Pvt. Lmt.','','',2,0,0,0,'gaurav4478','2019-03-16 17:27:43.000','gaurav4478','2019-03-16 17:27:43.000'),(1206,1273,'1273',1223,'9616498a-08f7-4464-9ca8-d1e8ddf49a77','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-01-20 16:05:07.000','RISHI KUMAR GUPTA','agamjund_advocate@yahoo.com',9780269386,0,253992356271,'V & PO MULLANPUR GARIBDASS','NEAR POLICE STATION',28,507,'140901','1','V & PO MULLANPUR GARIBDASS','NEAR POLICE STATION',28,507,'140901','AGAM KUMAR JUND','agamjund_advocate@yahoo.com',9780269387,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0351','SANSKRITI HOMES (DLF HYDE PARK)','DLF UNIVERSAL LTD. & SANSKRITI GOLDEN OAK REAL ESTATE PVT. LTD.','info@sanskritihomes.com',7814700800,0,'M/s. Sanskriti Golden Oak Real Estate Pvt. Ltd.,','DLF Pocket R-2, New Chandigarh Mullanpur',28,507,'140901','0','DLF Universal Ltd. ','SCO 190,191,192  Sector 8-C',6,128,'160017','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:13.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:Mangal;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi\">Applicant had (9\r\nAcres 37 Biswe i.e. 9.385 Acre) ancestral land at village Devi Nagar, S.A.S\r\nNagar. Respondent approached applicant for purchasing land. On being induced by\r\nthe representation of respondent, Applicant agreed to sell his land at Rs.3\r\nCrore per Acre. Agreement to sell @ 2 Crore 36 Lakh per Acre was signed between\r\nparties on 21.11.11. Respondent assured that balance amount will be given separately;\r\nas registered deed has to be executed under value to avoid state taxes i.e.\r\nRs.2 Crore 36 Lakh per acre. A separate MOU was prepared to adjust balance\r\namount of Rs.6 Crore of applicant. As per MOU,<b> </b>respondent had to give four plots of 500 Sq Yd of Rs.1 Crore 50\r\nlakh each to applicant. During gap period, without asking choice, respondent\r\nallotted four plots No.R-1/C-209, R-1/C-210, R-1/C-211 &amp; R-1/C-212 to\r\napplicant. On 29.05.12, applicant executed registered sale deed of 9.385 Acre land\r\nin favour of respondent, after receiving Rs 22,14,95,833/- along with\r\nconfirmation letter of four plots. For transferring plots in name of applicant\r\nas per MOU and to show a valid transaction for these four plots, on 28.03.13,\r\nrespondent had transferred Rs. 3 Cr 90 Lakh in account of applicant, i.e. Rs.\r\n97 Lakh 50 Thousand for each plot. Accordingly four cheques of Rs. 92,62,500/- each\r\nwere taken from the applicant by respondent. In this way respondent had taken\r\nback Rs.3,70,50,000/- from applicant. On 27.12.13, plot buyer’s agreement for\r\nfour plots separately were signed between applicant and respondent. Respondent\r\nissued demand notices of Rs.62,761/- on 15.10.13 and of Rs.26,45,532.60/- on\r\n15.11.14 for each plot. </span><span style=\"font-size:13.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Instead of paying actual balance amount of Rs.6 Crore to\r\napplicant, respondent has cheated applicant with Rs. 2 Crore 99 lakh. Till date\r\nplots possession has not been delivered and whole land of applicant has been\r\nutilized by respondent. Copy of representation/notice dated 22.12.2018 may\r\nkindly be read as facts of the case.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size:13.0pt;\r\nline-height:115%\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size: 13pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">Registration granted under section 5 of the Real\r\nEstate (Regulation and Development) Act, to the respondent may kindly be\r\nrevoked&nbsp;under Section 7(1) (d) of this act&nbsp;as the respondent promoter\r\nis indulges in unfair and fraudulent practices&nbsp;by cheating the applicant,\r\nafter preparing many documents and by not providing any clear information to\r\nthe applicant regarding the policy/procedure adopted by the company&nbsp;and\r\nhad created loss to the state exchequer by not paying the legal state\r\ntaxes.&nbsp;Respondent be directed to pay the actual amount of </span><span style=\"font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif; font-size: 17.3333px;\">Plot No. R1-C 209</span><span style=\"font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif; font-size: 13pt;\">&nbsp; &nbsp;(i.e. Rs. 1.5 Crore) purchased from the applicant along with interest, as\r\napplicant does not want to take any plot from them. Further compensation on\r\naccount of delaying the payment of the applicant by preparing false documents\r\njust to commit fraud with the applicant and the state as per the Rules of\r\nPunjab State Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Rules which provides\r\nState Bank of India highest marginal cost of lending rate plus 2% from the\r\nrespective date of deposit made by the complainants. Further directions may\r\nkindly be issued to the respondents to pay Rs. 10 Lacs to the applicant for\r\nmental and physical harassment and on the account of the deficiency in the\r\nservices and unfair trade practice committed by the respondents.&nbsp;Further\r\ndirections may kindly be issued to the respondents to pay Rs. 1,00,000/- on\r\naccount of litigation charges to the applicant.&nbsp;It is further prayed that\r\nthis Hon\'ble Tribunal may grant any other relief, which it deems fit and\r\nproper, in the facts and circumstances of the present case, in the interest of\r\njustice, equity and fair play.</span></p>',15000000.00,15000000.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:13.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif; font-size: 17.3333px;\">Complainant is filing this complaint in respect of Plot no. R1-C209 and Complainant is filing separate complaints for rest of three plots.</span><span style=\"font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif; font-size: 17.3333px;\">&nbsp;</span>As these complaints are outcome of single transaction between same parties. therefore all the complaints be heard together. Bank\r\nAccounts of the Respondent may kindly be freezed during the pendency of present\r\npetition.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:13.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Sale\r\nand purchase of Plots/Flats constructed therein the project of the respondent may\r\nkindly be stopped.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:13.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Respondent\r\nmay kindly be directed not to alter in the land or may be stopped from creating\r\nany third party right over the land in dispute.</span><span style=\"font-size:\r\n13.0pt;line-height:115%\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>','1','','2012-05-29 00:00:00','2011-11-21 00:00:00','R-1/C/209  DLF HYDE PARK, ESTATE PROJECT, NEW CHANDIGARH','','',2,0,0,0,'AGAM','2019-03-17 17:54:44.000','AGAM','2019-03-17 17:54:44.000'),(1207,1273,'1273',1223,'9616498a-08f7-4464-9ca8-d1e8ddf49a77','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-03-17 21:12:33.000','RISHI KUMAR GUPTA','agamjund_advocate@yahoo.com',9780269386,0,253992356271,'V & PO MULLANPUR GARIBDASS','NEAR POLICE STATION',28,507,'140901','1','V & PO MULLANPUR GARIBDASS','NEAR POLICE STATION',28,507,'140901','AGAM KUMAR JUND','agamjund_advocate@yahoo.com',9780269387,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0351','SANSKRITI HOMES (DLF HYDE PARK)','DLF UNIVERSAL LTD. & SANSKRITI GOLDEN OAK REAL ESTATE PVT. LTD.','info@sanskritihomes.com',7814700800,0,'M/s. Sanskriti Golden Oak Real Estate Pvt. Ltd.,','DLF Pocket R-2, New Chandigarh Mullanpur',28,507,'140901','0','DLF Universal Ltd. ','SCO 190,191,192  Sector 8-C',6,128,'160017','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:13.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:Mangal;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi\">Applicant had (9\r\nAcres 37 Biswe i.e. 9.385 Acre) ancestral land at village Devi Nagar, S.A.S\r\nNagar. Respondent approached applicant for purchasing land. On being induced by\r\nthe representation of respondent, Applicant agreed to sell his land at Rs.3\r\nCrore per Acre. Agreement to sell @ 2 Crore 36 Lakh per Acre was signed between\r\nparties on 21.11.11. Respondent assured that balance amount will be given separately;\r\nas registered deed has to be executed under value to avoid state taxes i.e.\r\nRs.2 Crore 36 Lakh per acre. A separate MOU was prepared to adjust balance\r\namount of Rs.6 Crore of applicant. As per MOU,<b> </b>respondent had to give four plots of 500 Sq Yd of Rs.1 Crore 50\r\nlakh each to applicant. During gap period, without asking choice, respondent\r\nallotted four plots No.R-1/C-209, R-1/C-210, R-1/C-211 &amp; R-1/C-212 to\r\napplicant. On 29.05.12, applicant executed registered sale deed of 9.385 Acre land\r\nin favour of respondent, after receiving Rs 22,14,95,833/- along with\r\nconfirmation letter of four plots. For transferring plots in name of applicant\r\nas per MOU and to show a valid transaction for these four plots, on 28.03.13,\r\nrespondent had transferred Rs. 3 Cr 90 Lakh in account of applicant, i.e. Rs.\r\n97 Lakh 50 Thousand for each plot. Accordingly four cheques of Rs. 92,62,500/- each\r\nwere taken from the applicant by respondent. In this way respondent had taken\r\nback Rs.3,70,50,000/- from applicant. On 27.12.13, plot buyer’s agreement for\r\nfour plots separately were signed between applicant and respondent. Respondent\r\nissued demand notices of Rs.62,761/- on 15.10.13 and of Rs.26,45,532.60/- on\r\n15.11.14 for each plot. </span><span style=\"font-size:13.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Instead of paying actual balance amount of Rs.6 Crore to\r\napplicant, respondent has cheated applicant with Rs. 2 Crore 99 lakh. Till date\r\nplots possession has not been delivered and whole land of applicant has been\r\nutilized by respondent. Copy of representation/notice dated 22.12.2018 may\r\nkindly be read as facts of the case.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size:13.0pt;\r\nline-height:115%\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size: 13pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">Registration granted under section 5 of the Real\r\nEstate (Regulation and Development) Act, to the respondent may kindly be\r\nrevoked&nbsp;under Section 7(1) (d) of this act&nbsp;as the respondent promoter\r\nis indulges in unfair and fraudulent practices&nbsp;by cheating the applicant,\r\nafter preparing many documents and by not providing any clear information to\r\nthe applicant regarding the policy/procedure adopted by the company&nbsp;and\r\nhad created loss to the state exchequer by not paying the legal state\r\ntaxes.&nbsp;Respondent be directed to pay the actual amount of </span><span style=\"font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif; font-size: 17.3333px;\">Plot No. R1-C 209</span><span style=\"font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif; font-size: 13pt;\">&nbsp; &nbsp;(i.e. Rs. 1.5 Crore) purchased from the applicant along with interest, as\r\napplicant does not want to take any plot from them. Further compensation on\r\naccount of delaying the payment of the applicant by preparing false documents\r\njust to commit fraud with the applicant and the state as per the Rules of\r\nPunjab State Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Rules which provides\r\nState Bank of India highest marginal cost of lending rate plus 2% from the\r\nrespective date of deposit made by the complainants. Further directions may\r\nkindly be issued to the respondents to pay Rs. 10 Lacs to the applicant for\r\nmental and physical harassment and on the account of the deficiency in the\r\nservices and unfair trade practice committed by the respondents.&nbsp;Further\r\ndirections may kindly be issued to the respondents to pay Rs. 1,00,000/- on\r\naccount of litigation charges to the applicant.&nbsp;It is further prayed that\r\nthis Hon\'ble Tribunal may grant any other relief, which it deems fit and\r\nproper, in the facts and circumstances of the present case, in the interest of\r\njustice, equity and fair play.</span></p>',15000000.00,15000000.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:13.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif; font-size: 17.3333px;\">Complainant is filing this complaint in respect of Plot no. R1-C209 and Complainant is filing separate complaints for rest of three plots.</span><span style=\"font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif; font-size: 17.3333px;\">&nbsp;</span>As these complaints are outcome of single transaction between same parties. therefore all the complaints be heard together.</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:13.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"> Bank\r\nAccounts of the Respondent may kindly be freezed during the pendency of present\r\npetition.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:13.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Sale\r\nand purchase of Plots/Flats constructed therein the project of the respondent may\r\nkindly be stopped.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size:13.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Respondent\r\nmay kindly be directed not to alter in the land or may be stopped from creating\r\nany third party right over the land in dispute.</span><span style=\"font-size:\r\n13.0pt;line-height:115%\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>','1','','2012-05-29 00:00:00','2011-11-21 00:00:00','R-1/C/209  DLF HYDE PARK, ESTATE PROJECT, NEW CHANDIGARH','','',1,1,0,0,'AGAM','2019-03-17 20:26:07.000','AGAM','2019-03-17 20:26:07.000'),(1208,1275,'1275',1353,'e8ac273a-1078-4419-9fe1-68696ab55f3e','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-03-17 21:38:59.000','Parvesh Bansal','parvesh.vicky@gmail.com',8054776864,0,0,'H. NO 124, Sector 2-A, Adarsh Nagar','Mandi Gobindgarh',28,204,'147301','1','H. NO 124, Sector 2-A, Adarsh Nagar','Mandi Gobindgarh',28,204,'147301','Gaurav Gupta','gaurav69g@gmail.com',9888139269,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0085','SUSHMA BUILDTECH\'S \'SUHMA GRANDE\'','BHARAT MITTAL','BHARAT@SUSHMABUILDTECH.COM',0,0,'Unit No. B-107, Business Complex at Elante Mall','1st Floor, Industrial Area, Phase – 1',6,128,'160009','1','Unit No. B-107, Business Complex at Elante Mall','1st Floor, Industrial Area, Phase – 1',6,128,'160009','1','<p><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font></p><p style=\"margin: 0in 0in 10pt;\"><font face=\"roboto, serif\">1. That the complainant applied for a Residential flat, in Respondent Project described as “SUSHMA CHANDIGARH GRANDE”. Respondent allotted the Residential Flat No.I701 on floor 7th in tower-I, 2250 Sq. Ft (Super Area) located at village Bishangarh and Bishanpura, MC Zirakpur, Mohali, to the complainant vide Allotment Letter dated 01.12.2014(Annexure C-1). \r\n</font></p><p style=\"margin: 0in 0in 10pt;\"><font face=\"roboto, serif\">2. That thereafter on requests of complainant respondent entered into an Apartment Buyers Agreement on 13.12.2016(Annexure C-2). The total Sale Price of the Flat was Rs. 71,67,500/- The complainants were required to make payments as per the Construction linked payment plan. \r\n</font></p><p style=\"margin: 0in 0in 10pt;\"><font face=\"roboto, serif\">4. That complainants as per time to time demands of the respondent builder paid total payment of Rs.62,50,088/-to respondent. Copy of demand letter, Payment receipts and  account statement are attached as Annexure C-3 to C-5. \r\n</font></p><p style=\"margin: 0in 0in 10pt;\"><font face=\"roboto, serif\">5. That builder had to deliver the fully developed possession of the said flat along with all basic amenities, to the complainant within 6 months from the date of execution of Apartment Buyers Agreement i.e till 13.06.2017. However respondent failed to deliver possession till today. It is pertinent to mention that the respondent has charged interest @24% per annum from the applicant for delay in making payment to him. However the respondent for his delay not paying any penalty to complainant. Moreover respondent not informing about the status of construction and date of delivery of possession. Complainant sent an email dated 12.03.2019 Annexure C-6 and no response to the mail was given by respondent. The complainant cannot wait for indefinite period. Hence the complainant is filing present&nbsp;</font></p>','<p><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:0in;\r\nmargin-left:1.0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\ntext-indent:-.25in;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level2 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\">a.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">Allow\r\nthe present complaint and direct the Respondents to immediately complete the\r\ndevelopment of project and construction of the apartment and deliver the\r\npossession of the apartment along with all amenities as per buyers agreement.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:0in;\r\nmargin-left:1.0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\ntext-indent:-.25in;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level2 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\">b.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">To&nbsp; pay interest to the Complainant from the\r\nrespective date of payment to till the date of delivery of the possession of\r\nthe apartment in accordance with&nbsp; the Real Estate Regulation and\r\ndevelopment Act 2016;</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:0in;\r\nmargin-left:1.0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;\r\ntext-indent:-.25in;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level2 lfo1\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\">c.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">Any\r\nother relief as deemed fit &amp; proper in the peculiar circumstances of the\r\npresent lis may also be granted to the Complainant; in the interest of justice,\r\nfair play &amp; equity.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin: 0in 0in 10pt;\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>',7167500.00,6250088.00,'2017-06-13 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>NA</p>','1','','2014-12-01 00:00:00','2016-12-13 00:00:00','I-703','','',1,0,0,0,'ParveshBansal','2019-03-17 20:43:55.000','ParveshBansal','2019-03-17 20:43:55.000'),(1209,1225,'1225',1223,'9616498a-08f7-4464-9ca8-d1e8ddf49a77','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-03-18 17:29:56.000','RISHI KUMAR GUPTA','agamjund_advocate@yahoo.com',9780269386,0,253992356271,'V & PO MULLANPUR GARIBDASS','NEAR POLICE STATION',28,507,'140901','1','V & PO MULLANPUR GARIBDASS','NEAR POLICE STATION',28,507,'140901','AGAM KUMAR JUND','agamjund_advocate@yahoo.com',9780269387,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0351','SANSKRITI HOMES','DLF UNIVERSAL LTD. & SANSKRITI GOLDEN OAK REAL ESTATE PVT. LTD.','info@sanskritihomes.com',7814700800,0,'M/s. Sanskriti Golden Oak Real Estate Pvt. Ltd.,','DLF Pocket R2, New Chandigarh (Mullanpur)',28,507,'140901','1','DLF Universal Ltd. ','SCO 190,191,192  Sector 8-C',6,128,'160017','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif; font-size: 13pt;\">Applicant had (9 Acres 37 Biswe i.e. 9.385 Acre)\r\nancestral land at village Devi Nagar, S.A.S Nagar. Respondent approached\r\napplicant for purchasing land. On being induced by the representation of\r\nrespondent, Applicant agreed to sell his land at Rs.3 Crore per Acre. Agreement\r\nto sell @ 2 Crore 36 Lakh per Acre was signed between parties on 21.11.11.\r\nRespondent assured that balance amount will be given separately; as registered\r\ndeed has to be executed under value to avoid state taxes i.e. Rs.2 Crore 36\r\nLakh per acre. A separate MOU was prepared to adjust balance amount of Rs.6\r\nCrore of applicant. As per MOU,</span><b style=\"font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif; font-size: 13pt;\">&nbsp;</b><span style=\"font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif; font-size: 13pt;\">respondent had to give four plots\r\nof 500 Sq Yd of Rs.1 Crore 50 lakh each to applicant. During gap period,\r\nwithout asking choice, respondent allotted four plots No.R-1/C-209, R-1/C-210, R-1/C-211\r\n&amp; R-1/C-212 to applicant. On 29.05.12, applicant executed registered sale\r\ndeed of 9.385 Acre land in favour of respondent, after receiving Rs\r\n22,14,95,833/- along with confirmation letter of four plots. For transferring\r\nplots in name of applicant as per MOU and to show a valid transaction for these\r\nfour plots, on 28.03.13, respondent had transferred Rs. 3 Cr 90 Lakh in account\r\nof applicant, i.e. Rs. 97 Lakh 50 Thousand for each plot. Accordingly four\r\ncheques of Rs. 92,62,500/- each were taken from the applicant by respondent. In\r\nthis way respondent had taken back Rs.3,70,50,000/- from applicant. On\r\n27.12.13, plot buyer’s agreement for four plots separately were signed between\r\napplicant and respondent. Respondent issued demand notices of Rs.62,761/- on\r\n15.10.13 and of Rs.26,45,532.60/- on 15.11.14 for each plot.&nbsp;Instead of\r\npaying actual balance amount of Rs.6 Crore to applicant, respondent has cheated\r\napplicant with Rs. 2 Crore 99 lakh. Till date plots possession has not been\r\ndelivered and whole land of applicant has been utilized by respondent. Copy of\r\nrepresentation/notice dated 22.12.2018 may kindly be read as facts of the\r\ncase.&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 13pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:\r\njustify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;line-height:200%;tab-stops:0in\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:11.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-bidi-theme-font:\r\nminor-bidi\">&nbsp;&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 13pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">Registration granted under section 5 of the Real\r\nEstate (Regulation and Development) Act, to the respondent may kindly be\r\nrevoked&nbsp;under Section 7(1) (d) of this act&nbsp;as the respondent promoter\r\nis indulges in unfair and fraudulent practices&nbsp;by cheating the applicant,\r\nafter preparing many documents and by not providing any clear information to\r\nthe applicant regarding the policy/procedure adopted by the company&nbsp;and\r\nhad created loss to the state exchequer by not paying the legal state\r\ntaxes.&nbsp;Respondent be directed to pay the actual amount of&nbsp;Plot No.\r\nR1-C 210&nbsp; &nbsp;(i.e. Rs. 1.5 Crore) purchased from the applicant along\r\nwith interest, as applicant does not want to take any plot from them. Further\r\ncompensation on account of delaying the payment of the applicant by preparing\r\nfalse documents just to commit fraud with the applicant and the state as per\r\nthe Rules of Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Rules which\r\nprovides State Bank of India highest marginal cost of lending rate plus 2% from\r\nthe respective date of deposit made by the complainants. Further directions may\r\nkindly be issued to the respondents to pay Rs. 10 Lacs to the applicant for\r\nmental and physical harassment and on the account of the deficiency in the\r\nservices and unfair trade practice committed by the respondents.&nbsp;Further\r\ndirections may kindly be issued to the respondents to pay Rs. 1,00,000/- on\r\naccount of litigation charges to the applicant.&nbsp;It is further prayed that\r\nthis Hon\'ble Tribunal may grant any other relief, which it deems fit and\r\nproper, in the facts and circumstances of the present case, in the interest of\r\njustice, equity and fair play.<o:p></o:p></span></p>',15000000.00,15000000.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:7.5pt;text-align:justify;text-justify:\r\ninter-ideograph;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size: 13pt; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif;\">Complainant\r\nis filing this complaint in respect of Plot no. R1-C210 and Complainant is\r\nfiling separate complaints for rest of three plots.&nbsp;As these complaints\r\nare outcome of single transaction between same parties. therefore all the\r\ncomplaints be heard together.</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:7.5pt;text-align:justify;text-justify:\r\ninter-ideograph;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size: 13pt; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif;\"> Bank Accounts of the Respondent may kindly be\r\nfreezed during the pendency of present petition.</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:7.5pt;text-align:justify;text-justify:\r\ninter-ideograph;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size: 13pt; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif;\">Sale\r\nand purchase of Plots/Flats constructed therein the project of the respondent\r\nmay kindly be stopped.</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:7.5pt;text-align:justify;text-justify:\r\ninter-ideograph;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size: 13pt; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif;\">Respondent\r\nmay kindly be directed not to alter in the land or may be stopped from creating\r\nany third party right over the land in dispute.</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>','1','','2012-05-29 00:00:00','2011-11-21 00:00:00','R1-C210','','',1,1,0,0,'AGAM','2019-03-17 20:50:24.000','AGAM','2019-03-17 20:50:24.000'),(1210,1334,'1334',1361,'a52599d4-e47a-4877-8e30-d95c9ef9cf7f','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-02-26 10:20:11.000','SUMAN DHAUNDIYAL','kailashicwai@gmail.com',9818401409,0,0,'D-102,ARYA SAMAJ ROAD','UTTAM NAGAR',10,628,'110059','1','D-102,ARYA SAMAJ ROAD','UTTAM NAGAR',10,628,'110059','Ved Parkash','csvedparkash@gmail.com',7837223098,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0096','SBP HOUSING PARK','AMAN SINGLA','info@sbpgroup.in',9316004240,0,'SCO-146-148','1st floor sector -43B',6,128,'160043','1','SCO-146-148','1st floor sector -43B',6,128,'160043','1','<p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"background: white; margin: 0px 0px 0px 72px; text-align: justify; line-height: 12.65pt;\">That the complainant Ms Suman Dhaundiyal D/o Shri Harish Dhaundiyal, resident of House No D-102, Arya Samaj Road, Uttam Nagar, New Delhi booked a flat No 950, Floor No 9, Tower-04 in SBP Housing Park Project at Village Rauni, Tehsil Derabassi, District Mohali, Punjab vide application dated 10.01.2013, which is promoted by M/s Singla Builders &amp; Promoters Limited, wherein after mentioned as Respondent.The complainant paid booking amount of Rs. 3,82,500/- to the respondent as per details annexed at Annexure C/1(Colly). That the respondent issued an allotment letter dated 20.01.2013 and entered into an agreement for sale with the complainant dated 20.01.2013 containing detailed terms and conditions which is annexed herewith as C/II(Colly). That as per the allotment letter/agreement for sale, the total sales consideration for the allotted unit was Rs. 25,50,000/-.&nbsp; As per the agreement for sale, the possession was to be delivered by 31.12.2014 as per clause 4(a) (i) of Article 4 under the heading of Possession. That as per the payment plan specified in clause 2(c) (i) of Article 2 under the heading of Sales Consideration, the complainant made further payment of Rs. 3,82,500/- vide cheque No 642627 on 17.04.2013 which was duly acknowledged by the respondent and a payment receipt No HP566 dated 19.04.2013 was issued which is annexed herewith as Annexure C/III. That the complainant paid an amount of Rs. 3,82,500/- on 22.08.2013 from the loan account of the axis bank, and also made subsequent payments dated 3.10.2013 of Rs. 3,82,500/-, 21.11.2014 of Rs. 2,55,000/-, 6.06.2016 of Rs. 2,66,321/-, 17.09.2016 of Rs. 1,33,620/-, 28.12.2016 of Rs. 1,33,238/-, 16.12.2015 of Rs. 1,87,338/-. A copy of bank statement from 22.08.2013 to 10.01.2017 is annexed herewith as annexure C/IV. That complainant was served with a demand letter dated 11.04.2017 asking to pay an amount of Rs. 192,675/- which also acknowledged the payments made by the complainant of Rs. 25,05,517/- which&nbsp; is at C/V.</p>','<p><br></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"background: white; margin: 0px 0px 0px 75.6px; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\'margin: 0px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: \"Verdana\",\"sans-serif\";\'>&nbsp;</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n<font face=\"Times New Roman\"></font>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">The\r\noffer of possession was issued on 5.05.2017 along with the final demand letter.\r\nThe said offer of possession was contested by the complainant vide email dated\r\n7.06.2017 asking for the occupancy /completion certificate. These documents are\r\nannexed herewith as Annexure C/VI(Colly). </span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">That\r\nthe respondent served legal notice to the complainant on 10.12.2018 to make\r\npayment of Rs. 1,82,869/- within 15 days. The said legal notice was replied by\r\nthe complainant on 18.12.2018 again asking the respondent about the\r\ncompletion/occupancy certificate. Without considering the queries of the\r\ncomplainant, the respondent issued Second Legal Notice dated 28.12.2018\r\ndemanding an amount of Rs. 182,869/-. The documents are annexed herewith as\r\nAnnexure C/VII (Colly). </span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">The\r\nrespondent issued termination/cancellation notice to the complainant on\r\n17.01.2019 and asked the complainant to seek refund of the amount as per the\r\nterms and conditions of the buyers’ agreement executed between the\r\ncomplainant/respondent. The said termination notice is annexed herewith as\r\nAnnexure C/VIII.</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">The\r\nproject “SBP housing Park” is a RERA registered Project with Regn Number\r\nPBRERA-SAS79-PR0096, being an ongoing project. Therefore, the provisions of the Act\r\nwould apply with respect to offer of possession, refund, interest and\r\ncompensation etc in the present case.</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">The\r\nrespondent has not been able to offer possession of the allotted unit within\r\nthe specified period as per builder buyer agreement and thus violated the\r\nprovisions of the Section 18 of the Act. </span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">It\r\nis humbly prayed that the respondent may be directed to offer possession of the\r\nallotted unit after obtaining completion/occupancy certificate by setting aside\r\nthe cancellation letter issued to the complainant. </span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><br></p><p>\r\n\r\n<b></b><i></i><u></u><sub></sub><sup></sup><strike></strike><br></p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p><span style=\"display: inline !important; float: none; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: roboto; font-size: 12pt; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: 115%; orphans: 2; text-align: justify; text-decoration: none; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; word-spacing: 0px;\">It\r\nis further prayed that respondent may be directed to pay interest as per\r\nprovisions of RERA Act/Rules for the delayed period till the possession is\r\noffered.</span><b></b><i></i><u></u><sub></sub><sup></sup><strike></strike><br></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'sumandhaundiyal','2019-03-18 10:35:04.000','sumandhaundiyal','2019-03-18 10:35:04.000'),(1211,1334,'1334',1361,'a52599d4-e47a-4877-8e30-d95c9ef9cf7f','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-03-18 10:47:02.000','SUMAN DHAUNDIYAL','kailashicwai@gmail.com',9818401409,0,0,'D-102,ARYA SAMAJ ROAD','UTTAM NAGAR',10,628,'110059','1','D-102,ARYA SAMAJ ROAD','UTTAM NAGAR',10,628,'110059','Ved Parkash','csvedparkash@gmail.com',7837223098,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PR0096','SBP HOUSING PARK','AMAN SINGLA','info@sbpgroup.in',9316004240,0,'SCO-146-148','1st floor sector -43B',6,128,'160043','1','SCO-146-148','1st floor sector -43B',6,128,'160043','1','<p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"background: white; margin: 0px 0px 0px 72px; text-align: justify; line-height: 12.65pt;\">That the complainant Ms Suman Dhaundiyal D/o Shri Harish Dhaundiyal, resident of House No D-102, Arya Samaj Road, Uttam Nagar, New Delhi booked a flat No 950, Floor No 9, Tower-04 in SBP Housing Park Project at Village Rauni, Tehsil Derabassi, District Mohali, Punjab vide application dated 10.01.2013, which is promoted by M/s Singla Builders &amp; Promoters Limited, wherein after mentioned as Respondent.The complainant paid booking amount of Rs. 3,82,500/- to the respondent as per details annexed at Annexure C/1(Colly). That the respondent issued an allotment letter dated 20.01.2013 and entered into an agreement for sale with the complainant dated 20.01.2013 containing detailed terms and conditions which is annexed herewith as C/II(Colly). That as per the allotment letter/agreement for sale, the total sales consideration for the allotted unit was Rs. 25,50,000/-.&nbsp; As per the agreement for sale, the possession was to be delivered by 31.12.2014 as per clause 4(a) (i) of Article 4 under the heading of Possession. That as per the payment plan specified in clause 2(c) (i) of Article 2 under the heading of Sales Consideration, the complainant made further payment of Rs. 3,82,500/- vide cheque No 642627 on 17.04.2013 which was duly acknowledged by the respondent and a payment receipt No HP566 dated 19.04.2013 was issued which is annexed herewith as Annexure C/III. That the complainant paid an amount of Rs. 3,82,500/- on 22.08.2013 from the loan account of the axis bank, and also made subsequent payments dated 3.10.2013 of Rs. 3,82,500/-, 21.11.2014 of Rs. 2,55,000/-, 6.06.2016 of Rs. 2,66,321/-, 17.09.2016 of Rs. 1,33,620/-, 28.12.2016 of Rs. 1,33,238/-, 16.12.2015 of Rs. 1,87,338/-. A copy of bank statement from 22.08.2013 to 10.01.2017 is annexed herewith as annexure C/IV. That complainant was served with a demand letter dated 11.04.2017 asking to pay an amount of Rs. 192,675/- which also acknowledged the payments made by the complainant of Rs. 25,05,517/- which&nbsp; is at C/V.</p>','<p><br></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"background: white; margin: 0px 0px 0px 75.6px; text-align: justify; line-height: normal;\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\'margin: 0px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: \"Verdana\",\"sans-serif\";\'>&nbsp;</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n<font face=\"Times New Roman\"></font>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">The\r\noffer of possession was issued on 5.05.2017 along with the final demand letter.\r\nThe said offer of possession was contested by the complainant vide email dated\r\n7.06.2017 asking for the occupancy /completion certificate. These documents are\r\nannexed herewith as Annexure C/VI(Colly). </span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">That\r\nthe respondent served legal notice to the complainant on 10.12.2018 to make\r\npayment of Rs. 1,82,869/- within 15 days. The said legal notice was replied by\r\nthe complainant on 18.12.2018 again asking the respondent about the\r\ncompletion/occupancy certificate. Without considering the queries of the\r\ncomplainant, the respondent issued Second Legal Notice dated 28.12.2018\r\ndemanding an amount of Rs. 182,869/-. The documents are annexed herewith as\r\nAnnexure C/VII (Colly). </span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">The\r\nrespondent issued termination/cancellation notice to the complainant on\r\n17.01.2019 and asked the complainant to seek refund of the amount as per the\r\nterms and conditions of the buyers’ agreement executed between the\r\ncomplainant/respondent. The said termination notice is annexed herewith as\r\nAnnexure C/VIII.</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">The\r\nproject “SBP housing Park” is a RERA registered Project with Regn Number\r\nPBRERA-SAS79-PR0096, being an ongoing project. Therefore, the provisions of the Act\r\nwould apply with respect to offer of possession, refund, interest and\r\ncompensation etc in the present case.</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">The\r\nrespondent has not been able to offer possession of the allotted unit within\r\nthe specified period as per builder buyer agreement and thus violated the\r\nprovisions of the Section 18 of the Act. </span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN\">It\r\nis humbly prayed that the respondent may be directed to offer possession of the\r\nallotted unit after obtaining completion/occupancy certificate by setting aside\r\nthe cancellation letter issued to the complainant. </span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><br></p><p>\r\n\r\n<b></b><i></i><u></u><sub></sub><sup></sup><strike></strike><br></p>',2550000.00,2505517.00,'2014-12-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p><span style=\"display: inline !important; float: none; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: roboto; font-size: 12pt; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: 115%; orphans: 2; text-align: justify; text-decoration: none; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; word-spacing: 0px;\">It\r\nis further prayed that respondent may be directed to pay interest as per\r\nprovisions of RERA Act/Rules for the delayed period till the possession is\r\noffered.</span><b></b><i></i><u></u><sub></sub><sup></sup><strike></strike><br></p>','1','','2013-01-20 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Flat no-950, Floor-9, Tower-4, SBP Housing Park. Vill-Rauni, Derabassi, Distt-Mohali','','',1,1,0,0,'sumandhaundiyal','2019-03-18 10:38:13.000','sumandhaundiyal','2019-03-18 10:38:13.000'),(1212,1357,'1357',1431,'0787530d-1e75-4c59-a072-b71ad9aa4a1f','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-03-18 12:15:29.000','Anuradha Sharma','radha.anu12175@gmail.com',9988802712,0,0,'27 E, New Kitchlu Nagar','Opposite Radha Swami Satsang Ghar',28,366,'141001','1','27 E, New Kitchlu Nagar','Opposite Radha Swami Satsang Ghar',28,366,'141001','prabhjot Singh Sachdeva','',9988126268,1615009615,'Promoter','PBRERA-LDH45-PR0052','Ireo Waterfront Pvt. Ltd.','Varun Khanna','varun.khanna@ireo.in',0,0,'Ireo Campus, Archview Drive, Ireo City','Golf Course Extension Road, Sector 59',13,5,'122101','1','Ireo Campus, Archview Drive, Ireo City','Golf Course Extension Road, Sector 59',13,5,'122101','1','<p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:150%\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\'font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:\"Arial\",\"sans-serif\"\'>Brief\r\nfacts of the complaint are, Complainants had booked a Plot with the respondents\r\nin November 2013. The respondents had allotted Plot Type-T-Plot-X122 having\r\narea of 126.05 sq yards and the agreement to the effect was executed on\r\n26.09.2014 (copy enclosed). Total sale consideration of the said plot is\r\nRs.27,76,145/- The complainants had made the payments, by availing bank loan of\r\nRs.17,66,512/- lacs @ 8.80%, as and when demanded <span style=\"mso-spacerun:yes\">&nbsp;</span>by the respondents and till\r\ndateRs.26,06,301/-<span style=\"mso-spacerun:yes\">&nbsp; </span>had been paid in\r\ntotal (Annexure and relevant documents enclosed). As per the terms of agreement\r\nnotice of completion is to be given by the respondents within the period of 24\r\nmonths + 180 days (Grace Period) i.e. by 25.03.2017. But till date i.e. more\r\nthan four years from the date of execution of agreement respondents had not\r\ndelivered the possession of plot. We approached respondents number of times but\r\nthey kept on lingering on the matter on one pretext or the other by making\r\nwhimsical or illogical excuses and also insisted the complainant to take\r\nanother plot/unit but as and when the complainants intends to accept their\r\noffer, then on very next meeting, they changed their earlier proposal and\r\noffered some another proposal (emails attached). The respondents are pressurizing\r\nthe complainants to get an alternative plot/unit which is neither agreed\r\nbetween the parties nor acceptable/feasible to the complainants.</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n<b></b><i></i><u></u><sub></sub><sup></sup><strike></strike><br></p>','<p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:150%\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\'font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:11.0pt;line-height:150%;&#10;font-family:\"Arial\",\"sans-serif\"\'>It is, therefore, respectfully prayed that\r\nthe respondents may kindly be directed to refund the amount of Rs.26,06,301/-\r\nalong with interest over and above the interest which the complainants are\r\npaying to the HDFC bank from which they have availed the loan facility for\r\npurchase the property, from the date of execution of the agreement till the\r\nrealization of the amount, the complainants are also entitled to get a\r\ncompensation to the tune of Rs.5 Lakh on account of mental pain, agony and\r\nharassment suffered by them as provided U/s 14 (3) and Section 19 of the said\r\nAct. </span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:150%\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\'font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:11.0pt;line-height:150%;&#10;font-family:\"Arial\",\"sans-serif\"\'><span style=\"mso-tab-count:1\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span>The\r\nstrict action U/s 7 &amp; 8 is also required to be taken against the\r\nrespondents for violating the provisions of The Real Estate (Regulation &amp;\r\nDevelopment Act).</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\'font-family:\"Arial\",\"sans-serif\"\'></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:150%\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\'font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:11.0pt;line-height:150%;&#10;font-family:\"Arial\",\"sans-serif\"\'><span style=\"mso-tab-count:2\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span>Any\r\nother relief which the complainants seems entitled to by this Hon\'ble\r\nAuthority, may also be granted to the complainants in the interest of justice\r\nand equity. </span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\'font-family:\"Arial\",\"sans-serif\"\'></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:150%\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">&nbsp;</span></p><p>\r\n\r\n<b></b><i></i><u></u><sub></sub><sup></sup><strike></strike><br></p>',2776145.00,2606301.00,'2017-03-25 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p><br></p>','1','','2014-08-12 00:00:00','2014-09-26 00:00:00','Plot No. X122, Type -T, Ireo Waterfront Pvt. Lmt.','','',1,1,0,0,'radha.anu12175','2019-03-18 12:15:22.000','radha.anu12175','2019-03-18 12:15:22.000'),(1213,1360,'1360',1439,'35c554d4-d838-4da3-81f7-e90909ac017c','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Madhur Kumaria','madhur.kumaria@gmail.com',9815846949,0,0,'Flat No. 940, Second Floor','Sector 115, Gillco Palms',28,507,'140301','1','Flat No. 940, Second Floor','Sector 115, Gillco Palms',28,507,'140301','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0037','Gillco Developers and Builders Pvt Ltd','Dhaliwal','gillcovalley@gmail.com',9988700097,0,'Gillco Palms','Sector 115',28,507,'140301','1','Gillco Palms','Sector 115',28,507,'140301','0','<p>I am having a flat in Gillco Palms (Sector 115). As the time of flat booking/agreement (Aug 2016) the date of possession was given to me was December 2016. In our agreement its clearly mentioned the following clause:</p><p style=\"margin-left: 25px;\">39. That the BUILDER, subject to force mature, shall offer the possession of the SAID APARTMENT to the BUYER within 04 months from the date of this agreement with a grace period of 02 months subject to the payment of SAID CONSIDERATION and other charges, strictly in accordance with the PAYMENT SCHEDULE.<br></p><p style=\"margin-left: 25px;\">42. That in the event the BUILDER delays in handing over possession, the BUILDER shall pay compensation @ Rs. 5/- per sq.ft. for every months delay beyond as per the clause no 39, which shall be adjusted at the time of calculation of the final bill.<br></p><p>Here I would like to mention that there was no delay in payment from my side at any point of time. We got the possession of the said flat in Aug 2017, which is 6 months delay from grace period of 2 months. Since Aug 2017, I am in touch with Builder\'s official staff and even contacted their management for the payment. They are delaying the payment without giving any genuine reason. It is also mentioned in the same agreement that if I delay in any payment, I will need to pay additional interest to builder @15%.<br></p><p>I would like to appeal and register a complaint against the builder so that they make the payment including interest. Also as its now been 19 months since I am in continues touch with them.<br></p>','<p>Rs. 70,591/- is the total due from builder\'s end including interest till date.<br></p>',4345000.00,4345000.00,'2016-12-12 00:00:00.000','2017-08-16 00:00:00.000','<p>NA</p>','1','','2017-08-12 00:00:00','2016-08-22 00:00:00','940','','',2,0,0,0,'madhur.kumaria','2019-03-18 12:47:39.000','madhur.kumaria','2019-03-18 12:47:39.000'),(1214,1360,'1360',1439,'35c554d4-d838-4da3-81f7-e90909ac017c','FormTypeM',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Madhur Kumaria','madhur.kumaria@gmail.com',9815846949,0,0,'Flat No. 940, Second Floor','Sector 115, Gillco Palms',28,507,'140301','1','Flat No. 940, Second Floor','Sector 115, Gillco Palms',28,507,'140301','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0037','Gillco Developers and Builders Pvt Ltd','Gillco Developers and Builders Pvt Ltd','gillcovalley@gmail.com',9988700097,0,'Gillco Palms','Sector 115',28,507,'140301','1','Gillco Palms','Sector 115',28,507,'140301','0','<p>I am having a flat in Gillco Palms (Sector 115). As the time of flat booking/agreement (Aug 2016) the date of possession was given to me was December 2016. In our agreement its clearly mentioned the following clause:</p><p style=\"margin-left: 25px;\">39. That the BUILDER, subject to force mature, shall offer the possession of the SAID APARTMENT to the BUYER within 04 months from the date of this agreement with a grace period of 02 months subject to the payment of SAID CONSIDERATION and other charges, strictly in accordance with the PAYMENT SCHEDULE.<br></p><p style=\"margin-left: 25px;\">42. That in the event the BUILDER delays in handing over possession, the BUILDER shall pay compensation @ Rs. 5/- per sq.ft. for every months delay beyond as per the clause no 39, which shall be adjusted at the time of calculation of the final bill.<br></p><p>Here I would like to mention that there was no delay in payment from my side at any point of time. We got the possession of the said flat in Aug 2017, which is 6 months delay from grace period of 2 months. Since Aug 2017, I am in touch with Builder\'s official staff and even contacted their management for the payment. They are delaying the payment without giving any genuine reason. It is also mentioned in the same agreement that if I delay in any payment, I will need to pay additional interest to builder @15%.<br></p><p>I would like to appeal and register a complaint against the builder so that they make the payment including interest. Also as its now been 19 months since I am in continues touch with them.<br></p>','<p>Rs. 70,591/- is the total due from builder\'s end including interest till date.<br></p>',4345000.00,4345000.00,'2016-12-12 00:00:00.000','2017-08-16 00:00:00.000','<p>NA</p>','1','','2017-08-12 00:00:00','2016-08-22 00:00:00','940','','',1,0,0,0,'madhur.kumaria','2019-03-18 13:31:22.000','madhur.kumaria','2019-03-18 13:31:22.000'),(1215,1361,'1361',1223,'9616498a-08f7-4464-9ca8-d1e8ddf49a77','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-03-18 18:55:26.000','AGAM JUND','agamjund_advocate@yahoo.com',9780269386,0,253992356271,'V & PO MULLANPUR GARIBDASS','RATWARA SAHIB ROAD',28,507,'140901','1','V & PO MULLANPUR GARIBDASS','RATWARA SAHIB ROAD',28,507,'140901','AGAM KUMAR JUND','agamjund_advocate@yahoo.com',9780269387,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0351','Sanskriti Homes (DLF Hyde Park)','DLF UNIVERSAL LTD. & SANSKRITI GOLDEN OAK REAL ESTATE PVT. LTD.','info@sanskritihomes.com',7814700800,0,'M/s. Sanskriti Golden Oak Real Estate Pvt. Ltd.,','DLF Pocket R-2, New Chandigarh Mullanpur',28,507,'140901','0','DLF Universal Ltd. ','SCO 190,191,192  Sector 8-C',6,128,'160017','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 13pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">Applicant had (9 Acres 37 Biswe i.e. 9.385 Acre)\r\nancestral land at village Devi Nagar, S.A.S Nagar. Respondent approached\r\napplicant for purchasing land. On being induced by the representation of\r\nrespondent, Applicant agreed to sell his land at Rs.3 Crore per Acre. Agreement\r\nto sell @ 2 Crore 36 Lakh per Acre was signed between parties on 21.11.11.\r\nRespondent assured that balance amount will be given separately; as registered\r\ndeed has to be executed under value to avoid state taxes i.e. Rs.2 Crore 36\r\nLakh per acre. A separate MOU was prepared to adjust balance amount of Rs.6\r\nCrore of applicant. As per MOU,<b>&nbsp;</b>respondent had to give four plots\r\nof 500 Sq Yd of Rs.1 Crore 50 lakh each to applicant. During gap period,\r\nwithout asking choice, respondent allotted four plots No.R-1/C-209, R-1/C-210, R-1/C-211\r\n&amp; R-1/C-212 to applicant. On 29.05.12, applicant executed registered sale\r\ndeed of 9.385 Acre land in favour of respondent, after receiving Rs\r\n22,14,95,833/- along with confirmation letter of four plots. For transferring\r\nplots in name of applicant as per MOU and to show a valid transaction for these\r\nfour plots, on 28.03.13, respondent had transferred Rs. 3 Cr 90 Lakh in account\r\nof applicant, i.e. Rs. 97 Lakh 50 Thousand for each plot. Accordingly four\r\ncheques of Rs. 92,62,500/- each were taken from the applicant by respondent. In\r\nthis way respondent had taken back Rs.3,70,50,000/- from applicant. On\r\n27.12.13, plot buyer’s agreement for four plots separately were signed between\r\napplicant and respondent. Respondent issued demand notices of Rs.62,761/- on\r\n15.10.13 and of Rs.26,45,532.60/- on 15.11.14 for each plot.&nbsp;Instead of\r\npaying actual balance amount of Rs.6 Crore to applicant, respondent has cheated\r\napplicant with Rs. 2 Crore 99 lakh. Till date plots possession has not been\r\ndelivered and whole land of applicant has been utilized by respondent. Copy of\r\nrepresentation/notice dated 22.12.2018 may kindly be read as facts of the\r\ncase.&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 13pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">Registration granted under section 5 of the Real\r\nEstate (Regulation and Development) Act, to the respondent may kindly be\r\nrevoked&nbsp;under Section 7(1) (d) of this act&nbsp;as the respondent promoter\r\nis indulges in unfair and fraudulent practices&nbsp;by cheating the applicant,\r\nafter preparing many documents and by not providing any clear information to\r\nthe applicant regarding the policy/procedure adopted by the company&nbsp;and\r\nhad created loss to the state exchequer by not paying the legal state\r\ntaxes.&nbsp;Respondent be directed to pay the actual amount of&nbsp;Plot No.\r\nR1-C 211&nbsp; &nbsp;(i.e. Rs. 1.5 Crore) purchased from the applicant along\r\nwith interest, as applicant does not want to take any plot from them. Further\r\ncompensation on account of delaying the payment of the applicant by preparing\r\nfalse documents just to commit fraud with the applicant and the state as per\r\nthe Rules of Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Rules which\r\nprovides State Bank of India highest marginal cost of lending rate plus 2% from\r\nthe respective date of deposit made by the complainants. Further directions may\r\nkindly be issued to the respondents to pay Rs. 10 Lacs to the applicant for\r\nmental and physical harassment and on the account of the deficiency in the\r\nservices and unfair trade practice committed by the respondents.&nbsp;Further\r\ndirections may kindly be issued to the respondents to pay Rs. 1,00,000/- on\r\naccount of litigation charges to the applicant.&nbsp;It is further prayed that\r\nthis Hon\'ble Tribunal may grant any other relief, which it deems fit and\r\nproper, in the facts and circumstances of the present case, in the interest of\r\njustice, equity and fair play.<o:p></o:p></span></p>',15000000.00,15000000.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:7.5pt;text-align:justify;text-justify:\r\ninter-ideograph;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size: 13pt; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif;\">Complainant\r\nis filing this complaint in respect of Plot no. R1-C211 and Complainant is\r\nfiling separate complaints for rest of three plots.&nbsp;As these complaints\r\nare outcome of single transaction between same parties. Therefore all the\r\ncomplaints be heard together. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:7.5pt;text-align:justify;text-justify:\r\ninter-ideograph;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size: 13pt; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif;\">Bank\r\nAccounts of the Respondent may kindly be freezed during the pendency of present\r\npetition.</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:7.5pt;text-align:justify;text-justify:\r\ninter-ideograph;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size: 13pt; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif;\">Sale\r\nand purchase of Plots/Flats constructed therein the project of the respondent\r\nmay kindly be stopped.</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:7.5pt;text-align:justify;text-justify:\r\ninter-ideograph;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size: 13pt; font-family: Tahoma, sans-serif;\">Respondent\r\nmay kindly be directed not to alter in the land or may be stopped from creating\r\nany third party right over the land in dispute.</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: roboto, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>','1','','2012-05-29 00:00:00','2011-11-21 00:00:00','R-1/C/211 DLF HYDE PARK, ESTATE PROJECT, NEW CHANDIGARH ','','',1,1,0,0,'AGAM','2019-03-18 17:52:17.000','AGAM','2019-03-18 17:52:17.000'),(1216,1362,'1362',1223,'9616498a-08f7-4464-9ca8-d1e8ddf49a77','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-03-18 18:55:04.000','RISHI KUMAR GUPTA','agamjund_advocate@yahoo.com',9780269387,0,253992356271,'V & PO MULLANPUR GARIBDASS','NEAR POLICE STATION',28,507,'140901','1','V & PO MULLANPUR GARIBDASS','NEAR POLICE STATION',28,507,'140901','AGAM KUMAR JUND','agamjund_advocate@yahoo.com',9780269387,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0351','Sanskriti Homes (DLF HYDE PARK)','DLF UNIVERSAL LTD. & SANSKRITI GOLDEN OAK REAL ESTATE PVT. LTD.','info@sanskritihomes.com',7814700800,0,'M/s. Sanskriti Golden Oak Real Estate Pvt. Ltd.,','DLF Pocket R-2, New Chandigarh Mullanpur',28,507,'140901','0','DLF Universal Ltd. ','SCO 190,191,192  Sector 8-C',6,128,'160017','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 13