ies that respondent will give the interest on the amount of loan taken by the complainant.Respondent also gave the interest for 2 months but failed to give the interest for the remaining period i.e from the date of loan to the date of possession.Rate was arrived on the basis of carpet area of Rs. 1350 sq ft but the actual area in the flat is much less than that.Complainant has paid Rs. 2602139 till date.Old agreement as C-7.Receipts &amp; loan papers C-8</span></font></p>','<p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">To direct the respondent to handover the actual physical\r\npossession of the unit complete in all aspects as per the specifications\r\nmentioned in the brochure, after obtaining the occupancy certificate.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">To direct the respondent to pay interest for causing delay in\r\ndelivery of possession to be calculated from the committed date of possession i.e.\r\n01.04.2018 till the date of handing over the actual physical possession\r\ncomplete in all aspects, after obtaining the occupancy certificate. The Complainant has paid Rs. 2602139/- to respondent i.e. Rs. 20000 on 26.12.2016, Rs. 240000/- on 17.01.2017, Rs. 1905339 on 28.6.2018, &amp; Rs. 436800/- on 20.08.2018.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">To direct the respondent to complete all the remaining work\r\ninside the unit and complete the same as early as possible, as per the\r\nspecifications mentioned in the brochure.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">To direct the respondent to complete all the pending work in\r\nrespect of parking space, green area, street lights, power back up along with\r\nother basic amenities.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">To direct the respondent to provide the detail of GST deposited\r\nby the respondent in respect of unit belonging to the complainant along with\r\ndetail of GST being charged by the respondent from other allottees.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">To direct the respondent to refund the excess amount which\r\nhas been charged by it towards carpet area since the area which was to be provided\r\nby the respondent comes to 1350 sq ft and the respondent has duly charged the price from the complainant on the basis of carpet area.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\"><o:p>To direct the respondent to provide all the facilities as promised by the respondent, which are duly mentioned in the brochure.</o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\"><o:p>To direct the respondent to complete all the works as per the approved layout plan &amp; approved building plan.</o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">To provide any other relief which this Hon’ble Authority may\r\ndeem fit in the facts &amp; circumstances of the present case.&nbsp;</span><br></p>',2600000.00,2602139.00,'2018-03-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>To direct the respondent to complete all the remaining work and apply for the occupancy certificate as early as possible.</p>','1','','2018-03-07 00:00:00','2017-12-23 00:00:00','Unit No. DDD-3, 2nd Floor, 1350 sq ft,casa homes','','',2,0,0,0,'Ravikant','2019-03-21 12:49:43.000','Ravikant','2019-03-21 12:49:43.000'),(1241,1217,'1217',1141,'971b1ae7-f8bc-4323-80a7-088b81f8b7db','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-03-04 14:25:39.000','Kirandeep Kaur','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9815143759,0,0,'HOUSE NO. 38','PHASE IX',28,507,'160062','1','HOUSE NO.253','Sector 4, Mansa Devi Complex',13,15,'134114','Sanjeev Gupta','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0093','PALM GARDEN','M/s Manohar Infrastructure & Constructions Pvt Ltd','nbs@manoharrealty.com',0,1725033524,'SCO 139-142','Sector-17C',6,128,'160017','1','SCO 139-142','Sector-17C',6,128,'160017','1','<p>Plot measuring 500 sq yards@18500 per sq yard was booked by complainant in&nbsp; Palm Garden being developed by the respondent vide application C-1 dated 18.12.11 &amp; booking amount of Rs. 2775000 i.e. 30% of sale consideration was paid. Before purchasing the said plot, respondent had assured the complainant that it is having all the approvals for the development of project except layout plan approval which will be approved within 30 days &amp; possession be delivered within 2 years &amp; buyer’s agreement will executed within 3 months.It was assured that next installment would be demanded at the time of starting of development.But inspite of repeated requests by the complainant,the respondent has failed to issue any allotment letter &amp; execute buyer’s agreement within the said period &amp; even till date.Many times complainant visited the office of respondent for getting the allotment letter &amp; buyer agreement but to no avail.There was no development on the site &amp; the respondent kept the complainant in dark about the approvals.A legal notice (C-2)dated 30.8.18 was sent to respondent for refund,in which sequence of events have been duly incorporated,which may kindly be treated as part of pleadings.After that complainant received a call from respondent who invited him to its office for redressal of his grievances.Accordingly,complainant along with their family friend Mrs Suparna Randhawa who also received the similar call,went there in 3rd week of October, 2018,where the respondent assured that allotment letter would be duly issued &amp; buyer’s agreement would also be executed if the complainant further deposit a sum of Rs. 1850000 i.e20% sale consideration.But the complainant asked the respondent to first issue the allotment letter &amp; execute the agreement.Respondent refused to issue the same without getting any further amount.Complainant has been harassed for so many years due to unfair trade practices on the part of respondent.A list of dates of approvals C-3 &amp; copy of approvals C-4 &amp; 5.</p>','<ol><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">To\r\ndirect the respondent to issue allotment letter in respect of 500 sq yard plot\r\nand execute the buyer’s agreement in compliance with Section 13 of RERA.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">To\r\nhand over the actual physical possession of the plot after issuing the\r\nallotment letter and execution of buyer’s agreement. The complainant is ready\r\nto pay the balance sale consideration. The respondent was not having any\r\nauthority to collect the money from general public before 25.1.2017. <o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">To\r\ndirect the respondent not to charge any other charges from the complainant\r\nexcept EDC and PLC (if any) since the plot was sold to the complainant @Rs18500/-\r\nper sq yards excluding EDC and PLC (if any).<o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">To\r\ndirect the respondent to pay interest at the rate as contemplated under Rule 16\r\nof Punjab RERA Rules, for the period of delay in delivering the possession to\r\nbe calculated from the committed date of possession i.e. 18.12.2013 till the\r\ndate of handing over the actual physical possession after obtaining the\r\ncompletion certificate. <o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">To\r\ntake action against the respondent under Section 61 of RERA for not complying\r\nthe provision of Section 13 which makes it mandatory for a promoter to execute\r\nthe buyer agreement on receiving 10% of sale consideration. Inspite of repeated\r\nrequest the respondent has not offered the buyer’s agreement even after getting itself registered under RERA rather it is\r\ndemanding more money for executing the same which is a clear violation of\r\nSection 13. The respondent was not even having any approval, rather it had not\r\neven applied the necessary permissions when the plot was sold to the\r\ncomplainant. The respondent got the exemption under Section 44 of PAPRA on\r\n25.1.2017. Before the said date it could not collect any money from general\r\npublic. In the present case the respondent collected the money form the\r\ncomplainant in 2011-12.</span></li><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">To\r\ntake action against the respondent for collecting the money from the\r\ncomplainant before getting all the approvals and for indulging into unfair\r\ntrade practices<o:p></o:p></span></li></ol>',9250000.00,2775000.00,'2013-12-18 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<ol><li style=\"margin-left: 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">The respondent be directed to issue the allotment letter to the\r\ncomplainant and execute the buyer’s agreement in respect of 500 sq yards plot\r\nbooked by the complainant.</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"margin: 12pt 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">The respondent be directed to provide the list of allottees to whom\r\nit has allotted/sold the 862 residential plots as per the layout plan approved\r\nby GMADA on 6.10.2015 and for which it is duly registered under RERA. The fact is that the respondent has overbooked the plot. It has collected money from around 3000 people.As per the layout plan approved in 2015, it is having only 862 plot.&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"margin: 12pt 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">&nbsp;The respondent be directed\r\nto provide the details in respect of funds collected from the general public\r\nsince 2010 in lieu of 862 residential plots which are part of approved layout\r\nand registered under Section 3 of RERA and also, the detail where such amount\r\nhas been utilized by the respondent. Also, the respondent be directed to\r\nprovide all the bank details where such amount has been deposited along with\r\nthe statement of accounts, since the year 2010 and where such amount has been\r\nutilized.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"margin: 12pt 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 7pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">The respondent be\r\ndirected to provide the details in respect of number of bookings done by it\r\nsince the year 2010 for the said 862 residential plots along with the list of\r\napplicants who had applied for booking of plots.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"margin: 12pt 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">The respondent be directed to provide the details as regards the\r\ncriteria adopted by it for allotting the plot numbers to different applicants\r\nthrough pick and choose policy.</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"margin: 12pt 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">The respondent be directed to provide the list of total applicants\r\nand further, the list to whom it has already allotted the plot along with the list\r\nof applicants to whom it has not allotted the plots till date. </span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"margin: 12pt 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">The respondent be directed to provide the list of hypothecated\r\nplots which are hypothecated to GMADA, out of the approved 862 residential\r\nplots and 73 commercial plots. Also, the respondent be directed to provide the\r\nlist of hypothected plots sold to general public.</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></li></ol><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:12.0pt;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:\r\n0in;margin-left:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:12.0pt;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:\r\n0in;margin-left:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;line-height:200%;\r\nmso-layout-grid-align:none;text-autospace:none\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'rerafilingformm','2019-03-21 13:36:15.000','rerafilingformm','2019-03-21 13:36:15.000'),(1242,1217,'1217',1141,'971b1ae7-f8bc-4323-80a7-088b81f8b7db','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-03-21 13:40:58.000','Kirandeep Kaur','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9815143759,0,0,'HOUSE NO. 38','PHASE IX',28,507,'160062','1','HOUSE NO.253','Sector 4, Mansa Devi Complex',13,15,'134114','Sanjeev Gupta','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0093','PALM GARDEN','M/s Manohar Infrastructure & Constructions Pvt Ltd','nbs@manoharrealty.com',0,1725033524,'SCO 139-142','Sector-17C',6,128,'160017','1','SCO 139-142','Sector-17C',6,128,'160017','1','<p>Plot measuring 500 sq yards@18500 per sq yard was booked by complainant in&nbsp; Palm Garden being developed by the respondent vide application C-1 dated 18.12.11 &amp; booking amount of Rs. 2775000 i.e. 30% of sale consideration was paid. Before purchasing the said plot, respondent had assured the complainant that it is having all the approvals for the development of project except layout plan approval which will be approved within 30 days &amp; possession be delivered within 2 years &amp; buyer’s agreement will executed within 3 months.It was assured that next installment would be demanded at the time of starting of development.But inspite of repeated requests by the complainant,the respondent has failed to issue any allotment letter &amp; execute buyer’s agreement within the said period &amp; even till date.Many times complainant visited the office of respondent for getting the allotment letter &amp; buyer agreement but to no avail.There was no development on the site &amp; the respondent kept the complainant in dark about the approvals.A legal notice (C-2)dated 30.8.18 was sent to respondent for refund,in which sequence of events have been duly incorporated,which may kindly be treated as part of pleadings.After that complainant received a call from respondent who invited him to its office for redressal of his grievances.Accordingly,complainant along with their family friend Mrs Suparna Randhawa who also received the similar call,went there in 3rd week of October, 2018,where the respondent assured that allotment letter would be duly issued &amp; buyer’s agreement would also be executed if the complainant further deposit a sum of Rs. 1850000 i.e20% sale consideration.But the complainant asked the respondent to first issue the allotment letter &amp; execute the agreement.Respondent refused to issue the same without getting any further amount.Complainant has been harassed for so many years due to unfair trade practices on the part of respondent.A list of dates of approvals C-3 &amp; copy of approvals C-4 &amp; 5.</p>','<ol><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">To\r\ndirect the respondent to issue allotment letter in respect of 500 sq yard plot\r\nand execute the buyer’s agreement in compliance with Section 13 of RERA.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">To\r\nhand over the actual physical possession of the plot after issuing the\r\nallotment letter and execution of buyer’s agreement. The complainant is ready\r\nto pay the balance sale consideration. The respondent was not having any\r\nauthority to collect the money from general public before 25.1.2017. <o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">To\r\ndirect the respondent not to charge any other charges from the complainant\r\nexcept EDC and PLC (if any) since the plot was sold to the complainant @Rs18500/-\r\nper sq yards excluding EDC and PLC (if any).<o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">To\r\ndirect the respondent to pay interest at the rate as contemplated under Rule 16\r\nof Punjab RERA Rules, for the period of delay in delivering the possession to\r\nbe calculated from the committed date of possession i.e. 18.12.2013 till the\r\ndate of handing over the actual physical possession after obtaining the\r\ncompletion certificate. <o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">To\r\ntake action against the respondent under Section 61 of RERA for not complying\r\nthe provision of Section 13 which makes it mandatory for a promoter to execute\r\nthe buyer agreement on receiving 10% of sale consideration. Inspite of repeated\r\nrequest the respondent has not offered the buyer’s agreement even after getting itself registered under RERA rather it is\r\ndemanding more money for executing the same which is a clear violation of\r\nSection 13. The respondent was not even having any approval, rather it had not\r\neven applied the necessary permissions when the plot was sold to the\r\ncomplainant. The respondent got the exemption under Section 44 of PAPRA on\r\n25.1.2017. Before the said date it could not collect any money from general\r\npublic. In the present case the respondent collected the money form the\r\ncomplainant in 2011-12.</span></li><li style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">To\r\ntake action against the respondent for collecting the money from the\r\ncomplainant before getting all the approvals and for indulging into unfair\r\ntrade practices<o:p></o:p></span></li></ol>',9250000.00,2775000.00,'2013-12-18 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<ol><li style=\"margin-left: 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">Respondent be directed to issue the allotment letter to the\r\ncomplainant and execute the buyer’s agreement in respect of 500 sq yards plot\r\nbooked by the complainant.</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"margin: 12pt 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">Respondent be directed to provide the list of allottees to whom\r\nit has allotted/sold the 862 residential plots as per the layout plan approved\r\nby GMADA on 6.10.2015 and for which it is duly registered under RERA. The fact is that the respondent has overbooked the plot. It has collected money from around 3000 people.As per the layout plan approved in 2015, it is having only 862 plot.&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"margin: 12pt 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">&nbsp;Respondent be directed\r\nto provide the details in respect of funds collected from the general public\r\nsince 2010 in lieu of 862 residential plots which are part of approved layout\r\nand registered under Section 3 of RERA and also, the detail where such amount\r\nhas been utilized by the respondent. Also, the respondent be directed to\r\nprovide all the bank details where such amount has been deposited along with\r\nthe statement of accounts, since the year 2010 and where such amount has been\r\nutilized.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"margin: 12pt 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 7pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">&nbsp; &nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">﻿</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">﻿</span><span style=\"font-size: 18px;\">﻿R</span><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">espondent be\r\ndirected to provide the details in respect of number of bookings done by it\r\nsince the year 2010 for the said 862 residential plots along with the list of\r\napplicants who had applied for booking of plots.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"margin: 12pt 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">Respondent be directed to provide the details as regards the\r\ncriteria adopted by it for allotting the plot numbers to different applicants\r\nthrough pick and choose policy.</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"margin: 12pt 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">Respondent be directed to provide the list of total applicants\r\nand further, the list to whom it has already allotted the plot along with the list\r\nof applicants to whom it has not allotted the plots till date. </span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></li><li style=\"margin: 12pt 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">Respondent be directed to provide the list of hypothecated\r\nplots which are hypothecated to GMADA, out of the approved 862 residential\r\nplots &amp; 73 commercial plots. Also, the respondent be directed to provide the\r\nlist of hypothected plots sold to general public.</span></li><li style=\"margin: 12pt 0in 0.0001pt 0.25in; text-align: justify; line-height: 200%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">Applicant being an NRI reserve the right to take action against&nbsp; respondent in NRI cell.</span></li></ol><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:12.0pt;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:\r\n0in;margin-left:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\">&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:12.0pt;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:\r\n0in;margin-left:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:justify;line-height:200%;\r\nmso-layout-grid-align:none;text-autospace:none\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',1,1,0,0,'rerafilingformm','2019-03-21 13:40:50.000','rerafilingformm','2019-03-21 13:40:50.000'),(1243,1363,'1363',1246,'96086989-2e6b-40cc-800e-d883e1db44eb','FormTypeM',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Sushil Kumari','ravi.choudhary@yahoo.co.in',9878988441,0,0,'Flat No.505, 5th Floor, Tower-1','SBP North Valley, Kharar-Landran road, Santemajra, Kharar Mohali ',28,507,'140307','0','House No 253','Sector 4, Mansa Devi Complex',13,15,'134114','SANJEEV GUPTA','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0242','CASA Homes','Future city Developers Pvt Ltd','casahomes2016@gmail.com',9815623019,0,'Future City developers Pvt Ltd','Sector 115, Kharar-Landran highway, SAS Nagar 140307',28,507,'140307','1','Future City developers Pvt Ltd','Sector 115, Kharar-Landran highway, SAS Nagar 140307',28,507,'140307','1','<p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in\"><font face=\"Calibri Light, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px;\">Complainant booked a unit bearing No. DDD-3,2nd Floor,Casa homes vide application dated 16.12.2016.Brochure C-1)was given to the complainant,in which all facilities which were to be provided by the respondent were duly mentioned.Total sale consideration was fixed as Rs.26 lacs.Agreement(C-2)in respect of said apartment measuring 1350 sq ft was executed on 23.12.17.As per clause 7,the possession was to be handed over by 31.3.18.Complainant was also given 60% roof rights(C-3).Respondent vide its letter dated 5.8.18(C-4)demanded balance amount of Rs. 436800/-.Thereafter vide letter dated 8.10.18 respondent issued possession letter(C-5)&amp; demanded the balance amount of Rs. 291201/-which was due at the time of possession.It was mentioned in the said letter that the possession,complete in all aspects is being delivered.But the reality is that still lot of pending work is there.Respondent has not competed the work as specified in the brochure &amp; also most of the work in the unit is substandard.Respondent has not even obtained the occupancy certificate.Construction of club house not been started.Roads are very narrow though respondent agreed to provide wider roads as per approved layout.Green area,parking space,street lights,gated security,power back up &amp; other basic amenities are not there,GST has been charged on the higher side.Work done by respondent is not as per approved plans.Complainant has also written letters(C-6)but no response came from it.Though there was no formal agreement,it was orally agreed between the parties that respondent will give the interest on the amount of loan taken by the complainant.Respondent also gave the interest for 2 months but failed to give the interest for the remaining period i.e from the date of loan to the date of possession.Rate was arrived on the basis of carpet area of Rs. 1350 sq ft but the actual area in the flat is much less than that.Complainant has paid Rs. 2602139 till date.Old agreement as C-7.Receipts &amp; loan papers C-8</span></font></p>','<p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">To direct the respondent to handover the actual physical\r\npossession of the unit complete in all aspects as per the specifications\r\nmentioned in the brochure, after obtaining the occupancy certificate.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">To direct the respondent to pay interest for causing delay in\r\ndelivery of possession to be calculated from the committed date of possession i.e.\r\n01.04.2018 till the date of handing over the actual physical possession\r\ncomplete in all aspects, after obtaining the occupancy certificate. The Complainant has paid Rs. 2602139/- to respondent i.e. Rs. 20000 on 26.12.2016, Rs. 240000/- on 17.01.2017, Rs. 1905339 on 28.6.2018, &amp; Rs. 436800/- on 20.08.2018.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">To direct the respondent to complete all the remaining work\r\ninside the unit and complete the same as early as possible, as per the\r\nspecifications mentioned in the brochure.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">To direct the respondent to complete all the pending work in\r\nrespect of parking space, green area, street lights, power back up along with\r\nother basic amenities.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">To direct the respondent to provide the detail of GST deposited\r\nby the respondent in respect of unit belonging to the complainant along with\r\ndetail of GST being charged by the respondent from other allottees.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">To direct the respondent to refund the excess amount which\r\nhas been charged by it towards carpet area since the area which was to be provided\r\nby the respondent comes to 1350 sq ft and the respondent has duly charged the price from the complainant on the basis of carpet area.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\"><o:p>To direct the respondent to provide all the facilities as promised by the respondent, which are duly mentioned in the brochure.</o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\"><o:p>To direct the respondent to complete all the works as per the approved layout plan &amp; approved building plan.</o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">To provide any other relief which this Hon’ble Authority may\r\ndeem fit in the facts &amp; circumstances of the present case.&nbsp;</span><br></p>',2600000.00,2602139.00,'2018-03-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>To direct the respondent to complete all the remaining work and apply for the occupancy certificate as early as possible.</p>','1','','2018-03-07 00:00:00','2017-12-23 00:00:00','Unit No. DDD-3, 2nd Floor, 1350 sq ft,casa homes','','',2,0,0,0,'Ravikant','2019-03-21 14:20:59.000','Ravikant','2019-03-21 14:20:59.000'),(1244,1363,'1363',1246,'96086989-2e6b-40cc-800e-d883e1db44eb','FormTypeM',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Sushil Kumari','ravi.choudhary@yahoo.co.in',9878988441,0,0,'Flat No.505, 5th Floor, Tower-1','SBP North Valley, Kharar-Landran road, Santemajra, Kharar Mohali ',28,507,'140307','0','House No 253','Sector 4, Mansa Devi Complex',13,15,'134114','SANJEEV GUPTA','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0242','CASA Homes','Future city Developers Pvt Ltd','casahomes2016@gmail.com',9815623019,0,'Future City developers Pvt Ltd','Sector 115, Kharar-Landran highway, SAS Nagar 140307',28,507,'140307','1','Future City developers Pvt Ltd','Sector 115, Kharar-Landran highway, SAS Nagar 140307',28,507,'140307','1','<p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in\"><font face=\"Calibri Light, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px;\">Complainant booked a unit bearing No. DDD-3,2nd Floor,Casa homes vide application dated 16.12.2016.Brochure C-1)was given to the complainant,in which all facilities which were to be provided by the respondent were duly mentioned.Total sale consideration was fixed as Rs.26 lacs.Agreement(C-2)in respect of said apartment measuring 1350 sq ft was executed on 23.12.17.As per clause 7,the possession was to be handed over by 31.3.18.Complainant was also given 60% roof rights(C-3).Respondent vide its letter dated 5.8.18(C-4)demanded balance amount of Rs. 436800/-.Thereafter vide letter dated 8.10.18 respondent issued possession letter(C-5)&amp; demanded the balance amount of Rs. 291201/-which was due at the time of possession.It was mentioned in the said letter that the possession,complete in all aspects is being delivered.But the reality is that still lot of pending work is there.Respondent has not competed the work as specified in the brochure &amp; also most of the work in the unit is substandard.Respondent has not even obtained the occupancy certificate.Construction of club house not been started.Roads are very narrow though respondent agreed to provide wider roads as per approved layout.Green area,parking space,street lights,gated security,power back up &amp; other basic amenities are not there,GST has been charged on the higher side.Work done by respondent is not as per approved plans.Complainant has also written letters(C-6)but no response came from it.Though there was no formal agreement,it was orally agreed between the parties that respondent will give the interest on the amount of loan taken by the complainant.Respondent also gave the interest for 2 months but failed to give the interest for the remaining period i.e from the date of loan to the date of possession.Rate was arrived on the basis of carpet area of Rs. 1350 sq ft but the actual area in the flat is much less than that.Complainant has paid Rs. 2602139 till date.Old agreement as C-7.Receipts &amp; loan papers C-8</span></font></p>','<p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">To direct the respondent to handover the actual physical\r\npossession of the unit complete in all aspects as per the specifications\r\nmentioned in the brochure, after obtaining the occupancy certificate.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">To direct the respondent to pay interest for causing delay in\r\ndelivery of possession to be calculated from the committed date of possession i.e.\r\n01.04.2018 till the date of handing over the actual physical possession\r\ncomplete in all aspects, after obtaining the occupancy certificate. The Complainant has paid Rs. 2602139/- to respondent i.e. Rs. 20000 on 26.12.2016, Rs. 240000/- on 17.01.2017, Rs. 1905339 on 28.6.2018(as demanded), &amp; Rs. 436800/-(as demanded) on 20.08.2018. It is relevant to mention that after making payment of Rs 240000/- , the respondent raised the demand in 2018 which was duly paid.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">To direct the respondent to complete all the remaining work\r\ninside the unit and complete the same as early as possible, as per the\r\nspecifications mentioned in the brochure.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">To direct the respondent to complete all the pending work in\r\nrespect of parking space, green area, street lights, power back up along with\r\nother basic amenities.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">To direct the respondent to provide the detail of GST deposited\r\nby the respondent in respect of unit belonging to the complainant along with\r\ndetail of GST being charged by the respondent from other allottees.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">To direct the respondent to refund the excess amount which\r\nhas been charged by it towards carpet area since the area which was to be provided\r\nby the respondent comes to 1350 sq ft and the respondent has duly charged the price from the complainant on the basis of carpet area.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\"><o:p>To direct the respondent to provide all the facilities as promised by the respondent, which are duly mentioned in the brochure.</o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\"><o:p>To direct the respondent to complete all the works as per the approved layout plan &amp; approved building plan.</o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">To provide any other relief which this Hon’ble Authority may\r\ndeem fit in the facts &amp; circumstances of the present case.&nbsp;</span><br></p>',2600000.00,2602139.00,'2018-03-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>To direct the respondent to complete all the remaining work and apply for the occupancy certificate as early as possible.</p>','1','','2018-03-07 00:00:00','2017-12-23 00:00:00','Unit No. DDD-3, 2nd Floor, 1350 sq ft,casa homes','','',2,0,0,0,'Ravikant','2019-03-21 14:27:03.000','Ravikant','2019-03-21 14:27:03.000'),(1245,1363,'1363',1246,'96086989-2e6b-40cc-800e-d883e1db44eb','FormTypeM',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Sushil Kumari','ravi.choudhary@yahoo.co.in',9878988441,0,0,'Flat No.505, 5th Floor, Tower-1','SBP North Valley, Kharar-Landran road, Santemajra, Kharar Mohali ',28,507,'140307','0','House No 253','Sector 4, Mansa Devi Complex',13,15,'134114','SANJEEV GUPTA','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0242','CASA Homes','Future city Developers Pvt Ltd','casahomes2016@gmail.com',9815623019,0,'Future City developers Pvt Ltd','Sector 115, Kharar-Landran highway, SAS Nagar 140307',28,507,'140307','1','Future City developers Pvt Ltd','Sector 115, Kharar-Landran highway, SAS Nagar 140307',28,507,'140307','1','<p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in\"><font face=\"Calibri Light, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px;\">Complainant booked a unit bearing No. DDD-3,2nd Floor,Casa homes vide application dated 16.12.2016.Brochure C-1)was given to the complainant,in which all facilities which were to be provided by the respondent were duly mentioned.Total sale consideration was fixed as Rs.26 lacs.Agreement(C-2)in respect of said apartment measuring 1350 sq ft was executed on 23.12.17.As per clause 7,the possession was to be handed over by 31.3.18.Complainant was also given 60% roof rights(C-3).Respondent vide its letter dated 5.8.18(C-4)demanded balance amount of Rs. 436800/-.Thereafter vide letter dated 8.10.18 respondent issued possession letter(C-5)&amp; demanded the balance amount of Rs. 291201/-which was due at the time of possession.It was mentioned in the said letter that the possession,complete in all aspects is being delivered.But the reality is that still lot of pending work is there.Respondent has not competed the work as specified in the brochure &amp; also most of the work in the unit is substandard.Respondent has not even obtained the occupancy certificate.Construction of club house not been started.Roads are very narrow though respondent agreed to provide wider roads as per approved layout.Green area,parking space,street lights,gated security,power back up &amp; other basic amenities are not there,GST has been charged on the higher side.Work done by respondent is not as per approved plans.Complainant has also written letters(C-6)but no response came from it.Though there was no formal agreement,it was orally agreed between the parties that respondent will give the interest on the amount of loan taken by the complainant.Respondent also gave the interest for 2 months but failed to give the interest for the remaining period i.e from the date of loan to the date of possession.Rate was arrived on the basis of carpet area of Rs. 1350 sq ft but the actual area in the flat is much less than that.Complainant has paid Rs. 2602139 till date.Old agreement as C-7.Receipts &amp; loan papers C-8</span></font></p>','<p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">To direct the respondent to handover the actual physical\r\npossession of the unit complete in all aspects as per the specifications\r\nmentioned in the brochure, after obtaining the occupancy certificate.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">To direct the respondent to pay interest for causing delay in\r\ndelivery of possession to be calculated from the committed date of possession i.e.\r\n01.04.2018 till the date of handing over the actual physical possession\r\ncomplete in all aspects, after obtaining the occupancy certificate. The Complainant has paid Rs. 2602139/- to respondent i.e. Rs. 20000 on 26.12.2016, Rs. 240000/- on 17.01.2017, Rs. 1905339 on 28.6.2018(as demanded), &amp; Rs. 436800/-(as demanded) on 20.08.2018. It is relevant to mention that after making payment of Rs 240000/- , the respondent raised the demand in 2018 which was duly paid.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">To direct the respondent to complete all the remaining work\r\ninside the unit and complete the same as early as possible, as per the\r\nspecifications mentioned in the brochure.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">To direct the respondent to complete all the pending work in\r\nrespect of parking space, green area, street lights, power back up along with\r\nother basic amenities.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">To direct the respondent to provide the detail of GST deposited\r\nby the respondent in respect of unit belonging to the complainant along with\r\ndetail of GST being charged by the respondent from other allottees.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\">To direct the respondent to refund the excess amount which\r\nhas been charged by it towards carpet area since the area which was to be provided\r\nby the respondent comes to 1350 sq ft and the respondent has duly charged the price from the complainant on the basis of carpet area.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\"><o:p>To direct the respondent to provide all the facilities as promised by the respondent, which are duly mentioned in the brochure.</o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; line-height: 200%;\"><o:p>To direct the respondent to complete all the works as per the approved layout plan &amp; approved building plan.</o:p></span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:justify;line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">To provide any other relief which this Hon’ble Authority may\r\ndeem fit in the facts &amp; circumstances of the present case.&nbsp;</span><br></p>',2600000.00,2602139.00,'2018-03-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>To direct the respondent to complete all the remaining work and apply for the occupancy certificate as early as possible.</p>','1','','2018-03-07 00:00:00','2017-12-23 00:00:00','Unit No. DDD-3, 2nd Floor, 1350 sq ft,casa homes','','',2,0,0,0,'Ravikant','2019-03-21 14:27:28.000','Ravikant','2019-03-21 14:27:28.000'),(1246,1363,'1363',1246,'96086989-2e6b-40cc-800e-d883e1db44eb','FormTypeM',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Sushil Kumari','ravi.choudhary@yahoo.co.in',9878988441,0,0,'Flat No.505, 5th Floor, Tower-1','SBP North Valley, Kharar-Landran road, Santemajra, Kharar Mohali ',28,507,'140307','0','House No 253','Sector 4, Mansa Devi Complex',13,15,'134114','SAN