clause 2.24 of the allotment, it was promised that the possession would be handed over within a period of 18 months. Before booking of said unit, it was also assured by the representative of the company that possession would be delivered within 18 months from the date of allotment letter. The complainants have already paid the demanded amount without any default on their part. It is the respondent who has committed the default by not delivering the possession.Till date, the complainant has already paid the amount of Rs. 9786477/- (Receipts as C-2) and balance amount is payable at the time of delivery of possession. The respondent&nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>\r\n</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p>','<ul><li>To direct the respondent to handover the actual physical possession of the said apartment complete in all aspects, after obtaining the occupancy certificate.</li><li>To direct the respondent to pay interest for the delayed period to be calculated w.e.f 22.12.2016 upto the date handing over the actual physical possession after obtaining the occupancy certificate</li><li>To take action against the respondent under Section 61 for committing violation of Section 13 of RERA , by not offering the buyer agreement for execution, till date.</li><li>To direct the respondent to execute the buyer agreement as per RERA rules.</li><li>To direct the respondent to pay litigation charges to the tune of Rs. 50000/-</li><li>The complainants reserve the right to file separate application for claiming compensation for the harassment both physical &amp; mental, due to non delivery of possession within time and for causing unreasonable delay</li><li>To direct the respondent to issue separate receipt for the service tax charged from the complainants</li><li>Any other relief which this Hon\'ble authority may deem fit, be also granted to the complainants.</li></ul>',10268967.00,9786477.00,'2016-12-22 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<ul><li>To direct the respondent to complete the development&nbsp; of project and construction of the apartment and apply for occupation certificate.</li></ul>','1','','2018-06-23 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','1402 E Wing Falcon View\r\nSector 66-A Mohali','','',2,0,0,0,'vf18jan','2019-03-23 14:18:10.000','vf18jan','2019-03-23 14:18:10.000'),(1259,1223,'1223',1299,'f05423d6-8aeb-41cc-9669-749a50a90d4d','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-03-22 22:38:40.000','VICKY  FRANCIS','vf18jan@gmail.com',9996767263,0,0,'217 Rajesh Colony','Near old court',13,21,'135003','1','253','Sector 4, Mansa Devi Complex',13,1,'134114','Sanjeev Gupta','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PM0004','Falcon View Apartments','Janta Land Promoters Pvt. Ltd.','janta@jantahousing.com',8427100082,0,'SCO 39-42','Sector 82 JLPL',28,507,'140306','1','SCO 39-42','Sector 82 JLPL',28,507,'140306','1','<p>The complainants&nbsp; purchased the apartment No. E-1402, Facing Green in Wing “E” at 14th Floor in (Super Mega) Falcon View, Phase-1, Sector 66-A, Mohali for an amount of Rs. 96,92,942/-. Allotment letter(C-1) was issued to the complainants. The complainants opted for down payment plan.The total sale consideration inclusive of all charges &amp; facilities came to Rs.10268967. As per clause 2.24 of the allotment, it was promised that the possession would be handed over within a period of 18 months. Before booking of said unit, it was also assured by the representative of the company that possession would be delivered within 18 months from the date of allotment letter. The complainants have already paid the demanded amount without any default on their part. It is the respondent who has committed the default by not delivering the possession.Till date, the complainant has already paid the amount of Rs. 9786477/- (Receipts as C-2) &amp; balance amount is payable at the time of delivery of possession. The respondent has not offered any buyer agreement to the complainants till date, thus it has committed violation of Section 13 of RERA.The respondent only paid Rs. 154807 &amp; Rs. 116026/- as compensation to complainant No.1 &amp; 2 respectively. Rather the respondent ought to have paid the interest on the amount paid by the complainants w.e.f 22/12/2016 till the date of handing over the actual physical possession of the apartment complete in all aspects, after obtaining the occupancy certificate. When the complainant No.1 resisted about not paying the interest, the respondent told him they will only pay the said amount.The complainant accepted the cheques under protest. Only complainant No.1 encashed the cheque. Cheque issued to complainant No.2 has not been encashed. Thereafter the complainants several times requested the respondent to pay interest on the amount paid by them w.e.f 22.12.2016 till date of delivery of possession, But the respondent has refused to pay interest to them.</p><p><br></p><p>\r\n</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p>','<ul><li>To direct the respondent to handover the actual physical possession of the said apartment complete in all aspects, after obtaining the occupancy certificate.</li><li>To direct the respondent to pay interest for the delayed period to be calculated w.e.f 22.12.2016 upto the date handing over the actual physical possession after obtaining the occupancy certificate. The respondent may deduct Rs. Rs. 154807 from the delayed period interest, which was accepted by the complainant under protest.</li><li>To take action against the respondent under Section 61 for committing violation of Section 13 of RERA , by not offering the buyer agreement for execution, till date.</li><li>To direct the respondent to execute the buyer agreement as per RERA rules.</li><li>To direct the respondent to pay litigation charges to the tune of Rs. 50000/-</li><li>The complainants reserve the right to file separate application for claiming compensation for the harassment both physical &amp; mental, due to non delivery of possession within time and for causing unreasonable delay</li><li>To direct the respondent to issue separate receipt for the service tax charged from the complainants</li><li>Any other relief which this Hon\'ble authority may deem fit, be also granted to the complainants.</li></ul>',10268967.00,9786477.00,'2016-12-22 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<ul><li>To direct the respondent to complete the development&nbsp; of project and construction of the apartment and apply for occupation certificate.</li></ul>','1','','2018-06-23 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','1402 E Wing Falcon View\r\nSector 66-A Mohali','','',2,0,0,0,'vf18jan','2019-03-23 14:32:11.000','vf18jan','2019-03-23 14:32:11.000'),(1260,1223,'1223',1299,'f05423d6-8aeb-41cc-9669-749a50a90d4d','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-03-25 10:38:53.000','VICKY  FRANCIS','vf18jan@gmail.com',9996767263,0,0,'217 Rajesh Colony','Near old court',13,21,'135003','1','253','Sector 4, Mansa Devi Complex',13,1,'134114','Sanjeev Gupta','sanjeevgupta253@gmail.com',9501142800,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PM0004','Falcon View Apartments','Janta Land Promoters Pvt. Ltd.','janta@jantahousing.com',8427100082,0,'SCO 39-42','Sector 82 JLPL',28,507,'140306','1','SCO 39-42','Sector 82 JLPL',28,507,'140306','1','<p>The complainants&nbsp; purchased the apartment No. E-1402, Facing Green in Wing “E” at 14th Floor in (Super Mega) Falcon View, Phase-1, Sector 66-A, Mohali for an amount of Rs. 96,92,942/-. Allotment letter(C-1) was issued to the complainants. The complainants opted for down payment plan.The total sale consideration inclusive of all charges &amp; facilities came to Rs.10268967. As per clause 2.24 of the allotment, it was promised that the possession would be handed over within a period of 18 months. Before booking of said unit, it was also assured by the representative of the company that possession would be delivered within 18 months from the date of allotment letter. The complainants have already paid the demanded amount without any default on their part. It is the respondent who 