phCxSpLast\" style=\"margin-left:1.0in;mso-add-space:auto;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;\r\nmso-ascii-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-hansi-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-bidi-theme-font:\r\nminor-latin\">iv)<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;\r\nline-height:200%;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;mso-ascii-theme-font:minor-latin;\r\nmso-hansi-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\">Any other\r\nrelief to which the Complainants may be found entitled to under law and equity.<o:p></o:p></span></p>',7884975.00,6798225.00,'2014-07-16 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>NIL</p>','1','','2011-07-08 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Commercial Plot No. E-114','','',1,0,0,0,'manishmalhotra','2019-03-24 19:30:20.000','manishmalhotra','2019-03-24 19:30:20.000'),(1265,1371,'1371',1436,'08bbfbbc-c37f-4ab1-87ac-faf6af8bda3d','FormTypeM',1,0,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Rajinder Pathak','pathakrajinder2000@gmail.com',9501525401,0,0,'# 3126, Sector 71','SAS Nagar',28,507,'160071','1','# 3126, Sector 71','SAS Nagar ',28,507,'160071','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PM0091','POSH CITY','BABA BANDA SINGH BAHADUR ENTERPRISES','bbsbikpmohali@gmail.com',9915322330,0,'Baba Banda Singh Bahadur Enterprises','Village Chapparchiri Kalan (HB No. 195) Sector 92',28,507,'140308','1','Baba Banda Singh Bahadur Enterprises','Village Chapparchiri Kalan (HB No. 195) Sector 92',28,507,'140308','1','<p>With due respect the facts are given below:</p><p>We booked a plot No. 129 in the so called Posh City, Sector 91 &amp; 92 Mohali prior to its layout plan approved from the concerned Authority. We paid a sum of Rs. 6,15,500/- against booked plot no. 129 of 125 sq.yds. on dated 27-04-2017 and an agreement was also made. The Promoter issued us provisionally allotment letter on 31-05-2017.</p><p>It was only after the approvals; the company asked us to pay the balance amount of the said plot and also made another agreement. We paid Rs. 6,71,500/- on 02/07/2018 against the plot and company/promoter made an agreement with us dated 2/7/18 and allotted us the plot no. 159 in BBSE Enterprises, Sector 91-92 Mohali</p><p>Since the project is at good location, so we purchased another plot No. 177 size 231.11 sq.yds. with all the due payment at that time and made an agreement of this plot also from the same layout plan. We paid Rs. 19,00,000/- for this plot on 4/7/18 and balance of Amount was agreed to be given at the time of registration of said plot.</p><p>Here we want to confirm you that as per agreement clause No. 5 Company had to give the possession of both the plots by 31/10/2018. But it did not happen. We made a request to company to give us the possession and do the registry of both plots, so that we may be able to construct it. But company had asked us to change the location of these plots and take possession of some another location as per their revised layout plan. The Promoter said that one of your plot area 125 sq. yds. is not available. On repeated request for registry and possession of plots the promoter is not paying any attention to my request and compelling me to change the location of the plots. on U/s 18 a legal notice as served upon their but there was not fruitful action. Now the promoter says go to the court and we will see how the court will give the plot.&nbsp;</p><p>we request you to kindly look into the matter. we will be obliged and thankful to the Authority.</p>','<p>Sir,</p><p>We wish to get back my plots as per the agreement done.</p><p>I want relief for mentally torture and harassment i.e. Rs. 1,00,000/-</p><p>I want litigation fee of Rs. 1,00,000/-</p><p>or&nbsp;</p><p>Total relief of Rs. 2,00,000/-&nbsp; along with refund of my amount plus interest till date.&nbsp;</p>',6188000.00,3087000.00,'2018-10-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>I want total relief of Rs. 2,00,000/- i.e. 1,00,000 for mentally torture and 1,00,000/- for litigation fee along with my plots as per the agreement done</p><p>or</p><p>I want relief of Rs. 2,00,000/- along with refund of my total amount paid along with interest till date.</p>','1','','2017-05-31 00:00:00','2018-07-02 00:00:00','Plot No. 159 and 177 Posh City Sector 92 Mohali','','',2,0,0,0,'rajinder2000','2019-03-24 22:45:17.000','rajinder2000','2019-03-24 22:45:17.000'),(1266,1371,'1371',1436,'08bbfbbc-c37f-4ab1-87ac-faf6af8bda3d','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-03-25 16:55:31.000','Rajinder Pathak','pathakrajinder2000@gmail.com',9501525401,0,0,'# 3126, Sector 71','SAS Nagar',28,507,'160071','1','# 3126, Sector 71','SAS Nagar ',28,507,'160071','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PM0091','POSH CITY','BABA BANDA SINGH BAHADUR ENTERPRISES','bbsbikpmohali@gmail.com',9915322330,0,'Baba Banda Singh Bahadur Enterprises','Village Chapparchiri Kalan (HB No. 195) Sector 92',28,507,'140308','1','Baba Banda Singh Bahadur Enterprises','Village Chapparchiri Kalan (HB No. 195) Sector 92',28,507,'140308','1','<p>With due respect the facts are given below:</p><p>We booked a plot No. 129 in the so called Posh City, Sector 91 &amp; 92 Mohali prior to its layout plan approved from the concerned Authority. We paid a sum of Rs. 6,15,500/- against booked plot no. 129 of 125 sq.yds. on dated 27-04-2017 and an agreement was also made. The Promoter issued us provisionally allotment letter on 31-05-2017.</p><p>It was only after the approvals; the company asked us to pay the balance amount of the said plot and also made another agreement. We paid Rs. 6,71,500/- on 02/07/2018 against the plot and company/promoter made an agreement with us dated 2/7/18 and allotted us the plot no. 159 in BBSE Enterprises, Sector 91-92 Mohali</p><p>Since the project is at good location, so we purchased another plot No. 177 size 231.11 sq.yds. with all the due payment at that time and made an agreement of this plot also from the same layout plan. We paid Rs. 19,00,000/- for this plot on 4/7/18 and balance of Amount was agreed to be given at the time of registration of said plot.</p><p>Here we want to confirm you that as per agreement clause No. 5 Company had to give the possession of both the plots by 31/10/2018. But it did not happen. We made a request to company to give us the possession and do the registry of both plots, so that we may be able to construct it. But company had asked us to change the location of these plots and take possession of some another location as per their revised layout plan. The Promoter said that one of your plot area 125 sq. yds. is not available. On repeated request for registry and possession of plots the promoter is not paying any attention to my request and compelling me to change the location of the plots. on U/s 18 a legal notice as served upon their but there was not fruitful action. Now the promoter says go to the court and we will see how the court will give the plot.&nbsp;</p><p>we request you to kindly look into the matter. we will be obliged and thankful to the Authority.</p>','<p>Sir,</p><p>We wish to get back my plots as per the agreement done.</p><p>I want relief for mentally torture and harassment i.e. Rs. 1,00,000/-</p><p>I want litigation fee of Rs. 1,00,000/-</p><p>or&nbsp;</p><p>Total relief of Rs. 2,00,000/-&nbsp; along with refund of my amount plus interest till date.&nbsp;</p>',6188000.00,3087000.00,'2018-10-31 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>I want total relief of Rs. 2,00,000/- i.e. 1,00,000 for mentally torture and 1,00,000/- for litigation fee along with my plots as per the agreement done</p><p>or</p><p>I want relief of Rs. 2,00,000/- along with refund of my total amount paid along with interest till date.</p>','1','','2017-05-31 00:00:00','2018-07-02 00:00:00','Plot No. 159 and 177 Posh City Sector 92 Mohali','','',1,0,0,0,'rajinder2000','2019-03-24 23:09:43.000','rajinder2000','2019-03-24 23:09:43.000'),(1267,1372,'1372',1446,'9cd007eb-499d-49cd-ad24-954c4ee507d5','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-03-25 14:51:20.000','Ms Surinder  Chopra','choprasurinder39@yahoo.com',9988370789,1722582510,0,'510 sector 16 Panchkula','same',13,15,'134109','1','510 sector 16 Panchkula','same',13,15,'134109','','',0,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS79-PC0010','CHANDIGARH CITI CENTER','Pankaj Gupta,Managing Director,Chandigarh Citi Center Developers  ','ccc.ritesh@gmail.com',9023490234,0,'VIP ROAD,ZIRAKPUR','SAME',28,507,'140603','1','VIP ROAD,ZIRAKPUR','SAME',28,507,'140603','1','<p>&nbsp;</p><span style=\'font-family: \"Bookman Old Style\",\"serif\"; font-size: 12pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 10.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: \"Times New Roman\"; mso-bidi-font-family: \"Times New Roman\"; mso-ansi-language: EN-US; mso-fareast-language: EN-US; mso-bidi-language: AR-SA;\'><p>That Mr. Rajeev Bhatt, Property Dealer of\r\nVertical Heights Realtors approached me in the month of October 2018 with a\r\nAssured Lease Guarantee (For 9 years)Scheme.The place offered to me was Fully Furnished Office Suites (Block D &amp; E) (All A Block Facing Unit) at 11<sup><font size=\"2\">th</font></sup> Floor (Hereinafter referred as “Office Space”). Then I was thereafter taken to visit the property on 27.10.2018.</p><span style=\'line-height: 150%; font-family: \"Bookman Old Style\",\"serif\"; font-size: 12pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 10.0pt;\'><p>Mr. Sachin Verma who is the General Manager met <span style=\"mso-spacerun: yes;\">&nbsp;</span>and offered Office Space No. 1108 at 11<sup><font size=\"2\">th</font></sup> Floor with Carpet area of 525 sq ft at the price of Rs. 7350 per sq. ft.</p><span style=\'font-family: \"Bookman Old Style\",\"serif\"; font-size: 12pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 10.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: \"Times New Roman\"; mso-bidi-font-family: \"Times New Roman\"; mso-ansi-language: EN-US; mso-fareast-language: EN-US; mso-bidi-language: AR-SA;\'><p>The possession as promised by them&nbsp;was to be given on or\r\nbefore 31/12/2018 if the entire payment is made up&nbsp;front.<span style=\'line-height: 150%; font-family: \"Bookman Old Style\",\"serif\"; font-size: 12pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 10.0pt;\'>&nbsp;<strong>Considering\r\nthat I was making Full Payment of the above said Office Space, after much negotiations, agreed and finalized the final price for the\r\ncarpet area of 525 sq.ft to be Rs. 5665.76 per sq. ft. Hence forth after making\r\nthe calculations I was informed that the final amount which needs to be paid is\r\nRs. 31,53,000/- inclusive of GST.</strong><span style=\'font-family: \"Bookman Old Style\",\"serif\"; font-size: 12pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 10.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: \"Times New Roman\"; mso-bidi-font-family: \"Times New Roman\"; mso-ansi-language: EN-US; mso-fareast-language: EN-US; mso-bidi-language: AR-SA;\'><strong>On\r\nbelieving their representations as regards completion certificate and getting\r\npossession of the Office Space by 31/12/2018, I depoisted the amount of Rs.\r\n31,53,000/- via RTGS from my PNB Account with UTR PUNBR52018102914135067 to the\r\naccount of CITI CENTRE DEVELOPERS on dated 29.10.2018.</strong><span style=\'font-family: \"Bookman Old Style\",\"serif\"; font-size: 12pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 10.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: \"Times New Roman\"; mso-bidi-font-family: \"Times New Roman\"; mso-ansi-language: EN-US; mso-fareast-language: EN-US; mso-bidi-language: AR-SA;\'> T<strong>hat\r\nthey have prepared the Allotment Letter and on being shown the said Allotment\r\nLetter which was dated 05.12.2018, I was perplexed to see that the full and\r\nfinal amount paid by me was mentioned as “earnest money” and that the carpet\r\narea was also reduced to 373.50 sq ft.I also learnt of the fraud being\r\ncommitted against me as there were no Office Spaces\r\napproved for 11<sup><font size=\"2\">th</font></sup> Floor but only SOHO suites.</strong><span style=\'font-family: \"Bookman Old Style\",\"serif\"; font-size: 12pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 10.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: \"Times New Roman\"; mso-bidi-font-family: \"Times New Roman\"; mso-ansi-language: EN-US; mso-fareast-language: EN-US; mso-bidi-language: AR-SA;\'>That I has been approaching them for refund of\r\nmy entire amount being paid by me time and again since February 2019, they\r\nneither completed the formalities nor have refunded the amount in total to me.That till dae they have not given me the claimed amount even when I approached them time and again </span></span></span></span></p><p><font face=\"Times New Roman\">\r\n\r\n</font></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 10pt 0.5in;\"><span style=\'line-height: 115%; font-family: \"Bookman Old Style\",\"serif\"; font-size: 12pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 11.0pt;\'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p><p><font face=\"Times New Roman\">\r\n\r\n</font></p></span><p></p></span><p></p><span style=\'font-family: \"Bookman Old Style\",\"serif\"; font-size: 12pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 10.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: \"Times New Roman\"; mso-bidi-font-family: \"Times New Roman\"; mso-ansi-language: EN-US; mso-fareast-language: EN-US; mso-bidi-language: AR-SA;\'><p></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\'line-height: 150%; font-family: \"Bookman Old Style\",\"serif\"; font-size: 12pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 10.0pt;\'><o:p></o:p></span>&nbsp;</p><p><font face=\"Times New Roman\">\r\n\r\n</font></p></span><p></p></span><p></p>','<p>&nbsp;</p><span style=\'font-family: \"Bookman Old Style\",\"serif\"; font-size: 12pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 10.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: \"Times New Roman\"; mso-bidi-font-family: \"Times New Roman\"; mso-ansi-language: EN-US; mso-fareast-language: EN-US; mso-bidi-language: AR-SA;\'><p>Inspite of giving false assurances that the\r\namount will be repaid to me within a few days’ time, there is no&nbsp;<font face=\"Times New Roman\">refu</font>nd which has been affected till date.<span style=\'line-height: 150%; font-family: \"Bookman Old Style\",\"serif\"; font-size: 12pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 10.0pt;\'>&nbsp;This is\r\nhumble request to the Regulatory authority to action on the above mentioned\r\nnotices for to refund the entire money i.e. 31,53,000/- <span style=\"mso-spacerun: yes;\">&nbsp;</span>received by you along with up to date interest\r\nof 2.5% per month and Rs. 10,000,00/- towards mental harassment and torture. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p><font face=\"Times New Roman\">\r\n\r\n</font></p></span><p></p>',0.00,3153000.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>&nbsp;please issue the notice to the respondent as soon as .And humbly request to mediate and settle the dispute between us.</p><p>Thanks&nbsp;</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'SURINDERCHOPRA','2019-03-25 13:45:33.000','SURINDERCHOPRA','2019-03-25 13:45:33.000'),(1268,1373,'1373',1443,'12f7000e-33bd-4fcb-9db0-8ce5cc94c23b','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','GIETA KHOSLA','luvmalhotra.rkm@gmail.com',9815361021,0,0,'GEETANJALI FARM NO.27','GADAIPUR MEHRAULI',10,120,'110030','1','GEETANJALI FARM NO.27','GADAIPUR MEHRAULI',10,120,'110030','LUV MALHOTRA','',9815361021,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-LDH45-PR0166','THE IMPERIAL GOLF ESTATE','M/S. EMERALD LANDS(INDIA) PRIVATE LTD.','ASHOK.SHARMA@IMPERIALGOLFESTATE.COM',0,1244550340,'SECOND FLOOR C-8/1A ','VASANT VIHAR NEW DELHI',10,120,'110001','1','SECOND FLOOR C-8/1A ','VASANT VIHAR NEW DELHI',10,120,'110001','1','<p>ABCD</p>','<p>ABCD</p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>ABCD</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'LUVMALHOTRA','2019-03-25 20:52:27.000','LUVMALHOTRA','2019-03-25 20:52:27.000'),(1269,1373,'1373',1443,'12f7000e-33bd-4fcb-9db0-8ce5cc94c23b','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','GIETA KHOSLA','luvmalhotra.rkm@gmail.com',9815361021,0,0,'GEETANJALI FARM NO.27','GADAIPUR MEHRAULI',10,120,'110030','1','GEETANJALI FARM NO.27','GADAIPUR MEHRAULI',10,120,'110030','LUV MALHOTRA','',9815361021,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-LDH45-PR0166','THE IMPERIAL GOLF ESTATE','M/S. EMERALD LANDS(INDIA) PRIVATE LTD.','ASHOK.SHARMA@IMPERIALGOLFESTATE.COM',0,1244550340,'SECOND FLOOR C-8/1A ','VASANT VIHAR NEW DELHI',10,120,'110001','1','SECOND FLOOR C-8/1A ','VASANT VIHAR NEW DELHI',10,120,'110001','1','<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: roboto, serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">At that time of booking, respondent represented of having all sufficient\r\napprovals, clear ownership and clear and well approach from main\r\nLudhiana-Ferozpur Road as per master plan of Glada and is an approachable\r\nproject to live with 18 Hole Golf Course, 8ft. boundary wall with long trees\r\nbesides boundary, ultra modern club house with swimming pool and many more\r\nfacilities would be there. Complainant under their representation got booked a Flat/unit\r\nno. H-34B, 1600 sq.ft. which was allotted to complainant by vide Allotment\r\nLetter dated 24.10.2011. BSP of the plot was Rs. 62,50,000/- excluding EDC,\r\nIFSD,PLC and Golf Club Membership fee. Till date a sum of Rs.61,38,026/- has\r\nalready been paid by complainant which is almost 95% of total price. Flat buyer\r\nagreement was not executed till date. Respondent promised to handover possession\r\nwithin 24 months from the date of allotment along with the entire basic\r\namenities as per their broachers and advertisement. Construction of flat is still\r\nnot completed. Possession not offered till date. No sign of development is\r\nobserved as promised by respondents. Roads are in pathetic condition, internal\r\nroads are still unconstructed, there are no electricity connection arrangements\r\nas well as basic amenities such as water, sewerage, park roads, boundary wall\r\nis not constructed as yet. Club house as promised by respondent at the time of\r\nbooking is still not constructed. Further there are no signs of 18 Hole Golf\r\ncourses as promised by respondent. Revenue Rastas of the villages have not been\r\nyet acquired resulting which people of the village roaming within the township\r\nwith their cattle as such there are insufficient security arrangements have\r\nbeen made. Respondents were supposed to handover the possession of said plot to\r\ncomplainant till Oct. 2014 but inspite of the lapse of almost 5 years, there is\r\nno development at site.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.25in;text-align:justify;text-justify:\r\ninter-ideograph;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;font-family:\r\n&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">Complainant is a Senior Citizen. In view of the factual matrix as mentioned above\r\nin para 4 of this complaint and in view of the facts that despite lapse of 5\r\nyears&nbsp; respondent even failed to get the Flat\r\nbuyer agreement executed with complainant and further failed to complete construction\r\nof flat and further failed to offer possession alongwith all basic amenities as\r\nper their advertisement and brouchers and with clear approach from Ludhiana\r\nFerozepur Road, complainant seeks kind indulgence of this Hon’ble Authority in\r\ngranting following reliefs: 1. To refund the entire amount paid by complainant\r\ni. e. </span><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">Rs. 6138026/-</span><span style=\"font-size:\r\n14.0pt;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"> alongwith interest @ 18% per\r\nannum from the date of respective payments till the realization alongwith Rs.5\r\nLac as compensation for mental harassment suffered by complainant and Rs.55,000/-\r\ncost of Litigation 2. Any other relief that this Hon’ble Authority may deem fit\r\nand appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances of the present\r\ncomplaint.<o:p></o:p></span></p>',7249272.00,0.00,'2014-10-24 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>NIL</p>','1','','2011-10-24 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Flat no. H-34B, Imperial Golf Estate, Ludhiana','','',2,0,0,0,'LUVMALHOTRA','2019-03-25 21:07:07.000','LUVMALHOTRA','2019-03-25 21:07:07.000'),(1270,1373,'1373',1443,'12f7000e-33bd-4fcb-9db0-8ce5cc94c23b','FormTypeM',1,1,1,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','GIETA KHOSLA','luvmalhotra.rkm@gmail.com',9815361021,0,0,'GEETANJALI FARM NO.27','GADAIPUR MEHRAULI',10,120,'110030','1','GEETANJALI FARM NO.27','GADAIPUR MEHRAULI',10,120,'110030','LUV MALHOTRA','',9815361021,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-LDH45-PR0166','THE IMPERIAL GOLF ESTATE','M/S. EMERALD LANDS(INDIA) PRIVATE LTD.','ASHOK.SHARMA@IMPERIALGOLFESTATE.COM',0,1244550340,'SECOND FLOOR C-8/1A ','VASANT VIHAR NEW DELHI',10,120,'110001','1','SECOND FLOOR C-8/1A ','VASANT VIHAR NEW DELHI',10,120,'110001','1','<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt; font-family: roboto, serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">At that time of booking, respondent represented of having all sufficient\r\napprovals, clear ownership and clear and well approach from main\r\nLudhiana-Ferozpur Road as per master plan of Glada and is an approachable\r\nproject to live with 18 Hole Golf Course, 8ft. boundary wall with long trees\r\nbesides boundary, ultra modern club house with swimming pool and many more\r\nfacilities would be there. Complainant under their representation got booked a Flat/unit\r\nno. H-34B, 1600 sq.ft. which was allotted to complainant by vide Allotment\r\nLetter dated 24.10.2011. BSP of the plot was Rs. 62,50,000/- excluding EDC,\r\nIFSD,PLC and Golf Club Membership fee. Till date a sum of Rs.64,10,408/- has\r\nalready been paid by complainant which is almost 95% of total price. Flat buyer\r\nagreement was not executed till date. Respondent promised to handover possession\r\nwithin 24 months from the date of allotment along with the entire basic\r\namenities as per their broachers and advertisement. Construction of flat is still\r\nnot completed. Possession not offered till date. No sign of development is\r\nobserved as promised by respondents. Roads are in pathetic condition, internal\r\nroads are still unconstructed, there are no electricity connection arrangements\r\nas well as basic amenities such as water, sewerage, park roads, boundary wall\r\nis not constructed as yet. Club house as promised by respondent at the time of\r\nbooking is still not constructed. Further there are no signs of 18 Hole Golf\r\ncourses as promised by respondent. Revenue Rastas of the villages have not been\r\nyet acquired resulting which people of the village roaming within the township\r\nwith their cattle as such there are insufficient security arrangements have\r\nbeen made. Respondents were supposed to handover the possession of said plot to\r\ncomplainant till Oct. 2014 but inspite of the lapse of almost 5 years, there is\r\nno development at site.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left:.25in;text-align:justify;text-justify:\r\ninter-ideograph;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;font-family:\r\n&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">Complainant is a Senior Citizen. In view of the factual matrix as mentioned above\r\nin para 4 of this complaint and in view of the facts that despite lapse of 5\r\nyears&nbsp; respondent even failed to get the Flat\r\nbuyer agreement executed with complainant and further failed to complete construction\r\nof flat and further failed to offer possession alongwith all basic amenities as\r\nper their advertisement and brouchers and with clear approach from Ludhiana\r\nFerozepur Road, complainant seeks kind indulgence of this Hon’ble Authority in\r\ngranting following reliefs: 1. To refund the entire amount paid by complainant\r\ni. e. </span><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">Rs. 64,10,408/-</span><span style=\"font-size:\r\n14.0pt;font-family:&quot;Bookman Old Style&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"> alongwith interest @ 18% per\r\nannum from the date of respective payments till the realization alongwith Rs.5\r\nLac as compensation for mental harassment suffered by complainant and Rs.55,000/-\r\ncost of Litigation 2. Any other relief that this Hon’ble Authority may deem fit\r\nand appropriate in view of the facts and circumstances of the present\r\ncomplaint.<o:p></o:p></span></p>',7249272.00,0.00,'2014-10-24 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>NIL</p>','1','','2011-10-24 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Flat no. H-34B, Imperial Golf Estate, Ludhiana','','',1,0,0,0,'LUVMALHOTRA','2019-03-25 21:19:20.000','LUVMALHOTRA','2019-03-25 21:19:20.000'),(1271,1369,'1369',1448,'a7813333-38f0-43a0-989d-54439ebd8c18','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-03-27 15:55:30.000','Manish Malhotra','manishm0602@gmail.com',9815796644,0,214785597487,'149, Sector 70 SAS Nagar','',28,507,'160055','1','# 381/2, Sector 44-A','',6,128,'600044','ramnik gupta','ramnikgupta115@yahoo.co.in',9855506205,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0271','GOLF Link-II','Ansal Properties & Infrastructure Ltd and Ors.','info@ansalapi.com',0,0,'115, Ansal Bhawan, 16 K.G. Marg, New Delhi.','SCO No. 183-184, Sector 9-C, Chandigarh.',10,429,'110001','1','115, Ansal Bhawan, 16 K.G. Marg, New Delhi.','SCO No. 183-184, Sector 9-C, Chandigarh.',10,429,'110001','1','<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: roboto, serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">That one Monga Realtors Private\r\nLimited&nbsp;</span>booked one commercial plot in Golf &nbsp;Link-II &nbsp;project of the Respondents, now registered as\r\nPBRERA-SAS80-PR0271, and accordingly plot no. E-114 was allotted &nbsp;by Respondents vide allotment letter dated\r\n08.07.2011 and followed by execution of Commercial Plot Buyers Agreement\r\ninter-se them.<o:p></o:p></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: roboto, serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">The said allottee vide Sale\r\nAgreement dated 15.07.2011 sold the said plot to the Complainants and after due\r\ncompliance of the procedure, the Respondents endorsed the said Buyers Agreement\r\nin favor of &nbsp;the Complainants &nbsp;&nbsp;followed\r\nby issuance of Transfer Letter dated&nbsp;\r\n18.11.2011. The Complainants regularly paid the due amount towards BSP,\r\nEDC etc. totaling Rs.67,98,225/- out of the total consideration &nbsp;price of Rs. 78,84,975/-&nbsp; as acknowledged by the Respondents vide\r\nStatement of accounts. A sum of &nbsp;Rs. 7,24,500/-\r\nwas paid on 18.09.2015</span><span style=\"font-size:14.0pt;line-height:115%;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\"> </span><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: roboto, serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">out of total paid up. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: roboto, serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">That the Respondents have failed\r\nto deliver the possession of the plot despite committing to deliver within 36\r\nmonths of the Buyers Agreement &nbsp;i.e. by\r\n16/07/2014. The Respondents have neither invoked the force majeure clause nor\r\never communicated any circumstance beyond their control hence were\r\ncontractually and legally bound to deliver the possession within 36 months as\r\nthey were not entitled to any further period.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: roboto, serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">That the plot was purchased by\r\nthe Complainants for their personal use and/or for earning return on&nbsp; their savings in better way and as such are\r\nnot withdrawing from the project but are entitled for the specified interest on\r\ntheir paid up amount u/s 18(1) of the RERA Act read with Rule 16. The\r\nRespondents have also not complied with Rule 17 &nbsp;as they have failed to pay the interest\r\ndespite becoming due after 90 days from 16/07/2014.&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<h6 style=\"margin-left:1.0in;mso-add-space:auto;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;text-indent:-.5in;line-height:\r\n200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\"><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: roboto, serif;\">i)<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: roboto, serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">To grant interest on the paid up amount of Rs. 60,73,725/-&nbsp; w.e.f. 16/07/2014 and on Rs. 7,24,500/-\r\nw.e.f. 18.09.2015 at the specified rate under section 18 (1) of the RERA Act\r\n2016 read with Rule 16 of The Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation and\r\nDevelopment) Rules 2017 till the possession is actually delivered by the\r\nRespondents.<br><o:p></o:p></span><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: roboto, serif;\">ii)<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: roboto, serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">Directions to the Respondents to pay the entire arrears of interest as within\r\nthe specified time and further directing them to regularly pay the awarded\r\ninterest on every month when it becomes due till the possession is offered.<br><o:p></o:p></span><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: roboto, serif;\">iii)<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: roboto, serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">To pay Rs. 1,10,000/- towards the litigation costs.<br><o:p></o:p></span><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: roboto, serif;\">iv)<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 10pt; line-height: 200%; font-family: roboto, serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">Any other relief to which the Complainants may be found entitled to\r\nunder law and equity.<o:p></o:p></span></h6><p class=\"MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst\" style=\"margin-left:1.0in;mso-add-space:auto;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in;line-height:200%;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p>',7884975.00,6798225.00,'2014-07-16 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>NA</p>','1','','2011-07-08 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','Commercial Plot No. E-114','','',1,0,0,0,'manishmalhotra','2019-03-26 09:55:59.000','manishmalhotra','2019-03-26 09:55:59.000'),(1272,1374,'1374',1135,'7ce4ff29-c893-46aa-aac9-b9c5d5926814','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Mandeep Kaur','akhilesh@vyaslawassociates.com',9855004557,0,0,'4451, Ranjit Pura, Putlighar, ','',28,39,'143001','1','4451, Ranjit Pura, Putlighar, ','',28,39,'143001','Akhilesh Vyas','akhilesh@vyaslawassociates.com',9855004557,0,'Allottee','PBRERA-ASR02-PR0169','Guru Ramdas Urban Estate, Ajnala Road, Amritsar.','Punjab Urban Planning Development Authority','ca@puda.gov.in',0,0,'PUDA Bhawan','green avenue',28,39,'143001','1','PUDA Bhawan','green avenue',28,39,'143001','1','<p>That on the basis of advertisement published by respondent for allotment of 389 of residential plots at Guru Ramdas Urban Estate, Ajnala Road, Amritsar. The complainant believing the advertisement and brochure applied for allotment. On 09.03.2016 the respondents held draw for allotment of plot in which the complainant was successful. As per advertisement and brochure possession was to be given on 25% payment as earnest money. The complainant deposited the initial amount and letter of intent was issued on 12.05.2016. The tentative price of the plot is Rs.54,00,000/- @ 18000 per Sq. Yards.&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"line-height: 1.42857143;\">That the respondent further demanded the balance amount without even completion of any development at the site. The relevant clause of condition no.7 (II) in letter of intent with regard to payment and extension of time would be relevant. On 26.05.2016 the complainant moved an application for extension of time for deposit of 15% of tentative price. Respondent filed reply dated 27.06.2016. The complainant filed RTI dated 30.06.2016. No basic amenities have been provided as per the terms and conditions mentioned in the brochure. The respondent vide order dated 20.01.2017 cancel the plot arbitrarily. Complainant ready and willing to pay the amount as settled. Complainant also approached High court vide CWP-3536 of 2017 and also filed appeal under section 45 (5) of Punjab Regional and Town Planing Act, 1995 which was also dismissed. Now he challenges the cancellation of allotment alongwith the order 20.01.2017 passed by Estate Officer, PUDA and 05.06.2017 passed by Chief Administrator, PUDA as the complainant is ready and willing to pay the amount. He further challenges order dated 18.10.2018 passed by Special Secretary cum Revisional Authority, Department of Housing and &nbsp;Urban Development, Punjab. Complainant was allottee of plot No.297. Even earlier cancel plots 138, 136, 135, 156 and 10-C have earlier been reinstated by respondents.&nbsp;</span></p>','<p>1. The complainant prays for reinstatement of her residential plot measuring 300 Sq. Yards as allotted to her vide letter of intent dated 12.05.2016.&nbsp;</p><p>2. The complainant prays for setting aside of cancellation order vide its order dated 20.01.2017 &nbsp;passed by Estate Officer, PUDA. </p><p>3. The complainant prays for setting aside the cancellation order vide its order dated&nbsp;<span style=\"line-height: 1.42857143;\">&nbsp;05.06.2017&nbsp;</span><span style=\"line-height: 1.42857143;\">passed by Chief Administrator, PUDA.&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"line-height: 1.42857143;\">4.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"line-height: 1.42857143;\">The complainant prays for setting aside the cancellation order vide its order dated&nbsp;</span><span style=\"line-height: 1.42857143;\">&nbsp;</span><span style=\"line-height: 1.42857143;\">&nbsp;</span><span style=\"line-height: 1.42857143;\">18.10.2018 passed by Special Secretary cum Revisional Authority, Department of Housing and &nbsp;Urban Development, Punjab.&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"line-height: 1.42857143;\">5. That no interest or penal interest shall be charged from the complainant for delayed payments as no development has been done by the respondent department uptill now in the project.&nbsp;</span></p>',5400000.00,0.00,'2016-08-12 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>1. That the plots allotted to the complainant shall not be allotted to some other person during the pendency of this case.&nbsp;</p><p>2. That the interest and penal interest to be charged by the respondents on delayed payment of the complainant may be waived off during the pendency of this petition. As the payment got delayed due to non development of the project by the respondent.&nbsp;</p>','1','','2016-12-05 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','297','','',1,0,0,0,'akhilesh','2019-03-26 20:35:15.000','akhilesh','2019-03-26 20:35:15.000'),(1273,1375,'1375',1450,'99509e83-b468-4aae-973b-0c821afca0cc','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-03-29 11:53:58.000','AKHILESH KHANNA','khanna.chd@gmail.com',9815509469,0,0,'#3299 , SECTOR 19-D ','',6,128,'160019','1','#3299 First Floor, SECTOR 19-D ','',6,128,'160019','D.KHANNA Adv.','khanna.chd@gmail.com',9815509469,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PB0116','750 PLOT SCHEME (IT CITY, MOHALI)','ESTATE OFFICER, GMADA','helpdesk@gmada.gov.in',0,0,'PUDA BHAVAN , SECTOR-62, MOHALI(S.A.S .NAGAR)','',28,507,'160062','1','PUDA BHAVAN , SECTOR-62, MOHALI(S.A.S .NAGAR)','',28,507,'160062','1','<p style=\"margin-bottom: 0px; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 12px; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;; color: rgb(69, 69, 69);\">That one Mr.Vikram Rai , s/o Sh.Himmat Rai, was allocated an LOI for the allotment of Residential Plot measuring 256.66 Sq.yds. in category \'\'Schedule cast /Schedule tribe (750 Plots category scheme) against Application Form no.8596&nbsp; for the draw of Lots held by the GMADA on dated 21.09.2016 (Serial No.155) in I.T. CITY S.A.S. Nagar (Mohali), issued vide GMADA \'s Letter of Intent /Memo No.GMADA-EO/2047/6460 , dtd: 22.02.2017. On an application having been made by&nbsp; aforesaid allottee Mr.Vikram Rai for transfer of Letter of Intent in favour of the complainant i.e.Mr.Akhilesh Khanna, the respondent pursuant to the request transferred the LOI&nbsp; in the name of complainant vide memo no.9554 dated 10.03.2017 subject to the condition to abide by the terms and condition mentioned in the LOI as well as the provisions of Punjab Regional Town Planning &amp; Development Act, 1995.As per CL.15 of LOI the possession of plot was to be given to the allottee within one year i.e.by 21.02.2018. The&nbsp; possession of the&nbsp; plot has not been given by the respondent till today as promised.The complainant has paid &nbsp;complete price &amp; made full &nbsp;payment along with taxes , transfer fees and interest&nbsp;amounting to&nbsp;Rs.5209620 /-. It is submitted that the respondent has miserably failed to carry development works of the area so as to hand over possession to the allottee\'s/holder of LOIs as promised and&nbsp; which is likely total further considerable time . Thus, the complainant is entitled for interest&nbsp; @12% PA (as charged/calculated/applied by the respondent as per LOI for non payment of instalments)&nbsp;&nbsp;on the payment made to respondent till actual possession of the plot is handed over by the respondent.&nbsp;</p><div><br></div>','<p style=\"margin-bottom: 0px; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 12px; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;; color: rgb(69, 69, 69);\">In view of the facts mentioned in Para no.4 above, the complainant prays that the respondent be directed to pay interest @12% PA(as charged/calculated/applied by the respondent as per LOI for non payment of instalments) from the date of issuance of LOI &nbsp;22.02.2017 till the actual possession is handed over to the complainant. As the relief claimed involves future interest as well &nbsp;for uncertain period , the respondent may be directed to deposit in this Hon\'ble tribunal Rs15 lacs as security .&nbsp;</p>',5209620.00,5209620.00,'2018-02-21 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p style=\"margin-bottom: 0px; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 12px; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;; color: rgb(69, 69, 69);\">Deposit an amount of Rs 15 lacs as prayed above in para no.5.</p>','1','','2017-02-22 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'khanna3299','2019-03-28 18:03:48.000','khanna3299','2019-03-28 18:03:48.000'),(1274,1280,'1280',1253,'70b12b4c-e79c-4d06-9369-5f060352ed65','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-03-29 13:15:20.000','Tejbir Singh Sawhney','tssawhney@yahoo.com',9876604020,0,0,'Flat No 2302, Wing A, Ajmera Zeon','Ajmera I-Land, Bhakti Park, Anik Wadala Link Road, Wadala East',21,400,'400037','1','Flat No 2302, Wing A, Ajmera Zeon','Ajmera I-Land, Bhakti Park, Anik Wadala Link Road, Wadala East',21,400,'400037','Ankit Chowdhri','ankit_chowdhri@hotmail.com',9814433585,1724630585,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PM0004','Falcon View Apartments \r\nTower C','Janta Land Promoters Pvt Ltd ','janta@jantahousing.com',0,0,'SCO 39 - 42 , Sector 82 ','SAS Nagar , Mohali ',28,507,'140306','1','SCO 39 - 42 , Sector 82 ','SAS Nagar , Mohali ',28,507,'140306','1','<p>i)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That the Respondent was engaged in the development of the Super Mega Mixed Use Integrated Industrial Park Project of 263.38 acre of land in sector 66 – A,82 and 83, Mohali.&nbsp;</p><p>ii)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That the Applicant had applied for allotment of one 4 BHk flat in the above sated project vide application form dated 01.06.2013 which is annexed herewith as Annexure C-1.</p><p>iii)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That in reference thereof the applicant was allotted a Unit No./ Apartment No. C-901 in the above-mentioned project along with a construction linked plan vide an allotment letter 27.04.2013 which is annexed herewith as Annexure C-2.</p><p>iv)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>The as per the Construction Linked Installment Plan appended to the aforesaid Agreement in pursuance wherein the applicant was required to pay Rs.1,08,43,200/- out of which the complainant had already paid Rs.27,94,563/- (Principal Rs.26,94,595/- and Service Tax of Rs.99,968/-) vide receipts Nos. 4422 and 4889 dated 01.06.2013 and 18.07.2013 respectively.&nbsp; An amount of Rs.10,934,794.00/- was paid by the Applicant to the Respondent upto 21.02.2018 as reflected in the flat holders card annexed herewith as Annexure C-3.</p><p>v)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That the respondent was to hand over possession within 30 months from date of allotment As per Clause 2.24 of Annexure C-2 which has not been complied with till date despite repeated reminders.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>vi)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That finally reminder dated 02.10.2018 vide email is annexed herewith as Annexure C-4 to no avail.</p><p>vii)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>That aggrieved therewith the applicant seeks to invoke the jurisdiction of this Hon’ble forum for relief as the provisions of RERA have been violated owing to undue delay in delivery of possession of the flat to the complainant.&nbsp;</p><div><br></div>','<p>i)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To direct the respondent to deliver the flat to the complainant immediately without any increased charges.</p><p>ii)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To direct the respondent to pay interest on the Amount of Rs.1,09,34,794/- i.e. the payment made by the applicant till date as prescribed by the Act and the Rules framed there under.&nbsp;</p><p>iii)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To waive off GST applicable on the outstanding amount.</p><p>iv)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To issue directions to pay cost of litigation so incurred by the complainant to the tune of Rs.2,00,000/-.</p><p>v)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>To issue direction to pay compensation to the complainant for the compensation for his mental agony, pain and harassment to the tune of Rs.5,00,000/-.&nbsp;</p><p>vi)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">	</span>Any other relief which the Applicant is entitled for under the Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Act, 2016 and the Punjab State Real Estate (Regulation &amp; Development) Rules, 2017.&nbsp;</p><div><br></div>',13021778.00,10934794.00,'2016-10-27 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>To direct the respondent to deliver the flat to the complainant immediately without any increased charges.</p><p><br></p>','1','','2013-04-27 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00',' C-901, Facing Green of 3012 sq. ft., Wing C, 9th Floor, Falcon View, Phase 1, Sector 66A, Mohali, Punjab.','','',1,1,0,0,'AnkitChowdhri','2019-03-29 13:14:07.000','AnkitChowdhri','2019-03-29 13:14:07.000'),(1275,1376,'1376',1393,'d33e1b7d-de22-43e0-97c8-115b8ed3d62e','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Balwinder Singh ','harish635@rediffmail.com',9855582067,0,754090988006,'House No.2213','Sector 71',28,507,'160062','1','House No.2213','Sector 71',28,507,'160062','Harish Goyal','harish635@rediffmail.com',9815628635,1722217635,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PM0121','Sector 88 and 89 including purab premium apartments','Estate Officer GMADA','eo@gmada.gov.in',0,1722213535,'PUDA Bhawan','Sector 62',28,507,'160062','1','PUDA Bhawan','Sector 62',28,507,'160062','1','<p><span style=\"font-size:13.0pt;line-height:115%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:Calibri;\r\nmso-fareast-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN;mso-fareast-language:\r\nEN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\">Respondents acquired land vide award dated\r\n15/11/11. In lieu of compensation GMADA has given land pooling scheme,\r\naccording to which owner will get developed land in lieu of his acquired land.\r\nNeither land owner required to pay anything nor GMADA has to pay anything for\r\nthe same(Anne C/2). As per LOI dated 17/6/13, issued to the vendor of the\r\ncomplainant, he can transfer the LOI on paying the 2.5% of price of plot, which\r\nwas fixed by GMADA @25,000/- per sq. Yds. Complainant purchased the Plot from Harmeet\r\nSingh etc. vide transfer letter dated 12/4/2017, after paying Rs.147961 as\r\ntransfer fee (Ann C/4). Orally GMADA have promised that they will develop land\r\nin 1.5 to 2 years. However now on 10/1/2019 they have issued allotment letter and\r\noffer of possession, without completing the development on the spot(Ann C/5).\r\nThey have also demanded extra amount for Corner, which was not mention either\r\nin award or policy of land pooling or in LOI. Possession also offered without\r\ncompleting the development work. Even in High Court in CWP No.398/2016, EO has\r\nstated that they will complete development work by 30/11/2018. But to develop\r\nthe parks they have issued the tenders only on 8/2/2019 to be completed in 8\r\nMonths. (Ann C/6) Although some development work is going but same is not\r\ncompleted. No street light was working. Sewerage System was lying open. Even\r\ndevelopment of Parks has not been started yet. Roads are only half done. So\r\nthere is no question of the handing over the possession. There is a huge delay\r\nin handing over the possession, whereas they have developed the area for\r\nprivate builder in 2016 itself. Further even demand for extra amount for Corner\r\nis also not justified, as Nothing such condition in Award, or in Policy or in\r\nOriginal LOI. Further in ECO City matter also in case of Land pooling scheme,\r\nGMADA has itself withdrawn such charges, when people approached HIGH COURT by\r\nway of CWP No.25715/15 (Ann C/7). One Similar LOI is (Ann C/3)</span><br></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\">1. Prayer for issuance of\r\ndirection to the Respondent to handover the possession of the Plot after\r\ncompletion of the Development work, as defined under Section 2(t), 2(w), 2(zb)\r\nof the The Real Estate (Reg. and Development), Act 2006, as allotment letter\r\nissued on 10/1/2019, whereas till date development work is not complete. Roads\r\nare not complete, street lights are not working, even for parks, they have\r\nissued tenders just on 8/2/2019, after issuance of allotment letter. 2. To Pay\r\ninterest @18% p.a. (or as per the provisions of the Act) for delayed period of\r\nPossession, from the date of issuance of LOI till handing over the actual\r\npossession, after completing the development work, since entire consideration\r\nhas already paid to them, in form of land. Further they have developed the land\r\nfor the private builder Hero Homes, within 6 months in the year 2016,\r\ndevelopment for the common people only started after intervention of the\r\nHon\'ble High Court in CWP No.398 of 2016. Further even allotment letters are\r\nissued only to show in the Hon\'ble High Court, otherwise development is still\r\nincomplete. There is a huge delay of 6 years in handing over the possession.\r\nThey have violated the various provisions of the RERA Act. 3. Refund\r\nRs.5,00,000/- along with interest @18% P.a. paid as extra amount on account of\r\nPreferential Location Charges, being beyond the Scope of LOI, Award and Land\r\nacquisition Policy and in view of withdrawal of such charges by themselves in\r\nECO City. In the LOI no such condition was mentioned. Now they cannot of their\r\nown, could not start charging extra amount as per their own whim and caprice.\r\n4. This Hon\'ble Court may grant any other relief, which this Hon\'ble Court may\r\ndeem fit and proper in the peculiar facts and circumstances of the present\r\ncase.<o:p></o:p></p>',5000000.00,5500000.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>NA</p>','1','','2019-01-10 00:00:00','2013-06-17 00:00:00','Plot No.2204, Sector 89, Block C, SAS Nagar, Mohali','','',2,0,0,0,'harish635','2019-03-30 12:56:28.000','harish635','2019-03-30 12:56:28.000'),(1276,1376,'1376',1393,'d33e1b7d-de22-43e0-97c8-115b8ed3d62e','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Balwinder Singh ','harish635@rediffmail.com',9855582067,0,754090988006,'House No.2213','Sector 71',28,507,'160062','1','House No.2213','Sector 71',28,507,'160062','Harish Goyal','harish635@rediffmail.com',9815628635,1722217635,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PM0121','Sector 88 and 89 including purab premium apartments','Estate Officer GMADA','eo@gmada.gov.in',0,1722213535,'PUDA Bhawan','Sector 62',28,507,'160062','1','PUDA Bhawan','Sector 62',28,507,'160062','1','<p><span style=\"font-size:13.0pt;line-height:115%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:Calibri;\r\nmso-fareast-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-ansi-language:EN-IN;mso-fareast-language:\r\nEN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\">Respondents acquired land vide award dated\r\n15/11/11. In lieu of compensation GMADA has given land pooling scheme,\r\naccording to which owner will get developed land in lieu of his acquired land.\r\nNeither land owner required to pay anything nor GMADA has to pay anything for\r\nthe same(Anne C/2). As per LOI dated 17/6/13, issued to the vendor of the\r\ncomplainant, he can transfer the LOI on paying the 2.5% of price of plot, which\r\nwas fixed by GMADA @25,000/- per sq. Yds. Complainant purchased the Plot from Harmeet\r\nSingh etc. vide transfer letter dated 12/4/2017, after paying Rs.147961 as\r\ntransfer fee (Ann C/4). Orally GMADA have promised that they will develop land\r\nin 1.5 to 2 years. However now on 10/1/2019 they have issued allotment letter and\r\noffer of possession, without completing the development on the spot(Ann C/5).\r\nThey have also demanded extra amount for Corner, which was not mention either\r\nin award or policy of land pooling or in LOI. Possession also offered without\r\ncompleting the development work. Even in High Court in CWP No.398/2016, EO has\r\nstated that they will complete development work by 30/11/2018. But to develop\r\nthe parks they have issued the tenders only on 8/2/2019 to be completed in 8\r\nMonths. (Ann C/6) Although some development work is going but same is not\r\ncompleted. No street light was working. Sewerage System was lying open. Even\r\ndevelopment of Parks has not been started yet. Roads are only half done. So\r\nthere is no question of the handing over the possession. There is a huge delay\r\nin handing over the possession, whereas they have developed the area for\r\nprivate builder in 2016 itself. Further even demand for extra amount for Corner\r\nis also not justified, as Nothing such condition in Award, or in Policy or in\r\nOriginal LOI. Further in ECO City matter also in case of Land pooling scheme,\r\nGMADA has itself withdrawn such charges, when people approached HIGH COURT by\r\nway of CWP No.25715/15 (Ann C/7). One Similar LOI is (Ann C/3)</span><br></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\">1. Prayer for issuance of\r\ndirection to the Respondent to handover the possession of the Plot after\r\ncompletion of the Development work, as defined under Section 2(t), 2(w), 2(zb)\r\nof the The Real Estate (Reg. and Development), Act 2006, as allotment letter\r\nissued on 10/1/2019, whereas till date development work is not complete. Roads\r\nare not complete, street lights are not working, even for parks, they have\r\nissued tenders just on 8/2/2019, after issuance of allotment letter. 2. To Pay\r\ninterest @18% p.a. (or as per the provisions of the Act) for delayed period of\r\nPossession, from the date of issuance of LOI till handing over the actual\r\npossession, after completing the development work, since entire consideration\r\nhas already paid to them, in form of land. Further they have developed the land\r\nfor the private builder Hero Homes, within 6 months in the year 2016,\r\ndevelopment for the common people only started after intervention of the\r\nHon\'ble High Court in CWP No.398 of 2016. Further even allotment letters are\r\nissued only to show in the Hon\'ble High Court, otherwise development is still\r\nincomplete. There is a huge delay of 6 years in handing over the possession.\r\nThey have violated the various provisions of the RERA Act. 3. Refund\r\nRs.5,00,000/- along with interest @18% P.a. paid as extra amount on account of\r\nPreferential Location Charges, being beyond the Scope of LOI, Award and Land\r\nacquisition Policy and in view of withdrawal of such charges by themselves in\r\nECO City. In the LOI no such condition was mentioned. Now they cannot of their\r\nown, could not start charging extra amount as per their own whim and caprice.\r\n4. This Hon\'ble Court may grant any other relief, which this Hon\'ble Court may\r\ndeem fit and proper in the peculiar facts and circumstances of the present\r\ncase.<o:p></o:p></p>',5000000.00,5500000.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>NA</p>','1','','2019-01-10 00:00:00','2013-06-17 00:00:00','Plot No.2204, Sector 89, Block C, SAS Nagar, Mohali','','',2,0,0,0,'harish635','2019-03-30 14:31:30.000','harish635','2019-03-30 14:31:30.000'),(1277,1376,'1376',1393,'d33e1b7d-de22-43e0-97c8-115b8ed3d62e','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-03-30 16:15:51.000','Balwinder Singh ','harish635@rediffmail.com',9855582067,0,754090988006,'House No.2213','Sector 71',28,507,'160062','1','House No.2213','Sector 71',28,507,'160062','Harish Goyal','harish635@rediffmail.com',9815628635,1722217635,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PM0121','Sector 88 and 89 including purab premium apartments','Estate Officer GMADA','eo@gmada.gov.in',0,1722213535,'PUDA Bhawan','Sector 62',28,507,'160062','1','PUDA Bhawan','Sector 62',28,507,'160062','1','<p><span style=\"font-size:13.0pt;line-height:115%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;