 LOI. Further in ECO City matter also in case of Land pooling scheme,\r\nGMADA has itself withdrawn such charges, when people approached HIGH COURT by\r\nway of CWP No.25715/15 (Ann C/7). One Similar LOI is (Ann C/3)</span><br></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\">1. Prayer for issuance of\r\ndirection to the Respondent to handover the possession of the Plot after\r\ncompletion of the Development work, as defined under Section 2(t), 2(w), 2(zb)\r\nof the The Real Estate (Reg. and Development), Act 2006, as allotment letter\r\nissued on 10/1/2019, whereas till date development work is not complete. Roads\r\nare not complete, street lights are not working, even for parks, they have\r\nissued tenders just on 8/2/2019, after issuance of allotment letter. 2. To Pay\r\ninterest @18% p.a. (or as per the provisions of the Act) for delayed period of\r\nPossession, from the date of issuance of LOI till handing over the actual\r\npossession, after completing the development work, since entire consideration\r\nhas already paid to them, in form of land. Further they have developed the land\r\nfor the private builder Hero Homes, within 6 months in the year 2016,\r\ndevelopment for the common people only started after intervention of the\r\nHon\'ble High Court in CWP No.398 of 2016. Further even allotment letters are\r\nissued only to show in the Hon\'ble High Court, otherwise development is still\r\nincomplete. There is a huge delay of 6 years in handing over the possession.\r\nThey have violated the various provisions of the RERA Act. 3. Refund\r\nRs.5,00,000/- along with interest @18% P.a. paid as extra amount on account of\r\nPreferential Location Charges, being beyond the Scope of LOI, Award and Land\r\nacquisition Policy and in view of withdrawal of such charges by themselves in\r\nECO City. In the LOI no such condition was mentioned. Now they cannot of their\r\nown, could not start charging extra amount as per their own whim and caprice.\r\n4. This Hon\'ble Court may grant any other relief, which this Hon\'ble Court may\r\ndeem fit and proper in the peculiar facts and circumstances of the present\r\ncase.<o:p></o:p></p>',5000000.00,5500000.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>NA</p>','1','','2019-01-10 00:00:00','2013-06-17 00:00:00','Plot No.2204, Sector 89, Block C, SAS Nagar, Mohali','','',1,1,0,0,'harish635','2019-03-30 14:45:28.000','harish635','2019-03-30 14:45:28.000'),(1278,1377,'1377',1393,'d33e1b7d-de22-43e0-97c8-115b8ed3d62e','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-03-30 18:43:01.000','Kamaldeep Kaur','harish635@rediffmail.com',9501814455,0,580355861836,'H No. 222','Sector 80',28,507,'160062','1','H No. 222','Sector 80',28,507,'160062','Harish Goyal','harish635@rediffmail.com',9815628635,1722217635,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PM0121','Sector 88 and 89 including purab premium apartments','Estate Officer GMADA','eo@gmada.gov.in',0,1722213535,'PUDA Bhawan','Sector 62',28,507,'160062','1','PUDA Bhawan','Sector 62',28,507,'160062','0','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\">Respondents acquired land vide\r\naward dated 15/11/11. In lieu of compensation GMADA has given land pooling\r\nscheme, according to which owner will get developed land in lieu of his\r\nacquired land. Neither land owner required to pay anything nor GMADA has to pay\r\nanything for the same(Anne C/2). As per LOI dated 27/9/2013, issued to the\r\nvendor of the complainant, he can transfer the LOI on paying the 2.5% of price\r\nof plot, which was fixed by GMADA @25,000/- per sq. Yds. (C/3) Complainant\r\npurchased the Plot from Avtar Singh etc. vide transfer letter dated 18/3/2017,\r\nafter paying Rs.219836 as transfer fee (Ann C/4). Orally GMADA have promised\r\nthat they will develop land in 1.5 to 2 years. However now on 12/3/2019 they\r\nhave issued allotment letter and offer of possession, without completing the\r\ndevelopment on the spot(Ann C/5). They have also demanded extra amount for Park\r\nFacing, which was not mention either in award or policy of land pooling or in\r\nLOI. Possession also offered without completing the development work. Even in\r\nHigh Court in CWP No.398/2016, EO has stated that they will complete\r\ndevelopment work by 30/11/2018. But to develop the parks they have issued the\r\ntenders only on 8/2/2019 to be completed in 8 Months. (Ann C/6) Although some\r\ndevelopment work is going on but same is not completed. No street light was\r\nworking. Sewerage System was lying open. Even development of Parks has not been\r\nstarted yet. Roads are only half done. So there is no question of the handing\r\nover the possession. There is a huge delay in handing over the possession,\r\nwhereas they have developed the area for private builder in 2016 itself.\r\nFurther even demand for extra amount for Park Facing is also not justified, as\r\nNothing such condition in Award, or in Policy or in Original LOI. Further in\r\nECO City matter also in case of Land pooling scheme, GMADA has itself withdrawn\r\nsuch charges, when people approached HIGH COURT by way of CWP No.25715/15 (Ann\r\nC/7).&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\">1. Prayer for issuance of\r\ndirection to the Respondent to handover the possession of the Plot after\r\ncompletion of the Development work, as defined under Section 2(t), 2(w), 2(zb)\r\nof the The Real Estate (Reg. and Development), Act 2006, as allotment letter\r\nissued on 12/3/2019, whereas till date development work is not complete. Roads\r\nare not complete, street lights are not working, even for parks, they have\r\nissued tenders just on 8/2/2019, after issuance of allotment letter. 2. To Pay\r\ninterest @18% p.a. (or as per the provisions of the Act) for delayed period of\r\nPossession, from the date of issuance of LOI till handing over the actual\r\npossession, after completing the development work, since entire consideration\r\nhas already paid to them, in form of land. Further they have developed the land\r\nfor the private builder Hero Homes, within 6 months in the year 2016,\r\ndevelopment for the common people only started after intervention of the\r\nHon\'ble High Court in CWP No.398 of 2016. Further even allotment letters are\r\nissued only to show in the Hon\'ble High Court, otherwise development is still\r\nincomplete. There is a huge delay of 6 years in handing over the possession.\r\nThey have violated the various provisions of the RERA Act. 3. Not to charge any\r\nextra amount on account of Preferential Location Charges, being beyond the\r\nScope of LOI, Award and Land acquisition Policy and in view of withdrawal of\r\nsuch charges by themselves in ECO City. In the LOI no such condition was\r\nmentioned. Now they cannot of their own, could not start charging extra amount\r\nas per their own whim and caprice. 4. This Hon\'ble Court may grant any other\r\nrelief, which this Hon\'ble Court may deem fit and proper in the peculiar facts\r\nand circumstances of the present case.<o:p></o:p></p>',7500000.00,7500000.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>For issuance of direction not to charge any amount on account of PLC, during the pendency of the present complaint and also not to cancel/Resume the plot during the pendency of the present complaint.</p>','1','','2019-03-12 00:00:00','2013-09-27 00:00:00','Plot No.1234, Sector 89, Block B, SAS Nagar, Mohali','','',1,1,0,0,'harish635','2019-03-30 15:58:02.000','harish635','2019-03-30 15:58:02.000'),(1279,1378,'1378',1393,'d33e1b7d-de22-43e0-97c8-115b8ed3d62e','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-03-31 14:05:57.000','Tejwant Singh','harish635@rediffmail.com',9988400388,0,979924653886,'H. No.44, MECO','Sector 68',28,507,'160062','1','H. No.44, MECO','Sector 68',28,507,'160062','Harish Goyal','harish635@rediffmail.com',9815628635,1722217635,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PM0121','Sector 88 and 89 including Purab Premium Apartments','Estate Officer GMADA','eo@gmada.gov.in',0,1722213535,'PUDA Bhawan','Sector 6