ty matter also in case of Land pooling scheme, GMADA has itself withdrawn\r\nsuch charges, when people approached HIGH COURT by way of CWP No.25715/15 (Ann\r\nC/7).&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></p>','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\">1. Prayer for issuance of\r\ndirection to the Respondent to handover the possession of the Plot after\r\ncompletion of the Development work, as defined under Section 2(t), 2(w), 2(zb)\r\nof the The Real Estate (Reg. and Development), Act 2006, as allotment letter\r\nissued on 28/1/2019, whereas till date development work is not complete. Roads\r\nare not complete, street lights are not working, even for parks, they have\r\nissued tenders just on 8/2/2019, after issuance of allotment letter. 2. To Pay\r\ninterest @18% p.a. (or as per the provisions of the Act) for delayed period of\r\nPossession, from the date of issuance of LOI till handing over the actual\r\npossession, after completing the development work, since entire consideration\r\nhas already paid to them, in form of land. Further they have developed the land\r\nfor the private builder Hero Homes, within 6 months in the year 2016,\r\ndevelopment for the common people only started after intervention of the\r\nHon\'ble High Court in CWP No.398 of 2016. Further even allotment letters are\r\nissued only to show in the Hon\'ble High Court, otherwise development is still\r\nincomplete. There is a huge delay of 6 years in handing over the possession.\r\nThey have violated the various provisions of the RERA Act. 3. Not to charge any\r\nextra amount on account of Preferential Location Charges, being beyond the\r\nScope of LOI, Award and Land acquisition Policy and in view of withdrawal of\r\nsuch charges by themselves in ECO City. In the LOI no such condition was\r\nmentioned. Now they cannot of their own, could not start charging extra amount\r\nas per their own whim and caprice. 4. This Hon\'ble Court may grant any other\r\nrelief, which this Hon\'ble Court may deem fit and proper in the peculiar facts\r\nand circumstances of the present case.<o:p></o:p></p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>',7500000.00,7500000.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Prayed for not to charge any thing on account of PLC and further not to resume/cancel the plot on account of demand of PLC.</p>','1','','2019-01-28 00:00:00','2013-09-30 00:00:00','Plot No.1131, Sector 89, Block B, SAS Nagar, Mohali','','',1,1,0,0,'harish635','2019-03-31 08:03:44.000','harish635','2019-03-31 08:03:44.000'),(1280,1379,'1379',1450,'99509e83-b468-4aae-973b-0c821afca0cc','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-04-04 14:42:27.000','AKHILESH KHANNA','khanna.chd@gmail.com',9815509469,0,0,'#3299 , SECTOR 19-D ','',6,128,'160019','1','#3299 , SECTOR 19-D ','',6,128,'160019','D.KHANNA Advocate','khanna.chd@gmail.com',9815509469,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PM0116','ESTATE OFFICER, GMADA','ESTATE OFFICER, GMADA','helpdesk@gmada.gov.in',0,0,'PUDA BHAVAN,SECTOR-62,MOHALI(S.A.S.NAGAR)','',28,507,'160062','1','PUDA BHAVAN,SECTOR-62,MOHALI(S.A.S.NAGAR)','',28,507,'160062','1','<p style=\"margin-bottom: 0px; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 12px; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;; color: rgb(69, 69, 69);\">That&nbsp; Mr.Vivek Goel, s/o Sh.Shiv Charn and Ms.Ekta Goel w/o Vivek Goel residents of # 301, III Floor Maya Gardens, Phase 2 , VIP road ,Zirakpur,Punjab were holders of LOI number 25201 , dated 06-Jun-2016 issued under Sector 82A/83A- Land Pooling(Ref.No.82-0540/-) in respect of commercial booth measuring 20.00 Sq.Yards. This LOI was transferred vide No.12029 dated 27.03.2017 in favour of the complainants after having made payment of about Rs.30 lacs to them along with Rs.34700/- as transfer fee.It may be mentioned here that as per brochure of respondent/GMADA , this commercial area of 20.00 Sq.Yards commercial booths adjoins another residential plotted area offered by respondent GMADA known as 750 Plots&nbsp; Scheme (IT City , Mohali), S.A.S .Nagar (each measuring 256.66 Sq.Yards) it is further stated here that the respondent/GMADA in residential , 750 Plots&nbsp; Scheme (IT City , Mohali), S.A.S .Nagar had promised to deliver the possession within one year issuance of first LOI i.e. by 05-Jun-2017(As per original LOI). The respondent /GMADA has miserably failed to develop the area so as to further hand over the possession to the allottees/ holders of LOIs, which is causing great financial loss to the complainants. It may be added here that the present cost of 20.00 Sq Yard commercial booth in the vicinity is about Rs 36 lacs .It is also relevant to assert that various builders are offering 10-15% rental on the deposited money. Therefore, the complainants are entitled for interest @12% on equal amount or as decided by this Honble Authority.The complainants are aggrieved by the inaction of the respondent GMADA and are thus entitled for interest as prayed for.</p><p>\r\n</p><p style=\"margin-bottom: 0px; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 12px; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;; color: rgb(69, 69, 69); min-height: 14px;\"><br></p>','<p style=\"margin-bottom: 0px; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 12px; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;; color: rgb(69, 69, 69);\">In view of the facts mentioned in Para no.4 above, the complainants pray that the respondent be directed to pay interest @12% (as charged/calculated/applied by the respondent as per LOI for non payment of instalments) from the date of issuance of LOI dated&nbsp; 27.03.2017 till the actual possession is handed over to the complainants . As the relief claimed involves future interest as well as for uncertain period , the respondent may be directed to deposit in this Hon\'ble Authority Rs15 lacs as security .&nbsp;</p>',3600000.00,0.00,'2017-06-05 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p style=\"margin-bottom: 0px; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 12px; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;; color: rgb(69, 69, 69);\">Deposit an amount of Rs 15 lacs as prayed above in para no.5.</p><div><br></div>','1','','2017-03-27 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',2,0,0,0,'khanna3299','2019-04-01 19:19:45.000','khanna3299','2019-04-01 19:19:45.000'),(1281,1380,'1380',1461,'e6eeaa94-243d-4097-9316-b3a4a286d8d7','FormTypeM',1,0,0,0,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','Maninder singh','mandeepkhuranj@gmail.com',9417422227,0,0,'House no. 43','old mohinder nagar, kanal road',15,267,'180001','1','House no. 43','old mohinder nagar, kanal road',15,267,'180001','Amarbir Dhaliwal','amarbir67@hotmail.com',9914900723,0,'Promoter','PBRERA-SAS81-PM0010','fashion technology park','Chandigarh overseas private limited','chdoverseas@gmail.com',0,0,'S.C.O. No. 196-197, ','Sector-34-A, Top Floor,',6,128,'160022','0','Sohana-Landran road,','adjoining BSF, Sector 90, Mohali,',28,507,'160062','1','<p>ABCD</p>','<p>ABCDE</p>',125000.00,125000.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>ABCDE</p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',1,0,0,0,'ManinderSingh','2019-04-02 13:12:55.000','ManinderSingh','2019-04-02 13:12:55.000'),(1282,1330,'1330',1112,'29af80b1-85ed-4b88-8344-b429d2f24eca','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-04-02 16:53:14.000','Bee Gee Builtech','savindersinghgill@gmail.com',9988861126,0,0,'SCF 44-45, Ist Floor','Sector-9',13,15,'134108','1','SCF 44-45, Ist Floor','Sector-9',13,15,'134108','Savinder Singh Gill','savindersinghgill@gmail.com',9988861126,0,'Allottee','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0103','Palm Village','Manoj Kumar Arora','mka150266@gmaik.com',9958115380,0,'B-1102, 11th Floor, Tower-B, Palm Village ','Village-Desumajra, Sector-126',28,507,'140301','1','B-1102, 11th Floor, Tower-B, Palm Village ','Village-Desumajra, Sector-126',28,507,'140301','0','<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: roboto, serif; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\">That\r\nthe complainant no. 1 is a promoter having RERA registration no.\r\nPBRERA-SAS80-PR0103, which has developed project under the name and style of\r\n“PALM VILLAGE”, located in Sector-126, NH-21, S.A.S. Nagar, Mohali. The\r\ncomplainant no. 2 is a maintenance agency which has been entrusted upon with\r\nthe maintenance of the project of the complainant no. 1. It is pertinent to\r\nmention here that both the complainants have entered into an agreement for the\r\nsaid reason. That the respondents are allottees of the complainant no. 1 who\r\nhad purchased an apartment measuring 2180 sq. ft. (Approximate Super Area) in\r\nresale on 17.05.2016 in the abovementioned project and they were allotted flat\r\nno. B-1102 on 11th Floor in Tower-B vide re-allotment letter dated 19.05.2016.\r\nThat a buyer’s agreement was signed between the complainant no. 1 and the\r\noriginal allotees on 17.09.2012. The respondents were thereafter offered\r\npossession of the said apartment and the possession was taken over by the\r\noriginal allottee on 20.04.2016. The said agreement was endorsed in the name of\r\nrespondents after resale of the said apartment and all the rights and\r\nliabilities were undertaken by the respondents as they had stepped into the\r\nshoes of the original allottee.&nbsp; It is pertinent to mention here that in\r\nthe possession handing over letter, the respondents had undertaken to pay the\r\nmaintenance charges after taking over possession of the said apartment and had\r\nalso undertaken to enter into a maintenance agreement. The original allottees\r\nthereafter, entered into a maintenance agreement dated 20.04.2016 with the\r\ncomplainant no. 2. That the respondents despite been in possession of the said\r\napartment, has not been paying the maintenance charges fixed as per the maintenance\r\nagreement and is enjoying all the services free of cost.<o:p></o:p></span></p>','<p>&nbsp;Directing the respondents to pay the amount of Rs. 34,727/- due towards the maintenance charges.\r\nDirecting the respondents to pay interest on the amount due toward maintenace charges in terms of Section 19 (7) of RERA&nbsp; to the complainants.<br></p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Directing the respondents to pay interest on the due amount as mentioned in the maintenance agreement\r\ntill the pendency of the present complaint till actual payment.&nbsp;<br></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',1,1,0,0,'BeeG','2019-04-02 16:53:05.000','BeeG','2019-04-02 16:53:05.000'),(1283,1319,'1319',1112,'29af80b1-85ed-4b88-8344-b429d2f24eca','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-04-02 16:56:49.000','Bee Gee Builtech','savindersinghgill@gmail.com',9988861126,0,0,'SCF 44-45, Ist Floor','Sector-9',13,15,'134108','1','SCF 44-45, Ist Floor','Sector-9',13,15,'134108','Savinder Singh Gill','savindersinghgill@gmail.com',9988861126,0,'Allottee','PBRERA-SAS80-PR0103','Palm Village','Rohit Bhayana','r.bhayana28@gmail.com',9877777767,0,'C-901, 9th floor, Tower-C, Palm Village','village-Desumajra, sector-126',28,507,'140301','1','C-901, 9th floor, Tower-C, Palm Village','village-Desumajra, sector-126',28,507,'140301','1','<p>That the complainant no. 1 is the promoter having RERA registration no. PBRERA-SAS80-PR0103, has\r\ndeveloped project under the name and style of “PALM VILLAGE”, located in Sector-126, NH-21, S.A.S.\r\nNagar, Mohali. The complainant no. 2 is a maintenance agency which has been entrusted upon with the\r\nmaintenance of the project of the complainant no. 1. It is pertinent to mention here that both the\r\ncomplainants have entered into an agreement for the said reason. That the respondents are allottees of\r\nthe complainant no. 1 who had applied for an apartment measuring 2180 sq. ft. (Approximate Super Area)\r\non 15.03.2016 in the abovementioned project and in pursuance of the said booking, they were allotted flat\r\nno. C-901 on 9th Floor in Tower-C vide allotment letter dated 21.03.2016. That a buyer’s agreement\r\nwas signed between the complainant no. 1 and the respondents on 21.03.2016. The respondents were\r\nthereafter offered possession of the said apartment and the possession was taken over by the\r\nrespondents on 31.03.2016. Further it is pertinent to mention here that in the possession handing over\r\nletter, the respondents had undertaken to pay the maintenance charges after taking over possession of\r\nthe said apartment and had also undertaken to enter into a maintenance agreement. The respondents\r\nthereafter, entered into a maintenance agreement dated 31.03.2016 with the complainant no. 2. That the\r\nrespondents despite been in possession of the said apartment, has not been paying the maintenance\r\ncharges fixed as per the maintenance agreement and is enjoying all the services free of cost. It is further\r\npertinent to mention here that a number of public notices has been got attached in the society whereby\r\nthe respondents were called upon various times for payment of the maintenance charges but no heed\r\nwas paid to the said notices by the respondents.&nbsp;<br></p>','<p>Directing the respondents to pay the amount of Rs. 45,878/- due towards the maintenance charges.\r\nDirecting the respondent to pay interest on the amount due toward maintenace charges in terms of Section 19 (7) of RERA&nbsp; to the complainants.<br></p>',0.00,0.00,'0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','0001-01-01 00:00:00.000','<p>Directing the respondents to pay interest on the due amount as mentioned in the maintenance agreement\r\ntill the pendency of the present complaint till actual payment.<br></p>','1','','0001-01-01 00:00:00','0001-01-01 00:00:00','','','',1,1,0,0,'BeeG','2019-04-02 16:56:47.000','BeeG','2019-04-02 16:56:47.000'),(1284,1307,'1307',1112,'29af80b1-85ed-4b88-8344-b429d2f24eca','FormTypeM',1,1,1,1,'2019-04-